0034-7426,fer-hji-zer.pdf,fer-hji-zer_0,en,Renormalized Solutions for Nonlinear,"This work is centered around the study of the following noncoercive elliptic problem : ( Au + g(x, u, ∇u) = f(x) + |u|p0−2u |x|p0 in Ω, u = 0 on ∂Ω, In the anisotropic Sobolev space, where Ωis a bounded open subset of RN (N ≥2) that includes the origin, with g(x, s, ξ) subject to certain growth conditions and f ∈L1(Ω). We prove the existence of renormalized solutions for the strongly nonlinear and non-coercive elliptic Dirichlet problem. Furthermore, we establish several regularity results","and phrases. Anisotropic Sobolev spaces, strongly nonlinear elliptic equation, non-coercive problems, renormalized solutions. 2020 Mathematics Subject Classification. Primary 35J15; Secondary 35J25",marcadores,renormaliz solution nonlinear,work center around study follow noncoercive elliptic problem au p0-2u p0 anisotropic sobolev space where ois bound open subset rn includ origin subject certain growth condition l1 we prove existence renormaliz solution strongly nonlinear non-coercive elliptic dirichlet problem furthermore we establish several regularity result,phras anisotropic sobolev spac strongly nonlinear elliptic equation non-coercive problem renormaliz solution 2020 mathematic subject classification primary 35j15 secondary 35j25,renormaliz solution nonlinear work center around study follow noncoercive elliptic problem au p0-2u p0 anisotropic sobolev space where ois bound open subset rn includ origin subject certain growth condition l1 we prove existence renormaliz solution strongly nonlinear non-coercive elliptic dirichlet problem furthermore we establish several regularity result phras anisotropic sobolev spac strongly nonlinear elliptic equation non-coercive problem renormaliz solution 2020 mathematic subject classification primary 35j15 secondary 35j25,1.0.0,482df55ef0f510b4
0034-7426,lalili.pdf,lalili_0,en,Solving Strongly Sublinear,"We study the existence of weak solutions to the nonlinear elliptic problem −∆p(x)u = λ|u|s(x)−2u + f(x, u, ∇u) in a bounded domain Ω⊂RN with smooth boundary ∂Ω, under homogeneous Dirichlet conditions. The equation features a variable exponent p(x) in the p(x)-Laplacian operator, an eigenvalue term λ|u|s(x)−2u, and a Carath´eodory perturbation f with sublinear growth, depending on both u and ∇u. Using a topological approach based on fixed-point theorems, we establish the existence of weak solutions to the problem","and phrases. Strongly nonlinear elliptic problem, p(x)-Laplacian, generalized Lebesgue-Sobolev spaces, fixed point. 2020 Mathematics Subject Classification. 35J60, 46E35, 47H05, 47H11",marcadores,solv strongly sublinear,we study existence weak solution nonlinear elliptic problem -p -2u bound domain orn smooth boundary under homogeneou dirichlet condition equation featur variable exponent -laplacian operator eigenvalue term -2u carath eodory perturbation sublinear growth depend both using topological approach based fixed-point theorem we establish existence weak solution problem,phras strongly nonlinear elliptic problem -laplacian generaliz lebesgue-sobolev spac fixed point 2020 mathematic subject classification 35j60 46e35 47h05 47h11,solv strongly sublinear we study existence weak solution nonlinear elliptic problem -p -2u bound domain orn smooth boundary under homogeneou dirichlet condition equation featur variable exponent -laplacian operator eigenvalue term -2u carath eodory perturbation sublinear growth depend both using topological approach based fixed-point theorem we establish existence weak solution problem phras strongly nonlinear elliptic problem -laplacian generaliz lebesgue-sobolev spac fixed point 2020 mathematic subject classification 35j60 46e35 47h05 47h11,1.0.0,6c7c6c6caaa3d214
