0120-0283,Aplicación+de+técnicas+de+clustering+y+machine+learning+en+Google+Earth+Engine+para+detectar+estructuras+asociadas+a+hidrógeno+natural.pdf,Aplicación+de+técnicas+de+clustering+y+machine+learning+en+Google+Earth+Engine+para+detectar+estructuras+asociadas+a+hidrógeno+natural_0,es,Aplicación de técnicas de clustering y machine,"El estudio aborda la posibilidad de que los datos satelitales y el aprendizaje automático permitan predecir, con soporte estadístico, estructuras superficiales potencialmente asociadas a emanaciones naturales de hidrógeno (círculos de hadas) en el norte de La Guajira (Colombia). Se integraron imágenes Sentinel‑2 y el modelo ALOS World 3D en Google Earth Engine para generar un mosaico multibanda de 88 km², del cual se derivaron índices espectrales (NDVI, NDBI, MNDWI, BSI), variables topográficas y un modelo de contexto espacial NDVI (vecindad 3 × 3). Sobre esta base se entrenó un clasificador random forest con 455 puntos de campo distribuidos en 7 clases de cobertura, posteriormente depuradas a 6, y se aplicó una validación explícita mediante particiones entrenamientovalidación y matrices de confusión. La precisión global del modelo mejoró de 78,94 % a 91,11 % tras eliminar la clase “urbano” y optimizar los hiperparámetros (130 árboles, partición 70/30), mientras que el análisis de importancia de variables destacó el papel de la elevación y del contraste espectral. Finalmente, se implementaron técnicas de clustering espacial y métricas de conectividad de píxeles que refinaron la detección de patrones asociados a círculos de hadas; esto consolidó una rutina clasificatoria estadísticamente consistente para apoyar la exploración de hidrógeno natural",Teledetección; Sentinel-2; Círculos de hadas; Índices espectrales; Clasificación supervisada; Hiperparámetros. Application of clustering and machine learning techniques in Google Earth Engine to detect structures associated with natural hydrogen emissions,marcadores,aplicacion tecnic clustering machine,estudio aborda posibilidad datos satelital aprendizaje automatico permitan predecir soporte estadistico estructur superficial potencial asociad eman natural hidrogeno circul hadas norte guajira colombia integraron imagen sentinel-2 modelo alos world 3d google earth engine generar mosaico multibanda 88 km2 cual derivaron indic espectral ndvi ndbi mndwi bsi variabl topografic modelo contexto espacial ndvi vecindad sobre esta base entreno clasificador random forest 455 punt campo distribuid clas cobertura posterior depurad aplico validacion explicita mediante particion entrenamientovalidacion matric confusion precision global modelo mejoro 78 94 91 11 tras eliminar clase urbano optimizar hiperparametr 130 arbol particion 70 30 mientr analisis importancia variabl destaco papel elevacion contraste espectral final implementaron tecnic clustering espacial metric conectividad pixel refinaron deteccion patron asociad circul hadas esto consolido rutina clasificatoria estadistica consistente apoyar exploracion hidrogeno natural,teledeteccion sentinel-2 circul hadas indic espectral clasificacion supervisada hiperparametr application of clustering and machine learning techniqu in google earth engine to detect structur associated with natural hydrogen emissions,aplicacion tecnic clustering machine estudio aborda posibilidad datos satelital aprendizaje automatico permitan predecir soporte estadistico estructur superficial potencial asociad eman natural hidrogeno circul hadas norte guajira colombia integraron imagen sentinel-2 modelo alos world 3d google earth engine generar mosaico multibanda 88 km2 cual derivaron indic espectral ndvi ndbi mndwi bsi variabl topografic modelo contexto espacial ndvi vecindad sobre esta base entreno clasificador random forest 455 punt campo distribuid clas cobertura posterior depurad aplico validacion explicita mediante particion entrenamientovalidacion matric confusion precision global modelo mejoro 78 94 91 11 tras eliminar clase urbano optimizar hiperparametr 130 arbol particion 70 30 mientr analisis importancia variabl destaco papel elevacion contraste espectral final implementaron tecnic clustering espacial metric conectividad pixel refinaron deteccion patron asociad circul hadas esto consolido rutina clasificatoria estadistica consistente apoyar exploracion hidrogeno natural teledeteccion sentinel-2 circul hadas indic espectral clasificacion supervisada hiperparametr application of clustering and machine learning techniqu in google earth engine to detect structur associated with natural hydrogen emissions,1.0.0,dbdaa527909c19b2
0120-0283,Aplicación+de+técnicas+de+clustering+y+machine+learning+en+Google+Earth+Engine+para+detectar+estructuras+asociadas+a+hidrógeno+natural.pdf,Aplicación+de+técnicas+de+clustering+y+machine+learning+en+Google+Earth+Engine+para+detectar+estructuras+asociadas+a+hidrógeno+natural_0,en,que el análisis de importancia de variables destacó el papel de la elevación y del contraste espectral.,"This study addresses whether satellite data and machine learning can reliably predict surface morphological structures potentially associated with natural hydrogen seepages (fairy circles) in northern La Guajira, Colombia. Multispectral Sentinel-2 imagery and ALOS World 3D topographic data were integrated in Google Earth Engine to generate a multiband composite over an 88 km² area, from which spectral indices (NDVI, NDBI, MNDWI, BSI), topographic variables, and an NDVI-based spatial context model (3×3 neighborhood) were derived. On this basis, a Random Forest classifier was trained using 455 ground-truth points distributed across seven land-cover classes, later refined to six, and explicitly validated through train–validation splits and confusion matrices. Overall accuracy improved from 78.94% to 91.11% after removing the urban class and tuning hyperparameters (130 Forma de citar: Zafra-Dulcey, M.G. (2026). Aplicación de técnicas de clustering y machine learning en Google Earth Engine para detectar estructuras asociadas a hidrógeno natural. Boletín de Geología, 48(2), 13-28. https://doi.org/10.18273/revbol.v48n2-2026001 14 Boletín de Geología - vol. 48, n.° 2 Aplicación de técnicas de clustering y machine learning en Google Earth Engine para detectar estructuras asociadas a hidrógeno natural trees, 70/30 split), while feature importance analysis highlighted the key contribution of elevation and spectral contrast. Finally, spatial clustering and connected-pixel metrics were applied as post-classification refinement, enhancing the detection of patterns associated with fairy circles and yielding a statistically consistent classification routine to support natural hydrogen exploration",Remote sensing; Sentinel-2; Fairy circles; Spectral indices; Supervised classification; Hyperparameters,marcadores,que el analisi de importancia de variabl destaco el papel de la elevacion del contraste espectral,study address whether satellite data machine learn can reliably predict surface morphological structur potentially associat natural hydrogen seepag fairy circl northern la guajira colombia multispectral sentinel-2 imagery alos world 3d topographic data integrat google earth engine generate multiband composite over 88 km2 area which spectral indic ndvi ndbi mndwi bsi topographic variabl ndvi-bas spatial context model 3x3 neighborhood deriv basi random forest classifier train using 455 ground-truth point distribut acros seven land-cover class later refin six explicitly validat through train-validation split confusion matric overall accuracy improv 78 94 91 11 after remov urban clas tuning hyperparameter 130 forma de citar zafra-dulcey 2026 aplicacion de tecnica de cluster machine learn en google earth engine para detectar estructura asociada hidrogeno natural boletin de geologia 48 13-28 http doi org 10 18273 revbol v48n2-2026001 14 boletin de geologia vol 48 deg aplicacion de tecnica de cluster machine learn en google earth engine para detectar estructura asociada hidrogeno natural tree 70 30 split while feature importance analysi highlight key contribution elevation spectral contrast finally spatial cluster connected-pixel metric appli post-classification refinement enhanc detection pattern associat fairy circl yield statistically consistent classification routine support natural hydrogen exploration,remote sens sentinel-2 fairy circl spectral indic supervis classification hyperparameter,que el analisi de importancia de variabl destaco el papel de la elevacion del contraste espectral study address whether satellite data machine learn can reliably predict surface morphological structur potentially associat natural hydrogen seepag fairy circl northern la guajira colombia multispectral sentinel-2 imagery alos world 3d topographic data integrat google earth engine generate multiband composite over 88 km2 area which spectral indic ndvi ndbi mndwi bsi topographic variabl ndvi-bas spatial context model 3x3 neighborhood deriv basi random forest classifier train using 455 ground-truth point distribut acros seven land-cover class later refin six explicitly validat through train-validation split confusion matric overall accuracy improv 78 94 91 11 after remov urban clas tuning hyperparameter 130 forma de citar zafra-dulcey 2026 aplicacion de tecnica de cluster machine learn en google earth engine para detectar estructura asociada hidrogeno natural boletin de geologia 48 13-28 http doi org 10 18273 revbol v48n2-2026001 14 boletin de geologia vol 48 deg aplicacion de tecnica de cluster machine learn en google earth engine para detectar estructura asociada hidrogeno natural tree 70 30 split while feature importance analysi highlight key contribution elevation spectral contrast finally spatial cluster connected-pixel metric appli post-classification refinement enhanc detection pattern associat fairy circl yield statistically consistent classification routine support natural hydrogen exploration remote sens sentinel-2 fairy circl spectral indic supervis classification hyperparameter,1.0.0,c0aa8ee77ebe7765
0120-0283,Inversión+conjunta+de+datos+TDEM+de+bajo+y+alto+momento+para+el+mejoramiento+de+los+modelos+del+subsuelo.pdf,Inversión+conjunta+de+datos+TDEM+de+bajo+y+alto+momento+para+el+mejoramiento+de+los+modelos+del+subsuelo_0,en,Joint Inversion of Low and High Moment TDEM,"Time-Domain Electromagnetic (TDEM) method has been widely used in environmental, hydrogeological, and mining studies. TDEM uses a transient current as its source, described by a waveform that presents two transmission moments: High Moment (HM) and Low Moment (LM), characterized by high and low currents, respectively. In typical TDEM surveys, LM and HM data are acquired simultaneously. Different studies have shown that LM data are more sensitive to early-time responses, providing detailed information about the near-surface layers, and HM data enable deeper investigation. Although LM and HM data provide complementary sensitivity to shallow and deep layers, in the state-of-the-art workflows, they are typically inverted independently. In this work, we propose a joint inversion method that integrates LM and HM data, minimizing the misfit between the observed and predicted values from the LM and HM data with a model regularization term. This approach yields a subsurface model that is consistent with both LM and HM data. We tested the proposed method using synthetic data in two scenarios: one with the same number of LM and HM data, and another with a lower number of LM data, to evaluate the method in situations where one of the measurements contains fewer data points due to noise contamination. In both scenarios, the proposed method outperformed single inversions in estimating resistive subsurface structures, as evidenced both visually in the models obtained and by the improvement in the RMS and metrics. In addition, we tested the proposed method using field data, where the model obtained is consistent with a VES model acquired at the same TDEM sounding location",Electromagnetic,marcadores,joint inversio