udy underscor complex significant role parental involvement shap student behaviour highli ghts importance emotional engagement-relat pathway educational outcom home-school cooperation learn engagement learn anxiety classroom disciplinary behaviour chinese student 2025 fundacion universitaria konrad lorenz open acces article under cc by-nc-nd license http creativecommon org licens by-nc-nd colaboracion familia-escuela analizando su impacto en la conducta disciplinaria en el aula la ansiedad ante el aprend,1.0.0,3aa4767ba8a52893
0120-0534,4d2f6389-9d91-4d1b-b5ba-90277d61d908.pdf,4d2f6389-9d91-4d1b-b5ba-90277d61d908_0,en,the CC BY-NC-ND license (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/).,"| Introduction: This study aimed to quantify and analyse scientific activity in Comparative Psychology and Animal Behaviour across the 19 Spanish-speaking countries in Latin America. This was achieved by examining articles published in journals indexed in the Web of Science Core Collection from 1975 to 2024 by authors affiliated with institutions in these countries. Method: A bibliometric analysis was conducted using 26 journals specialised in Comparative Psychology and Animal Behaviour, covering aspects such as historical production, authorship analysis, manuscripts, citations, countries, affiliations, and funding sources. The most relevant",", thematic mapping, thematic trends, and most frequently studied species were also identified. Results: A total of 1,971 articles were found. Most of the research output from Spanish-speaking countries in Latin America was concentrated in Mexico (35.1%), Argentina (21.6%), and Panama (12.8%). The contributions were mainly from authors associated with the Universidad Nacional Autónoma de México (",marcadores,cc by-nc-nd license http creativecommon org licens by-nc-nd,introduction study aimed quantify analyse scientific activity comparative psychology animal behaviour acros 19 spanish-speak countri latin america achiev examin articl publish journal index web science core collection 1975 2024 author affiliat institution these countri method bibliometric analysi conduct using 26 journal specialis comparative psychology animal behaviour cover aspect such historical production authorship analysi manuscript citation countri affili fund sourc most relevant,thematic mapp thematic trend most frequently studi speci also identifi result total 971 articl found most research output spanish-speak countri latin america concentrat mexico 35 argentina 21 panama 12 contribution mainly author associat universidad nacional autonoma de mexico,cc by-nc-nd license http creativecommon org licens by-nc-nd introduction study aimed quantify analyse scientific activity comparative psychology animal behaviour acros 19 spanish-speak countri latin america achiev examin articl publish journal index web science core collection 1975 2024 author affiliat institution these countri method bibliometric analysi conduct using 26 journal specialis comparative psychology animal behaviour cover aspect such historical production authorship analysi manuscript citation countri affili fund sourc most relevant thematic mapp thematic trend most frequently studi speci also identifi result total 971 articl found most research output spanish-speak countri latin america concentrat mexico 35 argentina 21 panama 12 contribution mainly author associat universidad nacional autonoma de mexico,1.0.0,030aaec2470b8ed0
0120-0534,4d2f6389-9d91-4d1b-b5ba-90277d61d908.pdf,4d2f6389-9d91-4d1b-b5ba-90277d61d908_0,es,"with the Universidad Nacional Autónoma de México (16%), the","| Introducción: El objetivo de este artículo es cuantificar y analizar la actividad científica en Psicología Comparada y Comportamiento Animal en 19 países hispanoamericanos, estudiando los artículos publicados en revistas indexadas en Web of Science Core Collection entre 1975 y 2024, por autores y autoras firmantes con dirección en estos países. Método: Se realizó un análisis bibliométrico ocupando 26 revistas especializadas en Psicología Comparada y Comportamiento Animal incluyendo los siguientes índices: producción histórica, análisis de autoría, manuscritos, citaciones, países, afiliación y fuentes de financiamiento. También se identificaron las","más relevantes, mapa temático, tendencia temática y especies más utilizadas. Resultados: Se encontraron un total de 1971 artículos. La mayoría de la producción 2 P. Herrera-Aroca et al. Comparative Psychology fundamentally aims to document the similarities and differences in behaviour and its underlying mechanisms across various species (Papini, 2009). By seeking to understand the evolutionary p",marcadores,with the universidad nacional autonoma mexico 16 the,introduccion objetivo este articulo cuantificar analizar actividad cientifica psicologia comparada comportamiento animal 19 pais hispanoamerican estudi articul publicad revist indexad web of science core collection entre 1975 2024 autor autor firmant direccion estos pais metodo realizo analisis bibliometrico ocup 26 revist especializad psicologia comparada comportamiento animal incluyendo siguient indic produccion historica analisis autoria manuscrit citacion pais afiliacion fuent financiamiento tambien identificaron,mas relevant mapa tematico tendencia tematica especi mas utilizad resultad encontraron total 1971 articul mayoria produccion herrera-aroca et comparative psychology fundamentally aims to document t