0120-0534,a1c90d59-e93b-4663-925b-97d01218923b.pdf,a1c90d59-e93b-4663-925b-97d01218923b_0,en,rfaz de Biblioshiny de RStudio v.4.4.1 y VOSviewer. Resultados: se muestran cómo los,"| Introduction: The literature points out that mental health has addictive consumption as a risk factor and/or the absence of mental health can lead to addictive disorder. However, sport is a protective factor against the development of addictive behaviour and deterioration of mental health. Objective: To analyse trends and patterns in the scientific liter ature on education, mental health, healthy living, sport and substance use in adolescents through a bibliometric analysis. Method: A quantitative-bibliometric review methodology is used by exploring the Core Collection of the Web of Science and obtaining a sample of 240 academic-scientific articles during the period 2014 and 2024, collected during June 2024. The variables taken as variables are the titles, abstracts,","plus and authors keywords, and use the filters Highly Cited 71 Factores de protección y de riesgo sobre la salud mental en la adolescencia: un estudio bibliométrico El término actual “adolescencia” se entiende como una época de paso de la inmadurez de la infancia a la madu rez de la edad adulta en un periodo lleno de transiciones biológicas, psicológicas, sociales y económicas (Stein berg, 2022)",marcadores,rfaz de biblioshiny de rstudio vosviewer resultado se muestran como los,introduction literature point out mental health has addictive consumption risk factor absence mental health can lead addictive disorder however sport protective factor against development addictive behaviour deterioration mental health objective analyse trend pattern scientific liter ature education mental health healthy living sport substance use adolescent through bibliometric analysi method quantitative-bibliometric review methodology used explor core collection web science obtain sample 240 academic-scientific articl during period 2014 2024 collect during june 2024 variabl taken variabl titl abstract,plus author keyword use filter highly cited 71 factor de proteccion de riesgo sobre la salud mental en la adolescencia un estudio bibliometrico el termino actual adolescencia se entiende como una epoca de paso de la inmadurez de la infancia la madu rez de la edad adulta en un periodo lleno de transicion biologica psicologica social economica stein berg 2022,rfaz de biblioshiny de rstudio vosviewer resultado se muestran como los introduction literature point out mental health has addictive consumption risk factor absence mental health can lead addictive disorder however sport protective factor against development addictive behaviour deterioration mental health objective analyse trend pattern scientific liter ature education mental health healthy living sport substance use adolescent through bibliometric analysi method quantitative-bibliometric review methodology used explor core collection web science obtain sample 240 academic-scientific articl during period 2014 2024 collect during june 2024 variabl taken variabl titl abstract plus author keyword use filter highly cited 71 factor de proteccion de riesgo sobre la salud mental en la adolescencia un estudio bibliometrico el termino actual adolescencia se entiende como una epoca de paso de la inmadurez de la infancia la madu rez de la edad adulta en un periodo lleno de transicion biologica psicologica social economica stein berg 2022,1.0.0,e43586bde03fb886
0120-0534,b36ec163-3fa3-46a2-ab6d-c36a7e956d9d.pdf,b36ec163-3fa3-46a2-ab6d-c36a7e956d9d_0,en,* Corresponding author.,"| Introduction/Objective: Ghosting, defined as the abrupt termination of a relationship without explanation or further contact, has become increasingly common among youth and emerging adults, largely due to the widespread use of digital platforms. This systematic review aims to synthesise empirical evidence on the characteristics of individuals in volved in ghosting, their motivations, emotional and psychological consequences, and the instruments used to assess the phenomenon. Method: A total of 11 studies published between 2019 and 2024 were analysed, including 4,981 participants up to 29 years of age. The selected studies employed quantitative, qualitative, mixed, and experimental methodologies. Results: Ghosting is associated with avoidant attachment styles, the need for closure, and specific personality traits among those who ghost, while victims tend to display anxious attachment and high levels of social comparison. Motiva tions for ghosting are diverse and include conflict avoidance, emotional self-protection, disinterest, and poor communi cation. Although it is often perceived as a quick and less confrontational way to end a relationship, ghosting can lead to significant psychological effects for both the initiator and the recipient, including anxiety, sadness, guilt, or relief. Digital communication facilitates this behaviour by minimising the discomfort of direct confrontation. Normative perceptions and cultural factors influence its acceptance and emotional consequences. A notable lack of validated and consistent ins truments for assessing ghosting was identified. Conclusions: Ghosting can affect the mental health of those involved. Its inclusion in affective-sexual health interventions is recommended, along with the development of valid instruments that allow for rigorous evaluation","Relational psychology, emotional impact, social dynamics, digital communication, breakup strategies © 2025 Fundación Universitaria Konrad Lorenz. This is an open access article under the CC BY-NC-ND license (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/ by-nc-nd/4.0/). Revisión sistemática del ghosting como método de disolución de relaciones en adultos emergentes",marcadores,correspond author,introduction objective ghost defin abrupt termination relationship without explanation further contact has become increas common among youth emerg adult largely due widespread use digital platform systematic review aims synthesise empirical evidence characteristic individual volv ghost their motiv emotional psychological consequenc instrument used asses phenomenon method total 11 studi publish between 2019 2024 analys includ 981 participant up 29 year age select studi employ quantitative qualitative mixed experimental methodologi result ghost associat avoidant attachment styl need closure specific personality trait among those who ghost while victim tend display anxiou attachment high level social comparison motiva tion ghost diverse include conflict avoidance emotional self-protection disinterest poor communi cation although often perceiv quick less confrontational way end relationship ghost can lead significant psychological effect both initiator recipient includ anxiety sadnes guilt relief digital communication facilitat behaviour minimis discomfort direct confrontation normative perception cultural factor influence its acceptance emotional consequenc notable lack validat consistent ins trument assess ghost identifi conclusion ghost can affect mental health those involv its inclusion affective-sexual health intervention recommend along development valid instrument allow rigorou evaluation,relational psychology emotional impact social dynamic digital communication breakup strategi 2025 fundacion universitaria konrad lorenz open acces article under cc by-nc-nd license http creativecommon org licens by-nc-nd revision sistematica del ghost