esult ob tain result show factorial invariance metric invariance strong invariance all three variabl strict variance concern sex variable also confirm men people who do not cohabit people without chil dren more satisfi their relationship than women people who cohabit people children conclusion scale has demonstrat adequate factorial invariance analys variabl confirm possibility us ing different sample type instrument validation scale factorial invariance couple relationship marital satisfaction 2025 fundacion universitaria konrad lorenz open acces article under cc by-nc-nd license http creativecommon org licens by-nc-nd invariancia factorial de la escala de satisfaccion en la relacion de pareja scr en funcion de las variabl sexo convivencia tener hijo,1.0.0,2ef80dfb7dc12bbe
0120-0534,eca5e543-2b5d-4482-a66a-718ed4e552ff.pdf,eca5e543-2b5d-4482-a66a-718ed4e552ff_0,en,ss article under,"| Introduction: Clinical psychology professionals and trainees face significant occupational stress, which can lead to repetitive negative thinking (RNT). The Perseverative Thinking Questionnaire for Clinical Psychology Trainees (PTQ-CPT) measures RNT in this population. This study aimed to examine the psychometric properties and cross-national measurement invariance of the PTQ-CPT in three Latin American countries. Method: The sample comprised 475 partici pants from Colombia (n = 101), Mexico (n = 253), and Peru (n = 121). The participants were clinical psychology professionals and trainees. Data were collected via an online survey. The PTQ-CPT, along with measurements of depressive symptoms, anxiety symptoms, and confidence in clinical skills, were administered. Confirmatory factor analysis, measurement in variance testing, a graded response model, and correlational analyses were conducted. Results: A unidimensional struc ture with a pair of correlated errors provided the best fit for the PTQ-CPT. Metric invariance across countries was con firmed, while scalar invariance was supported by the pragmatic criterion (difference in CFI < .01) but not by the strict criterion (difference in 2). The graded response model showed that item 5 had the greatest informative capacity. PTQ-CPT scores correlated positively with depressive (r = .45) and anxiety (r = .56) symptoms, and negatively with confidence in clinical skills (r = -.58). Conclusions: The PTQ-CPT demonstrated adequate psychometric properties and cross-national measurement invariance. It is a reliable and valid tool for assessing RNT in clinical psychology professionals and trainees across Colombia, Mexico, and Peru. These findings support the use of the PTQ-CPT in cross-cultural research and clinical practice","Repetitive negative thinking, health personnel, health science trainees, psychometric analysis, rumination, worry © 2025 Fundación Universitaria Konrad Lorenz. This is an open access article under the CC BY-NC-ND license (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/ by-nc-nd/4.0/). Invarianza de medición transnacional del Cuestionario de Pensamiento Perseverativo para profesionales y estudiantes de ps",marcadores,ss article under,introduction clinical psychology professional traine face significant occupational stres which can lead repetitive negative think rnt perseverative think questionnaire clinical psychology traine ptq-cpt measur rnt population study aimed examine psychometric properti cross-national measurement invariance ptq-cpt three latin american countri method sample compris 475 partici pant colombia 101 mexico 253 peru 121 participant clinical psychology professional traine data collect via online survey ptq-cpt along measurement depressive symptom anxiety symptom confidence clinical skill administer confirmatory factor analysi measurement variance test grad response model correlational analys conduct result unidimensional struc ture pair correlat error provid best fit ptq-cpt metric invariance acros countri con firm while scalar invariance support pragmatic criterion difference cfi 01 but not strict criterion difference grad response model show item had greatest informative capacity ptq-cpt scor correlat positively depressive 45 anxiety 56 symptom negatively confidence clinical skill 58 conclusion ptq-cpt demonstrat adequate psychometric properti cross-national measurement invariance reliable valid tool assess rnt clinical psychology professional traine acros colombia mexico peru these finding support use ptq-cpt cross-cultural research clinical practice,repetitive negative think health personnel health science traine psychometric analysi rumination worry 2025 fundacion universitaria konrad lorenz open acces article under cc by-nc-nd license http creativecommon org licens by-nc-nd invarianza de medicion transnacional del cuestionario de pensamiento p