0120-100X,ION_Vol_38N3_25_ART5.pdf,ION_Vol_38N3_25_ART5_0,en,que presente las propiedades de la U. dioica y el MeSal puede ofrecer una solución alternativa,"The review article presents the properties of flavonoids present in Nettle (Urtica dioica sp) and methyl salicylate (MeSal) for the formulation of a topical cream, based on the anti-inflammatory, antioxidant, antimicrobial and analgesic properties of these compounds, thus verifying their possible synergy for the formulation of a topical cream, based on the anti-inflammatory, antioxidant, antimicrobial and analgesic properties of these compounds, thus verifying their possible synergy. The aim was to evaluate, from a theoretical perspective, the potential of these compounds to alleviate muscular pain and skin inflammations. The methodology included a systematic search, where databases such as Scopus, SpringerLink, MDPI and Google Scholar were consulted, looking for research articles, reviews and books. However, U. dioica is attributed with properties due to its flavonoids and phenolic content, making it useful against problems such as arthritis and allergies. MeSal is also effective and widely used in dermatological treatments as, due to its analgesic and anti-inflammatory action, it penetrates the skin and reduces inflammation without generating adverse effects, making it an ideal compound in the formulation of topical creams. From the above, it can be concluded from a theoretical perspective that the formulation of a topical cream that presents the properties of U. dioica and MeSal can offer an alternative and effective solution for the treatment of skin and muscle disorders; however, it is recommended that experimental trials be carried out to contribute to the natural therapeutic field for the formulation of such a cream",Anti-inflammatory; Antioxidant; Analgesics; Flavonoids; Antimicrobial. Efeito sinérgico dos grupos flavonóides presentes na Urtiga (Urtica dioica) com o salicilato de metilo para a formulação