ce observ among consumer purchaser individual responsible cook lamb animal category purchas 85 respondent occasional consumption 44 consumption home 68 most frequently report pattern overall ovine meat consumption low therefore advanc effort addres factor associat ovine meat consumption relevant input contemporary policy discussion transformation regional ovine sector argentina consumer lamb meat market analisi del consumo de carne ovina en la plata bueno aire argentina,1.0.0,c9e7da3868f29762
0120-2952,Rev+Med+Vet+Zoot+72(3)_e120626_Silva+(2).pdf,Rev+Med+Vet+Zoot+72(3)_e120626_Silva+(2)_0,en,Veterinary medicine and canine aging: general aspects of the,"Life expectancy in dogs has increased due to advances in veterinary medicine, making the systematic monitoring of senior animals essential. This article presents a narrative literature review conducted between July and November 2025 using the PubMed, SciELO, and ScienceDirect databases, including publications from 2020 to 2025 that address physiological, clinical, and therapeutic aspects of geriatric dogs, with emphasis on studies from South America, North America, and Europe. The review describes criteria for age classification, physiological changes associated with aging, and the main conditions affecting this population, such as osteoarticular, renal, endocrine, cognitive, and neoplastic diseases. The literature highlights the importance of early identification of these alterations and the role of owners in adherence to care. The objective of this article is to synthesize current knowledge on the most prevalent diseases in elderly dogs and to present evidence-based measures that support adequate monitoring and management","dogs, treatments, aging, pathologies. Medicina veterinária e o envelhecimento canino: aspectos gerais da identificação e tratamento das principais doenças em cães idosos",marcadores,veterinary medicine canine aging general aspect,life expectancy dogs has increas due advanc veterinary medicine making systematic monitor senior animal essential article present narrative literature review conduct between july november 2025 using pubm scielo sciencedirect databas includ public 2020 2025 addres physiological clinical therapeutic aspect geriatric dogs emphasi studi south america north america europe review describ criteria age classification physiological chang associat aging main condition affect population such osteoarticular renal endocrine cognitive neoplastic diseas literature highlight