0120-2952,Rev+Med+Vet+Zoot+72(3)_e121043_Perdomo-Ayola.pdf,Rev+Med+Vet+Zoot+72(3)_e121043_Perdomo-Ayola_0,en,Behavioral and adaptive evaluation of lactating Costeño,"Heat stress is one of the main challenges for cattle production in tropical regions, as it affects both animal welfare and productive efficiency. This study aimed to characterize the behavior of Costeño con Cuernos (CCC) and Gyrolando cattle under tropical dry forest conditions in Colombia, assessing their behavioral responses across different time periods and microclimatic conditions. The research was conducted in a silvopastoral system at the Motilonia Research Center of Agrosavia, located at an altitude of 106 m a.s.l., with a multiyear average temperature of 29.4 °C and an average relative humidity of 70%. Twelve lactating cows (six CCC and six Gyrolando) were observed from July to September 2023, and 20 behavioral variables, along with bioclimatic indicators such as the temperature–humidity index, were recorded. Data were analyzed using multiple correspondence analysis and hierarchical clustering. Results revealed two behavioral clusters: Cluster 1 (adverse climatic conditions) grouped animals that were more active during the hottest hours (12:00–14:00), with increased grazing activity and reduced resting behavior. This cluster consisted mainly of CCC cows. Cluster 2 (moderate climatic conditions) was characterized by predominant lying rumination, shaded resting, and lower overall activity, primarily involving Gyrolando cows. It is concluded that the native CCC breed exhibits more adaptive behavioral patterns under hot environmental conditions, underscoring its potential value for sustainable cattle production systems. The integration of multivariate tools and environmental monitoring allows the identification of management strategies aimed at improving animal welfare and productivity under extreme climatic conditions","animal welfare, adaptation, heat stress, microclimate. 1 Colombian Corporation for Agricultural Research (Agrosavia). Motilonia Research Center, km 5, Becerril Road, Agustín Codazzi, Cesar, Colombia. * Corresponding author: sperdomo@agrosavia.co 2 Colombian Corporation for Agricultural Research (Agrosavia). La Libertad Research Center, km 17, Puerto López Road, Villavicencio, Meta, Colombia. ht",marcadores,behavioral adaptive evaluation lactat costeno,heat stres one main challeng cattle production tropical region affect both animal welfare productive efficiency study aimed characterize behavior costeno con cuerno ccc gyrolando cattle under tropical dry forest condition colombia assess their behavioral respons acros different time period microclimatic condition research conduct silvopastoral system motilonia research center agrosavia locat altitude 106 multiyear average temperature 29 degc average relative humidity 70 twelve lactat cows six ccc six gyrolando observ july september 2023 20 behavioral variabl along bioclimatic indicator such temperature-humidity index record data analyz using multiple correspondence analysi hierarchical cluster result reveal two behavioral cluster cluster adverse climatic condition group animal more active during hottest hour 12 00-14 00 increas graz activity reduc rest behavior cluster consist mainly ccc cows cluster moderate climatic condition characteriz predominant lying rumination shad rest lower overall activity primarily involv gyrolando cows conclud native ccc breed exhibit more adaptive behavioral pattern under hot environmental condition underscor its potential value sustainable cattle production system integration multivariate tool environmental monitor allow identification management strategi aimed improv animal welfare productivity under extreme climatic condition,animal welfare adaptation heat stres microclimate colombian corporation agricultural research agrosavia motilonia research center km becerril road agustin codazzi cesar colombia correspond author sperdomo agrosavia co colombian corporation agricultural research agrosavia la libertad research center km 17 puerto lopez road villavicencio meta colombia ht,behavioral adaptive evaluation lactat costeno heat stres one main challeng cattle production tropical region affect both animal welfare productive efficiency study aimed characterize behavior costeno con cuerno ccc gyrolando cattle under tropical dry forest condition colombia assess their behavioral respons acros different time period microclimatic condition research conduct silvopastoral system motilonia research center agrosavia locat altitude 106 multiyear average temperature 29 degc average relative humidity 70 twelve lactat cows six ccc six gyrolando observ july september 2023 20 behavioral variabl along bioclimatic indicator such temperature-humidity index record data analyz using multiple correspondence analysi hierarchical cluster result reveal two behavioral cluster cluster adverse climatic condition group animal more active during hottest hour 12 00-14 00 increas graz activity reduc rest behavior cluster consist mainly ccc cows cluster moderate climatic condition characteriz predominant lying rumination shad rest lower overall activity primarily involv gyrolando cows conclud native ccc breed exhibit more adaptive behavioral pattern under hot environmental condition underscor its potential value sustainable cattle production system integration multivariate tool environmental monitor allow identification management strategi aimed improv animal welfare productivity under extreme climatic condition animal welfare adaptation heat stres microclimate colombian corporation agricultural research agrosavia motilonia research center km becerril road agustin codazzi cesar colombia correspond author sperdomo agrosavia co colombian corporation agricultural research agrosavia la libertad research center km 17 puerto lopez road villavicencio meta colombia ht,1.0.0,5ad7c35b0a825386
0120-2952,Rev+Med+Vet+Zoot+72(3)_e121043_Perdomo-Ayola.pdf,Rev+Med+Vet+Zoot+72(3)_e121043_Perdomo-Ayola_0,es,"stainability of production systems,","El estrés por calor es uno de los principales desafíos para la producción bovina en regiones tropicales, afectando el bienestar animal y la eficiencia productiva. Este estudio tuvo como objetivo caracterizar el comportamiento de bovinos de las razas Costeño con Cuernos (CCC) y Gyrolando en condiciones de bosque seco tropical en Colombia, evaluando su respuesta comportamental ante diferentes rangos horarios y condiciones microclimáticas. La investigación se realizó en un sistema silvopastoril del centro de investigación Motilonia de Agrosavia a una altitud de 106 m s. n. m. con temperatura promedio multianual de 29,4 °C y humedad relativa promedio del 70%. Se observaron 12 vacas en lactancia (6 CCC y 6 Gyrolando) durante los meses de julio a septiembre de 2023, registrando 20 variables comportamentales e indicadores bioclimáticos como índice temperatura-humedad. Los datos fueron analizados mediante análisis factorial de múltiples correspondencias y clasificación jerárquica. Los resultados revelaron dos clústeres de comportamiento: clúster 1 (condiciones climáticas adversas) agrupó animales más activos durante las horas de mayor calor (12:00–14:00), con mayor pastoreo y menor descanso. Este grupo estuvo compuesto principalmente por la raza CCC. El clúster 2 (condiciones climáticas moderadas) presentó mayor rumia echado, descanso en sombra y menor actividad general, predominando la raza Gyrolando. Se concluye que la raza criolla CCC muestra actividades comportamentales más adaptativas en ambientes calurosos, lo que podría reforzar su valor en sistemas ganaderos sostenibles. La integración de herramientas multivariantes y monitoreo ambiental permite identificar estrategias de manejo orientadas al bienestar animal y la productividad bajo condiciones climáticas extremas","bienestar animal, adaptación, estrés por calor, microclima. Perdomo–Ayola, et al. (2025). Behavioral and adaptive evaluation of lactating Costeño con Cuernos and Gyrolando cows under tropical dry forest conditions (Colombia). Investigación __________________________ Rev Med Vet Zoot. 72(3), septiembre-diciembe 2025: 3 de 15 compromising animal welfare (Collier et al., 2019; Summer et al., 2019",marcadores,stainability of production systems,estr calor uno principal desafi produccion bovina region tropical afect bienestar animal eficiencia productiva este estudio tuvo como objetivo caracterizar comportamiento bovin razas costeno cuern ccc gyrol condicion bosque seco tropical colombia evalu respuesta comportamental ante diferent rang horari condicion microclimatic investigacion realizo sistema silvopastoril centro investigacion motilonia agrosavia altitud 106 temperatura promedio multianual 29 degc humedad relativa promedio 70 observaron 12 vacas lactancia ccc gyrol durante meses julio septiembre 2023 registr 20 variabl comportamental indicador bioclimatic como indice temperatura-humedad datos fueron analizad mediante analisis factorial multipl correspondenci clasificacion jerarquica resultad revelaron dos cluster comportamiento cluster condicion climatic advers agrupo animal mas activ durante horas mayor calor 12 00-14 00 mayor pastoreo menor descanso este grupo estuvo compuesto principal raza ccc cluster condicion climatic moderad presento mayor rumia echado descanso sombra menor actividad general predomin raza gyrol concluye raza criolla ccc muestra actividad comportamental mas adaptativ ambient caluros podria reforzar valor sistem ganader sostenibl integracion herramient multivariant monitoreo ambiental permite identificar estrategi manejo orientad bienestar animal productividad bajo condicion climatic extrem,bienestar animal adaptacion estr calor microclima perdomo-ayola et 2025 behavioral and adaptive evaluation of lactating costeno cuern and gyrol cows under tropical dry forest conditions colombia investigacion ____