0120-2952,Rev+Med+Vet+Zoot+73(1)_e116100_Reátegui+(2).pdf,Rev+Med+Vet+Zoot+73(1)_e116100_Reátegui+(2)_0,en,Effect of Dictyoloma vandellianum A. Juss. (Huamansamana) formulations,"Huamansamana (Dictyoloma vandellianum A. Juss) is a plant resource particularly abundant in the Amazon region, whose leaves have traditionally and empirically been used for the control and prevention of ectoparasites in poultry (Mallophaga and Acari). However, its effects under field and laboratory conditions remain poorly understood. The objective of this study was to determine the effect of formulations derived from Dictyoloma vandellianum A. Juss (huamansamana) on lice and mites affecting domestic poultry raised under family-based production systems. Nine formulations were prepared, including a control group, fresh leaves (extract, powder, and macerate), and stems (fresh and macerated). A total of 567 lice and fleas were collected from domestic poultry raised under backyard conditions. A completely randomized design with split plots and 3 × 3 factors was implemented under field conditions, and an additional experimental design was conducted under laboratory conditions. Subsequently, 252 ectoparasites were obtained, comprising lice (79.36%) and mites (20.64%). The results demonstrated that the formulation based on stem maceration achieved complete effectiveness (100%) against ectoparasites in both field and laboratory phases. The effectiveness observed in backyard poultry suggests that this plant-based formulation may support the adoption of more efficient integrated management strategies, reducing reliance on empirical practices in the field, incorporating a natural active component, and avoiding the excessive use of chemical products that could lead to resistance in the future","poultry, pest control, sustainable development, plant-based product. Efecto de formulaciones de Dictyoloma vandellianum A. Juss. (Huamansamana) en el control de piojos y ácaros en gallinas domésticas, San Martín, Perú",marcadores,effect dictyoloma vandellianum juss huamansamana formul,huamansamana dictyoloma vandellianum juss plant resource particularly abundant amazon region whose leav have traditionally empirically been used control prevention ectoparasit poultry mallophaga acari however its effect under field laboratory condition remain poorly understood objective study determine effect formul deriv dictyoloma vandellianum juss huamansamana lice mite affect domestic poultry rais under family-bas production system nine formul prepar includ control group fresh leav extract powder macerate stem fresh macerat total 567 lice flea collect domestic poultry rais under backyard condition completely randomiz design split plot factor implement under field condition additional experimental design conduct under laboratory condition subsequently 252 ectoparasit obtain compris lice 79 36 mite 20 64 result demonstrat formulation based stem maceration achiev complete effectivenes 100 against ectoparasit both field laboratory phas effectivenes observ backyard poultry suggest plant-bas formulation may support adoption more efficient integrat management strategi reduc reliance empirical practic field incorporat natural active component avoid excessive use chemical product could lead resistance future,poultry pest control sustainable development plant-bas product efecto de formulacion de dictyoloma vandellianum juss huamansamana en el control de piojo acaro en gallina domestica san martin peru,effect dictyoloma vandellianum juss huamansamana formul huamansamana dictyoloma vandellianum juss plant resource particularly abundant amazon region whose leav have traditionally empirically been used control prevention ectoparasit poultry mallophaga acari however its effect under field laboratory condition remain poorly understood objective study determine effect formul deriv dictyoloma vandellianum juss huamansamana lice mite affect domestic poultry rais under family-bas production system nine formul prepar includ control group fresh leav extract powder macerate stem fresh macerat total 567 lice flea collect domestic poultry rais under backyard condition completely randomiz design split plot factor implement under field condition additional experimental design conduct under laboratory condition subsequently 252 ectoparasit obtain compris lice 79 36 mite 20 64 result demonstrat formulation based stem maceration achiev complete effectivenes 100 against ectoparasit both field laboratory phas effectivenes observ backyard poultry suggest plant-bas formulation may support adoption more efficient integrat management strategi reduc reliance empirical practic field incorporat natural active component avoid excessive use chemical product could lead resistance future poultry pest control sustainable development plant-bas product efecto de formulacion de dictyoloma vandellianum juss huamansamana en el control de piojo acaro en gallina domestica san martin peru,1.0.0,c02afd053b8d08f3
0120-2952,Rev+Med+Vet+Zoot+73(1)_e122795_Silva-Igua.pdf,Rev+Med+Vet+Zoot+73(1)_e122795_Silva-Igua_0,en,Indirect measurement of welfare in companion animals according to the alignment,"This study aimed to establish an indicator of welfare in dogs and cats to analyze predictive variables and evaluate the association between owners’ knowledge and their preventive practices. An analytical cross-sectional observational study was conducted through in-person administration of a survey designed for the quantitative assessment of animal welfare. The survey was applied to 354 companion animal owners residing in Chía who were randomly approached in public areas. Participants belonged to different socioeconomic strata and voluntarily agreed to participate. Animal welfare was quantified based on indicators derived from the scientific literature. Descriptive and bivariate analyses were performed to evaluate the association between welfare and owners’ knowledge. In addition, a binary logistic regression analysis was conducted using welfare as the outcome variable to develop a predictive regression model of welfare in these species. The prevalence of welfare was estimated at 27.7% in dogs, 18.7% in cats, and 24.7% when both species were considered together. Statistically significant associations were identified between overall welfare and owner knowledge (PR 1.25; 95% CI 1.12–1.30; p < 0.001), adherence to preventive measures (PR 1.15; 95% CI 1.05–1.30; p < 0.01), physical welfare (PR 1.15; 95% CI 1.08–1.21; p < 0.001), and mental welfare (PR 1.34; 95% CI 1.18–1.40; p < 0.001) PR (Prevalence Ratio); CI (Confidence Interval). The main predictors of welfare in dogs and cats were owner knowledge, adherence to preventive practices, physical welfare, and mental welfare. These findings provide scientific evidence regarding the prevalence of welfare in these species, as well as gaps in knowledge and limited adherence to primary prevention measures among small-animal owners, highlighting the need for further research to better understand the factors associated with animal welfare in companion animals","companion animals, welfare, primary prevention. Medición indirecta de bienestar en animales de compañía según alineación de su manejo con recomendaciones científicas en Chía, Colombia",marcadores,indirect measurement welfare companion animal accord alignment,study aimed establish indicator welfare dogs cats analyze predictive variabl evaluate association between owner knowledge their preventive practic analytical cross-sectional observational study conduct through in-person administration survey design quantitative assessment animal welfare survey appli 354 companion animal owner resid chia who randomly approach public area participant belong different socioeconomic strata voluntarily agre participate animal welfare quantifi based indicator deriv scientific literature descriptive bivariate analys perform evaluate association between welfare owner knowledge addition binary logistic regression analysi conduct using welfare outcome variable develop predictive regression model welfare these speci prevalence welfare estimat 27 dogs 18 cats 24 when both speci consider together statistically significant associ identifi between overall welfare owner knowledge pr 25 95 ci 12-1 30 001 adherence preventive measur pr 15 95 ci 05-1 30 01 physical welfare pr 15 95 ci 08-1 21 001 mental welfare pr 34 95 ci 18-1 40 001 pr prevalence ratio ci confidence interval main predictor welfare dogs cats owner knowledge adherence preventive practic physical welfare mental welfare these finding provide scientific evidence regard prevalence welfare these speci well gaps knowledge limit adherence primary prevention measur among small-animal owner highlight need further research better understand factor associat animal welfare companion animal,companion animal welfare primary prevention medicion indirecta de bienestar en animal de compania segun alineacion de su manejo con recomendacion cientifica en chia colombia,indirect measurement welfare companion animal accord alignment study aimed establish indicator welfare dogs cats analyze predictive variabl evaluate association between owner knowledge their preventive practic analytical cross-sectional observational study conduct through in-person administration survey design quantitative assessment animal welfare survey appli 354 companion animal owner resid chia who randomly approach public area participant belong different socioeconomic strata voluntarily agre participate animal welfare quantifi based indicator deriv scientific literature descriptive bivariate analys perform evaluate association between welfare owner knowledge addition binary logistic regression analysi conduct using welfare outcome variable develop predictive regression model welfare these speci prevalence welfare estimat 27 dogs 18 cats 24 when both speci consider together statistically significant associ identifi between overall welfare owner knowledge pr 25 95 ci 12-1 30 001 adherence preventive measur pr 15 95 ci 05-1 30 01 physical welfare pr 15 95 ci 08-1 21 001 mental welfare pr 34 95 ci 18-1 40 001 pr prevalence ratio ci confidence interval main predictor welfare dogs cats owner knowledge adherence preventive practic physical welfare mental welfare these finding provide scientific evidence regard prevalence welfare these speci well gaps knowledge limit adherence primary prevention measur among small-animal owner highlight need further research better understand factor associat animal welfare companion animal companion animal welfare primary prevention medicion indirecta de bienestar en animal de compania segun alineacion de su manejo con recomendacion cientifica en chia colombia,1.0.0,2cf474868ee15716
0120-3630,01_122503.FINAL.pdf,01_122503.FINAL_0,es,rsidad Nacional de Colombia.,"Se presenta un modelo geofísico integrado para la caracterización geotécnica del subsuelo en el km 17+100 de la Troncal Amazónica (Sucúa–Logroño), en la provincia de Morona Santiago, Ecuador, una zona de alta complejidad geológica. A diferencia de estudios convencionales con técnicas aisladas, se integran sísmica de refracción, MASW, ReMi y tomografía de resistividad eléctrica para obtener perfiles estratigráficos y derivar parámetros elásticos dinámicos (Edin, G y μ), correlacionados con módulos estáticos y de deformación empleados en diseño geotécnico. El análisis evidenció heterogeneidad lateral significativa, variaciones en la profundidad del estrato competente y zonas profundas de posible saturación hídrica, factores determinantes en la estabilidad vial amazónica. Se identificaron dos unidades principales: una capa superficial de suelos limoso-arenosos y una unidad inferior de limos consolidados y roca meteorizada. El estudio propone un modelo geofísico 2D predictivo para optimizar la ubicación de sondeos directos y reducir incertidumbre técnica y costos de exploración","caracterización geofísica; estructura superficial; resistividad eléctrica; sísmica de refracción. Geophysical characterization for geotechnical purposes along the Amazon Trunk Road, Ecuador: the case of the Sucúa–Logroño section",marcadores,rsidad nacional colombia,presenta modelo geofisico integrado caracterizacion geotecnica subsuelo km 17 100 troncal amazonica sucua-logrono provincia morona santiago ecuador zona alta complejidad geologica diferencia estudi convencional tecnic aislad integran sismica refraccion masw remi tomografia resistividad electrica obtener perfil estratigrafic derivar parametr elastic dinamic edin correlacionad modul estatic deformacion emplead diseno geotecnico analisis evidencio heterogeneidad lateral significativa vari profundidad estrato competente zonas profund posible saturacion hidrica factor determinant estabilidad vial amazonica identificaron dos unidad principal capa superficial suel limoso-arenos unidad inferior limos consolidad roca meteorizada estudio propone modelo geofisico 2d predictivo optimizar ubicacion sonde direct reducir incertidumbre tecnica cost exploracion,caracterizacion geofisica estructura superficial resistividad electrica sismica refraccion geophysical characterization for geotechnical purpos along the amazon trunk road ecuador the case of the sucua-logrono section,rsidad nacional colombia presenta modelo geofisico integrado caracterizacion geotecnica subsuelo km 17 100 troncal amazonica sucua-logrono provincia morona santiago ecuador zona alta complejidad geologica diferencia estudi convencional tecnic aislad integran sismica refraccion masw remi tomografia resistividad electrica obtener perfil estratigrafic derivar parametr elastic dinamic edin correlacionad modul estatic deformacion emplead diseno geotecnico analisis evidencio heterogeneidad lateral significativa vari profundidad estrato competente zonas profund posible saturacion hidrica factor determinant estabilidad vial amazonica identificaron dos unidad principal capa superficial suel limoso-arenos unidad inferior limos consolidad roca meteorizada estudio propone modelo geofisico 2d predictivo optimizar ubicacion sonde direct reducir incertidumbre tecnica cost exploracion caracterizacion geofisica estructura superficial resistividad electrica sismica refraccion geophysical characterization for geotechnical purpos along the amazon trunk road ecuador the case of the sucua-logrono section,1.0.0,a1d5189cd251fd1c
0120-3630,01_122503.FINAL.pdf,01_122503.FINAL_0,en,"s dinámicos (Edin, G y μ), correlacionados con módulos estáticos y de deformación","We characterized the geophysical structure of the subsurface at kilometer 17+100 of the Troncal Amazónica road (the Sucúa–Logroño route) in the Morona Santiago province of Ecuador. This was accomplished by integrating seismic methods (refraction, MASW, and ReMi) with electrical resistivity tomography. The results delineate two main units: a shallow surface layer of silty-sandy soil overlying a deeper unit of consolidated silts and weathered rock. The data reveal a notable heterogeneity in the subsurface, with significant variations in both wave velocity and electrical resistivity. We conclude that this structural complexity is a key factor for the engineering of this project. Therefore, the generated geophysical model is a critical predictive tool for optimizing the planning and location of direct geotechnical studies (e.g., boreholes), ensuring a more efficient and cost-effective site characterization",electrical resistivity; geophysical characterization; seismic refraction; surface structure. 1,marcadores,dinamico edin correlacionado con modulo estatico de deformacion,we characteriz geophysical structure subsurface kilometer 17 100 troncal amazonica road sucua-logrono route morona santiago province ecuador accomplish integrat seismic method refraction masw remi electrical resistivity tomography result delineate two main unit shallow surface layer silty-sandy soil overly deeper unit consolidat silt weather rock data reveal notable heterogeneity subsurface significant vari both wave velocity electrical resistivity we conclude structural complexity key factor engineer project therefore generat geophysical model critical predictive tool optimiz plann location direct geotechnical studi borehol ensur more efficient cost-effective site character,electrical resistivity geophysical character seismic refraction surface structure,dinamico edin correlacionado con modulo estatico de deformacion we characteriz geophysical structure subsurface kilometer 17 100 troncal amazonica road sucua-logrono route morona santiago province ecuador accomplish integrat seismic method refraction masw remi electrical resistivity tomography result delineate two main unit shallow surface layer silty-sandy soil overly deeper unit consolidat silt weather rock data reveal notable heterogeneity subsurface significant vari both wave velocity electrical resistivity we conclude structural complexity key factor engineer project therefore generat geophysical model critical predictive tool optimiz plann location direct geotechnical studi borehol ensur more efficient cost-effective site character electrical resistivity geophysical character seismic refraction surface structure,1.0.0,b83686982d555745
0120-3630,02_125006.FINAL.pdf,02_125006.FINAL_0,es,CIENCIAS DE LA TIERRA,"Este estudio aborda una inconsistencia ontológica fundamental en cartografía geomorfológica: la clasificación de estructuras tectónicas (ej., fallas) como formas del relieve, confundiendo entidades genética y dimensionalmente distintas. Mediante un marco metodológico que integra la tríada ProcesoEstructura-Forma, el análisis multiescala y la geometría fractal, se demuestra cuantitativamente esta diferencia ontológica. El análisis del gradiente de cambio dimensional fractal (dD₀/dε) revela que las estructuras (Falla Pinar como caso de estudio) presentan un comportamiento crítico y discontinuo ante el escalado, con un salto dimensional abrupto en la escala crítica donde la zona de daño se vuelve resoluble, mientras que las formas (Cordillera de Guaniguanico) exhiben una convergencia asintótica continua. Los resultados validan cuantitativamente la necesidad de una segregación categórica en los modelos de datos SIG, proponiendo un protocolo para corregir esta dicotomía y fortalecer el rigor conceptual del mapeo del relieve","cartografía geomorfológica; dicotomía estructura-forma; análisis fractal; dimensión de capacidad (D₀); Sistemas de Información Geográfica (SIG); Falla Pinar. The Structure-Form dichotomy in Geomorphology: towards a conceptual and methodological correction in relief mapping using GIS, multiscale analysis and fractal metrics",marcadores,cienci tierra,este estudio aborda inconsistencia ontologica fundamental cartografia geomorfologica clasificacion estructur tectonic ej fall como form relieve confund entidad genetica dimensional distint mediante marco metodologico integra triada procesoestructura-forma analisis multiescala geometria fractal demuestra cuantitativa esta diferencia ontologica analisis gradiente cambio dimensional fractal dd0 revela estructur falla pinar como caso estudio presentan comportamiento critico discontinuo ante escalado salto dimensional abrupto escala critica donde zona dano vuelve resoluble mientr form cordillera guaniguanico exhiben convergencia asintotica continua resultad validan cuantitativa necesidad segregacion categorica model datos sig propon protocolo corregir esta dicotomia fortalecer rigor conceptual mapeo relieve,cartografia geomorfologica dicotomia estructura-forma analisis fractal dimension capacidad d0 sistem informacion geografica sig falla pinar the structure-form dichotomy in geomorphology towards conceptual and methodological correction in relief mapping using gis multiscale analysis and fractal metrics,cienci tierra este estudio aborda inconsistencia ontologica fundamental cartografia geomorfologica clasificacion estructur tectonic ej fall como form relieve confund entidad genetica dimensional distint mediante marco metodologico integra triada procesoestructura-forma analisis multiescala geometria fractal demuestra cuantitativa esta diferencia ontologica analisis gradiente cambio dimensional fractal dd0 revela estructur falla pinar como caso estudio presentan comportamiento critico discontinuo ante escalado salto dimensional abrupto escala critica donde zona dano vuelve resoluble mientr form cordillera guaniguanico exhiben convergencia asintotica continua resultad validan cuantitativa necesidad segregacion categorica model datos sig propon protocolo corregir esta dicotomia fortalecer rigor conceptual mapeo relieve cartografia geomorfologica dicotomia estructura-forma analisis fractal dimension capacidad d0 sistem informacion geografica sig falla pinar the structure-form dichotomy in geomorphology towards conceptual and methodological correction in relief mapping using gis multiscale analysis and fractal metrics,1.0.0,a617cead47086f6c
0120-3630,02_125006.FINAL.pdf,02_125006.FINAL_0,en,que las estructuras (Falla Pinar como caso de estudio) presentan un comportamiento crítico y discontinuo ante,"This study addresses a fundamental ontological inconsistency in geomorphological mapping: the classification of tectonic structures (e.g., faults) as landforms, thus conflating genetically and dimensionally distinct entities. Using a methodological framework that integrates the Process-Structure-Form triad, multiscale analysis, and fractal geometry, this ontological difference is quantitatively demonstrated. Analysis of the fractal dimensional change gradient (dD₀/dε) reveals that structures (Pinar Fault) exhibit critical and discontinuous behavior under scaling, with an abrupt dimensional jump at the critical scale where the damage zone becomes solvable, while landforms (Guaniguanico Range) exhibit continuous asymptotic convergence. The results quantitatively validate the need for categorical segregation in GIS data models, proposing a protocol to correct this dichotomy and strengthen the conceptual rigor of landform mapping",geomorphological mapping; structure-form dichotomy; fractal analysis; capacity dimension (D₀); Geographic Information Systems (GIS); Pinar Fault. 1,marcadores,que las estructura falla pinar como caso de estudio presentan un comportamiento critico discontinuo ante,study address fundamental ontological inconsistency geomorphological mapp classification tectonic structur fault landform thus conflat genetically dimensionally distinct entiti using methodological framework integrat process-structure-form triad multiscale analysi fractal geometry ontological difference quantitatively demonstrat analysi fractal dimensional change gradient dd0 de reveal structur pinar fault exhibit critical discontinuou behavior under scal abrupt dimensional jump critical scale where damage zone becom solvable while landform guaniguanico range exhibit continuou asymptotic convergence result quantitatively validate need categorical segregation gis data model propos protocol correct dichotomy strengthen conceptual rigor landform mapp,geomorphological mapp structure-form dichotomy fractal analysi capacity dimension d0 geographic information system gis pinar fault,que las estructura falla pinar como caso de estudio presentan un comportamiento critico discontinuo ante study address fundamental ontological inconsistency geomorphological mapp classification tectonic structur fault landform thus conflat genetically dimensionally distinct entiti using methodological framework integrat process-structure-form triad multiscale analysi fractal geometry ontological difference quantitatively demonstrat analysi fractal dimensional change gradient dd0 de reveal structur pinar fault exhibit critical discontinuou behavior under scal abrupt dimensional jump critical scale where damage zone becom solvable while landform guaniguanico range exhibit continuou asymptotic convergence result quantitatively validate need categorical segregation gis data model propos protocol correct dichotomy strengthen conceptual rigor landform mapp geomorphological mapp structure-form dichotomy fractal analysi capacity dimension d0 geographic information system gis pinar fault,1.0.0,2e942d8e265b0736
0120-3630,03_1122602.FINAL.pdf,03_1122602.FINAL_0,es,para la determinación del perfil del suelo y los parámetros,"Este estudio presenta la aplicación de los métodos geofísicos indirectos de Tomografía de Refracción Sísmica (TRS), Análisis Multicanal de Ondas Superficiales (MASW, por sus siglas en inglés) y Tomografía de Resistividad Eléctrica (TRE) en dos sectores del municipio de Tocancipá, Cundinamarca, Colombia. El alcance de este trabajo fue la clasificación del tipo de suelo según la velocidad de onda cortante promedio de los 30 primeros metros (VS30) y la obtención de los parámetros dinámicos del suelo como Poisson, peso unitario, Rigidez, Young y Bulk que son útiles en la caracterización geotécnica y como insumo para estudios detallados de Amenaza, Vulnerabilidad y Riesgo. Estos parámetros son calculados a partir de los valores de velocidad sísmica tipo P (VP) y tipo S (VS). La metodología contó con las fases de adquisición, procesamiento e interpretación de 6 secciones de Tomografía de Refracción Sísmica, 6 perfiles de Análisis Multicanal de Ondas Superficiales y 5 secciones de Tomografía de Resistividad Eléctrica. En la zona de estudio se identificó una primera capa de suelo residual arcilloso, seguida por una capa de textura areno-gravosa y, finalmente, un basamento cretácico fracturado correspondiente a la Formación Labor Tierna (K2t). El Vs30 calculado indicó suelos muy densos o rocas blandas (Tipo C según NSR-10). Los parámetros dinámicos mostraron un aumento con la profundidad, sugiriendo mayor grado de compactación y mejora en las propiedades geomecánicas de los materiales. La integración de los métodos sísmicos y geoeléctrico permitió una caracterización detallada del subsuelo, superando las limitaciones intrínsecas de cada técnica por separado","parámetros dinámicos del suelo; refracción sísmica; MASW; resistividad eléctrica; VS30. An application of Seismic Refraction Tomography (SRT), the MASW test and Electrical Resistivity Tomography (ERT) for the determination of the soil profile and dynamic parameters in the urban area of the municipality of Tocancipá, Cundinamarca",marcadores,determinacion perfil suelo parametr,este estudio presenta aplicacion metod geofisic indirect tomografia refraccion sismica trs analisis multicanal ondas superficial masw sus sigl ingl tomografia resistividad electrica tre dos sector municipio tocancipa cundinamarca colombia alcance este trabajo fue clasificacion tipo suelo segun velocidad onda cortante promedio 30 primer metr vs30 obtencion parametr dinamic suelo como poisson peso unitario rigidez young bulk son util caracterizacion geotecnica como insumo estudi detallad amenaza vulnerabilidad riesgo estos parametr son calculad partir valor velocidad sismica tipo vp tipo vs metodologia conto fases adquisicion procesamiento interpretacion seccion tomografia refraccion sismica perfil analisis multicanal ondas superficial seccion tomografia resistividad electrica zona estudio identifico primera capa suelo residual arcilloso seguida capa textura areno-gravosa final basamento cretacico fracturado correspondiente formacion labor tierna k2t vs30 calculado indico suel muy dens rocas bland tipo segun nsr-10 parametr dinamic mostraron aumento profundidad sugir mayor grado compactacion mejora propiedad geomecanic material integracion metod sismic geoelectrico permitio caracterizacion detallada subsuelo super limit intrinsec cada tecnica separado,parametr dinamic suelo refraccion sismica masw resistividad electrica vs30 an application of seismic refraction tomography srt the masw test and electrical resistivity tomography ert for the determination of the soil profile and dynamic parameters in the urban area of the municipality of tocancipa cundinamarca,determinacion perfil suelo parametr este estudio presenta aplicacion metod geofisic indirect tomografia refraccion sismica trs analisis multicanal ondas superficial masw sus sigl ingl tomografia resistividad electrica tre dos sector municipio tocancipa cundinamarca colombia alcance este trabajo fue clasificacion tipo suelo segun velocidad onda cortante promedio 30 primer metr vs30 obtencion parametr dinamic suelo como poisson peso unitario rigidez young bulk son util caracterizacion geotecnica como insumo estudi detallad amenaza vulnerabilidad riesgo estos parametr son calculad partir valor velocidad sismica tipo vp tipo vs metodologia conto fases adquisicion procesamiento interpretacion seccion tomografia refraccion sismica perfil analisis multicanal ondas superficial seccion tomografia resistividad electrica zona estudio identifico primera capa suelo residual arcilloso seguida capa textura areno-gravosa final basamento cretacico fracturado correspondiente formacion labor tierna k2t vs30 calculado indico suel muy dens rocas bland tipo segun nsr-10 parametr dinamic mostraron aumento profundidad sugir mayor grado compactacion mejora propiedad geomecanic material integracion metod sismic geoelectrico permitio caracterizacion detallada subsuelo super limit intrinsec cada tecnica separado parametr dinamic suelo refraccion sismica masw resistividad electrica vs30 an application of seismic refraction tomography srt the masw test and electrical resistivity tomography ert for the determination of the soil profile and dynamic parameters in the urban area of the municipality of tocancipa cundinamarca,1.0.0,d637d3c85198a706
0120-3630,03_1122602.FINAL.pdf,03_1122602.FINAL_0,en,"eno-gravosa y, finalmente, un basamento cretácico fracturado","This study presents the application of indirect geophysical methods, specifically Seismic Refraction Tomography (SRT), Multichannel Analysis of Surface Waves (MASW), and Electrical Resistivity Tomography (ERT), in two sectors of the municipality of Tocancipá, Cundinamarca, Colombia. The scope of this work was to classify the soil type according to the average shear wave velocity of the first 30 meters (VS30) and to obtain dynamic soil parameters such as Poisson's ratio, unit weight, stiffness, Young's ratio, and Bulk’s modulus, How to cite: Arango-Serrano, D.E., Torres-Peña, J.A., Benavides-Fajardo, D.F., Gonzáles-Melo, Y.A., López-Castro, L.M., and Wandurraga-Jiménez, L., (2026). Una aplicación de la Tomografía de Refracción Sísmica (TRS), el ensayo MASW y la Tomografía de Resistividad Eléctrica (TRE) para la determinación del perfil del suelo y los parámetros dinámicos en el casco urbano del municipio de Tocancipá, Cundinamarca. BOLETÍN DE CIENCIAS DE LA TIERRA. 59, pp. 27-46. DOI:https://doi.org/10.15446/rbct.n59.122602 Arango-Serrano et al / BOLETÍN DE CIENCIAS DE LA TIERRA, 59 Enero - Junio, 2026 28 which are useful in geotechnical applications and as input for detailed hazard, vulnerability, and risk studies. These parameters are calculated from the P-type (VP) and S-type (VS) seismic velocity values obtained through Seismic Refraction Tomography and Multichannel Analysis of Surface Waves tests, respectively. The methodology included the acquisition, processing, and interpretation of six Seismic Refraction Tomography sections, six Multichannel Analysis of Surface Waves profiles, and five Electrical Resistivity Tomography sections. In the study area, a first layer of clayey residual soil was identified, followed by a sandy-gravelly layer, and finally, a fractured Cretaceous basement corresponding to the Labor Tierna Formation (K2t). The calculated VS30 indicated very dense soil or soft rocks (Type C according to NSR-10). The dynamic parameters showed an increase with depth, suggesting a greater degree of compaction and an improvement in the geomechanical properties of the materials. The integration of seismic and geoelectric methods allowed for a detailed characterization of the subsoil, overcoming the intrinsic limitations of each technique separately",dynamic soil parameters; seismic refraction; MASW; electrical resistivity; VS30. 1,marcadores,eno-gravosa finalmente un basamento cretacico fracturado,study present application indirect geophysical method specifically seismic refraction tomography srt multichannel analysi surface wave masw electrical resistivity tomography ert two sector municipality tocancipa cundinamarca colombia scope work classify soil type accord average shear wave velocity first 30 meter vs30 obtain dynamic soil parameter such poisson ratio unit weight stiffnes young ratio bulk modulu how cite arango-serrano torres-pena benavides-fajardo gonzales-melo lopez-castro wandurraga-jimenez 2026 una aplicacion de la tomografia de refraccion sismica trs el ensayo masw la tomografia de resistividad electrica tre para la determinacion del perfil del suelo los parametro dinamico en el casco urbano del municipio de tocancipa cundinamarca boletin de ciencia de la tierra 59 pp 27-46 doi http doi org 10 15446 rbct n59 122602 arango-serrano et al boletin de ciencia de la tierra 59 enero junio 2026 28 which useful geotechnical applic input detail hazard vulnerability risk studi these parameter calculat p-type vp s-type vs seismic velocity valu obtain through seismic refraction tomography multichannel analysi surface wave test respectively methodology includ acquisition process interpretation six seismic refraction tomography section six multichannel analysi surface wave profil five electrical resistivity tomography section study area first layer clayey residual soil identifi follow sandy-gravelly layer 