0120-3800,Articulo+3+(2025).pdf,Articulo+3+(2025)_0,desconocido,Articulo 3 (2025),"Revista Interamericana de Psicología Ocupacional 2025 Vol. 40 37 Artículo de Reflexión Bridging the Gap between the Brain and Behavior in Organizations: Perspectives from Organizational Neuroscience and Industrial and Organizational Psychology Carlos A. Andujar Rojas University of Puerto Rico at Arecibo Correspondence: carlos.andujar@upr.edu Recibido: 4-VI-2024 Aceptado: 14-IX-2024 Keywords: Brain, Behavior, Organizational Neuroscience, Industrial/ Organizational Psychology, Behavior in Organizations, This article explores the contributions of organizational neuroscience (ON) to industrial-organizational psychology (IOP) through a literature review of books, professional articles, and peer-reviewed journals from the past decade. The study aims to evaluate the relationship between ON and IOP, highlighting advances, synergies, and multidisciplinary applications. Key areas examined include job analysis, personnel selection, training, leadership, teamwork, coaching, and neuroethics, based on the quantity, quality, and relevance of the literature. Findings reveal that ON has gradually contributed to these areas, yet IOP research shows limited interest in studying brain mechanisms and their influence on workplace behavior. Resistance to incorporating ON knowledge and tools persists, suggesting a need for enhanced training to help I/O psychologists recognize neuroscience's potential. The article calls for exploring ON’s applications in emerging fields like neuroeconomics, neuromarke",,respaldo_sin_marcadores,articulo 2025,revista interamericana psicologia ocupacional 2025 vol 40 37 articulo reflexion bridg gap between brain behavior organiz perspectiv organizational neuroscience industrial organizational psychology carl andujar roja university puerto rico arecibo correspondence carl andujar upr edu recibido 4-vi-2024 aceptado 14-ix-2024 keyword brain behavior organizational neuroscience industrial organizational psychology behavior organiz article explor contribution organizational neuroscience industrial-organizational psychology iop through literature review book professional articl peer-review journal past decade study aims evaluate relationship between iop highlight advanc synergi multidisciplinary applic key area examin include job analysi personnel selection train leadership teamwork coach neuroethic based quantity quality relevance literature finding reveal has gradually contribut these area yet iop research show limit interest study brain mechanism their influence workplace behavior resistance incorporat knowledge tool persist suggest need enhanc train help psychologist recognize neuroscience potential article call explor applic emerg field like neuroeconomic neuromarke,,articulo 2025 revista interamericana psicologia ocupacional 2025 vol 40 37 articulo reflexion bridg gap between brain behavior organiz perspectiv organizational neuroscience industrial organizational psychology carl andujar roja university puerto rico arecibo correspondence carl andujar upr edu recibido 4-vi-2024 aceptado 14-ix-2024 keyword brain behavior organizational neuroscience industrial organizational psychology behavior organiz article explor contribution organizational neuroscience industrial-organizational psychology iop through literature review book professional articl peer-review journal past decade study aims evaluate relationship between iop highlight advanc synergi multidisciplinary applic key area examin include job analysi personnel selection train leadership teamwork coach neuroethic based quantity quality relevance literature finding reveal has gradually contribut these area yet iop research show limit interest study brain mechanism their influence workplace behavior resistance incorporat knowledge tool persist suggest need enhanc train help psychologist recognize neuroscience potential article call explor applic emerg field like neuroeconomic neuromarke,1.0