0120-3800,Articulo+9+Humor.pdf,Articulo+9+Humor_0,en,Psychometric Validation and Adaptation of the Humor Climate,"Recibido: 23-VI-2025 Aceptado: 21-VII-2025 Humor plays a vital role in workplace dynamics, influencing employee satisfaction, team cohesion, stress reduction, and creativity. This study aimed to validate the Humor Climate Questionnaire (HCQ) within a diverse organizational context, examining its applicability and reliability across various employment types, sectors, and demographic variables. A total of 300 participants from different sectors— including education, healthcare, finance, and food services—completed the HCQ and the Workplace Boredom Scale (WBS). Exploratory and confirmatory factor analyses supported the HCQ's four-factor structure: Positive Humor, Negative Humor, Outgroup Humor, and Supervisor Support, with moderate to high internal consistency. A bifactor model demonstrated better fit but revealed limited support for a global humor climate score, reinforcing the multidimensional nature of the instrument. Descriptive comparisons indicated variability in humor climate perceptions across employment status, job type, generation, and sector. Positive Humor was associated with higher job satisfaction and team cohesion, while Negative Humor correlated with increased workplace boredom and potential interpersonal tension. Outgroup Humor, while sometimes fostering bonding, often reflected dissatisfaction with organizational policies. Supervisor Support emerged as a protective factor in reducing boredom. These findings highlight the dual nature of humor in the workplace and underscore the importance of fostering positive humor climates to enhance well-being, communication, and productivity. This study offers practical implications for organizations seeking to harness humor strategically and calls for future research to refine the HCQ, assess measurement invariance, and explore humor’s evolving role in organizational life","Humor Climate, Workplace Dynamics, HCQ, Internal Structure, Validity, Reliability, Organizational Behavior Validación psicométrica y adaptación del Humor Climate Questionnaire (HCQ) en contextos organizacionales",marcadores,psychometric validation adaptation humor climate,recibido 23-vi-2025 aceptado 21-vii-2025 humor play vital role workplace dynamic influenc employee satisfaction team cohesion stres reduction creativity study aimed validate humor climate questionnaire hcq within diverse organizational context examin its applicability reliability acros variou employment type sector demographic variabl total 300 participant different sectors-- includ education healthcare finance food services--complet hcq workplace boredom scale wbs exploratory confirmatory factor analys support hcq four-factor structure positive humor negative humor outgroup humor supervisor support moderate high internal consistency bifactor model demonstrat better fit but reveal limit support global humor climate score reinforc multidimensional nature instrument descriptive comparison indicat variability humor climate perception acros employment statu job type generation sector positive humor associat higher job satisfaction team cohesion while negative humor correlat increas workplace boredom potential interpersonal tension outgroup humor while sometim foster bond often reflect dissatisfaction organizational polici supervisor support emerg protective factor reduc boredom these finding highlight dual nature humor workplace underscore importance foster positive humor climat enhance well-be communication productivity study offer practical implic organiz seek harnes humor strategically call future research refine hcq asses measurement invariance explore humor evolv role organizational life,humor climate workplace dynamic hcq internal structure validity reliability organizational behavior validacion psicometrica adaptacion del humor climate questionnaire hcq en contexto organizacional,psychometric validation adaptation humor cl