0120-3886,Derecho-v55n143-art02-pago-incapacidad-medico-laboral-origen-comun-colombia.pdf,Derecho-v55n143-art02-pago-incapacidad-medico-laboral-origen-comun-colombia_0,en,ablece responsables del,"In the case of workers who contribute to the General System of Social Security in Health, a medical disability leads to the recognition of an economic benefit that allows their livelihood during the period of recovery of the state of health. Colombian regulations establish that disabilities can be of common origin and labor origin. The payment of medical-labor disabilities of common origin in Colombia is an issue that, despite the regulatory progress, still continues to generate controversies regarding the process for payment by the administrators of the General System of Integral Social Security and to this extent the tutelage action continues to be resorted to by the affiliates. In other words, the current normative regulation in Colombia establishes who is responsible for the payment of disabilities, but gaps persist in terms of the procedures to obtain the effective recognition of the benefits, since the differences in the procedures of each entity and their interpretation of regulations, generate delays in the process for workers. This article highlights the relevance of the topic by highlighting the difficulties faced by Colombian workers when requesting the recognition and payment of disabilities. Likewise, a review is carried out on problematic aspects such as the favorable concept of rehabilitation, 3 Sebastián Orozco Rodríguez, Luz Andrea Quintero Salgado, Natalia Eugenia Gómez Rúa Revista de la Facultad de Derecho y Ciencias Políticas ISSN: 2390-0016 (En línea) / Vol 55, Núm. 143 (2025) / Medellín, Colombia the qualification of timely loss of work capacity and the right to disabilities and situations that consider abuse of the right by members","Disability, Health, Illness, Insurer, Social Security, Worker, Employer, Right to Health, Right to work, Economic benefits. 4 Sebastián Orozco Rodríguez, Luz Andrea Quintero Salgado, Natalia Eugenia Gómez Rúa Revista de la Facultad de Derecho y Ciencias Políticas ISSN: 2390-0016 (En línea) / Vol 55, Núm. 143 (2025) / Medellín, Colombia",marcadores,ablece responsabl del,case worker who contribute general system social security health medical disability lead recognition economic benefit allow their livelihood during period recovery state health colombian regul establish disabiliti can common origin labor origin payment medical-labor disabiliti common origin colombia issue despite regulatory progres still continu generate controversi regard proces payment administrator general system integral social security extent tutelage action continu resort affiliat other word current normative regulation colombia establish who responsible payment disabiliti but gaps persist term procedur obtain effective recognition benefit since differenc procedur each entity their interpretation regul generate delay proces worker article highlight relevance topic highlight difficulti faced colombian worker when request recognition payment disabiliti likewise review carri out problematic aspect such favorable concept rehabilitation sebastian orozco rodriguez luz andrea quintero salgado natalia eugenia gomez rua revista de la facultad de derecho ciencia politica issn 2390-0016 en linea vol 55 num 143 2025 medellin colombia qualification timely loss work capacity right disabiliti situ consider abuse right member,disability health illnes insurer social security worker employer right health right work economic benefit sebastian orozco rodriguez luz andrea quintero salgado natalia eugenia gomez rua revista de la facultad de derecho ciencia politica issn 2390-0016 en linea vol 55 num 143 2025 medellin colombia,ablece responsabl del case worker who contribute general system social security health medical disability lead recognition economic benefit allow their livelihood during period recovery state health colombian re