0120-4211,2936+BISTUA+2025+No1.pdf,2936+BISTUA+2025+No1_0,es,© Autores; Licencia Universidad de Pamplona,"El estudio comparó la eficiencia productiva de la tilapia roja criada en estanques de geomembrana con tecnología biofloc y raceways. Se analizaron los parámetros fisicoquímicos clave en ambos sistemas, destacando correlaciones entre variables y su impacto en la calidad del agua y el rendimiento de los peces. En biofloc, se encontró una correlación positiva moderada entre oxígeno disuelto, pH y temperatura, resaltando la importancia de mantener niveles óptimos de oxígeno. En raceways, se halló una fuerte correlación positiva entre oxígeno disuelto y pH, subrayando la influencia del pH en la disponibilidad de oxígeno. No se encontraron diferencias significativas en tasas de alimentación, conversión alimenticia, mortalidad y supervivencia entre los sistemas, indicando su igual eficacia productiva y control de la mortalidad. Estos hallazgos respaldan que tanto biofloc como raceways son opciones viables para el cultivo de tilapia, con resultados comparables en calidad del agua, rendimiento de los peces y eficiencia económica. Este estudio puede orientar a productores acuícolas en la elección del sistema de cultivo más adecuado según sus necesidades y condiciones específicas",Acuicultura; Tilapia; Biofloc; Raceways,marcadores,autor licencia universidad pamplona,estudio comparo eficiencia productiva tilapia roja criada estanqu geomembrana tecnologia biofloc raceways analizaron parametr fisicoquimic clave ambos sistem destac correl entre variabl impacto calidad agua rendimiento peces biofloc encontro correlacion positiva moderada entre oxigeno disuelto ph temperatura resalt importancia mantener nivel optim oxigeno raceways hallo fuerte correlacion positiva entre oxigeno disuelto ph subray influencia ph disponibilidad oxigeno no encontraron diferenci significativ tasas alimentacion conversion alimenticia mortalidad supervivencia entre sistem indic igual eficacia productiva control mortalidad estos hallazg respaldan tanto biofloc como raceways son opcion viabl cultivo tilapia resultad comparabl calidad agua rendimiento peces eficiencia economica este estudio puede orientar productor acuicol eleccion sistema cultivo mas adecuado segun sus necesidad condicion especific,acuicultura tilapia biofloc raceways,autor licencia universidad pamplona estudio comparo eficiencia productiva tilapia roja criada estanqu geomembrana tecnologia biofloc raceways analizaron parametr fisicoquimic clave ambos sistem destac correl entre variabl impacto calidad agua rendimiento peces biofloc encontro correlacion positiva moderada entre oxigeno disuelto ph temperatura resalt importancia mantener nivel optim oxigeno raceways hallo fuerte correlacion positiva entre oxigeno disuelto ph subray influencia ph disponibilidad oxigeno no encontraron diferenci significativ tasas alimentacion conversion alimenticia mortalidad supervivencia entre sistem indic igual eficacia productiva control mortalidad estos hallazg respaldan tanto biofloc como raceways son opcion viabl cultivo tilapia resultad comparabl calidad agua rendimiento peces eficiencia economica este estudio puede orientar productor acuicol eleccion sistema cultivo mas adecuado segun sus necesidad condicion especific acuicultura tilapia biofloc raceways,1.0.0,99f1673d46643ac3
0120-4211,2936+BISTUA+2025+No1.pdf,2936+BISTUA+2025+No1_0,en,da entre oxígeno,"The study compared the productive efficiency of red tilapia raised in geomembrane ponds with biofloc and raceways technology. Key physicochemical parameters in both systems were analyzed, highlighting correlations between variables and their impact on water quality and fish performance. In biofloc, a moderate positive correlation was found between dissolved oxygen, pH and temperature, highlighting the importance of maintaining optimal oxygen levels. In raceways, a strong positive correlation was found between dissolved oxygen and pH, underlining the influence of pH on oxygen availability. No significant differences were found in feeding rates, feed conversion, mortality, and survival between the systems, indicating their equal productive efficiency and mortality control. These findings support that both biofloc and raceways are viable options for tilapia culture, with comparable results in water quality, fish performance and economic efficiency. This study can guide aquaculture producers in choosing the most appropriate culture system according to their specific needs and conditions",Aquaculture; Tilapia; Biofloc; Raceways. 1,marcadores,da entre oxigeno,study compar productive efficiency red tilapia rais geomembrane pond biofloc raceway technology key physicochemical parameter both system analyz highlight correl between variabl their impact water quality fish performance biofloc moderate positive correlation found between dissolv oxygen ph temperature highlight importance maintain optimal oxygen level raceway strong positive correlation found between dissolv oxygen ph underlin influence ph oxygen availability no significant differenc found feed rate feed conversion mortality survival between system indicat their equal productive efficiency mortality control these finding support both biofloc raceway viable option tilapia culture comparable result water quality fish performance economic efficiency study can guide aquaculture producer choos most appropriate culture system accord their specific need condition,aquaculture tilapia biofloc raceway,da entre oxigeno study compar productive efficiency red tilapia rais geomembrane pond biofloc raceway technology key physicochemical parameter both system analyz highlight correl between variabl their impact water quality fish performance biofloc moderate positive correlation found between dissolv oxygen ph temperature highlight importance maintain optimal oxygen level raceway strong positive correlation found between dissolv oxygen ph underlin influence ph oxygen availability no significant differenc found feed rate feed conversion mortality survival between system indicat their equal productive efficiency mortality control these finding support both biofloc raceway viable option tilapia culture comparable result water quality fish performance economic efficiency study can guide aquaculture producer choos most appropriate culture system accord their specific need condition aquaculture tilapia biofloc raceway,1.0.0,84002c3f2f22fb7a
0120-4211,3497+BISTUA+v23i1+2025.pdf,3497+BISTUA+v23i1+2025_0,en,© Athors; License Universidad de Pamplona,"This study presents a descriptive mineralogical and textural analysis of sedimentary rocks located at the top of Paleogene formations in the Middle Magdalena Valley Basin, specifically within the La Paz, Esmeralda, Colorado, and Mugrosa formations. These units exhibit clearly distinguishable sedimentary structures, depositional environments, and mineral compositions. Advanced techniques such as X-ray computed tomography (CT), petrography, X-ray diffraction (XRD), and scanning electron microscopy (SEM) were used to thoroughly characterize the sedimentological, mineralogical, and porosity properties of the samples. X-ray CT enabled the identification of sedimentary and biogenic structures, as well as syn-sedimentary deformations, and provided density and effective atomic number values that are useful for facies differentiation. Petrographic analysis revealed sandstones with variable grain sizes, typical of fluvial environments, showing significant variations in grain size, a wide range of cementing materials, and well-developed secondary porosity that enhances reservoir permeability. XRD identified quartz, feldspars, and clay minerals as the main components, while SEM highlighted the distribution of clay minerals within the pores. The observed lithologies include polymictic conglomerates, shales, sandy shales, sublithic sandstones, and lithic sandstones, associated with fluvial channels, floodplains, and meandering river systems. Computed tomography is consolidated as a key nondestructive tool in sedimentological interpretation, offering highresolution imaging and valuable data on density, mineralogy, lithology, porosity, and facies. This multidisciplinary approach provides essential information for reservoir characterization, the reconstruction of depositional environments, and the understanding of geological history, contributing to the advancement of geological research and resource exploration in the Middle Magdalena Valley Basin",clay minerals; petrophysical properties; reservoirs; sedimentary sequences; Colombia,marcadores,athor license universidad de pamplona,study present descriptive mineralogical textural analysi sedimentary rock locat top paleogene form middle magdalena valley basin specifically within la paz esmeralda colorado mugrosa form these unit exhibit clearly distinguishable sedimentary structur depositional environment mineral composition advanc techniqu such x-ray comput tomography ct petrography x-ray diffraction xrd scann electron microscopy sem used thoroughly characterize sedimentological mineralogical porosity properti sampl x-ray ct enabl identification sedimentary biogenic structur well syn-sedimentary deform provid density effective atomic number valu useful faci differentiation petrographic analysi reveal sandston variable grain size typical fluvial environment show significant vari grain size wide range cement material well-develop secondary porosity enhanc reservoir permeability xrd identifi quartz feldspar clay mineral main component while sem highlight distribution clay mineral within pore observ lithologi include polymictic conglomerat shal sandy shal sublithic sandston lithic sandston associat fluvial channel floodplain meander river system comput tomography consolidat key nondestructive tool sedimentological interpretation offer highresolution imag valuable data density mineralogy lithology porosity faci multidisciplinary approach provid essential information reservoir character reconstruction depositional environment understand geological history contribut advancement geological research resource exploration middle magdalena valley basin,clay mineral petrophysical properti reservoir sedimentary sequenc colombia,athor license universidad de pamplona study present descriptive mineralogical textural analysi sedimentary rock locat top paleogene form middle magdalena valley basin specifically within la paz esmeralda colorado mugrosa form these unit exhibit clearly distinguishable sedimentary structur depositional environment mineral composition advanc techniqu such x-ray comput tomography ct petrography x-ray diffraction xrd scann electron microscopy sem used thoroughly characterize sedimentological mineralogical porosity properti sampl x-ray ct enabl identification sedimentary biogenic structur well syn-sedimentary deform provid density effective atomic number valu useful faci differentiation petrographic analysi reveal sandston variable grain size typical fluvial environment show significant vari grain size wide range cement material well-develop secondary porosity enhanc reservoir permeability xrd identifi quartz feldspar clay mineral main component while sem highlight distribution clay mineral within pore observ lithologi include polymictic conglomerat shal sandy shal sublithic sandston lithic sandston associat fluvial channel floodplain meander river system comput tomography consolidat key nondestructive tool sedimentological interpretation offer highresolution imag valuable data density mineralogy lithology porosity faci multidisciplinary approach provid essential information reservoir character reconstruction depositional environment understand geological history contribut advancement geological research resource exploration middle magdalena valley basin clay mineral petrophysical properti reservoir sedimentary sequenc colombia,1.0.0,b2cfd54109523dc2
0120-4211,3497+BISTUA+v23i1+2025.pdf,3497+BISTUA+v23i1+2025_0,es,highlighted the distribution of clay minerals within the pores.,"Este estudio realiza un análisis descriptivo mineralógico y textural de las rocas sedimentarias ubicadas en los topes formacionales del Paleógeno en la cuenca del Valle Medio del Magdalena, específicamente en las formaciones La Paz, Esmeralda, Colorado y Mugrosa. Estas unidades muestran estructuras sedimentarias, ambientes de depósito y composiciones minerales claramente diferenciables. Se utilizaron técnicas avanzadas como tomografía computarizada (TC) por rayos X, petrografía, difracción de rayos X (DRX) y microscopía electrónica de barrido (MEB) para caracterizar detalladamente las propiedades sedimentológicas, mineralógicas y de porosidad de las muestras. La TC por rayos X permitió identificar estructuras sedimentarias, biogénicas y deformaciones sin-sedimentarias, además de proporcionar valores de densidad y número atómico efectivo útiles en la diferenciación de facies. El análisis petrográfico mostró areniscas con granulometría variable, típicas de ambientes fluviales, con importantes variaciones en el tamaño de grano, diversidad de cementos y desarrollo de porosidad secundaria, lo cual mejora la permeabilidad del reservorio. La DRX identificó cuarzo, feldespatos y minerales arcillosos como componentes principales, mientras que la MEB evidenció la distribución de minerales arcillosos en los poros. Las litologías observadas incluyen conglomerados polimícticos, lutitas, lutitas arenosas, sublitosandstones y litosandstones, asociadas a canales fluviales, llanuras de inundación y ríos meandriformes. La tomografía computarizada se consolida como una herramienta no destructiva clave en la interpretación sedimentológica, al ofrecer imágenes de alta resolución y datos sobre densidad, mineralogía, litología, porosidad y facies. Este enfoque multidisciplinario aporta información esencial para la caracterización de yacimientos, la reconstrucción de ambientes deposicionales y la comprensión de la historia geológica, contribuyendo al avance en la investigación geológica y la exploración de recursos en la cuenca del Valle Medio del Magdalena","minerales arcillosos; propiedades petrofísicas; reservorios; secuencias sedimentarias; Colombia. BISTUA Rev. FCB, Vol. 23 (1), (2025) 2 1",marcadores,highlighted the distribution of clay minerals within the pores,este estudio realiza analisis descriptivo mineralogico textural rocas sedimentari ubicad topes formacional paleogeno cuenca valle medio magdalena especifica form paz esmeralda colorado mugrosa estas unidad muestran estructur sedimentari ambient deposito composicion mineral clara diferenciabl utilizaron tecnic avanzad como tomografia computarizada tc rayos petrografia difraccion rayos drx microscopia electronica barrido meb caracterizar detallada propiedad sedimentologic mineralogic porosidad muestr tc rayos permitio identificar estructur sedimentari biogenic deform sin-sedimentari adem proporcionar valor densidad numero atomico efectivo util diferenciacion faci analisis petrografico mostro arenisc granulometria variable tipic ambient fluvial important vari tamano grano diversidad cement desarrollo porosidad secundaria cual mejora permeabilidad reservorio drx identifico cuarzo feldespat mineral arcillos como component principal mientr meb evidencio distribucion mineral arcillos poros litologi observad incluyen conglomerad polimictic lutit lutit arenos sublitosandston litosandston asociad canal fluvial llanur inundacion rios meandriform tomografia computarizada consolida como herramienta no destructiva clave interpretacion sedimentologica ofrecer imagen alta resolucion datos sobre densidad mineralogia litologia porosidad faci este enfoque multidisciplinario aporta informacion esencial caracterizacion yacimient reconstruccion ambient deposicional comprension historia geologica contribuyendo avance investigacion geologica exploracion recurs cuenca valle medio mag