0120-4211,3588+BISTUA+23i1+2025.pdf,3588+BISTUA+23i1+2025_0,en,reactores como biodisco,"This study evaluates the effectiveness of DIFAFS (two-stage) and TRI-FAFS (three-stage) systems for treating landfill leachate (LFL), comparing them with reactors such as rotating biological contactor (RBC), trickling filter (TF), and UASB. The results showed that TRI-FAFS achieved the highest COD removal efficiency (85%-95%), followed by DI-FAFS (70%-85%), due to its staged configuration, which enhances the degradation of recalcitrant compounds and reduces metabolic inhibition. COD loads ranged from 12–25 g/m²-day (RBC) to 18.65 kg/m³-day (UASB), under controlled pH (8–9) and temperature (18–34 °C) conditions. The developed kinetic models accurately described substrate degradation and methane production, highlighting the influence of temperature on microbial activity and the stable generation of biomass (100–102 CFU/mL/h) and methane (10⁻² mg/d per mg/L/h). Microbial characterization in TRI-FAFS revealed a functional stage-wise distribution: hydrolytic and acidogenic bacteria in the first stage, acidogenic and acetogenic bacteria BISTUA, Vol.23 (1), (2025) 2 primera, acidogénicas y acetogénicas en la segunda, y metanogénicas en la tercera. Esta progresión mejoró la solubilización de contaminantes y la estabilidad del sistema. En conclusión, los sistemas multietapa (DI-FAFS y TRI-FAFS) son alternativas viables y sostenibles para LRS complejos, superando a reactores convencionales. Su diseño favorece la adaptación microbiana, maximiza la biodegradación y ofrece un marco para optimizar reactores anaeróbicos mediante modelos cinéticos. Este trabajo resalta el potencial de la tecnología escalonada en el tratamiento de lixiviados, combinando eficiencia operativa y sostenibilidad ambiental. Palabras clave: Lixiviados; Reactores anaeróbicos; Microorganismos; Degradación de materia orgánica; Producción de metano. in the second, and methanogens in the third. This progression improved contaminant solubilization and system stability. In conclusion, multistage systems (DI-FAFS and TRI-FAFS) are viable and sustainable alternatives for complex LFL, outperforming conventional reactors. Their design promotes microbial adaptation, maximizes biodegradation, and provides a framework for optimizing anaerobic reactors through kinetic modeling. This work underscores the potential of staged technology in leachate treatment, combining operational efficiency and environmental sustainability",Leachates; Anaerobic reactors; Microorganisms; Degradation of organic matter; Methane production. 1,marcadores,reactor como biodisco,study evaluat effectivenes difaf two-stage tri-faf three-stage system treat landfill leachate lfl compar them reactor such rotat biological contactor rbc trickl filter tf uasb result show tri-faf achiev highest cod removal efficiency 85 -95 follow di-faf 70 -85 due its stag configuration which enhanc degradation recalcitrant compound reduc metabolic inhibition cod load rang 12-25 m2-day rbc 18 65 kg m3-day uasb under controll ph 8-9 temperature 18-34 degc condition develop kinetic model accurately describ substrate degradation methane production highlight influence temperature microbial activity stable generation biomas 100-102 cfu ml methane 10-2 mg per mg microbial character tri-faf reveal functional stage-wise distribution hydrolytic acidogenic bacteria first stage acidogenic acetogenic bacteria bistua vol 23 2025 primera acidogenica acetogenica en la segunda metanogenica en la tercera esta progresion mejoro la solubilizacion de contaminant la estabilidad del sistema en conclusion los sistema multietapa di-faf tri-faf son alternativa viabl sostenibl para lrs complejo superando reactor convencional su diseno favorece la adaptacion microbiana maximiza la biodegradacion ofrece un marco para optimizar reactor anaerobico mediante modelo cinetico este trabajo resalta el potencial de la tecnologia escalonada en el tratamiento de lixiviado combinando e