0120-4319,UO2025v44n06_Morales_etal(Eng+listo).pdf,UO2025v44n06_Morales_etal(Eng+listo)_0,en,são sistemática,"Background: Cocaine abuse produces severe oral and maxillofacial damage, yet these manifestations are often underrecognized in clinical practice. Purpose: To analyze and synthesize current evidence on the oral and maxillofacial abnormalities associated with cocaine use. Methods: This systematic review was conducted following the Preferred Reporting Items for Systematic Reviews and Meta-Analyses (PRISMA) guidelines. The protocol was registered in the International Prospective Register of Systematic Reviews (CRD42024583820). A comprehensive search of articles published from 2019 to 2024 was performed in the following databases: EBSCOhost, ScienceDirect, PubMed, LiLACS, and SciELO. Extracted data included: origin and terminology of cocaine, pharmacology, general symptomatology, oral and maxillofacial effects, medical–dental management, and dental management. Results: A total of 10,529 records were identified, of which 17 studies met the inclusion criteria. More than 80% of the selected articles were written in English. Several uncommon oral and maxillofacial complications were identified, such as retinal artery branch occlusion and cervicocephalic arterial dissection. Conclusions: The evidence indicates that cocaine use is associated with a wide spectrum of oral and maxillofacial manifestations, including rare vascular complications. Continued research is needed to deepen the understanding of these alterations and to explore potential adjunctive therapies in this population",cocaine; dental pharmacology; dentistry; disease attributes; maxillofacial abnormalities; oral abnormalities; oral health; toxicology,marcadores,sao sistematica,background cocaine abuse produc severe oral maxillofacial damage yet these manifest often underrecogniz clinical practice purpose analyze synthesize current evidence oral maxillofacial abnormaliti associat cocaine use method systematic review conduct follow preferr report item systematic review meta-analys prisma guidelin protocol register international prospective register systematic review crd42024583820 comprehensive search articl publish 2019 2024 perform follow databas ebscohost sciencedirect pubm lilac scielo extract data includ origin terminology cocaine pharmacology general symptomatology oral maxillofacial effect medical-dental management dental management result total 10 529 record identifi which 17 studi met inclusion criteria more than 80 select articl written english several uncommon oral maxillofacial complic identifi such retinal artery branch occlusion cervicocephalic arterial dissection conclusion evidence indicat cocaine use associat wide spectrum oral maxillofacial manifest includ rare vascular complic continu research need deepen understand these alter explore potential adjunctive therapi population,cocaine dental pharmacology dentistry disease attribut maxillofacial abnormaliti oral abnormaliti oral health toxicology,sao sistematica background cocaine abuse produc severe oral maxillofacial damage yet these manifest often underrecogniz clinical practice purpose analyze synthesize current evidence oral maxillofacial abnormaliti associat cocaine use method systematic review conduct follow preferr report item systematic review meta-analys prisma guidelin protocol register international prospective register systematic review crd42024583820 comprehensive search articl publish 2019 2024 perform follow databas ebscohost sciencedirect pubm lilac scielo extract data includ origin terminology cocaine pharmacology general symptomatology oral maxillofacial effect medical-dental management dental management result total 10 529 record identifi which 17 studi met inclusion criteria more than 80 select articl written english several uncommon oral maxillofacial complic identifi such retinal artery branch occlusion cervicocephalic arterial dissection conclusion evidence indicat cocaine use associat wide spectrum oral maxillofacial manifest includ rare vascular complic continu research need deepen understand these alter explore potential adjunctive therapi population cocaine dental pharmacology dentistry disease attribut maxillofacial abnormaliti oral abnormaliti oral health toxicology,1.0.0,1c9966ed06f40f97
0120-4319,UO2025v44n06_Morales_etal(Eng+listo).pdf,UO2025v44n06_Morales_etal(Eng+listo)_0,es,"macology, general symptomatology, oral and maxillofacial","Antecedentes: El consumo de cocaína produce daños orales y maxilofaciales graves; sin embargo, estas manifestaciones a menudo no se reconocen adecuadamente en la práctica clínica. Objetivo: Analizar y sintetizar la evidencia actual sobre las anomalías orales y maxilofaciales asociadas al consumo de cocaína. Métodos: Esta revisión sistemática se realizó siguiendo las directrices PRISMA (Preferred Reporting Items for Systematic Reviews and Meta-Analyses). El protocolo se inscribió en el Registro Internacional Prospectivo de Revisiones Sistemáticas (CRD42024583820). Se realizó una búsqueda exhaustiva de artículos publicados entre 2019 y 2024 en las siguientes bases de datos: EBSCOhost, ScienceDirect, PubMed, LiLACS y SciELO. Los datos extraídos incluyeron: origen y terminología de la cocaína, farmacología, sintomatología general, efectos orales y maxilofaciales, manejo médico-dental y manejo odontológico. Resultados: Se identificó un total de 10.529 registros, de los cuales 17 estudios cumplieron con los criterios de inclusión. Más del 80% de los artículos seleccionados estaban escritos en inglés. Se identificaron varias complicaciones orales y maxilofaciales poco comunes, como la oclusión de la rama de la arteria retiniana y la disección arterial cervicocefálica. Conclusiones: La evidencia indica que el consumo de cocaína se asocia con un amplio espectro de manifestaciones orales y maxilofaciales, incluidas complicaciones vasculares raras. Se necesita investigación continua para profundizar en la comprensión de estas alteraciones y explorar posibles terapias complementarias en esta población",anomalías maxilofaciales; anomalías orales; características de la enfermedad; cocaína; farmacología dental; odontología; salud bucal; toxicología,marcadores,macology general symptomatology oral and maxillofacial,antecedent consumo cocaina produce danos oral maxilofacial grav sin embargo estas manifest menudo no reconocen adecuada practica clinica objetivo analizar sintetizar evidencia actual sobre anomali oral maxilofacial asociad consumo cocaina metod esta revision sistematica realizo sigu directric prisma preferred reporting items for systematic reviews and meta-analys protocolo inscribio registro internacional prospectivo revision sistematic crd42024583820 realizo busqueda exhaustiva articul publicad entre 2019 2024 siguient bases datos ebscohost sciencedirect pubmed lilacs scielo datos extraid incluyeron origen terminologia cocaina farmacologia sintomatologia general efect oral maxilofacial manejo medico-dental manejo odontologico resultad identifico total 10 529 registr cual 17 estudi cumplieron criteri inclusion mas 80 articul seleccionad estaban escrit ingl identificaron vari complic oral maxilofacial poco comun como oclusion rama arteria retiniana diseccion arterial cervicocefalica conclusion evidencia indica consumo cocaina asocia amplio espectro manifest oral maxilofacial incluid complic vascular raras necesita investigacion continua profundizar comprension estas alter explorar posibl terapi complementari esta poblacion,anomali maxilofacial anomali oral caracteristic enfermedad cocaina farmacologia dental odontologia salud bucal toxicologia,macology general symptomatology oral and maxillofacial antecedent consumo cocaina produce danos oral maxilofacial grav sin embargo estas manifest menudo no reconocen adecuada practica clinica objetivo analizar sintetizar evidencia actual sobre anomali oral maxilofacial asociad consumo cocaina metod esta revision sistematica realizo sigu directric prisma preferred reporting items for systematic reviews and meta-analys protocolo inscribio registro internacional prospectivo revision sistematic crd42024583820 realizo busqueda exhaustiva articul publicad entre 2019 2024 siguient bases datos ebscohost sciencedirect pubmed lilacs scielo datos extraid 