0120-4319,UO2025v44n07_Giraldo_etal(Eng+listo).pdf,UO2025v44n07_Giraldo_etal(Eng+listo)_0,en,Edgar Enrique García-Hurtado a,"Background: The use of bovine dentin in dental research has gained relevance due to its easy availability, lower structural and compositional variability, and morphological similarity to human dentin. Purpose: To compare the elastic modulus of human and bovine dentin at the dentinoenamel junction and the dentin-pulp junction. Methods: An in vitro experimental study was conducted on 30 recently extracted human molars (20–30 years old) and 30 bovine incisors (2–3 years old). The teeth were preserved in 2% chloramine T to maintain moisture. Thirty dentin bars were obtained: 15 from the dentinoenamel junction and 15 from the dentin-pulp junction. Each bar measured 2 mm wide by 1.5 mm thick. The specimens were observed under a stereomicroscope and measured with a digital caliper. The data were entered into the three-point bending test program (Instron® universal testing machine) to calculate the elastic modulus. The test was performed using two instruments designed for the setup: a sample holder and a load application pin (p = 0.05). Results: In human dentin, the elastic modulus was 8.89 GPa at the dentinoenamel junction and 6.7064 GPa at the dentin-pulp junction. In bovine dentin, it was 9.0078 GPa at the dentinoenamel junction and 6.0388 GPa at the dentin-pulp junction. Conclusions: The elastic modulus values in human and bovine dentin, both at the dentinoenamel junction and the dentin-pulp junction, do not suggest significant differences",biophysics; bovine dentin; dental biology; dentin biomechanics; dentinoenamel junction; dentin-pulp junction; dentistry; elastic modulus; experimental research; human dentin,marcadores,edgar enrique garcia-hurtado,background use bovine dentin dental research has gain relevance due its easy availability lower structural compositional variability morphological similarity human dentin purpose compare elastic modulu human bovine dentin dentinoenamel junction dentin-pulp junction method vitro experimental study conduct 30 recently extract human molar 20-30 year old 30 bovine incisor 2-3 year old teeth preserv chloramine maintain moisture thirty dentin bars obtain 15 dentinoenamel junction 15 dentin-pulp junction each bar measur mm wide mm thick specimen observ under stereomicroscope measur digital caliper data enter into three-point bend test program instron universal test machine calculate elastic modulu test perform using two instrument design setup sample holder load application pin 05 result human dentin elastic modulu 89 gpa dentinoenamel junction 7064 gpa dentin-pulp junction bovine dentin 0078 gpa dentinoenamel junction 0388 gpa dentin-pulp junction conclusion elastic modulu valu human bovine dentin both dentinoenamel junction dentin-pulp junction do not suggest significant differenc,biophysic bovine dentin dental biology dentin biomechanic dentinoenamel junction dentin-pulp junction dentistry elastic modulu experimental research human dentin,edgar enrique garcia-hurtado background use bovine dentin dental research has gain relevance due its easy availability lower structural compositional variability morphological similarity human dentin purpose compare elastic modulu human bovine dentin dentinoenamel junction dentin-pulp junction method vitro experimental study conduct 30 recently extract human molar 20-30 year old 30 bovine incisor 2-3 year old teeth preserv chloramine maintain moisture thirty dentin bars obtain 15 dentinoenamel junction 15 dentin-pulp junction each bar measur mm wide mm thick specimen observ under stereomicroscope measur digital caliper data enter into three-point bend test program instron universal test machine calculate elastic modulu test perform using two instrument design setup sample holder load application pin 05 result human dentin elastic modulu 89 gpa dentinoenamel junction 7064 gpa dentin-pulp junction bovine dentin 0078 gpa dentinoenamel junction 0388 gpa dentin-pulp junction conclusion elastic modulu valu human bovine dentin both dentinoenamel junction dentin-pulp junction do not suggest significant differenc biophysic bovine dentin dental biology dentin biomechanic dentinoenamel junction dentin-pulp junction dentistry elastic modulu experimental research human dentin,1.0.0,7902b3d0cb286f44
0120-4319,UO2025v44n07_Giraldo_etal(Eng+listo).pdf,UO2025v44n07_Giraldo_etal(Eng+listo)_0,es,asured with a digital caliper. The data were entered into the three-point bending test program,"Antecedentes: El uso de dentina bovina en investigación odontológica ha adquirido relevancia debido a su fácil obtención, su menor variabilidad estructural y composicional, y su similitud morfológica con la dentina humana. Objetivo: Comparar el módulo elástico de la dentina humana y bovina en la unión amelo-dentinal y en la unión dentino-pulpar. Métodos: Se realizó un estudio experimental in vitro en el que se analizaron 30 molares humanos (20–30 años) y 30 incisivos bovinos (2– 3 años), recién extraídos. Los dientes se conservaron en cloramina T al 2% para mantener la humedad. Se obtuvieron 30 barras de dentina: 15 de la unión amelo-dentinal y 15 de la unión dentino-pulpar. Cada barra midió 2 mm de ancho por 1,5 mm de espesor. Los especímenes se observaron con estereomicroscopio y se midieron con calibrador digital. Los datos se ingresaron al programa del ensayo de flexión en tres puntos (máquina universal de pruebas Instron®) para calcular el módulo elástico. La prueba se realizó con dos instrumentos diseñados para el montaje: un sujetador de la muestra y un pin de aplicación de carga (p = 0.05). Resultados: En dentina humana, el módulo elástico fue 8,89 GPa en la unión amelo-dentinal y 6,7064 GPa en la unión dentino-pulpar. En dentina bovina, fue 9,0078 GPa en la unión amelo-dentinal y 6,0388 GPa en la unión dentino-pulpar. Conclusiones: Los valores del módulo elástico en dentina humana y bovina, tanto en la unión amelodentinal como en la unión dentino-pulpar, no sugieren diferencias relevantes",biofísica; biología dental; biomecánica dentinal; dentina bovina; dentina humana; investigación experimental; módulo de elasticidad; odontología; unión amelo-dentinal; unión dentino-pulpar,marcadores,asured with digital caliper the data were entered into the three-point bending test program,antecedent uso dentina bovina investigacion odontologica ha adquirido relevancia debido facil obtencion menor variabilidad estructural composicional similitud morfologica dentina humana objetivo comparar modulo elastico dentina humana bovina union amelo-dentinal union dentino-pulpar metod realizo estudio experimental in vitro analizaron 30 molar human 20-30 anos 30 incisiv bovin 2- anos recien extraid dient conservaron cloramina mantener humedad obtuvieron 30 barr dentina 15 union amelo-dentinal 15 union dentino-pulpar cada barra midio mm ancho mm espesor especimen observaron estereomicroscopio midieron calibrador digital datos ingresaron programa ensayo flexion tres punt maquina universal prueb instron calcular modulo elastico prueba realizo dos instrument disenad montaje sujetador muestra pin aplicacion carga 05 resultad dentina humana modulo elastico fue 89 gpa union amelo-dentinal 7064 gpa union dentino-pulpar dentina bovina fue 0078 gpa union amelo-dentinal 0388 gpa union dentino-pulpar conclusion valor modulo elastico dentina humana bovina tanto union amelodentinal como union dentino-pulpar no sugieren diferenci relevant,biofisica biologia dental biomecanica dentinal dentina bovina dentina humana investigacion experimental modulo elasticidad odontologia union amelo-dentinal union dentino-pulpar,asured with digital caliper the data were entered into the three-point bending test program antecedent uso dentina bovina investigacion odontologica ha adquirido relevancia debido facil obtencion menor variabilidad estructural composicional similitud morfologica dentina humana objetivo comparar modulo elastico dentina humana bovina union amelo-dentinal union dentino-pulpar metod realizo estudio experimental in vitro analizaron 30 molar human 20-30 anos 30 incisiv bovin 2- anos recien extraid dient conservaron cloramina mantener humedad obtuvieron 30 barr dentina 15 union amelo-dentinal 15 union dentino-pulpar cada barra midio mm ancho mm espesor especimen observaron estereomicroscopio midieron calibrador digital datos ingresaron programa ensayo flexion tres punt maquina universal prueb instron calcular modulo elastico prueba realizo dos instrument disenad montaje sujetador muestra pin aplicacion carga 05 resultad dentina humana modulo elastico fue 89 gpa union amelo-dentinal 7064 gpa union dentino-pulpar dentina bovina fue 0078 gpa union amelo-dentinal 0388 gpa union dentino-pulpar conclusion valor modulo elastico dentina humana bovina tanto union amelodentinal como union dentino-pulpar no sugieren diferenci relevant biofisica biologia dental biomecanica dentinal dentina bovina dentina humana investigacion experimental modulo elasticidad odontologia union amelo-dentinal union dentino-pulpar,1.0.0,f20c695d71da60da
0120-4319,UO2025v44n09_Ayala&Paltas(Eng+listo).pdf,UO2025v44n09_Ayala&Paltas(Eng+listo)_0,en,Oral Public Health and Epidemiology,"Background: The prevalence of impacted incisors varies between 0.01% and 16.92%. This variability may be due to differences in sampling and assessment methods. Purpose: To identify the prevalence and characteristics of impacted incisors by analyzing digital panoramic radiographs in patients with dental age 6 to 12 years, treated between January 2016 and August 2021 in Quito, Ecuador. Methods: Cross-sectional study. 8,000 digital panoramic radiographs from a radiology center in southern Quito were reviewed; 758 met the inclusion and exclusion criteria. Dental age, sex, presence of impacted incisors, type, number, height, angle, and distance from the midline, and associated alterations were recorded. The data were entered into a matrix and analyzed using SPSS v25. Descriptive statistics and the chi-square test were applied, with a 95% confidence level. Results: The prevalence was 11.9% (95% CI). It was more frequent in males (7.5%) and in the 8.0–8.9 year age group (4.3%). Tooth 21 was the most frequently affected (32%). In 67% of cases, a single impacted incisor was observed. Fifty percent were located 6–10 mm above the midline. Seventy-five percent presented an angle <20° with respect to the midline. Ninety percent had a distance greater than 0 from the midline. Conclusions: The prevalence of impacted incisors was higher in males and in dental ages between 7.0 and 8.9 years. Sex and age were associated with the presence and characteristics of dental impaction","dentistry; impacted teeth; incisors; mixed dentition; oral epidemiology; orthopantomography; prevalence; Quito, Ecuador",marcadores,oral public health epidemiology,background prevalence impact incisor vari between 01 16 92 variability may due differenc sampl assessment method purpose identify prevalence characteristic impact incisor analyz digital panoramic radiograph patient dental age 12 year treat between january 2016 august 2021 quito ecuador method cross-sectional study 000 digital panoramic radiograph radiology center southern quito review 758 met inclusion exclusion criteria dental age sex presence impact incisor type number height angle distance midline associat alter record data enter into matrix analyz using spss v25 descriptive statistic chi-square test appli 95 confidence level result prevalence 11 95 ci more frequent male 0-8 year age group tooth 21 most frequently affect 32 67 case single impact incisor observ fifty percent locat 6-10 mm above midline seventy-five percent present angle 20deg respect midline ninety percent had distance greater than midline conclusion prevalence impact incisor higher male dental ages between year sex age associat presence characteristic dental impaction,dentistry impact teeth incisor mixed dentition oral epidemiology orthopantomography prevalence quito ecuador,oral public health epidemiology background prevalence impact incisor vari between 01 16 92 variability may due differenc sampl assessment method purpose identify prevalence characteristic impact incisor analyz digital panoramic radiograph patient dental age 12 year treat between january 2016 august 2021 quito ecuador method cross-sectional study 000 digital panoramic radiograph radiology center southern quito review 758 met inclusion exclusion criteria dental age sex presence impact incisor type number height angle distance midline associat alter record data enter into matrix analyz using spss v25 descriptive statistic chi-square test appli 95 confidence level result prevalence 11 95 ci more frequent male 0-8 year age group tooth 21 most frequently affect 32 67 case single impact incisor observ fifty percent locat 6-10 mm above midline seventy-five percent present angle 20deg respect midline ninety percent had distance greater than midline conclusion prevalence impact incisor higher male dental ages between year sex age associat presence characteristic dental impaction dentistry impact teeth incisor mixed dentition oral epidemiology orthopantomography prevalence quito ecuador,1.0.0,f20804cc79a76c94
0120-4319,UO2025v44n09_Ayala&Paltas(Eng+listo).pdf,UO2025v44n09_Ayala&Paltas(Eng+listo)_0,es,"into a matrix and analyzed using SPSS v25. Descriptive statistics and the chi-square test were applied, with a 95% confidence","Antecedentes: La prevalencia de retención de incisivos varía entre 0,01% y 16,92%. Esta variabilidad puede deberse a diferencias muestrales y métodos de evaluación. Objetivo: Identificar la prevalencia y las características de incisivos retenidos mediante el análisis de ortopantomografías digitales en pacientes con edad dental de 6 a 12 años, atendidos entre enero de 2016 y agosto de 2021, en Quito Ecuador. Métodos: Estudio de corte transversal. Se revisaron 8000 ortopantomografías digitales de un centro radiológico del sur de Quito; 758 cumplieron criterios de inclusión y exclusión. Se registraron edad dental, sexo, presencia de incisivos retenidos, tipo, cantidad, altura, ángulo y distancia respecto a la línea media, y alteraciones asociadas. Los datos se consignaron en una matriz y se analizaron en SPSS v25. Se aplicó estadística descriptiva y prueba de Chi cuadrado, con 95% de confianza. Resultados: La prevalencia fue 11,9% (IC 95%). Fue más frecuente en hombres (7,5%) y en el grupo de 8,0 a 8,9 años (4,3%). El diente 21 fue el más afectado (32%). En el 67% de los casos se observó un solo incisivo retenido. El 50% se ubicó a 6–10 mm de altura. El 75% presentó un ángulo <20° con respecto a la línea media. El 90% tuvo una distancia mayor que 0 respecto a la línea media. Conclusiones: La prevalencia de incisivos retenidos fue mayor en hombres y en edades dentales entre 7,0 y 8,9 años. El sexo y la edad se asociaron con la presencia y con características de la retención dental","dientes retenidos; dentición mixta; epidemiología oral; incisivos; odontología; ortopantomografía; prevalencia; Quito, Ecuador",marcadores,into matrix and analyzed using spss v25 descriptive statistics and the chi-square test were applied with 95 confidence,antecedent preva