0120-4319,UO2025v44n10_Amaya_etal(Eng+Listo).pdf,UO2025v44n10_Amaya_etal(Eng+Listo)_0,en,idadores familiares en,"Background: Social representations held by adults responsible for the development of children during their early years guide their caregiving practices. Purpose: To describe the social representations regarding oral health care in childhood among family caregivers of first-grade students enrolled in a comprehensive support program in Bogotá. Methods: A qualitative study based on semi-structured interviews. Purposive sampling was employed, guided by the criterion of data saturation. Six family caregivers participated in the study. The data were analyzed using thematic analysis. Results: Participants' narratives revealed a concept of oral health centered primarily on its functional roles in eating and expression. The preventive importance of oral hygiene, proper nutrition, and dental visits was acknowledged. However, the caregivers described a lack of adaptation to oral hygiene routines among the children, as well as a fear of dental consultations. Warning signs regarding the children's oral health status—such as dental caries, bruxism, and gingival bleeding—were also identified. Representations concerning tooth exfoliation (losing teeth)—perceived as a potentially traumatic process—were found to be intertwined with specific cultural beliefs and practices, such as the act of ""loosening"" a tooth. The caregivers expressed interest in receiving educational resources on pediatric oral health and showed openness to non-face-to-face, technology-based strategies. Conclusions: The social representations regarding oral health care reflect a comprehensive understanding that interacts with cultural beliefs and practices related to tooth exfoliation. The presence of warning signs—coupled with the children's limited adaptation to oral hygiene routines and dental care—underscores the need to transform existing cultural paradigms","Bogotá, Colombia; caregivers; childhood; community dentistry; dentistry; oral health; public health; qualitative research; social representation",marcadores,idador familiar en,background social represent held adult responsible development children during their early year guide their caregiv practic purpose describe social represent regard oral health care childhood among family caregiver first-grade student enroll comprehensive support program bogota method qualitative study based semi-structur interview purposive sampl employ guid criterion data saturation six family caregiver participat study data analyz using thematic analysi result participant narrativ reveal concept oral health center primarily its functional role eating expression preventive importance oral hygiene proper nutrition dental visit acknowledg however caregiver describ lack adaptation oral hygiene routin among children well fear dental consult warn sign regard children oral health status--such dental cari bruxism gingival bleeding--were also identifi represent concern tooth exfoliation losing teeth --perceiv potentially traumatic process--were found intertwin specific cultural belief practic such act loosen tooth caregiver express interest receiv educational resourc pediatric oral health show opennes non-face-to-face technology-bas strategi conclusion social represent regard oral health care reflect comprehensive understand interact cultural belief practic relat tooth exfoliation presence warn signs--coupl children limit adaptation oral hygiene routin dental care--underscor need transform exist cultural paradigm,bogota colombia caregiver childhood community dentistry dentistry oral health public health qualitative research social representation,idador familiar en background social represent held adult responsible development children during their early year guide their caregiv practic purpose describe social represent regard oral health care childhood among family caregiver first-grade student enroll comprehensive support program bogota method qualitative study based semi-structur interview purposive sampl employ guid criterion data saturation six family caregiver participat study data analyz using thematic analysi result participant narrativ reveal concept oral health center primarily its functional role eating expression preventive importance oral hygiene proper nutrition dental visit acknowledg however caregiver describ lack adaptation oral hygiene routin among children well fear dental consult warn sign regard children oral health status--such dental cari bruxism gingival bleeding--were also identifi represent concern tooth exfoliation losing teeth --perceiv potentially traumatic process--were found intertwin specific cultural belief practic such act loosen tooth caregiver express interest receiv educational resourc pediatric oral health show opennes non-face-to-face technology-bas strategi conclusion social represent regard oral health care reflect comprehensive understand interact cultural belief practic relat tooth exfoliation presence warn signs--coupl children limit adaptation oral hygiene routin dental care--underscor need transform exist cultural paradigm bogota colombia caregiver childhood community dentistry dentistry oral health public health qualitative research social representation,1.0.0,142597486dd6067b
0120-4319,UO2025v44n10_Amaya_etal(Eng+Listo).pdf,UO2025v44n10_Amaya_etal(Eng+Listo)_0,es,concerning tooth exfoliation (losing,"Antecedentes: Las representaciones sociales de los adultos responsables del desarrollo de los niños y las niñas en los primeros años de vida orientan sus prácticas de cuidado. Objetivo: Describir las representaciones sociales sobre el cuidado de la salud oral en la infancia en cuidadores familiares de niños y niñas de primero de primaria vinculados a un programa de apoyo integral en Bogotá. Métodos: Estudio cualitativo basado en entrevistas semiestructuradas. Se realizó muestreo propositivo con criterio de saturación. Participaron seis cuidadores familiares. La información se analizó mediante análisis temático. Resultados: Los relatos mostraron una noción de salud oral centrada en la función alimentaria y expresiva. Se reconoció la importancia preventiva de la higiene oral, la alimentación y la visita al odontólogo. No obstante, se describió poca adaptación a la higiene oral y temor a la consulta odontológica en los niños y las niñas. También se identificaron signos de alarma del estado de salud oral infantil, como caries, bruxismo y sangrado gingival. Las representaciones sobre el recambio dentario, percibido como un proceso traumático, se asociaron con creencias y prácticas culturales, como “aflojar” el diente. Los cuidadores manifestaron interés en recibir educación en salud oral infantil y consideraron estrategias tecnológicas no presenciales. Conclusiones: Las representaciones sobre el cuidado de la salud oral reflejan una comprensión integral, en interacción con creencias y prácticas culturales relacionadas con el recambio dentario. La presencia de signos de alarma y la baja adaptación a la higiene y a la atención odontológica en los niños y las niñas indican la necesidad de transformar paradigmas culturales","Bogotá, Colombia; cuidadores; infancia; investigación cualitativa; odontología; odontología comunitaria; representación social; salud bucal; salud pública",marcadores,concerning tooth exfoliation losing,antecedent represent social adult responsabl desarrollo ninos ninas primer anos vida orientan sus practic cuidado objetivo describir represent social sobre cuidado salud oral infancia cuidador familiar ninos ninas primero primaria vinculad programa apoyo integral bogota metod estudio cualitativo basado entrevist semiestructurad realizo muestreo propositivo criterio saturacion participaron seis cuidador familiar informacion analizo mediante analisis tematico resultad relat mostraron nocion salud oral centrada funcion alimentaria expresiva reconocio importancia preventiva higiene oral alimentacion visita odontologo no obstante describio poca adaptacion higiene oral temor consulta odontologica ninos ninas tambien identificaron sign alarma estado salud oral infantil como cari bruxismo sangrado gingival represent sobre recambio dentario percibido como proceso traumatico asociaron creenci practic cultural como aflojar diente cuidador manifestaron inter recibir educacion salud oral infantil consideraron estrategi tecnologic no presencial conclusion represent sobre cuidado salud oral reflejan comprension integral interaccion creenci practic cultural relacionad recambio dentario presencia sign alarma baja adaptacion higiene atencion odontologica ninos ninas indican necesidad transformar paradigm cultural,bogota colombia cuidador infancia investigacion cualitativa odontologia odontologia comunitaria representacion social salud bucal salud publica,concerning tooth exfoliation losing antecedent represent social adult responsabl desarrollo ninos ninas primer anos vida orientan sus practic cuidado objetivo describir represent social sobre cuidado salud oral infancia cuidador familiar ninos ninas primero primaria vinculad programa apoyo integral bogota metod estudio cualitativo basado entrevist semiestructurad realizo muestreo propositivo criterio saturacion participaron seis cuidador familiar informacion analizo mediante analisis tematico resultad relat mostraron nocion salud oral centrada funcion alimentaria expresiva reconocio importancia preventiva higiene oral alimentacion visita odontologo no obstante describio poca adaptacion higiene oral temor consulta odontologica ninos ninas tambien identificaron sign alarma estado salud oral infantil como cari bruxismo sangrado gingival represent sobre recambio dentario percibido como proceso traumatico asociaron creenci practic cultural como aflojar diente cuidador manifestaron inter recibir educacion salud oral infantil consideraron estrategi tecnologic no presencial conclusion represent sobre cuidado salud oral reflejan comprension integral interaccion creenci practic cultural relacionad recambio dentario presencia sign alarma baja adaptacion higiene atencion odontologica ninos ninas indican necesidad transformar paradigm cultural bogota colombia cuidador infancia investigacion cualitativa odontologia odontologia comunitaria representacion social salud bucal salud publica,1.0.0,8c35eaf67c0b05e4
0120-4319,UO2025v44n11_Ortega_etal(Eng+Listo).pdf,UO2025v44n11_Ortega_etal(Eng+Listo)_0,en,e práticas relacionados à higiene bucal entre estudantes do ensino médio,"Background: Persistent poor oral hygiene habits among high school students suggest gaps in knowledge, attitudes, and practices, shaped by educational and sociocultural contexts. Purpose: To describe knowledge, attitudes, and practices (KAPs) related to oral hygiene and their association with sociodemographic factors among high school students. Methods: A cross-sectional survey was conducted with 458 students aged 11–19 years in Cartagena, Colombia. Participants completed an oral hygiene KAP questionnaire retrieved from the literature. The instrument underwent face validity assessment and cultural adaptation by the authors. Data were analyzed using frequencies, the χ² test, and logistic regression to explore associations (p<0.05). Results: Acceptable knowledge was the most frequent finding. Favorable attitudes predominated and were associated with school grade (p=0.008), age (p=0.01), and parents’ education level (p=0.013). Unfavorable practices were more common. In multivariate analysis, only attitudes remained significantly associated with age, school grade, and parents’ education level (χ²=23.6; p<0.001). Conclusions: Although knowledge and attitudes were acceptable, reported practices did not support effective oral health maintenance. These practices may represent vulnerability factors for oral health preservation","adolescents; attitudes; Cartagena, Colombia; dental habits; dentistry; knowledge; oral health education; oral hygiene; practices; preventive dentistry; school students",marcadores,pratica relacionado higiene bucal entre estudant do ensino medio,background persistent poor oral hygiene habit among high school student suggest gaps knowledge attitud practic shap educational sociocultural context purpose describe knowledge attitud practic kaps relat oral hygiene their association sociodemographic factor among high school student method cross-sectional survey conduct 458 student aged 11-19 year cartagena colombia participant complet oral hygiene kap questionnaire retriev literature instrument underwent face validity assessment cultural adaptation author data analyz using frequenci kh2 test logistic regression explore associ 05 result acceptable knowledge most frequent find favorable attitud predominat associat school grade 008 age 01 parent education level 013 unfavorable practic more common multivariate analysi only attitud remain significantly associat age school grade parent education level kh2 23 001 conclusion although knowledge attitud acceptable report practic did not support effective oral health maintenance these practic may represent vulnerability factor oral health preservation,adolescent attitud cartagena colombia dental habit dentistry knowledge oral health education oral hygiene practic preventive dentistry school student,pratica relacionado higiene bucal entre estudant do ensino medio background persistent poor oral hygiene habit among high school student suggest gaps knowledge attitud practic shap educational sociocultural context purpose describe knowledge attitud practic kaps relat oral hygiene their association sociodemographic factor among high school student method cross-sectional survey conduct 458 student aged 11-19 year cartagena colombia participant complet oral hygiene kap questionnaire retriev literature instrument underwent face validity assessment cultural adaptation author data analyz using frequenci kh2 test logistic regression explore associ 05 result acceptable knowledge most frequent find favorable attitud predominat associat school grade 008 age 01 parent education level 013 unfavorable practic more common multivariate analysi only attitud remain significantly associat age school grade parent education level kh2 23 001 conclusion although knowledge attitud acceptable report practic did not support effective oral health maintenance these practic may represent vulnerability factor oral health preservation adolescent attitud cartagena colombia dental habit dentistry knowledge oral health education oral hygiene practic preventive dentistry school student,1.0.0,9aae037a8e794da8
0120-4319,UO2025v44n11_Ortega_etal(Eng+Listo).pdf,UO2025v44n11_Ortega_etal(Eng+Listo)_0,es,"ors. Data were analyzed using frequencies, the","Antecedentes: La persistencia de hábitos deficientes de higiene bucal entre estudiantes de secundaria sugiere la existencia de brechas en conocimientos, actitudes y prácticas, las cuales están moldeadas por contextos educativos y socioculturales. Objetivo: Describir los conocimientos, actitudes y prácticas (CAP) relacionados con la higiene bucal, así como su asociación con factores sociodemográficos, entre estudiantes de secundaria. Métodos: Se realizó un transversal por medio de una encuesta a 458 estudiantes de entre 11 y 19 años en Cartagena, Colombia. Los participantes completaron un cuestionario sobre CAP en higiene bucal, que se obtuvo de la literatura científica. El instrumento fue sometido a una evaluación de validez aparente y a una adaptación cultural por parte de los autores. Los datos se analizaron mediante frecuencias, la prueba χ² y regresión logística para explorar las asociaciones (p<0,05). Resultados: Un nivel de conocimientos aceptable fue el hallazgo más frecuente. Predominaron las actitudes favorables, las cuales se asociaron con el grado escolar (p = 0,008), la edad (p = 0,01) y el nivel educativo de los padres (p = 0,013). Las prácticas desfavorables resultaron ser las más comunes. En el análisis multivariado, solo las actitudes mantuvieron una asociación significativa con la edad, el grado escolar y el nivel educativo de los padres (χ² = 23,6; p < 0,001). Conclusiones: Si bien los conocimientos y las actitudes resultaron aceptables, las prácticas reportadas no respaldaron un mantenimiento eficaz de la salud bucal. Estas prácticas podrían constituir factores de vulnerabilidad para la preservación de la salud bucal","adolescentes; actitudes; Cartagena, Colombia; conocimientos; educación en salud bucal; escolares; hábitos de salud bucal; higiene bucal; odontología; odontología preventiva; prácticas",marcador