0120-4807,upsala6592891008.pdf,upsala6592891008_0,en,"ra el Antropoceno, para indagar por la pregunta ¿qué tienen los","is research article presents some of my ndings regarding some of the bodies of water in the Bolivarian Mojana region of Colombia, which I was able to discover during my ethnographic eldwork, thanks to the expert local knowledge of the region’s traditional shermen, who introduced me to them. In my dual capacity as a lawyer advising some of these shermen and as an anthropologist, I identied connectivity and movement as characteristics of the swamps and rivers studied. I was also able to view them as besieged bodies whose lives are in jeopardy, as I describe in relation to the transformations brought about by water infrastructure and illegal land grabbing. I bring the two aforementioned characteristics to the eld of studies on law for the Anthropocene, to investigate the question: What do bodies of water have to teach the law? And in dialogue with authors such as Grear (2020), Davies (2022), Wheeler, Grear, and Burdon (2023), who have considered that the environmental and social context in which we nd ourselves merits the emergence of a post-humanist and post-anthropocentric Wild Law (in which matter is neither immutable nor passive, nor can it be considered xed or localized), I propose that a conceptual shi involves considering that the principles of law arise from non-humans and more-than-humans to regulate the human world, and not the other way around. With this research, we are invited to consider what a wild law for the Anthropocene would be based on bodies of water and what a justice of that nature would entail","Wild Law, Connectivity, Movement, Expert-Local Knowledge, Landslide",marcadores,ra el antropoceno para indagar por la pregunta que tienen los,research article present some my nding regard some bodi water bolivarian mojana region colombia which able discover during my ethnographic eldwork thank expert local knowledge region traditional shermen who introduc me them my dual capacity lawyer advis some these shermen anthropologist identi connectivity movement characteristic swamp river studi also able view them besieg bodi whose live jeopardy describe relation transform brought about water infrastructure illegal land grabb bring two aforemention characteristic eld studi law anthropocene investigate question what do bodi water have teach law dialogue author such grear 2020 davi 2022 wheeler grear burdon 2023 who have consider environmental social context which we nd ourselv merit emergence post-humanist post-anthropocentric wild law which matter neither immutable nor passive nor can consider xed localiz propose conceptual shi involv consider principl law arise non-human more-than-human regulate human world not other way around research we invit consider what wild law anthropocene would based bodi water what justice nature would entail,wild law connectivity movement expert-local knowledge landslide,ra el antropoceno para indagar por la pregunta que tienen los research article present some my nding regard some bodi water bolivarian mojana region colombia which able discover during my ethnographic eldwork thank expert local knowledge region traditional shermen who introduc me them my dual capacity lawyer advis some these shermen anthropologist identi connectivity movement characteristic swamp river studi also able view them besieg bodi whose live jeopardy describe relation transform brought about water infrastructure illegal land grabb bring two aforemention characteristic eld studi law anthropocene investigate question what do bodi water have teach law dialogue author such grear 2020 davi 2022 wheeler grear burdon 2023 who have consider environmental social context which we nd ourselv merit emergence post-humanist post-anthropocentric wild law which matter neither immutable nor passive nor can consider xed localiz propose conceptual shi involv consider principl law arise non-human more-than-human regulate human world not other way around research we invit consider what wild law anthropocene would based bodi water what justice nature would entail wild law connectivity movement expert-local knowledge landslide,1.0.0,24a079064546ef86
0120-4874,Revista+45(1)+art+1+chequeo+1.pdf,Revista+45(1)+art+1+chequeo+1_0,es,Universidad de Antioquía.,"Objetivo: describir los factores relacionados con la mortalidad en población pediátrica menor de 5 años, debida a infección respiratoria aguda (IRA), en Antioquia durante el año 2022. Métodos: estudio cuantitativo, transversal y descriptivo que incluyó el universo de Fichas de Notificación número 591 de menores de 5 años fallecidos por IRA confirmada y su respectiva unidad de análisis, recolección de información posterior a la aprobación del Comité de Ética de la Institución Educativa y de la Secretaría Seccional de Salud de Antioquia. Análisis de información en el programa estadístico Jamovi 2.3. Resultados: el 53,5 % de los menores fallecidos eran niños, la tercera parte residía en centro poblado o área rural. El 60,6 % pertenecía a los estratos socioeconómicos 1 y 2 y al régimen subsidiado en salud, mientras que otros no contaban con afiliación al sistema de salud. El 10,7 % pertenecían a comunidades indígenas. Un 39,3 % de las madres no tenía ningún grado de escolaridad y el 75 % de las muertes sucedieron en el hospital. Como factores relacionados se identificó la ignorancia sobre los síntomas y signos de alerta por parte de la persona encargada del cuidado, incumplimiento de acciones de demanda inducida por el personal de salud, debilidad en la calidad de la atención recibida y demora de los cuidadores para buscar atención oportuna. Conclusiones: determinantes sociales de la salud, por ejemplo, la baja escolaridad materna o la pobreza, aumentan el riesgo de muerte en por infección respiratoria aguda en Antioquía, en la población estudiada",Mortalidad infantil; Menores; Determinantes sociales de la salud; Educación para la salud; Signos y síntomas,marcadores,universidad antioquia,objetivo describir factor relacionad mortalidad poblacion pediatrica menor anos debida infeccion respiratoria aguda ira antioquia durante ano 2022 metod estudio cuantitativo transversal descriptivo incluyo universo fich notificacion numero 591 menor anos fallecid ira confirmada respectiva unidad analisis recoleccion informacion posterior aprobacion comite etica institucion educativa secretaria seccional salud antioquia analisis informacion programa estadistico jamovi resultad 53 menor fallecid eran ninos tercera parte residia centro poblado area rural 60 pertenecia estrat socioeconomic regimen subsidiado salud mientr otros no contaban afiliacion sistema salud 10 pertenecian comunidad indigen 39 madr no tenia ningun grado escolaridad 75 muert sucedieron hospital como factor relacionad identifico ignorancia sobre sintom sign alerta parte persona encargada cuidado incumplimiento accion demanda inducida personal salud debilidad calidad atencion recibida demora cuidador buscar atencion oportuna conclusion determinant social salud ejemplo baja escolaridad materna pobreza aumentan riesgo muerte infeccion respiratoria aguda antioquia poblacion estudiada,mortalidad infantil menor determinant social salud educacion salud sign sintom,universidad antioquia objetivo describir factor relacionad mortalidad poblacion pediatrica menor anos debida infeccion respiratoria aguda ira antioquia durante ano 2022 metod estudio cuantitativo transversal descriptivo incluyo universo fich notificacion numero 591 menor anos fallecid ira confirmada respectiva unidad analisis recoleccion informacion posterior aprobacion comite etica institucion educativa secretaria seccional salud antioquia analisis informacion programa estadistico jamovi resultad 53 menor fallecid eran ninos tercera parte residia centro poblado area rural 60 pertenecia estrat socioeconomic regimen subsidiado salud mientr otros no contaban afiliacion sistema salud 10 pertenecian comunidad indigen 39 madr no tenia ningun grado escolaridad 75 muert sucedieron hospital como factor relacionad identifico ignorancia sobre sintom sign alerta parte persona encargada cuidado incumplimiento accion demanda inducida personal salud debilidad calidad atencion recibida demora cuidador buscar atencion oportuna conclusion determinant social salud ejemplo baja escolaridad materna pobreza aumentan riesgo muerte infeccion respiratoria aguda antioquia poblacion estudiada mortalidad infantil menor determinant social salud educacion salud sign sintom,1.0.0,68d19643c537e52b
0120-4874,Revista+45(1)+art+1+chequeo+1.pdf,Revista+45(1)+art+1+chequeo+1_0,en,"alud, mientras que otros no contaban con afiliación al sistema","Objective: To describe the factors related to the mortality of minors under five years due to Acute Respiratory Infection in Antioquia during 2022. Methods: Cross-sectional descriptive study. It includes the universe of Notification Cards number 591 of children under five years who died of verified ARI and their respective Analysis Unit. Information collection after approval by the Ethics Committee of the Educational Institution and the Sectional Health Secretariat of Antioquia. The information was analyzed in the statistical software Jamovi 2.3. Results: 53.5% of the deceased children were boys, a third of whom lived in populated centers or rural areas. 60.6% belonged to socioeconomic strata 1 and 2 and were enrolled in subsidized health care, while the rest were not affiliated with the health system. 10.7% were from indigenous communities. 39.3% of the mothers had no schooling, and 75% of the deaths occurred in hospitals. Related factors were identified: caregiver ignorance of 2-11 López Herrera FE, et al. : MEDICINA U.P.B. 45(1) | enero-junio 2026 | 3 warning signs and symptoms, failure to comply with actions induced by demand by health personnel, poor quality of care received, and caregivers’ delay in seeking timely care. Conclusions: Social determinants of health such as poverty and low maternal schooling increase the risk of death due to Acute Respiratory Infection in children under five years in Antioquia",Infant Mortality; Minors; Determinants of Social Health; Health Education; Signs and Symptoms,marcadores,alud mientra que otro no contaban con afiliacion al sistema,objective describe factor relat mortality minor under five year due acute respiratory infection antioquia during 2022 method cross-sectional descriptive study includ universe notification card number 591 children under five year who died verifi ari thei