0120-548X,123341_Versión_Final_2026.pdf,123341_Versión_Final_2026_0,en,"El Alto Sinú presentó la mayor abundancia, lo que indica una comunidad","The family Chrysomelidae, one of the most diverse groups of beetles, includes the subfamily Cassidinae. In Colombia, particularly in Córdoba, studies on this group are scarce; therefore, this research aims to characterize their diversity and distribution. Insect sampling was carried out in Córdoba using transects and manual collection during both dry and rainy seasons. The samples were processed in the laboratory for morphological identification. Diversity was assessed using the Shannon-Weaver and Simpson indices, and its relationship with environmental variables was analyzed through a CCA (Canonical Correspondence Analysis). The results reveal a diversity gradient among subregions, recording ten tribes and 30 species. Alto Sinú exhibited the highest abundance, indicating a balanced community, while the Coastal subregion showed the lowest diversity. The results showed that Cassidinae species diversity was positively associated with higher precipitation and thermal stability, particularly in the Alto Sinú subregion, where vegetation heterogeneity favors a greater availability of host plants. In contrast, more homogeneous environments, such as those in the Coastal subregion, limited species richness by reducing the variety of plant formations. It is concluded that the distribution of Cassidinae is linked to the availability of specific food resources for these phytophagous insects, which exhibit high host specificity","Coleoptera, habitat heterogeneity, multivariate ordination, Neotropical Region, seasonality. Composición taxonómica y ecología de las especies de Cassidinae en Córdoba… Acta Biol. Colomb., 31(2) 36-48 Mayo - Agosto 2026 37",marcadores,el alto sinu presento la mayor abundancia lo que indica una comunidad,family chrysomelidae one most diverse group beetl includ subfamily cassidinae colombia particularly cordoba s