0120-548X,124267_Versión_Final_2026.pdf,124267_Versión_Final_2026_0,en,tran variaciones en la calidad de la miel,"The study provides information on the bioactive properties of honey and propolis from eight species of stingless bees from the “Tua Ta Uypi” Meliponary (Cochabamba, Bolivia). The quality of honey from seven stingless bee species and Apis mellifera was evaluated, along with its antimicrobial activity using the agar diffusion method against ATCC strains (25922 Escherichia coli and 25923 Staphylococcus aureus). Additionally, metabolites were extracted from the propolis of five species through ethanol maceration and preliminarily identified using thin-layer chromatography. Finally, propolis extracts from four species were, in vitro, tested against strains of Leishmania amazonensis, L. braziliensis and Giardia lamblia. The results reveal variations in honey quality among species, with the antimicrobial activity of Scaptotrigona depilis, Melipona rufiventris, and Tetragona goettei honey showing inhibition zones greater than Variación de las propiedades bioactivas de miel y propóleos de abejas sin aguijón Acta Biol. Colomb., 31(2) 70-80 Mayo - Agosto 2026 71 17 mm for E. coli and 16 mm for S. aureus, like the positive controls (Amikacin and Erythromycin). In the propolis of Melipona eburnea and Tetragonisca angustula, were observed compounds consistent with terpenes and poliphenols. In the antiparasitic tests, T. angustula propolis showed activity against both Leishmania strains and Giardia, while the propolis from S. polysticta and S. yungasensis exhibited activity against G. lamblia. These findings highlight the therapeutic potential of the products from these stingless bees","antimicrobial, anti-parasitic, propolis extracts, physicochemical, phytochemical",marcadores,tran variacion en la calidad de la miel,study provid information bioactive properti honey propoli eight speci stingles bees tua ta uypi meliponary cochabamba bolivia quality honey seven stingles