0120-5587,10Edición89.pdf,10Edición89_0,en,"Resumen: El objetivo es describir el jágaɨ, género narrativo oral y escrito del pueblo múrui-múina del Amazonas colombiano, así como su","The objective is to describe jágaɨ, an oral and written narrative genre of the múrui-múina people of the Colombian Amazon, as well as its relationship with other narrative genres, based on the múrui-múina narrative theory of kɨrɨ́gaɨaɨ (Vivas, 2012) and Ricœur›s (2009) analysis of narrated time. The paper addresses perspectives, problems and methodologies of narratological analysis and written fixation in specialized books on jágaɨ during the last decade. It concludes that zójikaiya (transformation), járede (fear), and jejɨ́maja (compositional form of oral narration) are constitutive elements of the narrative identity of jágaɨ","jágaɨ, múrui-múina, failure narrative, intercultural literature, literary research. Narrar el jágaɨ: hacia una narratología propia múrui-múina lingüística y literatura · n°89, enero - junio 2026 234| 1. Introducción1 Jágaɨ se puede traducir, de modo sintético, como un relato antiguo del pueblo múrui-múina que trata, entre otros, el tema del fracaso. Ha sido narrado oralmente a través de generac",marcadores,resumen el objetivo es describir el jagai genero narrativo oral escrito del pueblo murui-muina del amazona colombiano asi como su,objective describe jagai oral written narrative genre murui-muina people colombian amazon well its relationship other narrative genr based murui-muina narrative theory kirigaiai viva 2012 ricoeur 2009 analysi narrat time paper address perspectiv problem methodologi narratological analysi written fixation specializ book jagai during last decade conclud zojikaiya transformation jarede fear jejimaja compositional form oral narration constitutive element narrative identity jagai,jagai murui-muina failure narrative intercultural literature literary research narrar el jagai hacia una narratologia propia murui-muina linguistica literatura n