0120-9957,57-121-PB.pdf,57-121-PB_3,en,"7%). El 28,3% presentó al menos una complicación","Introduction: Ulcerative colitis is a chronic inflammatory bowel disease whose clinical course and therapeutic requirements have been described mainly in North American and European cohorts. In Latin America, information from real-world longitudinal studies remains limited. Methodology: Researchers conducted a retrospective case series that included adult patients with a confirmed diagnosis of ulcerative colitis treated at a Colombian referral center between January 2020 and April 2025. They collected sociodemographic variables, disease extent, treatments received, intestinal and extraintestinal complications, surgical requirements, and use of advanced therapies. The analysis was descriptive. Results: The study included 53 patients, with a predominance of women (60.4%). Proctitis was the most frequent presentation (41.7%). A total of 28.3% experienced at least one intestinal complication, and bleeding requiring hospitalization was the most common (18.9%). Extraintestinal manifestations occurred in 15.1%, while 9.4% required surgical management. A total of 30.2% were refractory to conventional therapy and required escalation to advanced therapies, initiated on average 46 months after diagnosis; vedolizumab was the most frequently used agent. Conclusions: A significant proportion of patients with ulcerative colitis in this Colombian case series developed complications and required advanced therapies, generally at a late stage. These findings provide local real-world evidence and highlight the need to optimize follow-up and timely therapeutic escalation","Ulcerative colitis, inflammatory bowel diseases, longitudinal studies, biological therapy. https://doi.org/10.22516/25007440.1535 Trabajo original Revista. colomb. Gastroenterol. 2026;41(3):303-308. https://doi.org/10.22516/25007440.1535 304 Trabajo original En este contexto, el presente estudio describe las carac terísticas clínicas, la evolución, la aparición de complica ciones intestinales y ex",marcadores,el 28 presento al meno una complicacion,introduction ulcerative coliti chronic inflammatory bowel disease whose clinical course therapeutic requirement have been describ mainly north american european cohort latin america information real-world longitudinal studi remain limit methodology researcher conduct retrospective case seri includ adult patient confirm diagnosi ulcerative coliti treat colombian referral center between january 2020 april 2025 they collect sociodemographic variabl disease extent treatment receiv intestinal extraintestinal complic surgical requirement use advanc therapi analysi descriptive result study includ 53 patient predominance women 60 proctiti most frequent presentation 41 total 28 experienc least one intestinal complication bleed requir hospital most common 18 extraintestinal manifest occurr 15 while requir surgical management total 30 refractory conventional therapy requir escalation advanc therapi initiat average 46 month after diagnosi vedolizumab most frequently used agent conclusion significant proportion patient ulcerative coliti colombian case seri develop complic requir advanc therapi generally late stage these finding provide local real-world evidence highlight need optimize follow-up timely therapeutic escalation,ulcerative coliti inflammatory bowel diseas longitudinal studi biological therapy http doi org 10 22516 25007440 1535 trabajo original revista colomb gastroenterol 2026 41 303-308 http doi org 10 22516 25007440 1535 304 trabajo original en este contexto el presente estudio describe las carac teristica clinica la evolucion la aparicion de complica cion intestinal ex,el 28 presento al meno una complicacion introduction ulcerative coliti chronic inflammatory bowel disease whose clinical course therapeutic requirement have been describ mainly north american european cohort latin america information real-world longitudinal studi remain limit m