estoriforme serologia mostro nivel igg4 veces limite superior paciente presento adem hipertrofia glandul salival adenopati cervical respuesta clinica completa tratamiento glucocorticoid discusion caso corresponde fenotipo clinico multiorganico descrito literatura cumpl criteri clasificacion acr eular 2019 er-igg4 sospecha inicial neoplasia pancreatica condujo intervencion quirurgica innecesaria ilustra dificultad diagnostica esta entidad este seria primer caso reportado region caribe colombia paciente afrodescendiente cual aporta evidencia sobre variabilidad fenotipica necesidad abordaje multidisciplinario conclusion er-igg4 debe considerarse diagnostico diferencial masas pancreatic biliar reconocimiento temprano evita proced invasiv innecesari permite instaurar tratamiento glucocorticoid logra remision clinica enfermedad relacionada inmunoglobulina g4 pancreatitis autoinmune glandul salival,1.0.0,88c57942e007e2ae
0120-9957,57-121-PB.pdf,57-121-PB_9,en,sión: el caso corresponde,"Introduction: IgG4-related disease (IgG4-RD) is a recently described systemic fibroinflammatory disorder characterized by dense lymphoplasmacytic infiltrate, storiform fibrosis, obliterative phlebitis, and a favorable response to glucocorticoids. Its diagnosis remains challenging because it often mimics neoplastic or autoimmune processes. Case presentation: A 60-year-old Afro-Colombian woman with a history of obstructive jaundice, weight loss, and a pancreatic lesion initially suspected to be a neoplasm. She underwent cholecystectomy, with histopathological findings of lymphoplasmacytic sclerosing pancreatitis, showing an infiltrate rich in IgG4-positive cells and storiform fibrosis. Serology showed IgG4 levels >5 times the upper limit of normal. The patient also presented salivary gland hypertrophy and cervical lymphadenopathy, with a complete clinical response to glucocorticoid treatment. Discussion: The case corresponds to the multiorgan clinical phenotype described in the literature, meeting the 2019 ACR/EULAR classification criteria for IgG4-RD. The initial suspicion of pancreatic neoplasia led to an unnecessary surgical intervention, illustrating the diagnostic difficulty of this entity. This would be the first case reported in the Caribbean region of Colombia in an Afro-descendant patient, contributing evidence on phenotypic variability and the need for a multidisciplinary approach. Conclusion: IgG4-RD should be considered in the differential diagnosis of pancreatic and biliary masses. Early recognition prevents unnecessary invasive procedures and allows initiation of glucocorticoid treatment, which achieves clinical remission","Immunoglobulin G4-related disease, autoimmune pancreatitis, salivary glands. https://doi.org/10.22516/25007440.1447 Reporte de caso 343 Enfermedad relacionada con IgG4: un caso de compromiso pancreático y extrapancreático en una mujer afrocolombiana PRESENTACIÓN DEL CASO Se trata de una mujer de 60 años, fototipo IV. Ingresó a Reumatología remitida del servicio de Hepatología con diag nóstico de",marcadores,sion el caso corresponde,introduction igg4-related disease igg4-rd recently describ systemic fibroinflammatory disorder characteriz dense lymphoplasmacytic infiltrate storiform fibrosi obliterative phlebiti favorable response glucocorticoid its diagnosi remain challeng because often mimic neoplastic autoimmune process case presentation 60-year-old afro-colombian woman history obstructive jaundice weight loss pancreatic lesion initially suspect neoplasm she underwent cholecystectomy histopathological finding lymphoplasmacytic scleros pancreatiti show infiltrate rich igg4-positive cell storiform fibrosi serology show igg4 level time upper limit normal patient also present salivary gland hypertrophy cervical lymphadenopathy complete clinical response glucocorticoid treatment discussion case correspond multiorgan clinical phenotype describ literature meet 2019 acr eular classification criteria igg4-rd initial suspicion pancreatic neoplasia led unnecessary surgical intervention illustrat diagnostic difficulty entity would first case report caribbean region colombia afro-descendant patient contribut evidence phenotypic variability need multidisciplinary approach conclusion igg4-rd should consider differential diagnosi pancreatic biliary mass early recognition prevent unnecessary invasive procedur allow initiation glucocorticoid treatment which achiev clinical remission,immunoglobulin g4-related disease autoimmune pancreatiti salivary gland http doi org 10 22516 25007440 1447 reporte de caso 343 enfermedad relacionada con igg4 un caso de compromiso pancreatico extrapancreatico en una mujer afrocolombiana presentacion del caso se trata de una mujer de 60 anos fototipo iv ingreso reumatologia remitida del servicio de hepatologia con diag nostico de,sion el caso corresponde introduction igg4-related disease igg4-rd recently describ syste