0120-9957,57-121-PB.pdf,57-121-PB_10,en,"manejo definitivo con dilatación de la vía biliar con SpyGlass, en la que","Introduction: Cholangitis is an infection of the biliary tract usually caused by gram-negative bacilli. Comamonas testosteroni is a bacterium commonly found in the environment; however, it is not part of the human microbiome. To date, no cases of bacteremia secondary to cholangitis caused by C. testosteroni have been described. Case presentation: A 77-year-old female patient with benign biliary stenosis and recurrent choledocholithiasis presented with Tokyo II cholangitis, with isolation of multidrug-susceptible C. testosteroni in both blood cultures and bile fluid culture, showing the same susceptibility profile. She received ten days of antibiotic treatment with piperacillin/tazobactam, and follow-up blood cultures were negative. Definitive management included biliary tract dilation with SpyGlass, during which biopsies were taken and showed severe chronic and acute inflammatory changes with reactive epithelial changes, negative for malignancy, with favorable clinical progression. Discussion: Infection in humans caused by Comamonas species is unusual, and the most frequent species is C. testosteroni, mainly associated with intra-abdominal infections (most secondary to perforation of the cecal appendix). MALDI-TOF (Matrix Assisted Laser Desorption Ionization Time of Flight) has become a useful tool for differentiating Comamonas species. Conclusion: C. testosteroni is a possible causative agent of cholangitis. The arrival and expansion of technologies such as MALDI-TOF make it possible to identify unusual microorganisms and guide treatment","Comamonas testosteroni, bacteremia, cholangitis. https://doi.org/10.22516/25007440.1467 Reporte de caso Revista. colomb. Gastroenterol. 2026;41(3):349-355. https://doi.org/10.22516/25007440.1467 350 Reporte de caso realizó mediante espectrometría de masas MALDI-TOF y la evaluación de sensibilidad antimicrobiana mediante el método automatizado Vitek 2®. El perfil de sensibilidad de la bacteria s",marcadores,manejo definitivo con dilatacion de la via biliar con spyglas en la que,introduction cholangiti infection biliary tract usually caus gram-negative bacilli comamona testosteroni bacterium commonly found environment however not part human microbiome date no case bacteremia secondary cholangiti caus testosteroni have been describ case presentation 77-year-old female patient benign biliary stenosi recurrent choledocholithiasi present tokyo ii cholangiti isolation multidrug-susceptible testosteroni both blood cultur bile fluid culture show same susceptibility profile she receiv ten days antibiotic treatment piperacillin tazobactam follow-up blood cultur negative definitive management includ biliary tract dilation spyglas during which biopsi taken show severe chronic acute inflammatory chang reactive epithelial chang negative malignancy favorable clinical progression discussion infection human caus comamona speci unusual most frequent speci testosteroni mainly associat intra-abdominal infection most secondary perforation cecal appendix maldi-tof matrix assist laser desorption ionization time flight has become useful tool differentiat comamona speci conclusion testosteroni possible causative agent cholangiti arrival expansion technologi such maldi-tof make possible identify unusual microorganism guide treatment,comamona testosteroni bacteremia cholangiti http doi org 10 22516 25007440 1467 reporte de caso revista colomb gastroenterol 2026 41 349-355 http doi org 10 22516 25007440 1467 350 reporte de caso realizo mediante espectrometria de masa maldi-tof la evaluacion de sensibilidad antimicrobiana mediante el metodo automatizado vitek el perfil de sensibilidad de la bacteria,manejo definitivo con dilatacion de la via biliar con spyglas en la que introduction cholangiti infection biliary tract usually caus gram-negative bacilli comamona testosteroni bacterium commonly found environ