se report revista colomb gastroenterol 2026 41 356-362 http doi org 10 22516 25007440 1481 358 reporte de caso endoscopico endosonografico normal cabeza cuerpo del pancrea normal con conducto de wirsung normal en la cola del pancrea una lesion tumoral solido-quistica que mide 39 mm 40 mm de diametro,bilidad en comparacion con el adenocarcinoma ductal pan introduction pancreatic adenosquamou carcinoma uncommon exocrine neoplasm repre sent between pancreatic tumor characteriz presence glandular squamou component associat highly aggressive behavior poor prognosi diagnosi usually occur advanc stag because its nonspecific clinical presentation rapid progression case presentation we present case 82-year-old female patient abdominal pain jaundice constitutional syndrome laboratory studi show cholestasi cytolysi direct hyperbilirubi nemia comput tomography abdominal magnetic resonance imag show solid-cystic lesion tail pancrea involvement adjacent structur multiple liver lesion suggestive metastas endoscopic ultrasound biopsy confirm diagnosi adenosquamou carcinoma through histopathological immunohistochemical studi p63 positive squamou component carcinoembryonic antigen positive glandular component patient had unfavorable clini cal course died two month after diagnosi discussion tumor subtype associat high rate early dissemination lymphovascular invasion perineural invasion which limit therapeutic option although surgical resection treatment choice early stag most case unresecta ble diagnosi no standardiz chemotherapy regimen exist reflect limit available evidence conclusion pancreatic adenosquamou carcinoma rare entity poor prognosi its timely recognition histological confirmation essential additional studi requir optimize its diag nostic therapeutic approach consultation information time manag pathology rare poorly known pancreatic neoplasm endoscopic ultrasonography elderly biopsy case report revista colomb gastroenterol 2026 41 356-362 http doi org 10 22516 25007440 14