0120-9957,57-121-PB.pdf,57-121-PB_19,en,request of the Editorial Committee. Editorials must,"length: 250 words. Maximum paper length: 6000 words. Maximum num ber of references: 80. • Literature Reviews: These must be submitted only by experts in the topic to be addressed if requested directly by the Editorial Committee. • Case Reports: These are papers intended to report one or more cases considered to have a special interest by authors. This type of paper must also include a brief review of the relevant literature. Case reports are peer reviewed by at least one external peer review. Maximum abstract length: 250 words. Maximum paper length: 3500 words. Maximum number of references:40. • Resident’s section: In this section, gastroenterology or related specialties fellows can openly submit origi nal or review articles performed alone or together with their professors. These articles are peer reviewed by external peers. • Letters to the Editor: These are brief comments on a paper published in the Journal. The Editorial Committee is responsible for deciding on the publica tion of Letters to the Editor. The Colombian Journal of Gastroenterology accepts sub missions of scientific articles that conform to the following editorial guidelines. Non-compliance with them shall be cause for rejection. 1. All works submitted to the Journal must be original and unpublished. Papers that have been already published will not be accepted. In this sense, articles that partially or subs tantially reproduce works that have been published, even in other languages, shall not be submitted. Plagiarism detec tion tools are used in the editorial review process. 2. Authors: Authors’ names and the order in which they appear must be carefully reviewed before making a sub mission so that they are recorded correctly in the website. Changes involving the addition, removal or rearrangement of authors must be done before the paper is accepted for publication and prior approval of the Editor of the Journal. Authors’ identifying information must be included only in the submission made through the OJS website of the journal; it should not be included in the file that contains the article to be peer reviewed. Also, the ORCID ID code of all authors must be included, so that each author can be Guidelines for Authors identified unambiguously. Any reference to the authors’ identity or institutional affiliation must be omitted in the name of the file, its contents and supplementary materials (figures). Information regarding the institutional affiliation of all authors must be registered in the submission made in the website of the journal. • Authorship: As established in the Recommendations for the Conduct, Reporting, Editing and Publication of Scholarly Work in Medical Journals (the Uniform Requirements for Manuscripts) of the ICMJE, to be considered an author, substantial contributions regar ding a) the conception and design of the work, or the acquisition, analysis, or interpretation of data for the work; b) the drafting or planning of the paper or the revision of important intellectual content, and c) the final approval of the version to be published, must have been made. Authors must meet all these conditions to be considered as such. “Courtesy Authorship” is unac ceptable. For example, being involved only in the provi sion of samples or the recruitment of patients, although essential for conducting the research, is not enough to be considered and author, since giving credit to the per son responsible for these processes in the acknowledg ments is usually enough. Also, authors must state their individual contributions in the making of the paper. 3. Papers must be written in Spanish and must be submit ted in a .doc or .docx file at the www.revistagastrocol.com website. Articles must have a minimum length of 3.000 words and a maximum of 6.000 words. The English version of the title, abstract and","must be also included. The text format shall be as follows: • Single column, letter sized. • 2.5 cm. margins, double spaced. • All pages must be numbered in the lower right-hand corner • Text: Verdana 12-pt font, justified paragraphs. 4. The title and subtitle shall not exceed 15 words together. They must be brief, but clearly inform the main contents of the study; besides, an English version",marcadores,request editorial committee editorial must,length 250 word maximum paper length 6000 word maximum num ber referenc 80 literature review these must submitt only expert topic address if request directly editorial committee case report these paper intend report one more case consider have special interest author type paper must also include brief review relevant literature case report peer review least one external peer review maximum abstract length 250 word maximum paper length 3500 word maximum number referenc 40 resident section section gastroenterology relat specialti fellow can openly submit origi nal review articl perform alone together their professor these articl peer review external peer letter editor these brief comment paper publish journal editorial committee responsible decid publica tion letter editor colombian journal gastroenterology accept sub mission scientific articl conform follow editorial guidelin non-compliance them shall cause rejection all work submitt journal must original unpublish paper have been already publish will not accept sense articl partially subs tantially reproduce work have been publish even other languag shall not submitt plagiarism detec tion tool used editorial review proces author author name order which they appear must carefully review before making sub mission so they record correctly website chang involv addition removal rearrangement author must done before paper accept publication prior approval editor journal author identify information must includ only submission made through ojs website journal should not includ file contain article peer review also orcid id code all author must includ s