0121-3814,Ted+59+Art.+22993.pdf,Ted+59+Art.+22993_0,en,ieron evaluar el desempeño de los estudiantes en habilidades científicas,"Science, with its empirical, theoretical, and methodological approach, has long been essential for generating knowledge, enabling the understanding of phenomena and the resolution of problems through the formulation of hypotheses, theories, and laws. In this context, the main objective of this study was to develop scientific thinking skills in Year 11 students at the Institución Educativa Agropecuaria El Ejido, in Policarpa (Nariño), using a School Technological Activity (sta) focused on optimising water resources. The research adopted a qualitative action–participation approach and involved the administration of a diagnostic test, the design and implementation of the sta, continuous monitoring through a field journal, and a post-test assessment. These procedures made it possible to evaluate students’ performance in key scientific skills such as observing, measuring, inferring, predicting, and experimenting. The results indicate that the sta proved to be an effective didactic strategy for improving students’ scientific skills, enhancing their development, and strengthening their ability to address issues related to water resource optimisation. It is concluded that the sta is a relevant educational strategy for promoting problem-solving, environmental engagement, teamwork, and a sense of belonging in rural education contexts",scientific skills; school technological activity; water resources; rural education; secondary education,marcadores,ieron evaluar el desempeno de los estudiant en habilidad cientifica,science its empirical theoretical methodological approach has long been essential generat knowledge enabl understand phenomena resolution problem through formulation hypothes theori laws context main objective study develop scientific think skill year 11 student institucion educativa agropecuaria el ejido policarpa narino using school technological activity sta focus optimis water resourc research adopt qualitative action-participation approach involv administration diagnostic test design implementation sta continuou monitor through field journal post-test assessment these procedur made possible evaluate student performance key scientific skill such observ measur inferr predict experiment result indicate sta prov effective didactic strategy improv student scientific skill enhanc their development strengthen their ability addres issu relat water resource optimisation conclud sta relevant educational strategy promot problem-solv environmental engagement teamwork sense belong rural education context,scientific skill school technological activity water resourc rural education secondary education,ieron evaluar el desempeno de los estudiant en habilidad cientifica science its empirical theoretical methodological approach has long been essential generat knowledge enabl understand phenomena resolution problem through formulation hypothes theori laws context main objective study develop scientific think skill year 11 student institucion educativa agropecuaria el ejido policarpa narino using school technological activity sta focus optimis water resourc research adopt qualitative action-participation approach involv administration diagnostic test design implementation sta continuou monitor through field journal post-test assessment these procedur made possible evaluate student performance key scientific skill such observ measur inferr predict experiment result indicate sta prov effective didactic strategy improv student scientific skill enhanc their development strengthen their ability addres issu relat water resource optimisation conclud sta relevant educational strategy promot problem-solv environmental engagement teamwork sense belong rural education context scientific skill school technological activity water resourc rural education secondary education,1.0.0,8d943ff0a7914869
0121-3814,Ted+59+Art.+23023.pdf,Ted+59+Art.+23023_0,es,"Fundación Universitaria Juan de Castellanos. Docente,","En este artículo se presentan los resultados de una investigación en donde se describen los cambios en las construcciones explicativas (escritas) de un grupo de estudiantes de 9º de secundaria sobre fenómenos relacionados con genética molecular, luego de la implementación de una unidad didáctica mediada por el modelo de aprendizaje basado en problemas (abp). La metodología cualitativa de alcance descriptivo se abordó desde la estructuración de niveles de desem peño explicativo sobre conceptos de genética molecular que comprendió la adaptación de la rúbrica propuesta por pisa (2015), que establece el índice de rendimiento para la competencia ‘explicación de fenómenos científicamente’. Se aplicaron dos instrumentos para la recolección de datos y su triangulación: un cuestionario abierto que planteaba situaciones relacionadas con fenómenos sobre genética molecular, antes y después de la intervención didáctica para identificar los niveles de desempeño explicativo, y una entrevista semiestruc turada que permitió conocer los aportes que dejó la intervención desde la 191 No 59 • Primer semestre de 2026 • pp. 190- 207 ISSN 2665-3184 impreso • ISSN 2323-0126 Web TED perspectiva de los estudiantes participantes. En la evidencia recuperada se puede apreciar que algunos estudiantes mejoraron la habilidad para construir explicaciones científicas, a su vez que incorporan conocimientos nuevos acerca del modelo biomolecular en genética",aprendizaje basado en problemas; competencia científica; genética molecular; niveles de des empeño explicativo,marcadores,fundacion universitaria juan castellan docente,este articulo presentan resultad investigacion donde describen cambi construccion explicativ escrit grupo estudiant 9o secundaria sobre fenomen relacionad genetica molecular luego implementacion unidad didactica mediada modelo aprendizaje basado problem abp metodologia cual