0121-747X,Art1V15N2-8-25.pdf,Art1V15N2-8-25_0,en,RESEARCH TRENDS AND HOTSPOTS RELATED TO NITROGEN,"Simulation models are tools that allow the representation of systems and the evaluation of scenarios, supporting decision-making in crop management. This study systematically identified the knowledge base, recent advances, and research gaps modeling in agricultural systems, with an emphasis on coffee crops. A bibliometric analysis was conducted using data from the ISI Web of Science database for the period 2017–2025, analyzed with VOSviewer software. A total of 640 publications were identified after removing duplicates and refining the dataset","co-occurrence analysis made it possible to identify the main research trends and thematic areas. The results show a growing trend in scientific production, with the United States leading in the number of publications and the Chinese Academy of Sciences as the most active institution. Nitrogen models have been predominantly applied to crops such as maize and wheat, while their application to coffee",marcadores,research trend hotspot relat nitrogen,simulation model tool allow representation system evaluation scenario support decision-mak crop management study systematically identifi knowledge base recent advanc research gaps model agricultural system emphasi coffee crop bibliometric analysi conduct using data isi web science database period 2017-2025 analyz vosviewer software total 640 public identifi after remov duplicat refin dataset,co-occurrence analysi made possible identify main research trend thematic area result show grow trend scientific production unit stat lead number public chinese academy scienc most active institution nitrogen model have been predominantly appli crop such maize wheat while their application coffee,research trend hotspot relat nitrogen simulation model tool allow representation system evaluation scenario support decision-mak crop management study systematically identifi knowledge base recent advanc r