0121-747X,Art4V15N2-65-75.pdf,Art4V15N2-65-75_0,es,EFECTO ESTIMULANTE DEL QUITOMAX® EN LA PRODUCCIÓN DE,"El Quitomax® “cuyo compuesto activo principal es una mezcla de polímeros de quitosano” es un bioestimulante de origen natural que beneficia el desarrollo de los cultivos y activa la respuesta antiestrés en las plantas. El objetivo del trabajo fue evaluar bajas dosis (300, 400, 500 mg ha−1) de quitosano aplicado a los 28 días después de la siembra en semilleros de tabaco en bandejas aéreas. Se empleó la variedad comercial ‘Corojo 2012’ y se aplicaron cuatro tratamientos por aspersión foliar que se distribuyeron en un diseño de Bloques al Azar con tres réplicas. Se evaluaron indicadores morfo-agronómicos de crecimiento en el momento del trasplante. Las tres dosis de Quitomax® empleadas favorecieron el crecimiento de las plántulas y la proporción de plantas útiles para el trasplante respecto al control. Estos resultados demuestran que es posible emplear el bioestimulante Quitomax®, con dosis entre 300 y 500 mg ha−1, para incrementar la productividad y la calidad de las plántulas de tabaco en semilleros en bandejas aéreas",Bioestimulante; quitosano; Quitomax® Nicotiana tabacum L.; semilleros,marcadores,efecto estimulante quitomax produccion,quitomax cuyo compuesto activo principal mezcla polimer quitosano bioestimulante origen natural beneficia desarrollo cultiv activa respuesta antiestr plant objetivo trabajo fue evaluar bajas dosis 300 400 500 mg ha-1 quitosano aplicado 28 dias despu siembra semiller tabaco bandej aere empleo variedad comercial corojo 2012 aplicaron cuatro trat aspersion foliar distribuyeron diseno bloqu azar tres replic evaluaron indicador morfo-agronomic crecimiento momento trasplante tres dosis quitomax emplead favorecieron crecimiento plantul proporcion plant util trasplante respecto control estos resultad demuestran posible emplear bioestimulante quitomax dosis entre 300 500 mg ha-1 incrementar productividad calidad plantul tabaco semiller bandej aere,bioestimulante quitosano quitomax nicotiana tabacum semiller,efecto estimulante quitomax produccion quitomax cuyo compuesto activo principal mezcla polimer quitosano bioestimulante origen natural beneficia desarrollo cultiv activa respuesta antiestr plant objetivo trabajo fue evaluar bajas dosis 300 400 500 mg ha-1 quitosano aplicado 28 dias despu siembra semiller tabaco bandej aere empleo variedad comercial corojo 2012 aplicaron cuatro trat aspersion foliar distribuyeron diseno bloqu azar tres replic evaluaron indicador morfo-agronomic crecimiento momento trasplante tres dosis quitomax emplead favorecieron crecimiento plantul proporcion plant util trasplante respecto control estos resultad demuestran posible emplear bioestimulante quitomax dosis entre 300 500 mg ha-1 incrementar productividad calidad plantul tabaco semiller bandej aere bioestimulante quitosano quitomax nicotiana tabacum semiller,1.0.0,1836160b1817acd9
0121-747X,Art4V15N2-65-75.pdf,Art4V15N2-65-75_0,en,la siembra en semilleros de tabaco en bandejas aéreas. Se empleó la variedad comercial ‘Corojo 2012’ y se aplicaron,"Quitomax® whose main active compound is a mixture of chitosan polymers is a natural origin biostimulant that benefits the crops development and activates plant anti-stress responses. The objective of the work was to evaluate low doses (300, 400, 500 mg ha−1) of chitosan applied 28 days after sowing in nursery tobacco seedlings in aerial trays. ‘Corojo 2012’ commercial variety was used and four treatments distributed in a Random Block design with three replications were applied by foliar spray. Morpho-agronomic growth indicators were evaluated at transplantation. All three Quitomax® doses favored the seedlings growth and the plants rate useful for transplanting compared to control. Results demonstrate that Quitomax® biostimulant, with doses between 300 and 500 mg ha−1, can be used to increase productivity and quality of tobacco seedlings in aerial tray seedbeds","Biostimulant; chitosan; Quitomax®; Nicotiana tabacum L.; seedlings. aGonzález Sotolongo, J. C., León González, Y., Falcón Rodríguez, A. B. & Reyes Pozo, J. L. (2026). Efecto estimulante del QUITOMAX® en la producción de plántulas de tabaco en bandejas aéreas. Rev. Fac. Cienc., 15 (2), 65–75. DOI: https://doi.org/10.15446/rev.fac.cienc.v15n2.123154 bEstación Experimental del Tabaco de San Juan y M",marcadores,la siembra en semillero de tabaco en bandeja aerea se empleo la variedad comercial corojo 2012 se aplicaron,quitomax whose main active compound mixture chitosan polymer natural origin biostimulant benefit crop development activat plant anti-stres respons objective work evaluate low dose 300 400 500 mg ha-1 chitosan appli 28 days after sowing nursery tobacco seedling aerial tray corojo 2012 commercial variety used four treatment distribut random block design three replic appli foliar spray morpho-agronomic growth indicator evaluat transplantation all three quitomax dose favor seedling growth plant rate useful transplant compar control result demonstrate quitomax biostimulant dose between 300 500 mg ha-1 can used increase productivity quality tobacco seedling aerial tray seedbed,biostimulant chitosan quitomax nicotiana tabacum seedling agonzalez sotolongo leon gonzalez falcon rodriguez reye pozo 2026 efecto estimulante del quitomax en la produccion de plantula de tabaco en bandeja aerea rev fac cienc 15 65-75 doi http doi org 10 15446 rev fac cienc v15n2 123154 bestacion experimental del tabaco de san juan,la siembra en semillero de tabaco en bandeja aerea se empleo la variedad comercial corojo 2012 se aplicaron quitomax whose main active compound mixture chitosan polymer natural origin biostimulant benefit crop development activat plant anti-stres respons objective work evaluate low dose 300 400 500 mg ha-1 chitosan appli 28 days after sowing nursery tobacco seedling aerial tray corojo 2012 commercial variety used four treatment distribut random block design three replic appli foliar spray morpho-agronomic growth indicator evaluat transplantation all three quitomax dose favor seedling growth plant rate useful transplant compar control result demonstrate quitomax biostimulant dose between 300 500 mg ha-1 can used increase productivity quality tobacco seedling aerial tray seedbed biostimulant chitosan quitomax nicotiana tabacum seedling agonzalez sotolongo leon gonzalez falcon rodriguez reye pozo 2026 efecto estimulante del quitomax en la produccion de plantula de tabaco en bandeja aerea rev fac cienc 15 65-75 doi http doi org 10 15446 rev fac cienc v15n2 123154 bestacion experimental del tabaco de san juan,1.0.0,aa8b0c94fa021a08
0121-747X,Art5V15N2-76-84.pdf,Art5V15N2-76-84_0,en,ANALYSIS OF IRON CONCENTRATION IN SOME TISSUES: A,"Background: Although iron is essential for many physiological and biological functions, increased iron levels in malignant tissues may be linked to more rapid tumor growth and colonization. Objective: The purpose of this study was to compare the iron levels in tumor and non-tumor tissues and assess how they relate to the size and stage of the tumor. Methodology: Following chemical analysis, tissue samples were obtained from individuals with malignant tumors from a number of hospitals in the Dhi Qar Governorate. ICP-MS analysis was performed on the samples, and standard measurement formulae were developed to guarantee accuracy. Following sample classification, the data was examined using a t-test and Pearson statistical analysis, with a significance level of p < 0.05. Findings: There was a definite relationship between iron levels and tumor development. When compared to unaffected tissues, the values in damaged tissues were noticeably greater. Additionally, compared to early tumors, the concentrations were greater in advanced cancers. In conclusion, iron has a role in fostering an atmosphere that supports the formation of tumors. Iron management techniques should thus be investigated as a possible treatment component, particularly in high-risk locations. aMathloom, Ahmed R., Nazal, Ferial Y. & Kadhem, Sana Thamer & Alhusseinawi, Nooralhuda Kareem Hanoon (2026). Analysis of iron concentration in some tissues: a comparative study using sensitive analysis techniques and evaluation of the effect of iron on tumor colonization. Rev. Fac. Cienc., 15 (2), 76–84. DOI: https://doi.org/10.15446/rev.fac.cienc.v15n2.125288 bDepartment of Physics, College of Education for Pure Sciences, University of Thi-Qar, Thi-Qar 64001, Iraq. ahmedrasool30.eps@utq.edu.iq *Corresponding author: ahmedrasool30.eps@utq.edu.iq cCollege of Medicine, Department of Medical Physics & Physiology, University of Thi-Qar, Thi-Qar 64001, Iraq. ferialy@utq.edu.iq dsana_t@utq.edu.iq enoor-alhuda-k@utq.edu.iq 76 ANALYSIS OF IRON CONCENTRATION IN SOME TISSUES: A COMPARATIVE STUDY USING SENSITIVE ANALYSIS TECHNIQUES AND EVALUATION OF THE EFFECT OF IRON ON TUMOR COLONIZATION",Heavy Metals; Iron; cancer; Breast; colon; lung; ICP MS,marcadores,analysi iron concentration some tissu,background although iron essential many physiological biological function increas iron level malignant tissu may link more rapid tumor growth colon objective purpose study compare iron level tumor non-tumor tissu asses how they relate size stage tumor methodology follow chemical analysi tissue sampl obtain individual malignant tumor number hospital dhi qar governorate icp-m analysi perform sampl standard measurement formulae develop guarantee accuracy follow sample classification data examin using t-test pearson statistical analysi significance level 05 finding there definite relationship between iron level tumor development when compar unaffect tissu valu damag tissu noticeably greater additionally compar early tumor concentr greater advanc cancer conclusion iron has role foster atmosphere support formation tumor iron management techniqu should thus investigat possible treatment component particularly high-risk location amathloom ahmed nazal ferial kadhem sana thamer alhusseinawi nooralhuda kareem hanoon 2026 analysi iron concentration some tissu comparative study using sensitive analysi techniqu evaluation effect iron tumor colon rev fac cienc 15 76-84 doi http doi org 10 15446 rev fac cienc v15n2 125288 bdepartment physic college education pure scienc university thi-qar thi-qar 64001 iraq ahmedrasool30 eps utq edu iq correspond author ahmedrasool30 eps utq edu iq ccollege medicine department medical physic physiology university thi-qar thi-qar 64001 iraq ferialy utq edu iq dsana_t utq edu iq enoor-alhuda-k utq edu iq 76 analysi iron concentration some tissu comparative study using sensitive analy