0122-5197,"ananoguera17,+2.2+Mora.pdf","ananoguera17,+2.2+Mora_0",en,Indústria da memória coletiva. Apontamentos para a sistematização de um conceito,"This article seeks to address the prob lems and effects derived from the media tization of collective memories, especially when considering the power relations in volved in mass media structures, in par ticular the television industry. Here, the events occurred after a series of TV docu mentaries were aired in 2013 on the occa sion of the 40th anniversary of the Chilean coup d’état were selected to contribute to the systematization of the concept of in dustry of the memory",television; collective memory; cultural in dustry of collective memory; hegemony; dis course; modeling,marcadores,industria da memoria coletiva apontamento para sistematizacao de um conceito,article seek addres prob lems effect deriv media tization collective memori especially when consider power relation volv mass media structur par ticular television industry here event occurr after seri tv docu mentari aired 2013 occa sion 40th anniversary chilean coup etat select contribute systemat concept dustry memory,television collective memory cultural dustry collective memory hegemony dis course model,industria da memoria coletiva apontamento para sistematizacao de um conceito article seek addres prob lems effect deriv media tization collective memori especially when consider power relation volv mass media structur par ticular television industry here event occurr after seri tv docu mentari aired 2013 occa sion 40th anniversary chilean coup etat select contribute systemat concept dustry memory television collective memory cultural dustry collective memory hegemony dis course model,1.0.0,3d7d6fbcbcc76455
0122-5197,"ananoguera17,+2.3+Bonvini.pdf","ananoguera17,+2.3+Bonvini_0",es,La Battaglia di Sant’Antonio,"Entre 1835 y 1848, decenas de exiliados del movimiento mazziniano salieron de la penín sula italiana para instalarse en Uruguay. Desde Montevideo continuaron su lucha política fun dando nuevos periódicos, estableciendo alianzas con otros grupos de la diáspora republicana y formando fuerzas militares que tomaron parte en los conflictos locales. El exilio en tierra rio platense fue una experiencia fundamental para la reactivación de la Joven Italia y el desarrollo del republicanismo en el mundo atlántico, pues creó nuevas conexiones políticas entre el Viejo Continente y el Nuevo Mundo",Giuseppe Mazzini; historia atlántica; republi canismo; Generación del 37; Legión Italiana,marcadores,battaglia di sant antonio,entre 1835 1848 decen exiliad movimiento mazziniano salieron penin sula italiana instalarse uruguay desde montevideo continuaron lucha politica fun dando nuev periodic establec alianz otros grup diaspora republicana form fuerz militar tomaron parte conflict local exilio tierra rio platense fue experiencia fundamental reactivacion joven italia desarrollo republicanismo mundo atlantico pues creo nuev conexion politic entre viejo continente nuevo mundo,giuseppe mazzini historia atlantica republi canismo generacion 37 legion italiana,battaglia di sant antonio entre 1835 1848 decen exiliad movimiento mazziniano salieron penin sula italiana instalarse uruguay desde montevideo continuaron lucha politica fun dando nuev periodic establec alianz otros grup diaspora republicana form fuerz militar tomaron parte conflict local exilio tierra rio platense fue experiencia fundamental reactivacion joven italia desarrollo republicanismo mundo atlantico pues creo nuev conexion politic entre viejo continente nuevo mundo giuseppe mazzini historia atlantica republi canismo generacion 37 legion italiana,1.0.0,c16e22a952e98115
0122-5197,"ananoguera17,+2.3+Bonvini.pdf","ananoguera17,+2.3+Bonvini_0",en,the Risorgimento. Mazzinianism in the Southern Cone,"Between 1835 and 1848, tens of exiles from the Mazzinian movement left the Italian Pen insula to settle in Uruguay. From Montevi deo, they continued their political struggle by founding new newspapers, establishing alli ances with other diaspora communities and building military forces, which took part in local conflicts. In this way, exile was a funda mental experience for the revival of a Young Italy in the Rio de la Plata area, the develop ment of republicanism in the Atlantic world and the creation of new connections between the Old Continent and America",Giuseppe Mazzini; Atlantic History; Republi canism; Generation of 37; Italian Legion,marcadores,risorgimento mazzinianism southern cone,between 1835 1848 tens exil mazzinian movement left italian pen insula settle uruguay montevi deo they continu their political struggle found new newspaper establish alli ance other diaspora communiti build military forc which took part local conflict way exile funda mental experience revival young italy rio de la plata area develop ment republicanism atlantic world creation new connection between old continent america,giuseppe mazzini atlantic history republi canism generation 37 italian legion,risorgimento mazzinianism southern cone between 1835 1848 tens exil mazzinian movement left italian pen insula settle uruguay montevi deo they continu their political struggle found new newspaper establish alli ance other diaspora communiti build military forc which took part local conflict way exile funda mental experience revival young italy rio de la plata area develop ment republicanism atlantic world creation new connection between old continent america giuseppe mazzini atlantic history republi canism generation 37 italian legion,1.0.0,277e3c1c98c291cd
0122-5197,"ananoguera17,+2.4+Rodríguez.pdf","ananoguera17,+2.4+Rodríguez_0",es,"La sepultura de un guerrillero, de Alberto Urdaneta, grabado de Greñas y Rodríguez","Este trabajo se ocupa de la triple relación en tre cultura visual, guerras civiles y proyecto na ción en el periodo comprendido entre 1871 y 1885 del siglo XIX colombiano, en clave de lo que implica una cierta circulación de objetos y modos de representación visual comunes tanto en Europa como en América. Metodológica mente, a través del trabajo de archivo se ana liza la cultura visual en medio de los grandes conflictos civiles y los proyectos de nación. En esta línea, la producción de imágenes que tuvo lugar en este tiempo revela: 1) una cierta lógica de la promoción nacional que hace visibles sus contradicciones; 2) la formación de una cul tura visual que se lee en clave internacional, y, 3) el imaginario del tiempo nacional en el que se imposta un futuro desde un pasado común, al tiempo que este mismo se pone en cuestión por las diferencias que comportan los distintos conflictos civiles",Cultura visual; guerras civiles; proyecto nación; cosmopolitismo,marcadores,sepultura guerrillero alberto urdaneta grabado gren rodriguez,este trabajo ocupa triple relacion tre cultura visual guerr civil proyecto na cion periodo comprendido entre 1871 1885 siglo xix colombiano clave implica cierta circulacion objet modos representacion visual comun tanto europa como america metodologica mente trav trabajo archivo ana liza cultura visual medio grand conflict civil proyect nacion esta linea produccion imagen tuvo lugar este tiempo revela cierta logica promocion nacional hace visibl sus contradiccion formacion cul tura visual lee clave internacional imaginario tiempo nacional imposta futuro desde pasado comun tiempo este mismo pone cuestion diferenci comportan distint conflict civil,cultura visual guerr civil proyecto nacion cosmopolitismo,sepultura guerrillero alberto urdaneta grabado gren rodriguez este trabajo ocupa triple relacion tre cultura visual guerr civil proyecto na cion periodo comprendido entre 1871 1885 siglo xix colombiano clave implica cierta circulacion objet modos representacion visual comun tanto europa como america metodologica mente trav trabajo archivo ana liza cultura visual medio grand conflict civil proyect nacion esta linea produccion imagen tuvo lugar este tiempo revela cierta logica promocion nacional hace visibl sus contradiccion formacion cul tura visual lee clave internacional imaginario tiempo nacional imposta futuro desde pasado comun tiempo este mismo pone cuestion diferenci comportan distint conflict civil cultura visual guerr civil proyecto nacion cosmopolitismo,1.0.0,cffcb1436c1ccec8
0122-5197,"ananoguera17,+2.4+Rodríguez.pdf","ananoguera17,+2.4+Rodríguez_0",en,en el periodo comprendido entre 1871 y,"This article focuses on the tripled relation among visual culture, civil wars and natio nal plan of the period from 1871 and 1885 in the Colombian twenty century; this im plies a certain circulation of objects and types of visual illustration common both in Euro pe and America. The aim is to examine the visual culture in the middle of big civil con flicts and the national promotion, on the ba sis that the production of images, in this time, reveal: 1) a specific logic about national pro motion and a reflection which became visi ble its contradictions; 2) the configuration of a visual culture that it’s possible to unders tand since international clue and 3) it beco mes apparent the comprehension of national time where is strengthened a future since the common past, at the same time it is questio ned, since the present characterized by the di fferences which imply the civil wars",Visual culture; Civil wars; National plan; Cosmopolitanism,marcadores,en el periodo comprendido entre 1871,article focus tripl relation among visual culture civil wars natio nal plan period 1871 1885 colombian twenty century im plie certain circulation object type visual illustration common both euro pe america aim examine visual culture middle big civil con flict national promotion ba sis production imag time reveal specific logic about national pro motion reflection which became visi ble its contradiction configuration visual culture possible under tand since international clue beco mes apparent comprehension national time where strengthen future since common past same time questio ned since present characteriz di fferenc which imply civil wars,visual culture civil wars national plan cosmopolitanism,en el periodo comprendido entre 1871 article focus tripl relation among visual culture civil wars natio nal plan period 1871 1885 colombian twenty century im plie certain circulation object type visual illustration common both euro pe america aim examine visual culture middle big civil con flict national promotion ba sis production imag time reveal specific logic about national pro motion reflection which became visi ble its contradiction configuration visual culture possible under tand since international clue beco mes apparent comprehension national time where strengthen future since common past same time questio ned since present characteriz di fferenc which imply civil wars visual culture civil wars national plan cosmopolitanism,1.0.0,d30e2354e3ba51c8
0122-5197,"ananoguera17,+2.5+Zarama.pdf","ananoguera17,+2.5+Zarama_0",es,Primer folio del libro que contiene la cuenta general de la Administración de,"Este artículo es una contribución a las investi gaciones en torno a la participación de las mu jeres en la guerra de Independencia. El objetivo es analizar la posición realista de las religiosas conceptas de Pasto (Colombia) y explicar las manifestaciones de esa adherencia. Ese com promiso político se extendió a lo largo de doce años (1812-1824), sin embargo, adquirió ma yor relevancia en los dos últimos años de la contienda. La derrota de sus aliados las obli gó a aceptar el nuevo gobierno, pero no salie ron ilesas del conflicto: resultaron derrotadas políticamente y sus bienes fueron saqueados",independencia; Pasto; conceptas; participación política y mujer,marcadores,primer folio libro contiene cuenta general administracion,este articulo contribucion investi gacion torno participacion mu jeres guerra independencia objetivo analizar posicion realista religios concept pasto colombia explicar manifest esa adherencia ese com promiso politico extendio largo doce anos 1812-1824 sin embargo adquirio ma yor relevancia dos ultim anos contienda derrota sus aliad obli go aceptar nuevo gobierno pero no salie ron iles conflicto resultaron derrotad politica sus bien fueron saquead,independencia pasto concept participacion politica mujer,primer folio libro contiene cuenta general administracion este articulo contribucion investi gacion torno participacion mu jeres guerra independencia objetivo analizar posicion realista religios concept pasto colombia explicar manifest esa adherencia ese com promiso politico extendio largo doce anos 1812-1824 sin embargo adquirio ma yor relevancia dos ultim anos contienda derrota sus aliad obli go aceptar nuevo gobierno pero no salie ron iles conflicto resultaron derrotad politica sus bien fueron saquead independencia pasto concept participacion politica mujer,1.0.0,6d86588c66c90496
0122-5197,"ananoguera17,+2.5+Zarama.pdf","ananoguera17,+2.5+Zarama_0",en,Conceição de Pasto «Conceptas de Pasto» defensoras da justa causa,"This article refers to the women’s participation in the War of Independence. The aim is to an alyze the realistic position of the Conceptas of Pasto, a religious congregation in Colom bia, in order to explain their participation in the political scene of that time. Their commit ment lasted over twelve years (1812-1824), but it was during the last two years of war where it became particularly relevant. Also, while the defeat of their allies forced them to accept the new government, they were not unscathed from the conflict: they were politically defeat ed, and their properties were looted",independency; Pasto; conceptas; political par ticipation and woman,marcadores,conceicao de pasto concepta de pasto defensora da justa causa,article refer women participation war independence aim alyze realistic position concepta pasto religiou congregation colom bia order explain their participation political scene time their commit ment last over twelve year 1812-1824 but during last two year war where became particularly relevant also while defeat their alli forc them accept new government they not unscath conflict they politically defeat ed their properti loot,independency pasto concepta political par ticipation woman,conceicao de pasto concepta de pasto defensora da justa causa article refer women participation war independence aim alyze realistic position concepta pasto religiou congregation colom bia order explain their participation political scene time their commit ment last over twelve year 1812-1824 but during last two year war where became particularly relevant also while defeat their alli forc them accept new government they not unscath conflict they politically defeat ed their properti loot independency pasto concepta political par ticipation woman,1.0.0,f7fbf97bd3322395
0122-5197,"ananoguera17,+2.6+Mansilla,+Muñoz,+Piñones.pdf","ananoguera17,+2.6+Mansilla,+Muñoz,+Piñones_0",es,Memoria de un olvido. La exclusión de mujeres de la memoria fundacional del,"Las reconstrucciones que la historia apologé tica pentecostal, la teología y las ciencias so ciales han realizado sobre los orígenes del pentecostalismo chileno, se caracterizan por una limitación significativa: la elaboración de una imagen negativa o el olvido de las mujeres de su memoria fundacional. El objetivo de este artículo es describir y analizar este fenómeno. A partir del análisis de fuentes primarias y se cundarias, mostraremos que este olvido y difa mación de la imagen femenina no se debe solo a una limitación metodológico-epistemológi ca, sino que obedece a una estrategia de poder liderada por pastores posicionados en los cen tros hegemónicos del pentecostalismo chileno",memoria; exclusión; poder; mujeres; pentecos talismo; Chile,marcadores,memoria olvido exclusion mujer memoria fundacional,reconstruccion historia apologe tica pentecostal teologia cienci so cial han realizado sobre origen pentecostalismo chileno caracterizan limitacion significativa elaboracion imagen negativa olvido mujer memoria fundacional objetivo este articulo describir analizar este fenomeno partir analisis fuent primari cundari mostrarem este olvido difa macion imagen femenina no debe solo limitacion metodologico-epistemologi ca sino obedece estrategia poder liderada pastor posicionad cen tros hegemonic pentecostalismo chileno,memoria exclusion poder mujer pentec talismo chile,memoria olvido exclusion mujer memoria fundacional reconstruccion historia apologe tica pentecostal teologia cienci so cial han realizado sobre origen pentecostalismo chileno caracterizan limitacion significativa elaboracion imagen negativa olvido mujer memoria fundacional objetivo este articulo describir analizar este fenomeno partir analisis fuent primari cundari mostrarem este olvido difa macion imagen femenina no debe solo limitacion metodologico-epistemologi ca sino obedece estrategia poder liderada pastor posicionad cen tros hegemonic pentecostalismo chileno memoria exclusion poder mujer pentec talismo chile,1.0.0,896205f9ffd31864
0122-5197,"ananoguera17,+2.6+Mansilla,+Muñoz,+Piñones.pdf","ananoguera17,+2.6+Mansilla,+Muñoz,+Piñones_0",en,aña); Laboratoire d’Anthropologie,"The reconstructions on the origins of Chil ean Pentecostalism delivered by the Pentecos tal apologetics, theology and social sciences are characterized by a significant limitation: the construction of a negative image or the exclu sion of women in the movement´s foundation al memory. This article aims to describe and analyze this phenomenon. Based on the analy sis of primary and secondary sources, it will be shown that the exclusion and the defamation of the female image is not only due to a meth odological and epistemological limitation, but also to a power strategy lead by pastors posi tioned in the hegemonic centers of Chilean Pentecostalism",memory; exclusion; power; women; Pentecos talism; Chile,marcadores,ana laboratoire anthropologie,reconstruction origin chil ean pentecostalism deliver penteco tal apologetic theology social scienc characteriz significant limitation construction negative image exclu sion women movement foundation al memory article aims describe analyze phenomenon based analy sis primary secondary sourc will shown exclusion defamation female image not only due meth odological epistemological limitation but also power strategy lead pastor posi tion hegemonic center chilean pentecostalism,memory exclusion power women penteco talism chile,ana laboratoire anthropologie reconstruction origin chil ean pentecostalism deliver penteco tal apologetic theology social scienc characteriz significant limitation construction negative image exclu sion women movement foundation al memory article aims describe analyze phenomenon based analy sis primary secondary sourc will shown exclusion defamation female image not only due meth odological epistemological limitation but also power strategy lead pastor posi tion hegemonic center chilean pentecostalism memory exclusion power women penteco talism chile,1.0.0,de04759c77c6cf47
0122-7483,Art-890_Ajem.pdf,Art-890_Ajem_0,en,ORIGINAL ARTICLE,"Colombia is the second country with the highest number of Amerindian ethnic groups, with autonomy and self-governance, allowing them to preserve their culture and Amerindian genetic heritage. In some of these communities, studies using markers such as mitochondrial DNA (mtDNA), the non-recombining region of the Y chromosome (NRY), and Ancestry Informative Markers (AIMs) have helped clarify the settlement processes and genetic admixture of these populations. In this study, we analyzed genome-wide Single Nucleotide Polymorphism (SNP) data from four indigenous populations of Colombia, the Wayuu, Nasa-Páez, Pijao, and Embera-Kátio, genotyped on the Axiom SpainBA panel. We were interested in determining the genetic ancestry and structure, as well as patterns of genetic variation in these populations. We collected personal questionnaires to determine family relationships and included only unrelated individuals for further analyses. Population genetic analyses, including other Native and non-Indigenous American populations, showed genetic affinities to other Indigenous American populations and varied levels of genetic admixture with non-American sources. Furthermore, our analyses suggest that distinct demographic histories, including isolation, genetic drift associated with reduced effective population size (Ne), and admixture, have shaped patterns of genetic variation and population structure among Colombian Indigenous populations","Ancestry; Colombian ethnic groups; Population structure; Array, Variability; Genetic dynamics. 1",marcadores,original article,colombia second country highest number amerindian ethnic group autonomy self-governance allow them preserve their culture amerindian genetic heritage some these communiti studi using marker such mitochondrial dna mtdna non-recombin region chromosome nry ancestry informative marker aims have help clarify settlement process genetic admixture these popul study 