0123-4471,Virajes+28(1)_8.pdf,Virajes+28(1)_8_0,en,Oliver Duarte-Herrera,"In 1992, the UNESCO World Heritage Convention pioneered the recognition and protection of cultural landscapes, defined as the joint work of nature and humankind. The region of La Serena (Badajoz, Spain) is an example of this balance between human communities and their natural environment. For approximately five millennia, its inhabitants have exploited the environment in a sustainable manner, developing an economy based on the breeding of Merino sheep, from which they obtain milk, meat, and wool. This activity has generated a network of occupations that includes breeding and grazing, wool production, and the manufacture of renowned cheeses. Methodologically, the study is based on ethnographic research combining participant observation, semi-structured interviews, focus groups and documentary analysis, carried out in the nineteen municipalities of the region between 2021 and 2022. The article analyses the contradictions present in the economic and cultural policies affecting this ancient cultural landscape and demonstrates how the merinocracy shapes a socio-productive system in which sheep farming, artisanal cheese-making, wool processing and related trades constitute an intangible cultural heritage that is at odds with institutional agendas. It concludes by highlighting the need to strengthen community and institutional participation in order to minimise these tensions and ensure the sustainability of this heritage","Extremadura, merinocracy, cultural landscape, grazing, intangible heritage",marcadores,oliver duarte-herrera,1992 unesco world heritage convention pioneer recognition protection cultural landscap defin joint work nature humankind region la serena badajoz spain example balance between human communiti their natural environment approximately five millennia its inhabitant have exploit environment sustainable manner develop economy based breed merino sheep which they obtain milk meat wool activity has generat network occup includ breed graz wool production manufacture renown chees methodologically study based ethnographic research combin participant observation semi-structur interview focu group documentary analysi carri out nineteen municipaliti region between 2021 2022 article analys contradiction present economic cultural polici affect ancient cultural landscape demonstrat how merinocracy shap socio-productive system which sheep farm artisanal cheese-mak wool process relat trad constitute intangible cultural heritage odds institutional agenda conclud highlight need strengthen community institutional participation order minimise these tension ensure sustainability heritage,extremadura merinocracy cultural landscape graz intangible heritage,oliver duarte-herrera 1992 unesco world heritage convention pioneer recognition protection cultural landscap defin joint work nature humankind region la serena badajoz spain example balance between human communiti their natural environment approximately five millennia its inhabitant have exploit environment sustainable manner develop economy based breed merino sheep which they obtain milk meat wool activity has generat network occup includ breed graz wool production manufacture renown chees methodologically study based ethnographic research combin participant observation semi-structur interview focu group documentary analysi carri out nineteen municipaliti region between 2021 2022 article analys contradiction present economic cultural polici affect ancient cultural landscape demonstrat how merinocracy shap socio-productive system which sheep farm artisanal cheese-mak wool process relat trad constitute intangible cultural heritage odds institutional agenda conclud highlight need strengthen community institutional participation order minimise these tension ensure sustainability heritage extremadura merinocracy cultural landscape graz intangible heritage,1.0.0,3d2e9e07b1b1b8fb
0123-4641,22952+V28_N1_Art5_22952+RV1.pdf,22952+V28_N1_Art5_22952+RV1_0,en,Colomb. Appl. Linguist. J.,"Educational institutions use response-to-intervention (RtI) to identify, support, and monitor students with poor academic or behavioral performance. In this qualitative descriptive case study, the problem was students’ poor English reading performance at an international school in northern China. The purpose was to explore teachers’ perceptions of the influence of a one-month, two-tier response-to-intervention pilot on students’ English reading proficiency in a content and language integrated learning (CLIL)-oriented primary school in northern China, with Tier 1 comprising whole-class supports and Tier 2 targeted small-group work. This study aimed to address a specific gap by implementing a month-long project designed to support reading in a CLIL-oriented school while documenting teachers’ perceptions of the model. Using purposive sampling, five English literature teachers were selected to reflect on their experiences developing a two-tier intervention framework and discuss their perceptions of the framework’s influence on young English language learners’ reading proficiency. Based on the results and findings, participants highly valued RtI and the theoretical structure of each tier. They perceived Tier 2 as effective, but they noted that the lack of practical structure and professional support is an obstacle to helping students meet grade-level benchmarks. These perceptions suggest that school leaders could standardize RtI support to strengthen implementation as perceived by teachers","ELT, English teaching in China, response-to-intervention, teachers’ perceptions 1 King’s Academy Binfield, England. Email: akeem.nash@kingsacademies.uk R E S E A R C H A R T I C L E S 76 Colomb. Appl. Linguist. J. Printed ISSN 0123-4641 Online ISSN 2248-7085 • January - June 2026. Vol. 28 • Issue 1 pp. 75-90. R E S E A R C H A R T I C L E S Percepción de docentes sobre un piloto de RtI de dos n",marcadores,colomb appl linguist,educational institution use response-to-intervention rti identify support monitor student poor academic behavioral performance qualitative descriptive case study problem student poor english read performance international school northern china purpose explore teacher perception influence one-month two-tier response-to-intervention pilot student english read proficiency content language integrat learn clil -orient primary school northern china tier compris whole-clas support tier target small-group work study aimed addres specific gap implement month-long project design support read clil-orient school while document teacher perception model using purposive sampl five english literature teacher select reflect their experienc develop two-tier intervention framework discus their perception framework influence young english language learner read proficiency based result finding participant highly valu rti theoretical structure each tier they perceiv tier effective but they noted lack practical structure professional support obstacle help student meet grade-level benchmark these perception suggest school leader could standardize rti support strengthen implementation perceiv teacher,elt english teach china response-to-intervention teacher perception king academy binfield england email akeem nash kingsacademi uk 76 colomb appl linguist print issn 0123-4641 online issn 2248-7085 january june 2026 vol 28 issue pp 75-90 percepcion de docent sobre un piloto de rti de dos,colomb appl linguist educational institution use response-to-intervention rti identify support monitor student poor academic behavioral performance qualitative descriptive case study problem student poor english read performance international school northern china purpose explore teacher perception influence one-month two-tier response-to-intervention pilot student english read proficiency content language integrat learn clil -orient primary school northern china tier compris whole-clas support tier target small-group work study aimed addres specific gap implement month-long project design support read clil-orient school while document teacher perception model using purposive sampl five english literature teacher select reflect their experienc develop two-tier intervention framework discus their perception framework influence young english language learner read proficiency based result finding participant highly valu rti theoretical structure each tier they perceiv tier effective but they noted lack practical structure professional support obstacle help student meet grade-level benchmark these perception suggest school leader could standardize rti support strengthen implementation perceiv teacher elt english teach china response-to-intervention teacher perception king academy binfield england email akeem nash kingsacademi uk 76 colomb appl linguist print issn 0123-4641 online issn 2248-7085 january june 2026 vol 28 issue pp 75-90 percepcion de docent sobre un piloto de rti de dos,1.0.0,29f0c7ae97cde44d
0123-4641,22952+V28_N1_Art5_22952+RV1.pdf,22952+V28_N1_Art5_22952+RV1_0,es,"results and findings, participants highly valued RtI and the theoretical structure of each tier. They perceived Tier 2 as effective,","Las instituciones educativas utilizan la respuesta a la intervención (RtI) para identificar, apoyar y monitorear a estudiantes con bajo rendimiento académico o conductual. En este estudio de caso descriptivo cualitativo, el problema fue el bajo rendimiento en lectura en inglés de los estudiantes de una escuela internacional en el norte de China. El propósito fue explorar las percepciones de los docentes sobre la influencia de un piloto de respuesta a la intervención de dos niveles y un mes de duración en la competencia lectora en inglés de los estudiantes, en una escuela primaria orientada al aprendizaje integrado de contenidos y lengua (CLIL) en el norte de China, donde el Nivel 1 comprendía apoyos para toda la clase y el Nivel 2, trabajo dirigido en grupos pequeños. Este estudio tuvo como objetivo abordar una brecha específica mediante la implementación de un proyecto de un mes diseñado para apoyar la lectura en una escuela orientada al CLIL, a la vez que se documentaban las percepciones de los docentes sobre el modelo. Mediante un muestreo intencional, se seleccionaron cinco docentes de literatura en inglés para que reflexionaran sobre sus experiencias en el desarrollo de un marco de intervención de dos niveles y compartieran sus percepciones sobre la influencia de dicho marco en la competencia lectora de los jóvenes aprendices de inglés como lengua extranjera. Con base en los resultados y hallazgos, los participantes valoraron altamente la RtI y la estructura teórica de cada nivel. Percibieron el Nivel 2 como efectivo, pero señalaron que la falta de estructura práctica y de apoyo profesional constituye un obstáculo para ayudar a los estudiantes a alcanzar los estándares correspondientes a su grado. Estas percepciones sugieren que los líderes escolares podrían estandarizar el apoyo de la RtI para fortalecer su implementación, según la percepción de los docentes","ELT, enseñanza de inglés en China, modelo de respuesta a la intervención, percepciones de profesores Teachers’ Perception of a Two-Tier RtI Pilot to Support English Learners’ Reading Performance 77 Nash, A. A. (2025) • Colomb. Appl. Linguist. J. Printed ISSN 0123-4641 Online ISSN 2248-7085 • January - June 2026. Vol. 28 • Issue 1 pp. 75-90",marcadores,results and findings participants highly valued rti and the theoretical structure of each tier they perceived tier as effective,institucion educativ utilizan respuesta intervencion rti identificar apoyar monitorear estudiant bajo rendimiento academico conductual este estudio caso descriptivo cualitativo problema fue bajo rendimiento lectura ingl estudiant escuela internacional norte china proposito fue explorar percepcion docent sobre influencia piloto respuesta intervencion dos nivel mes duracion competencia lectora ingl estudiant escuela primaria orientada aprendizaje integrado contenid lengua clil norte china donde nivel comprendia apoy toda clase nivel trabajo dirigido grup pequen este estudio tuvo como objetivo abordar brecha especifica mediante implementacion proyecto mes disenado apoyar lectura escuela orientada clil vez documentaban percepcion docent sobre modelo mediante muestreo intencional seleccionaron cinco docent literatura ingl reflexionaran sobre sus experienci desarrollo marco intervencion dos nivel compartieran sus percepcion sobre influencia dicho marco competencia lectora joven aprendic ingl como lengua extranjera base resultad hallazg participant valoraron alta rti estructura teorica cada nivel percibieron nivel como efectivo pero senalaron falta estructura practica apoyo profesional constituye obstaculo ayudar estudiant alcanzar estandar correspondient grado estas percepcion sugieren lider escolar podrian estandarizar apoyo rti fortalecer implementacion segun percepcion docent,elt ensenanz