0123-4641,22956+CALJ+28-22956+final.pdf,22956+CALJ+28-22956+final_0,en,Colomb. Appl. Linguist. J.,"This study explores the potential of ELSA (English Language Speech Assistant), a mobile-based artificial intelligence application, to support English pronunciation development among university students in self-directed learning contexts. Using a one-group pre-test post-test experimental design, we recruited 28 second-year university students (mixed gender) who had previously completed a pronunciation practice course. Participants engaged with ELSA’s AI-powered pronunciation features throughout the intervention period. Pre-test and post-test assessments were administered to examine changes in pronunciation proficiency, with data analyzed using paired-sample t-tests. Results revealed a substantial increase in mean pronunciation scores from 55.54 (SD = 13.077) to 80.18 (SD = 10.583) following the intervention (t (27) = -15.36, p < 0.001, Cohen’s d = 2.90). These findings illustrate ELSA’s practical utility in supporting autonomous pronunciation improvement among university learners. The application’s accessibility, immediate feedback mechanisms, and self-paced learning structure demonstrate its viability as a supplementary tool in English language instruction. The observed gains highlight the usefulness of mobile-based AI applications in addressing pronunciation development needs within higher education contexts. Future research could explore sustained engagement patterns with ELSA, identify which specific features contribute most to learning outcomes, and examine its applicability across diverse proficiency levels and learning environments",ELSA; Mobile-Based AI; Pronunciation Development; Self-Directed Learning; Practical Utility. 1 This article is the result of students learning experience using ELSA's AI to improve English pronunciation collaboration between King Saud University and La Tansa Mashiro University. 2 King Saud University. Email: haldayel@ksu.edu.sa 3 La Tansa Mashiro University. Email: hikmah.pravitasari@unilam.ac.i,marcadores,colomb appl linguist,study explor potential elsa english language speech assistant mobile-bas artificial intelligence application support english pronunciation development among university student self-direct learn context using one-group pre-test post-test experimental design we recruit 28 second-year university student mixed gender who had previously complet pronunciation practice course participant engag elsa ai-power pronunciation featur throughout intervention period pre-test post-test assessment administer examine chang pronunciation proficiency data analyz using paired-sample t-test result reveal substantial increase mean pronunciation scor 55 54 sd 13 077 80 18 sd 10 583 follow intervention 27 -15 36 001 cohen 90 these finding illustrate elsa practical utility support autonomou pronunciation improvement among university learner application accessibility immediate feedback mechanism self-pac learn structure demonstrate its viability supplementary tool english language instruction observ gain highlight usefulnes mobile-bas ai applic address pronunciation development need within higher education context future research could explore sustain engagement pattern elsa identify which specific featur contribute most learn outcom examine its applicability acros diverse proficiency level learn environment,elsa mobile-bas ai pronunciation development self-direct learn practical utility article result student learn experience using elsa ai improve english pronunciation collaboration between king saud university la tansa mashiro university king saud university email haldayel ksu edu sa la tansa mashiro university email hikmah pravitasari unilam ac,colomb appl linguist study explor potential elsa english language speech assistant mobile-bas artificial intelligence application support english pronunciation development among university student self-direct learn context using one-group pre-test post-test experimental design we recruit 28 second-year university student mixed gender who had previously complet pronunciation practice course participant engag elsa ai-power pronunciation featur throughout intervention period pre-test post-test assessment administer examine chang pronunciation proficiency data analyz using paired-sample t-test result reveal substantial increase mean pronunciation scor 55 54 sd 13 077 80 18 sd 10 583 follow intervention 27 -15 36 001 cohen 90 these finding illustrate elsa practical utility support autonomou pronunciation improvement among university learner application accessibility immediate feedback mechanism self-pac learn structure demonstrate its viability supplementary tool english language instruction observ gain highlight usefulnes mobile-bas ai applic address pronunciation development need within higher education context future research could explore sustain engagement pattern elsa identify which specific featur contribute most learn outcom examine its applicability acros diverse proficiency level learn environment elsa mobile-bas ai pronunciation development self-direct learn practical utility article result student learn experience using elsa ai improve english pronunciation collaboration between king saud university la tansa mashiro university king saud university email haldayel ksu edu sa la tansa mashiro university email hikmah pravitasari unilam ac,1.0.0,4c8a23bcbdd51a85
0123-4641,22956+CALJ+28-22956+final.pdf,22956+CALJ+28-22956+final_0,es,pecific features contribute most to learning,"Este estudio explora el potencial de ELSA (English Language Speech Assistant), una aplicación de inteligencia artificial móvil, para apoyar el desarrollo de la pronunciación en inglés entre estudiantes universitarios en aprendizaje autodirigido. Mediante un diseño experimental con pretest y postest, 28 estudiantes universitarios de segundo año utilizaron las funciones de pronunciación de ELSA durante el período de intervención. Los resultados revelaron un aumento en las puntuaciones medias de pronunciación, de 55.54 (DE = 13.077) a 80.18 (DE = 10.583) (t(27) = -15.36, p < 0.001, d de Cohen = 2.90). Estos hallazgos muestran la utilidad práctica de ELSA para apoyar la mejora autónoma de la pronunciación. La accesibilidad de la aplicación, su retroalimentación inmediata y su estructura autodidacta demuestran su viabilidad como herramienta complementaria en la enseñanza del inglés. Las mejoras observadas destacan la utilidad de las aplicaciones móviles basadas en IA para abordar necesidades de pronunciación en educación superior. Investigaciones futuras podrían explorar patrones de uso sostenido, identificar funciones específicas más contributivas y examinar su aplicabilidad en distintos niveles de competencia y entornos educativos","ELSA; inteligencia artificial móvil; desarrollo de la pronunciación; aprendizaje autodirigido; utilidad práctica. Fostering Students’ Autonomous Learning English Pronunciation Using Mobile-Based Artificial Intelligence 93 Aldayel, H, S. and Pravitasari, H. (2025) • Colomb. Appl. Linguist. J. Printed ISSN 0123-4641 Online ISSN 2248-7085 • January - June 2026. Vol. 28 • Issue 1 pp. 91-110. Introd",marcadores,pecific featur contribute most to learning,este estudio explora potencial elsa english language speech assistant aplicacion inteligencia artificial movil apoyar desarrollo pronunciacion ingl entre estudiant universitari aprendizaje autodirigido mediante diseno experimental pretest postest 28 estudiant universitari segundo ano utilizaron funcion pronunciacion elsa durante periodo intervencion resultad revelaron aumento puntu medi pronunciacion 55 54 13 077 80 18 10 583 27 -15 36 001 cohen 90 estos hallazg muestran utilidad practica elsa apoyar mejora autonoma pronunciacion accesibilidad aplicacion retroalimentacion inmediata estructura autodidacta demuestran viabilidad como herramienta complementaria ensenanza ingl mejor observad destacan utilidad aplic movil basad ia abordar necesidad pronunciacion educacion superior investig futur podrian explorar patron uso sostenido identificar funcion especific mas contributiv examinar aplicabilidad distint nivel competencia entorn educativ,elsa inteligencia artificial movil desarrollo pronunciacion aprendizaje autodirigido utilidad practica fostering students autonomous learning english pronunciation using mobile-based artificial intelligence 93 aldayel and pravitasari 2025 colomb appl linguist printed issn 0123-4641 online issn 2248-7085 january june 2026 vol 28 issue pp 91-110 introd,pecific featur contribute most to learning este estudio explora potencial elsa english language speech assistant aplicacion inteligencia artificial movil apoyar desarrollo pronunciacion ingl entre estudiant universitari aprendizaje autodirigido mediante diseno experimental pretest postest 28 estudiant universitari segundo ano utilizaron funcion pronunciacion elsa durante periodo intervencion resultad revelaron aumento puntu medi pronunciacion 55 54 13 077 80 18 10 583 27 -15 36 001 cohen 90 estos hallazg muestran utilidad practica elsa apoyar mejora autonoma pronunciacion accesibilidad aplicacion retroalimentacion inmediata estructura autodidacta demuestran viabilidad como herramienta complementaria ensenanza ingl mejor observad destacan utilidad aplic movil basad ia abordar necesidad pronunciacion educacion superior investig futur podrian explorar patron uso sostenido identificar funcion especific mas contributiv examinar aplicabilidad distint nivel competencia entorn educativ elsa inteligencia artificial movil desarrollo pronunciacion aprendizaje autodirigido utilidad practica fostering students autonomous learning english pronunciation using mobile-based artificial intelligence 93 aldayel and pravitasari 2025 colomb appl linguist printed issn 0123-4641 online issn 2248-7085 january june 2026 vol 28 issue pp 91-110 introd,1.0.0,b308ef697f13a2a5
0123-4641,23158+V28_N1_Art1_23158+RV2+(1).pdf,23158+V28_N1_Art1_23158+RV2+(1)_0,en,Colomb. Appl. Linguist. J.,"Following the social cognitive theory, this cross-sectional, correlational study aimed to explore Iranian English as Foreign Language (EFL) teachers’ preferred teaching style and its effect on their perceived self-efficacy in accomplishing specific classroom tasks. To this aim, Grasha’s Teaching Style Inventory (TSI) and Tschannen-Moran Teachers’ Sense of Efficacy Scale (TSES) were used to test teaching style preferences and self-efficacy. To this aim, 233 EFL teachers from both Iranian public schools and private language institutes were included. Data were analyzed using the chi-square test, one-way ANOVA, and Bonferroni post hoc comparisons. Results showed that facilitator and personal model teaching styles were the two most frequent styles. Regarding participants’ self-efficacy, those who adopted a facilitator teaching style reported the highest scores across all subscales of self-efficacy. Additionally, a statistically significant difference was found between the self-efficacy levels of teachers with facilitator versus formal authority teaching styles (p = 0.000). These findings have important implications for teacher education programs in Iran, highlighting the need for the programs to provide teachers with enough opportunities to develop communicative teaching practices, engage students effectively, and enhance their sense of self-efficacy. Teacher trainers can monitor teachers’ progress in self-efficacy and accordingly modify the teaching methods, to acknowledge teacher psychology involved in teacher practice","EFL, self-efficacy, social cognitive theory, teachers, teaching style 1 Bahar Institute of Higher Education. hamed.sadough@gmail.com 2 Attar Institute of Higher Education. yazdanmehr@attar.ac.ir R E S E A R C H A R T I C L E S 2 Colomb. Appl. Linguist. J. Printed ISSN 0123-4641 Online ISSN 2248-7085 • January - June 2026. Vol. 28 • Issue 1 pp. 1-24. R E S E A R C H A R T I C L E S Explorando la",marcadores,colomb appl linguist,follow social cognitive theory cross-sectional correlational study aimed explore iranian english foreign language efl teacher preferr teach style its effect their perceiv self-efficacy accomplish specific classroom task aim grasha teach style inventory tsi tschannen-moran teacher sense efficacy scale tses used test teach style preferenc self-efficacy aim 233 efl teacher both iranian public school private language institut includ data analyz using chi-square test one-way anova bonferroni post hoc comparison result show facilitator personal model teach styl two most frequent styl regard participant self-efficacy those who adopt facilitator teach style report highest scor acros all subscal self-efficacy additionally statistically significant difference found between self-efficacy level teacher facilitator versu formal authority teach styl 000 these finding have important implic teacher education program iran highlight need program provide teacher enough opportuniti develop communicative teach practic engage student effectively enhance their sense self-efficacy teacher trainer can monitor teacher progres self-efficacy accord modify teach method acknowledge teacher psychology involv teacher practice,efl self-efficacy social cognitive theory teacher teach style bahar institute higher education hamed sadough gmail com attar institute higher education yazdanmehr attar ac ir colomb appl linguist print issn 0123-4641 online issn 2248-7085 january june 2026 vol 28 issue pp 1-24 explorando la,colomb appl linguist follow social cognitive theory cross-sectional correlational study aimed explore iranian english foreign language efl teacher preferr teach style its effect their perceiv self-efficacy accomplish specific classroom task aim grasha teach style inventory tsi tschannen-moran teacher sense efficacy scale tses used test teach style preferenc self-efficacy aim 233 efl teacher both iranian public school private language institut includ data analyz using chi-square test one-way anova bonferroni post hoc comparison result show facilitator personal model teach styl two most frequent styl regard participant self-efficacy those who adopt facilitator teach style report highest scor acros all subscal self-efficacy additionally statistically significant difference found between self-efficacy level teacher facilitator versu formal authority teach styl 000 these finding have important implic teacher education program iran highlight need program provide teacher enough opportuniti develop communicative teach practic engage student effectively enhance their sense self-efficacy teacher trainer can monitor teacher progres self-efficacy accord modify teach method acknowledge teacher psychology involv teacher practice efl self-efficacy social cognitive theory teacher teach style bahar institute higher education hamed sadough gmail com attar institute higher education yazdanmehr attar ac ir colomb appl linguist print issn 0123-4641 online issn 2248-7085 january june 2026 vol 28 issue pp 1-24 explorando la,1.0.0,2f7f8c1b97ec8b71
0123-4641,23158+V28_N1_Art1_23158+RV2+(1).pdf,23158+V28_N1_Art1_23158+RV2+(1)_0,es,hlighting the need for the programs to,"Siguiendo la teoría sociocognitiva, el presente estudio transversal y correlacional tuvo como objetivo explorar el estilo de enseñanza preferido de los profesores iraníes de inglés como lengua extranjera (EFL) y su efecto en su autoeficacia percibida en el desempeño de una tarea de enseñanza específica en clase. Se utilizaron el Inventario de Estilo de Enseñanza de Grasha (TSI) y la Escala de Sentido de Eficacia de los Profesores de Tschannen-Moran (TSES) para evaluar las preferencias de estilo de enseñanza y la autoeficacia. Un total de 233 profesores de EFL de escuelas secundarias públicas iraníes e institutos de idiomas privados fueron incluidos en este estudio. Los datos fueron analizados mediante la prueba de chi-cuadrado, ANOVA de una vía y el post hoc de Duncan. Los resultados mostraron que los estilos de enseñanza más preferidos entre los profesores iraníes de EFL fueron el estilo de facilitador y el estilo de modelo personal. Con respecto al estado de autoeficacia de los participantes, el estilo de enseñanza de facilitador mostró tener las puntuaciones más altas en todas las subescalas de autoeficacia que los profesores de EFL percibieron en clase. Los hallazgos también evidenciaron una diferencia estadísticamente significativa entre la autoeficacia de los docentes en los estilos de enseñanza de facilitador y de autoridad formal (p = 0,000). Este estudio tiene implicaciones para los programas de formación docente en Irán, ya que destaca la necesidad de proporcionar a los profesores oportunidades suficientes para aprender a enseñar comunicativamente, involucrar adecuadamente a los estudiantes y mejorar su sentido de autoeficacia docente. Los capacitadores docentes pueden monitorear el progreso o los cambios en la autoeficacia docente y, en consecuencia, modificar los métodos de enseñanza para reconocer la psicología docente involucrada en la práctica docente","autoeficacia, docentes, EFL, estilo de enseñanza, teoría cognitiva social Exploring the Relationship Between Iranian EFL Teachers’ Teaching Style and Multiple Dimensions of Self-Efficacy 3 Sadoughvanini, S. and Yazdanmehr, E. (2025) • Colomb. Appl. Linguist. J. Printed ISSN 0123-4641 Online ISSN 2248-7085 • January - June 2026. Vol. 28 • Issue 1 pp. 1-24",marcadores,hlighting the need for the programs to,sigu teoria sociocognitiva presente estudio transversal correlacional tuvo como objetivo explorar estilo ensenanza preferido profesor irani ingl como lengua extranjera efl efecto autoeficacia percibida desempeno tarea ensenanza especifica clase utilizaron inventario estilo ensenanza grasha tsi escala sentido eficacia profesor tschannen-moran tses evaluar preferenci estilo ensenanza autoeficacia total 233 profesor efl escuel secundari public irani institut idiom privad fueron incluid este estudio datos fueron analizad mediante prueba chi-cuadrado anova via post hoc duncan resultad mostraron estil ensenanza mas preferid entre profesor irani efl fueron estilo facilitador estilo modelo personal respecto estado autoeficacia participant estilo ensenanza facilitador mostro tener puntu mas altas todas subescal autoeficacia profesor efl percibieron clase hallazg tambien evidenciaron diferencia estadistica significativa entre autoeficacia docent estil ensenanza facilitador autoridad formal 000 este estudio tiene implic program formacion docente iran ya destaca necesidad proporcionar profesor oportunidad suficient aprender ensenar comunicativa involucrar adecuada estudiant mejorar sentido autoeficacia docente capacitador docent pueden monitorear progreso cambi autoeficacia docente consecuencia modificar metod ensenanza reconocer psicologia docente involucrada practica docente,autoeficacia docent efl estilo ensenanza teoria cognitiva social exploring the relationship between iranian efl teachers teaching style and multiple dimensions of self-efficacy sad