0123-4641,23179+V28_N1_Art3_23179+RV1.pdf,23179+V28_N1_Art3_23179+RV1_0,en,Colomb. Appl. Linguist. J.,"This study examines Colombian English teachers’ knowledge, experiences, and views regarding speaking assessments. Semi-structured interviews were conducted with Colombian teachers, some of whom also shared classroom assessment samples. Thematic analysis was used for the interviews, and content analysis was applied to the assessment materials. Findings revealed a clear link between teachers’ perceptions of testing and their approach to presenting it to students. Furthermore, a correlation exists between their knowledge and experience in designing, administering, and evaluating speaking tests. Lastly, there is evidence of teachers’ awareness of the issues surrounding these testing practices. The shared concern about the effectiveness of current practices, along with the expressed need for further training, underscore the importance of developing targeted professional development programs to better prepare teachers in this area","Experiences; Language Testing; Speaking; Opinions; Knowledge 1 This article is a result of dissertation research to achieve the title of Master in Applied Linguistic to TESOL from the University of Leicester, England. 2 British Council, London, Great Britain, Email: Lorena.idarraga@hotmail.com R E S E A R C H A R T I C L E S 44 Colomb. Appl. Linguist. J. Printed ISSN 0123-4641 Online ISSN 2248",marcadores,colomb appl linguist,study examin colombian english teacher knowledge experienc view regard speak assessment semi-structur interview conduct colombian teacher some whom also shar classroom assessment sampl thematic analysi used interview content analysi appli assessment material finding reveal clear link between teacher perception test their approach present student furthermore correlation exist between their knowledge experience design administer evaluat speak test lastly there evidence teacher awarenes issu surround these test practic shar concern about effectivenes current practic along express need further train underscore importance develop target professional development program better prepare teacher area,experienc language test speak opinion knowledge article result dissertation research achieve title master appli linguistic tesol university leicester england british council london great britain email lorena idarraga hotmail com 44 colomb appl linguist print issn 0123-4641 online issn 2248,colomb appl linguist study examin colombian english teacher knowledge experienc view regard speak assessment semi-structur interview conduct colombian teacher some whom also shar classroom assessment sampl thematic analysi used interview content analysi appli assessment material finding reveal clear link between teacher perception test their approach present student furthermore correlation exist between their knowledge experience design administer evaluat speak test lastly there evidence teacher awarenes issu surround these test practic shar concern about effectivenes current practic along express need further train underscore importance develop target professional development program better prepare teacher area experienc language test speak opinion knowledge article result dissertation research achieve title master appli linguistic tesol university leicester england british council london great britain email lorena idarraga hotmail com 44 colomb appl linguist print issn 0123-4641 online issn 2248,1.0.0,d60eb8ffdfc3e833
0123-4641,23179+V28_N1_Art3_23179+RV1.pdf,23179+V28_N1_Art3_23179+RV1_0,es,ounding these testing practices. The,"Este estudio examina los conocimientos, experiencias y percepciones de los docentes colombianos de inglés en relación con la evaluación de la habilidad de habla. Se llevaron a cabo entrevistas semiestructuradas con profesores colombianos, algunos de los cuales también compartieron muestras de evaluaciones utilizadas en el aula. Para el análisis de las entrevistas, se empleó un análisis temático, mientras que las muestras de evaluación se examinaron mediante el análisis de contenido. Los hallazgos revelaron una relación clara entre las percepciones de los docentes sobre la evaluación y la manera en que la presentan a los estudiantes. Así mismo, se identificó una correlación entre sus conocimientos y experiencias en el diseño, aplicación y evaluación de pruebas orales. Finalmente, se evidenció que los docentes eran conscientes respecto a los desafíos asociados con estas prácticas evaluativas. La preocupación compartida sobre la efectividad de las prácticas actuales, junto con la necesidad expresada de recibir mayor formación, subrayan la importancia de desarrollar programas de desarrollo profesional específicos que fortalezcan las competencias docentes en esta área","conocimientos; experiencias; habilidad de habla; opiniones; prueba Exploring Teacher’s Cognition and Practices of Testing Speaking in Colombian Universities 45 Idarraga, L. (2025) • Colomb. Appl. Linguist. J. Printed ISSN 0123-4641 Online ISSN 2248-7085 • January - June 2026. Vol. 28 • Issue 1 pp. 43-58",marcadores,ounding these testing practic the,este estudio examina conoc experienci percepcion docent colombian ingl relacion evaluacion habilidad habla llevaron cabo entrevist semiestructurad profesor colombian algun cual tambien compartieron muestr evalu utilizad aula analisis entrevist empleo analisis tematico mientr muestr evaluacion examinaron mediante analisis contenido hallazg revelaron r