0123-4641,23270+CALJ+28-23270+Final.pdf,23270+CALJ+28-23270+Final_0,en,Colomb. Appl. Linguist. J.,"This study aims to understand the family of genres linked to didactic planning (DPGs), focusing on their epistemic and argumentative potential. It highlights how associated reading and writing practices contribute to university teacher education. To this end, a mixed-method design was adopted, combining corpus analysis (93 lesson plans, 66 syllabi, and 3 curricular designs) with interviews conducted with pre-service and in-service teachers from diverse teacher training programs. The results reveal a typology of didactic planning genres organized into two subfamilies: authorial genres (lesson plans, didactic sequences, syllabi) and critical reading genres (curricular designs, study programs). These genres are characterized linguistically as polyphonic, polymorphic, and multi-targeted. Although DPGs display highly technical structures, they cannot be reduced to formulated or ritualized writing. Instead, they embody epistemic and argumentative functions that enable reflection, justification, and decision-making in teaching. The implications of these findings for teacher education are twofold. First, they highlight the need to explicitly address the teaching and learning of didactic planning genres as part of professional and training writing practices. Second, they provide linguistic and didactic orientations to foster the development of generic competence among future teachers, promoting critical and reflective engagement with planning as a discursive practice at the core of professional development","Didactic planning; teacher education; genre analysis; argumentation. 1 This paper presents results developed in a research project where the author is a lead member: Project PICT-2021-I-A-00096, named Dialogical teaching practices that promote the epistemic potential of orality, reading, and writing in ecological contexts of secondary and higher education, directed by Dr. Constanza Padilla (CON",marcadores,colomb appl linguist,study aims understand family genr link didactic plann dpgs focus their epistemic argumentative potential highlight how associat read writ practic contribute university teacher education end mixed-method design adopt combin corpu analysi 93 lesson plan 66 syllabi curricular design interview conduct pre-service in-service teacher diverse teacher train program result reveal typology didactic plann genr organiz into two subfamili authorial genr lesson plan didactic sequenc syllabi critical read genr curricular design study program these genr characteriz linguistically polyphonic polymorphic multi-target although dpgs display highly technical structur they cannot reduc formulat ritualiz writ instead they embody epistemic argumentative function enable reflection justification decision-mak teach implic these finding teacher education twofold first they highlight need explicitly addres teach learn didactic plann genr part professional train writ practic second they provide linguistic didactic orient foster development generic competence among future teacher promot critical reflective engagement plann discursive practice core professional development,didactic plann teacher education genre analysi argumentation paper present result develop research project where author lead member project pict-2021-i-a-00096 named dialogical teach practic promote epistemic potential orality read writ ecological context secondary higher education direct dr constanza padilla con,colomb appl linguist study aims understand family genr link didactic plann dpgs focus their epistemic argumentative potential highlight how associat read writ practic contribute university teacher education end mixed-method design adopt combin corpu analysi 93 lesson plan 66 syllabi curricular design interview conduct pre-service in-service teacher diverse teacher train program result reveal typology didactic plann genr organiz into two subfamili authorial genr lesson plan didactic sequenc syllabi critical read genr curricular design study program these genr characteriz linguistically polyphonic polymorphic multi-target although dpgs display highly technical structur they cannot reduc formulat ritualiz writ instead they embody epistemic argumentative function enable reflection justification decision-mak teach implic these finding teacher education twofold first they highlight need explicitly addres teach learn didactic plann genr part professional train writ practic second they provide linguistic didactic orient foster development generic competence among future teacher promot critical reflective engagement plann discursive practice core professional development didactic plann teacher education genre analysi argumentation paper present result develop research project where author lead member project pict-2021-i-a-00096 named dialogical teach practic promote epistemic potential orality read writ ecological context secondary higher education direct dr constanza padilla con,1.0.0,7b7e8d6578c104bb
0123-4641,23270+CALJ+28-23270+Final.pdf,23270+CALJ+28-23270+Final_0,es,"Dialogical teaching practices that promote the epistemic potential of orality, reading, and writing in ecological contexts of secondary and","Este estudio tiene como objetivo comprender la familia de géneros vinculados con la planificación didáctica, centrándose en su potencial epistémico y argumentativo. Así, destaca cómo las prácticas de lectura y escritura asociadas contribuyen a la formación del profesorado universitario. Para ello, se adoptó un diseño de métodos mixtos que combinó el análisis de corpus (93 planificaciones de clase, 66 programas de asignaturas y 3 diseños curriculares) con entrevistas a docentes en formación y en ejercicio de distintos profesorados. Los resultados revelan una tipología de géneros de planificación didáctica organizados en dos subfamilias: géneros de autoría (planificaciones de clases, secuencias didácticas, programas de asignaturas) y géneros de lectura crítica (diseños curriculares, programas de estudio). Estos géneros se caracterizan lingüísticamente por ser polifónicos, polimorfos y con múltiples destinatarios. Aunque estos géneros presentan estructuras muy técnicas, no pueden reducirse a una escritura ritualizada. En cambio, encarnan funciones epistémicas y argumentativas que permiten la reflexión, la justificación y la toma de decisiones en la enseñanza. Las implicaciones de estos hallazgos para la formación del profesorado son dobles. En primer lugar, ponen de relieve la necesidad de abordar explícitamente la enseñanza y el aprendizaje de los géneros vinculados con la planificación didáctica como parte de las prácticas de escritura profesional y formativa. En segundo lugar, proporcionan orientaciones lingüísticas y didácticas para fomentar el desarrollo de la competencia genérica entre los futuros docentes, promoviendo un compromiso crítico y reflexivo con la planificación como práctica discursiva en el centro del desarrollo profesional","planificación didáctica; formación docente; análisis de géneros; argumentación. Family of Genres Linked to Didactic Planning: A Genre Analysis 113 Molina, M. E. (2025) • Colomb. Appl. Linguist. J. Printed ISSN 0123-4641 Online ISSN 2248-7085 • January - June 2026. Vol. 28 • Issue 1 pp. 101-126",marcadores,dialogical teaching practic that promote the epistemic potential of orality reading and writing in ecological contexts of secondary and,este estudio tiene como objetivo comprender familia gener vinculad planificacion didactica centrandose potencial epistemico argumentativo asi destaca como practic lectura escritura asociad contribuyen formacion profesorado universitario ello adopto diseno metod mixt combino analisis corpus 93 planific clase 66 program asignatur disen curricular entrevist docent formacion ejercicio distint profesorad resultad revelan tipologia gener planificacion didactica organizad dos subfamili gener autoria planific clas secuenci didactic program asignatur gener lectura critica disen curricular program estudio estos gener caracterizan linguistica ser polifonic polimorf multipl destinatari aunque estos gener presentan estructur muy tecnic no pueden reducirse escritura ritualizada cambio encarnan funcion epistemic argumentativ permiten reflexion justificacion toma decision ensenanza implic estos hallazg formacion profesorado son dobl primer lugar ponen relieve necesidad abordar explicita ensenanza aprendizaje gener vinculad planificacion didactica como parte practic escritura profesional formativa segundo lugar proporcionan orient linguistic didactic fomentar desarrollo competencia generica entre futur docent promov compromiso critico reflexivo planificacion como practica discursiva centro desarrollo profesional,planificacion didactica formacion docente analisis gener argumentacion family of genr linked to didactic planning genre analysis 113 molina 2025 colomb appl linguist printed issn 0123-4641 online issn 2248-7085 january june 2026 vol 28 issue pp 101-126,d