ad hallazg muestran equipo docente interpreta paz ensenanza lengu divers maner taller formativ constituyeron herramienta efectiva construccion colectiva conocimiento alrededor este tema desarrollo profesional educacion paz ensenanza lengu ensenanza superior formacion docent este articulo derivado proyecto investigacion construir cultura paz colombia perspectiv discursiv accion educativ realizado investigador universidad antioquia universite grenoble alpes entre 2022 2024 proyecto fue fina,1.0.0,9958e63cd99926ca
0123-4641,23285+V28_N1_Art4_23285+RV1.pdf,23285+V28_N1_Art4_23285+RV1_0,en,1 Este artículo es derivado del proyecto de investigación: “Construir una cultura de la paz en Colombia: perspectivas discursivas y acciones,"Peace education initiatives in foreign language teaching have been increasing yet remain limited. The qualitative research project reported in this article intended to create professional development spaces to reflect on this topic in Colombia through free online workshops, tailored to university foreign language educators. The workshops created collaborative spaces for teachers to deepen their understanding of concepts related to peace education. They were conducted as part of a larger project on peace discourses and education for peace carried out by a Colombian university and another French university from 2022 to 2024. In this article, we present the understandings of peace held by these three teachers, and the potential for implementation in foreign language classrooms, as well as the impact of the workshops on their professional development. Data came from recordings of the workshops, lesson plans designed by the teachers, questionnaires, and in-depth interviews. Findings reveal that teachers interpret peace education in foreign language classrooms uniquely, and the professional development workshops played a vital role in the collective construction of knowledge around this topic","Foreign Language Education; Peace Education; Professional Development; Teachers’ Training; Tertiary Education Voces de paz: reflexiones de docentes de lenguas extranjeras sobre la educación para la paz 61 Arismendi, F. A., Aristizábal A. J., Cárdenas Y. M. and Meza, J. P. (2025) • Colomb. Appl. Linguist. J. Printed ISSN 0123-4641 Online ISSN 2248-7085 • January - June 2026. Vol. 28 • Issue 1 pp",marcadores,este articulo es derivado del proyecto de investigacion construir una cultura de la paz en colombia perspectiva discursiva accion,peace education initiativ foreign language teach have been increas yet remain limit qualitative research project report article intend create professional development spac reflect topic colombia through free online workshop tailor university foreign language educator workshop creat collaborative spac teacher deepen their understand concept relat peace education they conduct part larger project peace discours education peace carri out colombian university another french university 2022 2024 article we present understanding peace held these three teacher potential implementation foreign language classroom well impact workshop their professional development data came recording workshop lesson plan design teacher questionnair in-depth interview finding reveal teacher interpret peace education foreign language classroom uniquely professional development workshop play vital role collective construction knowledge around topic,foreign language education peace education professional development teacher train tertiary education voce de paz reflexion de docent de lengua extranjera sobre la educacion para la paz 61 arismendi aristizabal cardena meza 2025 colomb appl linguist print issn 0123-4641 online issn 2248-7085 january june 2026 vol 28 issue pp,este articulo es derivado del proyecto de investigacion construir una cultura de la paz en colombia perspectiva discursiva accion peace education initiativ foreign language teach have been increas yet remain limit qualitative research project report article intend create professional development spac reflect topic colombia through free online workshop tailor university foreign language educator workshop creat collaborative spac teacher deepen their understand concept relat peace education they conduct part larger project peace discours education peace carri out colombian university another french university 2022 2024 article we present understanding peace held these three teacher potential implementation foreign language classroom well impact workshop their professional development data came recording workshop lesson plan design teacher questionnair in-depth interview finding reveal teacher interpret peace education foreign language classroom uniquely professional development workshop play vital role collective construction knowledge around topic foreign language education peace education professional development teacher train tertiary education voce de paz reflexion de docent de lengua extranjera sobre la educacion para la paz 61 arismendi aristizabal cardena meza 2025 colomb appl linguist print issn 0123-4641 online issn 2248-7085 january june 2026 vol 28 issue pp,1.0.0,6708d7a5bea3bfb2
0123-4641,23728+CALJ+28-23728+final.pdf,23728+CALJ+28-23728+final_0,en,Colomb. Appl. Linguist. J.,"Opening opportunities for language engagement through multimodal practices that start in the classroom and continue to develop in pre-service teachers’ lives turns out to be a resource to build teacher knowledge. Moreover, the use of digital resources and multiple modes of communication are alternatives that connect with today’s learning environments. This study, framed within a qualitative approach and a hermeneutic perspective, aims to develop understandings of elementary school preservice teachers’ multimodal practices while implementing a multiliteracies approach. Data were collected through a teaching diary, two questionnaires, and the implementation of a pedagogical multimodal proposal. As a result, this project contributed to developing understandings of participants’ initial multimodal practices; narratives unveiled their funds of knowledge; stories connected image, action, graphics, and sound; built confidence for teacher development while conceptualizing and applying multimodal practices; and raised awareness of the need to contextually and ethically use digital tools in their current and future teaching careers","Elementary school; pre-service teachers; multimodal practices; digital tools; pedagogy of multiliteracies. 1 Research financed by Vicerrectoría de Investigaciones, Universidad del Cauca. Project ID: 6377 2 Universidad del Cauca. Email: aycastro@unicauca.edu.co 3 Universidad del Cauca. Email: ajgomez@unicauca.edu.co R E S E A R C H A R T I C L E S 128 Colomb. Appl. Linguist. J. Printed ISSN 012",marcadores,colomb appl linguist,open opportuniti language engagement through multimodal practic start classroom continue develop pre-service teacher live turn out resource build teacher knowledge moreover use digital resourc multiple mode communication alternativ connect today learn environment study fram within qualitative approach hermeneutic perspective aims develop understanding elementary school preservice teacher multimodal practic while implement multiliteraci approach data collect through teach diary two questionnair implementation pedagogical multimodal proposal result project contribut develop understanding participant initial multimodal practic narrativ unveil their fund knowledge stori connect image action graphic sound built confidence teacher development while conceptualiz apply multimodal practic rais awarenes need contextually ethically use digital tool their current future teach career,elementary school pre-service teacher multimodal practic digital tool pedagogy multiliteraci research financ vicerrectoria de investigacion universidad del cauca project id 6377 universidad del cauca email aycastro unicauca edu co universidad del cauca email ajgomez unicauca edu co 128 colomb appl linguist print issn 012,colomb appl linguist open opportuniti language engagement through multimodal practic start classroom continue develop pre-service teacher live turn out resource build teacher knowledge moreover use digital resourc multiple mode communication alternativ connect today learn environment study fram within qualitative approach hermeneutic perspective aims develop understanding elementary school preservice teacher multimodal practic while implement multiliteraci approach data collect through teach diary two questionnair implementation pedagogical multimodal proposal result project contribut develop understanding participant initial multimodal practic narrativ unveil their fund knowledge stori connect image action graphic sound built confidence teacher development while conceptualiz apply multimodal practic rais awarenes need contextually ethically use digital tool their current future teach career elementary school pre-service teacher multimodal practic digital tool pedagogy multiliteraci research financ vicerrectoria de investigacion universidad del cauca project id 6377 universidad del cauca email aycastro unicauca edu co universidad del cauca email ajgomez unicauca edu co 128 colomb appl linguist print issn 012,1.0.0,20514190cfb73b6b
0123-4641,23728+CALJ+28-23728+final.pdf,23728+CALJ+28-23728+final_0,es,knowledge; stories,"Las oportunidades de interacción lingüística a través de prácticas multimodales, que comienzan en el aula y continúan desarrollándose en la vida de los futuros docentes, resultan ser un recurso para construir conocimiento educativo. Además, el uso de recursos digitales y múltiples modos de comunicación son alternativas que conectan con los entornos de aprendizaje actuales. Este estudio, enmarcado en un enfoque cualitativo y una perspectiva hermenéutica, busca comprender las prácticas multimodales de futuros docentes de primaria, implementando un enfoque de multiliteracidades. Los datos se recolectaron mediante un diario pedagógico, dos cuestionarios y la implementación de una propuesta pedagógica multimodal. Como resultado, este proyecto contribuyó a comprender las prácticas multimodales iniciales de los participantes; las narrativas develaron sus fondos de conocimiento; las historias conectaron imágenes, acciones, gráficos y sonidos; se fortaleció la confianza para el desarrollo docente y a través de la conceptualización y aplicación de prácticas multimodales; y se concientizó sobre la necesidad de utilizar herramientas digitales de forma contextual y ética en sus carreras docentes actuales y futuras","Escuela primaria; futuros docentes; prácticas multimodales; pedagogía de las multiliteracidades. Elementary School Pre-service Teachers’ Multimodal Practices: A Multiliteracies Approach 129 Castro-Garcés, A. Y., & Gómez-Vargas, A. J. (2025) • Colomb. Appl. Linguist. J. Printed ISSN 0123-4641 Online ISSN 2248-7085 • January - June 2026. Vol. 28 • Issue 1 pp. 127-144",marcadores,knowledge stori,oportunidad interaccion linguistica trav practic multimodal comienzan aula continuan desarrollandose vida futur docent resultan ser recurso construir conocimiento educativo adem uso recurs digital multipl modos comunicacion son alternativ conectan entorn aprendizaje actual este estudio enm