ducacion primaria inteligencia artificial estrategi aprendizaje educacion salud geografia impact of teaching proposal on health literacy and the development of learning strategi in primary education,1.0.0,48b0a118bfb1184d
0123-7756,Dialnet-ImpactoDeUnaPropuestaDidacticaEnLaAlfabetizacionEn-10709967.pdf,Dialnet-ImpactoDeUnaPropuestaDidacticaEnLaAlfabetizacionEn-10709967_0,en,indican que no se observaron diferencias significativas en la adquisición de,"Artificial Intelligence (AI) has gained increasing prominence in recent years, with its applications extending across various fields, including education through the development of didactic strategies. The aim of this study is to analyze the impact of a didactic proposal on health literacy—understood broadly as comprehension, informed decision-making, and the development of healthy habits—and the development of learning strategies supported by AI. Specifically, the study examines the implementation of the Khan Academy platform, which enables individualized attention to students by monitoring learning progress and adapting strategies, while also promoting health education. Impacto de una propuesta didáctica en la alfabetización en salud y el desarrollo de estrategias de aprendizaje en Educación Primaria 37 Rev.His.Educ.Colomb-Vol. 35 N° 35, jul-dic-2025-San Juan de Pasto-Col. ISSN 0123-7756-ISSN en línea 2422-2348-pp. 35-64 A quasi-experimental design was carried out with an experimental group and a control group, involving fifth-grade Primary Education students. A quantitative data analysis approach was used before and after the didactic intervention, whose purpose was to foster health literacy. The hypothesis is that, by working in this way, students will acquire greater competence in health, thereby improving their learning-to-learn competence. The main results indicate that no significant differences were found in the acquisition of learning strategies when AI-based feedback was used. However, notable improvements in health literacy were observed after the educational intervention. These findings suggest that the design of didactic intervention played a key role in promoting literacy on healthrelated topics. At the same time, the use of AI in this context appears to have functioned more as a tool to enhance cognitive and literacy skills rather than directly fostering the development of learning strategies",primary education; artificial intelligence; learning strategies; health education; geography. Impacto de uma proposta de ensino na literacia em saúde e no desenvolvimento de estratégias de aprendizagem no Ensino Básico,marcadores,indican que no se observaron diferencia significativa en la adquisicion de,artificial intelligence ai has gain increas prominence recent year its applic extend acros variou field includ education through development didactic strategi aim study analyze impact didactic proposal health literacy--understood broadly comprehension inform decision-mak development healthy habits--and development learn strategi support ai specifically study examin implementation khan academy platform which enabl individualiz attention student monitor learn progres adapt strategi while also promot health education impacto de una propuesta didactica en la alfabetizacion en salud el desarrollo de estrategia de aprendizaje en educacion primaria 37 rev his educ colomb-vol 35 ndeg 35 jul-dic-2025-san juan de pasto-col issn 0123-7756-issn en linea 2422-2348-pp 35-64 quasi-experimental design carri out experimental group control group involv fifth-grade primary education student quantitative data analysi approach used before after didactic intervention whose purpose foster health literacy hypothesi work way student will acquire greater competence health thereby improv their learning-to-learn competence main result indicate no significant differenc found acquisition learn strategi when ai-bas feedback used however notable improvement health literacy observ after educational intervention these finding suggest design didactic intervention play key role promot literacy healthrelat topic same time use ai context appear have function more tool enhance cognitive literacy skill rather than directly foster development learn strategi,primary education artificial intelligence learn strategi health education geography impacto de uma proposta de ensino na literacia em saude no desenvolvimento de estrategia de aprendizagem no ensino basico,indican que no se observaron diferencia significativa en la adquisicion de artificial intelligence ai has gain increas prominence recent year its applic extend acros variou field includ education through development didactic strategi aim study analyze impact didactic proposal health literacy--understood broadly comprehension inform decision-mak development healthy habits--and development learn strategi support ai specifically study examin implementation khan academy platform which enabl individualiz attention student monitor learn progres adapt strategi while also promot health education impacto de una propuesta didactica en la alfabetizacion en salud el desarrollo de estrategia de aprendizaje en educacion primaria 37 rev his educ colomb-vol 35 ndeg 35 jul-dic-2025-san juan de pasto-col issn 0123-7756-issn en linea 2422-2348-pp 35-64 quasi-experimental design carri out experimental group control group involv fifth-grade primary education student quantitative data analysi approach used before after didactic intervention whose purpose foster health literacy hypothesi work way student will acquire greater competence health thereby improv their learning-to-learn competence main result indicate no significant differenc found acquisition learn strategi when ai-bas feedback used however notable improvement health literacy observ after educational intervention these finding suggest design didactic intervention play key role promot literacy healthrelat topic same time use ai context appear have function more tool enhance cognitive literacy skill rather than directly foster development learn strategi primary education artificial intelligence learn strategi health education geography impacto de uma proposta de ensino na literacia em saude no desenvolv