0123-9015,100-87-PB.pdf,100-87-PB_0,en,International Organization for Standardization [ISO]. ISO 56006:,"Objective: Testicular germ cell tumors (GCTs) are the leading cause of cancer in men aged 15 to 45 years. Management consists of radical orchiectomy, and in patients with metastatic tumors, adjuvant platinum-based chemotherapy is administered. Residual lung disease has been reported in 25.0% of cases following first-line chemotherapy, in which pulmonary metastasectomy is essential to rule out residual tumor activity. This study aimed to describe the clinical outcomes of patients with testicular GCTs who underwent pulmonary metastasectomy between 2010 and 2023 after receiving chemotherapy at the Instituto Nacional de Cancerología (INC) in Colombia. Methods: A descriptive, longitudinal, retrospective study was conducted. Trends in overall survival (OS) and progression-free survival (PFS) were described according to clinically relevant characteristics in these patients. Results: Nineteen patients were included. At 24 months, OS was 89.2%, and PFS was 63.6%. The highest OS and PFS estimates were observed in patients with metastatic lung disease at diagnosis. High OS estimates were also observed in those with a low-risk prognostic classification according to the International Germ Cell Collaborative Cancer Group (IGCCCG), and high PFS estimates were observed in patients with histopathological findings of non-viable tumor at pulmonary resection following chemotherapy. Catalina Castañeda-Motta1 , Rafael José Beltrán-Jiménez2 , Fernando Alvarado-Sarzosa2 , Miguel Ricardo Buitrago-Ramírez2 , Marino Cabrera-Fierro3, 4 , Ricardo Elías Bruges-Maya5 , Marcela Nuñez-Lemus6 , Carlos Andrés Carvajal-Fierro2, 7 1 Especialista en entrenamiento de la Especialización en Cirugía de Tórax, convenio Universidad El Bosque - Instituto Nacional de Cancerología, Bogotá, D. C., Colombia. 2 Tórax, Instituto Nacional de Cancerología, Bogotá, D. C., Colombia. 3 Urología, Instituto Nacional de Cancerología, Bogotá, D. C., Colombia. 4 Unidad Funcional Clínica de Urología Oncológica, Centro de Tratamiento e Investigación sobre Cáncer Luis Carlos Sarmiento Angulo (CTIC), Bogotá, D. C., Colombia. 5 Oncología, Instituto Nacional de Cancerología, Bogotá, D. C., Colombia. 6 Apoyo Integral a la Gestión de la Información, Instituto Nacional de Cancerología, Bogotá, D. C., Colombia. 7 Unidad Funcional Clínica de Oncología Torácica, Centro de Tratamiento e Investigación sobre Cáncer Luis Carlos Sarmiento Angulo (CTIC), Bogotá, D. C., Colombia. Citación Castañeda-Motta C, Beltrán-Jiménez R, AlvaradoSarzosa F, Buitrago-Ramírez M, Cabrera-Fierro M, Bruges-Maya R, et al. Caracterización de los pacientes con tumores de células germinales testi culares llevados a metastasectomía pulmonar: experiencia de un centro oncológico. Rev Col Cancerol. 2026;30(2): 207-22. https://doi.org/10.35509/ 01239015.1123 Conflictos de interés Los autores declaran no presentar conflictos de interés. Correspondencia Catalina Castañeda Motta Especialista en entrenamiento de la Especializa ción en Cirugía de Tórax, convenio Universidad El Bosque - Instituto Nacional de Cancerología, Bogotá, D. C., Colombia. Correo electrónico: catalina103_3@hotmail.com Characterization of patients with testicular germ cell tumors undergoing pulmonary metastasectomy: experience of a cancer center Caracterización de los pacientes con tumores de células germinales testiculares llevados a metastasectomía pulmonar: experiencia de un centro oncológico Fecha de sometimiento: Fecha de aceptación: Disponible en internet: 18/06/2025 12/05/2026 01/09/2026 Revista Colombiana de Cancerología 208 Conclusions: Pulmonary metastasectomy is a relevant therapeutic alternative in patients with testicular GCTs and residual pulmonary disease after chemotherapy. In this cohort, favorable survival outcomes were observed, especially in patients with clinical and histopathological characteristics linked to better prognosis in other studies",testicular neoplasms; lung neoplasms; metastasectomy; risk assessment; prognosis; survival rate,marcadores,international organ standard iso iso 56006,objective testicular germ cell tumor gcts lead cause cancer men aged 15 45 year management consist radical orchiectomy patient metastatic tumor adjuvant platinum-bas chemotherapy administer residual lung disease has been report 25 case follow first-line chemotherapy which pulmonary metastasectomy essential rule out residual tumor activity study aimed describe clinical outcom patient testicular gcts who underwent pulmonary metastasectomy between 2010 2023 after receiv chemotherapy instituto nacional de cancerologia inc colombia method descriptive longitudinal retrospective study conduct trend overall survival os progression-free survival pfs describ accord clinically relevant characteristic these patient result nineteen patient includ 24 month os 89 pfs 63 highest os pfs estimat observ patient metastatic lung disease diagnosi high os estimat also observ those low-risk prognostic classification accord international germ cell collaborative cancer group igcccg high pfs estimat observ patient histopathological finding non-viable tumor pulmonary resection follow chemotherapy catalina castaneda-motta1 rafael jose beltran-jimenez2 fernando alvarado-sarzosa2 miguel ricardo buitrago-ramirez2 marino cabrera-fierro3 ricardo elia bruges-maya5 marcela nunez-lemus6 carlo andr carvajal-fierro2 especialista en entrenamiento de la especializacion en cirugia de torax convenio universidad el bosque instituto nacional de cancerologia bogota colombia torax instituto nacional de cancerologia bogota colombia urologia instituto nacional de cancerologia bogota colombia unidad funcional clinica de urologia oncologica centro de tratamiento investigacion sobre cancer luis carlo sarmiento angulo ctic bogota colombia oncologia instituto nacional de cancerologia bogota colombia apoyo integral la gestion de la informacion instituto nacional de can