0123-9015,100-87-PB.pdf,100-87-PB_0,es,Characterization of patients with testicular germ cell tumors,"Objetivo: los tumores de células germinales (TCG) testiculares son la principal causa de cáncer en hombres con edades de 15 a 45 años. El tratamiento comprende la orquiectomía radical y, en pacientes con tumores metastásicos, se da manejo adyuvante con quimioterapia basada en platino. Se ha reportado enfermedad residual pulmonar posterior a la primera línea de quimioterapia en el 25,0 % de los casos, en los que la metastasectomía pulmonar es esencial para excluir actividad residual tumoral. El objetivo de este estudio consistió en describir los desenlaces clínicos de los pacientes con TCG testiculares llevados a metastasectomía pulmonar entre 2010 y 2023, tras recibir quimioterapia adyuvante, en el Instituto Nacional de Cancerología (INC) de Colombia. Métodos: se realizó un estudio descriptivo, longitudinal, retrospectivo. Se describieron las tendencias en la supervivencia global (SG) y en la supervivencia libre de progresión (SLP) según algunas características de relevancia clínica en estos pacientes. Resultados: se incluyeron 19 pacientes. A los 24 meses, la SG fue del 89,2 %, y la SLP fue del 63,6 %. Las mayores estimaciones de SG y SLP se observaron en pacientes con enfermedad metastásica pulmonar al momento del diagnóstico; además, se obtuvieron estimaciones altas de SG en aquellos con clasificación pronóstica de bajo riesgo según el Grupo Colaborativo Internacional sobre Cáncer de Células Germinales (IGCCCG) y de SLP en pa cientes con hallazgo histopatológico de ausencia de viabilidad tumoral en la resección pulmonar posterior a la quimioterapia. Conclusiones: la metastasectomía pulmonar constituye una alternativa terapéutica relevante en pacientes con TCG testiculares y enfermedad pulmonar residual tras quimioterapia. En esta cohorte se observaron resultados favorables de supervivencia, especialmente en pacientes con características clínicas e histopatológicas que otros estudios han vinculado con un mejor pronóstico",neoplasias testiculares; neoplasias pulmonares; metastasec tomía; medición de riesgo; pronóstico; tasa de supervivencia. Revista Colombiana de Cancerología C. Castañeda-Motta et al. 209,marcadores,characterization of patients with testicular germ cell tumors,objetivo tumor celul germinal tcg testicular son principal causa cancer hombr edad 15 45 anos tratamiento comprende orquiectomia radical pacient tumor metastasic da manejo adyuvante quimioterapia basada platino ha reportado enfermedad residual pulmonar posterior primera linea quimioterapia 25 casos metastasectomia pulmonar esencial excluir actividad residual tumoral objetivo este estudio consistio describir desenlac clinic pacient tcg testicular llevad metastasectomia pulmonar entre 2010 2023 tras recibir quimioterapia adyuvante instituto nacional cancerologia inc colombia metod realizo estudio descriptivo longitudinal retrospectivo describieron tendenci supervivencia global sg supervivencia libre progresion slp segun algun caracteristic relevancia clinica estos pacient resultad incluyeron 19 pacient 24 meses sg fue 89 slp fue 63 mayor estim sg slp observaron pacient enfermedad metastasica pulmonar momento diagnostico adem obtuvieron estim altas sg aquell clasificacion pronostica bajo riesgo segun grupo colaborativo internacional sobre cancer celul germinal igcccg slp pa cient hallazgo histopatologico ausencia viabilidad tumoral reseccion pulmonar posterior quimioterapia conclusion metastasectomia pulmonar constituye alternativa terapeutica relevante pacient tcg testicular enfermedad pulmonar residual tras quimioterapia esta cohorte observaron resultad favorabl supervivencia especial pacient caracteristic clinic histopatologic otros estudi han vinculado mejor pronostico,neoplasi testicular neoplasi pulmonar metastasec tomia medicion riesgo pronostico tasa supervivencia revista colombiana cancerologia castaneda-motta et 209,characterization of patients with testicular germ cell tumors objetivo tumor celul germinal tcg testicular son principal causa cancer hombr edad 15 45 anos tratamiento comprende orquiectomia radical pacient tumor metastasic da manejo adyuvante quimioterapia basada platino ha reportado enfermedad residual pulmonar posterior primera linea quimioterapia 25 casos metastasectomia pulmonar esencial excluir actividad residual tumoral objetivo este estudio consistio describir desenlac clinic pacient tcg testicular llevad metastasectomia pulmonar entre 2010 2023 tras recibir quimioterapia adyuvante instituto nacional cancerologia inc colombia metod realizo estudio descriptivo longitudinal retrospectivo describieron tendenci supervivencia global sg supervivencia libre progresion slp segun algun caracteristic relevancia clinica estos pacient resultad incluyeron 19 pacient 24 meses sg fue 89 slp fue 63 mayor estim sg slp observaron pacient enfermedad metastasica pulmonar momento diagnostico adem obtuvieron estim altas sg aquell clasificacion pronostica bajo riesgo segun grupo colaborativo internacional sobre cancer celul germinal igcccg slp pa cient hallazgo histopatologico ausencia viabilidad tumoral reseccion pulmonar posterior quimioterapia conclusion metastasectomia pulmonar constituye alternativa terapeutica relevante pacient tcg testicular enfermedad pulmonar residual tras quimioterapia esta cohorte observaron resultad favorabl supervivencia especial pacient caracteristic clinic histopatologic otros estudi han vinculado mejor pronostico neoplasi testicular neoplasi pulmonar metastasec tomia medicion riesgo pronostico tasa supervivencia revista colombiana cancerologia castaneda-motta et 209,1.0.0,f54df6e183af4ac5
0123-9015,100-87-PB.pdf,100-87-PB_1,en,con clasificación pronóstica de bajo riesgo según el Grupo Colaborativo,"Objective: Testicular germ cell tumors (GCTs) are the leading cause of cancer in men aged 15 to 45 years. Management consists of radical orchiectomy, and in patients with metastatic tumors, adjuvant platinum-based chemotherapy is administered. Residual lung disease has been reported in 25.0% of cases following first-line chemotherapy, in which pulmonary metastasectomy is essential to rule out residual tumor activity. This study aimed to describe the clinical outcomes of patients with testicular GCTs who underwent pulmonary metastasectomy between 2010 and 2023 after receiving chemotherapy at the Instituto Nacional de Cancerología (INC) in Colombia. Methods: A descriptive, longitudinal, retrospective study was conducted. Trends in overall survival (OS) and progression-free survival (PFS) were described according to clinically relevant characteristics in these patients. Results: Nineteen patients were included. At 24 months, OS was 89.2%, and PFS was 63.6%. The highest OS and PFS estimates were observed in patients with metastatic lung disease at diagnosis. High OS estimates were also observed in those with a low-risk prognostic classification according to the International Germ Cell Collaborative Cancer Group (IGCCCG), and high PFS estimates were observed in patients with histopathological findings of non-viable tumor at pulmonary resection following chemotherapy. Conclusions: Pulmonary metastasectomy is a relevant therapeutic alternative in patients with testicular GCTs and residual pulmonary disease after chemotherapy. In this cohort, favorable survival outcomes were observed, especially in patients with clinical and histopathological characteristics linked to better prognosis in other studies",testicular neoplasms; lung neoplasms; metastasectomy; risk assessment; prognosis; survival rate. Revista Colombiana de Cancerología C. Castañeda-Motta et al. 225,marcadores,con clasificacion pronostica de bajo riesgo segun el grupo colaborativo,objective testicular germ cell tumor gcts lead cause cancer men aged 15 45 year management consist radical orchiectomy patient metastatic tumor adjuvant platinum-bas chemotherapy administer residual lung disease has been report 25 case follow first-line chemotherapy which pulmonary metastasectomy essential rule out residual tumor activity study aimed describe clinical outcom patient testicular gcts who underwent pulmonary metastasectomy between 2010 2023 after receiv chemotherapy instituto nacional de cancerologia inc colombia method descriptive longitudinal retrospective study conduct trend overall survival os progression-free survival pfs describ accord clinically relevant characteristic these patient result nineteen patient includ 24 month os 89 pfs 63 highest os pfs estimat observ patient metastatic lung disease diagnosi high os estimat also observ those low-risk prognostic classification accord international germ cell collaborative cancer group igcccg high pfs estimat observ patient histopathological finding non-viable tumor pulmonary resection follow chemotherapy conclusion pulmonary metastasectomy relevant therapeutic alternative patient testicular gcts residual pulmonary disease after chemotherapy cohort favorable survival outcom observ especially patient clinical histopathological characteristic link better prognosi other studi,testicular neoplasm lung neoplasm metastasectomy risk assessment prognosi survival rate revista colombiana de cancerologia castaneda-motta et al 225,con clasificacion pronostica de bajo riesgo segun el grupo colaborativo objective testicular germ cell tumor gcts lead cause cancer men aged 15 45 year management consist radical orchiectomy patient metastatic tumor adjuvant platinum-bas chemotherapy administer residual lung disease has been report 25 case follow first-line chemotherapy which pulmonary metastasectomy essential rule out residual tumor activity study aimed describe clinical outcom patient testicular gcts who underwent pulmonary metastasectomy between 2010 2023 after receiv chemotherapy instituto nacional de cancerologia inc colombia method descriptive longitudinal retrospective study conduct trend overall survival os progression-free survival pfs describ accord clinically relevant characteristic these patient result nineteen patient includ 24 month os 89 pfs 63 highest os pfs estimat observ patient metastatic lung disease diagnosi high os estimat also observ those low-risk prognostic classification accord international germ cell collaborative cancer group igcccg high pfs estimat observ patient histopathological finding non-viable tumor pulmonary resection follow chemotherapy conclusion pulmonary metastasectomy relevant therapeutic alternative patient testicular gcts residual pulmonary disease after chemotherapy cohort favorable survival outcom observ especially patient clinical histopathological characteristic link better prognosi other studi testicular neoplasm lung neoplasm metastasectomy risk assessment prognosi survival rate revista colombiana de cancerologia castaneda-motta et al 225,1.0.0,4d60972a3e2c2a30
0123-9015,100-87-PB.pdf,100-87-PB_2,en,"73. Schirren J, Trainer S, Eberlein M, Lorch A, Beyer J, Bölükbas S.","Objective: To develop the translation and cross-cultural adaptation of the Cancer Loneliness Scale for use with cancer patients in Colombia. Methods: With authorization from the original authors, the translation and cross-cultural adaptation process was conducted in accordance with the procedure established by the EORTC Quality of Life Group to ensure semantic, conceptual, and cultural equivalence with the original English version. The process included independent forward translation by two translators, reconciliation, backward translation, and a pilot test for linguistic validation with 20 Colombian oncology patients treated at the Instituto Nacional de Cancerología. Results: The translations of the instructions and response options showed agreement between translators, requiring no modifications. During forward translation of the items, a discrepancy was identified regarding the adverb ""how often""; by consensus, the research team adopted the expression ""qué tan a menudo,"" for its greater semantic precision and appropriateness for Colombian Spanish. The adjustments made to two items CL3 and CL5 did not alter the original meaning. In the pilot test, most participants considered the statements clear and understandable, with no significant difficulties or offensive terms; therefore, the reconciled version was retained as the final version. Conclusion: A Colombian Spanish version of the Cancer Loneliness Scale was developed, demonstrating semantic, conceptual, and cultural equivalence to the original. This version constitutes the basis for evaluating its psychometric properties in Colombian cancer patients, a phase already completed and reported by the same research team as part of the project from which this work is derived","loneliness; surveys and questionnaires; neoplasms; translating; health impact assessment; reproducibility of results. Ana Milena Parra-Alfonso1 , Ricardo Sánchez-Pedraza1,2 1 Investigación Clínica, Instituto Nacional de Cancerología, Bogotá, D. C., Colombia. 2 Facultad de Medicina, Universidad Nacional de Colombia, Bogotá, D. C., Colombia. Citación Parra-Alfonso A, Sánchez-Pedraza R. Adaptac",marcadores,73 schirren trainer eberlein lorch beyer bolukba,objective develop translation cross-cultural adaptation cancer lonelines scale use cancer patient colombia method author original author translation cross-cultural adaptation proces conduct accordance procedure establish eortc quality life group ensure semantic conceptual cultural equivalence original english version proces includ independent forward translation two translator reconciliation backward translation pilot test linguistic validation 20 colombian oncology patient treat instituto nacional de cancerologia result transl instruction response option show agreement between translator requir no modific during forward translation item discrepancy identifi regard adverb how often consensu research team adopt expression que tan menudo its greater semantic precision appropriatenes colombian spanish adjustment made two item cl3 cl5 did not alter original mean pilot test most participant consider statement clear understandable no significant difficulti offensive term therefore reconcil version retain final version conclusion colombian spanish version cancer lonelines scale develop demonstrat semantic conceptual cultural equivalence original version constitut basi evaluat its psychometric properti colombian cancer patient phase already complet report same research team part project which work deriv,lonelines survey questionnair neoplasm translat health impact assessment reproducibility result ana milena parra-alfonso1 ricardo sanchez-pedraza1 investigacion clinica instituto nacional de cancerologia bogota colombia facultad de medicina universidad nacional de colombia bogota colombia citacion parra-alfonso sanchez-pedraza adaptac,73 schirren trainer e