0124-2121,8030_Educación+ambiental+y+derechos+de+la+Amazonia.pdf,8030_Educación+ambiental+y+derechos+de+la+Amazonia_0,en,"integración limitada de la educación climática. Se subraya la urgencia de reestructurar los PRAE,","Objective: to analyze the incorporation of the STC 4360 de 2018 Ruling in the School Environmental Projects (PRAE) in Florencia, Caquetá. Methodology: qualitative with an action-research design, reviewing the PRAE documents in 12 educational institutions. Semi-structured interviews were conducted with environmental education experts and local officials, to understand the current perspectives and practices around the implementation of the Ruling. Results: the findings revealed deficiencies in the implementation of the Ruling in the PRAE, especially in the teaching of climate change and the conservation of the Amazon. A poor alignment was observed between the PRAE and national and local policies in relation to climate change in addition to a limited integration of climate education. The urgency of restructuring the PRAE is underlined, adopting participatory approaches that promote scientific and investigative skills and a stronger environmental awareness of educational communities. Conclusion: greater coordination and monitoring is needed between educational and environmental policies to foster commitment to biodiversity conservation and climate change mitigation. This coordination is essential to train citizens in schools who are aware of and committed to contemporary environmental challenges, as well as to the care and preservation of the Amazon","environmental education, climate change, Amazon, conservation, STC 4360 de 2018 ruling, School Environmental Projects (PRAE)",marcadores,integracion limitada de la educacion climatica se subraya la urgencia de reestructurar los prae,objective analyze incorporation stc 4360 de 2018 ruling school environmental project prae florencia caqueta methodology qualitative action-research design review prae document