esion politic rendicion cuent configuran como escenario adaptacion individualizada emocional exigente conclusion adaptacion profesorado migrante requiere ser comprendida como fenomeno relacional condicionado cultura escolar politic educativ este panorama invita fortalecer estrategi acompanamiento reconocimiento profesional propiciar transicion reintegracion mas enriquecedora sistema educativo adaptacion diferencial migracion docent migrant sistema escolar como citar este articulo apa ferrada-quezada espinoza-espinoza 2026 adaptacion profesor migrant cultura sistema escolar chile educacion humanismo 28 50 pp 1-22 https doi org 10 17081 eduhum 28 50 8692 educacion humanismo vol 28 50 pp 1-22,1.0.0,73ef352823761216
0124-2121,8692-Adaptación+de+profesores+migrante+a+la+cultura.pdf,8692-Adaptación+de+profesores+migrante+a+la+cultura_0,en,apoyos formales y la presión de,"Objective: this study analyzes the professional adaptation experiences of migrant teachers to the culture and school system in Chile. Methodology: the study adopts a phenomenological approach and uses semi-structured interviews and a focus group with seven teachers trained abroad. The data were analyzed through an inductive thematic approach, which allowed the identification of common patterns and differences in their professional trajectories. Results: the findings indicate that the process of adaptation is neither linear nor uniform; rather, it involves complex processes of identity negotiation and professional reconstruction. These processes are shaped by various factors, including professional recognition, understanding of the national curriculum, and relationships with key school actors. It was also observed that institutional structures, the absence of formal support, and the pressure of accountability policies create a context of individualized and emotionally demanding adaptation. Conclusions: the study suggests that the adaptation of migrant teachers should be understood as a relational phenomenon shaped by school culture and educational policies. This context highlights the need to strengthen support and professional recognition strategies in order to facilitate a more comprehensive transition and reintegration into the education system","differential adaptation, migrant teachers, migration, school system",marcadores,apoyo formal la presion de,objective study analyz professional adaptation experienc migrant teacher culture school system chile methodology study adopt phenomenological approach uses semi-structur interview focu group seven teacher train abroad data analyz through inductive thematic approach which allow identification common pattern differenc their professional trajectori result finding indicate proces adaptation neither linear nor uniform rather involv complex process identity negotiation professional reconstruction these process shap variou factor includ professional recognition understand national curriculum relationship key school actor also observ institutional structur absence formal support pressure accountability polici create context individualiz emotionally demand adaptation conclusion study suggest adaptation migrant teacher should understood relational phenomenon shap school culture educational polici context highlight need strengthen support professional recognition strategi order facilitate more comprehensive transition reintegration into education system,differential adaptation migrant teacher migration school system,apoyo formal la presion de objective study analyz professional adaptation experienc migrant teacher culture school system chile methodology study adopt phenomenological approach uses semi-structur interview focu group seven teacher train abroad data analyz through inductive thematic approach which allow identification common pattern differenc their professional trajectori result finding indicate proces adaptation neither linear nor uniform rather involv complex process identity negotiation professional reconstruction these process shap variou factor includ professional recognition understand national curriculum relationship key school actor also observ institutional structur absence formal support pressure accountability polici create context individualiz emotionally demand adaptation conclusion study suggest adaptation migrant teacher should understood relational phenomenon shap school culture educational polici context highlight need strengthen support professional recognition strategi order facilitate more comprehensive transition reintegration into education system differential adaptation migrant teacher migration school system,1.0.0,99494e54bc0fcf1a
0124-2121,8710_Trayectorias+migratorias-educativas+de+estudiantes+venezolanos.pdf,8710_Trayectorias+migratorias-educativas+de+estudiantes+venezolanos_0,es,ARTÍCULO RESULTADO DE,"El artículo analizó las trayectorias migratorias-educativas de estudiantes venezolanos/as que asisten a la escuela primaria en Argentina y Chile. Objetivo: reconstruir sus experiencias, emociones y representaciones sociales en torno a dichas trayectorias, así como a su acceso y permanencia en los sistemas educativos de los países receptores. Metodología: estudio de casos múltiples en escuelas de la Ciudad Autónoma de Buenos Aires y la Región Metropolitana de Santiago con entrevistas en profundidad a estudiantes migrantes venezolanos. Resultados: se organizaron alrededor de cuatro núcleos temáticos: momentos previos a la migración, el viaje, primeros contactos con el sistema educativo del país receptor y constitución subjetiva como estudiantes migrantes venezolanos. A partir de su análisis se identificaron las siguientes categorías: ambivalencia de la experiencia emocional; ajenidad ante el nuevo contexto nacional y escolar; la escuela como punto de amortiguación; y modulaciones en la constitución subjetiva como estudiantes migrantes venezolanos. Conclusiones: la migración y la educación se configuran como procesos mutuamente imbricados, destacándose el valor heurístico del concepto trayectorias migratorias-educativas para comprenderlas","Argentina, Chile, escuela primaria, estudiantes migrantes, migración venezolana, trayectorias migratorias-educativas. Cómo citar este artículo (APA): Buratovich, P. (2026). Trayectorias migratorias-educativas de estudiantes venezolanos/as en Argentina y Chile. Educación y Humanismo, 28(50). 1-23. https://doi.org/10.17081/eduhum.28.50.8710 1 Doctorado en Ciencias Sociales de la FLACSO Argenti",marcadores,articulo resultado,articulo analizo trayectori migratorias-educativ estudiant venezolan as asisten escuela primaria argentina chile objetivo reconstruir sus 