0124-4108,4324-1151-PB.pdf,4324-1151-PB_6,en,eran un ciclo vicioso que afecta negativamente a la población,"Background: Currently, climate change and malnutrition are present in all countries worldwide. The double burden of nutrition at all levels is related to food security and climate change, not only regarding food availability but also due to phenomena such as economic crises, increasing food prices, acculturation, loss of food biodiversity, and the adop tion of new Westernized dietary patterns. Reflection: The interaction between the Double burden, food security, and climate change is a globally concerning issue that must be addressed beyond food availability, as it affects the health of millions of people worldwide and poses significant challenges to the sustainability and future of the planet. Conclu sion: The double burden of nutrition, food and nutrition security, and climate change constitute a triple challenge to global health. These three factors are closely interconnected and reinforce each other, creating a vicious cycle that negatively affects the world’s population, especially vulnerable communities","Climate change, food security, malnutrition, obesity, undernutrition, global health",marcadores,eran un ciclo vicioso que afecta negativamente la poblacion,background currently climate change malnutrition present all countri worldwide double burden nutrition all level relat food security climate change not only regard food availability but also due phenomena such economic cris increas food pric acculturation loss food biodiversity adop tion new westerniz dietary pattern reflection interaction between double burden food security climate change globally concern issue must address beyond food availability affect health million people worldwide pose significant challeng sustainability future planet conclu sion double burden nutrition food nutrition security climate change constitute triple challenge global health these three factor closely interconnect reinforce each other creat viciou cycle negatively affect world population especially vulnerable communiti,climate change food security malnutrition obesity undernutrition global health,eran un ciclo vicioso que afecta negativamente la poblacion background currently climate change malnutrition present all countri worldwide double burden nutrition all level relat food security climate change not only regard food availability but also due phenomena such economic cris increas food pric acculturation loss food biodiversity adop tion new westerniz dietary pattern reflection interaction between double burden food security climate change globally concern issue must address beyond food availability affect health million people worldwide pose significant challeng sustainability future planet conclu sion double burden nutrition food nutrition security climate change constitute triple challenge global health these three factor closely interconnect reinforce each other creat viciou cycle negatively affect world population especially vulnerable communiti climate change food security malnutrition obesity undernutrition global health,1.0.0,b95ee6755dda4b91
