0124-5376,BC-1291.pdf,BC-1291_0,en,(Elaeis spp.) de los Llanos,"This study describes the entomophagous habits of four species of armadillos (Cabassous unicinctus, Dasypus pastasae, Dasypus sabanicola, and Priodontes maximus) in oil palm (Elaeis spp.) agroecosystems in the Colombian Llanos Orientales. Through the analysis of 29 samples (23 excretions and 6 stomach contents) and the application of the Index of Relative Importance (IRI), the composition and relevance of arthropods in their diet were determined. The results classify the four species as opportunistic insectivores, with a clear preference for social insects and occasional consumption of other arthropods. These findings highlight the potential ecological role of armadillos in regulating invertebrate populations within agroecosystems","ecosystem services, biological control, neotropical savannas, mammal conservation, landscape ecology, agroindustrial matrices, entomophagy. ________________________________________________________________________________________________",marcadores,elaei spp de los llano,study describ entomophagou habit four speci armadillo cabassou unicinctu dasypu pastasae dasypu sabanicola priodont maximu oil palm elaei spp agroecosystem colombian llano oriental through analysi 29 sampl 23 excretion stomach content application index relative importance iri composition relevance arthropod their diet determin result classify four speci opportunistic insectivor clear preference social insect occasional consumption other arthropod these finding highlight potential ecological role armadillo regulat invertebrate popul within agroecosystem,ecosystem servic biological control neotropical savanna mammal conservation landscape ecology agroindustrial matric entomophagy ________________________________________________________________________________________________,elaei spp de los llano study describ entomophagou habit four speci armadillo cabassou unicinctu dasypu pastasae dasypu sabanicola priodont