0124-5376,BC-1306.pdf,BC-1306_0,en,Functional and taxonomic spatial structure of,"The distribution of vascular epiphytes on host trees has been linked to deterministic factors associated with host characteristics and microclimatic variation. To evaluate the taxonomic and functional spatial structure of vascular epiphytes in a lower montane cloud forest of the Colombian Andes, epiphytes were sampled following the SVERA protocol, and their position was recorded using Johansson’s zonation scheme. Taxonomic structure was assessed through patterns of species composition, richness, and diversity across host zones, while functional structure was evaluated using trait composition and functional indices: functional richness (FRic), functional evenness (FEve), and functional divergence (FDiv). Epiphytes showed higher abundance below the first branching zones (Z1 and Z2), which also exhibited the highest functional richness, encompassing most of the functional space on host trees. In contrast, specialized nutrient uptake strategies and CAM metabolism were more frequent in upper zones, suggesting environmental filtering along the host gradient. These results demonstrate clear taxonomic and functional spatial structuring of vascular epiphyte assemblages in this lower montane cloud forest","Andean biodiversity, canopy stratification, microclimatic gradients, trait-based ecology, community assembly processes. Arias, González & Zuluaga Functional and taxonomic spatial structure of vascular epiphytes BIOTA COLOMBIANA 27 - 2026 | 2",marcadores,functional taxonomic spatial structure,distribution vascular epiphyt host tree has been link deterministic factor associat host characteristic microclimatic variation evaluate taxonomic functional spatial structure vascular epiphyt lower montane cloud forest colombian ande epiphyt sampl follow svera protocol their position record using johansson zonation scheme taxonomic structure assess through pattern speci composition richnes diversity acros host zone while functional structure evaluat using trait composition functional indic functional richnes fric functional evennes feve functional divergence fdiv epiphyt show higher abundance below first branch zone z1 z2 which also exhibit highest functional richnes encompass most functional space host tree contrast specializ nutrient uptake strategi cam metabolism more frequent upper zone suggest environmental filter along host gradient these result demonstrate clear taxonomic functional spatial structur vascular epiphyte assemblag lower montane cloud forest,andean biodiversity canopy stratification microclimatic gradient trait-bas ecology community assembly process aria gonzalez zuluaga functional taxonomic spatial structure vascular epiphyt biota colombiana 27 2026,functional taxonomic spatial structure distribution vascular epiphyt host tree has been link deterministic factor associat host characteristic microclimatic variation evaluate taxonomic functional spatial structure vascular epiphyt lower montane cloud forest colombian ande epiphyt sampl follow svera protocol their position record using johansson zonation scheme taxonomic structure assess through pattern speci composition richnes diversity acros host zone while functional structure evaluat using trait composition functional indic functional richnes fric functional evennes feve functional divergence fdiv epiphyt show higher abundance below first branch zone z1 z2 which also exhibit highest functional richnes encompass most functional space host tree contrast specializ nutrient uptake strategi cam metabolism more frequent upper zone suggest environmental filter along host gradient these result demonstrate clear taxonomic functional spatial structur vascular epiphyte assemblag lower montane cloud forest andean biodiversity canopy stratification microclimatic gradient trait-bas ecology community assembly process aria gonzalez zuluaga functional taxonomic spatial structure vascular epiphyt biota colombiana 