comunicacion asertiva estrategi regulacion emocional concluye implementacion intervencion psicoeducativ este tipo favorece adaptacion educativa potencia habilidad socioemocional contribuye clima escolar positivo adaptacion estudiante aprendizaje socioemocional educacion resolucion problem,1.0.0,aa92b82726c64ffe
0124-5821,Art.+3.pdf,Art.+3_0,en,"ó un paradigma sociocrítico, con enfoque cualitativo y diseño de investigación acción,","In school settings, disruptive behaviors, defined as actions that interfere with academic activities and negatively affect school coexistence, constitute a significant pedagogical and psychoeducational challenge due to their impact on teaching and learning processes as well as on classroom and school climate dynamics. Within this framework, the present study examines the impact of an emotional management and problem-solving program on reducing disruptive behaviors among students in basic education. A qualitative approach was adopted, of the action research type and applying techniques such as performance tests, pedagogical workshops, functional analysis, and self-records with a sample of 30 students from grades 6, 7, and 8 in a school in Pasto, Colombia. Results show a 60% reduction in disruptive classroom behaviors and a 70% pass rate in formal subjects. Improvements were also found in inhibitory control, rule adherence, assertive communication, and emotional regulation strategies. It is concluded that the implementation of such psychoeducational interventions favors educational adaptation, enhances socio-emotional skills, and contributes to more harmonious and productive school environments. Gestión emocional y resolución | Revista Virtual Universidad Católica del Norte, 79, 61-86 ISSN: 0124-5821 (En línea) Gestión emocional y resolución 63",Student adjustment; Social and emotional learning; Education; Problem solving,marcadores,un paradigma sociocritico con enfoque cualitativo diseno de investigacion accion,school setting disruptive behavior defin action interfere academic activiti negatively affect school coexistence constitute significant pedagogical psychoeducational challenge due their impact teach learn process well classroom school climate dynamic within framework present study examin impact emotional management problem-solv program reduc disruptive behavior among student basic education qualitative approach adopt action research type apply techniqu such performance test pedagogical workshop functional analysi self-record sample 30 student grad school pasto colombia result show 60 reduction disruptive classroom behavior 70 pass rate formal subject improvement also found inhibitory control rule adherence assertive communication emotional regulation strategi conclud implementation such psychoeducational intervention favor educational adaptation enhanc socio-emotional skill contribut more harmoniou productive school environment gestion emocional resolucion revista virtual universidad catolica del norte 79 61-86 issn 0124-5821 en linea gestion emocional resolucion 63,student adjustment social emotional learn education problem solv,un paradigma sociocritico con enfoque cualitativo diseno de investigacion accion school setting disruptive behavior defin action interfere academic activiti negatively affect school coexistence constitute significant pedagogical psychoeducational challenge due their impact teach learn process well classroom school climate dynamic within framework present study examin impact emotional management problem-solv program reduc disruptive behavior among student basic education qualitative approach adopt action research type apply techniqu such performance test pedagogical workshop functional analysi self-record sample 30 student grad school pasto colombia result show 60 reduction disruptive classroom behavior 70 pass rate formal subject improvement also found inhibitory control rule adherence assertive communication emotional regulation strategi conclud implementation such psychoeducational intervention favor educational adaptation enhanc socio-emotional skill contribut more harmoniou productive school environment gestion emocional resolucion revista virtual universidad catolica del norte 79 61-86 issn 0124-5821 en linea gestion emocional resolucion 63 student adjustment social emo