0124-8170,Dialnet-ClasificacionDeMaduracionDelBananoUsandoModelacion-10775691.pdf,Dialnet-ClasificacionDeMaduracionDelBananoUsandoModelacion-10775691_0,en,ágenes. Los resultados confirman la viabilidad del uso de dispositivos móviles,"Globally, bananas are one of the most consumed fruits, representing a significant sector of the Colombian economy. Their stage of ripeness determines their quality, shelf life, and commer cial value; therefore, identifying the optimal harvest and marketing time is essential. Conventionally, this evaluation is manual and visual, which involves subjectivity and human error. This study pro poses an alternative based on artificial neural network modeling applied to digital images in the rgb color space, captured with mobile phones. Two artificial neural network models were developed and compared: a multilayer perceptron network (mlp) and a convolutional neural network (cnn). Both networks classified four ripening stages in Cavendish bananas. The mlp network achieved an over all accuracy of 0.77, demonstrating adequate performance for resource-constrained environments. The cnn network, for its part, achieved an accuracy of 0.99, with outstanding precision (0.98-1.00) and sensitivity (0.97-1.00) metrics, demonstrating its ability to extract relevant features directly from images. The results confirm the viability of using mobile devices as reliable capture tools and the po tential of neural network models for integration into real-time automatic classification applications. This work opens a future agenda focused on developing accessible solutions that drive the digital transformation of the Colombian banana sector",sensory analysis; deep learning; Cavendish; color science; Von Loesecke scale; Artificial Intelligence; fruit ripening; Musa sp. L.; artificial neural networks; artificial visión. Classificação de maturação da banana usando Modelagem Neural Artificial Aplicada ao espaço RGB em imagens,marcadores,agen los resultado confirman la viabilidad del uso de dispositivo movil,globally banana one most consum fruit represent significant sector colombian economy their stage ripenes determin their quality shelf life commer cial value therefore identify optimal harvest market time essential conventionally evaluation manual visual which involv subjectivity human error study pro pose alternative based artificial neural network model appli digital imag rgb color space captur mobile phon two artificial neural network model develop compar multilayer perceptron network mlp convolutional neural network cnn both network classifi four ripen stag cavendish banana mlp network achiev over all accuracy 77 demonstrat adequate performance resource-constrain environment cnn network its part achiev accuracy 99 outstand precision 98-1 00 sensitivity 97-1 00 metric demonstrat its ability extract relevant featur directly imag result confirm viability using mobile devic reliable capture tool po tential neural network model integration into real-time automatic classification applic work open future agenda focus develop accessible solution drive digital transformation colombian banana sector,sensory analysi deep learn cavendish color science von loesecke scale artificial intelligence fruit ripen musa sp artificial neural network artificial vision classificacao de maturacao da banana usando modelagem neural artificial aplicada ao espaco rgb em imagen,agen los resultado confirman la viabilidad del uso de dispositivo movil globally banana one most consum fruit represent significant sector colombian economy their stage ripenes determin their quality shelf life commer cial value therefore identify optimal harvest market time essential conventionally evaluation manual visual which involv subjectivity human error study pro pose alternative based artificial neural network model appli digital imag rgb color space captur mobile phon two artificial neural network model develop compar multilayer perceptron network mlp convolutional neural network cnn both network classifi four ripen stag cavendish banana mlp network achiev over all accuracy 77 demonstrat adequate performance resource-constrain environment cnn network its part achiev accuracy 99 outstand precision 98-1 00 sensitivity 97-1 00 metric demonstrat its ability extract relevant featur directly imag result confirm viability using mobile devic reliable capture tool po tential neural network model integration into real-time automatic classification applic work open future agenda focus develop accessible solution drive digital transformation colombian banana sector sensory analysi deep learn cavendish color science von loesecke scale artificial intelligence fruit ripen musa sp artificial neural network artificial vision classificacao de maturacao da banana usando modelagem neural artificial aplicada ao espaco rgb em imagen,1.0.0,1f891e496908af4a
0124-8170,Dialnet-DesarrolloDeUnPrototipoDeModeloCatastral3DAPartirD-10775688.pdf,Dialnet-DesarrolloDeUnPrototipoDeModeloCatastral3DAPartirD-10775688_0,es,"gíster en Ciencias – Estadística, Universidad Distrital Francisco José de Caldas. Bogotá, Colombia.","Este trabajo registra el desarrollo de la construcción de un prototipo de modelo catastral en 3D basado en CityGML 2,0, apoyado en FME y Google SketchUp, como herramientas de geoprocesa miento complementarias a los SIG. Este estudio está enfocado en el conjunto residencial Condominios II de Tejares, propiedad horizontal en Soacha (Cundinamarca); lugar en el cual se visualizó, mediante modelado 3D, los bienes privados y comunes de la copropiedad, para contribuir a diferentes aplica ciones catastrales. Representando el derecho real de la propiedad, demarcando los aspectos legales y físicos de la misma mediante un modelo interoperable. La metodología se centra en la recolección de datos, su procesamiento y almacenamiento; en el modelado 3D y su respectiva validación, con el fin de tener confiabilidad en los datos de representación y almacenamiento de los aspectos físicos y jurídicos en CityGML 2,0. El resultado permite, visualizar en un único modelo las relaciones entre objetos y los componentes físicos, jurídicos y económicos del catastro, incorporando características geométricas y semánticas, bajo estándares internacionales. Cumpliendo con el esquema y validación de geométrica en cada nivel de detalle (LOD), identificando que uno de los aspectos a mejorar es la autointersección de las diferentes geometrías para los diversos elementos modelados",cityGML; catastro 3D; catastro multipropósito; validación geométrica. Development of a Prototype of a 3D Cadastral Model Based on DOI: https://doi.org/10.18359/rcin.7882 2026 Editorial Neogranadina Revista Ciencia e Ingeniería Neogranadina enero - junio ISSN: 0124-8170 ▪ e-ISSN: 1909-7735 ■ 1-26 Vol. 36(1) 2 Geoprocessing Tools for the Visualization of the Legal and Physical Aspects of a Hor,marcadores,gister cienci estadistica universidad distrital francisco jose cald bogota colombia,este trabajo registra desarrollo construccion prototipo modelo catastral 3d basado citygml apoyado fme google sketchup como herramient geoprocesa miento complementari sig este estudio esta enfocado conjunto residencial condomini ii tejar propiedad horizontal soacha cundinamarca lugar cual visualizo mediante modelado 3d bien privad comun copropiedad contribuir diferent aplica cion catastral represent derecho real propiedad demarc aspect legal fisic misma mediante modelo interoperable metodologia centra recoleccion datos procesamiento almacenamiento modelado 3d respectiva validacion fin tener confiabilidad datos representacion almacenamiento aspect fisic juridic citygml resultado permite visualizar unico modelo relacion entre objet component fisic juridic economic catastro incorpor caracteristic geometric semantic bajo estandar internacional cumpl esquema validacion geometrica cada nivel detalle lod identific uno aspect mejorar autointerseccion diferent geometri divers element modelad,citygml catastro 3d catastro multiproposito validacion geometrica development of prototype of 3d cadastral model based on doi https doi org 10 18359 rcin 7882 2026 editorial neogranadina revista ciencia ingenieria neogranadina enero junio issn 0124-8170 e-issn 1909-7735 1-26 vol 36 geoprocessing tools for the visualization of the legal and physical aspects of hor,gister cienci estadistica universidad distrital francisco jose cald bogota colombia este trabajo registra desarrollo construccion prototipo modelo catastral 3d basado citygml apoyado fme google sketchup como herramient geoprocesa miento complementari sig este estudio esta enfocado conjunto residencial condomini ii tejar propiedad horizontal soacha cundinamarca lugar cual visualizo mediante modelado 3d bien privad comun copropiedad contribuir diferent aplica cion catastral represent derecho real propiedad demarc aspect legal fisic misma mediante modelo interoperable metodologia centra recoleccion datos procesamiento almacenamiento modelado 3d respectiva validacion fin tener confiabilidad datos representacion almacenamiento aspect fisic juridic citygml resultado permite visualizar unico modelo relacion entre objet component fisic juridic economic catastro incorpor caracteristic geometric semantic bajo estandar internacional cumpl esquema validacion geometrica cada nivel detalle lod identific uno aspect mejorar autointerseccion diferent geometri divers element modelad citygml catastro 3d catastro multiproposito validacion geometrica development of prototype of 3d cadastral model based on doi https doi org 10 18359 rcin 7882 2026 editorial neogranadina revista ciencia ingenieria neogranadina enero junio issn 0124-8170 e-issn 1909-7735 1-26 vol 36 geoprocessing tools for the visualization of the legal and physical aspects of hor,1.0.0,756fc3f5641ac750
0124-8170,Dialnet-DesarrolloDeUnPrototipoDeModeloCatastral3DAPartirD-10775688.pdf,Dialnet-DesarrolloDeUnPrototipoDeModeloCatastral3DAPartirD-10775688_0,en,n único modelo las relaciones entre,"This work records the development of the construction of a 3D cadastral model prototype based on CityGML 2.0, supported by FME and Google SketchUp, as geoprocessing tools complementa ry to GIS. This study is focused on the residential complex Condominios II de Tejares, a horizontal prop erty in Soacha (Cundinamarca); a place where private and common property of the co-ownership was visualized through 3D modeling to contribute to different cadastral applications. Representing the real right of property, delineating its legal and physical aspects through an interoperable model. The methodology focuses on the collection of data, its processing and storage; on 3D modeling and its respective validation, in order to have reliability in the data of representation and storage of the phys ical and legal aspects in CityGML 2.0. The result allows visualizing, in a single model, the relationships between objects and the physical, legal, and economic components of the cadastre, incorporating geometric and semantic characteristics, under international standards. Complying with the geomet ric scheme and validation at each level of detail (LOD), identifying that one of the aspects to improve is the self-intersection of the different geometries for the various modeled elements","CityGML; 3D Cadastre; Multipurpose Cadastre; Geometric Validation. Desenvolvimento de um Protótipo de Modelo Cadastral 3D Baseado em Ferramentas de Geoprocessamento para a Visualização dos Aspectos Legais e Físicos de uma Propriedade Horizontal no Município de Soacha, Cundinamarca",marcadores,unico modelo las relacion entre,work record development construction 3d cadastral model prototype based citygml support fme google sketchup geoprocess tool complementa ry gis study focus residential complex condominio ii de tejar h