1657-4702,00_b_editorial_RLB+26(1)+(2).pdf,00_b_editorial_RLB+26(1)+(2)_0,desconocido,00 b editorial RLB 26(1) (2),"1 Editorial / Editorial / Editorial DOI: https://doi.org/10.18359/rlbi.8468 * Editor – Revista Latinoamericana de Bioética. Associate Professor at. Email: revista.bioetica@unimilitar.edu.co. orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7125-4209 The Delhi Declaration on Artificial Intelligence (2026): Global Governance in the Age of Superintelligence Fabio Garzón-Díaz* The Delhi Declaration on Artificial Intelligence, signed in February 2026 during the AI Impact Summit in New Delhi, constitutes one of the broadest diplomatic agreements reached regarding this emerging technology (1). With the backing of 88 and 89 countries, including the United States, China, and the European Union, the document establishes global ethical principles and mechanisms for international cooperation in response to the rapid development of AI (1,2). This pact reflects the growing perception that AI has shifted from an experimental domain to a strategic infrastructure of global reach (3). Fundamental Principles The Declaration is structured around three main pillars: 1) Safety and Reliability: Signatories emphasize the importance of developing robust, reliable AI systems capable of minimizing risks and avoiding critical errors and harmful biases (2,5). 2) Ethics and Transparency: The consolidation of a global ethical framework is proposed as a common reference. Transparency in the design, development, and deployment of these systems is considered essential for building trust and facilitating international coope",,respaldo_sin_marcadores,00 editorial rlb 26,editorial editorial editorial doi http doi org 10 18359 rlbi 8468 editor revista latinoamericana bioetica associate professor email revista bioetica unimilitar edu co orcid http orcid org 0000-0001-7125-4209 delhi declaration artificial intelligence 2026 global governance age superintelligence fabio garzon-diaz delhi declaration artificial intelligence sign february 2026 during ai impact summit new delhi constitut one broadest diplomatic agreement reach regard emerg technology back 88 89 countri includ unit stat china european union document establish global ethical principl mechanism international cooperation response rapid development ai pact reflect grow perception ai has shift experimental domain strategic infrastructure global reach fundamental principl declaration structur around three main pillar safety reliability signatori emphasize importance develop robust reliable ai system capable minimiz risk avoid critical error harmful bias ethic transparency consolidation global ethical framework propos common reference transparency design development deployment these system consider essential build trust facilitat international coope,,00 editorial rlb 26 editorial editorial editorial doi http doi org 10 18359 rlbi 8468 editor revista latinoamericana bioetica associate professor email revista bioetica unimilitar edu co orcid http orcid org 0000-0001-7125-4209 delhi declaration artificial intelligence 2026 global governance age superintelligence fabio garzon-diaz delhi declaration artificial intelligence sign february 2026 during ai impact summit new delhi constitut one broadest diplomatic agreement reach regard emerg technology back 88 89 countri includ unit stat china european union document establish global ethical principl mechanism international cooperation response rapid development ai pact reflect grow perception ai has shift experimental domain strategic infrastructure global reach fundamental principl declaration structur around three main pillar safety reliability signatori emphasize importance develop robust reliable ai system capable minimiz risk avoid critical error harmful bias ethic transparency consolidation global ethical framework propos common reference transparency design development deployment these system consider essential build trust facilitat international coope,1.0.0,2504