1657-4702,05_7994_RLB+26(1)+(2).pdf,05_7994_RLB+26(1)+(2)_0,en,do la autonomía futura y redistribuyendo la agencia moral hacia actores actuales sin,"Germline genetic editing has radically expanded human capacities to intervene in the biological constitution of future individuals, raising unprecedented ethical challenges concerning identity, autonomy, and justice. This article examines the normative implications of such interventions through an interdisciplinary theoretical-normative approach, arguing that heritable modifications affect not only the biological and psychological dimensions of personal identity but also shape narrative and relational possibilities of the self, thereby compromising future autonomy and reallocating moral agency to present actors lacking direct legitimacy. Structural risks of inequality, stigmatization, and biotechnological exclusion are also identified. In response, the article proposes a transgenerational bioethical framework grounded in human dignity, protection of the open future, and inclusive justice, operationalized through multilevel governance structures and pluralistic public deliberation. This framework helps guide ethical decision-making in a global technoscientific context, fostering intergenerational responsibility and biopolitical equity",Germline genetic editing; personal identity; future autonomy; moral agency; intergenerational justice; normative bioethics. Identidade e agência moral: implicações normativas da edição genética germinal em contextos transgeracionais,marcadores,do la autonomia futura redistribuyendo la agencia moral hacia actor actual sin,germline genetic edit has radically expand human capaciti intervene biological constitution future individual rais unprecedent ethical challeng concern identity autonomy justice article examin normative implic such intervention through interdisciplinary theoretical-normative approach argu heritable modific affect not only biological psychological dimension personal identity but also shape narrative relational possibiliti self thereby compromis future autonomy reallocat moral agency present actor lack direct legitimacy structural risk inequality stigmat biotechnological exclusion also identifi response article propos transgenerational bioethical framework ground human dignity protection open future inclusive justice operationaliz through multilevel governance structur pluralistic public deliberation framework help guide ethical decision-mak global technoscientific context foster intergenerational responsibility biopolitical equity,germline genetic edit personal identity future autonomy moral agency intergenerational justice normative bioethic identidade agencia moral implicaco normativa da edicao genetica germinal em contexto transgeracionai,do la autonomia futura redistribuyendo la agencia moral hacia actor actual sin germline genetic edit has radically expand human capaciti intervene biological constitution future individual rais unprecedent ethical challeng concern identity autonomy justice article examin normative implic such intervention through interdisciplinary theoretical-normative approach argu heritable modific affect not only biological psychological dimension personal identity but also shape narrative relational possibiliti self thereby compromis future autonomy reallocat moral agency present actor lack direct legitimacy structural risk inequality stigmat biotechnological exclusion also identifi response article propos transgenerational bioethical framework ground human dignity protection open future inclusive justice operationaliz through multilevel governance structur pluralistic public deliberation framework help guide ethical decision-mak global technoscientific context foster intergenerational responsibility biopolitical equity germline genetic edit personal identity future autonomy moral agency intergenerational justice normative bioethic identidade agencia moral implicaco normativa da edicao genetica germinal em contexto transgeracionai,1.0.0,431ec06ea37eadb3
1657-4702,06_8027_RLB+26(1)+(3).pdf,06_8027_RLB+26(1)+(3)_0,es,Artículo de reflexión.,"La formulación del principio del doble efecto y su aplicación han sido objeto de intensos debates en los últimos años, debido a un historial de malentendidos o a aplicaciones incorrectas en el ámbito clínico. La bioética tiene una participación importante en las decisiones morales por su relación con la conducta humana, los principios y valores en los ámbitos de la vida y la salud, y por la aplicación del principio del doble efecto: en todo acto médico en el que el agente moral se encuentre obligado a actuar y la solución viable presente, al mismo tiempo, un efecto positivo y otro contrario a la beneficencia. Los médicos de cuidados intensivos y de urgencias deben conocer cómo aplicar el principio del doble efecto en el acto médico de la intubación orotraqueal y la ventilación mecánica ante situaciones especiales de patologías crónicas avanzadas que se presentan como insuficiencia respiratoria aguda. Para ello, se realizó una revisión no sistemática en PubMed y Google Scholar, así como en los buscadores Bioéticaweb y Bioéticawiki, para determinar cómo explicar los principios del doble efecto, de la proporcionalidad terapéutica y de la autonomía. Palabra clave: bioética; intubación orotraqueal; principio del doble efecto; enfermedad avanzada; insuficiencia respiratoria aguda; proporcionalidad; autonomía. doi: https://doi.org/10.18359/rlbi.8027 2 Bioethics and the Principle of Double Effect in the Medical Act of Orotracheal Intubation in Special Situations Abstract: The formulation of the principle of double effect and its application have been the subject of intense debate in recent years, due to a history of misunderstandings or incorrect applications in the clinical field. Bioethics plays a significant role in moral decision-making due to its connection to human behavior, principles, and values in the realms of life and health, as well as the application of the principle of double effect: in every medical act where the moral agent is compelled to act, the viable solution presents, simultaneously, a positive effect and one contrary to beneficence. Intensive care and emergency physicians must understand how to apply the principle of double effect in the medical act of orotracheal intubation and mechanical ventilation in special situations of advanced chronic pathologies that present as acute respiratory failure. To this end, a non-systematic review was conducted in PubMed and Google Scholar, as well as in the Bioéticaweb and Bioéticawiki search engines, to determine how to explain the principles of double effect, therapeutic proportionality, and autonomy",Bioethics; orotracheal intubation; principle of double effect; advanced illness; acute respiratory failure; proportionality; autonomy. Bioética e o Princípio do Duplo Efeito no Ato Médico de Intubação Orotraqueal em Situações Especiais,marcadores,articulo reflexion,formulacion principio doble efecto aplicacion han sido objeto intens debat ultim anos debido historial malentendid aplic incorrect ambito clinico bioetica tiene participacion importante decision moral relacion conducta humana principi valor ambit vida salud aplicacion principio doble efecto todo acto medico agente moral encuentre obligado actuar solucion viable presente mismo tiempo efecto positivo otro contrario beneficencia medic cuidad intensiv urgenci deben conocer como aplicar principio doble efecto acto medico intubacion orotraqueal ventilacion mecanica ante situ especial patologi cronic avanzad presentan como insuficiencia respiratoria aguda ello realizo revision no sistematica pubmed google scholar asi como buscador bioeticaweb bioeticawiki determinar como explicar principi doble efecto proporcionalidad terapeutica autonomia palabra clave bioetica intubacion orotraqueal principio doble efecto enfermedad avanzada insuficiencia respiratoria aguda proporcionalidad autonomia doi https doi org 10 18359 rlbi 8027 bioethics and t