1657-7027,7a1.pdf,7a1_0,en,tipo de metodología y variables,"Introduction: The Colombian health system has undergone a remarkable evolution since its inception, moving through various stages and transformations aimed at adapting to the changing needs of the population. The objective of this article is to analyze the challenges and trends of the Colombian health model based on a review of the published scientific literature. Methods: This study employed a qualitative, bibliographic, non-experimental, descriptive, and cross-sectional review approach, following the methodology proposed by Guevara. Information was obtained through four stages: (i) collection of the primary database; (ii) collection of the secondary database; (iii) identification of categories and bibliometric analysis; and (iv) interpretation and analysis. A total of 50 articles were initially selected, organized using reference managers and a search equation that facilitated their arrangement in the analysis matrix constructed by the research team. Subsequently, 20 articles were excluded due to methodological type and variables not directly related to the study. Finally, 30 investigations that met the inclusion criteria were analyzed. Results: The review identified the current landscape of the Colombian health system and possible improvement options that could contribute to better delivery of health services for all citizens. Conclusions: The current health system presents positive aspects; however, it is necessary to seek mechanisms to improve the implementation of primary care, the fiscal oversight of public resources, the hiring of health personnel, and the adjustment of the capitation payment unit (UPC). Additionally, efforts should focus on reducing or eliminating barriers to service delivery","Barriers to Access to Health Services, Health Care Economics and Organizations, Health Care Delivery, Health Systems, Social Security. Retos y tendencias del sistema de seguridad social en salud de Colombia: una revisión de la literatura*",marcadores,tipo de metodologia variabl,introduction colombian health system has undergone remarkable evolution since its inception moving through variou stag transform aimed adapt chang need population objective article analyze challeng trend colombian health model based review publish scientific literature method study employ qualitative bibliographic non-experimental descriptive cross-sectional review approach follow methodology propos guevara information obtain through four stag collection primary database ii collection secondary database iii identification categori bibliometric analysi iv interpretation analysi total 50 articl initially select organiz using reference manager search equation facilitat their arrangement analysi matrix construct research team subsequently 20 articl exclud due methodological type variabl not directly relat study finally 30 investig met inclusion criteria analyz result review identifi current landscape colombian health system possible improvement option could contribute better delivery health servic all citizen conclusion current health system present positive aspect however necessary seek mechanism improve implementation primary care fiscal oversight public resourc hiring health personnel adjustment capitation payment unit upc additionally effort should focu reduc eliminat barrier service delivery,barrier acces health servic health care economic organiz health care delivery health system social security reto tendencia del sistema de seguridad social en salud de colombia una revision de la literatura,tipo de metodologia variabl introduction colombian health system has undergone remarkable evolution since its inception moving through variou stag transform aimed adapt chang need population objective article analyze challeng trend colombian health model based review publish scientific literature method study employ qualitative bibliographic non-experimental descriptive cross-sectional review approach fol