1657-7663,"mprada,+a05v8n2.pdf","mprada,+a05v8n2_0",en,"Pontificia Universidad Javeriana, Sede Bogotá, Colombia","─ The following article presents a series of recommendations which should be taken into account when internationalized software is being developed. Internationalized software is software free of any cultural dependencies and it is also optimized to be located on another geographical region. First we present a brief introduction to the topic and the close relationship between software internationalization and software localization, and then 19 recommendations are presented in four first stages of the framework proposed by the SWEBOK[1]: requirements, design, development and testing","─ Software internationalization, i18n, Software localization, l10n, Globalization, Software engineering. I",marcadores,pontificia universidad javeriana sede bogota colombia,follow article present seri recommend which should taken into account when internationaliz software being develop internationaliz software software free any cultural dependenci also optimiz locat another geographical region first we present brief introduction topic close relationship between software international software local then 19 recommend present four first stag framework propos swebok requirement design development test,software international i18n software local l10n global software engineer,pontificia universidad javeriana sede bogota colombia follow article present seri recommend which should taken into account when internationaliz software being develop internationaliz software software free any cultural dependenci also optimiz locat another geographical region first we present brief introduction topic close relationship between software international software local then 19 recommend present four first stag framework propos swebok requirement design development test software international i18n software local l10n global software engineer,1.0.0,5127b6da68a71a33
1657-7663,"mprada,+a06v8n2.pdf","mprada,+a06v8n2_0",en,3D collaborative virtual environment for real-time GUI,"─ This paper describes the findings from 3 user studies conducted to identify the real functional and awareness information requirements of a group of graphical user interface (GUI) designers while they carry out a GUI sketching task. Special attention was paid to the natural and software restrictions, participants’ interaction and the way they use the information about the workspace, the team, the artifacts and the tasks. These findings are used in the design of a collaborative virtual environment in which designers can perform the task in a very natural, friendly and efficient way. The system built is explained in detail, remarking its architecture and functional improvements compared to similar existing programs. As future work, some already scheduled tasks are described and additional functionalities and possible improvements are proposed, so that the tool can be complemented","─ Awareness, Sketching, Prototyping, Collaborative virtual environments, graPhical user interfaces",marcadores,3d collaborative virtual environment real-time gui,paper describ finding user studi conduct identify real functional awarenes information requirement group graphical user interface gui designer while they carry out gui sketch task special attention paid natural software restriction participant interaction way they use information about workspace team artifact task these finding used design collaborative virtual environment which designer can perform task very natural friendly efficient way system built explain detail remark its architecture functional improvement compar similar exist program future work some already schedul task describ additional functionaliti possible improvement propos so tool can complement,awarenes sketch prototyp collaborative virtual environment graphical user interfac,3d collaborative virtual environment real-time gui paper describ finding user s