1657-7663,"mprada,+a10v8n2.pdf","mprada,+a10v8n2_0",en,s (SMA) constituyen un,"Multiagent Systems (MAS) are a computational paradigm in which several semi-autonomous agents interact with each other, either to solve a problem or achieve a number of individual or collective goals. Moreover, the production planning is a key activity in performance of the industry, so it is evident the need for applications that provide support in the development of these activities, to achieve the production goals with the maximum benefit. This work uses the MAS for solving the problem of Production Planning in Automation, specifically in the process of production of oil by gas-lift","─ MultiAgent systems, Industrial automation, Production planning, Artificial intelligence. I",marcadores,sma constituyen un,multiagent system mas computational paradigm which several semi-autonomou agent interact each other either solve problem achieve number individual collective goal moreover production plann key activity performance industry so evident need applic provide support development these activiti achieve production goal maximum benefit work uses mas solv problem production plann automation specifically proces production oil gas-lift,multiagent system industrial automation production plann artificial intelligence,sma constituyen un multiagent system mas computational paradigm which several semi-autonomou agent interact each other either solve problem achieve number individual collective goal moreover production plann key activity performance industry so evident need applic provide support development these activiti achieve production goal maximum benefit work uses mas solv problem production plann automation specifically proces production oil gas-lift multiagent system industrial automation production plann artificial intelligence,1.0.0,d2c3782c32d40828
1657-7663,"mprada,+a11v8n2.pdf","mprada,+a11v8n2_0",es,Pronóstico de la volatilidad usando perceptrones multicapa con funciones,"— Las redes neuronales artificiales han sido usadas exitosamente para la predicción de series de tiempo no lineales. En este artículo, se presenta una aproximación novedosa para modelar y pronosticar la volatilidad de una serie de tiempo financiera usando un perceptrón multicapa con una función adaptativa de activación; los parámetros del modelo son estimados maximizando el logaritmo natural de la función de verosimilitud de los residuos. Para garantizar que la varianza sea siempre cero o positiva, se impusieron algunas restricciones a la red neuronal artificial. Para evaluar habilidad predictiva de la aproximación propuesta, se compararon los pronósticos de un modelo ARCH y de la red neuronal; se encontró que la aproximación propuesta es capaz de pronosticar con mayor precisión la volatilidad que el modelo clásico","— ARCH no lineal, Modelos no lineales, Modelos de pronóstico, Heterocedasticidad, Modelos heterocedásticos condicionales, Precisión predictiva",marcadores,pronostico volatilidad usando perceptron multicapa funcion,-- redes neuronal artificial han sido usad exitosa prediccion seri tiempo no lineal este articulo presenta aproximacion novedosa modelar pronosticar volatilidad serie tiempo financiera usando perceptron multicapa funcion adaptativa activacion parametr modelo son estimad maximiz logaritmo natural funcion verosimilitud residu garantizar varianza sea siempre cero positiva impusieron algun restriccion red neuronal artificial evaluar habilidad predictiva aproximacion propuesta compararon pronostic modelo arch red neuronal encontro aproximacion propuesta capaz pronosticar mayor precision volatilidad modelo clasico,-- arch no lineal model no lineal model pronostico heterocedasticidad model heterocedastic condicional precision predictiva,pronostico volatilidad usando perceptron multicapa funcion -- redes neuronal artificial 