1657-9534,v56n2e2006613+Ing.pdf,v56n2e2006613+Ing_0,en,ORIGINAL ARTICLE,"Background: Although hormone therapy is a cornerstone in the treatment of breast cancer, low therapeutic adherence is commonly reported, and there is limited evidence on the predictors that contribute to improving adherence in this population. Objective: To identify factors associated with adherence to hormone therapy in women with breast cancer, in an oncology clinic in Medellín-Colombia (2019- 2023). Methods: Cross-sectional analytical study. Women >18 years old with hormone receptor-positive breast cancer who were undergoing hormone therapy were included. The MMAS-8 scale was used to measure and classify therapeutic adherence into three levels: low, medium, and high. Data was analyzed by multinomial logistic regression. Results: One hundred seventy-eight patients with a median age of 64.0 years were included. 50.0% were treated with tamoxifen. The prevalence of non-adherence was 48.9%. 70.2% had adverse effects of hormone therapy, and forgetfulness was the main reason for discontinuation (76.19%). Age was associated with therapeutic adherence, with older women being the most adherent (83.5%). Women with adverse effects, stage III-IV, low socioeconomic and educational level, and a lack of support network had lower therapeutic adherence. Conclusions: A high prevalence of moderate and low therapeutic adherence is demonstrated in younger women from lower socioeconomic and educational backgrounds. Preventive strategies are needed to mitigate factors that negatively influence therapeutic adherence. Citation: Puerta AK, Lema CC, Lema MM, Villa GP. Adherence with hormonal therapy in women with breast cancer: a cross-sectional study in Medellin, Colombia. Colomb Méd (Cali), 2025; 56(2):e2026613 http://doi.org/10.25100/ cm.v56i2.6613 Received: 11 dec 2024 Revised: 24 mar 2025 Accepted : 05 jun 2025 Published: 16 jun 2025",Treatment adherence and compliance; medication adherence; breast neoplasms; tamoxifen; drug-related side effects; adverse reactions Palabras clave Adherencia; cumplimiento del tratamiento; adherencia a la medicación; Neoplasias de Mama; Tamoxifeno; Efectos Secundarios; Reacciones Adversas a los Medicamentos. Copyright: © 2025 Universidad del Valle OPEN ACCESS CrossMark English version Ver,marcadores,original article,background although hormone therapy cornerstone treatment breast cancer low therapeutic adherence commonly report there limit evidence predictor contribute improv adherence population objective identify factor associat adherence hormone therapy women breast cancer oncology clinic medellin-colombia 2019- 2023 method cross-sectional analytical study women 18 year old hormone receptor-positive breast cancer who undergo hormone therapy includ mmas-8 scale used measure classify therapeutic adherence into three level low medium high data analyz multinomial logistic regression result one hundr seventy-eight patient median age 64 year includ 50 treat tamoxifen prevalence non-adherence 48 70 had adverse effect hormone therapy forgetfulnes main reason discontinuation 76 19 age associat therapeutic adherence older women being most adherent 83 women adverse effect stage iii-iv low socioeconomic educational level lack support network had lower therapeutic adherence conclusion high prevalence moderate low therapeutic adherence demonstrat younger women lower socioeconomic educational background preventive strategi need mitigate factor negatively influence therapeutic adherence citation puerta ak lema cc lema mm villa gp adherence hormonal therapy women breast cancer cross-sectional study medellin colombia colomb med cali 2025 56 e2026613 http doi org 10 25100 cm v56i2 6613 receiv 11 dec 2024 revis 24 mar 2025 accept 05 jun 2025 publish 16 jun 2025,treatment adherence compliance medication adherence breast neoplasm tamoxifen drug-relat side effect adverse reaction palabra clave adherencia cumplimiento del tratamiento adherencia la medicacion neopla