1692-5777,173-129-PB.pdf,173-129-PB_1,en,"Yoon, H.-J. (2016). Association strength of verb-noun collocations in English L2",", Introduction, Literature Review, Methodology, Results, Discussion, and Conclusion. AI was used to structure arguments, organize content, improve clarity, and synthesize information. All AIgenerated suggestions were thoroughly reviewed, critically evaluated, and edited by the author before inclusion in the final manuscript. The author bears full responsibility for all content and confirms that the use of AI has not altered the research methodology, data analysis, scientific findings, or fundamental contributions of the study. No AI tools were used to generate or modify images, graphics, or figures. The manuscript preparation has followed GiST’s ethical guidelines and editorial policies regarding AI usage. Author Liya Xue is a University Lecturer at the School of International Studies, Zhejiang University, China. She holds a PhD in Linguistics and Applied Linguistics from Zhejiang University. Her research interests include speech prosody, second language acquisition, lexical chunk instruction, technology- enhanced language learning, and the application of generative AI in EFL contexts. She has published on data-driven learning and formulaic language in international peer-reviewed journals. ORCID: https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5751-2099 36 No. 32 - ISSN 1692-5777 ChatGPT Chunking Strategies in EFL Classrooms How to reference this article: Xue, L. (2026). Why Chunks Go Unnoticed: A Longitudinal Study of a ChatGPT-Aided Chunking Approach in EFL Classrooms . GIST – Education and Learning Research Journal, 32(32). https://doi.org/10.26817/16925777.2153 The Role of Generative AI and Peer Feedback in Cooperative Writing Within a Feedforward Pedagogy: A Study of Iranian IELTS Test Takers El papel de la IA generativa y la retroalimentación entre pares en la escritura cooperativa dentro de una pedagogía de feedforward: un estudio de los examinados IELTS en Irán. Amir Ghajarieh1, Narges Sardabi2 & Shiva Roostan3 English Department, Ershad Damavand University, Tehran, Iran Received: February 8, 2026 / Accepted: June 24, 2026 1 ghajarieh.amir@edamavandihe.ac.ir 2 n.sardabi@e-damavandihe.ac.ir 3 shivaroostan88@gmail.com 37 No. 32 - ISSN 1692-5777 Gist Education and Learning Research Journal. ISSN 1692-5777. No. 32 (January - June, 2026). pp. 37-57. 38 No. 32 - ISSN 1692-5777 Abstract Despite growing evidence for Artificial Intelligence (AI) in writing, little is known about combining Generative AI (GenAI) with peer feedback in L2 writing instruction. This mixedmethods study, grounded in AI-assisted language learning and collaborative learning theory, investigated the hybrid effect of GenAI and peer feedback through cooperative learning on the Writing Task 2 performance of 60 Iranian IELTS candidates. The experimental group received instruction integrating ChatGPT-5 and peer corrective feedback within cooperative activities, while the control group received parallel teacher-led instruction without GenAI feedback or structured peer collaboration. Pre- and posttests, assessed by certified examiners, showed that the experimental group improved significantly in grammatical accuracy, lexical range, and discourse organization. Questionnaires and semi-structured interviews revealed that students perceived cooperative learning favorably and found GenAI feedback timely and useful for internalizing corrections, while peer collaboration reduced anxiety and enhanced idea development. Findings underscore the potential of large language models combined with peer feedforward to foster more effective and confident L2 writing, with implications for technologyenhanced instruction in high-stakes test preparation","Education Quality, Cooperative/collaborative learning, Distance education and online learning, Generative AI–Assisted Feedback, Hybrid Feedback Pedagogy",marcadores,yoon -j 2016 association strength verb-noun colloc english l2,in