1692-5777,173-129-PB.pdf,173-129-PB_4,en,"cle: Zaimoglu, S. (2026). Teaching English in the Age of Screens:","Inclusive education has become a universal human right. This type of education requires teachers to use teaching strategies that ensure both regular students and those with disabilities or neurodivergence receive the same learning opportunities. Consequently, this article aims to describe the challenges that undergraduate English language professors face when teaching English to students with disabilities or neurodivergence. Based on a qualitative case study, undergraduate English language teachers at a public university located in a southeastern state of México participated in a research interview. It was found that most of these teachers believed that having a disability or neurodivergence is not an impediment to studying a bachelor’s degree in English. However, a latent challenge for the participants was their lack of knowledge of teaching strategies for inclusive education, as well as the limited availability of educational resources for creating an inclusive language classroom. These results highlight the need for university professors to take courses on implementing inclusive education in the teaching of English as a foreign language","Challenges, Disability, Educative inclusion, English teaching, Neurodivergence",marcadores,cle zaimoglu 2026 teach english age screen,inclusive education has become universal human right type education requir teacher use teach strategi ensure both regular student those disabiliti neurodivergence receive same learn opportuniti consequently article aims describe challeng undergraduate english language professor face when teach english student disabiliti neurodivergence based qualitative case study undergraduate english language teacher public university locat southeastern state mexico participat research interview found most these teacher believ having disability neurodivergence not impediment study bachelor degree english however latent challenge participant their lack knowledge teach strategi inclusive education well limit availability educational resourc creat inclusive language classroom these result highlight need university professor take cours implement inclusive education teach english foreign language,challeng disability educative inclusion english teach neurodivergence,cle zaimoglu 2026 teach english age screen inclusive education has become universal human right type education requir teacher use teach strategi ensure both regular student those disabiliti neurodivergence receive same learn opportuniti consequently article aims describe challeng undergraduate english language professor face when teach english student disabiliti neurodivergence based qualitative case study undergraduate english language teacher public university locat southeastern state mexico participat research interview found most these teacher believ having disability neurodivergence not impediment study bachelor degree english however latent challenge participant their lack knowledge teach strategi inclusive education well limit availability educational resourc creat inclusive language classroom these result highlight need university professor take cours implement inclusive education teach english foreign language challeng disability educative inclusion english teach neurodivergence,1.0.0,5c55ca0fe3bac057
1692-5777,173-129-PB.pdf,173-129-PB_4,es,"English to students with disabilities or neurodivergence. Based on a qualitative case study,","La educación inclusiva se ha convertido en un derecho humano universal. Este tipo de educación requiere que los docentes empleen estrategias de enseñanza que garanticen que tanto los estudiantes regulares como aquellos con discapacidad o neurodivergencia reciban las mismas oportunidades de aprendizaje. Este artículo tiene como objetivo describir los desafíos que enfrentan los profesores universitarios de licenciatura en inglés al enseñar esta lengua a estudiantes con discapacidad o neurodivergencia. A partir de un estudio de caso cualitativo, profesores de licenciatura en inglés de una universidad pública ubicada en un estado del sureste de México participaron en una entrevista de investigación. Se encontró que la mayoría de estos docentes consideraba que tener una discapacidad o neurodivergencia no es un impedimento para cursar una licenciatura en inglés. Sin embargo, un desafío latente para los participantes fue su falta de conocimiento sobre estrategias de enseñanza para la educacióeducación inclusiva, así como la limitada disponibilidad de recursos educativos para crear un aula de idiomas incluyente. Estos resultados resaltan la necesidad de que los profesores universitarios tomen cursos sobre la implementación de la educación inclusiva en la enseñanza del inglés como lengua extranjera",Desafíos; Discapacidad; Inclusión educativa; Enseñanza del inglés; Neurodivergencia Faculty Perspectives on Equity and Inclusion 115 No. 32 - ISSN 1692-5777,marcadores,english to students with disabiliti or neurodivergence based on qualitative case study,educacion inclusiva ha convertido derecho humano universal este tipo educacion requiere docent empleen estrategi ensenanza garanticen tanto estudiant regular como aquell discapacidad neurodivergencia reciban mism oportunidad aprendizaje este articulo tiene como objetivo describir desafi enfrenta