1692-5777,173-129-PB.pdf,173-129-PB_5,en,a Mexican University .,"English has become a medium for intercultural communication, providing access to science, education, technology, business, and information. In education, it serves not only as a communicative tool but as a means to raise awareness of global challenges. Consequently, the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) have received increasing attention in educational research and policy worldwide, including in Colombia. However, limited attention has been paid to how SDG-related themes are represented in English language teaching (ELT) materials, particularly in higher education contexts. This study analyzes the presence and promotion of the 2030 Agenda in English courses at a private Colombian university, examining materials from both a Foreign Languages Teacher Education Program (FLTEP) and a Language Center (LC), and exploring the views of English embedded in these materials (Cates, 2022). Through a mixedmethods content analysis of 828 materials, including class presentations, texts, and audiovisual and digital resources collected during the first semester of 2024, the findings highlight the need to move beyond narrowly linguistic approaches toward more critical, action-oriented materials that promote English as a tool for intercultural dialogue and social engagement. While there is a growing awareness of global issues in this context, the limited explicit integration of the SDGs across courses suggests that institutional support and teachers’ agency are still needed to strengthen this alignment",ELT teaching and learning materials; Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs); views of English; Education for Sustainable Development (ESD); content analysis,marcadores,mexican university,english has become medium intercultural communication provid acces science education technology busines information education serv not only communicative tool but mean raise awarenes global challeng consequently sustainable development goal sdgs have receiv increas attention educational research policy worldwide includ colombia however limit attention has been paid how sdg-relat them represent english language teach elt material particularly higher education context study analyz presence promotion 2030 agenda english cours private colombian university examin material both foreign languag teacher education program fltep language center lc explor view english embedd these material cate 2022 through mixedmethod content analysi 828 material includ clas present text audiovisual digital resourc collect during first semester 2024 finding highlight need move beyond narrowly linguistic approach toward more critical action-orient material promote english tool intercultural dialogue social engagement while there grow awarenes global issu context limit explicit integration sdgs acros cours suggest institutional support teacher agency still need strengthen alignment,elt teach learn material sustainable development goal sdgs view english education sustainable development esd content analysi,mexican university english has become medium intercultural communication provid acces science education technology busines information education serv not only communicative tool but mean raise awarenes global challeng consequently sustainable development goal sdgs have receiv increas attention educational research policy worldwide includ colombia however limit attention has been paid how sdg-relat them represent english language teach elt material particularly higher education context study analyz presence promotion 2030 agenda english cours private colombian university examin material both foreign languag teacher education program fltep language center lc explor view english embedd these material cate 2022 through mixedmethod content analysi 828 material includ clas present text audiovisual digital resourc collect during first semester 2024 finding highlight need move beyond narrowly linguistic approach toward more critical action-orient material promote english tool intercultural dialogue social engagement while there grow awarenes global issu context limit explicit integration sdgs acros cours suggest institutional support teacher agency still need strengthen alignment elt teach learn material sustainable development goal sdgs view english education sustainable development esd content analysi,1.0.0,6af13290dc3b802e
1692-5777,173-129-PB.pdf,173-129-PB_5,es,"nd a Language Center (LC),","El inglés se ha convertido en un medio de comunicación intercultural que facilita el acceso a la ciencia, la educación, la tecnología, los negocios y la información. En el ámbito educativo, no solo funciona como herramienta comunicativa, sino también como n medio para generar conciencia sobre los desafíos globales. En consecuencia, los Objetivos de Desarrollo Sostenible (ODS) han recibido una atención creciente en la investigación educativa y en las políticas públicas en todo el mundo, incluida Colombia. Sin embargo, se ha prestado poca atención a cómo se representan los temas relacionados con los ODS en los materiales de enseñanza de inglés como lengua extranjera (ELT), particularmente en contextos de educación superior. Este estudio analiza la presencia y promoción de la Agenda 2030 en cursos de inglés de una universidad privada colombiana, examinando materiales tanto de un Programa de Licenciatura en Lenguas Extranjeras (FLTEP) como de un Centro de Idiomas (LC), y explorando las visiones del inglés presentes en dichos materiales (Cates, 2022). A través de un análisis de contenido de métodos mixtos aplicado a 828 materiales, incluyendo presentaciones de clase, textos y recursos audiovisuales y digitales recolectados durante el primer semestre de 2024, los hallazgos resaltan la necesidad de trascender los enfoques estrictamente lingüísticos hacia materiales más críticos y orientados a la acción, que promuevan el inglés como herramienta de diálogo intercultural y compromiso social. Si bien existe una conciencia creciente sobre los problemas globales en este contexto, la limitada integración explícita de los ODS en los cursos sugiere que aún se requiere apoyo institucional y agencia docente para fortalecer esta articulación. SDGs in English Language Teaching Materials 139 No. 32 - ISSN 1692-5777",Materiales de enseñanza y aprendizaje de ELT; Objetivos de Desarrollo Sostenible (ODS); Visiones del inglés; Educación para el Desarrollo Sostenible (EDS); Análisis de contenido,marcadores,nd language center lc,ingl ha convertido medio comunicacion intercultural facilita acceso ciencia educacion tecnologia negoci informacion ambito educativo no solo funciona como herramienta comunicativa sino tambien como medio generar conciencia sobre desafi global consecuencia objetiv desarrollo sostenible ods han recibido atencion creciente investigacion educativa politic public todo mundo incluida colombia sin embargo ha prestado poca atencion como representan temas relacionad ods material ensenanza ingl como lengua extranjera elt particular context educacion superior este estudio analiza presencia promocion agenda 2030 curs ingl universidad privada colombiana examin material tanto programa licenciatura lengu extranjer fltep como centro idiom lc explor vision ingl present dich material cates 2022 trav analisis contenido metod mixt aplicado 828 material incluyendo present clase text recurs audiovisual digital recolectad durante primer semestre 2024 hallazg resaltan necesidad trascender enfoqu estricta linguistic hacia material mas critic orientad accion promuevan ingl como herramienta dialogo intercultural compromiso social si bien existe conciencia creciente sobre problem global este contexto limitada integracion explicita ods curs sugiere aun requiere apoyo institucional agencia docente fortalecer esta articulacion sdgs in english language teaching materials 139 no 32 issn 1692-5777,material ensenanza aprendizaje elt objetiv desarrollo sostenible ods vision ingl educacion desarrollo sostenible eds analisis contenido,nd language center lc ingl ha convertido medio comunicacion intercultural facilita acceso ciencia educacion tecnologia negoci informacion ambito educativo no solo funciona como herramienta comunicativa sino tambien como medio generar conciencia sobre desafi global consecuencia objetiv desarrollo sostenible ods han recibido atencion creciente investigacion educativa politic public todo mundo incluida colombia sin embargo ha prestado poca atencion como representan temas relacionad ods material ensenanza ingl como lengua extranjera elt particular context educacion superior este estudio analiza presencia promocion agenda 2030 curs ingl universidad privada colombiana examin material tanto programa licenciatura lengu extranjer fltep como centro idiom lc explor vision ingl present dich material cates 2022 trav analisis contenido metod mixt aplicado 828 material incluyendo present clase text recurs audiovisual digital recolectad durante primer semestre 2024 hallazg resaltan necesidad trascender enfoqu estricta linguistic hacia material mas critic orientad accion promuevan ingl como herramienta dialogo intercultural compromiso social si bien existe conciencia creciente sobre problem global este contexto limitada integracion explicita ods curs sugiere aun requiere apoyo institucional agencia docente fortalecer esta articulacion sdgs in english language teaching materials 139 no 32 issn 1692-5777 material ensenanza aprendizaje elt objetiv desarrollo sostenible ods vision ingl educacion desarrollo sostenible eds analisis contenido,1.0.0,3fc25a88b4a3904e
1692-5777,173-129-PB.pdf,173-129-PB_6,en,erials at a private Colombian university,"We investigated the use of hedges within Interactive Meta Discourse Markers (IMDM) in a longitudinal learner corpus, comprising one semester of written data from 35 tertiary-level EFL students. The analysis involved both group-level observations to track collective trends in hedge usage over time and individual-level analyses focusing on five students’ use of hedges throughout the semester. A frequency-based approach was employed to identify the most common hedges, which were then compared to native-speaker data to assess similarities and differences, as well as the collective tendencies of both groups regarding hedge usage. The findings revealed that should was the most frequently used hedge in the non-native corpus, with students notably not employing noun phrases in their arguments. The common hedging expressions suggested a pattern of authorial stance, and log-likelihood analysis showed similarities in hedge use. A comparison of the most frequently used hedges indicated an overuse of should within the non-native corpus. Additionally, a correlation was observed between students’ use of hedges and their exam performance over the semester, alongside positive interaction evident in the collective analysis","Metadiscourse, Hedges, Learner Corpus, Argumentation, Stance",marcadores,erial private colombian university,we investigat use hedg within interactive meta discourse marker imdm longitudinal learner corpu compris one semester written data 35 tertiary-level efl student analysi involv both group-level observ track collective trend hedge usage over time individual-level analys focus five student use hedg throughout semester frequency-bas approach employ identify most common hedg which then compar native-speaker data asses similariti differenc well collective tendenci both group regard hedge usage finding reveal should most frequently used hedge non-native corpu student notably not empl