1692-6013,NOVUM+JUS+20-2+art+3+EL+CIBERPODER.pdf,NOVUM+JUS+20-2+art+3+EL+CIBERPODER_0,en,rsidad Sergio Arboleda; Ph. D. en Derecho,"This article aims to determine how the consolidation of a State’s digital sovereignty, given its capacity to exercise autonomous control over its digital resources, information systems, and technological platforms, constitutes the highest expression of state cyberpower. To this end, it analyzes the constituent elements of digital sovereignty—critical infrastructure, data flows, regulatory frameworks, emerging technologies, and strategic inputs—and argues that all of them may be protected or compromised through the deployment of cyberpower. It also examines the relationship between States and transnational technology companies, revealing structural tensions and scenarios of regulatory subordination. The study concludes that cyberpower, beyond its defensive function, should be understood as an active tool of digital governance capable of influencing regulatory formulation, infrastructure protection, diplomatic action, and sovereign technological development. Within this framework, digital sovereignty is redefined as a dynamic and contested construct that depends on the strategic articulation of national cyber capabilities",cyberpower; digital sovereignty; technological hegemony; cybersecurity; digital governance 81 El ciberpoder como capacidad estratégica para consolidar la soberanía digital NOVUM JUS • ISSN: 1692-6013 • E-ISSN: 2500-8692 • Volumen 20 No. 2 • mayo-agosto 2026 • Págs. 79-105,marcadores,rsidad sergio arboleda ph en derecho,article aims determine how consolidation state digital sovereignty given its capacity exercise autonomou control over its digital resourc information system technological platform constitut highest expression state cyberpower end analyz constituent element digital sovereignty--critical infrastructure data flow regulatory framework emerg technologi strategic inputs--and argu all them may protect compromis 