1692-7427,Art04_2026.pdf,Art04_2026_0,en,"Nieto Rojas, S., &","Introduction. University students play a dual role that combines their academic studies and sporting activities, which requires them to strike a balance between the two. Objective. The purpose was to understand the relationship between academic commitment and athletic performance in Colombian student-athletes. Method. Qualitative study of an interpretative-hermeneutic nature. The sample consisted of 11 studentathletes who were enrolled in the 2025-1 semester. A semi-structured interview was designed and validated by three experts in qualitative research. The categories identified were: i) sociodemographic profile of the students; ii) considerations of athletic performance; iii) considerations of academic commitment; iv) student-athlete relationship; v) factors influencing the student-athlete relationship. Results. Student-athletes mentioned that their social environments (friends, classmates, and coaches), demographics (place of residence and study), and family (parents, siblings, grandparents, friends) influenced their choice of sport to a certain extent. In addition, their sporting contexts gave them the perspective and vision to choose a professional career related to their role as athletes. Conclusion. There are factors that influence the pursuit of sports and academic activities, some of which were repeatedly mentioned by the participants interviewed. The main factors were: i) sociodemographic factors associated with travel (distance from training venues, university, home, and/or work); ii) economic factors (transportation, food, academic or sports expenses, travel, etc.); iii) academic factors, among which curricular flexibility stands out (severity with regard to academic absences, make-up activities, etc.)","undergraduate education, graduate student, athletic competition, education, college sports. internacional Creative Commons AtribuciónNoComercialSinDerivadas 4.0. 1",marcadores,nieto roja,introduction university student play dual role combin their academic studi sport activiti which requir them strike balance between two objective purpose understand relationship between academic commitment athletic performance colombian student-athlet method qualitative study interpretative-hermeneutic nature sample consist 11 studentathlet who enroll 2025-1 semester semi-structur interview design validat three expert qualitative research categori identifi sociodemographic profile student ii consider athletic performance iii consider academic commitment iv student-athlete relationship factor influenc student-athlete relationship result student-athlet mention their social environment friend classmat coach demographic place residence study family parent sibling grandparent friend influenc their choice sport certain extent addition their sport context gave them perspective vision choose professional career relat their role athlet conclusion there factor influence pursuit sport academic activiti some which repeat mention participant interview main factor sociodemographic factor associat travel distance train venu university home work ii economic factor transportation food academic sport expens travel etc iii academic factor among which curricular flexibility stand out severity regard academic absenc make-up activiti etc,undergraduate education graduate student athletic competition education college sport internacional creative common atribucionnocomercialsinderivada,nieto roja introduction university student play dual role combin their academic studi sport activiti which requir them strike balance between two objective purpose understand relationship between academic commitment athletic performance colombian student-athlet method qualitative study interpretative-hermeneutic nature sample consist 11 studentathlet who enroll 2025-1 semester semi-structur interview design validat three expert qualitative research categori identifi sociodemographic profile student ii consider athletic performance iii consider academic commitment iv student-athlete relationship factor influenc student-athlete relationship result student-athlet mention their social environment friend classmat coach demographic place residence study family parent sibling grandparent friend influenc their choice sport certain extent addition their sport context gave them perspective vision choose professional career relat their role athlet conclusion there factor influence pursuit sport academic activiti some which repeat mention participant interview main factor sociodemographic factor associat travel distance train venu university home work ii economic factor transportation food academic sport expens travel etc iii academic factor among which curricular flexibility stand out severity regard academic absenc make-up activiti etc undergraduate education graduate student athletic competition education college sport internacional creative common atribucionnocomercialsinderivada,1.0.0,cc91eec7bfd45712
1692-7427,Art05_2026.pdf,Art05_2026_0,es,PhD. Diana María García-Cardona,"Objetivo: Analizar la respuesta fisiológica y metabólica de un patinador de velocidad durante una sesión de entrenamiento de alta intensidad, mediante un diseño observacional descriptivo de caso único. Métodos: Se evaluaron variables de composición corporal, frecuencia cardíaca (FC), percepción del esfuerzo (PE), lactato, glucosa, gravedad específica urinaria (GEO) y masa corporal en distintos momentos de la sesión: pre y poscalentamiento, posprueba y recuperación. Resultados: En el deportista evaluado, la FC evidenció una activación cardiovascular marcada durante el esfuerzo, alcanzando valores máximos cercanos al esfuerzo competitivo y con recuperación rápida posterior. La PE se incrementó hasta valores altos al final de la prueba. El lactato mostró una elevación posprueba compatible con alta participación anaeróbica, mientras que la glucosa presentó un descenso transitorio durante el ejercicio con recuperación parcial posterior. La GEO y la masa corporal reflejaron cambios leves y reversibles, compatibles con un adecuado estado de hidratación. Conclusión: En este caso, la sesión de entrenamiento generó respuestas fisiológicas y metabólicas acordes con las demandas del patinaje de velocidad. Estos hallazgos corresponden exclusivamente al deportista evaluado y resaltan la utilidad de una valoración integrada para el control del rendimiento y la recuperación","Ejercicio; Frecuencia cardíaca; Glucosa; Lactato; Patinaje. Recibido: 15 dic 2025. Aceptado: 28 abril 2026. Publicado: 12 may 2026. Como citar: García-Cardona, D. M., Sánchez-Muñoz, O. E., & Rojas, D. A. (2026). Respuesta fisiológica y metabólica de un patinador durante una sesión de entrenamiento: Reporte de caso Actividad Física y Desarrollo Humano,17(1), 56–67. E",marcadores,phd diana maria garcia-cardona,objetivo analizar respuesta fisiologica metabolica patinador velocidad durante sesion entrenamiento alta intensidad mediante diseno observacional descriptivo caso unico metod evaluaron variabl composicion corporal frecuencia cardiaca fc percepcion esfuerzo pe lactato glucosa gravedad especifica urinaria geo masa corporal distint moment sesion pre poscalentamiento posprueba recuperacion resultad deportista evaluado fc evidencio activacion cardiovascular marcada durante esfuerzo alcanz valor maxim cercan esfuerzo competitivo recuperacion rapida posterior pe incremento hasta valor altos final prueba lactato mostro elevacion posprueba compatible alta participacion anaerobica mientr glucosa presento descenso transitorio durante ejercicio recuperacion parcial posterior geo masa corporal reflejaron cambi leves reversibl compatibl adecuado estado hidratacion conclusion este caso sesion entrenamiento genero respuest fisiologic metabolic acord demand patinaje velocidad estos hallazg corresponden exclusiva deportista evaluado resaltan utilidad valoracion integrada control rendimiento recuperacion,ejercicio frecuencia cardiaca glucosa lactato patinaje recibido 15 dic 2025 aceptado 28 abril 2026 publicado 12 may 2026 como citar garcia-cardona sanchez-munoz rojas 2026 respuesta fisiologica metabolica patinador durante sesion entrenamiento reporte caso actividad fisica desarrollo humano 17 56-67,phd diana maria garcia-cardona objetivo analizar respuesta fisiologica metabolica patinador velocidad durante sesion entrenamiento alta intensidad mediante diseno observacional descriptivo caso unico metod evaluaron variabl composicion corporal frecuencia cardiaca fc percepcion esfuerzo pe lactato glucosa gravedad especifica urinaria geo masa corporal distint moment sesion pre poscalentamiento posprueba recuperacion resultad deportista evaluado fc evidencio activacion cardiovascular marcada durante esfuerzo alcanz valor maxim cercan esfuerzo competitivo recuperacion rapida posterior pe incremento hasta valor altos final prueba lactato mostro elevacion posprueba compatible alta participacion anaerobica mientr glucosa presento descenso transitorio durante ejercicio recuperacion parcial posterior geo masa corporal reflejaron cambi leves reversibl compatibl adecuado estado hidratacion conclusion este caso sesion entrenamiento genero respuest fisiologic metabolic acord demand patinaje velocidad estos hallazg corresponden exclusiva deportista evaluado resaltan utilidad valoracion integrada control rendimiento recuperacion ejercicio frecuencia cardiaca glucosa lactato patinaje recibido 15 dic 2025 aceptado 28 abril 2026 publicado 12 may 2026 como citar garcia-cardona sanchez-munoz rojas 2026 respuesta fisiologica metabolica patinador durante sesion entrenamiento reporte caso actividad fisica desarrollo humano 17 56-67,1.0.0,dbd03684e5429504
1692-7427,Art05_2026.pdf,Art05_2026_0,en,de entrenamiento generó respuestas,"Objective: To analyze the physiological and metabolic response of a speed skater during a high-intensity training session using a single-case descriptive observational design. Methods: Body composition, heart rate (HR), rating of perceived exertion (RPE), lactate, glucose, urine specific gravity (USG), and body mass were assessed at different time points during the session: pre- and post-warm-up, post-test, and recovery. Results: In the athlete evaluated, HR showed marked cardiovascular activation during exercise, reaching peak values close to competitive effort, followed by rapid recovery. RPE increased to high values at the end of the test. Lactate showed a post-test increase consistent with high anaerobic contribution, whereas glucose showed a transient decrease during exercise with partial recovery afterward. USG and body mass reflected mild and reversible changes, consistent with an adequate hydration status. Conclusion: In this case, the training session generated physiological and metabolic responses consistent with the demands of speed skating. These findings apply exclusively to the athlete evaluated and highlight the usefulness of an integrated assessment for monitoring performance and recovery",Exercise; Glucose; Heart Rate; Lactate; Skating. 1,marcadores,de entrenamiento genero respuesta,objective analyze physiological metabolic response speed skater during high-intensity train session using single-case descriptive observational design method body composition heart rate hr rating perceiv exertion rpe lactate glucose urine specific gravity usg body mass assess different time point during session pre- post-warm-up post-test recovery result athlete evaluat hr show mark cardiovascular activation during exercise reach peak valu close competitive effort follow rapid recovery rpe increas high valu end test lactate show post-test increase consistent high anaerobic contribution wherea glucose show transient decrease during exercise partial recovery afterward usg body mass reflect mild reversible chang consistent adequate hydration statu conclusion case train session generat physiological metabolic respons consistent demand speed skat these finding apply exclusively athlete evaluat highlight usefulnes integrat assessment monitor performance recovery,exercise glucose heart rate lactate skat,de entrenamiento genero respuesta objective analyze physiological metabolic response speed skater during high-intensity train session using single-case descriptive observational design method body composition heart rate hr rating perceiv exertion rpe lactate glucose urine specific gravity usg body mass assess different time point during session pre- post-warm-up post-test recovery result athlete evaluat hr show mark cardiovascular activation during exercise reach peak valu close competitive effort follow rapid recovery rpe increas high valu end test lactate show post-test increase consistent high anaerobic contribution wherea glucose show transient decrease during exercise partial recovery afterward usg body mass reflect mild reversible chang consistent adequate hydration statu conclusion case train session generat physiological metabolic respons consistent demand speed skat these finding apply exclusively athlete evaluat highlight usefulnes integrat assessment monitor performance recovery exercise glucose heart rate lactate skat,1.0.0,8eb6888d56bc7237
1692-7427,Art06_2026.pdf,Art06_2026_0,es,Manuel Riverón Mayedo,"La Educación Física cubana está en constante evolución para incrementar el desarrollo físico e intelecto de los educandos; sin embargo en la práctica educativa los docentes y educandos desconocen los beneficios que brinda la práctica de Iyengar Yoga combinado a las actividades físicas del programa de Educación Física en educandos de Cuarto Grado, diseñándose como objetivo de la presente investigación documentar los beneficios que brinda la práctica de Iyengar Yoga combinado a las actividades físicas del programa de Educación Física en educandos de Cuarto Grado. Para su tratamiento se realizó un estudio descriptivo, de enfoque cuantitativo aplicándose métodos teóricos para garantizar que la investigación sea rigurosa y que sus hallazgos sean válidos y aplicables en la práctica educativa y los métodos empíricos tales como la observación a actividades prácticas donde participaron 12 educandos de Cuarto Grado así como la entrevista 6 especialista de la Educación Física para obtener evidencia concreta y fiable que respalde la implementación del Iyengar Yoga combinado con las actividades físicas en las clases de Educación Física. Las aportaciones teóricas realizadas sobre los beneficios que brinda la práctica de Iyengar Yoga combinado a las actividades físicas del programa contribuye al III Perfeccionamiento del Sistema Educativo Cubano","Iyengar Yoga 1, Educación Física 2, Actividad física 3",marcadores,manuel riveron mayedo,educacion fisica cubana esta constante evolucion incrementar desarrollo fisico intelecto educand sin embargo practica educativa docent educand desconocen benefici brinda practica iyengar yoga combinado actividad fisic programa educacion fisica educand cuarto grado disenandose como objetivo presente investigacion documentar benefici brinda practica iyengar yoga combinado actividad fisic programa educacion fisica educand cuarto grado tratamiento realizo estudio descriptivo enfoque cuantita