1794-0915,OC 29.pdf,OC 29_5,en,tern Tanager (Piranga ludoviciana) for Colombia,"The Western Tanager (Piranga ludoviciana) breeds in western North America, from southeast Alaska to northeastern Mexico, in open, coniferous and mixed forests. Its migratory distribution is documented in Central America, from the Baja California Peninsula (Mexico) to Costa Rica, with some records in Panama, Cuba, and the Bahamas in the Caribbean. Only two previous records are known in South America: one in Chile and one in Ecuador. This observation constitutes the first documented record for Colombia, made on March 16, 2025. The observation site consists of a cluster of farms surrounded by secondary dry forest, located in district of La Buitrera, Cali, Valle del Cauca","Cardinalidae, Cecropia sp., dry forest, La Buitrera-Cali, migration ORNITOLOGÍA COLOMBIANA © 2026 Los Autores Revista Ornitología Colombiana - Asociación Colombiana de Ornitología ACO Este es un articulo de acceso abierto bajo los términos de la licencia Creative Commons Atribución-NoComercial 4.0 Internacional DOI: 10.59517/oc.e651 Recibido 24 de septiembre de 2025 Aceptado 7 de mayo",marcadores,tern tanager piranga ludoviciana colombia,western tanager piranga ludoviciana breed western north america southeast alaska northeastern mexico open coniferou mixed forest its migratory distribution document central america baja california peninsula mexico costa rica some record panama cuba bahama caribbean only two previou record known south america one chile one ecuador observation constitut first document record colombia made march 16 2025 observation site consist cluster farm surround secondary dry forest locat district la buitrera cali valle del cauca,cardinalidae cecropia sp dry forest la buitrera-cali migration ornitologia colombiana 2026 los autor revista ornitologia colombiana asociacion colombiana de ornitologia aco este es un articulo de acceso abierto bajo los termino de la licencia creative common atribucion-nocomerci