1794-0915,OC 29.pdf,OC 29_10,es,"Zacarías-Alvarado, J.R. & R. Rosas-Valdez. 2018. Primer","Damos a conocer el hallazgo de dos nidos de la Caica suramericana (Gallinago paraguaiae) en el departamento de Casanare, lo que constituye la primera evidencia directa de reproducción de la especie en Colombia, dado que previamente se contaba con registros de despliegues aéreos como único indicio reproductivo","limícola, Llanos, ganaderos, reproducción, sabana",marcadores,zacarias-alvarado rosas-valdez 2018 primer,damos conocer hallazgo dos nidos caica suramericana gallinago paraguaiae departamento casanare constituye primera evidencia directa reproduccion especie colombia dado previa contaba registr despliegu aere como unico indicio reproductivo,limicola llan ganader reproduccion sabana,zacarias-alvarado rosas-valdez 2018 primer damos conocer hallazgo dos nidos caica suramericana gallinago paraguaiae departamento casanare constituye primera evidencia directa reproduccion especie colombia dado previa contaba registr despliegu aere como unico indicio reproductivo limicola llan ganader reproduccion sabana,1.0.0,a53f85daf2c93bab
1794-0915,OC 29.pdf,OC 29_10,en,k orb-weaver (Trichonephila,"We report two nests of the Pantanal Snipe (Gallinago paraguaiae) in the department of Casanare, representing the first direct evidence of breeding for this species in Colombia, as display flights had previously been the only indication of its breeding in the country","breeding, Llanos, ranchers, savanna, shorebird ORNITOLOGÍA COLOMBIANA © 2026 Los Autores Revista Ornitología Colombiana - Asociación Colombiana de Ornitología ACO Este es un articulo de acceso abierto bajo los términos de la licencia Creative Commons Atribución-NoComercial 4.0 Internacional DOI: 10.59517/oc.e655 Recibido 17 de octubre de 2025 Aceptado 2 de junio de 2026",marcadores,orb-weaver trichonephila,we report two nest pantanal snipe gallinago paraguaiae department casanare represent first direct evidence breed speci colombia display flight had previously been only indication its breed country,breed llano rancher savanna shorebird ornitologia colombiana 2026 los autor revista ornitologia colombiana asociacion colombiana de ornitologia aco este es un articulo de acceso abierto bajo los termino de la licencia creative common atribucion-nocomercial internacional doi 10 59517 oc e655 recibido 17 de octubre de 2025 aceptado de junio de 2026,orb-weaver trichonephila we report two nest pantanal snipe gallinago paraguaiae department casanare represent first direct evidence breed speci colombia display flight had previously been only indication its breed country breed llano rancher savanna shorebird ornitologia colombiana 2026 los autor revista ornitologia colombiana asociacion colombiana de ornitologia aco este es un articulo de acceso abierto bajo los termino de la licencia creative common atribucion-nocomercial internacional doi 10 59517 oc e655 recibido 17 de octubre de 2025 aceptado de junio de 2026,1.0.0,7decdd2441cfa086
1794-2470,V2+art+01+NOVA47+Bauhinia+picta.pdf,V2+art+01+NOVA47+Bauhinia+picta_0,es,"-Humanas. Facultad de ciencias, Universidad del Tolima, Ibagué-Colombia.","Introducción. El Glioblastoma multiforme es uno de los tipos de tumor más maligno del sistema nervioso central, por lo que se requiere de la búsqueda de nuevas terapias especí ficas y efectivas. Los tratamientos actuales como resección quirúrgica seguida de radiote rapia y quimioterapia adyuvante con temozolomida, no generan los resultados clínicos es perados en el paciente; por lo cual, las terapias basadas en productos naturales han ganado interés por ser un tratamiento efectivo y menos tóxico. En esta investigación, se evaluó el efecto citotóxico de la especie Bauhinia picta, una especie nativa de Colombia la cual es re conocida por su utilidad en trastornos del sistema circulatorio, propiedades antidiabéticas, antiinflamatorias y antioxidantes, pero aún se desconoce su efecto en la actividad antican cerígena. Objetivo. Evaluar el efecto citotóxico de la especie B. picta sobre la línea celular de Glioblastoma. Resultados. Nuestros resultados demuestran que la concentración de 500 μg/mL de esta especie es capaz de disminuir la viabilidad, reducir entre el 55-60% de la integridad de la membrana y aumentar el área nuclear de la línea celular T98G. Con clusión. La concentración de 500 μg/mL disminuye la viabilidad de la línea celular T98G Recibido: 11/01/2025 Aceptado: 04/02/2026 12 NOVA. 2026; 24 (47) y es posible que el mecanismo de acción esté relacionado con la pérdida de integridad de membrana a través de la interacción que realizan los flavonoides presentes en esta especie con los componentes de esta estructura celular","Bauhinia picta, efecto citotóxico, glioblastoma, T98G",marcadores,-human facultad cienci universidad tolima ibague-colombia,introduccion glioblastoma multiforme uno tipos tumor mas maligno sistema nervioso central requiere busqueda nuev terapi especi ficas efectiv trat actual como reseccion quirurgica seguida radiote rapia quimioterapia adyuvante temozolomida no generan resultad clinic perad paciente cual terapi basad product natural han ganado inter ser tratamiento efectivo menos toxico esta investigacion evaluo efecto citotoxico especie bauhinia picta especie nativa colombia cual re conocida utilidad trastorn sistema circulatorio propiedad antidiabetic antiinflamatori antioxidant pero aun desconoce efecto actividad antican cerigena objetivo evaluar efecto citotoxico especie picta sobre linea celular glioblastoma resultad nuestr resultad demuestran concentracion 500 mg ml esta especie capaz disminuir viabilidad reducir entre 55-60 integridad membrana aumentar area nuclear linea celular t98g clusion concentracion 500 mg ml disminuye viabilidad linea celular t98g recibido 11 01 2025 aceptado 04 02 2026 12 nova 2026 24 47 posible mecanismo accion este relacionado perdida integridad membrana trav interaccion realizan flavonoid present esta especie component esta estructura celular,bauhinia picta efecto citotoxico glioblastoma t98g,-human facultad cienci universidad tolima ibague-colombia introduccion glioblastoma multiforme uno tipos tumor mas maligno sistema nervioso central requiere busqueda nuev terapi especi ficas efectiv trat actual como reseccion quirurgica seguida radiote rapia quimioterapia adyuvante temozolomida no generan resultad clinic perad paciente cual terapi basad product natural han ganado inter ser tratamiento efectivo menos toxico esta investigacion evaluo efecto citotoxico especie bauhinia picta especie nativa colombia cual re conocida utilidad trastorn sistema circulatorio propiedad antidiabetic antiinflamatori antioxidant pero aun desconoce efecto actividad antican cerigena objetivo evaluar efecto citotoxico especie picta sobre linea celular glioblastoma resultad nuestr resultad demuestran concentracion 500 mg ml esta especie capaz disminuir viabilidad reducir entre 55-60 integridad membrana aumentar area nuclear linea celular t98g clusion concentracion 500 mg ml disminuye viabilidad linea celular t98g recibido 11 01 2025 aceptado 04 02 2026 12 nova 2026 24 47 posible mecanismo accion este relacionado perdida integridad membrana trav interaccion realizan flavonoid present esta especie component esta estructura celular bauhinia picta efecto citotoxico glioblastoma t98g,1.0.0,f4e048b3db5cacd3
1794-2470,V2+art+01+NOVA47+Bauhinia+picta.pdf,V2+art+01+NOVA47+Bauhinia+picta_0,en,"inflamatorias y antioxidantes, pero aún se desconoce su efecto en la actividad antican","Introduction. Glioblastoma multiforme is one of the most malignant tumor types of the central nervous system, which makes the search for new, specific, and effective therapies essential. Current treatments, such as surgical resection followed by radiotherapy and ad juvant chemotherapy with temozolomide, do not achieve the expected clinical outcomes; therefore, natural product–based therapies have gained interest as potentially effective and less toxic alternatives. In this study, we evaluated the cytotoxic effect of Bauhinia picta, a species native to Colombia that is known for its use in circulatory disorders and for its an tidiabetic, anti-inflammatory, and antioxidant properties, although its anticancer activity remains unknown. Objective. To evaluate the cytotoxic effect of B. picta on a glioblas toma cell line. Results. Our findings show that the concentration of 500 μg/mL reduces the viability of the T98G cell line Our results show that a concentration of 500 μg/mL of this species is capable of decreasing viability, reducing membrane integrity by 55-60%, and increasing the nuclear area of the T98G cell line. Conclusion. The concentration of 500 μg/mL decreases the viability of T98G cells, and the mechanism of action may be related to the loss of membrane integrity through interactions between the flavonoids present in this species and the components of the cell membrane","Bauhinia picta, cytotoxic effect, glioblastoma, T98G",marcadores,inflamatoria antioxidant pero aun se desconoce su efecto en la actividad antican,introduction glioblastoma multiforme one most malignant tumor type central nervou system which make search new specific effective therapi essential current treatment such surgical resection follow radiotherapy ad juvant chemotherapy temozolomide do not achieve expect clinical outcom therefore natural product-bas therapi have gain interest potentially effective less toxic alternativ study we evaluat cytotoxic effect bauhinia picta speci native colombia known its use circulatory disorder its tidiabetic anti-inflammatory antioxidant properti although its anticancer activity remain unknown objective evaluate cytotoxic effect picta gliobla toma cell line result our finding show concentration 500 mg ml reduc viability t98g cell line our result show concentration 500 mg ml speci capable decreas viability reduc membrane integrity 55-60 increas nuclear area t98g cell line conclusion concentration 500 mg ml decreas viability t98g cell mechanism action may relat loss membrane integrity through interaction between flavonoid present speci component cell membrane,bauhinia picta cytotoxic effect glioblastoma t98g,inflamatoria antioxidant pero aun se desconoce su efecto en la actividad antican introduction glioblastoma multiforme one most malignant tumor type central nervou system which make search new specific effective therapi essential current treatment such surgical resection follow radiotherapy ad juvant chemotherapy temozolomide do not achieve expect clinical outcom therefore natural product-bas therapi have gain interest potentially effective less toxic alternativ study we evaluat cytotoxic effect bauhinia picta speci native colombia known its use circulatory disorder its tidiabetic anti-inflammatory antioxidant properti although its anticancer activity remain unknown objective evaluate cytotoxic effect picta gliobla toma cell line result our finding show concentration 500 mg ml reduc viability t98g cell line our result show concentration 500 mg ml speci capable decreas viability reduc membrane integrity 55-60 increas nuclear area t98g cell line conclusion concentration 500 mg ml decreas viability t98g cell mechanism action may relat loss membrane integrity through interaction between flavonoid present speci component cell membrane bauhinia picta cytotoxic effect glioblastoma t98g,1.0.0,444e3030efd84413
1794-2470,V2+art+02+NOVA47+microbiological+quality.pdf,V2+art+02+NOVA47+microbiological+quality_0,en,"s, Department of Microbiology, University of Pamplona, Colombia.","Objective. This study evaluated the physicochemical and microbiological quality of raw cow’s milk and artisanal fresh cheeses produced in 22 municipalities of Nariño Depart ment, southwestern Colombia, to assess compliance with national food safety regulations and to identify potential food safety hazards. Methods. Physicochemical parameters were determined following AOAC International and Colombian Technical Standards (NTC) me thods. Microbiological analyses were performed according to International Organization for Standardization (ISO) procedures for enumeration of coliforms, Escherichia coli, and Staphylococcus aureus, and detection of Listeria monocytogenes and Salmonella spp. Selected bacterial isolates were genotypically identified through 16S ribosomal RNA (rRNA) gene sequencing. Additionally, processing plants were evaluated for compliance with Good Ma nufacturing Practices (GMP). Results. The physicochemical characteristics of milk and cheese samples complied with Colombian regulatory limits. However, significant patho genic contamination persisted: 45.5% of milk samples and 36.3% of cheese samples tested positive for L. monocytogenes, while E. coli counts exceeded permissible levels in 36.4% of Received: 20/10/2025 Accepted: 24/03/2026 32 NOVA. 2026; 24 (47) milk samples and 22.7% of cheese samples. Salmonella spp. was not detected in any sample (100% compliance for this pathogen). Molecular identification through 16S rRNA gene sequencing confirmed the pathogenic isolates initially identified through standard micro biological and biochemical techniques. Processing plant infrastructure compliance ranged from 36% to 93% (mean ± standard deviation = 66.5% ± 17.2%), strongly correlating with microbiological quality outcomes. Conclusion. While artisanal cheese production in Nariño Department meets physicochemical standards, there are still significant microbio logical hazards, particularly L. monocytogenes and E. coli contamination. Implementation of comprehensive hygiene protocols, enhanced GMP compliance, and formalized quality control systems are urgently needed to ensure food safety and public health protection","raw milk, fresh cheese, food safety, Listeria monocytogenes, Staphylococcus au reus, good manufacturing practices, Nariño",marcadores,department microbiology university pamplona colombia,objective study evaluat physicochemical microbiological quality raw cow milk artisanal fresh chees produc 22 municipaliti narino depart ment southwestern colombia asses compliance national food safety regul identify potential food safety hazard method physicochemical parameter determin follow aoac international colombian technical standard ntc me thod microbiological analys perform accord international organ standard iso procedur enumeration coliform escherichia coli staphylococcu aureu detection listeria monocytogen salmonella spp select bacterial isolat genotypically identifi through 16s ribosomal rna rrna gene sequenc additionally process plant evaluat compliance good ma nufactur practic gmp result physicochemical characteristic milk cheese sampl compli colombian regulatory limit however significant patho genic contamination persist 45 milk sampl 36 cheese sampl test positive monocytogen while coli count exceed permissible level 36 receiv 20 10 2025 accept 24 03 2026 32 nova 2026 24 47 milk sampl 22 cheese sampl salmonella spp not detect any sample 100 compliance pathogen molecular identification through 16s rrna gene sequenc confirm pathogenic isolat initially identifi through standard micro biological biochemical techniqu process plant infrastructure compliance rang 36 93 mean standard deviation 66 17 strongly correlat microbiological quality outcom conclusion while artisanal cheese production narino department meet physicochemical standard there still s