1794-2470,V2+art+09+NOVA47+salud+rural.pdf,V2+art+09+NOVA47+salud+rural_0,en,egresión logística. Resultados. El 98 % de los participantes manifestó,"Introduction. Rural populations in Latin America face barriers to accessing health ser vices, increasing their vulnerability to preventable diseases such as tuberculosis. This study aimed to identify sociodemographic and structural factors associated with percei ved barriers to healthcare access among rural residents in 12 municipalities of Valle del Cauca prioritized for TB notification and vulnerability conditions. Methods. Analytical cross-sectional study (August–December 2022) in 12 municipalities of Valle del Cauca, prioritized by rurality, poverty, and TB notification. We included 457 adults (≥18 years) enrolled in the subsidized health insurance scheme, selected through stratified random sampling from rural enrollee lists and surveyed using a structured questionnaire. The outcome was perceived difficulty accessing health services when needed in the past 12 months. Descriptive, bivariate, and logistic regression analyses were conducted. Results. Ninety-eight percent of participants reported being insured; over 80% had income at or below the minimum wage, and 47.5% reported difficulties accessing services. The stron gest barrier was the need to use multiple modes of transport (OR=4.15; 95% CI: 2.62– 6.59), with a trend for poorer self-rated health (OR=1.56; 95% CI: 0.99–2.45). Conclusion. Near-universal insurance coverage does not ensure access to health services in rural areas; mobility and transportation are the main barriers. Differential interventions focused on transport and territorial service coordination are needed","healthcare access, rural areas, tuberculosis, comprehensive healthcare, struc tural barriers. Holguín-Ruiz, et al. Acceso a salud rural en 12 municipios del Valle del Cauca priorizados por notificación de TB y condiciones de vulnerabilidad 165",marcadores,egresion logistica resultado el 98 de los participant manifesto,introduction rural popul latin america face barrier access health ser vice increas their vulnerability preventable diseas such tuberculosi study aimed identify sociodemographic structural factor associat percei ved barrier healthcare acces among rural resident 12 municipaliti valle del cauca prioritiz tb notification vulnerability condition method analytical cross-sectional study august-december 2022 12 municipaliti valle del cauca prioritiz rurality poverty tb notification we includ 457 adult 18 year enroll subsidiz health insurance scheme select through stratifi random sampl rural enrollee list survey using structur questionnaire outcome perceiv difficulty access health servic when need past 12 month descriptive bivariate logistic regression analys conduct result ninety-eight percent participant report being insur over 80 had income below minimum wage 47 report difficulti access servic stron gest barrier need use multiple mode transport 15 95 ci 62- 59 trend poorer self-rat health 56 95 ci 99-2 45 conclusion near-universal insurance coverage does not ensure acces health servic rural area mobility transportation main barrier differential intervention focus transport territorial service coordination need,healthcare acces rural area tuberculosi comprehensive healthcare struc tural barrier holguin-ruiz et al acceso salud rural en 12 municipio del valle del cauca priorizado por notificacion de tb condicion de vulnerabilidad 165,egresion logistica resultado el 98 de los participant manifesto introduction rural popul latin america face barrier access health ser vice increas their vulnerability preventable diseas such tuberculosi study aimed identify sociodemographic structural factor associat percei ved barrier healthcare acces among rural resident 12 municipaliti valle del cauca prioritiz tb notification vulnerability condition method analytical cross-sectional study august-december 2022 12 municipaliti valle del cauca prioritiz rurality poverty tb notification we includ 457 adult 18 year enroll subsidiz health insurance scheme select through stratifi random sampl rural enrollee list survey using structur questionnaire outcome perceiv difficulty access health servic when need past 12 month descriptive bivariate logistic regression analys conduct result ninety-eight percent participant report being insur over 80 had income below minimum wage 47 report difficulti access servic stron gest barrier need use multiple mode transport 15 95 ci 62- 59 trend poorer self-rat health 56 95 ci 99-2 45 conclusion near-universal insurance coverage does not ensure acces health servic rural area mobility transportation main barrier differential intervention focus transport territorial service coordination need healthcare acces rural area tuberculosi comprehensive healthcare struc tural barrier holguin-ruiz et al acceso salud rural en 12 municipio del valle del cauca priorizado por notificacion de tb condicion de vulnerabilidad 165,1.0.0,466012d4aebe31ab
1794-5240,5-+UIS_RM+V38+N3+-+ART+6.pdf,5-+UIS_RM+V38+N3+-+ART+6_0,es,"John Jaime Sprockel-Díaz1,2,3*","Introducción: la evaluación del riesgo es necesaria para la correcta toma de decisiones en pacientes hospitalizados por COVID-19. Existen reglas de predicción para estimar el riesgo de muerte o ingreso a cuidados intensivos de estos pacientes. Objetivo: validar el puntaje CALL, COVID-GRAM y ISARIC 4C para la admisión a cuidados intensivos o el fallecimiento en pacientes hospitalizados por COVID-19 en una cohorte de tres hospitales de Bogotá durante 2020. Métodos: estudio observacional analítico prospectivo multicéntrico que incluyó adultos hospitalizados por COVID-19, entre abril y noviembre de 2020, en tres hospitales de cuarto nivel en Bogotá. Para cada participante se calcularon las tres escalas. Se estimaron ¿Cómo citar este artículo? Sprockel-Díaz JJ, Tabares-Rodríguez S, Carrillo-Ayerbe MP, Acuña-Cortes IS, Montoya-Rumpf RP, Angarita-González E, Coral-Zúñiga VE, Cárdenas-Rodríguez H, Araque-Parra EC, Parra JE. Evaluation of CALL, COVID-GRAM, and ISARIC scores for intensive care unit admission and mortality risk in hospitalized COVID-19 patients: multicenter observational study, Bogotá, Colombia, 2020. Med. UIS. 2025; 38(3): 61-71. DOI: https://doi.org/10.18273/revmed.v38n3-2025007 62 Sprockel-Díaz JJ, Tabares-Rodríguez S, Carrillo-Ayerbe MP, Acuña-Cortes IS, Montoya-Rumpf RP, Angarita-González E, Coral-Zúñiga VE, Cárdenas-Rodríguez H, Araque-Parra EC, Parra JE. Med. UIS. 2025;38(3):61-71 curvas ROC con sus áreas bajo la curva e IC 95 %, se evaluó la calibración mediante estadística de Brier y LOESS, y la utilidad clínica mediante curvas de decisión. Resultados: de 793 pacientes, 358 tenían datos para calcular las tres escalas; 186 (26,2 %) fueron admitidos en cuidados intensivos y 120 (16,9 %) fallecieron. Las áreas bajo la curva para admisión a cuidados intensivos fueron: COVID-GRAM 0,67 (IC 95 %: 0,61-0,73), CALL 0,54 (IC 95 %: 0,48-0,60), ISARIC-4C 0,61 (IC 95 %: 0,55-0,67). Para la mortalidad fueron: COVID-GRAM 0,76 (IC 95 %: 0,70-0,81), puntaje CALL 0,65 (IC 95 %: 0,58-0,73), ISARIC-4C 0,75 (IC 95 %: 0,6-0,8). Conclusiones: las reglas de predicción mostraron un rendimiento pobre a moderado para la admisión en unidad de cuidados intensivos y un buen rendimiento para la mortalidad. El ISARIC-4C y COVID-GRAM podrían considerarse para evaluar el riesgo de muerte",COVID-19; SARS-CoV-2; mortalidad; pronóstico; reglas de predicción clínica; cuidados críticos,marcadores,john jaime sprockel-diaz1,introduccion evaluacion riesgo necesaria correcta toma decision pacient hospitalizad covid-19 existen regl prediccion estimar riesgo muerte ingreso cuidad intensiv estos pacient objetivo validar puntaje call covid-gram isaric 4c admision cuidad intensiv fallecimiento pacient hospitalizad covid-19 cohorte tres hospital bogota durante 2020 metod estudio observacional analitico prospectivo multicentrico incluyo adult hospitalizad covid-19 entre abril noviembre 2020 tres hospital cuarto nivel bogota cada participante calcularon tres escal estimaron como citar este articulo sprockel-diaz jj tabares-rodriguez carrillo-ayerbe mp acuna-cort is montoya-rumpf rp angarita-gonzalez coral-zuniga ve cardenas-rodriguez araque-parra ec parra je evaluation of call covid-gram and isaric scor for intensive care unit admission and mortality risk in hospitalized covid-19 patients multicenter observational study bogota colombia 2020 med uis 2025 38 61-71 doi https doi org 10 18273 revmed v38n3-2025007 62 sprockel-diaz jj tabares-rodriguez carrillo-ayerbe mp acuna-cort is montoya-rumpf rp angarita-gonzalez coral-zuniga ve cardenas-rodriguez araque-parra ec parra je med uis 2025 38 61-71 curv roc sus areas bajo curva ic 95 evaluo calibracion mediante estadistica brier loess utilidad clinica mediante curv decision resultad 793 pacient 358 tenian datos calcular tres escal 186 26 fueron admitid cuidad intensiv 120 16 fallecieron areas bajo curva admision cui