 ic 95 48-0 60 isaric-4c 61 ic 95 55-0 67 mortalidad fueron covid-gram 76 ic 95 70-0 81 puntaje call 65 ic 95 58-0 73 isaric-4c 75 ic 95 6-0 conclusion regl prediccion mostraron rendimiento pobre moderado admision unidad cuidad intensiv buen rendimiento mortalidad isaric-4c covid-gram podrian considerarse evaluar riesgo muerte covid-19 sars-cov-2 mortalidad pronostico regl prediccion clinica cuidad critic,1.0.0,44ab091bff505b87
1794-5240,5-+UIS_RM+V38+N3+-+ART+6.pdf,5-+UIS_RM+V38+N3+-+ART+6_0,en,unidad de cuidados intensivos y un buen rendimiento para la mortalidad. El ISARIC-4C y COVID-GRAM podrían considerarse,"Introduction: accurate risk assessment is essential for sound decision-making in patients hospitalized with COVID-19, and several prediction rules have been developed to estimate their risk of death or admission to intensive care. Objective: to validate the CALL, COVID-GRAM, and ISARIC-4C scores for predicting intensive care unit admission or death among patients hospitalized with COVID-19 in a cohort from three Bogotá hospitals during 2020. Methods: a prospective multicenter analytical observational study that included adults hospitalized for COVID-19 between April and November 2020 in three fourth-level hospitals in Bogotá. The scores from the three scales were calculated for each participant. Receiver-operatingcharacteristic curves were plotted and areas under the curve with 95 % confidence intervals were estimated; calibration was assessed with the Brier statistic and LOESS smoothing, and clinical utility was examined using decision-curve analysis. Results: of 793 patients, 358 had data to calculate the three prediction rules. 186 (26.2 %) were admitted to intensive care and 120 (16,9 %) died. The areas under the curve for intensive care admission were: COVID-GRAM 0,67 (95 % CI: 0,61-0,73), CALL score 0,54 (95 % CI: 0,48-0,60), ISARIC-4C 0,61 (95 % CI: 0,55-0,67). For mortality they were: COVID-GRAM 0,76 (95 % CI: 0,70-0,81), CALL score 0,65 (95 % CI: 0,58-0,73), ISARIC-4C 0,75 (95 % CI: 0,6-0,8). Conclusions: the clinical prediction rules evaluated showed poor to moderate performance for intensive care admission and good performance for mortality. The ISARIC-4C and COVID-GRAM could be considered to evaluate the risk of death",COVID-19; SARS-CoV-2; mortality; prognosis; clinical prediction rule; critical care,marcadores,unidad de cuidado intensivo un buen rendimiento para la m