1794-8932,S.1545.pdf,S.1545_0,en,"a la formación del aprendizaje socioemocional del estudiantado, y que la experiencia","Since 2020, the Chilean Ministry of Education has incorporated the elective subject of Theater for students in their third and fourth years of high school. This study established a link between the subject of Theater and Social-Emotional Learning (SEL), with the aim of understanding the perceptions and meaning that participants give to the development of SEL through their experiences in the subject Información del artículo Recibido: septiembre de 2024 Aceptado: octubre de 2025 Publicado: noviembre de 2025 Como citar: Benavente Inzunza, C., VeraSagredo, A. (2025). La asignatura de Teatro como escenario de aprendizaje socioemocional en secundaria. Sophia, 21(1). https://revistas.ugca.edu.co/ index.php/sophia/article/vi ew/1545 Sophia-Education Copyright 2025. Universidad La Gran Colombia Esta obra está bajo una Licencia AttributionShareAlike 4.0 International Conflicto de intereses: Los autores declaran no tener conflictos de intereses. *Autor para la correspondencia: benavente@ucsc.cl DOI: https://doi.org/10.18634/sophiaj.21v.1i.1545 Volumen 21, número 1, 2025, p: e1545 ISSN − −SOPHIA e1545 of Theater. The participants were 12th-grade students who took the course during the two years of its implementation in the Biobío region of Chile. The research was qualitative, exploratory, and descriptive in nature, using focus groups and semistructured interviews based on life stories to explore how the experience of the subject influences the development of self-assessment, self-esteem, and empathy for teamwork within the SLA educational framework. The results show that the Theater course makes a significant contribution to the students' social-emotional learning and that the theatrical experience is profound and meaningful, as it constitutes learning for life. It is concluded that students must be willing to go beyond curricular learning and acquire ASE. The Theater class proves to be an educational space in which this willingness occurs because there is personal and group motivation and because it is an activity that prioritizes emotional well-being. In this way, participants are able to develop the five dimensions of SEL: self-awareness, self-regulation, responsible decision-making, awareness of others, and social skills","socio-emotional learning, performing arts, secondary school, students, theater. __________________________________________________________________________",marcadores,la formacion del aprendizaje socioemocional del estudiantado que la experiencia,since 2020 chilean ministry education has incorporat elective subject theater student their third fourth year high school study establish link between subject theater social-emotional learn sel aim understand perception mean participant give development sel through their experienc subject informacion del articulo recibido septiembre de 2024 aceptado octubre de 2025 publicado noviembre de 2025 como citar benavente inzunza verasagredo 2025 la asignatura de teatro como escenario de aprendizaje socioemocional en secundaria sophia 21 http revista ugca edu co index php sophia article vi ew 1545 sophia-education copyright 2025 universidad la gran colombia esta obra esta bajo una licencia attributionsharealike international conflicto de interes los autor declaran no tener conflicto de interes autor para la correspondencia benavente ucsc cl doi http doi org 10 18634 sophiaj 21v 1i 1545 volumen 21 numero 2025 e1545 issn -sophia e1545 theater participant 12th-grade student who took course during two year its implementation biobio region chile research qualitative exploratory descriptive nature using focu group semistructur interview based life stori explore how experience subject influenc development self-assessment self-esteem empathy teamwork within sla educational framework result show theater course make significant contribution student social-emoti