1900-6004,Colombia_Internacional_126_04-act.pdf,Colombia_Internacional_126_04-act_0,en,flejar su rol en,"Objective/Context: Chile is a country in which the Presidency of the Republic plays a central role in the political system. We examine the presidential role in contexts of crisis and stability, based on an analysis of presidential speeches delivered before Congress between 1921 and 2024. Methodology: From an interdisciplinary perspective that combines systemic functional linguistics and discursive institutionalism, we identify discursive patterns and develop a typology of discursive strategies in these contexts. Based on a corpus of 104 presidential speeches and using a mixed-methods approach that combines qualitative discourse analysis with corpus systematization, we apply a model developed specifically for this study, integrating linguistic and sociopolitical dimensions to examine the presidential role in contexts of stability and crisis. Conclusions: The analysis reveals three recurring strategies, associated with the type of presidency (continuist or reformist) and the use of discursive skills (inherited or vanguard). It concludes that resilient institutional stability functions as a predominant discursive strategy, prevailing over rupture, in the symbolic configuration of presidential power. Originality: The study offers an innovative perspective by analyzing, in the Chilean case over a century, how the ideas and discursive patterns present in presidential speeches not only reflect their role in contexts of crisis or stability but also contribute to reproducing or reinterpreting the institutional order. It is a contribution to both discourse studies and the literature on presidential regimes",presidential speeches; discursive institutionalism; institutional stability; presidential power; Chile. A estabilidade institucional resiliente como estratégia: análise do poder sob a perspectiva dos discursos presidenciais no Chile (1921-2024),marcadores,flejar su rol 