ativo colombia 2022-2026 financiado convocatoria fond concursabl 2025 modalidad semiller universidad rosario realizo seno semillero desigualdad politica social facultad estudi internacional politic urban agradecem colaboracion manolo vasquez como asistente investigacion este articulo colomb int 126 issn 0121-5612 e-issn 1900-6004 abril-junio 2026 pp 3-39 https doi org 10 7440 colombiaint126 2026 01 democratizacion presion social ni herramient construccion coalicion legislativ identificad literatura sobre presidencialismo coalicional sino configuracion especifica factor politico-institucional sectorial metodologia reconstruyo tramite legislativo mediante rastreo proces process tracing analiz cambi articulado audienci public debat comision plenari cobertura mediatica document tecnic emplearon compar contrafactic reform gobierno evaluar plausibilidad cada condicion causal conclusion identificam secuencia causal cuatro condicion necesari conjunta suficient explicar exito reforma consenso tecnico-politico previo sobre necesidad reformar sistema pensional debilidad estructural perdedor opositor preconcertacion acoto disens redujo vetos negoci programatico-clientelar focalizad congreso originalidad articulo diferencia entre factor explican intencion reformista aquell explican aprobacion efectiva legislativo pone conversar literatur sobre expansion politica social relacion ejecutivolegislativo frente esta ultima muestra sus factor explicativ son mayoria invariant plano pais-ano variacion relevante encuentra nivel sectorial introduce consenso tecnico-politico preconcertacion debilidad opositor como condicion sectorial ignorad asimismo muestra papel complementario negoci programatic clientelar context partid volatil practic particularist reforma pensional politica social proteccion social consenso relacion ejecutivo-legislativo reforms in their labyrinth consensus pre-agreement and transaction in the approval of pension reform in colombia,1.0.0,83e0ca3117b1653f
1900-6004,"Las+reformas+en+su+laberinto_+consenso,+preconcertación+y+transacción+en+la+aprobación+de+la+reforma+pensional+en+Colombia.pdf","Las+reformas+en+su+laberinto_+consenso,+preconcertación+y+transacción+en+la+aprobación+de+la+reforma+pensional+en+Colombia_0",en,tención reformista y,"Objective/Context: This article analyzes why the Petro administration’s pension reform was approved through ordinary legislative procedures, whereas other social reforms failed or required extra-legislative pressure. We argue that the outcome cannot be explained solely by the government’s ideology, democratization, or social pressure, nor by the legislative coalition-building tools identified in the literature on coalition presidentialism. Rather, it is explained by a specific configuration of political-institutional and sectoral factors. Methodology: The legislative process was reconstructed through process tracing, analyzing changes to the articles, public hearings, committee and plenary debates, media coverage, and technical documents. Counterfactual comparisons with government reforms were used to assess the plausibility of each causal condition. Conclusions: We identified a causal sequence of four necessary and jointly sufficient conditions explaining the success of the reform: (1) a prior technical-political consensus on the need to reform the pension system; (2) the structural weakness of the losers and opponents; (3) a pre-agreement that limited dissent and reduced vetoes, and (4) programmaticclientelistic negotiations focused on Congress. Originality: The article distinguishes between the factors that explain reformist intentions and those that explain their 5 Las reformas en su laberinto: consenso, preconcertación y transacción en la aprobación... Silvia Otero, Daniela Acosta, Sebastián Cotes, José Miguel Jaimes y Amanda Murillo actual approval in the legislative branch; it brings the literature on the expansion of social policy and executive-legislative relations into dialogue. Regarding the latter, it shows that its explanatory factors are, for the most part, invariant at the countryyear level, with the relevant variation occurring at the sectoral level. It introduces technical-political consensus, pre-agreement, and the opposition's weakness as overlooked sectoral conditions. It also demonstrates the complementary role of programmatic and clientelistic negotiations in contexts of volatile parties and particularistic practices","pension reform, social policy, social protection, consensus, executivelegislative relations. Reformas em seu labirinto: consenso, pré-acordo e compromisso na aprovação da reforma da previdência na Colômbia",marcadores,tencion reformista,objective context article analyz why petro administration pension reform approv through ordinary legislative procedur wherea other social reform fail requir extra-legislative pressure we argue outcome cannot explain solely government ideology democrat social pressure nor legislative coalition-build tool identifi literature coalition presidentialism rather explain specific configuration political-institutional sectoral factor methodology legislative proces reconstruct through proces trac analyz chang articl public hearing committee plenary debat media coverage technical document counterfactual comparison government reform used asses plausibility each causal condition conclusion we identifi causal sequence four necessary jointly sufficient condition explain succes reform prior technical-political consensu need reform pension system structural weaknes loser opponent pre-agreement limit dissent reduc veto programmaticclientelistic negoti focus congres originality article distinguish between factor explain reformist intention those explain their las reforma en su laberinto consenso preconcertacion transaccion en la aprobacion silvia otero daniela acosta sebastian cote jose miguel jaim amanda murillo actual approval legislative branch bring literature expansion social policy exe