level relevant variation occurr sectoral level introduc technical-political consensu pre-agreement opposition weaknes overlook sectoral condition also demonstrat complementary role programmatic clientelistic negoti context volatile parti particularistic practic pension reform social policy social protection consensu executivelegislative relation reforma em seu labirinto consenso pre-acordo compromisso na aprovacao da reforma da previdencia na colombia,1.0.0,633942e832cbb4c6
1900-6004,Más+allá+del+“Tíbet+de+América+del+Sur”_+Colombia+y+el+rol+de+potencia+media+en+la+Guerra+Fría+temprana.pdf,Más+allá+del+“Tíbet+de+América+del+Sur”_+Colombia+y+el+rol+de+potencia+media+en+la+Guerra+Fría+temprana_0,en,Beyond the “Tibet of South America”:,"Objective/context: This article reevaluates Colombia’s place in Latin American international history by challenging what we call the López–Drekonja thesis, which portrays the country as passive or as an “Andean Tibet.” It argues that, between 1950 and 1962, Colombia adopted a middlepowermanship role conception that helps explain its selective activism in international peace and security. Methodology: Using a structured, focused comparison (George and Bennett, 2004), the study integrates role theory (Holsti, 1970; Harnisch, 2011) with middle power scholarship. Two cases—Colombia’s participation in the Korean War and its diplomatic leadership in Cuba’s expulsion from the Organization of American States (OAS)—trace how three interrelated motivations (status-seeking, self-interest, and moralism/idealism) shaped role conception and performance. Conclusions: Both cases reveal agency despite structural constraints. In Korea, self-interest predominated, followed by moralism/ idealism and status-seeking; in the “Cuban question,” the order was self-interest > status-seeking > moralism/idealism. Colombia pursued niche diplomacy and legalist multilateralism to punch above its weight, complicating materialist and dependency readings that assume automatic subordination to the United States. Originality: The article proposes a middlepowermanship role conception for a non-canonical Latin American case, linking identity and behavior without requiring explicit self-labeling as a “middle power.” It offers a theoretical–historical reinterpretation of a neglected period in Colombian foreign policy and extends role theory’s analytical scope to peripheral contexts",foreign policy; role theory; middle powers; multilateralism; Korean War; Organization of American States. 134 Colomb. int. 126 • issn 0121-5612 • e-issn 1900-6004 abril-junio 2026 • pp. 133-157 • https://doi.org/10.7440/colombiaint126.2026.05 Más allá del “Tíbet de América del Sur”: Colombia y el rol de potencia media en la Guerra Fría temprana,marcadores,beyond tibet south america,objective context article reevaluat colombia place latin american international history challeng what we call lopez-drekonja thesi which portray country passive andean tibet argu between 1950 1962 colombia adopt middlepowermanship role conception help explain its selective activism international peace security methodology using structur focus comparison george bennett 2004 study integrat role theory holsti 1970 harnisch 2011 middle power scholarship two cases--colombia participation korean war its diplomatic leadership cuba expulsion organ american stat oas --trace how three interrelat motiv status-seek self-interest moralism idealism shap role conception performance conclusion both case reveal agency despite structural constraint korea self-interest predominat follow moralism idealism status-seek cuban question order self-interest status-seek moralism idealism colombia pursu niche diplomacy legalist multilateralism punch above its weight complicat materialist dependency reading assume automatic subordination unit stat originality article propos middlepowermanship role conception non-canonical latin american case link identity behavior without requir explicit self-label middle power offer theoretical-historical reinterpretation neglect period colombian foreign policy extend role theory analytical scope peripheral context,foreign policy role theory middle power multilateralism korean war organ american stat 134 colomb int 126 issn 0121-5612 e-issn 1900-6004 abril-junio 2026 pp 133-157 http doi org 10 7440 colombiaint126 2026 05 mas alla del tibet de america del sur colombia el rol de potencia media en la guerra fria temprana,beyond tibet south america 