1909-5775,interfacial-yesik.pdf,interfacial-yesik_0,en,"dilatacional destaca como un método crucial para analizar propiedades interfaciales, al","To examine the interfacial properties of flours in the development of instant products, a bibliometric study of 633 articles (1983–present) was conducted using the Scopus database. The Science Mapping Analysis Tool (SciMAT) was employed to generate thematic evolution structures, strategic diagrams, and thematic networks, offering both bibliometric and visual insights into the field. The study identified strategic research clusters and key trends, including a growing focus on protein assessment in recent decades. Proteins in flours are essential for stabilizing interfaces, with their behavior influenced by factors such as pH, temperature, and interactions with other food components. Among the various methods available, dilatational rheology emerges as a critical approach for analyzing interfacial properties, as it measures expansion moduli that reflect both elastic and viscous behaviors. Additionally, advanced tools like microparticle size analyzers, interfacial rheometers, and adsorption spectroscopy provide precise insights into interface topography and molecular interactions. Computational models further enhance understanding by predicting complex interfacial behaviors, supporting the optimization of formulations to improve viscoelastic properties, functionality, and sensory quality. This integrative approach, emphasizing interfacial rheology and molecular interactions, is fundamental to driving innovation in the development of stable, functional, and sensorially appealing instant products","Interfacial properties; proteins; emulsions; intermolecular interactions; multiphase systems. DOI: https://doi.org/10.57173/ritc.v1n18a6 Recibido: 16/04/2024 Aceptado: fecha25/06/2024 Fecha de Publicación:27/11/2024 Derechos de autor:© 2024 I + T + C Investigación, Tecnología y Ciencia -Vol. 1, Número 18. 2024 2 1",marcadores,dilatac