1909-7700,04_MED+34(1)_7985.pdf,04_MED+34(1)_7985_0,en,"er consumido cigarrillos electrónicos al menos una vez, y","Introduction: E-cigarette use has increased significantly among young people, despite limited evidence regarding its long-term safety and potential impact on public health. In Colombia, this practice is on the rise, particularly in university settings, which requires a deeper understanding of the phenomenon. Objective: To determine the prevalence of e-cigarette, use among university students in Medellín and to characterize their perceptions, motivations, habits, and sociodemographic, academic, and health conditions. Materials and methods: An observational, descriptive, cross-sectional study with a primary source of information. A structured survey was administered to 225 undergraduate students using non-probability snowball sampling. Quantitative and qualitative variables related to vaping use were analyzed using Jamovi 2.3. Results: 71.6% of respondents reported having used e-cigarettes at least once, and 28% did so regularly. Sixty percent began using ecigarettes out of curiosity, and 18% persisted due to anxiety. Although 78% reported being aware of the risks, a significant portion continued using them. Only 17% considered e-cigarettes less harmful than conventional cigarettes. Conclusion: There is a worrying discrepancy between risk awareness and actual usage behaviors. The findings highlight the need to design educational and public health interventions aimed at reducing the normalization of vaping in university settings","electronic cigarette; students; perception; habits; public health; smokers. Percepções, motivações, hábitos e prevalência do consumo de cigarros eletrônicos (vapeadores) em estudantes universitários de Medellín, Antioquia, 2024-2025",marcadores,er consumido cigarrillo electronico al meno una vez,introduction e-cigarette use has increas significantly among young people despite limit evidence regard its long-term safety potential 