1909-7700,06_MED+34(1)_8099+(1).pdf,06_MED+34(1)_8099+(1)_0,en,"Bosque, Bogotá,","Introduction: The implementation of primary health care strategies requires a highly qualified workforce, in which the role of the family physician is particularly relevant. This study presents the results of surveys conducted in 2017, 2019, and 2021 on the role and employment situation of family medicine specialists in Colombia, and contextualizes the findings at the national and international levels. Materials and methods: A survey was designed using Google Forms. The initial version, consisting of 20 questions, was administered in 2017; for 2019 and 2021, it was adapted to a 22-item questionnaire with closed-ended questions. The survey was disseminated via WhatsApp, Telegram, email, and Facebook. Only board-certified family physicians currently practicing in Colombia were eligible to participate. Results: Family physicians in Colombia are primarily engaged in clinical care activities and, although their work has traditionally focused on outpatient consultations, recent years have shown an increased involvement in emergency care, inpatient care, and research. In contrast, their participation in administrative positions declined between 2017 and 2021. Conclusion: Family physicians in Colombia perform multiple roles in clinical care, administration, teaching, and research. This is related both to the defining characteristics of the specialty and to the dynamics of the health system. Despite advances in primary health care policies, robust regulations are still needed to appropriately position family physicians as key human resources within the Colombian health system",Family medicine; role; primary health care. Papel e situação laboral do médico de família na Colômbia,marcadores,bosque bogota,introduction implementation primary health care strategi requir highly qualifi workforce which role family physician particularly relevant study present result survey conduct 2017 2019 2021 role e