1909-7700,07_MED+34(1)_8197+(3).pdf,07_MED+34(1)_8197+(3)_0,en,empleo con condiciones adecuadas,"Objective: Analyze the barriers and limitations faced by family medicine specialists when practicing in different regions of Colombia. Method: A descriptive qualitative approach was employed, and eighteen family physicians from various areas of the country were intentionally selected. They participated in virtual semi-structured interviews conducted between December 2024 and January 2025, with theoretical saturation reached in the eighteenth interview. Transcripts were analyzed in ATLAS.ti using open and axial coding, with both deductive and inductive categories, and validation was carried out through investigator triangulation. Results: Multiple barriers were identified, including limited awareness of the specialty among patients, colleagues, and institutions, which constrains its recognition and proper integration into health services. Precarious working conditions were also reported, characterized by unstable contracts, outsourcing, and heavy workloads, as well as geographic challenges, particularly in rural and hard-to-reach areas, where deficient infrastructure and dispersed populations hinder the continuous provision of services. The limited availability of jobs with adequate conditions discourages retention in remote territories. Additionally, personal and family factors were observed to influence physicians’ decisions regarding where to practice, such as perceptions of safety, quality of life, access to education for their children, and employment opportunities for their partners. Conclusions: These barriers negatively affect the equitable distribution of family physicians in the country and limit their presence in remote regions, underscoring the need to raise the visibility of the specialty, improve working conditions, and promote comprehensive policies that strengthen primary health care in Colombia",Family medicine; physician distribution; working conditions; quality of life. Barreiras e limitações identificadas por médicos de família para o exercício profissional em diferentes regiões da Colômbia: um estudo qualitativo,marcadores,empleo con condicion adecuada,objective analyze barrier limit faced family medicine specialist when practic different region colombia method descriptive qualitative approach employ eighteen family physician variou area country intentionally select they participat virtual semi-structur interview conduct between december 2024 january 2025 theoretical saturation reach eighteenth interview transcript analyz atla ti using open axial coding both deductive inductive categori validation carri out through investigator triangulation result multiple barrier identifi includ limit awarenes specialty among patient colleagu institution which constrain its recognition proper integration into health servic precariou work condition also report characteriz unstable contract outsourc heavy workload well geographic challeng particularly rural hard-to-reach area where deficient infrastructure dispers popul hinder continuou provision servic limit availability jobs adequate condition discourag retention remote territori additionally personal family factor observ influence physician decision regard where practice such perception safety quality life acces education their children employment opportuniti their partner conclusion these barrier negatively affect equitable distribution family physician country limit their presence remote region underscor need raise visibility specialty improve work condition promote comprehensive polici strengthen primary health care colombia,family medicine physician distribution work condition quality life barreira limitaco identificada por medico de familia para exercicio profissional em diferent regio da colombia um estudo qualitativo,empleo con condicion adecuada objective analyze barrier limit faced family medicine specialist when practic different region colombia method descriptive qualitative approach employ eighteen family physician variou area country intentionally select they participat virtual semi-structur interview conduct between december 2024 january 2025 theoretical saturation reach eighteenth interview transcript analyz atla ti using open axial coding both deductive inductive categori validation carri out through investigator triangulation result multiple barrier identifi includ limit awarenes specialty among patient colleagu institution which constrain its recognition proper integration into health servic precariou work condition also report characteriz unstable contract outsourc heavy workload well geographic challeng particularly rural hard-to-reach area where deficient infrastructure dispers popul hinder continuou provision servic limit availability jobs adequate condition discourag retention remote territori additionally personal family factor observ influence physician decision regard where practice such perception safety quality life acces education their children employment opportuniti their partner conclusion these barrier negatively affect equitable distribution family physician country limit their presence remote region underscor need raise visibility specialty improve work condition promote comprehensive polici strengthen primary health care colombia family medicine physician distribution work condition quality life barreira limitaco identificada por medico de familia para exercicio profissional em diferent regio da colombia um estudo qualitativo,1.0.0,f58b6e2a5d2b8659
1909-7700,08_MED+34(1)_8498+(1).pdf,08_MED+34(1)_8498+(1)_0,es,Obesidad y trabajo de subsistencia,"Objetivo: identificar la relación existente entre las condiciones sociolaborales, hábitos alimentarios y la obesidad en trabajadores mayores (≥ 60 años) con empleos de subsistencia en Medellín-Colombia, 2021. Materiales y métodos: estudio transversal con fuente primaria de información, tomando a 656 trabajadores informales, utilizando muestreo tipo bola de nieve. Se incluyeron 208 ≥ 60 años del estudio macro. Variables: obesidad, clasificada según el índice de masa corporal (imc), condiciones sociodemográficas, laborales, hábitos alimentarios y comorbilidades. Análisis univariado, bivariado y multivariado. Resultados: el 68.7 % eran hombres; 72.6 % tenían 60-69 años; 73.1 % eran cabeza de familia; 54.8 % con > 30 años en su labor; 72.1 % activos/muy activos; 58.7 % comían 3 veces/día; consumo > 5 veces/semana de grasas/aceites, tubérculos/plátanos y cereales; 60.6 % percibía su peso como adecuado. El 72.3 % tenía hipertensión y el 24.6 % diabetes. La prevalencia de obesidad fue de 17.3 % y mayor (p < 0.05) en mujeres (rp = 2.20; ic 1.22-3.94), en edades de * Artículo de Investigación a Doctora en Epidemiología y Bioestadística; Docente-Investigadora. Universidad CES - Facultad de Ciencias de la Salud; Medellín; Colombia; Correo: mgarzon@ces.edu.co; mgarzonduque@gmail.com; ORCID: https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7261-3146 b Interna Medicina; Universidad CES, Facultad de Ciencias de la Salud; Medellín; Colombia. Correo: vargas. stefany@uces.edu.co. ORCID: https://orcid.org/0009-0002-8004-4988 c Interno Medicina; Universidad CES, Facultad de Ciencias de la Salud; Medellín; Colombia. Correo: santos. rodrigo@uces.edu.co. ORCID: https://orcid.org/0009-0009-3043-0435 d Doctor en Demografía. Docente – investigador. Universidad de Antioquia – Facultad Nacional de Salud Pública. Correo: fabio.rodriguez@udea.edu.co. ORCID: https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7791-6090 e Interna Medicina; Universidad CES, Facultad de Ciencias de la Salud; Medellín; Colombia. Correo: nader. sharif@uces.edu.co. ORCID: https://orcid.org/0009-0007-3495-3853 f Interna Medicina; Universidad CES, Facultad de Ciencias de la Salud; Medellín; Colombia. Correo: mantilla.sofia@uces.edu.co. ORCID: https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4790-8242 DOI: https://doi.org/10.18359/rmed.8498 2 60-69 (rp = 4.15; ic 1.32-13.00) y en quienes se percibían con sobrepeso, condición que más aportó a la explicación de mayor prevalencia (rpa = 13.68; ic 5.29-35.36). Conclusiones: la edad, sexo y percepción del peso se asociaron a la mayor prevalencia de obesidad, y esta fue menor en quienes realizaron actividad física. Se destacó un patrón alimentario rico en alimentos hipercalóricos y de bajo consumo de frutas, en un entorno laboral hostil. Se aporta evidencia que pudiera ser útil para el diseño e implementación de programas de educación alimentaria accesible y de reconocimiento temprano de exceso de peso en entornos cercanos a los lugares de trabajo",obesidad; adultos mayores; trabajadores informales; covid-19; hábitos alimentarios. Obesity and Subsistence Work among Older Adults,marcadores,obesidad trabajo subsistencia,objetivo identificar relacion existente entre condicion sociolaboral habit alimentari obesidad trabajador mayor 60 anos emple subsistencia medellin-colombia 2021 material metod estudio transversal fuente primaria informacion tomando 656 trabajador informal utiliz muestreo tipo bola nieve incluyeron 208 60 anos estudio macro variabl obesidad clasificada segun indice masa corporal imc condicion sociodemografic laboral habit alimentari comorbilidad analisis univariado bivariado multivariado resultad 68 eran hombr 72 tenian 60-69 anos 73 eran cabeza familia 54 30 anos labor 72 activ muy activ 58 comian veces dia consumo veces semana gras aceit tubercul platan cereal 60 percibia peso como adecuado 72 tenia hipertension 24 diabet prevalencia obesidad fue 17 mayor 05 mujer rp 20 ic 22-3 94 edad arti