da legitimidad competitividad implemento metodologia cualitativo-descriptiva metodo micmac analisis estructural veintid variabl estrategic examinad mediante matric influencia grado favorabilidad morfologica complementad proceso validacion doce expert sector agroindustrial entre 2023 2024 resultad permiten identificar corto plazo variabl como autenticidad producto export produccion import proteccion consumidor competencia son mas impactan sector presentan tres escenari prospectiv posibl pesimista tendencial optimista derivad vision expert consultad concluye certific dop igp constituyen factor estrategico clave diferenciacion posicionamiento competitivo sin embargo requiere transformacion profunda capacidad productiv tecnologic logistic empres latinoamerican garantizar sostenibilidad mercad extranjer consumidor denominacion origen protegida imagen marca indicacion geografica propiedad intelectual proteccion consumidor clasificacion jel d18 d24 f10 m2 articulo investigacion financiado universidad catolica luis amigo convocatoria interna radicado resolucion 02 comite investig 20 noviembre 2023 proyecto investigacion id,1.0.0,4464a9b0c157d5d8
1909-7719,7917_RFCE+34(1)_2.pdf,7917_RFCE+34(1)_2_0,en,"ción financiado por la Universidad Católica Luis Amigó, en la convocatoria interna","In the global scenario, Protected Designations of Origin (pdo) and Protected Geographical Indications (pgi) are considered strategic assets that enable organizations to differentiate their products in foreign markets. The objective of this research is to identify the benefits that companies obtain from these certifications regarding their internationalization processes, supported by institutional theory, which explains the adoption of certifications as a search for legitimacy and competitiveness. A qualitative-descriptive methodology was implemented using the MicMac method and the structural analysis of twenty-two strategic variables examined through influence, favorability, and morphological matrices, complemented by a validation process with twelve experts from the agroindustrial sector between 2023 and 2024. The results identify that, in the short term, variables such as product authenticity, exports, production, imports, consumer protection, and competition have the greatest impact on the sector. Three possible prospective scenarios (pessimistic, trend-based, and optimistic) derived from the perspectives of the consulted experts are presented. It is concluded that pdo and pgi certifications constitute a key strategic factor in differentiation and competitive positioning; however, a profound transformation in the productive, technological, and logistical capacities of Latin American companies is required to ensure sustainability in foreign markets",consumer; protected designation of origin; brand image; geographical indication; intellectual property; consumer protection. Denominação de origem protegida e indicações geográficas: impacto empresarial em mercados estrangeiros,marcadores,cion financiado por la universidad catolica luis amigo en la convocatoria interna,global scenario protect design origin pdo protect geographical