1909-7719,8036_RFCE+34(1)_2.pdf,8036_RFCE+34(1)_2_0,en,Ciencias Económicas,"The growing importance of the circular economy as a model for addressing various environmental and sustainability challenges has generated significant academic interest in its integration into supply chains. This article aims to analyze the evolution of scientific production and research perspectives on the circular economy and supply chains. The results of a bibliometric study are presented, in which tools such as R-Studio, Bibliometrix, Tree of Science, and Gephi were used to process 2,358 bibliographic records retrieved from Scopus and Web of Science between January 2013 and January 2025. Among the main findings, the study highlights an average annual growth rate of scientific production of 19.17%, the research hegemony of the United Kingdom, and the identification of different trends and future lines of study, including three research perspectives: (1) convergence between Industry 4.0 and the circular economy in industrial contexts, (2) implementation of circular business models, and (3) circular economy in food system losses. The analyses reveal the existence of adoption and systemic interoperability gaps in the supply chains of developed and developing countries, as well as opportunities to advance research integrating emerging technologies with a critical focus on environmental and social sustainability within strategic decision-making","circular economy; supply chains; circular models; servitization; sustainability; bibliometrics. Economia circular e cadeias de suprimentos: mapeamento científico, árvore da ciência e perspectivas de pesquisa",marcadores,ciencia economica,grow importance circular economy model address variou environmental sustainability challeng has generat significant academic interest its integration into supply chain article aims analyze evolution scientific production research perspectiv circular economy supply chain result bibliometric study present which tool such r-studio bibliometrix tree science gephi used proces 358 bibliographic record retriev scopu web science between january 2013 january 2025 among main finding study highlight average annual growth rate scientific production 19 17 research hegemony unit kingdom identification different trend future line study includ three research perspectiv convergence between industry circular economy industrial context implementation circular busines model circular economy food system loss analys reveal existence adoption systemic interoperability gaps supply chain develop develop countri well opportuniti advance research integrat emerg technologi critical focu environmental social sustainability within strategic decision-mak,circular economy supply chain circular model servit sustainability bibliometric economia circular cadeia de suprimento mapeamento cientifico arvore da ciencia perspectiva de pesquisa,ciencia economica grow importance circular economy model address variou environmental sustainability challeng has generat significant academic interest its integration into supply chain article aims analyze evolution scientific production research perspectiv circular economy supply chain result bibliometric study present which tool such r-studio bibliometrix tree science gephi used proces 358 bibliographic record retriev scopu web science between january 2013 january 2025 among main finding study highlight average annual growth rate scientific production 19 17 research hegemony unit kingdom identification different trend future line study includ three research perspectiv convergence between industry circular economy industrial context implementation circular busines model circular economy food system loss analys reveal existence adoption systemic interoperability gaps supply chain develop develop countri well opportuniti advance research integrat emerg technologi critical focu environmental social sustainability within strategic decision-mak circular economy supply chain circular