nergi renovabl grado diversificacion tecnologica efecto interaccion entre concentracion articulo investigacion doctor administracion docente-investigador departamento economia administracion universidad cald manizal colombia correo electronico pedro duque ucald edu co orcid https orcid org 0000-0003-4950-8262 especialista gerencia financiera internacional magister administracion financiera universidad eafit medellin colombia correo electronico jyariasf eafit edu co orcid https orcid org 0009-00075741-3008 especialista gerencia proyect magister administracion financiera universidad eafit medellin colombia correo electronico givelasqut eafit edu co orcid https orcid org 0009-0005-72275606 doi https doi org 10 18359 rfce 8249 2026 editorial neogranadina revista facultad cienci economic enero-junio issn 0121-6805 e-issn 1909-7719 pp 1-28 vol 34 participacion renovable no presentan relacion significativ indicador rentabilidad esto sugiere benefici asociad especializacion tecnologica manifiestan eficiencia capital mientr diversificacion portafolio --particular hacia fuent renovables-- no traduce mejor financier inmediat evidencia indica transicion energetica sector electrico no genera efect homogene corto plazo ni desempeno financiero plante necesidad evaluar sus impact horizont temporal mas ampli bajo condicion regulatori tecnologic proceso consolidacion calentamiento global fuent energia alternativ desarrollo sostenible econometria financiera finanz corporativ gobernanza codigo jel q54 t42 q01 c58 g30 effect of portfolio diversification on financial profitability evidence from the main power generation compani in colombia 2015-2024,1.0.0,e01a66d6337f5af4
1909-7719,8249_RFCE+34(1)_2.pdf,8249_RFCE+34(1)_2_0,en,energética en el sector eléctrico no genera efectos homogéneos a corto plazo ni en el desempeño,"This study seeks to analyze the relationship between diversification of the electricity generation portfolio (renewable and conventional sources) and the financial profitability of the main energy generation companies in Colombia between 2015 and 2024. Panel data models with fixed effects by company and year are employed, considering three key indicators of financial performance (roa, roce, and net margin) as dependent variables. The Herfindahl-Hirschman Index, the percentage of generation from renewable energy sources, and the number of technologies used constitute the explanatory variables. The findings indicate that greater technological concentration is positively and significantly associated with operational profitability measured by roce; however, this relationship is not statistically significant for roa or net margin. Factors such as the share of renewable energy, the degree of technological diversification, and the interaction effect between concentration and renewable participation do not show significant relationships with profitability indicators. This suggests that the benefits associated with technological specialization are reflected in capital efficiency, whereas portfolio diversification—particularly toward renewable sources—does not translate into immediate financial improvements. The evidence indicates that the energy transition in the electricity sector does not generate homogeneous short-term effects on financial performance, highlighting the need to assess its impacts over broader time horizons and under regulatory and technological conditions still undergoing consolidation",global warming; alternative energy sources; sustainable development; financial econometrics; corporate finance; governance. Efeito da diversificação do portfólio sobre a rentabilidade financeira: evidências das principais empresas geradoras de energia na Colômbia (2015-2024),marcadores,energetica en el sector electrico no genera efecto homogeneo corto plazo ni en el desempeno,study seek analyze relationship between diversification electricity generation portfolio renewable conventional sourc financial profitability main energy generation compani colombia between 2015 2024 panel data model fixed effect company year employ consider three key indicator financial performance roa roce net margin dependent variabl herfindahl-hirschman index percentage generation renewable energy sourc number technologi used constitute explanatory variabl finding indicate greater technological concentration positively significantly associat operational profitability measur roce however relationship not statistically significant roa net margin factor such share renewable energy degree technological diversification interaction effect between concentration renewable participation do not show significant relationship profitability indicator suggest benefit associat technological special reflect capital efficiency wherea portfolio diversification--particularly toward renewable sources--do not translate into immediate financial improvement evidence indicat energy transition electricity sector does not generate homogeneou short-term effect financial performance highlight need asses its impact over broader time horizon under regulatory technological condition still undergo consolidation,global warm alternative energy sourc sustainable development financial econometric corporate finance governance efeito da diversificacao do portfolio sobre rentabilidade financeira evidencia das principai empresa geradora de energia na colombia 2015-2024,energetica en el sector electrico no genera efecto homogeneo corto plazo ni en el desempeno study seek analyze relationship between diversification electricity generation portfolio renewable conventional sourc financial profitability main energy generation compani colombia between 201