1909-7719,8346_RFCE+34(1)_2.pdf,8346_RFCE+34(1)_2_0,en,d (España). Profesor asociado del,"In small and medium-sized enterprises, the benefits of Information and Communication Technologies are reflected in improved performance, growth, expansion, and the development of new products. However, the impact of ict on business performance remains widely debated, with inconclusive findings. Research in management and information systems often addresses ict in abstract terms, without distinguishing the effect of different types of technologies and their level of use within organizations. This study aimed to analyze the effect of the availability and level of use of different ict tools and applications, as well as digital competencies, on the operational performance of tourism smes in Valle del Cauca, Colombia. A survey was administered to 100 legal representatives or managers of tourism firms, drawn from a population of 2,434 smes. Partial Least Squares Structural Equation Modeling was used to analyze the relationships among the variables and between the constructs and their indicators. The results showed that the level of ict has a positive and significant influence on operational performance. However, digital competencies did not show a significant moderating effect on the relationship between ict level and operational performance. It is concluded that, in the analyzed sample, ict level is a relevant predictor of operational performance, although its effect does not necessarily depend on the general level of digital competencies. These findings provide empirical evidence on the strategic value of ict in tourism smes in emerging economies and suggest the need to further examine other organizational factors that may strengthen this relationship","digital competencies; operational performance; ict level; smes; tourism. Influência do nível de tic e das competências digitais no desempenho operacional de pmes do setor turístico do Valle del Cauca, Colômbia",marcadores,espana pro