perable metodologia centra recoleccion datos procesamiento almacenamiento modelado 3d respectiva validacion fin tener confiabilidad datos representacion almacenamiento aspect fisic juridic citygml resultado permite visualizar unico modelo relacion entre objet component fisic juridic economic catastro incorpor caracteristic geometric semantic bajo estandar internacional cumpl esquema validacion geometrica cada nivel detalle lod identific uno aspect mejorar autointerseccion diferent geometri divers element modelad citygml catastro 3d catastro multiproposito validacion geometrica development of prototype of 3d cadastral model based on doi https doi org 10 18359 rcin 7882 2026 editorial neogranadina revista ciencia ingenieria neogranadina enero junio issn 0124-8170 e-issn 1909-7735 1-26 vol 36 geoprocessing tools for the visualization of the legal and physical aspects of hor,1.0.0,845bebc19ac7f64c
1909-7735,7882_Cumbe&Castillo+CienciaEing+36(1)2026+UMNG.pdf,7882_Cumbe&Castillo+CienciaEing+36(1)2026+UMNG_0,en,n único modelo las relaciones entre,"This work records the development of the construction of a 3D cadastral model prototype based on CityGML 2.0, supported by FME and Google SketchUp, as geoprocessing tools complementa ry to GIS. This study is focused on the residential complex Condominios II de Tejares, a horizontal prop erty in Soacha (Cundinamarca); a place where private and common property of the co-ownership was visualized through 3D modeling to contribute to different cadastral applications. Representing the real right of property, delineating its legal and physical aspects through an interoperable model. The methodology focuses on the collection of data, its processing and storage; on 3D modeling and its respective validation, in order to have reliability in the data of representation and storage of the phys ical and legal aspects in CityGML 2.0. The result allows visualizing, in a single model, the relationships between objects and the physical, legal, and economic components of the cadastre, incorporating geometric and semantic characteristics, under international standards. Complying with the geomet ric scheme and validation at each level of detail (LOD), identifying that one of the aspects to improve is the self-intersection of the different geometries for the various modeled elements","CityGML; 3D Cadastre; Multipurpose Cadastre; Geometric Validation. Desenvolvimento de um Protótipo de Modelo Cadastral 3D Baseado em Ferramentas de Geoprocessamento para a Visualização dos Aspectos Legais e Físicos de uma Propriedade Horizontal no Município de Soacha, Cundinamarca",marcadores,unico modelo las relacion entre,work record development construction 3d cadastral model prototype based citygml support fme google sketchup geoprocess tool complementa ry gis study focus residential complex condominio ii de tejar horizontal prop erty soacha cundinamarca place where private common property co-ownership visualiz through 3d model contribute different cadastral applic represent real right property delineat its legal physical aspect through interoperable model methodology focus collection data its process storage 3d model its respective validation order have reliability data representation storage phys ical legal aspect citygml result allow visualiz single model relationship between object physical legal economic component cadastre incorporat geometric semantic characteristic under international standard comply geomet ric scheme validation each level detail lod identify one aspect improve self-intersection different geometri variou model element,citygml 3d cadastre multipurpose cadastre geometric validation desenvolvimento de um prototipo de modelo cadastral 3d baseado em ferramenta de geoprocessamento para visualizacao dos aspecto legai fisico de uma propriedade horizontal no municipio de soacha cundinamarca,unico modelo las relacion entre work record development construction 3d cadastral model prototype based citygml support fme google sketchup geoprocess tool complementa ry gis study focus residential complex condominio ii de tejar horizontal prop erty soacha cundinamarca place where private common property co-ownership visualiz through 3d model contribute different cadastral applic represent real right property delineat its legal physical aspect through interoperable model methodology focus collection data its process storage 3d model its respective validation order have reliability data representation storage phys ical legal aspect citygml result allow visualiz single model relationship between object physical legal economic component cadastre incorporat geometric semantic characteristic under international standard comply geomet ric scheme validation each level detail lod identify one aspect improve self-intersection different geometri variou model element citygml 3d cadastre multipurpose cadastre geometric validation desenvolvimento de um prototipo de modelo cadastral 3d baseado em ferramenta de geoprocessamento para visualizacao dos aspecto legai fisico de uma propriedade horizontal no municipio de soacha cundinamarca,1.0.0,f26b086f5e2de22d
1909-7735,7889_Ávila+eTaL+CienciaEing+36(1)2026+UMNG.pdf,7889_Ávila+eTaL+CienciaEing+36(1)2026+UMNG_0,es,"Especialista en Gerencia para el Desarrollo Organizacional. Universidad de Cundinamarca, Fusagasugá, Colombia.","Algunos procesos de inestabilidad y deformación superficial son continuos en el tiempo y es posible que desencadenen deslizamientos que pueden comprometer la integridad de las personas y la economía de los territorios. Esta investigación tuvo como objetivo principal identificar y mapear zonas de inestabilidad y deformación superficial en el municipio de Arbeláez, Cundinamarca, mediante el uso de técnicas avanzadas de interferometría diferencial con radar de apertura sintética (DInSAR). Para ello, se aplicaron dos metodologías complementarias: Persistent Scatterer (PS) y Small Baseline Subset (SBAS), y se analizaron 27 imágenes satelitales de radar en órbita descendente, obtenidas de la plataforma Sentinel-1 de la Agencia Espacial Europea. Como resultado principal, se lograron identificar y mapear zonas afectadas por movimientos de la superficie terrestre, destacándose áreas con deformaciones significativas. En la vereda de Hato Viejo se registraron desplazamientos de 12,8 mm/año en dirección vertical y 4,8 mm/año en dirección horizontal utilizando la metodología SBAS; mien tras que con la metodología PS se obtuvieron valores de 25,8 mm/año y 9,5 mm/año en las mismas direcciones, respectivamente. En la vereda San Luis se cuantificaron deformaciones de 14,7 mm/año (arriba-abajo) y 6,2 mm/ año (este-oeste) con SBAS, y 13,8 mm/año vertical y 5,6 mm/año horizontal con PS. Por otro lado, en la vereda Santa Bárbara se detectaron magnitudes de -9,98 mm/año (arriba-abajo) y -13,2 mm/año (este-oeste) con SBAS; -3,0 mm/año (este-oeste), y -4,2 mm/año (arriba-abajo) con PS. Estos resultados fueron validados mediante visi tas de campo, lo que confirmó la precisión y confiabilidad de los datos obtenidos","interferometría; radar; Sentinel-1; DInSAR; InSAR; PSI; SBAS