or rgb capturad te lefon movil dos model neuronal artificial elaboraron compararon red perceptron multicapa mlp red neuronal convolucional cnn ambas redes clasificaron cuatro estad maduracion banano variedad cavendish red mlp alcanzo exactitud general 77 mostr desempeno adecuado entorn limitad recurs parte red cnn logro exactitud 99 metric preci sion 98-1 00 sensibilidad 97-1 00 sobresalient evidenci capacidad extraer caracteristic relevant directa imagen resultad confirman viabilidad uso dispositiv movil como herramient captura confiabl potencial model neuronal integracion apli cacion clasificacion automatica tiempo real este trabajo abre agenda futura orientada desarrollo solucion accesibl impulsen transformacion digital sector bananero colombiano analisis sensorial aprendizaje profundo cavendish ciencia color escala von loesecke inteligencia artificial maduracion fruto musa sp redes neuronal artificial vision artificial doi https doi org 10 18359 rcin 8314 2026 editorial neogranadina revista ciencia ingenieria neogranadina enero junio issn 0124-8170 e-issn 1909-7735 1-15 vol 36 banana rip,1.0.0,6424ccf6f66ec9af
1909-7735,8314+LopezJimenez+EtAL+CienciaEing+36(1)2026+UMNG.pdf,8314+LopezJimenez+EtAL+CienciaEing+36(1)2026+UMNG_0,en,ágenes. Los resultados confirman la viabilidad del uso de dispositivos móviles,"Globally, bananas are one of the most consumed fruits, representing a significant sector of the Colombian economy. Their stage of ripeness determines their quality, shelf life, and commer cial value; therefore, identifying the optimal harvest and marketing time is essential. Conventionally, this evaluation is manual and visual, which involves subjectivity and human error. This study pro poses an alternative based on artificial neural network modeling applied to digital images in the rgb color space, captured with mobile phones. Two artificial neural network models were developed and compared: a multilayer perceptron network (mlp) and a convolutional neural network (cnn). Both networks classified four ripening stages in Cavendish bananas. The mlp network achieved an over all accuracy of 0.77, demonstrating adequate performance for resource-constrained environments. The cnn network, for its part, achieved an accuracy of 0.99, with outstanding precision (0.98-1.00) and sensitivity (0.97-1.00) metrics, demonstrating its ability to extract relevant features directly from images. The results confirm the viability of using mobile devices as reliable capture tools and the po tential of neural network models for integration into real-time automatic classification applications. This work opens a future agenda focused on developing accessible solutions that drive the digital transformation of the Colombian banana sector",sensory analysis; deep learning; Cavendish; color science; Von Loesecke scale; Artificial Intelligence; fruit ripening; Musa sp. L.; artificial neural networks; artificial visión. Classificação de maturação da banana usando Modelagem Neural Artificial Aplicada ao espaço RGB em imagens,marcadores,agen los resultado confirman la viabilidad del uso de dispositivo movi