1909-8391,Dialnet-ElGoceDeLaNadaDeLaDesaparicionForzada-10380301.pdf,Dialnet-ElGoceDeLaNadaDeLaDesaparicionForzada-10380301_0,en,de un discurso biopolítico que busca control total sobre la vida y la muerte. Ante,"The article reflects on forced disappearance and crematory ovens, among other devices, as extreme symbols of a death machinery designed with technological efficiency to execute the final solution to the so-called problem of difference. These devices represent a form of necropolitics aimed at radically eliminating the other, understood as the one who embodies difference and the impossibility of total appropriation. Within this logic, the goal is to construct a homogeneous and flawless society. Crematory ovens, as sinister expressions of this ideology, reveal how science and capitalism can instrumentalize subjects, reducing them to objects within a biopolitical discourse that seeks total control over life and death. In the face of increasingly efficient necropolitical devices in neoliberal capitalism, the aim is to place every subject in a state of nothingness—a neighbor turned into a likeness, a consumer who is also consumed. Against this state of affairs, the proposal from a psychoanalytic praxis is to sustain a space for listening to the subject-as-neighbor, creating devices that enable their emergence. This requires ethical-political listening that not only allows the subject and their suffering—caused by various violent experiences, including forced 3 Tesis psicológica | Vol. 20(1) Enero-junio /25| pp. 1-24| E- ISSN: 2422-045 disappearance—to be heard, but also opens possibilities for transforming that suffering into something else","jouissance, forced disappearance, emptiness, neighbor. Los hornos crematorios: haciendo nada con el prójimo Juan Frío es un corregimiento de Villa del Rosario en Norte de Santander, Colombia, frontera con Venezuela. El mismo nombre de este lugar parece extraído del texto de Lo siniestro freudiano. Allí se construyeron hornos crematorios para desaparecer los cuerpos y restos de quienes fueron",marcadores,de un discurso biopolitico que busca control total sobre la vida la muerte ante,article reflect forc disappearance crematory oven among other devic extreme symbol death machinery design technological efficiency execute final solution so-call problem difference these devic represent form necropolitic aimed radically eliminat other understood one who embodi difference impossibility total appropriation within logic goal construct homogeneou flawles society crematory oven sinister expression ideology reveal how science capitalism can instrumentalize subject reduc them object within biopolitical discourse seek total control over life death face increas efficient necropolitical devic neoliberal capitalism aim place every subject state nothingness--a neighbor turn into likenes consumer who also consum against state affair proposal psychoanalytic praxi sustain space listen subject-as-neighbor creat devic enable their emergence requir ethical-political listen not only allow subject their suffering--caus variou violent experienc includ forc tesi psicologica vol 20 enero-junio 25 pp 1-24 e- issn 2422-045 disappearance--to heard but also open possibiliti transform suffer into someth else,jouissance forc disappearance emptines neighbor los horno crematorio haciendo nada con el projimo juan frio es un corregimiento de villa del rosario en norte de santander colombia frontera con venezuela el mismo nombre de este lugar parece extraido del texto de lo siniestro freudiano alli se construyeron horno crematorio para desaparecer los cuerpo resto de quien fueron,de un discurso biopolitico que busca control total sobre la vida la muerte ante article reflect forc disappearance crematory oven among other devic extreme symbol death machinery design technological efficiency execute final solution so-call problem difference these devic represent form necropolitic aimed radically eliminat other understood one who 