1909-8391,Dialnet-HistoriaYMemoria-10380294.pdf,Dialnet-HistoriaYMemoria-10380294_0,en,"os Latinoamericanos (CELA), en la","The article presents a background in which memory is blocked, but due to the sudden events of the 20th century, it resurfaces and demands its incorporation as a necessary tool for understanding the past. At the same time, it establishes a new system of representations, revealing that past events can be transformed or manipulated to become a constructive principle of present reality. The text explores these shifts between history and memory, focusing on the uses and abuses of remembrance, and on the places where the distortion of the past is manifested. All of this is carried out through the narratives shaped by memory and ideology; on one hand, it attempts cultural integration through symbolic mediations, and on the other, it distributes distorted images and stories that serve as a preferred instrument of domination. In this way, through the manipulation of sources, texts, images, and symbols, the official, authorized, publicly learned and celebrated history is written—exalting false foundational events and imaginary tales of glory in order to legitimize order and justify power. At the end of this analysis, a theoretical alternative will be proposed from hermeneutics, offering a stance to contemplate, from different angles and perspectives, the nuances of the complexity of the past","history, memory, hermeneutics, past, manipulation Brecha en el tiempo Nuestra herencia nos fue legada sin testamento alguno. -Hannah Arendt Por sí mismos, los acontecimientos no tienen un significado inherente ni la suma de todos ellos reflejan un sentido único o último; la noción teleológica de la historia es una 3 Tesis psicológica | Vol. 20(1) Enero-junio /25| pp. 1-17| E- ISSN: 2422-045 es",marcadores,os latinoamericano cela en la,article present background which memory block but due sudden event 20th century resurfac demand its incorporation necessary tool und