1909-9746,1+20252.pdf,1+20252_0,desconocido,1 20252,"Visión Electrónica Vol. 19 No. 2 (2025) • Julio-Diciembre • ISSN 1909-9746 Visión Electrónica https://doi.org/10.14483/issn.2248-4728 A RESEARCH VISION Evaluation of Li-Fi performance with Trulifi 6002: Connectivity validation using distance ranges Evaluación del desempeño de Li-Fi con Trulifi 6002: validación de conectividad usando rangos de distancia Edith Paola Estupiñan Cuesta1 , Juan Carlos Martínez Quintero2 , Jhon Stiven Gamboa Suarez3 INFORMACIÓN DEL ARTÍCULO Historia del artículo: Enviado: 15/05/2025 Recibido: 01/07/2025 Aceptado: 17/11/2025 Keywords: Indoor ICMP Network Communication Li-Fi RTT Trulifi 6002 Palabras clave: Indoor ICMP Redes de comunicaciones Li-Fi RTT Trulifi 6002 ABSTRACT Li-Fi is an innovative technology that uses visible light to transmit data at high speeds. While it still faces some challenges, its potential to revolutionize wireless communications is undeniable. Unlike Wi-Fi, which uses radio waves to transmit data, Li-Fi leverages visible light, mainly emitted by light-emitting diodes (LEDs), to create a fast and secure communication medium. This work presents the results of an experimental study to evaluate the performance of Li-Fi technology using the Trulifi 6002 system in indoor environments. A Li-Fi network was implemented in a LAN environment evaluated in 3 scenarios with variations in luminosity and distance between the receiver and the transmitter. The objective was to validate the connectivity of the system at various distance ranges ",,respaldo_sin_marcadores,20252,vision electronica vol 19 no 2025 julio-diciembre issn 1909-9746 vision electronica http doi org 10 14483 issn 2248-4728 research vision evaluation li-fi performance trulifi 6002 connectivity validation using distance rang evaluacion desempeno li-fi trulifi 6002 validacion conectividad usando rang distancia edith paola estupinan cuesta1 juan carl martinez quintero2 jhon stiven gamboa suarez3 informacion articul