1909-9746,12+20252.pdf,12+20252_0,desconocido,12 20252,"Visión Electrónica Vol. 19 No. 2 (2025) • Julio-Diciembre • ISSN 1909-9746 Visión Electrónica https://doi.org/10.14483/issn.2248-4728 A RESEARCH VISION Maximizing winter comfort: A global bibliometric study of passive solar heating techniques Maximizar el confort invernal: Un estudio bibliométrico global de las técnicas de calefacción solar pasiva Antony Romero-GranadoS1 , Brayan Eduardo Tarazona-Romero2 , Javier Gonzalo Ascanio-Villabona3 INFORMACIÓN DEL ARTÍCULO Historia del artículo: Enviado: 20/05/2025 Recibido: 01/07/2025 Aceptado: 17/11/2025 Keywords: Bibliometric Analysis Passive Heating Solar Energy Solar Radiation Winter Comfort Palabras clave: Análisis bibliométrico calefacción pasiva energía solar radiación solar confort invernal ABSTRACT Passive heating techniques offer a sustainable alternative for harnessing solar energy to heat buildings during the winter months. This paper presents a bibliometric analysis of research on passive heating methods from 2004 to 2024. Using data from the Scopus database and VOSviewer software, the study examines the evolution of publications in this field, exploring the variety of passive heating techniques and their integration with solar radiation. Key research trends are identified through an analysis of term co-occurrence, leading authors, countries, continents, and institutions. The study highlights the most researched passive heating techniques and assesses their correlation with global solar radiation maps. Additionally, it e",,respaldo_sin_marcadores,12 20252,vision electronica vol 19 no 2025 julio-diciembre issn 1909-9746 vision electronica http doi org 10 14483 issn 2248-4728 research vision maximiz winter comfort global bibliometric study passive solar heat techniqu maximizar confort invernal estudio bibliometrico global tecnic calefaccion solar pasiva antony romero-granados1 brayan eduardo tarazona-romero2 javier gonzalo ascanio-villabona3 informacion arti