deportista indic mayor entrenamiento menor compensacion otros segment corporal optimiz gesto deportivo rendimiento relacion estabilidad estatica dinamica no evidencian diferenci relevant entre participant ciclismo cinematica electromiografia estabilidad kinematic stabilometric and electromyographic characterization of road bike pedaling case report,1.0.0,67da47a67dc7456f
1909-9762,1369-Texto del artículo-6864-3-10-20200830.pdf,1369-Texto del artículo-6864-3-10-20200830_0,en,"ional, las diferencias son más evidentes en tronco","─ Objective: To determine the characteristics of power, speed, heart rate, kinematics, stabilometric and electromyographic pedaling on a road bike in a professional and amateur cyclists. Methodology: The study type is a case study conducted with 2 cyclists (one professional and one amateur) who are tested for kinematics, stabilometry and electromyography with Bioengineering technology. Results: The power shows linear tendency being greater in the professional cyclist compared to the amateur. The speed with linear behavior is greater in the professional cyclist. The kinematic analysis shows greater consistency in the movements performed by the professional cyclist. The differences are more evident in the trunk and ankle, extreme-proximal and distal joints of the kinetic chain. Muscle activity showed more stable patterns and larger amplitudes in the professional cyclist, ψ Dirección para correspondencia: jcastellanos@autonoma.edu.co Revista Ingeniería Biomédica ISSN 1909-9762 / E-ISSN 1909-9991 Volumen 13 / Número 26 / julio-diciembre de 2019 / pp.47-59 Universidad EIA / Envigado, Colombia DOI: https://doi.org/10.24050/19099762.n26.2019.1369 48 REVISTA INGENIERÍA BIOMÉDICA according to stability, the Romberg index in both cyclists is normal with a value of 0,879 for the professional and 0,704 for the amateur. Conclusion: The resistance is related to the level of training of the athlete, indicating that the greater the training, the less compensation with other body segments; optimizing the sporting gesture and performance. In relation to static and dynamic stability, there are no relevant differences between the participants","─ cycling, kinematics, electromyography, stability Caracterização cinemática, estabilométrica e eletromiográfica do pedal de bicicleta de estrada. Relato de caso",marcadores,ional las diferencia son mas evident en tronco,objective determine characteristic power speed heart rate kinematic stabilometric electromyographic pedal road bike professional amateur cyclist methodology study type case study conduct cyclist one professional one amateur who test kinematic stabilometry electromyography bioengineer technology result power show linear tendency being greater professional cyclist compar amateur speed linear behavior greater professional cyclist kinematic analysi show greater consistency movement perform professional cyclist differenc more evident trunk ankle extreme-proximal distal joint kinetic chain muscle activity show more stable pattern larger amplitud professional cyclist ps direccion para correspondencia jcastellano autonoma edu co revista ingenieria biomedica issn 1909-9762 e-issn 1909-9991 volumen 13 numero 26 julio-diciembre de 2019 pp 47-59 universidad eia envigado colombia doi http doi org 10 24050 19099762 n26 2019 1369 48 revista ingenieria biomedica accord stability romberg index both cyclist normal value 879 professional 704 amateur conclusion resistance relat level train athlete indicat greater train less compensation other body segment optimiz sport gesture performance relation static dynamic stability there no relevant differenc between participant,cycl kinematic electromyography stability caracterizacao cinematica estabilometrica eletromiografica do pedal de bicicleta de estrada relato de caso,ional las diferencia son mas evident en tronco objective determine characteristic power speed heart rate kinematic stabilometric electromyographic pedal road bike professional amateur cyclist methodology study type case study conduct cyclist one professional one amateur who test kinematic stabilometry electromyography bioengineer technology result power show linear tendency being greater professional cyclist compar amateur speed linear behavior greater professional cyclist kinematic analysi show greater consistency movement perform professional cyclist differenc more evident trunk ankle extreme-proximal distal joint kinetic chain muscle activity show more stable pattern larger amplitud professional cyclist ps direccion para correspondencia jcastellano autonoma edu co revista ingenieria biomedica issn 1909-9762 e-issn 1909-9991 volumen 13 numero 26 julio-diciembre de 2019 pp 47-59 universidad eia envigado colombia doi http doi org 10 24050 19099762 n26 2019 1369 48 revista ingenieria biomedica accord stability romberg index both cyclist normal value 879 professional 704 amateur conclusion resistance relat level train athlete indicat greater train less compensation other body segment optimiz sport gesture performance relation static dynamic stability there no relevant differenc between participant cycl kinematic electromyography stability caracterizacao cinematica estabilometrica eletromiografica do pedal de bicicleta de estrada relato de caso,1.0.0,74a1983c62d2726f
1909-9762,1370-Texto del artículo-6768-3-10-20200913.pdf,1370-Texto del artículo-6768-3-10-20200913_0,en,Revista Ingeniería Biomédica,"─ Background: Breast cancer is a disease that affects a large part of the Brazilian female population. Especially, those bones metastasis developed in the spinal column. This can produce potential fractures with neurological compromise or reduction of the life’s quality of the patient due to chronic pain. Objective: Computational dosimetry study in vertebrae models simulating bone metastasis locating a radioactive bone cement with Sm-153, Ho-166 or Y-90 in the vertebral body. Methods: Radiological images of animal vertebrae was used to construct a model using the MCNPx code (MonteCarlo N-Particle code). Deposited doses were evaluated in the axial plane (XY) respect to implant of the radioactive bone cement into the metastasis. The nearest organ of risk (OAR) was the spinal cord and the planning target volume (PTV) was the implant itself on the vertebrae. The Samarium-153 (Sm-153), Holmium-166 (Ho-166) and Yttrium-90 (Y-90) radionuclides were considered. Results: The therapeutic deposited dose obtained in the implant plane by radioactive bone cement reaches levels above 70 Gy for specific activities close to 3 GBq∙mg-1 with suitable values for the Y-90 coupled to the cement. Exposure to Ho-166 produces a dose such that cover 76,49 % and 62,77 % for two cases with metastasis respect to PTV while Y-90 covers 94,30 % and 80,91 % on the PTV. Conclusions: The radioactive cement implant may potentially to make an optimal tumor control and lower side effects in organs at risk","Computational dosimetry, MCNPx, radioactive bone cement, Vertebroplasty. Evaluación dosimétrica computacional en modelos vertebrales usando un cemento óseo radioactivo con Sm-153, Ho-166, Y-90",marcadores,revista ingenieria biomedica,background breast cancer disease affect large part brazilian female population especially those bone metastasi develop spinal column can produce potential fractur neurological compromise reduction life quality patient due chronic pain objective computational dosimetry study vertebrae model simulat bone metastasi locat radioactive bone cement sm-153 ho-166 y-90 vertebral body method radiological imag animal vertebrae used construct model using mcnpx code montecarlo n-particle code deposit dose evaluat axial plane xy respect implant radioactive bone cement into metastasi nearest organ risk oar spinal cord plann target volume ptv implant itself vertebrae samarium-153 sm-153 holmium-166 ho-166 yttrium-90 y-90 radionuclid consider result therapeutic deposit dose obtain implant plane radioactive bone cement reach level above 70 gy specific activiti close gbqmg-1 suitable valu y-90 coupl cement exposure ho-166 produc dose such cover 76 49 62 77 two case metastasi respect ptv while y-90 cover 94 30 80 91 ptv conclusion radioactive cement implant may potentially make optimal tumor control lower side effect organ risk,computational dosimetry mcnpx radioactive bone cement vertebroplasty evaluacion dosimetrica computacional en modelo vertebral usando un cemento oseo radioactivo con sm-153 ho-166 y-90,revista ingenieria biomedica background breast cancer disease affect large part brazilian female population especially those bone metastasi develop spinal column can produce potential fractur neurological compromise reduction life quality patient due chronic pain objective computational dosimetry study vertebrae model simulat bone metastasi locat radioactive bone cement sm-153 ho-166 y-90 vertebral body method radiological imag animal vertebrae used construct model using mcnpx code montecarlo n-particle code deposit dose evaluat axial plane xy respect implant radioactive bone cement into metastasi nearest organ risk oar spinal cord plann target volume ptv implant itself vertebrae samarium-153 sm-153 holmium-166 ho-166 yttrium-90 y-90 radionuclid consider result therapeutic deposit dose obtain implant plane radioactive bone cement reach level above 70 gy specific activiti close gbqmg-1 suitable valu y-90 coupl cement exposure ho-166 produc dose such cover 76 49 62 77 two case metastasi respect ptv while y-90 cover 94 30 80 91 ptv conclusion radioactive cement implant may potentially make optimal tumor control lower side effect organ risk computational dosimetry mcnpx radioactive bone cement vertebroplasty evaluacion dosimetrica computacional en modelo vertebral usando un cemento oseo radioactivo con sm-153 ho-166 y-90,1.0.0,11874570453a183c
1909-9762,1370-Texto del artículo-6768-3-10-20200913.pdf,1370-Texto del artículo-6768-3-10-20200913_0,es,ng target volume (PTV) was the implant itself on the vertebrae. The Samarium-153,"─ Antecedentes: El Cáncer de seno es una enfermedad que afecta a gran parte de la población brasileña femenina. Especialmente, aquellas metástasis óseas desarrolladas en la columna vertebral. Esto puede producir potenciales fracturas con compromiso neurológico o reducción de la calidad de vida de la paciente debido al dolor crónico. Objetivo: Estudio de dosimetría computacional en modelos vertebrales simulando metástasis óseas, localizando un cemento óseo radioactivo con Sm-153, Ho-166 e Y-90 en el cuerpo vertebral. Métodos: Imágenes radiológicas de vértebras animales fueron usadas para construir un modelo usando ψ Dirección para correspondencia: carlmont@ucm.es DOI: https://doi.org/10.24050/19099762.n26.2019.1370 28 REVISTA INGENIERÍA BIOMÉDICA el código MCNPx (MonteCarlo N-Particle). Las dosis depositadas fueron evaluadas en el plano axial (XY) respecto al implante del cemento óseo radioactivo dentro de la metástasis. El órgano de riesgo (OAR) más próximo fue la médula espinal y el volumen blanco de planificación (PTV) fue el mismo implante en las vértebras. Los radionuclídeos Samario-153 (Sm-153), Holmio-166 (Ho-166) e Itrio-90 (Y-90) fueron considerados. Resultados: La dosis depositada terapeútica obtenida en el plano del implante por el cemento óseo radioactivo alcanza niveles arriba de 70 Gy para actividades específicas próximas a 3 GBq∙mg-1 con valores aceptables para el Y-90 acoplado al cemento. La exposición a Ho-166 produce una dosis tal que cubre 76,49 % y 62,77 % para dos casos con metástasis respecto al PTV mientras que Y-90 cubre 94,30 % y 80,91 % en el PTV. Conclusiones: The radioactive cement implant may potentially to make an optimal tumor control and lower side effects in organs at risk. El implante de cemento radioactivo puede potencialmente hacer un control óptimo del tumor y disminuir los efectos secundarios en los órganos de riesgo","─ Dosimetría computacional, MCNPx, cemento óseo radioactivo, Vertebroplastia. I",marcadores,ng target volume ptv was the implant itself on the vertebrae the samarium-153,antecedent cancer seno enfermedad afecta gran parte poblacion brasilena femenina especial aquell metastasis oseas desarrollad columna vertebral esto puede producir potencial fractur compromiso neurologico reduccion calidad vida paciente debido dolor cronico objetivo estudio dosimetria computacional model vertebral simul metastasis oseas localiz cemento oseo radioactivo sm-153 ho-166 y-90 cuerpo vertebral metod imagen radiologic vertebr animal fueron usad construir modelo usando ps direccion correspondencia carlmont ucm doi https doi org 10 24050 19099762 n26 2019 1370 28 revista ingenieria biomedica codigo mcnpx montecarlo n-particle dosis depositad fueron evaluad plano axial xy respecto implante cemento oseo radioactivo dentro metastasis organo riesgo oar mas proximo fue medula espinal volumen blanco planificacion ptv fue mismo implante vertebr radionuclide samario-153 sm-153 holmio-166 ho-166 itrio-90 y-90 fueron considerad resultad dosis depositada terapeutica obtenida plano implante cemento oseo radioactivo alcanza nivel arriba 70 gy actividad especific proxim gbqmg-1 valor aceptabl y-90 acoplado cemento exposicion ho-166 produce dosis tal cubre 76 49 62 77 dos casos metastasis respecto ptv mientr y-90 cubre 94 30 80 91 ptv conclusion the radioactive cement implant may potentially to make an optimal tumor control and lower side effects in organs at risk implante cemento radioactivo puede potencial hacer control optimo tumor disminuir efect secundari organ riesgo,dosimetria computacional mcnpx cemento oseo radioactivo vertebroplastia,ng target volume ptv was the implant itself on the vertebrae the samarium-153 antecedent cancer seno enfermedad afecta gran parte poblacion brasilena femenina especial aquell metastasis oseas 