2011-0731,8245_ACAD+19(2)ok.pdf,8245_ACAD+19(2)ok_0,en,julio-diciembre,"The article examines the peculiarities of organizing and delivering education at Ukrainian universities in the context of Russian aggression. The purpose of the study was to analyze the transformations in the educational process of higher education institutions in Ukraine under wartime conditions and to identify the main challenges and prospects for their development. The study is based on a qualitative analytical approach, including the methods of analysis, synthesis, comparison, and generalization of scientific sources and empirical data. It is shown that, during the war, the organization and delivery of education at Ukrainian universities have undergone significant changes due to security risks, destruction of infrastructure, and forced displacement of participants in the educational process. As a result, the vast majority of higher education institutions have switched to distance learning, while some have implemented blended learning formats combining online and * Research article. a Doctor of Philosophical Sciences. Professor. Deсan of the Faculty of Social and Behavioral Sciences of H. S. Skovoroda Kharkiv National Pedagogical University, Kharkiv, Ukraine. E-mail: irdden@gmail.com; orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1956-571X b Graduate student of the Department of Philosophy of the National Technical University “Kharkiv Polytechnic Institute,” Kharkiv, Ukraine. E-mail: vvchalapko@gmail.com; orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-00019833-9851 c Senior Lecturer Ivan Kozhedub National Air Force University, Kharkiv, Ukraine. E-mail: rzorkin76@gmail. com; orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0006-3934-956X d Master in Historical, Social and Cultural Studies. Professor Associated at the Department of Philosophy, History and Tourism, Academic at the University of Playa Ancha, Chile; E-mail: fvergara@upla.cl; orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3400-6123 e Head of the Department of National Security Law and Legal Work of the Military Legal Institute of Yaroslav Mudryi National Law University, Kharkiv, Ukraine. E-mail: fpn1978@ukr.net; orcid: https://orcid. org/0009-0003-6924-0811 DOI: https://doi.org/10.18359/ravi.8245 2 I. Denysenko ■ V. Chalapko ■ R. Zorkin ■ F. R. Vergara Lasnibat ■ P. Fivkin Revista Academia y Virtualidad ■ Vol. 19(2) face-to-face instruction. The findings indicate that the effective organization of education under wartime conditions requires appropriate technical resources, stable internet access, and well-developed digital competencies among both students and teachers. At the same time, a significant number of participants in the educational process still face difficulties in adapting to distance and blended learning formats, with teachers demonstrating a lower level of adaptation compared to students. It is concluded that distance and blended learning will remain relevant in Ukraine in the post-war period due to ongoing digital transformation. These conditions necessitate comprehensive reforms of the higher education system aimed at improving the quality of education, developing digital competencies, and integrating international, particularly European, experience",Russian aggression; organization and delivery of education; Ukrainian universities; digital technologies; distance and blended learning; martial law. La educación universitaria en Ucrania en el contexto de la agresión rusa,marcadores,julio-diciembre,article examin peculiariti organiz deliver education ukrainian universiti context russian aggression purpose study analyze transform educational proces higher education institution ukraine under wartime condition identify main challeng prospect their development study based qualitative analytical approach includ method analysi synthesi comparison general scientific sourc empirical data shown during war organ delivery education ukrainian universiti have undergone significant chang due security risk destruction infrastructure forc displacement p