2011-0731,8344_ACAD+19(2)ok.pdf,8344_ACAD+19(2)ok_0,en,s clave: actitudes del estudiante; educación media superior; estrés tecnológico; tecnologías,"Considering that Information and Communication Technologies (icts) are of great value as support in the learning process, but that their excessive or inadequate use also brings about conditions such as technostress, this article aimed to determine the relationship between the level of technostress and the level of attitudes, knowledge and use of icts in a sample of high school (upper secondary education) students in Mexico. The research was quantitative, non-experimental and correlational, applying the red-tic and acutic questionnaires to a total of 2,345 students. The main result reported a negative relationship between the variables; while specifically, a low level of technostress and a high level of attitudes, knowledge, and use of ict were found. Both findings differ from what has been reported in the analyzed literature, which may suggest that students have transitioned to lower levels of technostress and higher levels of attitudes, use, and knowledge of ict in recent years","student attitudes; upper secondary education; technological stress; information and communication technologies. Tecnoestresse, atitudes, conhecimento e uso das tic em estudantes do ensino médio no México",marcadores,clave actitud del estudiante educacion media superior estr tecnologico tecnologia,consider information communication technologi icts great value support learn proces but their excessive inadequate use also bring about condition such technostres article aimed determine relationship between level technostres level attitud knowledge use icts sample high school upper secondary education student mexico research quantitative non-experimental correlational apply red-tic acutic questionnair total 345 student main result report negative relationship between variabl while specifically low level technostres high level attitud knowledge use ict found both finding differ what has been report analyz literature which may suggest student have transition lower level technostres higher level attitud use knowledge ict recent year,student attitud upper secondary education technological stres information communication technologi tecnoestresse atitud conhecimento uso das tic em estudant do ensino medio no mexico,clave actitud del estudiante educacion media superior estr tecnologico tecnologia consider information communication technologi icts great value support learn proces but their excessive inadequate use also bring about condition such technostres article aimed determine relationship between level technostres level attitud knowledge use icts sample high school upper secondary education student mexico research quantitative non-experimental correlational apply red-tic acutic questionnair total 345 student main result report negative relationship between variabl while specifically low level technostres high level attitud knowledge use ict found both finding differ what has been report analyz literature which may suggest student have transition lower level technostres higher level attitud use knowledge ict recent year student attitud upper secondary education technological stres information communication technologi tecnoestresse atitud conhecimento uso das tic em estudant do ensino medio no mexico,1.0.0,90de1ce06f455c74
2011-0731,8350_ACAD+19(2)ok.pdf,8350_ACAD+19(2)ok_0,es,julio-diciembre,"La Universidad Autónoma del Estado de Morelos diseñó una estrategia curricular multimodal denominada unidad de aprendizaje transversal multimodal de lectura, análisis y síntesis de textos escritos, que se ha incorporado al currículo de diversos programas educativos. La investigación tuvo como objetivo comprender e interpretar los resultados del dispositivo en modalidad virtual en relación con la competencia lectora, a través de la convergencia del perfil del estudiantado y el desempeño de los asesores virtuales. Para ello se desarrolló un estudio de caso no experimental, transversal y explicativo en una carrera de ciencias a través de una triangulación de información de 89 estudiantes encuestados y 10 entrevistados, la e-observación de cinco aulas virtuales y dos entrevistas a asesores virtuales. Los resultados mostraron que, de 105 estudiantes matriculados, 38 culminaron el curso, y la media de calificaciones se situó en el 44,98 %. Los factores de mayor peso en dicho resultado se identificaron en el desempeño de los asesores virtuales, lo que derivó en el bajo rendimiento estudiantil. Se concluye que el dispositivo atiende los requerimientos de diseño curricular e instruccional; sin embargo, factores contextuales que inciden en su implantación derivan en resultados poco satisfactorios para el desarrollo de la competencia lectora","currículo; competencia lectora; unidad de aprendizaje transversal multimodal. * Artículo original resultado de investigación. a Maestra en Investigación Educativa. Correo-e: nylia@uaem.mx; orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-00063440-884X b Doctora en Educación, Universidad de Anglia del Este (Reino Unido). Profesora investigadora del Instituto de Ciencias de la Educación (uaem). Correo-e: maria.zor",marcadores,julio-diciembre,universidad autonoma estado morel diseno estrategia curricular multimodal denominada unidad aprendizaje transversal multimodal lectura analisis sintesis text escrit ha incorporado curriculo divers program educativ investigacion tuvo como objetivo comprender interpretar resultad dispositivo modalidad virtual relacion competencia lectora trav convergencia perfil estudiantado desempeno asesor virtual ello desarrollo estudio caso no experimental transversal explicativo carrera cienci trav triangulacion informacion 89 estudiant encuestad 10 entrevistad e-observacion cinco aulas virtual dos entrevist asesor virtual resultad mostraron 105 estudiant matriculad 38 culminaron curso media calific situo 44 98 factor mayor peso dicho resultado identificaron desempeno asesor virtual derivo bajo rendimiento estudiantil concluye dispositivo atiende requer diseno curricular instruccional sin embargo factor contextual inciden implantacion derivan resultad poco satisfactori desarrollo competencia lectora,curriculo competencia lectora unidad aprendizaje transversal multimodal articulo original resultado investigacion maestra investigacion educativa correo-e nylia uaem mx orcid https orcid org 0009-00063440-884x doctora educacion universidad anglia este reino unido profesora investigadora instituto cienci educacion uaem correo-e maria zor,julio-diciembre universidad autonoma estado morel diseno estrategia curricular multimodal denominada unidad aprendizaje transversal multimodal lectura analisis sintesis text escrit ha incorporado curriculo divers program educativ investigacion tuvo como objetivo comprender interpretar resultad dispositivo modalidad virtual relacion competencia lectora trav convergencia perfil estudiantado desempeno asesor virtual ello desarrollo estudio caso no experimental transversal explicativo carrera cienci trav triangulacion informacion 89 estudiant encuestad 10 entrevistad e-observacion cinco aulas virtual dos entrevist asesor virtual resultad mostraron 105 estudiant matriculad 38 culminaron curso media calific situo 44 98 factor mayor peso dicho resultado identificaron desempeno asesor virtual derivo bajo rendimiento estudiantil concluye dispositivo atiende requer diseno curricular instruccional sin embargo factor contextual inciden implantacion derivan resultad poco satisfactori desarrollo competencia lectora curriculo competencia lectora unidad aprendizaje transversal multimodal articulo original resultado investigacion maestra investigacion educativa correo-e nylia uaem mx orcid https orcid org 0009-00063440-884x doctora educacion universidad anglia este reino unido profesora investigadora instituto cienci educacion uaem correo-e maria zor,1.0.0,c4a7f43c6be865a4
2011-0731,8350_ACAD+19(2)ok.pdf,8350_ACAD+19(2)ok_0,en,entos de diseño,"The Autonomous University of the State of Morelos designed a multimodal curricular strategy known as the multimodal transversal learning unit for the reading, analysis, and synthesis of written texts, which has been incorporated into the curricula of various educational programs. This study aims to understand and interpret the results of the device in its virtual modality in relation to reading competence, through the convergence of the student profile and the performance of virtual advisors. To this end, a non-experimental, cross-sectional, and explanatory case study was conducted in a science degree program using triangulation of information from 89 surveyed students and 10 interviewed students, e-observation of five virtual classrooms, and two interviews with virtual advisors. The results showed that, of 105 enrolled students, 38 completed the course, with an average grade of 44.98%. The factors with the greatest weight in this outcome were identified in the performance of the virtual advisors, which resulted in low student achievement. It is concluded that the device meets the requirements of curricular and instructional design; however, contextual factors affecting its implementation lead to unsatisfactory results for the development of reading competence","curriculum, reading skills; multimodal transversal learning unit. Estratégia curricular multimodal para o desenvolvimento da competência leitora em estudantes de graduação",marcadores,ento de diseno,autonomou university state morelo design multimodal curricular strategy known multimodal transversal learn unit read analysi synthesi written text which has been incorporat into curricula variou educational program study aims understand interpret result device its virtual modality relation read competence through convergence student profile performance virtual advisor end non-experimental cross-sectional explanatory case study conduct science degree program using triangulation information 89 survey student 10 interview student e-observation five virtual classroom two interview virtual advisor result show 105 enroll student 38 complet course average grade 44 98 factor greatest weight outcome identifi performance virtual advisor which result low student achievement conclud device meet requirement curricular instructional design however contextual factor affect its implementation lead unsatisfactory result development read competence,curriculum read skill multimodal transversal learn unit estrategia curricular multimodal para desenvolvimento da competencia leitora em estudant de graduacao,ento de diseno autonomou university state morelo design multimodal curricular strategy known multimodal transversal learn unit read analysi synthesi written text which has been incorporat into curricula variou educational program study aims understand interpret result device its virtual modality relation read competence through convergence student profile performance virtual advisor end non-experimental cross-sectional explanatory case study conduct science degree program using triangulation information 89 survey student 10 interview student e-observation five virtual classroom two interview virtual advisor result show 105 enroll student 38 complet course average grade 44 98 factor greatest weight outcome identifi performance virtual advisor which result low student achievement conclud device meet requirement curricular instructional design however contextual factor affect its implementation lead unsatisfactory result development read competence curriculum read skill multimodal transversal learn unit estrategia curricular multimodal para desenvolvimento da competencia leitora em estudant de graduacao,1.0.0,f04182ea39e9f38a
2011-0731,8381_ACAD+19(2)ok.pdf,8381_ACAD+19(2)ok_0,es,julio-diciembre,"El metaverso integra tecnologías de realidad aumentada y realidad virtual para ofrecer experiencias inmersivas. Este artículo aborda una revisión sobre la implementación del metaverso en la educación, sus metodologías e implicaciones pedagógicas. También se muestran las posturas críticas del metaverso en educación. El artículo tiene un enfoque en las competencias digitales relacionadas con las áreas de ciencia, tecnología, ingeniería y matemáticas (stem). Se desarrolla una revisión sistemática y se presentan aplicaciones prácticas del metaverso en stem por medio de una selección de estudios. Luego del proceso de cribado, el corpus final quedó conformado por 69 artículos seleccionados para el análisis cualitativo y la categorización temática. Al final, se plantean los desafíos técnicos, éticos y sociales subyacentes a esta tecnología inmersiva. Se concluye que la transformación digital y la capacidad de personalización del aprendizaje en el metaverso posibilita una educación adaptada a las necesidades tecnológicas del contexto, lo cual genera oportunidades sensoriales alternas que podrían ser un complemento para las estrategias pedagógicas y didácticas","metaverso; stem; competencias digitales; realidad virtual; realidad aumentada; gamificación; e-learning. * Artículo de revisión producto de la investigación “Metaverso en la educación: una perspectiva centrada en las competencias digitales”. a Magíster en Educación. Correo-e: oscar.bedoya@upb.edu.co; orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0005-40909758 b PhD en Educación. Docente investigador, Univer",marcadores,julio-diciembre,metaverso integra tecnologi realidad aumentada realidad virtual ofrecer experienci inmersiv este articulo aborda revision sobre implementacion metaverso educacion sus metodologi implic pedagogic tambien muestran postur critic metaverso educacion articulo tiene enfoque competenci digital relacionad areas ciencia tecnologia ingenieri