2011-0731,8381_ACAD+19(2)ok.pdf,8381_ACAD+19(2)ok_0,en,"ológicas del contexto, lo cual genera oportunidades","The metaverse integrates Augmented Reality and Virtual Reality technologies to offer immersive experiences. This article provides a review of the implementation of the metaverse in education, its methodologies, and pedagogical implications. Critical perspectives on the metaverse in education are also presented. The article focuses on digital skills related to the fields of science, technology, engineering, and mathematics (stem). A systematic review is developed, and practical applications of the metaverse in stem are presented through a selection of studies. Following the screening process, the final corpus consisted of 69 articles selected for qualitative analysis and thematic categorization. Finally, the technical, ethical, and social challenges underlying this immersive technology are addressed. It is concluded that digital transformation and the capacity for personalized learning in the metaverse enable an education adapted to the technological needs of the context, generating alternative sensory opportunities that could complement pedagogical and didactical strategies","metaverse; stem; digital competences; virtual reality; augmented reality; gamification; e-learning. Metaverso, educação stem e competências digitais: uma revisão sistemática",marcadores,ologica del contexto lo cual genera oportunidad,metaverse integrat augment reality virtual reality technologi offer immersive experienc article provid review implementation metaverse education its methodologi pedagogical implic critical perspectiv metaverse education also present article focus digital skill relat field science technology engineer mathematic stem systematic review develop practical applic metaverse stem present through selection studi follow screen proces final corpu consist 69 articl select qualitative analysi thematic categor finally technical ethical social challeng underly immersive technology address conclud digital transformation capacity personaliz learn metaverse enable education adapt technological need context generat alternative sensory opportuniti could complement pedagogical didactical strategi,metaverse stem digital competenc virtual reality augment reality gamification e-learn metaverso educacao stem competencia digitai uma revisao sistematica,ologica del contexto lo cual genera oportunidad metaverse integrat augment reality virtual reality technologi offer immersive experienc article provid review implementation metaverse education its methodologi pedagogical implic critical perspectiv metaverse education also present article focus digital skill relat field science technology engineer mathematic stem systematic review develop practical applic metaverse stem present through selection studi follow screen proces final corpu consist 69 articl select qualitative analysi thematic categor finally technical ethical social challeng underly immersive technology address conclud digital transformation capacity personaliz learn metaverse enable education adapt technological need context generat alternative sensory opportuniti could complement pedagogical didactical strategi metaverse stem digital competenc virtual reality augment reality gamification e-learn metaverso educacao stem competencia digitai uma revisao sistematica,1.0.0,e2cb0ffd04f9c646
2011-2106,Art1-Percepção+de+Corrupçã.pdf,Art1-Percepção+de+Corrupçã_0,es,Percepção de corrupção e aprovação dos governos latinoamericanos,"Este estudo analisa a relação entre a percepção de corrupção do poder executivo e a aprovação governamental em 18 países latino-americanos. São utilizadas 11.582 observações do Latinobarómetro de 2018 e estima-se um modelo Logit Multinível. Os resultados indicam que maior percepção de corrupção no executivo reduz em 19,1 pontos percentuais a probabilidade de aprovação dos governos. Isso evidencia que a corrupção percebida compromete a credibilidade governamental, expõe fragilidades institucionais da região e limita a efetividade das políticas públicas. Palavras-chave: percepção de corrupção, poder executivo, aprovação governamental, logit multinível, América Latina. Abstract This study analyzes the relationship between perceptions of executive branch corruption and government approval in 18 Latin American countries. A total of 11,582 observations from the 2018 Latinobarómetro are used, and a Multilevel Logit model is estimated. Results show that higher perceptions of executive corruption reduce the probability of government approval by 19.1 percentage points. These findings indicate that perceived corruption undermines governmental credibility, reveals institutional fragilities in the region, and limits the effectiveness of public policies","perception of corruption; executive branch; government approval; multilevel logit; Latin America. 1. Introdução A corrupção pode ser entendida como a prática de atividades ilegais ou antiéticas voltadas à obtenção de vantagens indevidas. Esse fenômeno manifesta-se tanto no setor público quanto no privado, em formas como suborno, desvios de fundos, nepotismo e tráfico de influência (Koeswa",marcadores,percepcao corrupcao aprovacao dos govern latinoamerican,este estudo analisa relacao entre percepcao corrupcao do poder executivo aprovacao governamental em 18 pais latino-american sao utilizad 11