2011-2106,"fredysa,+Art2-Factores+climáticos+y.pdf","fredysa,+Art2-Factores+climáticos+y_0",en,Este estudio analiza la relación entre variables climáticas y macroeconómicas con el precio,"This study analyzes the relationship between climatic and macroeconomic variables and the price of Solanum phureja (criolla potato) in Bogotá, Colombia, during the 2014–2023 period. Time-lagged econometric models of up to six months, Pearson correlation coefficients, and multiple regression analyses were applied. Results show that the Representative Market Rate (TRM) and extreme climatic phenomena (El Niño/La Niña) are the main determinants of price dynamics, while rainfall and fertilizer prices exhibited no statistical significance. The findings provide empirical evidence on the drivers of price volatility in the criolla potato market and offer practical insights for risk management and policy design in the agricultural sector, particularly under the increasing influence of climatic and economic uncertainty","TRM, Solanum phureja, econometric models, climate, agricultural prices",marcadores,este estudio analiza la relacion entre variabl climatica macroeconomica con el precio,study analyz relationship between climatic macroeconomic variabl price solanum phureja criolla potato bogota colombia during 2014-2023 period time-lagg econometric model up six month pearson correlation coefficient multiple regression analys appli result show representative market rate trm extreme climatic phenomena el nino la nina main determinant price dynamic while rainfall fertilizer pric exhibit no statistical significance finding provide empirical evidence driver price volatility criolla potato market offer practical insight risk management policy design agricultural sector particularly under increas influence climatic economic uncertainty,trm solanum phureja econometric model climate agricultural pric,este estudio analiza la relacion entre variabl climatica macroeconomica con el precio study analyz relationship between climatic macroeconomic variabl price solanum phureja criolla potato bogota colombia during 2014-2023 period time-lagg econometric model up six month pearson correlation coefficient multiple regression analys appli result show representative market rate trm extreme climatic phenomena el nino la nina main determinant price dynamic while rainfall fertilizer pric exhibit no statistical significance finding provide empirical evidence driver price volatility criolla potato market offer practical insight risk management policy design agricultural sector particularly under increas influence climatic economic uncertainty trm solanum phureja econometric model climate agricultural pric,1.0.0,3e9372d0aee35926
2011-2106,"fredysa,+Art6-Digital+disruption+an.pdf","fredysa,+Art6-Digital+disruption+an_0",en,"1 Master in Business Administration por la Universidad Politécnica Salesiana, Ecuador. ORCID:","The impact that the digital era has had in recent years has driven significant progress in organizations, enabling them to overcome obstacles and achieve success. The purpose of this study was to analyze how digital disruption impacts the generation of value in virtual stores in the city of Guayaquil- Ecuador. This research adopts a correlational approach and uses quantitative methods. The results reveal a Pearson correlation coefficient of 0.979, with a p-value of 0.001, which is less than the significance level of 0.05. This indicates that digital disruption impacts the creation of value in virtual stores. In this sense, addressing the challenges associated with digital disruption, even those that already exist, will deliver superior performance that takes full advantage of new technologies","Value creation, digital culture, digital disruption, digital revolution, online stores",marcadores,master busines administration por la universidad politecnica salesiana ecuador orcid,impact digital era has had recent year has driven significant progres organiz enabl them overcome obstacl achieve succes purpose study analyze how digital disruption impact generation value virtual stor city guayaquil- ecuador research adopt correlational approach uses quantitative method result reveal pearson correlation coefficient 979 p-value 001 which less than significance level 05 indicat digital disruption impact creation value virtual stor sense address challeng associat digital disruption even those already exist will deliver superior performance take full advantage new technologi,value creation digital culture digital disruption digital revolution online stor,master busines administration por la universidad politecnica salesiana ecuador orcid impact digital era has had recent year has driven significant progres organiz enabl them overcome obstacl achieve succes purpose study analyze how digital disruption impact generation value virtual stor city guayaquil- ecuador research adopt correlational approach uses quantitative method result reveal pearson correlation coefficient 979 p-value 001 which less than significance level 05 indicat digital disruption impact creation value virtual stor sense address challeng associat digital disruption even those already exist will deliver superior performance take full advantage new technologi value creation digital culture digital disruption digital revolution online stor,1.0.0,07ea0101871f22f4
2011-2106,"fredysa,+Art6-Digital+disruption+an.pdf","fredysa,+Art6-Digital+disruption+an_0",es,e digital era has had in recent years has driven significant progress in,"El impacto que la era digital ha tenido en los últimos años ha impulsado un progreso significativo en las organizaciones, permitiéndoles superar obstáculos y alcanzar el éxito. El propósito de este estudio fue analizar cómo la disrupción digital impacta la generación de valor en las tiendas virtuales de la ciudad de Guayaquil-Ecuador. Esta investigación adopta un enfoque correlacional y utiliza métodos cuantitativos. Los resultados revelan un coeficiente de correlación de Pearson de 0.979, con un valor p de 0.001, que es menor que el nivel de significancia de 0.05. Esto indica que la disrupción digital impacta la creación de valor en las tiendas virtuales. En este sentido, abordar los desafíos asociados con la disrupción digital, incluso aquellos que ya existen, brindará un rendimiento superior que aproveche al máximo las nuevas tecnologías","Creación de valor, cultura digital, disrupción digital, revolución digital, tiendas en línea. 1",marcadores,digital era has had in recent years has driven significant progress in,impacto era digital ha tenido ultim anos ha impulsado progreso significativo organiz permitiendol superar obstacul alcanzar exito proposito este estudio fue analizar como disrupcion digital impacta generacion valor tiend virtual ciudad guayaquil-ecuador esta investigacion adopta enfoque correlacional utiliza metod cuantitativ resultad revelan coeficiente correlacion pearson 979 valor 001 menor nivel significancia 05 esto indica disrupcion digital impacta creacion valor tiend virtual este sentido abordar desafi asociad disrupcion digital incluso aquell ya existen brindara rendimiento superior aproveche maximo nuev tecnologi,creacion valor cultura digital disrupcion digital revolucion digital tiend linea,digital era has had in recent years has driven significant progress in impacto era digital ha tenido ultim anos ha impulsado progreso significativo organiz permitiendol superar obstacul alcanzar exito proposito este estudio fue analizar como disrupcion digital impacta generacion valor tiend virtual ciudad guayaquil-ecuador esta investigacion adopta enfoque correlacional utiliza metod cuantitativ resultad revelan coeficiente correlacion pearson 979 valor 001 menor nivel significancia 05 esto indica disrupcion digital impacta creacion valor tiend virtual este sentido abordar desafi asociad disrupcion digital incluso aquell ya existen brindara rendimiento superior aproveche maximo nuev tecnologi creacion valor cultura digital disrupcion digital revolucion digital tiend linea,1.0.0,eeb55f72623783ed
2011-2106,"fredysa,+Art7-Does+population+aging.pdf","fredysa,+Art7-Does+population+aging_0",en,"he University of Brasilia (UnB), postgraduate degree in BI, Big Data, Analytics (Data Science) by the","This paper empirically tests the relationship between productivity and the aging of the Brazilian population from 2012 to 2022, using quarterly data from IBGE and PNAD Contínua. The study follows a Solow-augmented model with the dependency ratio incorporated and employs Johansen cointegration and VECM methods. Results show that population aging exerts a positive and statistically significant effect on economic growth, while the savings rate has a negative long-term effect on per capita income. These findings contrast with much of the international literature, highlighting specific demographic and institutional features of Brazil. The results have policy implications for pension reform, labor participation of older adults, and active aging strategies","Population Aging, Economic Growth, Solow Model, VECM. JEL classification: C14, C67, E42, E58",marcadores,he university brasilia unb postgraduate degree bi big data analytic data science,paper empirically test relationship between productivity aging brazilian population 2012 2022 using quarterly data ibge pnad continua study follow solow-augment model dependency ratio incorporat employ johansen cointegration vecm method result show population aging exert positive statistically significant effect economic growth while saving rate has negative long-term effect per capita income these finding contrast much international literature highlight specific demographic institutional featur brazil result have policy implic pension reform labor participation older adult active aging strategi,population aging economic growth solow model vecm jel classification c14 c67 e42 e58,he university brasilia unb postgraduate degree bi big data analytic data science paper empirically test relationship between productivity aging brazilian population 2012 2022 using quarterly data ibge pnad continua study follow solow-augment model dependency ratio incorporat employ johansen cointegration vecm method result show population aging exert positive statistically significant effect economic growth while saving rate has negative long-term effect per capita income these finding contrast much international literature highlight specific demographic institutional featur brazil result have policy implic pension reform labor participation older adult active aging strategi population aging economic growth solow model vecm jel classification c14 c67 e42 e58,1.0.0,9debfdb18cfff19e
2011-2106,"fredysa,+Art8-Fiscal+communication.pdf","fredysa,+Art8-Fiscal+communication_0",en,azil: an analysis based on natural language processing,"The purpose of this article is to investigate how the tone of the fiscal authority's communications can influence monetary policy decisions. To this end, a fiscal policy sentiment index was developed using machine learning techniques, using the monthly public debt reports issued by the National Treasury as a source of information. The sentiment index was used as an explanatory variable in two approaches to achieve the central objective of the article. In the first, a traditional version of the central bank's reaction function was estimated using classic econometric techniques. In the second, the analysis was expanded towards a Dynamic Stochastic General Equilibrium model (DSGE), in order to estimate central bank reaction functions and, with this, produce inferences about the effect of fiscal policy sentiment in the behavior of monetary policy. The main results suggest that fiscal policy sentiment has influenced the monetary policy decision-making process in Brazil, indicating a possible scenario of fiscal dominance. In this sense, this article contributes an unprecedented approach to an important topic in public finance by reinforcing the fundamental role of communication and coordination between monetary and fiscal authorities","Machine Learning. Textual analysis. Natural Language Processing. Fiscal Dominance. JEL Code: C02, C63, E62",marcadores,azil analysi based natural language process,purpose article investigate how tone fiscal authority communic can influence monetary policy decision end fiscal policy sentiment index develop using machine learn techniqu using monthly public debt report issu national treasury source information sentiment index used explanatory variable two approach achieve central objective article first traditional version central bank reaction function estimat using classic econometric techniqu second analysi expand toward dynamic stochastic general equilibrium model dsge order estimate central bank reaction function produce inferenc about effect fiscal policy sentiment behavior monetary policy main result suggest fiscal policy sentiment has influenc monetary policy decision-mak proces brazil indicat possible scenario fiscal dominance sense article contribut unprecedent approach important topic public finance reinforc fundamental role communication coordination between monetary fiscal authoriti,machine learn textual analysi natural language process fiscal dominance jel code c02 c63 e62,azil analysi based natural language process purpose article investigate how tone fiscal authority communic can influence monetary policy decision end fiscal policy sentiment index develop using machine learn techniqu using monthly public debt report issu national treasury source information sentiment index used explanatory variable two approach achieve central objective article first traditional version central bank reaction function estimat using classic econometric techniqu second analysi expand toward dynamic stochastic general equilibrium model dsge order estimate central bank reaction function produce inferenc about effect fiscal policy sentiment behavior monetary policy main result suggest fiscal policy sentiment has influenc monetary policy decision-mak proces brazil indicat possible scenario fiscal dominance sense article contribut unprecedent approach important topic public finance reinforc fundamental role communication coordination between monetary fiscal authoriti machine learn textual analysi natural language process fiscal dominance jel code c02 c63 e62,1.0.0,0aea2e16d86f2410
2011-2106,"fredysa,+Art9+-+Gestión+relacional.pdf","fredysa,+Art9+-+Gestión+relacional_0",es,CRM relationship management and customer loyalty in Ecuadorian public,"El problema identificado en las instituciones públicas está relacionado a la escasa capacitación del personal, la resistencia al cambio e inadecuada planificación de estrategias que han provocado limitaciones en la efectividad del servicio público, a pesar de que en algunas de ellas exista un software de gestión relacional con el cliente (CRM). El objetivo del estudio se centró en examinar la gestión relacional del CRM (variable independiente) y su incidencia en la fidelización del usuario (variable dependiente) en instituciones públicas del Ecuador. En el estudio participaron 200 usuarios que hicieron uso de los servicios públicos, los cuales fueron seleccionados durante la realización del muestreo probabilístico sistemático. Se aplicó un enfoque cuantitativo, correlacional, descriptivo por medio de una encuesta estructurada. Los resultados encontrados indicaron que la fidelización del usuario mantenía una correlación significativa (Rho=0.873; p= 0.000) con la gestión del CRM, lo cual confirmó que la confianza del usuario se ve mejorada a medida que los servidores públicos corregían su capacidad de respuesta en los procesos burocráticos","Gestión relacional con el cliente CRM, fidelización del cliente, instituciones públicas, satisfacción del usuario",marcadores,crm relationship management and customer loyalty in ecuadorian public,problema identificado institucion public esta relacionado escasa capacitacion personal resistencia cambio inadecuada planificacion estrategi han provocado limit efectividad servicio publico pesar algun ellas exista software gestion relacional cliente crm objetivo estudio centro examinar gestion relacional crm variable independiente incidencia fidelizacion usuario variable dependiente institucion public ecuador estudio participaron 200 usuari hicieron uso servici public cual fueron seleccionad durante realizacion muestreo probabilistico sistematico aplico enfoque cuantitativo correlacional descriptivo medio encuesta estructurada resultad encontrad indicaron fidelizacion usuario mantenia correlacion significativa rho 873 000 gestion crm cual confirmo confianza usuario ve mejorada medida servidor public corregian capacidad respuesta proces burocratic,gestion relacional cliente crm fidelizacion cliente institucion public satisfaccion usuario,crm relationship management and customer loyalty in ecuadorian public problema identificado institucion public esta relacionado escasa capacitacion personal resistencia cambio inadecuada planificacion estrategi han provocado limit efectividad servicio publico pesar algun ellas exista software gestion relacional cliente crm objetivo estudio centro examinar gestion relacional crm variable independiente incidencia fidelizacion usuario variable dependiente institucion public ecuador estudio participaron 200 usuari hicieron uso servici public cual fueron seleccionad durante realizacion muestreo probabilistico sistematico aplico enfoque cuantitativo correlacional descriptivo medio encuesta estructurada resultad encontrad indicaron fidelizacion usuario mantenia correlacion significativa rho 873 000 gestion crm cual confirmo confianza usuario ve mejorada medida servidor public corregian capacidad respuesta proces burocratic gestion relacional cliente crm fidelizacion cliente institucion public satisfaccion usuario,1.0.0,2d193fe91213b69f
2011-2106,"fredysa,+Art9+-+Gestión+relacional.pdf","fredysa,+Art9+-+Gestión+relacional_0",en,tión relacional del CRM (variable independiente) y,"The problem identified in public institutions is related to insufficient staff training, resistance to change, and inadequate strategic planning, which have led to limitations in the effectiveness of public services, even though some institutions have customer relationship management (CRM) software. The objective of this study was to examine the relational management of CRM (independent variable) and its impact on user loyalty (dependent variable) in public institutions in Ecuador. Two hundred users of public services participated in the study, selected through systematic probabilistic sampling. A quantitative, correlational, and descriptive approach was applied using a structured survey. The results indicated a significant correlation (Rho = 0.873; p = 0.000) between user loyalty and CRM management, confirming that user trust improves as public servants enhance their responsiveness in bureaucratic processes","Customer relationship management (CRM), customer loyalty, public institutions, user satisfaction",marcadores,tion relacional del crm variable independiente,problem identifi public institution relat insufficient staff train resistance change inadequate strategic plann which have led limit effectivenes public servic even though some institution have customer relationship management crm software objective study examine relational management crm independent variable its impact user loyalty dependent variable public institution ecuador two hundr user public servic participat study select through systematic probabilistic sampl quantitative correlational descriptive approach appli using structur survey result indicat significant correlation rho 873 000 between user loyalty crm management confirm user trust improv public servant enhance their responsivenes bureaucratic process,customer relationship management crm customer loyalty public institution user satisfaction,tion relacional del crm variable independiente problem identifi public institution relat insufficient staff train resistance change inadequate strategic plann which have led limit effectivenes public servic even though some institution have customer relationship management crm software objective study examine relational management crm independent variable its impact user loyalty dependent variable public institution ecuador two hundr user public servic participat study select through systematic probabilistic sampl quantitative correlational descriptive approach appli using structur survey result indicat significant correlation rho 873 000 between user loyalty crm management confirm user trust improv public servant enhance their responsivenes bureaucratic process customer relationship management crm customer loyalty public institution user satisfaction,1.0.0,597ceb7ba634e608
2011-2106,ilovepdf_merged.pdf,ilovepdf_merged_0,es,man capital on the economic growth of municipalities in Paraná: a,"O artigo investiga o impacto do capital humano no crescimento econômico dos municípios do Paraná, Brasil, no período de 2002 a 2021, utilizando modelos econométricos espaciais. O estudo foca em variáveis-chave como matrículas no ensino superior, consumo de energia e crescimento populacional, analisando seus efeitos diretos e indiretos sobre o Produto Interno Bruto (PIB) desses municípios. Como principal resultado, verificou-se que investimentos estratégicos em educação superior devem ser acompanhados por melhorias na infraestrutura energética e políticas que incentivem o crescimento populacional de forma equilibrada, de tal forma que ocorra um ciclo um ciclo virtuoso de crescimento econômico que ultrapasse as fronteiras municipais, promovendo um desenvolvimento mais equilibrado e sustentável em todo o Estado. Palavras-chave: Capital humano, crescimento econômico, econometria espacial, desenvolvimento regional. Abstract This article investigates the impact of human capital on the economic growth of municipalities in Paraná, Brazil, from 2002 to 2021, using spatial econometric models. The study focuses on key variables such as higher education enrollment, energy consumption, and population growth, analyzing their direct and indirect effects on the Gross Domestic Product (GDP) of these municipalities. The main finding is that strategic investments in higher education must be accompanied by improvements in energy infrastructure and policies that encourage balanced population growth, creating a virtuous cycle of economic growth that transcends municipal boundaries, promoting more balanced and sustainable development throughout the state","Human capital, economic growth, spatial econometrics, regional development. 1. INTRODUÇÃO O crescimento econômico regional resulta de uma combinação complexa de fatores que interagem de forma simultânea e interdependente. Entre esses elementos, destacam-se o capital humano, a infraestrutura e as características demográficas, que influenciam diretamente a produtividade, a capacidade de inovaç",marcadores,man capital on the economic growth of municipaliti in parana,artigo investiga impacto do capital humano no crescimento economico dos municipi do parana brasil no periodo 2002 2021 utiliz model econometric espaciais estudo foca em variaveis-chave como matricul no ensino superior consumo energia crescimento populacional analis seus efeit diret indiret sobre produto interno bruto pib dess municipi como principal resultado verificou-se investiment estrategic em educacao superior devem ser acompanhad melhori na infraestrutura energetica politic incentivem crescimento populacional forma equilibrada tal forma ocorra um ciclo um ciclo virtuoso crescimento economico ultrapasse as fronteir municipais promovendo um desenvolvimento mais equilibrado sustentavel em todo estado palavras-chave capital humano crescimento economico econometria espacial desenvolvimento regional abstract this article investigat the impact of human capital on the economic growth of municipaliti in parana brazil from 2002 to 2021 using spatial econometric models the study focus on key variabl such as higher education enrollment energy consumption and population growth analyzing their direct and indirect effects on the gross domestic product gdp of these municipaliti the main finding is that strategic investments in higher education must be accompanied by improvements in energy infrastructure and polici that encourage balanced population growth creating virtuous cycle of economic growth that transcends municipal boundari promoting more balanced and sustainable development throughout the state,human capital economic growth spatial econometrics regional development introducao crescimento economico regional resulta uma combinacao complexa fator interagem forma simultanea interdependente entre esses element destacam-se capita