2011-2106,ilovepdf_merged.pdf,ilovepdf_merged_0,en,humano no crescimento econômico dos municípios,"This article investigates the impact of human capital on the economic growth of municipalities in Paraná, Brazil, from 2002 to 2021, using spatial econometric models. The study focuses on key variables such as higher education enrollment, energy consumption, and population growth, analyzing their direct and indirect effects on the Gross Domestic Product (GDP) of these municipalities. The main finding is that strategic investments in higher education must be accompanied by improvements in energy infrastructure and policies that encourage balanced population growth, creating a virtuous cycle of economic growth that transcends municipal boundaries, promoting more balanced and sustainable development throughout the state","Human capital, economic growth, spatial econometrics, regional development. 1. INTRODUÇÃO O crescimento econômico regional resulta de uma combinação complexa de fatores que interagem de forma simultânea e interdependente. Entre esses elementos, destacam-se o capital humano, a infraestrutura e as características demográficas, que influenciam diretamente a produtividade, a capacidade de inovaç",marcadores,humano no crescimento economico dos municipio,article investigat impact human capital economic growth municipaliti parana brazil 2002 2021 using spatial econometric model study focus key variabl such higher education enrollment energy consumption population growth analyz their direct indirect effect gros domestic product gdp these municipaliti main find strategic investment higher education must accompani improvement energy infrastructure polici encourage balanc population growth creat virtuou cycle economic growth transcend municipal boundari promot more balanc sustainable development throughout state,human capital economic growth spatial econometric regional development introducao crescimento economico regional resulta de uma combinacao complexa de fator que interagem de forma simultanea interdependente entre esse elemento destacam-se capital humano infraestrutura caracteristica demografica que influenciam diretamente produtividade capacidade de inovac,humano no crescimento economico dos municipio article investigat impact human capital economic growth municipaliti parana brazil 2002 2021 using spatial econometric model study focus key variabl such higher education enrollment energy consumption population growth analyz their direct indirect effect gros domestic product gdp these municipaliti main find strategic investment higher education must accompani improvement energy infrastructure polici encourage balanc population growth creat virtuou cycle economic growth transcend municipal boundari promot more balanc sustainable development throughout state human capital economic growth spatial econometric regional development introducao crescimento economico regional resulta de uma combinacao complexa de fator que interagem de forma simultanea interdependente entre esse elemento destacam-se capital humano infraestrutura caracteristica demografica que influenciam diretamente produtividade capacidade de inovac,1.0.0,99af1c64a04ce299
2011-2173,10_Xylella+fastidiosa+management+2019+2025+A+review.pdf,10_Xylella+fastidiosa+management+2019+2025+A+review_0,en,Current strategies for managing Xylella fastidiosa,"Xylella fastidiosa (Wells et al.) represents a major global phytosanitary threat due to its broad host range, rapid dispersal, and frequent asymptomatic infections, which complicate early detection and facilitate pathogen spread. Early and accurate diagnosis is therefore critical as a foundational component of effective management, enabling timely intervention, resource prioritization, and minimization of unnoticed disease dissemination. This review systematically analyzed literature published between 2019 and 2025 in Scopus, Web of Science, and Google Scholar, selecting 50 studies addressing integrated management strategies classified into: (i) diagnostic tools and early detection, (ii) vector control, particularly of Philaenus spumarius, (iii) chemical and nanotechnological strategies, (iv) natural compounds and plant-based approaches, and (v) genetic resistance and varietal improvement, with special emphasis on the Colombian context. Results indicate that while chemical and nanotechnological optimizing strategies have received the greatest research attention, the integration of early diagnostic tools is essential for all other control measures. Vector management and genetic resistance complement these actions, and natural compounds emerge as promising sustainable alternatives. Overall, no single strategy is sufficient to eradicate X. fastidiosa. The most effective approach relies on combining early and accurate diagnosis with complementary control tools that balance scientific efficacy, environmental sustainability, and economic feasibility. This structured framework supports evidence-based decision-making and guides the implementation of integrated management strategies in regions under phytosanitary risk, including Colombia. Additional","integrate pest management; insect vector control; di