53 uptc 24223719 20284 revista colombiana de ciencia horticola vol 19 no 1-16 september-december 2025 e-issn 2422-3719 issn-l 2011-2173 instituto colombiano agropecuario ica division tecnica de sanidad vege,current strategi manag xylella fastidiosa xylella fastidiosa well et al represent major global phytosanitary threat due its broad host range rapid dispersal frequent asymptomatic infection which complicate early detection facilitate pathogen spread early accurate diagnosi therefore critical foundational component effective management enabl timely intervention resource priorit minim unnotic disease dissemination review systematically analyz literature publish between 2019 2025 scopu web science google scholar select 50 studi address integrat management strategi classifi into diagnostic tool early detection ii vector control particularly philaenu spumariu iii chemical nanotechnological strategi iv natural compound plant-bas approach genetic resistance varietal improvement special emphasi colombian context result indicate while chemical nanotechnological optimiz strategi have receiv greatest research attention integration early diagnostic tool essential all other control measur vector management genetic resistance complement these action natural compound emerge promis sustainable alternativ overall no single strategy sufficient eradicate fastidiosa most effective approach reli combin early accurate diagnosi complementary control tool balance scientific efficacy environmental sustainability economic feasibility structur framework support evidence-bas decision-mak guid implementation integrat management strategi region under phytosanitary risk includ colombia additional integrate pest management insect vector control disease resistance pierce disease olive quick decline syndrome coffee leaf scorch doi http doi org 10 19053 uptc 24223719 20284 revista colombiana de ciencia horticola vol 19 no 1-16 september-december 2025 e-issn 2422-3719 issn-l 2011-2173 instituto colo