2011-2173,19(3)_19666+Detection+and+molecular+RCCH19(3).pdf,19(3)_19666+Detection+and+molecular+RCCH19(3)_0,en,Detection and molecular characterization of potato yellow vein,"The potato yellow vein virus (PYVV) is a Crinivirus transmitted by the whitefly Trialeurodes vaporariorum and is associated with significant economic losses in potato (Solanum spp.) cultivation in the Andean region. Until now, the presence of PYVV had not been reported in the department of Norte de Santander, Colombia. In this study, we report for the first time the detection of PYVV in Solanum phureja plants exhibiting typical vein yellowing symptoms in the locality of Chitaga. Leaf samples were collected and subjected to molecular analysis by RT-PCR, confirming the presence of the virus. The obtained amplicon was sequenced and deposited in GenBank under accession number PV593540. Phylogenetic analysis revealed that the sequence shares 98.8% nucleotide identity with other Colombian isolates of PYVV and clusters closely with sequences from the department of Nariño. This finding suggests a possible introduction of the virus into Norte de Santander through infected seed tubers. These results underscore the importance of implementing robust epidemiological surveillance systems and promoting the use of virus-free certified seed to prevent the dissemination of PYVV and other pathogens across potato-growing regions. Additional","Crinivirus; geographic spread; phylogenetic analysis; vegetative propagation; whitefly transmission. Doi: https://doi.org/10.19053/uptc.24223719.19666 REVISTA COLOMBIANA DE CIENCIAS HORTÍCOLAS - Vol. 19 - No. 3, 1-9, September-December, 2025 e-ISSN: 2422-3719 · ISSN-L: 2011-2173 1 Universidad Francisco de Paula Santander– , Facultad de Ciencias Básicas, Grupo de investigación Fitobiomol, San",marcadores,detection molecular character potato yellow vein,potato yellow vein viru pyvv criniviru transmitt whitefly trialeurod vaporariorum associat significant economic loss potato solanum spp cultivation andean region until now presence pyvv had not been report department norte de santander colombia study we report first time detection pyvv solanum phureja plant exhibit typical vein yellow symptom locality chitaga leaf sampl collect subject molecular analysi rt-pcr confirm presence viru obtain amplicon sequenc deposit genbank under accession number pv593540 phylogenetic analysi reveal sequence shar 98 nucleotide identity other colombian isolat pyvv cluster closely sequenc department narino find suggest possible introduction viru into norte de santander through infect seed tuber these result underscore importance implement robust epidemiological surveillance system promot use virus-free certifi seed prevent dissemination pyvv other pathogen acros potato-grow region additional,criniviru geographic spread phylogenetic analysi vegetative propagation whitefly transmission doi http doi org 10 19053 uptc 24223719 19666 revista colombiana de ciencia horticola vol 19 no 1-9 september-december 2025 e-issn 2422-3719 issn-l 2011-2173 universidad francisco de paula santander- facultad de ciencia basica grupo de investigacion fitobiomol san,detection molecular character potato yellow vein potato yellow vein viru pyvv criniviru transmitt whitefly trialeurod vaporariorum associat significant economic loss potato solanum spp cultivation andean region until now presence pyvv had not been report department norte de santander colombia study we report first time detection pyvv solanum phureja plant exhibit typical vein yellow symptom locality chitaga leaf sampl collect subject molecular analysi rt-pcr confirm presence viru obtain amplicon sequenc deposit genbank under accession number pv593540 phylogenetic analysi reveal sequence shar 98 nucleotide identity other colombian isolat pyvv cluster closely sequenc department narino find suggest possible introduction viru into norte de santander through infect seed tuber these result underscore importance implement robust epidemiological surveillance system promot use virus-free certifi seed prevent dissemination pyvv other pathogen acros potato-grow region additional criniviru geographic spread phylogenetic analysi vegetative propagation whitefly transmission doi http doi org 10 19053 uptc 24223719 19666 revista colombiana de ciencia horticola vol 19 no 1-9 september-december 2025 e-issn 2422-3719 issn-l 2011-2173 universidad francisco de paula santander- facultad de ciencia basica grupo de investigacion fitobiomol san,1.0.0,80f2b3f65e81c25f
2011-2173,19(3)_19666+Detection+and+molecular+RCCH19(3).pdf,19(3)_19666+Detection+and+molecular+RCCH19(3)_0,es,"lly, the virus can","El virus del amarillamiento de las venas de la papa (PYVV) es un Crinivirus transmitido por la mosca blanca Trialeurodes vaporariorum y está asociado con importantes pérdidas económicas en el cultivo de papa (Solanum spp.) en la región andina. Hasta ahora, no se había reportado la presencia del PYVV en el departamento de Norte de Santander, Colombia. En este estudio, se reporta por primera vez la detección de PYVV en plantas de Solanum phureja que presentaban síntomas típicos de amarillamiento de las nervaduras en la localidad de Chitagá. Las muestras foliares de Solanum phureja se procesaron para su análisis molecular mediante RT-PCR, lo que confirmó la presencia del virus. El amplicón obtenido fue secuenciado y depositado en GenBank bajo el número de acceso PV593540. El análisis filogenético reveló que la secuencia comparte un 98,8% de identidad nucleotídica con otros aislamientos colombianos de PYVV y se agrupa estrechamente con secuencias del departamento de Nariño. Este resultado sugiere una posible introducción del virus a Norte de Santander a través de tubérculos-semilla infectados. Estos resultados destacan la importancia de implementar sistemas robustos de vigilancia epidemiológica y de promover el uso de semilla certificada libre de virus para prevenir la diseminación del PYVV y otros patógenos en las regiones productoras de papa",adicionales: Crinivirus; dispersión geográfica; análisis filogenético; propagación vegetativa; transmisión por mosca blanca. Received: 19-06-2025 Accepted: 10-11-2025 Published: 27-12-2025,marcadores,lly the virus can,virus amarillamiento venas papa pyvv crinivirus transmitido mosca blanca trialeurod vaporariorum esta asociado important perdid economic cultivo papa solanum spp region andina hasta ahora no habia reportado presencia pyvv departamento norte santander colombia este estudio reporta prime