2011-3080,7918-+Actitud+negativa+hacia+las+matemáticas+y+la+escuela.pdf,7918-+Actitud+negativa+hacia+las+matemáticas+y+la+escuela_0,en,s. Los resultados indicaron que la actitud negativa,"This quantitative study, employing a non-experimental design, analyzed the relationship and predictive value of negative attitudes toward mathematics and school on problem-solving performance in sixth-grade primary education students. Additionally, the attitudinal profile of students was examined according to their performance level (high, medium, and low). Participants (n = 91) completed questionnaires assessing negative attitudes toward mathematics and attitudes toward school, as well as a standardized problem-solving test. The results indicated that negative attitudes toward mathematics significantly predict success across different types of problems, with differences observed between groups in this variable in favor of the high-performing group. Negative attitudes toward school showed a weaker association, specifically related to fraction problems. It is concluded that attitudes specifically toward mathematics have greater predictive value and discriminative power than general attitudes toward school. These findings suggest that psychoeducational interventions should focus on promoting positive attitudes toward mathematics, complemented by fostering a positive perception of the school environment","Mathematics Attitudes; School Attitudes; Elementary Education; Mathematics Achievement; Problem Solving (mathematics). Mercader-Ruiz, J., Nácher-Ortiz, J., Abellán-Roselló, L., & Siegenthaler-Hierro, R. Vol. 19 No. 2 / Mayo – Agosto 2026 2",marcadores,los resultado indicaron que la actitud negativa,quantitative study employ non-experimental design analyz relationship predictive value negative attitud toward mathematic school problem-solv performance sixth-grade primary education student additionally attitudinal profile student examin accord their performance level high medium low par