2011-3080,7964-+Trayectorias+de+Recuperación+del+Desarrollo+Temprano+en+Acogimiento+Familiar.pdf,7964-+Trayectorias+de+Recuperación+del+Desarrollo+Temprano+en+Acogimiento+Familiar_0,es,"María Paula Moretti1,2* ","Introducción: en situaciones de maltrato, niñas y niños pueden ser derivados a cuidados alternativos. Si bien el impacto del maltrato temprano en el desarrollo ha sido estudiado, es necesario profundizar en los procesos de recuperación durante la primera infancia. Objetivos: (1) Analizar las trayectorias del desarrollo en la primera infancia con historial de maltrato durante los primeros cuatro meses de acogimiento familiar, en comparación con un grupo de referencia, y (2) explorar las diferencias en dichas trayectorias según la cohesión, flexibilidad y funcionamiento de las familias de acogida. Método: diseño longitudinal de panel con 60 participantes de hasta 36 meses: 30 en acogimiento familiar con antecedentes de maltrato (Grupo 1) y 30 en familias de origen sin historial de maltrato (Grupo 2 —de referencia). El desarrollo se evaluó en tres momentos —inicio del acogimiento, a los dos y a los cuatro meses— mediante las escalas argentinas: PRUNAPE e IODI. El Grupo 2 siguió el mismo esquema de evaluación. Las cuidadoras de acogida completaron la adaptación argentina del FACES III. Resultados: en las dos primeras evaluaciones, el Grupo 1 mostró puntuaciones significativamente menores. En la tercera, estas diferencias se atenuaron y en la mayoría de las áreas no fueron significativas. En el grupo de acogimiento, se registró mayor recuperación en niños integrados en familias con niveles intermedios de cohesión y flexibilidad, y un funcionamiento balanceado. Conclusiones: los hallazgos aportan evidencia sobre la relevancia del entorno familiar en la recuperación del desarrollo temprano tras experiencias de maltrato y subrayan la importancia del funcionamiento de las familias de acogida en este proceso",Desarrollo Infantil Temprano; Resiliencia; Familias de Acogida; Cohesión Familiar; Flexibilidad Familiar,marcadores,maria paula moretti1,introduccion situ maltrato ninas ninos pueden ser derivad cuidad alternativ si bien impacto maltrato temprano desarrollo ha sido estudiado necesario profundizar proces recuperacion durante primera infancia objetiv analizar trayectori desarrollo primera infancia historial maltrato durante primer cuatro meses acogimiento familiar comparacion grupo referencia explorar diferenci dich trayectori segun cohesion flexibilidad funcionamiento famili acogida metodo diseno longitudinal panel 60 participant hasta 36 meses 30 acogimiento familiar antecedent maltrato grupo 30 famili origen sin historial maltrato grupo --de referencia desarrollo evaluo tres moment --inicio acogimiento dos cuatro meses-- mediante escal argentin prunape iodi grupo siguio mismo esquema evaluacion cuidador acogida completaron adaptacion argentina faces iii resultad dos primer evalu grupo mostro puntu significativa menor tercera estas diferenci atenuaron mayoria areas no fueron significativ grupo acogimiento registro mayor recuperacion ninos integrad famili nivel intermedi cohesion flexibilidad funcionamiento balanceado conclusion hallazg aportan evidencia sobre relevancia entorno familiar recuperacion desarrollo temprano tras experienci maltrato subrayan importancia funcionamiento famili acogida este proceso,desarrollo infantil temprano resiliencia famili acogida cohesion familiar flexibilidad familiar,maria paula moretti1 introduccion situ maltrato ninas ninos pueden ser derivad cuidad alternativ si bien impacto maltrato temprano desarrollo ha sido estudiado necesario profundizar proces recuperacion durante primera infancia objetiv analizar trayectori desarrollo primera infancia historial maltrato durante primer cuatro meses acogimiento familiar comparacion grupo referencia explorar diferenci dich trayectori segun cohesion flexibilidad funcionamiento famili acogida metodo diseno longitudinal panel 60 participant hasta 36 meses 30 acogimiento familiar antecedent maltrato grupo 30 famili origen sin historial maltrato grupo --de referencia desarrollo evaluo tres moment --inicio acogimiento dos cuatro meses-- mediante escal argentin prunape iodi grupo siguio mismo esquema evaluacion cuidador acogida completaron adaptacion argentina faces iii resultad dos primer evalu grupo mostro puntu significativa menor tercera estas diferenci atenuaron mayoria areas no fueron significativ grupo acogimiento registro mayor recuperacion ninos integrad famili nivel intermedi cohesion flexibilidad funcionamiento balanceado conclusion hallazg aportan evidencia sobre relevancia entorno familiar recuperacion desarrollo temprano tras experienci maltrato subrayan importancia funcionamiento famili acogida este proceso desarrollo infantil temprano resiliencia famili acogida cohesion familiar flexibilidad familiar,1.0.0,295b47f74f7e98f1
2011-3080,7964-+Trayectorias+de+Recuperación+del+Desarrollo+Temprano+en+Acogimiento+Familiar.pdf,7964-+Trayectorias+de+Recuperación+del+Desarrollo+Temprano+en+Acogimiento+Familiar_0,en,e IODI. El Grupo 2 siguió el mismo esquema de evaluación. Las cuidadoras de acogida completaron,"Introduction: In maltreatment situations, children may be placed in alternative care. Although the impact of early maltreatment on development has been widely documented, further research is needed on recovery processes during early childhood. Aims: (1) To analyze developmental trajectories in early childhood among children with a history of maltreatment during the first four months of foster care, in comparison with a reference group, and (2) to explore differences in these trajectories according to family cohesion, flexibility, and functioning in foster families. Method: A longitudinal panel design was conducted with 60 participants aged up to 36 months: 30 in foster care with a history of maltreatment (Group 1) and 30 living with their birth families without a history of maltreatment (Group 2 - reference group). Development was assessed at three time points—at entry into foster care, and after two and four months—using Argentine developmental scales: PRUNAPE and IODI. The reference group followed the same assessment schedule. Foster caregivers completed the Argentine adaptation of FACES III. Results: In the first two assessments, Group 1 showed Moretti, M.P, Torrecilla, M., & Taborda, A. Vol. 19 No. 2 / Mayo – Agosto 2026 2 significantly lower scores. By the third assessment, these differences decreased, and in most domains were no longer significant. Within the foster care group, higher developmental gains were observed among children placed in families with intermediate levels of cohesion and flexibility, and balanced family functioning. Conclusions: The findings provide evidence on the relevance of the family environment in early developmental trajectories following maltreatment and highlight the importance of foster family functioning in these processes",Early Childhood Development; Resilience; Foster Families; Family Cohesion; Family Flexibility,marcadores,iodi el grupo siguio el mismo esquema de evaluacion las cuidadora de acogida completaron,introduction maltreatment situ children may plac alternative care although impact early maltreatment development has been widely document further research need recovery process during early childhood aims analyze developmental trajectori early childhood among children history maltreatment during first four month foster care comparison reference group explore differenc these trajectori accord family cohesion flexibility function foster famili method longitudinal panel design conduct 60 participant aged up 36 month 30 foster care history maltreatment group 30 living their birth famili without history maltreatment group reference group development assess three time points--at entry into foster care after two four months--us argentine developmental scal prunape iodi reference group follow same assessment schedule foster caregiver complet argentine adaptation face iii result first two assessment group show moretti torrecilla taborda vol 19 no mayo agosto 2026 significantly lower scor third assessment these differenc decreas most domain no longer significant within foster care group higher developmental gain observ among children plac famili intermediate level cohesion flexibility balanc family function conclusion finding provide evidence relevance family environment early developmental trajectori follow maltreatment highlight importance foster family function these process,early childhood development resilience foster famili family cohesion family flexibility,iodi el grupo siguio el mismo esquema de evaluacion las cuidadora de acogida completaron introduction maltreatment situ children may plac alternative care although impact early maltreatment development has been widely document further research need recovery process during early childhood aims analyze developmental trajectori early childhood among children history maltreatment during first four month foster care comparison reference group explore differenc these trajectori accord family cohesion flexibility function foster famili method longitudinal panel design conduct 60 participant aged up 36 month 30 foster care history maltreatment group 30 living their birth famili without history maltreatment group reference group development assess three time points--at entry into foster care after two four months--us argentine developmental scal prunape iodi reference group follow same assessment schedule foster caregiver complet argentine adaptation face iii result first two assessment group show moretti torrecilla taborda vol 19 no mayo agosto 2026 significantly lower scor third assessment these differenc decreas most domain no longer significant within foster care group higher developmental gain observ among children plac famili intermediate level cohesion flexibility balanc family function conclusion finding provide evidence relevance family environment early developmental trajectori follow maltreatment highlight importance foster family function these process early childhood development resilience foster famili family cohesion family flexibility,1.0.0,19caf0eca3aa1a8b
2011-3080,8013-+Psychometric+Properties+of+the+Argentinian+version.pdf,8013-+Psychometric+Properties+of+the+Argentinian+version_0,en,", Mirta Susana Ison5 ","Objectives: The therapeutic alliance is a strong predictor of outcomes in child psychotherapy. One widely used self-report measure is the Therapeutic Alliance Scale for Children (TASC), which includes different perspectives, such as the therapist's view (TASC-T). However, few studies have examined the psychometric properties of the TASC-T. This study aimed to evaluate its validity and reliability. Method: Fifty-nine child psychotherapists from Argentina participated, with an average of 6.79 years of clinical experience (SD = 5.31) across various theoretical orientations (CBT, psychodynamic, systemic, etc.). Therapists completed the 12-item TASC-T reflecting on different child patients. Content validity was evaluated by panel of 11 psychologists who rated item relevance and clarity; Aiken’s V was .70, indicating acceptable validity. Construct validity was examined via confirmatory factor analysis (CFA) in R, using responses for 214 patients. A bifactor model was tested, including a global factor and two specific factors (Bond and Task). Results: The bifactor model showed good fit (GFI = .94; CFI = .95; TLI = .92; SRMR = .06; RMSEA = .07, 90% CI [.05, .09]). Reliability was acceptable, with ordinal α = .88 for the global scale, .84 for Bond, and .82 for Task. Discussion: These findings support the TASC-T as a valid and reliable tool for assessing children’s therapeutic alliance from the therapist’s perspective. This study contributes to the limited literature on TASC psychometrics and provides evidence for its use in clinical research and practice",Therapeutic Alliance; Psychometrics; Psychotherapists; Child Psychology,marcadores,mirta susana ison5,objectiv therapeutic alliance strong predictor outcom child psychotherapy one widely used self-report measure therapeutic alliance scale children tasc which includ di