2011-4532,Eleuthera_Vol28_2+Art+2.pdf,Eleuthera_Vol28_2+Art+2_0,en,"labras clave: educación rural, desarrollo humano, pedagogía, subjetividad, identidad,","This paper focuses on analyzing the concept of human development from an ethnocentric perspective, applying it to the field of rural education. The main purpose is to provide a solid theoretical and methodological basis for an educational approach that reflects current discussions and trends in educational research. The ultimate goal is to broaden the pedagogical horizon towards a more inclusive and democratic perspective, incorporating ethnoecological principles that allow for shifts and convergences in rural education. An analytical and critical approach will be used to examine the implications of the concept of human development in the specific context of rural education. An exhaustive review of academic literature and previous research related to the topic will be conducted. Additionally, a comparative analysis of different methodological and didactic approaches applied in similar educational contexts will be carried out. The results of this study reveal that the incorporation of ethnoecological principles in rural education can have a significant impact on the reorganization of educational practices. Opportunities are identified to promote a humanistic, decolonial, and emancipatory approach that encourages active student participation, appreciation of cultural diversity, and the development of critical and reflective skills. In conclusion, this article highlights the importance of considering the concept of human development in the design and implementation of educational strategies in rural environments. It is recommended to adopt methodological and didactic approaches that integrate ethical, cultural, and ecological perspectives to improve the quality and relevance of rural education, thus contributing to the construction of more equitable and sustainable societies","rural education, human development, pedagogy, subjectivity, identity, curriculum",marcadores,labra clave educacion rural desarrollo humano pedagogia subjetividad identidad,paper focus analyz concept human development ethnocentric perspective apply field rural education main purpose provide solid theoretical methodological basi educational approach reflect current discussion trend educational research ultimate goal broaden pedagogical horizon toward more inclusive democratic perspective incorporat ethnoecological principl allow shift convergenc rural education analytical critical approach will used examine implic concept human development specific context rural education exhaustive review academic literature previou research relat topic will conduct additionally comparative analysi different methodological didactic approach appli similar educational context will carri out result study reveal incorporation ethnoecological principl rural education can have significant impact reorgan educational practic opportuniti identifi promote humanistic decolonial emancipatory approach encourag active student participation appreciation cultural diversity development critical reflective skill conclusion article highlight importance consider concept human development design implementation educational strategi rural environment recommend adopt methodological didactic approach integrate ethical cultural ecological perspectiv improve quality relevance rural education thus contribut construction more equitable sustainable societi,rural education human development pedagogy subjectivity identity curriculum,labra clave educacion rural desarrollo humano pedagogia subjetividad identidad paper focus analyz concept human development ethnocentric perspective apply field rural education main purpose provide solid theoretical methodological basi educational approach reflect current discussion trend educational research ultimate goal broaden pedagogical horizon toward more inclusive democratic perspective incorporat ethnoecological principl allow shift convergenc rural education analytical critical approach will used examine implic concept human development specific context rural education exhaustive review academic literature previou research relat topic will conduct additionally comparative analysi different methodological didactic approach appli similar educational context will carri out result study reveal incorporation ethnoecological principl rural education can have significant impact reorgan educational practic opportuniti identifi promote humanistic decolonial emancipatory approach encourag active student participation appreciation cultural diversity development critical reflective skill conclusion article highlight importance consider concept human development design implementation educational strategi rural environment recommend adopt methodological didactic approach integrate ethical cultural ecological perspectiv improve quality relevance rural education thus contribut construction more equitable sustainable societi rural education human development pedagogy subjectivity identity curriculum,1.0.0,93d945344db1e4ca
2011-4532,Eleuthera_Vol28_2+Art+3.pdf,Eleuthera_Vol28_2+Art+3_0,es,Caracterización y estrategias para circuitos,"El presente artículo examina las potencialidades del departamento de San Andrés, Providencia y Santa Catalina para la implementación de estrategias de circuitos cortos de comercialización (CCC), integrando los principios de la economía solidaria y la agricultura campesina, familiar, étnica y comunitaria (ACFEC). Esta propuesta surge como alternativa frente a la alta dependencia económica del turismo, con el objetivo de potenciar la producción y el consumo local mediante mecanismos de comercialización directa, con el fin de reducir la intermediación y fortalecer las economías endógenas. La metodología empleada es de tipo cualitativo, basada en una revisión documental rigurosa, con análisis bibliométrico y categorización analítica de fuentes relevantes del período 2000–2023. Se aplicó una matriz de sistematización con triangulación entre categorías teóricas y emergentes, como territorio, territorialidad, economía solidaria y circuitos alimentarios. Los resultados, indican que: (1) los CCC son viables técnica y estratégicamente en territorios insulares con baja densidad productiva; (2) su implementación favorece la cohesión social y la gobernanza comunitaria, al promover redes asociativas y economía solidaria; y (3) los CCC contribuyen al fortalecimiento de la soberanía alimentaria, la equidad territorial y la resiliencia socioeconómica del archipiélago. Estos hallazgos abren camino a nuevas políticas públicas que integran desarrollo local sostenible y comercio justo","derechos sociales y económicos, economía agraria, economía rural * Doctor en agrociencias de la Universidad de la Salle, Corporación Universitaria Agustiniana, Bogotá, Colombia, correo electrónico: dustin.gomez@uniagustiniana.edu.co https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5359-2300. Google Scholar Cómo citar este artículo: Gómez-Rodríguez, D. T. (2026). Caracterización y estrategias para circuitos cortos 