2011-4532,Eleuthera_Vol28_2+Art+3.pdf,Eleuthera_Vol28_2+Art+3_0,en,"ociales y económicos, economía agraria, economía rural","This article examines the potential of the department of San Andrés, Providencia, and Santa Catalina for the implementation of short marketing chain (SMC) strategies, integrating the principles of solidarity economy and peasant, family, ethnic, and community agriculture (PFECA). This proposal emerges as an alternative to high economic dependence on tourism, with the aim of boosting local production and consumption through direct marketing mechanisms in order to reduce intermediation and strengthen endogenous economies. The methodology used is qualitative, based on a rigorous documentary review, with bibliometric analysis and analytical categorization of relevant sources from the period 2000–2023. A systematization matrix was applied with triangulation between theoretical and emerging categories, such as territory, territoriality, solidarity economy, and food circuits. The results indicate that (1) CCCs are technically and strategically viable in island territories with low productive density; (2) their implementation favors social cohesion and community governance by promoting associative networks and solidarity economy; and (3) CCCs contribute to strengthening food sovereignty, territorial equity, and the socioeconomic resilience of the archipelago. These findings pave the way for new public policies that integrate sustainable local development and fair trade","agricultural economy, rural economy, social and economic rights",marcadores,ocial economico economia agraria economia rural,article examin potential department san andr providencia santa catalina implementation short market chain smc strategi integrat principl solidarity economy peasant family ethnic community agriculture pfeca proposal emerg alternative high economic dependence tourism aim boost local production consumption through direct market mechanism order reduce intermediation strengthen endogenou economi methodology used qualitative based rigorou documentary review bibliometric analysi analytical categor relevant sourc period 2000-2023 systemat matrix appli triangulation between theoretical emerg categori such territory territoriality solidarity economy food circuit result indicate cccs technically strategically viable island territori low productive density their implementation favor social cohesion community governance promot associative network solidarity economy cccs contribute strengthen food sovereignty territorial equity socioeconomic resilience archipelago these finding pave way new public polici integrate sustainable local development fair trade,agricultural economy rural economy social economic right,ocial economico economia agraria economia rural article examin potential department san andr providencia santa catalina implementation short market chain smc strategi integrat principl solidarity economy peasant family ethnic community agriculture pfeca proposal emerg alternative high economic dependence tourism aim boost local production consumption through direct market mechanism order reduce intermediation strengthen endogenou economi methodology used qualitative based rigorou documentary review bibliometric analysi analytical categor relevant sourc period 2000-2023 systemat matrix appli triangulation between theoretical emerg categori such territory territoriality solidarity economy food circuit result indicate cccs technically strategically viable island territori low productive density their implementation favor social cohesion community governance promot associative network solidarity economy cccs contribute strengthen food sovereignty territorial equity socioeconomic resilience archipelago these finding pave way new public polici integrate sustainable local development fair trade agricultural economy rural economy social economic right,1.0.0,8f0d092cce63bafb
2011-4532,Eleuthera_Vol28_2+Art+4.pdf,Eleuthera_Vol28_2+Art+4_0,en,Geohistorical cartography: a contribution from,"The following research presents a cartographic strategy for teaching and learning Social Sciences, with the aim of fostering the development of critical thinking and metacognitive awareness, in the face of a global and changing society that requires mechanisms to understand the territory it inhabits. The sample consisted of twenty-nine sixth-grade students from an educational institution in the municipality of Villamaría (Caldas). A quantitative methodology was chosen, under a pre-experimental design of a group with pre-test and post-test using two instruments: a rubric designed and approved by Expert Judgment for the measurement of critical thinking and the MAI Junior test developed by Huertas et al. (2014) to evaluate changes in students’ metacognitive awareness. As a result, it was obtained that the strategy was effective in the development of critical thinking and metacognitive awareness","cartography, critical thinking, Teaching strategy",marcadores,geohistorical cartography contribution,follow research present cartographic strategy teach learn social scienc aim foster development critical think metacognitive awarenes face global chang society requir mechanism understand territory inhabit sample consist twenty-nine sixth-grade student educational institution municipality villamaria calda quantitative methodology chosen under pre-experimental design group pre-test post-test using two instrument rubric design approv expert judgment measurement critical think mai junior test develop huerta et al 2014 evaluate chang student metacognitive awarenes result obtain strategy effective development critical think metacognitive awarenes,cartography critical think teach strategy,geohistorical cartography contribution follow research present cartographic strategy teach learn social scienc aim foster development critical think metacognitive awarenes face global chang society requir mechanism understand territory inhabit sample consist twenty-nine sixth-grade student educational institution municipality villamaria calda quantitative methodology chosen under pre-experimental design group pre-test post-test using two instrument rubric design approv expert judgment measurement critical think mai junior test develop huerta et al 2014 evaluate chang student metacognitive awarenes result obtain strategy effective development critical think metacognitive awarenes cartography critical think teach strategy,1.0.0,c2d855a286727d0c
2011-4532,Eleuthera_Vol28_2+Art+4.pdf,Eleuthera_Vol28_2+Art+4_0,es,"Sciences, with the aim of fostering the development of critical thinking and metacognitive awareness,","La siguiente investigación, presenta una estrategia cartográfica para la enseñanza y el aprendizaje de las Ciencias Sociales, con el fin de fomentar el desarrollo del pensamiento crítico y la conciencia metacognitiva, de cara a una sociedad global y cambiante que precisa de mecanismos para comprender el territorio que habita. La muestra estuvo representada por 29 estudiantes del grado sexto de una institución educativa en el municipio de Villamaría (Caldas). Se optó por una metodología cuantitativa, bajo un diseño preexperimental de un grupo con pre test y post test utilizando dos instrumentos: una rúbrica diseñada y aprobada por juicio de expertos para la medición del pensamiento * Research Professor at the Autonomous University of Manizales. Member of the Ethics and Politics Research Group, classified as Category A by Minciencias. Email:: yenny.gomezc@autonoma.edu.co https://orcid.org/0009-0004-9026-564X Google Scholar ** Faculty member of the Department of Educational Studies at the University of Caldas and professor in the Psychology Program at the University of Manizales. Contact email: diana.montoya@ucaldas.edu.co https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8007-0102 Google Scholar ** Research faculty member at the Autonomous University of Manizales. Member of the Ethics and Politics Research Group, classified as Category A by Minciencias. Contact email: ghmunoz@autonoma.edu.co https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2154-7246 Google Scholar Cómo citar este artículo: Gómez-Cabrera, Y. J., Montoya-Londoño, D. M. y Herrera-Muñoz, G. (2026). Geohistorical cartography: a contribution from critical thinking and metacognitive awareness. Revista Eleuthera, 28(2), 63-89. http://doi. org/10.17151/eleu.2026.28.2.4 rev. eleuthera. Vol. 28 n.º 2, julio-diciembre 2026, 63-89 Recibido: 12 de febrero de 2025. Aprobado: 12 de junio de 2025 ISSN: 2011-4532 (Impreso) ISSN: 2463-1469 (En línea) http://doi.org/10.17151/eleu.2026.28.2.4 64 Geohistorical cartography: a contribution from critical thinking and metacognitive awareness crítico y la prueba del MAI Junior elaborada por Huertas et al. (2014) con el fin de evaluar los cambios en la conciencia metacognitiva de los estudiantes. Como resultado se obtuvo que la estrategia fue efectiva en el desarrollo del pensamiento crítico y la conciencia metacognitiva","cartografía, estrategia de enseñanza, pensamiento crítico",marcadores,scienc with the aim of fostering the development of critical thinking and metacognitive awareness,siguiente investigacion presenta estrategia cartografica ensenanza aprendizaje cienci social fin fomentar desarrollo pensamiento critico conciencia metacognitiva cara sociedad global cambiante precisa mecanism comprender territorio habita muestra estuvo representada 29 estudiant grado sexto institucion educativa municipio villamaria cald opto metodologia cuantitativa bajo diseno preexperimental grupo pre test post test utiliz dos instrument rubrica disenada aprobada juicio expert medicion pensamiento research professor at the autonomous university of manizal member of the ethics and politics research group classified as category by mincienci email yenny gomezc autonoma edu co https orcid org 0009-0004-9026-564x google scholar faculty member of the department of educational studi at the university of cald and professor in the psychology program at the university of manizal contact email diana montoya ucald edu co https orcid org 0000-0001-8007-0102 google scholar research faculty member at the autonomous university of manizal member of the ethics and politics research group classified as category by mincienci contact email ghmunoz autonoma edu co https orcid org 0000-0002-2154-7246 google scholar como citar este articulo gomez-cabrera montoya-londono herrera-munoz 2026 geohistorical cartography contribution from critical thinking 