2011-7922,"Psychometric+Properties+of+the+EORTC+QLQ-LC29+Module+for+Assessing+Quality+of+Life+in+Patients+with+Lung+Cancer_+An+Observational+Study+in+Antioquia,+Colombia.pdf","Psychometric+Properties+of+the+EORTC+QLQ-LC29+Module+for+Assessing+Quality+of+Life+in+Patients+with+Lung+Cancer_+An+Observational+Study+in+Antioquia,+Colombia_0",desconocido,"Psychometric Properties of the EORTC QLQ-LC29 Module for Assessing Quality of Life in Patients with Lung Cancer  An Observational Study in Antioquia, Colombia","Abstract Resumen RESEARCH ARTICLE Psychometric Properties of the EORTC QLQ-LC29 Module for Assessing Quality of Life in Patients with Lung Cancer: An Observational Study in Antioquia, Colombia Propiedades psicométricas del módulo EORTC QLQ-LC29 para la evaluación de la calidad de vida en pacientes con cáncer de pulmón: un estudio observacional en Antioquia, Colombia Miguel Angel Medina-Pabón Michael Koller Applied and Epidemiological Research Group, Auna Ideas. MD, Epidemiologist, Magister Health Economics, Medellín, Colombia. Grupo Académico de Epidemiología Clínica-GRAEPIC, School of Medicine, Universidad de Antioquia, Medellín, Colombia. Applied and Epidemiological Research Group, Auna Ideas. Information Analyst, Medellín, Colombia. Center for Clinical Studies, University Hospital Regensburg, Regensburg, Germany. , Jose F. Tatis-Méndez 1 4 1 3 2 4 2 2 Purpose: The purpose of this study is to evaluate the psychometric properties of the Spain Spanish version of the European Organisation for Research and Treatment of Cancer - Quality of Life Questionnaire - Lung Cancer Module-29 (EORTC QLQ-LC29) in Colombia. Methods: Content validity was assessed with confirmatory factor analysis, concurrent criterion validity by comparing scores of the QLQ-LC29 and Functional Assessment of Cancer Therapy – Lung (FACT-L) scales, internal consistency by Cronbach’s alpha, test-retest reliability with Lin’s concordance coefficient, and sensitivity to change after therapeutic intervention by comp",,respaldo_sin_marcadores,psychometric properti eortc qlq-lc29 module assess quality life patient lung cancer observational study antioquia colombia,abstract resumen research article psychometric properti eortc qlq-lc29 module assess quality life patient lung cancer observational study antioquia colombia propiedad psicometric modulo eortc qlq-lc29 evaluacion calidad vida pacient cancer pulmon estudio observacional antioquia colombia miguel angel medina-pabon michael koller appli epidemiological research group auna idea md epidemiologist magister health economic medellin colombia grupo academico epidemiologia clinica-graepic school medicine universidad antioquia medellin colombia appli epidemiological research group auna idea information analyst medellin colombia center clinical studi university hospital regensburg regensburg germany jose tatis-mendez purpose purpose study evaluate psychometric properti spain spanish version european organisation research treatment cancer quality life questionnaire lung cancer module-29 eortc qlq-lc29 colombia method content validity assess confirmatory factor analysi concurrent criterion validity compar scor qlq-lc29 functional assessment cancer therapy lung fact-l scal internal consistency cronbach alpha test-retest reliability lin concordance coefficient sensitivity change after therapeutic intervention comp,,psychometric properti eortc qlq-lc29 module assess quality life patient lung cancer observational study antioquia colombia abstract resumen research article psychometric properti eortc qlq-lc29 module assess quality life patient lung cancer observational study antioquia colombia propiedad psicometric modulo eortc qlq-lc29 evaluacion calidad vida pacient cancer pulmon estudio observacional antioquia colombia miguel angel medina-pabon michael koller appli epidemiological research group auna idea md epidemiologist magister health economic medellin colombia grupo academico epidemiologia clinica-graepic school medicin