2011-799X,Dialnet-BeyondTheStage-10680212.pdf,Dialnet-BeyondTheStage-10680212_0,en,Beyond the Stage: Accessibility in Virtual,"Virtual reality (vr) concerts are an example of how technological advances are transforming the music industry. These immersive events can connect audiences around the world through interactive experiences, but they also raise significant accessibility challenges, particularly for people with dis abilities. This paper examines the potential integration of accessibility services in vr music events. Drawing on existing literature in vr accessibility, it proposes an analytical matrix that connects key design dimensions of these events with potential access barriers, affected user groups, available strat egies, and their limitations. Challenges include spatial navigation, sensory intensity, controller-based interaction, and multimodal communication, among others, while potential opportunities lie in mul timodal feedback, adaptable interfaces, and personalised interaction settings that can support more flexible and inclusive participation. While the analytical matrix presented here is informed primarily by broader vr accessibility research, empirical testing in real-world vr music events will be necessary to validate and refine these approaches. Ultimately, vr represents both an opportunity and a chal lenge: it can either reinforce existing accessibility barriers or establish new standards of inclusivity in the music industry. If vr concerts aim to broaden cultural participation, a collaborative effort between developers, artists, and accessibility experts is essential to ensure that these immersive experiences are engaging, inclusive, and accessible to all","virtual reality, accessibility, music, universal design, disability Más allá del escenario: la accesibilidad en los conciertos en entornos de realidad virtual",marcadores,beyond stage accessibility virtual,virtual reality vr concert example how technological advanc transform music industry t