2011-799X,Dialnet-ChartingVirtualWorlds-10680211.pdf,Dialnet-ChartingVirtualWorlds-10680211_0,en,Charting Virtual Worlds: Training,"The escalating global prominence of the game industry underscores the critical need for specialized translation and localization expertise. This article presents a case study of the Undergraduate Program in Translation at Universidade Federal de Uberlândia, a Brazilian public university that has been providing dedicated training in game localization for the last 15 years. The core of the Universidade Federal de Uberlândia’s offering is a 60-hour course, that spans foundational localization concepts like transcreation and culturalization, as well as advanced technical skills, including computer-assisted translation, machine translation, and generative artificial intelligence. Its pedagogical approach integrates theoretical knowledge with practical application through lectures, workshops, and game localization projects, frequently leveraging open-source resources. Students gain experience by collaborating in teams, and emulating professional workflows. Further enhancing the training, students complete a senior thesis, often focusing on game localization, where they detail their experiences in technically adapting games. This research draws upon existing literature and employs an autoethnographic approach, critically reflecting on our experiences as trainers and thesis supervisors through personal archives, didactic materials, and learning tasks. Complementarily, a bibliometric and content analysis of past senior theses provides empirical data. A notable challenge addressed is the scarcity of game localization-specific teaching materials, prompting the program’s proactive development of resources tailored to the Brazilian market. This study thus aims to contribute to a specialized localization training","autoethnographic approach, game industry, game localization, translator training Marileide Dias Esqueda & Igor Antônio Lourenço da Silva 148 Translation and Localization: New Approaches and Opportunities in the Digital Entertainment Industries Una cartografía de mundos virtuales: formación en traducción y localización de videojuegos en una universidad de Brasil",marcadores,chart virtual world train,escalat global prominence game industry underscor critical need specializ translation local expertise article present case study undergraduate program translation universidade federal de uberlandia brazilian public university has been provid dedicat train game local last 15 year core universidade federal de uberlandia offer 60-hour course span foundational local concept like transcreation cultural well advanc technical skill includ computer-assist translation machine translation generative artificial intelligence its pedagogical approach integrat theoretical knowledge practical application through lectur workshop game local project frequently leverag open-source resourc student gain experience collaborat team emulat professional workflow further enhanc train student complete senior thesi often focus game local where they detail their experienc technically adapt game research draw upon exist literature employ autoethnographic approach critically reflect our experienc trainer thesi supervisor through personal archiv didactic material learn task complementarily bibliometric content analysi past senior thes provid empirical data notable challenge address scarcity game localization-specific teach material prompt program proactive development resourc tailor brazilian market study thus aims contribute specializ local train,autoethnographic approach game industry game local translator train marileide dias esqueda igor antonio lourenco da silva 148 translation local new approach opportuniti digital entertainment industri una cartografia de mundo virtual formacion en traduccion localizacion de videojuego en una universidad de brasil,chart virtual world train escalat global prominence game industry underscor critical