iv universitari identifican benefici pedagogic como aumento motivacion mejora produccion oral escrita reduccion ansiedad fomento aprendizaje autono mo no obstante tambien evidencian limit relacionad diseno videojueg falta formacion docente barrer institucional este trabajo contribuye consolidar linea investigacion emergente propone futur line estudio como comparacion entre videojueg comercial jueg seri analisis longitudinal impacto diseno video jueg especific ensenanza aprendizaje franc como lengua extranjera ensenanza lengu franc como lengua extranjera jueg seri videojueg co mercial videojueg educativ video games in french-as-a-foreign-language teaching and learning systematic literature review 2014-2024,1.0.0,b81618524fd94229
2011-799X,Dialnet-LosVideojuegosEnLaEnsenanzaYElAprendizajeDeFrances-10680214.pdf,Dialnet-LosVideojuegosEnLaEnsenanzaYElAprendizajeDeFrances-10680214_0,en,"neficios pedagógicos como el aumento de la motivación, la","This article presents a systematic review of academic literature published between 2014 and 2024 on the use of video games in the teaching and learning of French as a foreign language. Based on a systematic search in databases such as Scopus, Web of Science, eric, Google Scholar, Dialnet, and Cairn.info, 18 studies were selected, including both empirical research and theoretical reflections. Due to the scarcity of specific studies in this field, a bibliometric approach was not feasible, leading to the adoption of a descriptive methodology. The findings reveal a growing trend toward the integration of video games— particularly serious games—into university-level educational contexts. Pedagogical benefits identified include increased motivation, improved oral and written production, reduced anxiety, and enhanced learner autonomy. However, limitations persist, such as issues in game design, lack of teacher training, Mutatis Mutandis. Revista Latinoamericana de Traducción Vol. 19, N.°1, 2026, enero-junio, pp. 214-233 Los videojuegos en la enseñanza y el aprendizaje de francés como lengua extranjera: revisión sistemática de la literatura (2014-2024) 215 and institutional barriers. This study contributes to consolidating an emerging research area and propos es future lines of inquiry, including comparisons between commercial and serious games, longitudinal analyses of their impact, and the design of games specifically tailored for fle","educational video games, French as a foreign language, language teaching, serious games, commercial video games Les jeux vidéo appliqués à l’enseignement et à l’apprentissage du fle : revue systématique de la littérature (2014–2024) Résumé Cet article propose une revue systématique de la littérature académique publiée entre 201