da segun eficacia mejorar motivacion evaluacion formativa competenci especific explorar percepcion participant investigador 60 estu diant sobre esta experiencia proyecto enmarca enfoque socioconstructivista aplica metodologia cualitativa primer fases investigacion basada diseno notas campo encuest como instrument coadyuvant resultad evidencian component area investigacion gamificacion uso diseno plataform interactiv ensenanza apren dizaje traduccion especializada proyect investigacion 2022 experienci aprendizaje interac tivas gamificad diseno implementacion clas lengua inglesa traduccion 2021 recurs digital material teorico-practic gamificacion ensenanza aprendizaje lengua tra duccion aulas virtual carrer grado ingl marco programa formacion investigador facultad lengu resolucion decanal 977 2022 ndeg 716 2021 proyect avalad subsidiad prosecretaria ciencia tecnologia facultad lengu universidad nacional cordoba argentina mutatis mutandis revista latinoamericana traduccion vol 19 deg 2026 enero-junio pp 68-97 secuencia evaluativa gamificada formacion profesional traduccion abordaje innovador desde cono sur 69 clave secuencia gamificada facilitaron proces evaluativ competenci traslativ digital dilucidaron armoni divergenci entre intencion pedagogica propuesta vivenci estudiant estos hallazg sirven base perfeccionar diseno pedagogico futuro estudio arroja luz sobre benefici experiencia ludica innovadora cuyas impli canci podrian trascender contexto esta propuesta didactica traduccion competencia traductora evaluacion formativa gamifica cion traduccion economico-financiera gamified formative assessment design for professional training innovative insights from the southern cone,1.0.0,2441a43862c33184
2011-799X,Dialnet-SecuenciaEvaluativaGamificadaParaLaFormacionProfes-10680208.pdf,Dialnet-SecuenciaEvaluativaGamificadaParaLaFormacionProfes-10680208_0,en,a de Traducción,"Gamification has emerged as a promising approach to foster meaningful learning in translation and interpreting training, yet its scope remains limited. Although numerous studies highlight gamification benefits in translator and interpreter training, most of these studies were carried out in European contexts, leaving a significant gap in Latin American public education. To address the need to shed light on other contexts, this study presents a gamified formative assessment sequence implemented in an economic and financial translation course at a public university in Argentina. The aim is twofold, namely, to evaluate the effectiveness of this gamified experience in enhancing students’ motivation and formative assessment of specific competencies, and to examine participants’ perceptions (three researchers and sixty students) regarding this experience. Framed within a socio-constructivist per spective, the study adopted a qualitative methodology grounded in the initial phases of design-based research, using field notes and surveys as complementary research instruments. The results highlight key components of the gamified sequence that supported the assessment of both translation and digital competencies. They also reveal areas of convergence and divergence between the pedagogical aims of the design and students’ experiences. These findings provide valuable input to refine this pedagogical design in the future. Finally, the study underscores the benefits of gamification as an innovative learning experience, the implications of which may extend beyond the immediate context of this research","translator training, translation competence, formative assessment, gamification, finan cial-business translation Gamification dans l’évaluation pendant la formation en traduction : une approche novatrice depuis le 