2027-1352,Art-939_Ajem.pdf,Art-939_Ajem_0,en,ORIGINAL ARTICLE,"Frailejones —endemic plants of high mountain páramo— exhibit morphological changes, which can lead to death. Some of these changes have been regarded as symptoms and are grouped as the Af-fectation Syndrome of Frailejones. Nonetheless, a standardized naming and description of these symptoms is lacking. Thus, research was conducted in six páramo complexes on the eastern range of the Colombian Andes to characterize the symptoms of Affectation Syndrome of Frailejones across different frailejón species, aiming at i) generating information about symptom specificity in certain frailejón species and páramos, and ii) naming and providing a thorough description of these symptoms. Plots of 5×5 m were randomly established in six páramo complexes, in which the features of each new symptom were documented. A name was assigned to each symptom, and the affected frailejón spe-cies was determined. Six new symptoms and one sign were found in all assessed páramos and frailejón species within the study area, thus broadening the spectrum of frailejón affectation syn-drome. No symptom was exclusive to a páramo or frailejón species. Moreover, the features of the novel signs and symptoms were all consistent among frailejón species. Thanks to this naming and description of each novel symptom and sign, further assessments of frailejón disease can be systemat-ically conducted",damage; endemic plant; Espeletia; Espeletiopsis; high mountain; páramo. 1,marcadores,original article,frailejon --endemic plant high mountain paramo-- exhibit morphological chang which can lead death some these chang have been regard symptom group af-fectation syndrome frailejon nonetheles standardiz naming description these symptom lack thus research conduct six paramo complex eastern range colombian ande characterize symptom affectation syndrome frailejon acros different frailejon speci aiming generat information about symptom specificity certain frailejon speci paramo ii naming provid thorough description these symptom plot 5x5 randomly establish six paramo complex which featur each new symptom document name assign each symptom affect frailejon spe-ci determin six new symptom one sign found all assess paramo frailejon speci within study area thus broaden spectrum frailejon affectation syn-drome no symptom exclusive paramo frailejon speci moreover featur novel sign symptom all consistent among frailejon speci thank naming description each novel symptom sign further assessment frailejon disease can systemat-ically conduct,damage endemic plant espeletia espeletiopsi high mountain paramo,original article frailejon --endemic plant high mountain paramo-- exhibit morphological chang which can lead death some these chang have been regard symptom group af-fectation syndrome frailejon nonetheles standardiz naming description these symptom lack thus research conduct six paramo complex eastern range colombian ande characterize symptom affectation syndrome frailejon acros different frailejon speci aiming generat information about symptom specificity certain frailejon speci paramo ii naming provid thorough description these symptom plot 5x5 randomly establish six paramo complex which featur each new symptom document name assign each symptom affect frailejon spe-ci determin six new symptom one sign found all assess paramo frailejon speci within study area thus broaden spectrum frailejon affectation syn-drome no symptom exclusive paramo frailejon speci moreover featur novel sign symptom all consistent among frailejon speci thank naming description each novel symptom sign further assessment frailejon disease can systemat-ically conduct damage endemic plant espeletia espeletiopsi high mountain paramo,1.0.0,087add0159bd019f
2027-1352,Art-939_Ajem.pdf,Art-939_Ajem_1,es,"[72] Teiba II, El-Bilawy EH, Elsheery NI, Rastogi A. Microbial allies in agriculture: harnessing","Los Frailejones —plantas endémicas de los páramos de alta montaña— presentan cambios morfológicos que pueden conducir a su muerte. Algunos de estos cambios se han considerado síntomas y se agrupan bajo el denominado Síndrome de Afectación de los Frailejones. No obstante, no existe una nomenclatura y descripción estandarizada de dichos síntomas. Por lo tanto, llevamos a cabo una investigación en seis complejos de páramo de la cordillera oriental de los Andes colombianos para caracterizar la sintomatología del síndrome en diversas especies de frailejón, con el fin de: i) generar información sobre la especificidad de los síntomas en determinadas especies y páramos, y ii) nombrar y proporcionar una descripción detallada de éstos. Se establecieron aleatoriamente parcelas de 5x5 m en los seis complejos de páramo, donde se documentaron las características de cada síntoma nuevo. Se asignó un nombre a cada síntoma y se determinó la especie de frailejón afectada. Se hallaron seis síntomas un signo nuevos en todos los páramos y especies evaluadas dentro del área de estudio, ampliando así el espectro del Síndrome de Afectación de los Frailejones. Ningún síntoma fue exclusivo de un páramo o especie en particular. Además, las características de los nuevos signos y síntomas fueron consistentes entre las distintas especies de frailejón. Gracias a esta nomenclatura y descripción, las evaluaciones posteriores sobre las patologías del frailejón podrán realizarse de manera sistemática","alta montaña; daño, Espeletia, Espeletiopsis, páramo, planta endémica. Universitas Scientiarum:1–21 http://ciencias.javeriana.edu.co/investigacion/universitas-scientiarum 20 New symptoms of frailejón affectation Novos Sintomas da Síndrome de Afetação dos Frailejones na Colombia",marcadores,72 teiba ii el-bilawy eh elsheery ni rastogi microbial alli in agriculture harnessing,frailejon --plant endemic param alta montana-- presentan cambi morfologic pueden conducir muerte algun estos cambi han considerado sintom agrupan bajo denominado sindrome afectacion frailejon no obstante no existe nomenclatura descripcion estandarizada dich sintom tanto llevam cabo investigacion seis complej paramo cordillera oriental andes colombian caracterizar sintomatologia sindrome divers especi frailejon fin generar informacion sobre especificidad sintom determinad especi param ii nombrar proporcionar descripcion detallada estos establecieron aleatoria parcel 5x5 seis complej paramo donde documentaron caracteristic cada sintoma nuevo asigno nombre cada sintoma determino especie frailejon afectada hallaron seis sintom signo nuev todos param especi evaluad dentro area estudio ampli asi espectro sindrome afectacion frailejon ningun sintoma fue exclusivo paramo especie particular adem caracteristic nuev sign sintom fueron consistent entre distint especi frailejon graci esta nomenclatura descripcion evalu posterior sobre patologi frailejon podran realizarse manera sistematica,alta montana dano espeletia espeletiopsis paramo planta endemica universit scientiarum 1-21 http cienci javeriana edu co investigacion universitas-scientiarum 20 new symptoms of frailejon affectation novos sintom da sindrome afetacao dos frailejon na colombia,72 teiba ii el-bilawy eh elsheery ni rastogi microbial alli in agriculture harnessing frailejon --plant endemic param alta montana-- presentan cambi morfologic pueden conducir muerte algun estos cambi han considerado sintom agrupan bajo denominado sindrome afectacion frailejon no obstante no existe nomenclatura descripcion estandarizada dich sintom tanto llevam cabo investigacion seis complej paramo cordillera oriental andes colombian caracterizar sintomatologia sindrome divers especi frailejon fin generar informacion sobre especificidad sintom determinad especi param ii nombrar proporcionar descripcion detallada estos establecieron aleatoria parcel 5x5 seis complej paramo donde documentaron caracteristic cada sintoma nuevo asigno nombre cada sintoma determino especie frailejon afectada hallaron seis sintom signo nuev todos param especi evaluad dentro area estudio ampli asi espectro sindrome afectacion frailejon ningun sintoma fue exclusivo paramo especie particular adem caracteristic nuev sign sintom fueron consistent entre distint especi frailejon graci esta nomenclatura descripcion evalu posterior sobre patologi frailejon podran realizarse manera sistematica alta montana dano espeletia espeletiopsis paramo planta endemica universit scientiarum 1-21 http cienci javeriana edu co investigacion universitas-scientiarum 20 new symptoms of frailejon affectation novos sintom da sindrome afetacao dos frailejon na colombia,1.0.0,a47306c51f7e50f4
2027-1352,Art-954_ajem.pdf,Art-954_ajem_0,en,ORIGINAL ARTICLE,"Neuropathic pain follows nervous system dysfunction or damage, significantly affecting patients’ quality of life. The need for more effective and safer pain management has drawn attention to voltage-gated sodium channels as druggable therapeutic targets in medicinal chemistry, leading to the discovery of various compounds with pharmacological potential, among which heterocycles with pyrazole and indolone cores have stood out for their versatility. Aiming to discover new potential modulators of neuropathic pain, this research studied a series of 35 compounds with a 3-hydroxy-3-pyrazolyl-1H-indolin-2-one nucleus (molecular hybrids with pyrazole and indolone cores) by bioavailability screening, using the computational tools MedChem DesignerTM and AdmetSar 2.0, which predicted good potential to cross biological barriers and suggested theoretically favorable safety profiles. The potential use of these compounds as modulators of the voltage-gated sodium channel NaV1.7 (PDB code: 6J8G), an important molecular target in the treatment of neuropathic pain, was evaluated using molecular docking with AutoDock suite and DOCK6 software. Docking protocols were validated by redocking crystallized endogenous ligands, and results were validated using the rank-consensus approach. From those computational studies, four compounds, with the highest rank consensus values (0.52-0.59), emerged as promising candidates for experimental assays as NaV1.7 modulators. This study highlights the importance of computer-aided rational design in the discovery of new compounds with therapeutic potential in the treatment of neuropathic pain","Molecular docking, ADMETox, NaV1.7, pyrazole-indolone hybrid, anti-neuropathy agents. 1",marcadores,original article,neuropathic pain follow nervou system dysfunction damage significantly affect patient quality life need more effective safer pain management has drawn attention voltage-gat sodium channel