2027-1840,"admin,+1228-3380-1-CE.pdf","admin,+1228-3380-1-CE_0",en,"MSc 2; Marcela Ríos, MSc2; Fernando Ariza, PhD2.","The aim of this study was assigned by linkage map the Endothelin-1 gene (END1) to the Chicken chromosome 2 (GGA2). The microsatellites MCW0314, MCW0245, ADL0164, MCW0264 were used and primers for amplification of specific sequences END1 were designed. The PCR-SSCP technique, and the use of denaturing gels allowed the characterization of the genotype. The genotypes identified in 200 broilers Cobb500 and Mapmaker® version 3.0b program were used in the map construction. The result, a map in which END1 is linked to microsatellites that it was reported in quantitative trait loci (QTL) for susceptibility of broilers to develop pulmonary hypertension syndrome in the GGA2","Pulmonary Hypertension Syndrome, broilers, microsatellites. 1 Grupo de Investigación en Inmunobiología y Patogénesis. Departamento de Producción Pecuaria, Facultad de Medicina Veterinaria y Zootecnia, Universidad del Tolima, Ibagué, Colombia. 2Departamento de Producción Animal, Facultad de Medicina Veterinaria y de Zootecnia, Universidad Nacional de Colombia, Bogotá, Colombia. *Autor de corre",marcadores,msc marcela rios msc2 fernando ariza phd2,aim study assign linkage map endothelin-1 gene end1 chicken chromosome gga2 microsatellit mcw0314 mcw0245 adl0164 mcw0264 used primer amplification specific sequenc end1 design pcr-sscp technique use denatur gels allow character genotype genotyp identifi 200 broiler cobb500 mapmaker version 0b program used map construction result map which end1 link microsatellit report quantitative trait loci qtl susceptibility broiler develop pulmonary hypertension syndrome gga2,pulmonary hypertension syndrome broiler microsatellit grupo de investigacion en inmunobiologia patogenesi departamento de produccion pecuaria facultad de medicina veterinaria zootecnia universidad del tolima ibague colombia 2departamento de produccion animal facultad de medicina veterin