2027-5366,Díkaion35(1)_25871-LaDoctrina_7_PDF_Dúber+Armando+Celis+Vela.pdf,Díkaion35(1)_25871-LaDoctrina_7_PDF_Dúber+Armando+Celis+Vela_0,es,"formas de exteriorización no parece compatible con sus principios constitutivos,","3 Díkaion - eISSN 2027-5366, Año 40 - Vol. 35 Núm. 1 - Chía, Colombia - 2026 / e3514 Dúber Armando Celis Vela Abstract In administrative law, doctrine usually holds that the administrative function is expressed through acts, operations, facts, omissions, and de facto actions. If one assumes that the administrative function is the materialization of the State’s goals, the inclusion of facts, omissions, and de facto actions among its forms of manifestation does not appear to be compatible with its constitutive principles, particularly with the fulfillment of the public interest. This article aims to review its specific manifestations to clarify their conceptual articulation. The methodology applied is rational reconstruction, as it examines the internal consistency of the categories used to identify concrete instances in legal practice. The text argues that, conceptually speaking, facts, omissions, and de facto actions are not autonomous expressions of the administrative function. Not every legal situation is based on administrative action",Administrative function; acts; facts; operations; omissions; de facto actions. 4 Díkaion - eISSN 2027-5366 / e3514 La doctrina sobre las formas de exteriorización de la función administrativa en la cultura jurídica,marcadores,form exteriorizacion no parece compatible sus principi constitutiv,dikaion eissn 2027-5366 ano 40 vol 35 num chia colombia 2026 e3514 duber armando celis vela abstract in administrative law doctrine usually holds that the administrative function is expressed through acts operations facts omissions and facto actions if one assum that the administrative function is the materialization of the state goals the inclusion of facts omissions and facto actions among its forms of manifestation does 