2027-5366,Díkaion35(1)_25871-LaDoctrina_7_PDF_Dúber+Armando+Celis+Vela.pdf,Díkaion35(1)_25871-LaDoctrina_7_PDF_Dúber+Armando+Celis+Vela_0,en,cción del interés general. El objetivo de este artículo es revisar sus manifestaciones específicas en aras de evaluar su articulación,"In administrative law, doctrine usually holds that the administrative function is expressed through acts, operations, facts, omissions, and de facto actions. If one assumes that the administrative function is the materialization of the State’s goals, the inclusion of facts, omissions, and de facto actions among its forms of manifestation does not appear to be compatible with its constitutive principles, particularly with the fulfillment of the public interest. This article aims to review its specific manifestations to clarify their conceptual articulation. The methodology applied is rational reconstruction, as it examines the internal consistency of the categories used to identify concrete instances in legal practice. The text argues that, conceptually speaking, facts, omissions, and de facto actions are not autonomous expressions of the administrative function. Not every legal situation is based on administrative action",Administrative function; acts; facts; operations; omissions; de facto actions. 4 Díkaion - eISSN 2027-5366 / e3514 La doctrina sobre las formas de exteriorización de la función administrativa en la cultura jurídica,marcadores,ccion del inter general el objetivo de este articulo es revisar sus manifestacion especifica en aras de evaluar su articulacion,administrative law doctrine usually hold administrative function express through acts oper fact omission de facto action if one assum administrative function material state goal inclusion fact omission de facto action among its form manifestation does not appear compatible its constitutive principl particularly fulfillment public interest article aims review its specific manifest clarify their conceptual articulation methodology a