2027-5846,2__Permanencia_académica.pdf,2__Permanencia_académica_0,en,"académico, situación económica, asistencia y","Academic persistence is a critical quality indicator in higher education, closely linked to institutional performance and student academic success. This article presents an applied study conducted at the Institución Universitaria de Envigado (IUE), aimed at analyzing factors associated with student dropout and at developing and validating a predictive model based on logistic regression. Academic, sociodemographic, and behavioral variables were integrated into the analysis (age, academic average, economic situation, attendance, and employment status). The results show that academic average and attendance are the most significant predictors of persistence, while economic situation and employment increase the probability of dropout. The model achieved solid performance metrics (AUC = 0.85; accuracy = 0.86; sensitivity = 0.87; specificity = 0.85), demonstrating its relevance for institutional processes of academic support and risk management. Institutional implications, limitations, and future lines of work related to educational analytics and early-warning systems are discussed","Academic persistence, student dropout, higher education, educational analytics, logistic regression, academic risk prediction, socioeconomic factors, academic performance, early-warning systems, statistical models. Ingenierías USBMed | Vol. 17, No 1 | Enero–Junio–2026 | Medellín–Colombia | L-ISSN 2027-5846 6 6 𝜋 A. F. Hernández Marulanda, D. Rangel, A. M. Cárdenas y Y. Londoño",marcadores,academico situacion economica asistencia,academic persistence critical quality indicator higher education closely link institutional performance student academic succes article present appli study conduct institucion universitaria de envigado iue aimed analyz factor associat student dropout develop validat predictive model based logistic regression academic sociodemographic behavioral variabl i