2027-5846,3__Arquitectura_multicore.pdf,3__Arquitectura_multicore_0,en,eclarado que no existen conflictos de intereses.,This work presents a model for evaluating the performance of a parallel simulation of multi-core computer architectures. The model is built upon the computational costs of a sequential simulation compared to the computational complexity of its parallel counterpart. An analysis of the number of cores in the simulated architecture is conducted as the most important variable in this study. The model allows for establishing how many cores the parallelized simulation outperforms the sequential counterpart. The model is validated with results from experiments that measured the latencies of sequential and parallel simulators with real test programs,"Simulation model, computational parallelization, computational cost, computer architecture. Ingenierías USBMed | Vol. 17, No 1 | Enero–Junio–2026 | Medellín–Colombia | L-ISSN 2027-5846 14 14 𝜋 J. B. Buitrago Paniagua",marcadores,eclarado que no existen conflicto de interes,work present model evaluat performance parallel simulation multi-core computer architectur model built upon computational cost sequential simulation compar computational complexity its parallel counterpart analysi number core simulat architecture conduct most important variable study model allow establish how many core paralleliz simulation outperform sequential counterpart model validat result experiment measur latenci sequential parallel simulator real test program,simulation model computational parallel computational cost computer architecture ingenieria usbm vol 17 no enero-junio-2026 medellin-colombia l-issn 2027-5846 14 14 buitrago paniagua,eclarado que no existen conflicto de interes work present model evaluat performance parallel simulation multi-core computer architectur model built upon computational cost sequential simulation compar computational complexity its parallel counterpart analysi number core simulat architecture conduct 