2027-5846,4__Implementación_de_herramientas.pdf,4__Implementación_de_herramientas_0,en,dos para proponer,"The primary objective of this research is to identify the causes of the lack of standardization in the production processes of food processing companies, with a specific focus on the production of chicken skewers. The issue addressed centers on the high variability observed in production times, material usage, product weight, final quality, and packaging and storage stages. Using a methodology based on direct observation, detailed process characterization, and rigorous data recording, the study analyzes the deviations that affect the value chain prior to shipment to customers or distribution centers. Using industrial engineering tools and operational excellence frameworks such as Lean Six Sigma and Kaizen, the study organizes the collected data to propose technical solutions for the identified opportunities for improvement. The analysis reveals that productivity is directly impacted by factors such as human talent, machinery, work methods, and metrics. It concludes that processes with a high manual component are inherently susceptible to variations; therefore, the improvement proposal emphasizes the need to adopt automated or semi-automated processes to mitigate deviations. Although the final implementation rests with the company, the scope of this work provides a clear roadmap for optimizing direct costs, selling prices, and service levels, ensuring that the transition toward a culture of continuous improvement strengthens profitability and operational efficiency in a highly competitive market","Systematic literature review, serious games, vocational guidance, engineering, higher education. Ingenierías USBMed | Vol. 17, No 1 | Enero–Junio–2026 | Medellín–Colombia | L-ISSN 2027-5846 20 20 𝜋 R. M. Usuga Rueda, V. Rodríguez Bonilla, P. A. Suarez Agudelo y M. C. Correa Vera",marcadores,dos para proponer,primary objective research identify caus lack standard product