2027-7458,Dialnet-ParaQueHacerAnalisisCriticoDelDiscurso-10837058.pdf,Dialnet-ParaQueHacerAnalisisCriticoDelDiscurso-10837058_0,en,"ultados de una investigación propia sobre el discurso político, legislativo e institucional","This paper is framed within the framework of Critical Discourse Analysis (CDA) and proposes three interrelated objectives. First, we problematize the social and political function of CDA from a reflection on the concept of “critique” in one of its major referents, Norman Fairclough. Our hypothesis is that the emancipatory objectives that the CDA claims (and should) have, as proposed by Fairclough himself, are weakening as he modifies his vision of the characteristics that the “critical” component of research within this theoretical current should have and moves away from its historical materialist | 3 Rocío Flax Enero - junio 2026 | Vol. 16 | No. 30 | Analecta Política roots. Therefore, as a second objective, we present Alejandro Raiter's proposal and suggest that it constitutes, within the ACD itself, a theoretical alternative that reinforces the objectives of Fairclough's first formulations, since it explicitly states the role that analysts should play in social transformations from a materialist linguistic point of view. Finally, as a third objective, we seek to demonstrate the productivity of this proposal by presenting the results of our own research on the political, legislative and institutional discourse on migrants in Argentina. We conclude that the discourse of multiculturalism is part of the dominant discourse together with the discourse that criminalizes migrants. The discourses that seek to value the presence of migrants do so from a utilitarian viewpoint, constituting an opposing discourse that reinforces the dominant discourse and fails to generate a discursive transformation. Finally, we outline some characteristics that an emerging discourse could have and reflect on the importance of this type of proposals by analysts",Critical Discourse Analysis - Historical Materialism - Frankfurt School - Neoliberalism - Common Sense - Dominant Discourse - Emergent Discourse - Discursive Transformation - Political Discourse - Migrants - Political Discourse,marcadores,ultado de una investigacion propia sobre el discurso politico legislativo institucional,paper fram within framework critical discourse analysi cda propos three interrelat objectiv first we problematize social political function cda reflection concept critique one its major referent norman fairclough our hypothesi emancipatory objectiv cda claim should have propos fairclough himself weaken he modifi his vision characteristic critical component research within theoretical current should have move away its historical materialist rocio flax enero junio 2026 vol 16 no 30 analecta politica root therefore second objective we present alejandro raiter proposal suggest constitut within acd itself theoretical alternative reinforc objectiv fairclough first formul since explicitly stat role analyst should play social transform materialist linguistic point view finally third objective we seek demonstrate productivity proposal present result our own research political legislative institutional discourse migrant argentina we conclude discourse multiculturalism part dominant discourse together discourse criminaliz migrant discours seek value presence migrant do so utilitarian viewpoint constitut oppos discourse reinforc dominant discourse fail generate discursive transformation finally we outline some characteristic emerg discourse could have reflect importance type proposal analyst,critical discourse analysi historical materialism frankfurt school neoliberalism common sense dominant discourse emergent discourse discursive transformation political discourse migrant political discourse,ultado de una investigacion propia sobre el discurso politico legislativo institucional paper fram within framework critical discourse analysi cda propos three interrelat ob