2027-7458,Dialnet-SufrimientoAmbiental-10837065.pdf,Dialnet-SufrimientoAmbiental-10837065_0,en,"prende la lingüística sistémico funcional, la geografía humana, la historia y el análisis","The political and economic reforms implemented during the dictatorship of Augusto Pinochet (1973–1990) in Chile led to the approval of the Water Code, which established water as a markettradeable resource. This legal framework has shaped the foundations of current debates on the prolonged drought affecting north-central Chile since 2011. The purpose of this article is to examine the intersubjective perspectives that different social actors construct around the water crisis and the ways in which these stances are connected to discursive macro-strategies that either support or challenge inherited neoliberal practices. From an interdisciplinary approach that brings together systemic functional linguistics, human geography, history, and critical discourse analysis, the study analyzes two types of sources: interviews with farmers in the municipality of Combarbalá and documents produced by the think tanks Instituto Libertad y Desarrollo and the Centro de 1 Posicionamientos convergentes o divergentes de miembros de una comunidad en relación con las realidades sociales a las que están expuestos los miembros de comunidades socioculturales (White, 2003; 2010). 2 Centros de estudios interdisciplinarios para brindar asesoramiento respecto de temas de interés a gobiernos y entidades públicas o privadas. En muchos casos, estos organismos pueden estar vinculados a partidos políticos. | 3 María Cristina Arancibia Enero - junio 2026 | Vol. 16 | No. 30 | Analecta Política Estudios Públicos. The findings reveal a significant contrast in the role that dialogic contraction assumes in each actor’s voice. While the farmers’ testimonies contract dialogical space to express collective resistance in the face of water scarcity, the texts produced by the think tanks reinforce the legitimacy of water rights privatization through dialogic contraction and the topos of disaster","drought, intersubjective perspectives, discursive macro-strategies, local knowledge, expert knowledge",marcadores,prende la linguistica sistemico funcional la geografia humana la historia el analisi,political economic reform implement during dictatorship augusto pinochet 1973-1990 chile led approval water code which establish water markettradeable resource legal framework has shap found current debat prolong drought affect north-central chile since 2011 purpose article examine intersubjective perspectiv different social actor construct around water crisi ways which these stanc connect discursive macro-strategi either support challenge inherit neoliberal practic interdisciplinary approach bring together systemic functional linguistic human geography history critical discourse analysi study analyz two type sourc interview farmer municipality combarbala document produc think tank instituto libertad desarrollo centro de posicionamiento convergent divergent de miembro de una comunidad en relacion con las realidad social las que estan expuesto los miembro de comunidad sociocultural white 2003 2010 centro de estudio interdisciplinario para brindar asesoramiento respecto de tema de inter gobierno entidad publica privada en mucho caso esto organismo pueden estar vinculado partido politico maria cristina arancibia enero junio 2026 vol 16 no 30 analecta politica estudio publico finding reveal significant contrast role dialogic contraction assum each actor voice while farmer testimoni contract dialogical space expres collective resistance face water scarcity text produc think tank reinforce legitimacy water right privat through dialogic contraction topo disaster,drought intersubjective perspectiv discursive macro-strategi local knowledge expert knowledge,prende la linguistica sistemico funcional la geografia humana la historia el analisi political economic reform implement during dictatorship augusto pinochet 