2027-7822,"Vol14,02_AO_Art01.pdf","Vol14,02_AO_Art01_0",en,"nto con hiperplasia en 23 (50%), vasos","Objective: To identify the histopathologic, demographic and clinical characteristics of periapical cyst in patients treated at the endodontic postgraduate course. Materials and Methods: A descriptive observational study was carried out. Forty-six biopsies of patients with histopathological diagnosis of periapical cyst during the period 2016-2021who underwent endodontic microsurgery were analyzed. For data collection, variables were categorized according to sex, age, type of tooth, maxilla, presence of fistula, tooth mobility and according to histopathological findings. The data were organized in Excel and exported to the statistical program SPSS version 22.0 in Windows for the statistical analysis of the absolute frequencies of the categorical data. Their respective microscopic interpretation and diagnosis was performed in the oral and maxillofacial pathology service of the Faculty of Dentistry of the National University (FOUN). Results: In the study the most affected group was male with an age range of 30-49 years with 43.47%, the most affected teeth were the molars 52.17%, more frequently in the upper jaw 51%, 30.46% presented fistula, the majority of the teeth presented grade 1 mobility. The histopathological findings of the 46 periapical cysts presented different histological characteristics, 100% evidenced stratified squamous lining epithelium with hyperplasia in 23 (50%), blood vessels in 29 (63.04%), acanthosis in 31 (67.39), fragmented epithelium in 20 (43.47%), devitalized bone spicules and dystrophic calcifications in 17 (36.95%), among others. The inflammatory infiltrate observed was predominantly severe/chronic (43.47%), severe/mixed (34.78%), moderate (21.75%). Conclusion: The most common histopathological findings in periapical cysts were stratified squamous epithelium, acanthosis and inflammatory infiltrate, suggesting that these cysts are associated with inflammatory and reactive processes. There is a greater predisposition of the male sex, and the presence of fistula and dental mobility may be related to the severity of the lesion",Histopathology; Periapical disease; Odontogenic cysts; Root cyst; Periapical cyst; Microsurgery. 1. Especialista en Endodoncia. Universidad Católica de Cuenca contacto: ferodriguezr@unal.edu.co. https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7253-3162 2. Especialista en Cirugía Oral y Maxilofacial. Especialista en Patología Oral. Magíster en Educación.Universidad Nacional de Colombia contacto: cppenav@unal.edu,marcadores,nto con hiperplasia en 23 50 vaso,objective identify histopathologic demographic clinical characteristic periapical cyst patient treat endodontic postgraduate course material method descriptive observational study carri out forty-six biopsi patient histopathological diagnosi periapical cyst during period 2016-2021who underwent endodontic microsurgery analyz data collection variabl categoriz accord sex age type tooth maxilla presence fistula tooth mobility accord histopathological finding data organiz excel export statistical program spss version 22 window statistical analysi absolute frequenci categorical data their respective microscopic interpretation diagnosi perform oral maxillofacial pathology service faculty dentistry national university foun result study most affect group male age range 30-49 year 43 47 most affect teeth molar 52 17 more frequently upper jaw 51 30 46 present fistula majority teeth present grade mobility histopathological finding 46 periapical cyst present different histological characteristic 100 evidenc stratifi squamou lining epithelium hyperplasia 23 50 blood vessel 29 63 04 acanthosi 31 67 39 fragment epithelium 20 43 47 devitaliz bone spicul dystrophic calcific 17 36 95 among other inflammatory infiltrate observ predominantly severe chronic 43 47 severe mixed 34 78 moderate 21 75 conclusion most common histopathological finding periapical cyst stratifi squa