2027-7822,"Vol14,02_AO_Art04 (1).pdf","Vol14,02_AO_Art04 (1)_0",en,"a los 3 meses de seguimiento (p<0,001). El grupo tratado con el probiótico durante","Background:Some probiotics could prevent or reduce the development of gingivoperiodontal diseases. Certain Lactobacillus strains inhibit the development of microorganisms related to them, such as Treponema dentícola, Tannarella forsythia or A. actinomycetemcomitans. Aim: To evaluate the clinical effects produced by repeated ingestion of Lactobacillus rhamnosus as the only probiotic in teeth of patients with periodontal diseases. Materials and methods: An experimental, simple randomized and controlled clinical study was carried out on 20 patients with periodontal diseases. All received periodontal scaling and planing therapy. The treated group received a daily capsule of the probiotic p.o. for 3 months. Periodontal bleeding indices, probing depth, and attachment loss were measured at 0, 30, 60, and 90 days.Results: Regarding bleeding and probing depth, both the control and the treated group improved after 3 months of treatment, compared to their pretreatment value (p<0.001). The group treated with the probiotic for 3 months decreased the percentage of bleeding compared to the control. The variables bleeding and treatment group are associated from a statistical point of view (Chi2= 13.998; p< 0.001). The relative risk (1.12; 95% CI 1.055-1.190) indicates that the treated group has a 12% greater probability than the control of preventing bleeding on probing. There were no statistically significant differences in probing depth or tooth attachment loss between control and treated. No relevant adverse effects were detected either.Conclusions: The complementary use of probiotics during periodontal therapy produces clinical improvements by reducing bleeding in teeth","Probiotics; Periodontal diseases; Lactobacillus rhamnosus. 1. Odontóloga contacto: patriciaherreraod@gmail.com https://orcid.org/0009-0007-2070-4098 2. Doctora en Bioquímica contacto: minivirjg@gmail.com https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9489-8370 3. Doctora en Ciencias químicas, orientación Bioquímica contacto: cristina.perez.acad@gmail.com https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0538-4819 4. contacto:mariais",marcadores,los mese de seguimiento 001 el grupo tratado con el probiotico durante,background some probiotic could prevent reduce development gingivoperiodontal diseas certain lactobacillu strain inhibit development microorganism relat them such treponema denticola tannarella forsythia actinomycetemcomitan aim evaluate clinical effect produc repeat ingestion lactobacillu rhamnosu only probiotic teeth patient periodontal diseas material method experimental simple randomiz controll clinical study carri out 20 patient periodontal diseas all receiv periodontal scal plan therapy treat group receiv daily capsule probiotic month periodontal bleed indic prob depth attachment loss measur 30 60 90 days result regard bleed prob depth both control treat group improv after month treatment compar their pretreatment value 001 group treat probiotic month decreas percentage bleed compar control variabl bleed treatment group associat statistical point view chi2 13 998 001 relative risk 12 95 ci 055-1 190 indicat treat group has 12 greater probability than control prevent bleed prob there no statistically significant differenc prob depth tooth attachment loss between control treat no relevant adverse effect detect either conclusion complementary use probiotic during periodontal therapy produc clinical improvement reduc bleed teeth,probiotic periodontal diseas lactobacillu rhamnosu odontologa contacto patriciaherreraod gmail com http orcid org 0009-0007-2070-4098 doctora en bioquimica contacto minivirjg gmail com http orcid org 0000-0002-9489-8370 doctora en ciencia quimica orientacion bioquimica contacto cristina perez acad gmail com http orcid org 0000-0003-0538-4819 contacto mariai,los mese de seguimiento 001 el grupo tratado con el probiotico durante background some probiotic could prevent reduce development gingivoperiodontal diseas certain lactobacillu strain inhibit development microorganism relat them such treponema denticola tannarella forsythia actinomycetemcomitan aim evaluate clinical effect produc repeat ingestion lactobacillu rhamnosu only probiotic teeth patient periodontal diseas material method experimental simple randomiz controll clinical study carri out 20 patient periodontal diseas all receiv periodontal scal plan therapy treat group receiv daily capsule probiotic month periodontal bleed indic prob depth attachment loss measur 30 60 90 days result regard bleed prob depth both control treat group improv after month treatment compar their pretreatment value 001 group treat probiotic month decreas percentage bleed compar control variabl bleed treatment group associat statistical point view chi2 13 998 001 relative risk 12 95 ci 055-1 190 indicat treat group has 12 greater probability than control prevent bleed prob there no statistically significant differenc prob depth tooth attachment loss between control treat no relevant adverse effect detect either conclusion complementary use probiotic during periodontal therapy produc clinical improvement reduc bleed teeth probiotic periodontal diseas lactobacillu rhamnosu odontologa contacto patriciaherreraod gmail com http orcid org 0009-0007-2070-4098 doctora en bioquimica contacto minivirjg gmail com http orcid org 0000-0002-9489-8370 doctora en ciencia quimica orientacion bioquimica contacto cristina perez acad gmail com http orcid org 0000-0003-0538-4819 contacto mariai,1.0.0,fba85ce2dcbf895e
2027-7822,"Vol14,02_AO_Art04.pdf","Vol14,02_AO_Art04_0",es,Patricia Herrera 1,"Antecedentes:Algunos probióticos podrían prevenir o reducir el desarrollo de enfer medades gingivo-periodontales. Ciertas cepas de Lactobacillus inhiben el crecimiento de microorganismos como Treponema dentícola, Tannarella forsythia o A. actinomyce temcomitans.Objetivo:Evaluar los efectos clínicos producidos por la ingesta repetida de una dosis exacta de Lactobacillus rhamnosus como único probiótico en dientes de pacientes con enfermedades periodontales. Materiales y métodos: Se realizó un estudio clínico experimental, aleatorio simple y controlado de 20 pacientes con enfer medades periodontales. Todos recibieron terapia periodontal de raspado y alisado. El grupo tratado recibió durante 3 meses una cápsula diaria del probiótico p.o. Se midieron los índices periodontales de sangrado, profundidad de sondaje y pérdida de inserción a los 0, 30, 60 y 90 días. Resultados: Respecto del sangrado y profundidad de sondaje, tanto el control como el tratado con Lactobacillus rhamnosus mejoraron a los 3 meses de seguimiento (p<0,001). El grupo tratado con el probiótico durante tres meses disminuyó el porcentaje de sangrado con respecto al control. El análisis estadístico muestra que las variables sangrado y grupo de tratamiento están asociadas (Chi2= 13,998; p< 0,001). El riesgo relativo (1,12; IC 95% 1,055-1,190) indica que el grupo tratado tiene una probabilidad 12 % mayor que el control de prevenir sangrado al son daje. No hubo diferencias estadísticamente significativas en profundidad de sondaje ni pérdida de inserción dentaria entre control y tratado durante 3 meses. Tampoco se detectaron efectos adversos relevantes en ninguno de los grupos.Conclusiones: El uso complementario de probióticos durante la terapia periodontal produce mejoría clínica al disminuir el sangrado en dientes",probióticos; enfermedades periodontales; Lactobacillus rhamnosus,marcadores,patricia herrera,antecedent algun probio