2145-132X,"historelo,+2145132X326_Monroy.pdf","historelo,+2145132X326_Monroy_0",en,ivo fundamental es mostrar cómo en un contexto de traslados se desarrollaron las cofradías en el pueblo y cómo en,"This article analyzes the development of the brotherhoods at the Suratá village of indigenous people before and after the Bourbon reforms in the eighteenth century based on the information found in the Books of the Santo Ecce Homo and Santísimo Sacramento Brotherhoods and other primary sources. This work initially describes the process of relocating the indigenous people from their original settlements in order to build the Suratá village of indigenous people, a process that occurred during the seventeenth century, with the corresponding assignment of communal land for indigenous reservations. Then, this work studies the process of aggregation of these villages during the eighteenth century as a consequence of the changes implemented in the regional production system in order to foster land circulation. The main objective of this work is to show the development of brotherhoods within this context of relocation occurring at the Suratá village of indigenous people, and how the Chitareros indigenous community managed to ethnically reorganize themselves within this context. It is concluded that the relocation dynamics marginalized the indigenous element inside their Brotherhoods and how poor neighbors, Spaniards and white people took control of these Brotherhoods as a result of the Bourbon gift-giving policies that promoted the organization of the land into parishes and the deprivation of the communal land initially planned for indigenous reservations","relocation; aggregations; brotherhoods; indigenous villages; reservation; neighbors. Transferir para desapropriar: a marginalização dos índios Chitareros do vale de Suratá das suas confrarias em el Virreinato de Nueva Granada, 1752-1795",marcadores,ivo fundamental es mostrar como en un contexto de traslado se desarrollaron las cofradia en el pueblo como en,article analyz development brotherhood surata village indigenou people before after bourbon reform eighteenth century based information found book santo ecce homo santisimo sacramento brotherhood other primary sourc work initially describ proces relocat indigenou people their original settlement order build surata village indigenou people proces occurr during seventeenth century correspond assignment communal land indigenou reserv then work studi proces aggregation these villag during eighteenth century consequence chang implement regional production system order foster land circulation main objective work show development brotherhood within context relocation occurr surata village indigenou people how chitarero indigenou community manag ethnically reorganize themselv within context conclud relocation dynamic marginaliz indigenou element inside their brotherhood how poor neighbor spaniard white people took control these brotherhood result bourbon gift-giv polici promot organ land into parish deprivation communal land initially plann indigenou reserv,relocation aggreg brotherhood indigenou villag reservation neighbor transferir para desapropriar marginalizacao dos indio chitarero do vale de surata das suas confraria em el virreinato de nueva granada 1752-1795,ivo fundamental es mostrar como en un contexto de traslado se desarrollaron las cofradia en el pueblo como en article analyz development brotherhood surata village indigenou people before after bourbon reform eighteenth century based information found book santo ecce homo santisimo sacramento brotherhood other primary sourc work initially describ proces relocat indigenou people their original settlement order build surata village indigenou people proces occurr during seventeenth century correspond assignment communal land indigenou reserv then work studi proces aggregation these villag during eighteenth century consequence chang implement regional production system order foster lan