siete especi abej sin aguijon determinaron humedad ph acidez total conductividad electrica actividad diastasa hidroximetilfurfural ceniz mineral mg mn na zn solid insolubl azucar reductor color adem evaluo actividad antioxidante fenol total perfil acid organic inocuidad evaluo cuanto metal pesad cu cr cd pb as hg microbiologica grup seleccionad muestr fueron tratad termica evaluar efecto sobre propiedad quimic microbiologic resultad miel mostraron alta variabilidad dentro entre especi abej respecto miel apis mellifera presentaron mayor contenido humedad 26 01 mayor acidez 49 59 15 68 meq kg ph 68 27 mayor contenido solid insolubl similar contenido azucar total 62 85 32 pero menor contenido azucar reductor 50 77 21 perfil acid organic revelo destacable contenido acido ascorbico todas miel 47 1-233 mg 100g relacionado actividad antioxidante observada tambien encontro acido lactico consistente presencia bacteri acido lactic sus posibl propiedad probiotic no detecto contaminacion plomo arsenico cadmio ni mercurio confirmo ausencia microorganism patogen trat termic afectaron diferencial bacteri lactic acido ascorbico tanto potencial funcional conclusion esta primera evaluacion integral calidad miel abej sin aguijon piedemonte amazonico colombiano destaca perfil bioactivo unico inocuidad contribuyendo desarrollo sostenible region bacteri acido lactic meliponicultura acid organic composicion miel pote desarrollo sostenible journal vitae https revist udea edu co index php vitae volume 33 number 01 article 361981 physicochemical bioactive and safety properti of honey produced by stingless bees in the colombian amazon piedmont conservation while providing economic and social development oppo,1.0.0,0fffecc11e387dd7
2145-2660,Vitae+33-1++362612+(2).pdf,Vitae+33-1++362612+(2)_0,en,rsidad Nacional Abierta y a,"Background: In Latin America, approximately 4,732 native potato varieties have been recorded, representing an autochthonous product that plays a crucial role in food security and nutrition for the population. However, there remains a need to explore new forms of consumption, such as native potato flour, and to recognize its technological potential and antioxidant capacity, positioning it as an alternative and innovative ingredient for the food industry. Objective: This research evaluated the technofunctional properties, color, and antioxidant capacity of six varieties of native potato flours. Methods: Six native potato varieties (Solanum tuberosum): Yana Shungo, Puca Shungo, Alcarrosa, Quincha, Valvanera, and Sangre de Toro, were studied. For analysis, the samples were dried and ground. Water and oil absorption capacities, swelling power, color parameters, total phenolic content, and antioxidant capacity (DPPH, ABTS, and FRAP) were determined. Results: The Puca Shungo variety exhibited the highest water absorption capacity (4.61 ± 0.28 g/g), while Valvanera showed the greatest swelling power (5.45 ± 0.40 mL/g). Sangre de Toro presented the highest oil absorption capacity (2.75 ± 0.03 g/g). Regarding color parameters, Valvanera displayed the highest lightness (L* = 78.91 ± 0.81), whereas Puca Shungo and Alcarrosa exhibited intense yellow coloration (b* = 21.25 ± 2.77 and 22.76 ± 2.67, respectively). In contrast, Sangre de Toro showed an intense red coloration (a* = 21.65 ± 1.32) and lower lightness (L* = 48.57 ± 1.73). Furthermore, the Sangre de Toro variety demonstrated significantly high antioxidant properties, with antioxidant capacities of 5.386 ± 0.209 µmol TE/g DM (ABTS), 3.528 ± 0.153 µmol TE/g DM (DPPH), and 5.104 ± 0.144 µmol TE/g DM (FRAP), as well as a total phenolic content of 1.442 ± 0.06 mg GAE/g DM. The Yana Shungo variety ranked second in terms of antioxidant capacity. Conclusion: The flours obtained from the evaluated varieties exhibit high antioxidant content and high water and oil absorption capacities. This study contributes to the recognition and characterization of native potatoes cultivated in the Cundiboyacense region of Colombia for their use as ingredients in the food industry","Antioxidant capacity, total phenolics, water absorption capacity, oil absorption capacity, swelling power, anthocyanins. ORIGINAL RESEARCH Published 26 January 2026 DOI: https://doi.org/10.17533/udea.vitae.v33n1a362612 2 Journal Vitae | https://revistas.udea.edu.co/index.php/vitae Volume 33 | Number 01 | Article 362612 Ruth Mary Benavides-Guevara, Yuneidys Mariet Oñate Perpiñán, Ibeth Rodríguez",marcadores,rsidad nacional abierta,background latin america approximately 732 native potato varieti have been record represent autochthonou product play crucial role food security nutrition population however there remain need explore new form consumption such native potato flour recognize its technological potential antioxidant capacity position alternative innovative ingredient food industry objective research evaluat technofunctional properti color antioxidant capacity six varieti native potato flour method six native potato varieti solanum tuberosum yana shungo puca shungo alcarrosa quincha valvanera sangre de toro studi analysi sampl dried ground water oil absorption capaciti swell power color parameter total phenolic content antioxidant capacity dpph abts frap determin result puca shungo variety exhibit highest water absorption capacity 61 28 while valvanera show greatest swell power 45 40 ml sangre de toro present highest oil absorption capacity 75 03 regard color parameter valvanera display highest lightnes 78 91 81 wherea puca shungo alcarrosa exhibit intense yellow coloration 21 25 77 22 76 67 respectively contrast sangre de toro show intense red coloration 21 65 32 lower lightnes 48 57 73 furthermore sangre de toro variety demonstrat