2145-2660,Vitae+33-1++362906.pdf,Vitae+33-1++362906_0,en,"a Universidad Central del Ecuador,","Background: Jackfruit is valued worldwide for its nutritional content. It is cultivated in tropical climates and primarily intended for local consumption; however, a significant proportion of the fruit is lost due to inadequate postharvest management and underutilization. Objective: To evaluate the effect of conventional (CF) and vacuum frying (VF) at different temperatures and times on the quality of jackfruit pulp chips, as an alternative agro-industrial product in cultivation regions. Methods: Color parameters were analyzed by colorimetry using L*, a*, and b* values; fat content was determined by multiple extractions with petroleum ether; and the moisture content of the final product was measured by gravimetry. Consumer acceptance level of the best treatments was assessed using a hedonic scale administered to 150 untrained evaluators. Results: In both processes, increased temperature and time significantly affected chip properties (p < 0.05), leading to reduced lightness (L*) and yellowness (b*), along with increased redness (a*) and oil absorption. Frying at 140 °C for 5 min (CF) and at 110 °C for 8 min (VF) resulted in chips with desirable color attributes, lower oil uptake, favorable sensory acceptance, and preservation of most fruit properties. Conclusions: VF provides superior final product quality. The chips exhibit favorable sensory acceptance and are a nutritious, viable snack option for production","Vacuum frying, Artocarpus heterophyllus, Fruit quality, Sensory analysis, Color parameters",marcadores,universidad central del ecuador,background jackfruit valu worldwide its nutritional content cultivat tropical climat primarily intend local consumption however significant proportion fruit lost due inadequate postharvest management underutil objective evaluate effect conventional cf vacuum frying vf different temperatur time quality jackfruit pulp chip alternative agro-industrial product cultivation region method color parameter analyz colorimetry using valu fat content determin multiple extraction petroleum ether moisture content final product measur gravimetry consumer acceptance level best treatment assess using hedonic scale administer 150 untrain evaluator result both process increas temperature time significantly affect chip properti 05 lead reduc lightnes yellownes along increas rednes oil absorption frying 140 degc min cf 110 degc min vf result chip desirable color attribut lower oil uptake favorable sensory acceptance preservation most fruit properti conclusion vf provid superior final product quality chip exhibit favorable sensory acceptance nutritiou viable snack option production,vacuum frying artocarpu heterophyllu fruit quality sensory analysi color parameter,universidad central del ecuador background jackfruit valu worldwide its nutritional content cultivat tropical climat primarily intend local consumption however significant proportion fruit lost due inadequate postharvest management underutil objective evaluate effect conventional cf vacuum frying vf different temperatur time quality jackfruit pulp chip alternative agro-industrial product cultivation region method color parameter analyz colorimetry using valu fat content determin multiple extraction petroleum ether moisture content final product measur gravimetry consumer acceptance level best treatment assess using hedonic scale administer 150 untrain evaluator result both process increas temperature time significantly affect chip properti 05 lead reduc lightnes yellownes along increas rednes oil absorption frying 140 degc min cf 110 degc min vf result chip desirable color attribut lower oil uptake favorable sensory acceptance preservation most fruit properti conclusion vf provid superior final product quality chip exhibit favorable sensory acceptance nutritiou viable snack option production vacuum frying artocarpu heterophyllu fruit quality sensory analysi