2145-2660,Vitae+33-1++363328+(3).pdf,Vitae+33-1++363328+(3)_0,en,"Engineering, National University of","Background: Snacks are highly appreciated by consumers of all ages; however, most commercial products are high in calories and low in nutritional value. This has generated interest in developing more nutritious and functional snacks by combining ingredients rich in protein and bioactive compounds with technologies such as germination and extrusion. Objective: The main goal of this study was to develop nutritionally enhanced and functional extruded snacks from germinated Andean grains and freeze-dried Cavia porcellus meat (FCPM). Methods: Three formulations were studied with rice flour (20%), germinated quinoa flour (48% to 44%), germinated amaranth flour (30%), and FCPM (2% to 6%). The formulations with 16% moisture were processed in a twin-screw extruder at 150 °C and 300 rpm. The extruded snacks were characterized by their protein content, total phenolic content (TPC), apparent density (DA), expansion index (EI), water absorption index (WAI), and water solubility index (WSI). Results: The results showed that the addition of FCPM significantly increased (p < 0.05) the protein content (from 10.93 to 15.93 g/100g), DA (0.11 to 0.28 g/cm³), and decreased the EI (2.97 to 2.29) and WAI (5.47 to 3.91 g/g) compared to the control sample. Likewise, the TPC of extruded snacks (115.93 to 136.54 mg GAE/100g) was 4.5 times higher than the control. Conclusions: These findings underscored the potential of incorporating plant- and animalbased products to develop more nutritious, functional extruded snacks that help address food and nutritional insecurity","Sprouted Andean grains, Cavia porcellus; extrusion, protein snacks, nutritional safety",marcadores,engineer national university,background snack highly appreciat consumer all ages however most commercial product high calori low nutritional value has generat interest develop more nutritiou functional snack combin ingredient rich protein bioactive compound technologi such germination extrusion objective main goal study develop nutritionally enhanc functional extrud snack germinat andean grain freeze-dri cavia porcellu meat fcpm method three formul studi rice flour 20 germinat quinoa flour 48 44 germinat amaranth flour 30 fcpm formul 16 moisture process twin-screw extruder 150 degc 300 rpm extrud snack characteriz their protein content total phenolic content tpc apparent density da expansion index ei water absorption index wai water solubility index wsi result result show addition fcpm significantly increas 05 protein content 10 93 15 93 100g da 11 28 cm3 decreas ei 97 29 wai 47 91 compar control sample likewise tpc extrud snack 115 93 136 54 mg gae 100g time higher than control conclusion these finding underscor potential incorporat plant- animalbas product develop more nutritiou functional extrud snack help addres food nutritional insecurity,sprout andean grain cavia porcellu extrusion protein snack nutritional safety,engineer national university background snack highly appreciat consumer all ages however most commercial product high calori low nutritional value has generat interest develop more nutritiou functional snack combin ingredient rich protein bioactive compound technologi such germination extrusion objective main goal study develop nutritionally enhanc functional extrud snack germinat andean grain freeze-dri cavia porcellu meat fcpm method three formul studi rice flour 20 germinat quinoa flour 48 44 germinat amaranth flour 30 fcpm formul 16 moisture process twin-screw extruder 150 degc 300 rpm extrud snack characteriz their protein content total phenolic content tpc apparent density da expansion index ei water absorption index wai water solubility index wsi result result show addition fcpm significantly increas 05 protein content 10 93 15 93 100g da 11 28 cm3 decreas ei 97 29 wai 47 91 compar control sample likewise tpc extrud snack 115 93 136 54 mg gae 100g time higher than co