2145-2660,Vitae+33-2++363359+(1).pdf,Vitae+33-2++363359+(1)_0,en,"(GICTACAB), Guadalajara de Buga –","BACKGROUND: Specialty coffee is widely consumed worldwide due to its energizing properties. However, there is a constant demand for innovations and improvements that mitigate the potential side effects of coffee through the inclusion of natural ingredients such as lion’s mane mushroom (Hericium erinaceus). Despite this, no studies have yet evaluated different formulations from both physicochemical and sensory perspectives. OBJECTIVE: To provide an initial approach to the formulation of a specialty coffee nutraceutical beverage including lion’s mane mushroom based on the physicochemical characterization and sensory evaluation of different formulations. METHODS: Two formulations were developed with different concentrations of lion’s mane (0.5 and 1.0 %), which were characterized physicochemically (soluble solids, titratable acidity, color, and pH) and evaluated through sensory analysis (fragrance/aroma, flavor, aftertaste, acidity, body, uniformity, sweetness, cup profile, and balance). RESULTS: The physicochemical results remained within the expected ranges for specialty coffee. Sensory evaluation showed that both formulations enriched with mushroom (0.5 % and 1.0 %) were well received by consumers. CONCLUSION: The 0.5 and 1.0 % Hericium erinaceus mushroom-enriched formulations in specialty coffee allow for a proper balance between the coffee’s flavor notes and the characteristics imparted by the mushroom","Coffee formulation, Hericium erinaceus, lion’s mane mushroom, consumer acceptance, functional beverage. ORIGINAL RESEARCH Published 06 May 2026 DOI: https://doi.org/10.17533/udea.vitae.v33n2a363359 2 Journal Vitae | https://revistas.udea.edu.co/index.php/vitae Volume 33 | Number 02 | Article 363359 Karol Campiño, Laura Parra, Mayra A. Mora, Mike Sánchez, Maria J. Virviescas, Tulio A. Lerma 1. IN",marcadores,gictacab guadalajara de buga,background specialty coffee 