on dos formul diferent concentr melena leon cual caracterizaron fisicoquimica solid solubl acidez titulable color ph evaluaron trav analisis sensorial fragancia aroma sabor sabor residual acidez cuerpo uniformidad dulzor taza balance resultad resultad fisicoquimic mantuvieron dentro rang esperad cafe especialidad evaluacion sensorial mostro ambas formul enriquecid hong fueron bien aceptad consumidor conclusion formul hongo hericium erinaceus cafe especial permiten mantener equilibrio adecuado entre notas cafe caracteristic aportad hongo formulacion cafe hericium erinaceus hongo melena leon aceptacion consumidor bebida funcional journal vitae https revist udea edu co index php vitae volume 33 number 02 article 363359 sensory and physicochemical evaluation of specialty coffee formulations including lion mane mushroom hericium erinaceus materials and,1.0.0,03da8352b5be67bb
2145-2660,Vitae+33-2++363403+(2).pdf,Vitae+33-2++363403+(2)_0,en,Harriette del Rosario Duran-Sandoval,"BACKGROUND: The Allium cepa (onion) test is a sensitive tool for genotoxicity studies used worldwide to assess environmental contamination and potential toxicity of natural products. OBJECTIVES: To standardize and validate the experimental parameters of the Allium cepa assay and apply the standardized protocol to six ethanolic plant extracts from the Colombian Caribbean flora. METHODS: Key experimental variables were systematically evaluated: onion supplier, type of onion, environmental conditions, stimulation phase, water replacement, type of water, and Cd+2 concentration as positive control. Genotoxicity was assessed through the mitotic index (MI) and aberration index (AI) in root meristems. RESULTS: The optimal conditions were white onions from chain store P2, bottled drinking water with total replacement every 24 h, 24±1°C with indirect fluorescent lighting, a 72-h stimulation phase, nine onions per concentration, a 72-h exposure phase, and Cd+2 at 5 mg/L as positive control. Under these conditions, ethanolic extracts of Chenopodium ambrosioides, Momordica charantia, and Tabebuia ochracea induced significant genotoxic effects, whereas Crescentia cujete, Cordia dentata, and Heliotropium indicum showed no adverse effects. CONCLUSIONS: A reproducible and validated protocol was obtained for the Allium cepa genotoxicity assay. Its application revealed significant genotoxic activity in C. ambrosioides, M. charantia, and T. ochracea, as evidenced by decreased MI and increased AI, underscoring the need for further toxicological assessment of these species",Genotoxicity; Allium cepa; plant extracts,marcadores,harriette del rosario duran-sandoval,background allium cepa onion test sensitive tool genotoxicity studi used worldwide asses environmental contamination potential toxicity natural product objectiv standardize validate experimental parameter allium cepa assay apply standardiz protocol six ethanolic plant extract colombian caribbean flora method key experimental variabl systematically evaluat onion supplier type onion environmental condition stimulation phase water replacement type water cd concentration positive control genotoxicity assess through mitotic index mi aberration index ai root meristem result optimal condition white onion chain store p2 bottl drink water total replacement every 24 24 -1degc indirect fluorescent light 72-h stimulation phase nine onion per concentration 72-h exposure phase cd mg positive control under these condition ethanolic extract chenopodium ambrosioid momordica charantia tabebuia ochracea induc significant genotoxic effect wherea crescentia cujete cordia dentata heliotropium indicum show no adverse effect conclusion reproducible validat protocol obtain allium cepa genotoxicity assay its application reveal significant genotoxic activity ambrosioid charantia ochracea evidenc decreas mi increas ai underscor need further toxicological assessment these speci,genotoxicity allium cepa plant extract,harriette del rosario duran-sandoval background allium cepa onion test sensitive tool genotoxicity studi used worldwide asses environmental contamination potential toxicity natural product objectiv standardize validate experimental parameter allium cepa assay apply standardiz protocol six ethanolic plant extract colombian caribbean flora method key experimental variabl systematically evaluat onion supplier type onion environmental condition stimulation phase water replacement type water cd concentration positive control genotoxicity assess through mitotic index mi aberration index ai root meristem result optimal condition white onion chain store p2 bottl drink water total replacement every 24 24 -1degc indirect fluorescent light 72-h stimulation phase nine onion per concentration 72-h exposure phase cd mg positive control under these condition ethanolic extract chenopodium ambrosioid momordica charantia tabebuia ochracea induc significant genotoxic effect wherea crescentia cujete cordia dentata heliotropium indicum show no adverse effect conclusion reproducible validat protocol obtain allium cepa genotoxicity assay its application reveal significant genotoxic activity ambrosioid charantia ochracea evidenc decreas mi increas ai underscor need further toxicological assessment these speci genotoxicity allium cepa plant extract,1.0.0,08df7f6d913201b7
2145-2660,Vitae+33-2++363403+(2).pdf,Vitae+33-2++363403+(2)_0,es,"hite onions from chain store P2, bottled drinking water with total replacement","ANTECEDENTES: La prueba de Allium cepa (cebolla) es una herramienta sensible para estudios de genotoxicidad utilizada para evaluar la seguridad de productos naturales. OBJETIVOS: Estandarizar y validar los parámetros experimentales del ensayo de Allium cepa y aplicar el protocolo a seis extractos etanólicos de plantas de la flora del Caribe colombiano. MÉTODOS: Se evaluaron sistemáticamente las variables experimentales clave: proveedor y tipo de cebolla, condiciones ambientales, fase de estimulación, reemplazo y tipo de agua, y concentración de Cd+2 como control positivo. La genotoxicidad se evaluó mediante los índices mitótico (IM) y de aberraciones (IA) en meristemos radiculares. RESULTADOS: Las condiciones óptimas fueron: cebollas blancas del proveedor P2, agua potable embotellada (APE) con reemplazo total cada 24 h, 24±1°C con iluminación fluorescente indirecta, fase de estimulación de 72 h, nueve cebollas por concentración, fase de exposición de 72 h y Cd+2 a 5 mg/L como control positivo. Bajo estas condiciones, los extractos etanólicos de C. ambrosioides, M. charantia y T. ochracea indujeron efectos genotóxicos significativos, mientras que C. cujete, C. dentata y H. indicum no mostraron efectos adversos. CONCLUSIONES: Se obtuvo un protocolo reproducible y validado para el ensayo de genotoxicidad con Allium cepa. Su aplicación reveló actividad genotóxica significativa de C. ambrosioides, M. charantia y T. ochracea, evidenciada por disminución del IM e incremento del IA, lo que sustenta la necesidad de evaluaciones toxicológicas adicionales de estas especies","Genotoxicidad; Allium cepa; extractos de plantas. ORIGINAL RESEARCH Published 01 May 2026 DOI: https://doi.org/10.17533/udea.vitae.v33n2a363403 2 Journal Vitae | https://revistas.udea.edu.co/index.php/vitae Volume 33 | Number 02 | Article 363403 Harriette del Rosario Duran-Sandoval, Jorge Eliecer Espitia-Baena, Julián Javier Martínez Zambrano, José Angel Navas Passos, Luis Alfredo Utria-Acevedo,",marcadores,hite onions from chain store p2 bottled drinking water with total replacement,antecedent prueba allium cepa cebolla herramienta sensible estudi genotoxicidad utilizada evaluar seguridad product natural objetiv estandarizar validar parametr experimental ensayo allium cepa aplicar protocolo seis extract etanolic plant flora caribe colombiano metod evaluaron sistematica variabl experimental clave proveedor tipo cebolla condicion ambiental fase estimulacion reemplazo tipo agua concentracion cd como control positivo genotoxicidad evaluo mediante indic mitotico im aberr ia meristem radicular resultad condicion optim fueron ceboll blanc proveedor p2 agua potable embotellada ape reemplazo total cada 24 24 -1degc iluminacion fluorescente indirecta fase estimulacion 72 nueve ceboll concentracion fase exposicion 72 cd mg como control positivo bajo estas condicion extract etanolic ambrosioid charantia ochracea indujeron efect genotoxic significativ mientr cujete dentata indicum no mostraron efect advers conclusion obtuvo protocolo reproducible validado ensayo genotoxicidad allium cepa aplicacion revelo actividad genotoxica significativa ambrosioid charantia ochracea evidenciada disminucion im incremento ia sustenta necesidad evalu toxicologic adicional estas especi,genotoxicidad allium cepa extract plant original research published 01 may 2026 doi https doi org 10 17533 udea vitae v33n2a363403 journal vitae https revist udea edu co index php vitae volume 33 number 02 article 363403 harriette rosario duran-sandoval jorge eliecer espitia-baena julian javier martinez zambrano jose angel navas pass luis alfredo utria-acevedo,hite onions from chain store p2 bottled drinking water with total replacement antecedent prueba allium cepa cebolla herramienta sensible estudi genotoxicidad utilizada evaluar seguridad product natural objetiv esta