2145-2660,Vitae+33-2++364805+(1).pdf,Vitae+33-2++364805+(1)_0,en,"ow to cite: Arrúa, W. J., Galeano, A.","Background: Currently available hemostatic agents have important limitations, including high cost, adverse effects, and limited accessibility. Vernonanthura tweedieana (Baker) H.Rob. is traditionally used in Paraguayan folk medicine as a topical hemostatic agent; however, its hemostatic activity has not been experimentally validated. Objective: To evaluate the hemostatic activity, preliminary phytochemical composition, and safety of the ethanolic leaf extract of V. tweedieana (EEVt) in a murine model. Methods: Acute oral toxicity was evaluated in accordance with OECD Guideline 423. Mice were orally treated with EEVt (50, 100, or 200 mg/kg) for 14 days. Hemostatic activity was assessed by measuring bleeding time, coagulation time, platelet count, prothrombin time (PT), activated partial thromboplastin time (APTT), fibrinogen levels, erythrocyte morphology, and body weight. A preliminary phytochemical screening of the extract was also performed. Results: Oral administration of V. tweedieana extract in mice promoted primary hemostasis by reducing bleeding time by 48–56% and coagulation time by 29–36% compared with the control group. In contrast, no significant effects were observed on platelet count, prothrombin time, activated partial thromboplastin time, fibrinogen levels, erythrocyte morphology, or body weight, suggesting no detectable effect on secondary hemostasis. EEVt exhibited low acute oral toxicity and produced no behavioral alterations or changes in body weight. Preliminary phytochemical screening revealed the presence of steroids/triterpenoids and terpene lactones. Conclusions: This study provides the first experimental evidence supporting the traditional hemostatic use of V. tweedieana. Oral administration of EEVt to mice promoted primary hemostasis without affecting coagulation parameters associated with secondary hemostasis. Although preliminary phytochemical analysis identified steroids/triterpenoids and terpene lactones, further bioassay-guided fractionation and mechanistic studies are required to identify the active(s) constituent(s) and elucidate the mechanism underlying its hemostatic activity","Vernonanthura tweedieana (Baker) H.Rob., hemostatic activity, bleeding time, coagulation, primary hemostasis ORIGINAL ARTICLE Published 17 August 2026 DOI: https://doi.org/10.17533/udea.vitae.v33n2a364805 2 Journal Vitae | https://revistas.udea.edu.co/index.php/vitae Volume 33 | Number 02 | Article 364805 Wilfrido J. Arrúa, Antonia K. Galeano, Olga Heinichen, Andrea Cáceres, Juan Centurión, Rosa",marcadores,ow cite arrua galeano,background currently available hemostatic agent have important limit includ high cost adverse effect limit accessibility vernonanthura tweedieana baker rob traditionally used paraguayan folk medicine topical hemostatic agent however its hemostatic activity has not been experimentally validat objective evaluate hemostatic activity preliminary phytochemical composition safety ethanolic leaf extract tweedieana eevt murine model method acute oral toxicity evaluat accordance oecd guideline 423 mice orally treat eevt 50 100 200 mg kg 14 days hemostatic activity assess measur bleed time coagulation time platelet count prothrombin time pt activat partial thromboplastin time aptt fibrinogen level erythrocyte morphology body weight preliminary phytochemical screen extract also perform result oral administration tweedieana extract mice promot primary hemostasi reduc bleed time 48-56 coagulation time 29-36 compar control group contrast no significant effect observ platelet count prothrombin time activat partial thromboplastin time fibrinogen level erythrocyte morphology body weight suggest no detectable effect secondary hemostasi eevt exhibit low acute oral toxicity produc no behavioral alter chang body weight preliminary phytochemical screen reveal presence steroid triterpenoid terpene lacton conclusion study provid first experimental evidence support traditional hemostatic use tweedieana oral administration eevt mice promot primary hemostasi without affect coagulation parameter associat secondary hemostasi although preliminary phytochemical analysi identifi steroid triterpenoid terpene lacton further bioassay-guid fractionation mechanistic studi requir identify active constituent elucidate mechanism underly its hemostatic activity,vernonanthura tweedieana baker rob hemostatic activity bleed time coagulation primary hemostasi original article publish 17 august 2026 doi http doi org 10 17533 udea vitae v33n2a364805 journal vitae http revista udea edu co index php vitae volume 33 number 02 article 364805 wilfrido arrua antonia galeano olga heinichen andrea cacer juan centurion rosa,ow cite arrua galeano background currently available hemostatic agent have important limit includ high cost adverse effect limit accessibility vernonanthura tweedieana baker rob traditionally used paraguayan folk medicine topical hemostatic agent however its hemostatic activity has not been experimentally validat objective evaluate hemostatic activity preliminary phytochemical composition safety ethanolic leaf extract tweedieana eevt murine model method acute oral toxicity evaluat accordance oecd guideline 423 mice orally treat eevt 50 100 200 mg kg 14 days hemostatic activity assess measur bleed time coagulation time platelet count prothrombin time pt activat partial thromboplastin time aptt fibrinogen level erythrocyte morphology body weight preliminary phytochemical screen extract also perform result oral administration tweedieana extract mice promot primary hemostasi reduc bleed time 48-56 coagulation time 29-36 compar control group contrast no significant effect observ platelet count prothrombin time activat partial thromboplastin time fibrinogen level erythrocyte morphology body weight suggest no detectable effect secondary hemostasi eevt exhibit low acute oral toxicity produc no behavioral alter chang body weight preliminary phytochemical screen reveal presence steroid triterpenoid terpene lacton conclusion study provid first experimental evidence support traditional hemostatic use tweedieana oral administration eevt mice promot primary hemostasi without affect coagulation parameter associat secondary hemostasi although preliminary phytochemical analysi identifi steroid triterpenoid terpene lacton further bioassay-guid fractionation mechanistic studi requir identify active constituent elucidate mechanism underly its hemostatic activity vernonanthura tweedieana baker rob hemostatic activity bleed time coagulation primary hemostasi original article publish 17 august 2026 doi http doi org 10 17533 udea vitae v33n2a364805 journal vitae http revista udea edu co index php vitae volume 33 number 02 article 364805 wilfrido arrua antonia galeano olga heinichen andrea cacer juan centurion rosa,1.0.0,59fb13c63dea0cb6
2145-2660,Vitae+33-2++364805+(1).pdf,Vitae+33-2++364805+(1)_0,es,"e management of bleeding, Vernonanthura","Antecedentes: Los agentes hemostáticos disponibles actualmente presentan importantes limitaciones, como su elevado coste, sus efectos adversos y su escasa accesibilidad. Vernonanthura tweedieana (Baker) H.Rob. se utiliza tradicionalmente en la medicina popular paraguaya como agente hemostático tópico; sin embargo, su actividad hemostática no ha sido validada experimentalmente. Objetivos: Evaluar la actividad hemostática, la composición fitoquímica preliminar y la seguridad del extracto etanólico de hojas de V. tweedieana (EEVt) en un modelo murino. Metodología: Se evaluó la toxicidad oral aguda según la Guía 423 de la OCDE. Se administró EEVt por vía oral a ratones (50, 100 o 200 mg/kg) durante 14 días. La actividad hemostática se evaluó midiendo el tiempo de sangrado, el tiempo de coagulación, el recuento de plaquetas, el tiempo de protrombina (TP), el tiempo de tromboplastina parcial activada (TTPA), los niveles de fibrinógeno, la morfología de los eritrocitos y el peso corporal. También se realizó un análisis fitoquímico preliminar del extracto. Resultados: La administración oral del extracto de V. tweedieana en ratones promovió la hemostasia primaria al reducir el tiempo de sangrado en un 48–56% y el tiempo de coagulación en un 29–36% en comparación con el grupo control. Por el contrario, no se observaron efectos significativos en el recuento de plaquetas, el tiempo de protrombina, el tiempo de tromboplastina parcial activada, los niveles de fibrinógeno, la morfología de los eritrocitos o el peso corporal, lo que sugiere que no hubo un efecto detectable en la hemostasia secundaria. El EEVt mostró baja toxicidad oral aguda y no produjo alteraciones del comportamiento ni cambios en el peso corporal. El análisis fitoquímico preliminar reveló la presencia de esteroides/triterpenoides y lactonas terpénicas. Conclusiones: Este estudio aporta la primera evidencia experimental que respalda el uso hemostático tradicional de V. tweedieana. La administración oral de EEVt promovió la hemostasia primaria sin afectar los parámetros de coagulación asociados a la hemostasia secundaria. Si bien el análisis fitoquímico preliminar identificó esteroides/triterpenoides y lactonas terpénicas, se requieren estudios adicionales de fraccionamiento guiados por bioensayos y estudios mecanísticos para identificar el(los) componente(s) activo(s) y dilucidar el mecanismo subyacente a su actividad hemostática","Vernonanthura tweedieana (Baker) H.Rob., actividad hemostática, tiempo de sangrado, coagulación, hemostasia primaria 3 Journal Vitae | https://revistas.udea.edu.co/index.php/vitae Volume 33 | Number 02 | Article 364805 Preliminary phytochemical analysis and hemostatic activity of the ethanolic leaf extract of Vernonanthura tweedieana (Baker) H.Rob. in mice aggregation, enhancing coagulation, or",marcadores,management of bleeding vernonanthura,antecedent agent hemostatic disponibl actual presentan important limit como elevado coste sus efect advers escasa accesibilidad vernonanthura tweedieana baker rob utiliza tradicional medicina popular paraguaya como agente hemostatico topico sin embargo actividad hemostatica no ha sido validada experimental objetiv evaluar actividad hemostatica composicion fitoquimica preliminar seguridad extracto etanolico hojas tweedieana eevt modelo murino metodologia evaluo toxicidad oral aguda segun guia 423 ocde administro eevt via oral raton 50 100 200 mg kg durante 14 dias actividad hemostatica evaluo midiendo tiempo sangrado tiempo coagulacion recuento plaquet tiempo protrombina tp tiempo tromboplastina parcial activada ttpa nivel fibrinogeno morfologia eritrocit peso corporal tambien realizo analisis fitoquimico preliminar extracto resultad administracion oral extracto tweedieana raton promovio hemostasia primaria reducir tiempo sangrado 48-56 tiempo coagulacion 29-36 comparacion grupo control contrario no observaron efect significativ recuento plaquet tiempo protrombina tiempo tromboplastina parcial activada nivel fibrinogeno morfologia eritrocit peso corporal sugiere no hubo efecto detectable hemostasia secundaria eevt mostro baja toxicidad oral aguda no produjo alter comportamiento ni cambi peso corporal analisis fitoquimico preliminar revelo presencia esteroid triterpenoid lacton terpenic conclusion este estudio aporta primera evidencia experimental respalda uso hemostatico tradicional tweedieana administracion oral eevt promovio hemostasia primaria sin afectar parametr coagulacion asociad hemostasia secundaria si bien analisis fitoquimico preliminar identifico esteroid triterpenoid lacton terpenic requieren estudi adicional fraccionamiento guiad bioensay estudi mecanistic identificar componente activo dilucidar mecanismo subyacente actividad hemostatica,vernonanthura tweedieana baker rob actividad hemostatica tiempo sangrado coagulacion hemostasia primaria journal vitae https revist udea edu co index php vitae volume 33 number 02 article 364805 preliminary phytochemical analysis and hemostatic activity of the ethanolic leaf extract of vernonanthura tweedieana baker rob in mice aggregation enhancing coagulation or,management of bleeding vernonanthura antecedent agent hemostatic disponibl actual presentan important limit como elevado coste sus efect advers escasa accesibilidad vernonanthura tweedieana baker rob utiliza tradicional medicina popular paraguaya como agente hemostatico topico sin embargo actividad hemostatica no ha sido validada experimental objetiv evaluar actividad hemostatica composicion fitoquimica preliminar seguridad extracto etanolico hojas tweedieana eevt modelo murino metodologia evaluo toxicidad oral aguda segun guia 423 ocde administro eevt via oral raton 50 100 200 mg kg durante 14 dias actividad hemostatica evaluo midiendo tiempo sangrado tiempo coagulacion recuento plaquet tiempo protrombina tp tiempo tromboplastina parcial activada ttpa nive