2145-2946,document (2).pdf,document (2)_0,en,"tatal”. Revista digital de Derecho Administrativo, Universidad Externado","This article analyzes the material and internal activity of the Administra tion as a substantive precondition for the development and implementation of administrative procedure in continental legal systems, with particular emphasis on public procurement. Consistent with this premise, adminis trative law scholarship has traditionally focused on formalized legal ins truments – regulations, administrative acts, and public contracts – and on the mechanisms governing their review, while relegating the study of those internal actions that are not procedurally formalized and that precede and shape administrative decision-making. Against this backdrop, the article argues that the internal activity of the Administration does not constitute a marginal or legally irrelevant manifestation, but rather an inherent dimen sion of the exercise of public power that performs a structural function in the configuration of administrative procedure","Administrative Procedure, Public Administration, Public Pro curement, Informal Administrative Action, Internal Activity",marcadores,tatal revista digital de derecho administrativo universidad externado,article analyz material internal activity administra tion substantive precondition development implementation administrative procedure continental legal system particular emphasi public procurement consistent premise admini trative law scholarship has traditionally focus formaliz legal ins trument regul administrative acts public contract mechanism govern their review while relegat study those internal action not procedurally formaliz precede shape administrative decision-mak against backdrop article argu internal activity administration does not constitute marginal legally irrelevant manifestation but rather inherent dimen sion exercise public power perform structural function configuration administrative procedure,administrative procedure public administration public pro curement informal administrative action internal activity,tatal revista digital de derecho administrativo universidad externado article analyz material internal activity administra tion substantive precondition development implementation administrative procedure continental legal system particular emphasi public procurement consistent premise admini trative law scholarship has traditionally focus formaliz legal ins trument regul administrative acts public contract mechanism govern their review while relegat study those internal action not procedurally formaliz precede shape administrative decision-mak against backdrop article argu internal activity administration does not constitute marginal legally irrelevant manifestation but rather inherent dimen sion exercise public power perform structural function configuration administrative procedure administrative procedure public administration public pro curement informal administrative action internal activity,1.0.0,c4c5b93b78af4a07
2145-2946,document (3).pdf,document (3)_0,es,Motivación del acto,"La incorporación de sistemas de decisión automatizada en las entidades públicas ha intensificado las tensiones entre la racionalidad algorítmica y la estructura dogmática del acto administrativo. En ese marco, el presente artículo tiene por objeto analizar las condiciones jurídicas bajo las cuales el uso de sistemas de decisión automatizada para asistir en la motivación del acto administrativo resulta compatible con los principios estructurales que rigen su validez. El análisis pone de manifiesto que dicha compatibili dad solo es posible cuando estos sistemas se subordinan a una arquitectura 1 Maestro en Gerencia Social DE la Pontificia Universidad Católica del Perú, Lima, Perú. Profesor de la Universidad Peruana de Norte (UPN), Lima, Perú. Correo-e: fer nandozaga@gmail.com. Enlace Orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6301-9460. Fecha de recepción: 15 de enero de 2026. Fecha de modificación: 27 de abril de 2026. Fecha de aceptación: 5 de mayo de 2026. Para citar el artículo: Ramos-Zaga, Fernando A., “Motivación del acto administrativo asistida por sistemas de decisión automatizada: fundamentos para su integración legítima y control”, Revista digital de Derecho Adminis trativo, Universidad Externado de Colombia, n.º 36, 2026, pp. 31-54. DOI: https://doi. org/10.18601/21452946.n36.03. Fernando A. Ramos-Zaga 32 Revista digital de Derecho Administrativo, n.º 36, segundo semestre/2026, pp. 31-54 jurídica que garantice la determinación jurídica de los hechos, la motivación suficiente, la imputación a autoridad competente y el control efectivo, con supervisión humana, trazabilidad y responsabilidad institucional","acto administrativo, inteligencia artificial, motivación, responsabilidad administrativa, procedimiento administrativo. Administrative Reason-Giving and AIEnabled Automated Decision-Making: Doctrinal Limits and Conditions for Legitimate Use and Control",marcadores,motivacion acto,incorporacion sistem