2145-4507,RCS-24-2_14668_Quiroz.pdf,RCS-24-2_14668_Quiroz_0,en,femenino y el 50.2 % manifestó pertenecer al,"Objective: To identify predictors of the practice of physical activity in young university students. Methods: Observational, cross-sectional, correlational study with analytical intent. A database containing 1240 records of university students from five educational institutions in Cali-Colombia was used. A Confirmatory Factor Analysis (cfa) and a Structural Equation Model (sem) were performed. For statistical processing, the ibm® spss® Statistics version 24 and ibm® spss® amos® version 24 packages were used. Results: The median age of the students was 20 years (iqr = 19-23), more than half (54.7%) of the participants were female and 50.2% stated that they belonged to the lower stratum. According to the standardized path weighting coefficients (β), the food (β = 0.11) and alcohol (β = −0.09) constructs had a direct and significant association (p < 0.5) with the practice of physical activity. Conclusion: There is a relationship between the adoption of eating habits and the practice of physical activity, showing that when young university students consume meat, dairy products, eggs, cereals/tubers, fast food, fruits/vegetables and legumes, they tend to be more physically active. No dependency relationship was found between cigarette consumption and sociodemographic characteristics with the level of physical activity",Colombia; physical activity; university students; eating behavior; cigarette smoking habit; sociodemographic factors,marcadores,femenino el 50 manifesto pertenecer al,objective identify predictor practice physical activity young university student method observational cross-sectional correlational study analytical intent database contain 1240 record university student five educational institution cali-colombia used confirmatory factor analysi cfa structural equation model sem perform statistical process ibm spss statistic version 24 ibm spss amos version 24 packag used result median age student 20 year iqr 19-23 more than half 54 participant female 50 stat they belong lower stratum accord standardiz path weight coefficient food 11 alcohol -0 09 construct had direct significant association practice physical activity conclusion there relationship between adoption eating habit practice physical activity show when young university student consume meat dairy product eggs cereal tuber fast food fruit vegetabl legum they tend more physically active no dependency relationship found between cigarette consumption sociodemographic characteristic level physical activity,colombia physical activity university student eating behavior cigarette smok habit sociodemographic factor,femenino el 50 manifesto pertenecer al objective identify predictor practice physical activity young university student method observational cross-sectional correlational study analytical intent database contain 1240 record university student five educational institution cali-colombia used confirmatory factor analysi cfa structural equation model sem perform statistical process ibm spss statistic version 24 ibm spss amos version 24 packag used result median age student 20 year iqr 19-23 more than half 54 participant female 50 stat they belong lower stratum accord standardiz path weight coefficient food 11 alcohol -0 09 construct had direct significant association practice physical activity conclusion there relationship between adoption eating habit practice physical activity show when young university student consume meat dairy product eggs cereal tuber fast food fruit vegetabl legum they tend more physically active no dependency relationship found between cigarette consumption sociodemographic characteristic level physical activity colombia physical activity university student eating behavior cigarette smok habit sociodemographic factor,1.0.0,fd0667dd3ca27307
2145-4507,RCS-24-2_14778_Alvarez (1).pdf,RCS-24-2_14778_Alvarez (1)_0,es,Escala de Estrés,"Introducción: la Escala de Estrés Percibido (eep) es uno de los instrumentos más utilizados para medir el estrés emocional en contextos de salud; sin embargo, pocos estudios analizan su desempeño psicométrico en personal sociosanitario colombiano. El objetivo de este trabajo fue examinar las evidencias psicométricas de la eep-10 en una muestra de trabajadores del sector de la salud de Cartagena de Indias (Colombia). Materiales y métodos: se desarrolló un estudio instrumental, con una muestra de 550 profesionales sociosanitarios, seleccionados mediante muestreo no probabilístico por conveniencia. Se evaluó idoneidad de los datos, dimensionalidad, validez interna y estructura factorial del instrumento. Se excluyeron 50 participantes por incapacidad temporal o restricciones para completar los cuestionarios. Resultados: se identificaron dos dimensiones: 1) percepción del estrés y 2) capacidad de afrontamiento, las cuales explicaron el 72.58 % de la varianza total. La idoneidad de los datos fue adecuada (kmo = 0.78; 1 Facultad de Ciencias Sociales y Educación, Programa de Psicología, Fundación Universitaria Tecnológico Comfenalco (Cartagena de Indias, Colombia). Facultad de Ciencias Humanas, Doctorado en Psicología, Pontificia Universidad Javeriana (sede Cali). Nicolás Álvarez Merlano, orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6320-1470 * Autor de correspondencia: nicolas.alvarezmerlano@gmail.com ARTÍCULOS DE INVESTIGACIÓN CLÍNICA O EXPERIMENTAL Escala de Estrés Percibido-10 (EEP-10): desempeño psicométrico en personal sociosanitario de Cartagena 2 Rev. Cienc. Salud. Bogotá, Colombia, vol. 24(2): 1-16, mayo-agosto de 2026 p < 0.01) y los índices de ajuste mostraron valores satisfactorios (χ²/gl = 1.16; cfi = 0.99; tli = 0.98; nfi = 0.96; srmr = 0.06; rmsea = 0.05). La consistencia interna global fue elevada (α = 0.86; ω = 0.86). Conclusiones: la eep-10 presenta propiedades psicométricas sólidas en personal sociosanitario colombiano, lo que respalda su uso en contextos clínicos, investigativos y de salud ocupacional",estudio de validación; psicometría; estrés psicológico,marcadores,escala estr,introduccion escala estr percibido eep uno instrument mas utilizad medir estr emocional context salud sin embargo pocos estudi analizan desempeno psicometrico personal sociosanitario colombiano objetivo este trabajo fue examinar evidenci psicometric eep-10 muestra trabajador sector salud cartagena indi colombia material metod desarrollo estudio instrumental muestra 550 profesional sociosanitari seleccionad mediante muestreo no probabilistico conveniencia evaluo idoneidad datos dimensionalidad validez interna estructura factorial instrumento excluyeron 50 participant incapacidad temporal restriccion completar cuestionari resultad identificaron dos dimension percepcion estr capacidad afrontamiento cual explicaron 72 58 varianza total idoneidad datos fue adecuada kmo 78 facultad cienci social educacion programa psicologia fundacion universitaria tecnologico comfenalco cartagena indi colombia facultad cienci human doctorado psicologia pontificia universidad javeriana sede cali nicol alvarez merlano orcid https orcid org 0000-0002-6320-1470 autor correspondencia nicol alvarezmerlano gmail com articul investigacion clinica experimental escala estr percibido-10 eep-10 desempeno psicometrico personal sociosanitario cartagena rev cienc salud bogota colombia vol 24 1-16 mayo-agosto 2026 01 indic ajuste mostraron valor satisfactori kh2 gl 16 cfi 99 tli 98 nfi 96 srmr 06 rmsea 05 consistencia interna global fue elevada 86 86 conclusion eep-10 presenta propiedad psicometric solid personal sociosanitario colombiano respalda uso context clinic investigativ salud ocupacional,estudio validacion psicometria estr psicologico,escala estr introduccion escala estr percibido eep uno instrument mas utilizad medir estr emocional context salud sin embargo pocos estudi analizan desempeno psicometrico personal sociosanitario colombiano objetivo este trabajo fue examinar evidenci psicometric eep-10 muestra trabajador sector salud cartagena indi colombia material metod desarrollo estudio instrumental muestra 550 profesional sociosanitari seleccionad mediante muestreo no probabilistico conveniencia evaluo idoneidad datos dimensionalidad validez interna estructura factorial instrumento excluyeron 50 participant incapacidad temporal restriccion completar cuestionari resultad identificaron dos dimension percepcion estr capacidad afrontamiento cual explicaron 72 58 varianza total idoneidad datos fue adecuada kmo 78 facultad cienci social educacion programa psicologia fundacion universitaria tecnologico comfenalco cartagena indi colombia facultad cienci human doctorado psicologia pontificia universidad javeriana sede cali nicol alvarez merlano orcid https orcid org 0000-0002-6320-1470 autor correspondencia nicol alvarezmerlano gmail com articul investigacion clinica experimental escala estr percibido-10 eep-10 desempeno psicometrico personal sociosanitario cartagena rev cienc salud bogota colombia vol 24 1-16 mayo-agosto 2026 01 indic ajuste mostraron valor satisfactori kh2 gl 16 cfi 99 tli 98 nfi 96 srmr 06 rmsea 05 consistencia interna global fue elevada 86 86 conclusion eep-10 presenta propiedad psicometric solid personal sociosanitario colombiano respalda uso context clinic investigativ salud ocupacional estudio validacion psicometria estr psicologico,1.0.0,920c96ed343066a7
2145-4507,RCS-24-2_14778_Alvarez (1).pdf,RCS-24-2_14778_Alvarez (1)_0,en,"Psicología, Pontificia Universidad Javeriana (sede Cali).","Introduction: The Perceived Stress Scale (pss) is one of the most widely used instruments for assessing emotional stress in health-related contexts. However, few studies have examined its psychometric performance among Colombian healthcare workers. The aim of this study was to examine the psychometric properties of the 10-item Perceived Stress Scale (pss-10) in a sample of healthcare personnel from Cartagena de Indias – Colombia. Materials and Methods: An instrumental study was conducted with a sample of 550 healthcare professionals, selected through non-probabilistic convenience sampling. The data adequacy, dimensionality, internal validity, and factorial structure of the instrument were evaluated. A total of 50 participants were excluded due to temporary incapacity or self-reported restrictions preventing completion of the questionnaire. Results: Two dimensions were identified: perceived stress and coping capacity, which explained 72.58 % of the total variance. Data adequacy was satisfactory (kmo = 0.78; p < 0.01), and the fit indices indicated a good model fit (χ²/df = 1.16; cfi = 0.99; tli = 0.98; nfi = 0.96; srmr = 0.06; rmsea = 0.05). The overall internal consistency was high (α = 0.86; ω = 0.86). Conclusions: The pss-10 demonstrated robust psychometric properties among Colombian healthcare workers, supporting its use in clinical, research, and occupational health settings",validation study; psychometrics; stress psychological,marcadores,psicologia pontificia universidad javeriana sede cali,introduction perceiv stres scale pss one most widely used instrument assess emotional stres health-relat context however few studi have examin its psychometric performance among colombian healthcare worker aim study examine psychometric properti 10-item perceiv stres scale pss-10 sample healthcare personnel cartagena de india colombia material method instrumental study conduct sample 550 healthcare professional select through non-probabilistic convenience sampl data adequacy dimensionality internal validity factorial structure instrument evaluat total 50 participant exclud due temporary incapacity self-report restriction prevent completion questionnaire result two dimension identifi perceiv stres coping capacity which explain 72 58 total variance data adequacy satisfactory kmo 78 01 fit indic indicat good model fit kh2 df 16 cfi 99 tli 98 nfi 96 srmr 06 rmsea 05 overall internal consistency high 86 86 conclusion pss-10 demonstrat robust psychometric properti among colombian healthcare worker support its use clinical research occupational health setting,validation study psychometric stres psychological,psicologia pontificia universidad javeriana sede cali introduction perceiv stres scale pss one most widely used instrument assess emotional stres health-relat context however few studi have examin its psychometric performance among colombian healthcare worker aim study examine psychometric properti 10-item perceiv stres scale pss-10 sample healthcare personnel cartagena de india colombia material method instrumental study conduct sample 550 healthcare professional select through non-probabilistic convenience sampl data adequacy dimensionality internal validity factorial structure instrument evaluat total 50 participant exclud due temporary incapacity self-report restriction prevent completion questionnaire result two dimension identifi perceiv stres coping capacity which explain 72 58 total variance data adequacy satisfactory kmo 78 01 fit indic indicat good model fit kh2 df 16 cfi 99 tli 98 nfi 96 srmr 06 rmsea 05 overall internal consistency high 86 86 conclusion pss-10 demonstrat robust psychometric properti among colombian healthcare worker support its use clinical research occupational health setting validation study psychometric stres psychological,1.0.0,1799b32d80e425f8
