fican configur heterogene barrer facilitador destacandose rol central apoy social autora correspondencia orcid https orcid org 0000-0002-4109-1362 correo electronico jcordoba psico edu uy orcid https orcid org 0009-0005-4482-6140 correo electronico fdutra psico edu uy orcid https orcid org 0000-0003-0139-9511 correo electronico cdifabio psico edu uy orcid https orcid org 0009-0005-8249-4757 correo electronico estefaniamiranda32 gmail com orcid https orcid org 0009-0009-5831-7602 correo electronico katiafumeroalen gmail com citar este articulo cordoba dutra di fabio miranda fumero 2026 entre contexto experiencia inclusion laboral person discapacidad uruguay avanc psicologia latinoamericana 44 1-31 https doi org 10 12804 revist urosario edu co apl 16301 julia cordoba florencia dutra chiara di fabio estefania mirandam katia fumero avanc psicologia latinoamericana bogota colombia vol 44 pp 1-31 2026 issne2145-4515 persistent tension vinculad accesibilidad modelo cdv evidencian desbalanc entre dimension bienestar aun context inclusion laboral activa subraya distancia entre inclusion formal experiencia subjetiva calidad vida articulacion ambos enfoqu aporta comprension integral proces inclusion laboral poniendo valor analisis casuistico complementariedad entre indicador contextual percepcion subjetiv hallazg refuerzan necesidad politic program integren apoy tecnic social psicosocial promover trayectori laboral significativ discapacidad inclusion laboral cif calidad vida enfoque mixto,1.0.0,3e816490459f6ba0
2145-4515,16301+Rev+APL+44-1+Cordoba.pdf,16301+Rev+APL+44-1+Cordoba_0,en,"nía Mirandam, Katia Fumero","This study analyzes the employment inclusion profiles of people with disabilities by linking the contextual factors of the International Classification of Functioning, Disability, and Health (ICF) with the Quality of Life (QoL) model. Using a mixed-methods, descriptive, and exploratory approach, the study examines four cases of participants in the SUMA Program, an initiative of the Municipality of Montevideo aimed at designing customized technical solutions for workplace adaptation. Standardized instruments (WHODAS 2.0 for assessing functioning and disability severity, and MOS for perceived social support) and semi-structured interviews were administered. The results were analyzed through a joint operationalization of both models, which allowed for the construction of individual profiles and their visualization via spider charts. From the ICF Model, heterogeneous configurations of barriers and facilitators are identified, highlighting the central role of social supports and the persistent tensions linked to accessibility. From the QoL Model, imbalances between dimensions of well-being are evident, even in contexts of active labor market inclusion, underscoring the gap between formal inclusion and the subjective experience of quality of life. The integration of both approaches provides a comprehensive understanding of labor inclusion processes, highlighting the value of case-by-case analysis and the complementarity between contextual indicators and subjective perceptions. The findings reinforce the need for policies and programs that integrate technical, social, and psychosocial supports to promote meaningful career trajectories","disability, workplace inclusion, ICF, quality of life, mixed approach",marcadores,nia mirandam katia fumero,study analyz employment inclusion profil people disabiliti link contextual factor international classification function disability health icf quality life qol model using mixed-method descriptive exploratory approach study examin four case participant suma program initiative municipality montevideo aimed design customiz technical solution workplace adaptation standardiz instrument whoda assess function disability severity mos perceiv social support semi-structur interview administer result analyz through joint operational both model which allow construction individual profil their visual via spider chart icf model heterogeneou configur barrier facilitator identifi highlight central role social support persistent tension link accessibility qol model imbalanc between dimension well-be evident even context active labor market inclusion underscor gap between formal inclusion subjective experience quality life integration both approach provid comprehensive understand labor inclusion process highlight value case-by-case analysi complementarity between contextual indicator subjective perception finding reinforce need polici program integrate technical social psychosocial support promote meaningful career trajectori,disability workplace inclusion icf quality life mixed approach,nia mirandam katia fumero study analyz employment inclusion profil people disabiliti link contextual factor international classification function disability health icf quality life qol model using mixed-method descriptive exploratory approach study examin four case participant suma program initiative municipality montevideo aimed design customiz technical solution workplace adaptation standardiz instrument whoda assess function disability severity mos perceiv social support semi-structur interview administer result analyz through joint operational both model which allow construction individual profil their visual via spider chart icf model heterogeneou configur barrier facilitator identifi highlight central role social support persistent tension link accessibility qol model imbalanc between dimension well-be evident even context