2145-4531,15405-Rev+SocioJuridicos+27-2_MGSanchez+et+al.pdf,15405-Rev+SocioJuridicos+27-2_MGSanchez+et+al_0,en,. Aunque el 95 % de las familias percibe que,"This study examines food sovereignty, the human right to food, and dietary patterns in the community of Molas, Yucatán, Mexico. Using a mixed-methods approach —inclu ding documentary analysis and surveys— demographic variables, consumption habits, access to food, and perceptions of the human right to food. Seventy-nine percent of households rely entirely on market purchases to obtain their food, highlighting a high vulnerability to fluctuations in prices or availability. Although 95% of families perceive their food intake as sufficient, the low production of native foods and the limited dietary diversity —particularly in fruits and vegetables— indicate a potential risk to food secu rity. Furthermore, while 57% of respondents report being aware of the right to food, the study did not explore the depth of their understanding, suggesting a possible lack of critical awareness regarding this right and its implications. The findings underscore the need to strengthen community-based strategies aimed at improving food security, promoting awareness and enforceability of the right to food, and revaluing traditional food practices as a central component of food sovereignty",human rights; food habits; food sovereignty; Yucatan,marcadores,aunque el 95 de las familia percibe que,study examin food sovereignty human right food dietary pattern community mola yucatan mexico using mixed-method approach --inclu ding documentary analysi surveys-- demographic variabl consumption habit acces food perception human right food seventy-nine percent household rely entirely market purchas obtain their food highlight high vulnerability fluctu pric availability although 95 famili perceive their food intake sufficient low production native food limit dietary diversity --particularly fruit vegetables-- indicate potential risk food secu rity furthermore while 57 respondent report being aware right food study did not explore depth their understand suggest possible lack critical awarenes regard right its implic finding underscore need strengthen community-bas strategi aimed improv food security promot awarenes enforceability right food revalu traditional food practic central component food sovereignty,human right food habit food sovereignty yucatan,aunque el 95 de las familia percibe que study examin food sovereignty human right food dietary pattern community mola yucatan mexico using mixed-method approach --inclu ding documentary analysi surveys-- demographic variabl consumption habit acces food perception human right food seventy-nine percent household rely entirely market purchas obtain their food highlight high vulnerability fluctu pric availability although 95 famili perceive their food intake sufficient low production native food limit dietary diversity --particularly fruit vegetables-- indicate potential risk food secu rity furthermore while 57 respondent report being aware right food study did not explore depth their understand suggest possible lack critical awarenes regard right its implic finding underscore need strengthen community-bas strategi aimed improv food security promot awarenes enforceability right food revalu traditional food practic central component food sovereignty human right food habit food sovereignty yucatan,1.0.0,a51befdb31d45128
2145-4531,15418-Rev+SocioJuridicos+28-1_CFainstein.pdf,15418-Rev+SocioJuridicos+28-1_CFainstein_0,es,of the Environmental Conflict in the Buenos Aires Metropolitan,"El objetivo de este artículo es indagar en los efectos de un litigio estructural de sanea miento ambiental en la cuenca más contaminada y poblada de Buenos Aires, dentro del Poder Judicial. Así, se pretende poner en tensión los abordajes sobre la judiciali zación del conflicto social y aquellos que analizan las burocracias judiciales. A su vez, el devenir de este caso da cuenta de las transformaciones políticas ocurridas en este campo durante el período 2004-2024 en Argentina. Se llevó adelante una metodología cualitativa que consistió en el relevamiento de resoluciones y documentos judiciales, así como en entrevistas en profundidad a operadores jurídicos intervinientes en la causa","judicialización; burocracias; conflicto ambiental; campo jurídico. 2 estud. socio-juríd., bogotá (colombia), 28(1) • enero-junio de 2026 • issn 0124-0579 issne 2145-4531 carla fainstein",marcadores,of the environmental conflict in the buen aires metropolitan,objetivo este articulo indagar efect litigio estructural sanea miento ambiental cuenca mas contaminada poblada buen aires dentro poder judicial asi pretende poner tension abordaj sobre judiciali zacion conflicto social aquell analizan burocraci judicial vez devenir este caso da cuenta transform politic ocurrid este campo durante periodo 2004-2024 argentina llevo adelante metodologia cualitativa consistio relevamiento resolucion document judicial asi como entrevist profundidad operador juridic intervinient causa,judicializacion burocraci conflicto ambiental campo juridico estud socio-jurid bogota colombia 28 enero-junio 2026 issn 0124-0579 issne 2145-4531 carla fainstein,of the environmental conflict in the buen aires metropolitan objetivo este articulo indagar efect litigio estructural sanea miento ambiental cuenca mas contaminada poblada buen aires dentro poder judicial asi pretende poner tension abordaj sobre judiciali zacion conflicto social aquell analizan burocraci judicial vez devenir este caso da cuenta transform politic ocurrid este campo durante periodo 2004-2024 argentina llevo adelante metodologia cualitativa consistio relevamiento resolucion document judicial asi como entrevist profundidad operador juridic intervinient causa judicializacion burocraci conflicto ambiental campo juridico estud socio-jurid bogota colombia 28 enero-junio 2026 issn 0124-0579 issne 2145-4531 carla fainstein,1.0.0,e4751694eef88809
2145-4531,15418-Rev+SocioJuridicos+28-1_CFainstein.pdf,15418-Rev+SocioJuridicos+28-1_CFainstein_0,en,El objetivo de este artículo es indagar en los efectos de un litigio estructural de sanea,"The objective of this article is to investigate the effects of a structural environmental sanitation lawsuit in the most polluted and populated basin of Buenos Aires, within the Judicial Branch. Thus, it aims to highlight the tension between approaches to the judicialization of social conflict and those that analyze judicial bureaucracies. At the same time, the evolution of this case reflects the political transformations that took place in this field during the period 2004-2024 in Argentina. A qualitative methodology was used, consisting of a survey of judicial decisions and documents, as well as in-depth interviews with legal practitioners involved in the case",judicialization; burocracies; environmental conflict; juridical field,marcadores,el objetivo de este articulo es indagar en los efecto de un litigio estructural de sanea,objective article investigate effect structural environmental sanitation lawsuit most pollut populat basin bueno aire within judicial branch thus aims highlight tension between approach judicial social conflict those analyze judicial bureaucraci same time evolution case reflect political transform took place field during period 2004-2024 argentina qualitative methodology used consist survey judicial decision document well in-depth interview legal practitioner involv case,judicial burocraci environmental conflict juridical field,el objetivo de este articulo es indagar en los efecto de un litigio estructural de sanea objective article investigate effect structural environmental sanitation lawsuit most pollut populat basin bueno aire within judicial branch thus aims highlight tension between approach judicial social conflict those analyze judicial bureaucraci same time evolution case reflect political transform took place field during period 2004-2024 argentina qualitative methodology used consist survey judicial decision document well in-depth interview legal practitioner involv case judicial burocraci environmental conflict juridical field,1.0.0,5c470c074795eea8
2145-4531,15459-Rev+SocioJuridicos+28-1_GALopez+et+al.pdf,15459-Rev+SocioJuridicos+28-1_GALopez+et+al_0,en,"estud. socio-juríd., bogotá (colombia), 28(1)","This article analyses the guarantees of citizen participation in Colombia, particularly in the context of fracking projects and their environmental impact. Based on the 1991 Constitution, it establishes participation as a fundamental right that allows citizens to influence political decisions through mechanisms such as voting, plebiscites, and popular consultations. It analyses the role of the Constitutional Court of Colombia, which has emphasized the importance of citizen participation in guaranteeing a democratic and pluralistic State, advocating for its adequate regulation. It underlines the need for a legal * Ph. D. Derecho constitucional. Profesor titular Universidad Surcolombiana (Colombia). E-mail: germanlo@usco.edu.co. Dirección: Cra 5 No. 23-40. Neiva, Huila, Colombia. orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4627-0295 ** MSc. Derecho Público. Docente e investigadora Universidad Surcolombiana. (Co lombia). E-mail: mariela.mendez@usco.edu.co. Dirección: Cra 5 No. 23-40. Neiva, Huila, Colombia. orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5120-4623 *** Abogado. Investigador Universidad Surcolombiana (Colombia). E-mail: luis.rodri guez@usco.edu.co. Dirección: Cra 5 No. 23-40. Neiva, Huila, Colombia. orcid: https://orcid. org/0000-0001-9973-1142 2 estud. socio-juríd., bogotá (colombia), 28(1) • enero-junio de 2026 • issn 0124-0579 issne 2145-4531 germán alfonso lópez daza, mariela méndez cuéllar, luis eduardo rodríguez quintero framework that adequately regulates the exploitation of natural resources, ensuring that decisions consider the well-being of the affected communities",Citizen participation; fracking; participatory democracy; mineral and energy resource exploitation,marcadores,estud socio-jurid bogota colombia 28,article analys guarante citizen participation colombia particularly context frack project their environmental impact based 1991 constitution establish participation fundamental right allow citizen influence political decision through mechanism such voting plebiscit popular consult analys role constitutional court colombia which has emphasiz importance citizen participation guarantee democratic pluralistic state advocat its adequate regulation underlin need legal ph derecho constitucional profesor titular universidad surcolombiana colombia e-mail germanlo usco edu co direccion cra no 23-40 neiva huila colombia orcid http orcid org 0000-0003-4627-0295 msc derecho publico docente investigadora universidad surcolombiana co lombia e-mail mariela mendez usco edu co direccion cra no 23-40 neiva huila colombia orcid http orcid org 0000-0002-5120-4623 abogado investigador universidad surcolombiana colombia e-mail luis rodri guez usco edu co direccion cra no 23-40 neiva huila colombia orcid http orcid org 0000-0001-9973-1142 estud socio-jurid bogota colombia 28 enero-junio de 2026 issn 0124-0579 issne 2145-4531 german alfonso lopez daza mariela mendez cuellar luis eduardo rodriguez quintero framework adequately regulat exploitation natural resourc ensur decision consider well-be affect communiti,citizen participation frack participatory democracy mineral energy resource exploitation,estud socio-jurid bogota colombia 28 article analys guarante citizen participation colombia particularly context frack project their environmental impact based 1991 constitution establish participation fundamental right allow citizen influence political decision through mechanism such voting plebiscit popular consult analys role constitutional court colombia which has emphasiz importance citizen participation guarantee democratic pluralistic state advocat its adequate regulation underlin need legal ph derecho constitucional profesor titular universidad surcolombiana colombia e-mail germanlo usco edu co direccion cra no 23-40 neiva huila colombia orcid http orcid org 0000-0003-4627-0295 msc derecho p