2145-7166,359824_ENG_Final.pdf,359824_ENG_Final_0,en,"¹ Instituto Federal do Ceará, Brazil.","Biometric seed characteristics, such as size, mass, and moisture, can significantly influence germination potential and possibly the efficiency of dormancy-breaking treatments. Leucaena leucocephala, an invasive exotic plant native to Central America, has dormant seeds, a mechanism that prevents immediate germination. Although this species has been extensively studied, no research has yet linked biometric seed characteristics to dormancy-breaking. Therefore, the aim of this study was to evaluate the influence of L. leucocephala seed size on the effectiveness of different dormancy-breaking treatments. The width, thickness, and length of seeds from both treatments were measured using a digital caliper. The moisture content was then assessed. For the germination test, small (mean width = 3.94 mm; mean length = 6.36 mm) and large (mean width = 5.23 mm; mean length = 9.59 mm) seeds were separated into four treatments (chemical scarification with 98% sulfuric acid for 15 minutes (CS), manual scarification with sandpaper 100 (MS), hot water immersion at 80 °C for 10 minutes (HWI), and a control treatment (C). In terms of germination percentage, both small and large seeds performed better in the MS and HWI treatments. The germination speed index was higher for both seed sizes when treated with MS. When MS was used, longer seeds showed higher germination percentages, and seeds with higher moisture produced shorter radicles. Thus, the efficiency of dormancy-breaking treatments may differ between large and small seeds","biometry, dormancy breaking, exotic species, seed",marcadores,instituto federal do ceara brazil,biometric seed characteristic such size mass moisture can significantly influence germination potential possibly efficiency dormancy-break treatment leucaena leucocephala invasive exotic plant native central america has dormant seed mechanism prevent immediate germination although speci has been extensively studi no research has yet link biometric seed characteristic dormancy-break therefore aim study evaluate influence leucocephala seed size effectivenes different dormancy-break treatment width thicknes length seed both treatment measur using digital caliper moisture content then assess germination test small mean width 94 mm mean length 36 mm large mean width 23 mm mean length 59 mm seed separat into four treatment chemical scarification 98 sulfuric acid 15 minut cs manual scarification sandpaper 100 ms hot water immersion 80 degc 10 minut hwi control treatment term germination percentage both small large seed perform better ms hwi treatment germination speed index higher both seed size when treat ms when ms used longer seed show higher germination percentag seed higher moisture produc shorter radicl thus efficiency dormancy-break treatment may differ between large small seed,biometry dormancy break exotic speci seed,instituto federal do ceara brazil biometric seed characteristic such size mass moisture can significantly influence germination potential possibly efficiency dormancy-break treatment leucaena leucocephala invasive exotic plant native central america has dormant seed mechanism prevent immediate germination although speci has been extensively studi no research has yet link biometric seed characteristic dormancy-break therefore aim study evaluate influence leucocephala seed size effectivenes different dormancy-break treatment width thicknes length seed both treatment measur using digital caliper moisture content then assess germination test small mean width 94 mm mean length 36 mm large mean width 23 mm mean length 59 mm seed separat into four treatment chemical scarification 98 sulfuric acid 15 minut cs manual scarification sandpaper 100 ms hot water immersion 80 degc 10 minut hwi control treatment term germination percentage both small large seed perform better ms hwi treatment germination speed index higher both seed size when treat ms when ms used longer seed show higher germination percentag seed higher moisture produc shorter radicl thus efficiency dormancy-break treatment may differ between large small seed biometry dormancy break exotic speci seed,1.0.0,31cbf8641d5061fc
2145-7166,360767_Ingles.pdf,360767_Ingles_0,en,Full scientific article,"Urbanization has transformed natural ecosystems, creating major challenges for biodiversity conservation. Ex situ conservation strategies implemented within cities can help mitigate species loss. This study evaluated the long-term survival of eight vascular epiphyte species established on urban trees as part of a biodiversity enrichment initiative in Medellín, Colombia. A total of 310 individuals belonging to four families (Araceae, Aspleniaceae, Bromeliaceae, and Orchidaceae) were established on 50 host trees across three parks within the Parques del Río ecological corridor and monitored over seven years (2016–2023). Kaplan–Meier survival curves and Cox proportional hazards models were used to identify factors associated with mortality. Overall, survival was 32%, with significant differences among species and sites. Anthurium salvinii showed the highest survival, whereas Asplenium sp. and Guzmania sp. experienced the greatest losses. Establishment height positively influenced survival, while position on the tree and bark type showed no consistent effects. Although host tree species identity did not significantly affect mortality risk, survival varied among individual trees, suggesting that fine-scale microhabitat conditions and tree-level management influence outcomes. These findings demonstrate that vascular epiphytes can persist in urban environments when planting height is carefully considered, and when individual host trees are selected based on favorable structural and management conditions rather than taxonomic identity. The study provides evidence-based guidelines for integrating epiphytes into tropical urban green infrastructure","ex situ conservation, species relocation, urban biodiversity, urban trees, vascular epiphytes",marcadores,full scientific article,urban has transform natural ecosystem creat major challeng biodiversity conservation ex situ conservation strategi implement withi