2145-7778,3697_18(39).pdf,3697_18(39)_0,en,"a Tecnología Sociedad, 18(39),","One of the central challenges of environmental education is establishing meaningful connections with students’ local realities. Particularly, environmental education in rural contexts should be closely linked to the sustainable development of local communities. Against this backdrop, the present study aimed to identify, design, and implement socio-environmental actions that foster environmental awareness and culture among students at the Institución Educativa Rural Arenoso in the municipality of San Vicente del Caguán, Colombia. To this end, a participatory action research methodology, structured in three phases, was employed to coordinate collaborative work between university students and those of the school community. This approach enabled a participatory diagnosis of perceptions, practices, and socio-environmental problems within the educational institution, as well as the design of contextspecific socio-environmental actions that would promote responsible values, attitudes, and practices towards the natural and social environment. The articulation also included the implementation and evaluation of these actions, ensuring feedback and the appropriation of sustainable strategies that would contribute to consolidating the school’s environmental culture. The findings provide comprehensive insights into the causes and consequences of environmental degradation. The study also evidences a transition from reflection to commitment through concrete initiatives such as the creation of ecological points and the organization of reforestation activities in the hydrographic basin of the Santa Marta rural settlement. Overall, these experiences demonstrated that small collective actions can generate significant transformations in local environmental culture while contributing to the achievement of the Sustainable Development Goals","environmental education, environment, sustainable practices, reforestation",marcadores,tecnologia sociedad 18 39,one central challeng environmental education establish meaningful connection student local realiti particularly environmental education rural context should closely link sustainable development local communiti against backdrop present study aimed identify design implement socio-environmental action foster environmental awarenes culture among student institucion educativa rural arenoso municipality san vicente del caguan colombia end participatory action research methodology structur three phas employ coordinate collaborative work between university student those school community approach enabl participatory diagnosi perception practic socio-environmental problem within educational institution well design contextspecific socio-environmental action would promote responsible valu attitud practic toward natural social environment articulation also includ implementation evaluation these action ensur feedback appropriation sustainable strategi would contribute consolidat school environmental culture finding provide comprehensive insight into caus consequenc environmental degradation study also evidenc transition reflection commitment through concrete initiativ such creation ecological point organ reforestation activiti hydrographic basin santa marta rural settlement overall these experienc demonstrat small collective action can generate significant transform local environmental culture while contribut achievement sustainable development goal,environmental education environment sustainable practic reforestation,tecnologia sociedad 18 39 one central challeng environmental education establish meaningful connection student local realiti particularly environmental education rural context should closely link sustainable development local communiti against backdrop present study aimed identify design implement socio-environmental action foster environmental awarenes culture among student institucion educativa rural arenoso municipality san vicente del caguan colombia end participatory action research methodology structur three phas employ coordinate collaborative work between university student those school community approach enabl participatory diagnosi perception practic socio-environmental problem within educational institution well design contextspecific socio-environmental action would promote responsible valu attitud practic toward natural social environment articulation also includ implementation evaluation these action ensur feedback appropriation sustainable strategi would contribute consolidat school environmental culture finding provide comprehensive insight into caus consequenc environmental degradation study also evidenc transition reflection commitment through concrete initiativ such creation ecological point organ reforestation activiti hydrographic basin santa marta rural settlement overall these experienc demonstrat small collective action can generate significant transform local environmental culture while contribut achievement sustainable development goal environmental education environment sustainable practic reforestation,1.0.0,027c2612ae3aad63
2145-7778,3715_18(39).pdf,3715_18(39)_0,es,Artículo de reflexión,"Este artículo examina la transformación contemporánea de la alteridad en el contexto de las inteligencias artificiales generativas. La ética computacional y los estudios críticos de la inteligencia artificial han abordado principalmente cuestiones de transparencia, sesgo y gobernanza algorítmica; sin embargo, persiste un vacío teórico en torno a la dimensión ontológica y afectiva de la relación entre sujetos humanos y sistemas generativos. Ante este vacío, el artículo propone un diálogo hermenéutico entre Emmanuel Levinas y Gilbert Simondon que articula la ética del rostro con la ontogénesis técnica. La metodología adoptada es de carácter teórico y hermenéutico: se parte de la lectura de textos primarios de Levinas y Simondon, articulados con pensadores contemporáneos de la técnica y la cultura digital. En la era digital, la mediación algorítmica disuelve la frontera entre lo humano y lo técnico, produciendo una «alteridad simulada»: una forma de presencia técnica que reconfigura las estructuras afectivas y éticas sin instanciar la vulnerabilidad que funda la responsabilidad levinasiana. El artículo argumenta que la relación con la inteligencia artificial inaugura una nueva sensibilidad tecnológica en la que el rostro se convierte en interfaz y la responsabilidad se desplaza hacia el diseño, el código y la gobernanza algorítmica. En la conclusión se propone una ética de la individuación que combine la sensibilidad levinasiana por la vulnerabilidad con la comprensión simondoniana de la interdependencia técnica, como vía para habitar críticamente el mundo algorítmico sin perder la experiencia del otro","ética de la alteridad, gubernamentalidad algorítmica, individuación técnica, inteligencia artificial. Cómo referenciar Bautista-Roa, M. A., & Díaz Sanabria, A. F. (2026). Del rostro a la interfaz: Levinas, Simondon y la ética de la alteridad en tiempos de inteligencia artificial. Trilogía Ciencia Tecnología Sociedad, 18(39), art. 3715. https://doi.org/10.22430/21457778.3715 * Este artículo es pro",marcadores,articulo reflexion,este articulo examina transformacion contemporanea alteridad contexto inteligenci artificial generativ etica computacional estudi critic inteligencia artificial han abordado principal cuestion transparencia sesgo gobernanza algoritmica sin embargo persiste vacio teorico torno dimension ontologica afectiva relacion entre sujet human sistem generativ ante este vacio articulo propone dialogo hermeneutico entre emmanuel levin gilbert simondon articula etica rostro ontogenesis tecnica metodologia adoptada caracter teorico hermeneutico parte lectura text primari levin simondon articulad pensador contemporane tecnica cultura digital era digital mediacion algoritmica disuelve frontera entre humano tecnico produc alteridad simulada forma presencia tecnica reconfigura estructur afectiv etic sin instanciar vulnerabilidad funda responsabilidad levinasiana articulo argumenta relacion inteligencia artificial inaugura nueva sensibilidad tecnologica rostro convierte interfaz responsabilidad desplaza hacia diseno codigo gobernanza algoritmica conclusion propone etica individuacion combine sensibilidad levinasiana vulnerabilidad comprension simondoniana interdependencia tecnica como via habitar critica mundo algoritmico sin perder experiencia otro,etica alteridad gubernamentalidad algoritmica individuacion tecnica inteligencia artificial como referenciar bautista-roa diaz sanabria 2026 rostro interfaz levin simondon etica alteridad tiemp inteligencia artificial trilogia ciencia tecnologia sociedad 18 39 art 3715 https doi org 10 22430 21457778 3715 este articulo pro,articulo reflexion este articulo examina transformacion contemporanea alteridad contexto inteligenci artificial generativ etica computacional estudi critic inteligencia artificial han abordado principal cuestion transparencia sesgo gobernanza algoritmica sin embargo persiste vacio teorico torno dimension ontologica afectiva relacion entre sujet human sistem generativ ante este vacio articulo propone dialogo hermeneutico entre emmanuel levin gilbert simondon articula etica rostro ontogenesis tecnica metodologia adoptada caracter teorico hermeneutico parte lectura text primari levin simondon articulad pensador contemporane tecnica cultura digital era digital mediacion algoritmica disuelve frontera entre humano tecnico produc alteridad simulada forma presencia tecnica reconfigura estructur afectiv etic sin instanciar vulnerabilidad funda responsabilidad levinasiana articulo argumenta relacion inteligencia artificial inaugura nueva sensibilidad tecnologica rostro convierte interfaz responsabilidad desplaza hacia diseno codigo gobernanza algoritmica conclusion propone etica individuacion combine sensibilidad levinasiana vulnerabilidad comprension simondoniana interdependencia tecnica como via habitar critica mundo algoritmico sin perder experiencia otro etica alteridad gubernamentalidad algoritmica individuacion tecnica inteligencia artificial como referenciar bautista-roa diaz sanabria 2026 rostro interfaz levin simondon etica alteridad tiemp inteligencia artificial trilogia ciencia tecnologia sociedad 18 39 art 3715 https doi org 10 22430 21457778 3715 este articulo pro,1.0.0,8f4ff1990ffa5d9d
2145-7778,3715_18(39).pdf,3715_18(39)_0,en,"la ética de la alteridad en tiempos de inteligencia artificial. Trilogía Ciencia Tecnología Sociedad,","This paper examines the contemporary transformation of otherness in the context of generative artificial intelligence. While computational ethics and critical studies of artificial intelligence have primarily addressed issues of transparency, bias, and algorithmic governance, a theoretical gap persists regarding the ontological and affective dimensions of the relationship between human subjects and generative systems. In response to this gap, the article proposes a hermeneutic dialogue between Emmanuel Levinas and Gilbert Simondon, bringing the ethics of the face into conversation with technical ontogenesis. The methodology adopted is theoretical and hermeneutic. It is based on a close reading of primary texts by Levinas and Simondon, examined alongside the work of contemporary thinkers on technology and digital culture. In the digital era, algorithmic mediation dissolves the boundary between the human and the technical, giving rise to a form of “simulated alterity”: a mode of technical presence that reconfigures affective and ethical structures without instantiating the vulnerability that underpins Levinasian responsibility. It is here argued that the relationship with artificial intelligence ushers in a new technological sensitivity in which the face becomes an interface, and responsibility shifts toward design, code, and algorithmic governance. Finally, the article proposes an ethics of individuation that combines Levinas’ sensitivity to vulnerability with Simondon’s understanding of technical interdependence as a way of critically inhabiting the algorithmic world without surrendering the experience of the other","ethics of alterity, algorithmic governmentality, technical individuation, artificial intelligence",marcadores,la etica de la alteridad en tiempo de inteligencia artificial trilogia ciencia tecnologia sociedad,paper examin contemporary transformation othernes context generative artificial intelligence while computational ethic critical studi artificial intelligence have primarily address issu transparency bias algorithmic governance theoretical gap persist regard ontological affective dimension relationship between human subject generative system response gap article propos hermeneutic dialogue between emmanuel levina gilbert simondon bring ethic face into conversation technical ontogenesi methodology adopt theoretical hermeneutic based close read primary text levina simondon examin alongside work contemporary thinker technology digital culture digital era algorithmic mediation dissolv boundary between human technical giving rise form simulat alterity mode technical presence reconfigur affective ethical structur without instantiat vulnerability underpin levinasian responsibility here argu relationship artificial intelligence usher new technological sensitivity which face becom interface responsibility shift toward design code algorithmic governance finally article propos ethic individuation combin levina sensitivity vulnerability simondon understand technical interdependence way critically inhabit algorithmic world without surrender experience other,ethic alterity algorithmic governmentality technical individuation artificial intelligence,la etica de la alteridad en tiempo de inteligencia artificial trilogia ciencia tecnologia sociedad paper examin contemporary transformation othernes context generative artificial intelligence while computational ethic critical studi artificial intelligence have primarily address issu transparency bias algorithmic governance theoretical gap persist regard ontological affective dimension relationship between human subject generative system response gap article propos hermeneutic dialogue between emmanuel levina gilbert simondon bring ethic face into conversation technical ontogenesi methodology adopt theoretical hermeneutic based close read primary text levina simondon examin alongside work contemporary thinker technology digital culture digital era algorithmic mediation dissolv boundary between human technical giving rise form simulat alterity mode technical presence reconfigur affective ethical structur without instantiat vulnerability underpin levinasian responsibility here argu relationship artificial intelligence usher new technological sensitivity which face becom interface responsibility shift toward design code algorithmic governance finally article propos ethic individuation combin levina sensitivity vulnerability simondon understand technical interdependence way critically inhabit algorithmic world without surrender experience other ethic alterity algorithmic governmentality technical individuation artificial intelligence,1.0.0,c17d9cfb25dd3d37
2145-7778,3723_18(39).pdf,3723_18(39)_0,en,Reflection Article,"This article theorizes technonecromancy as a novel regime of mediation that operationalizes spectral presence through generative models, voice cloning, and synthetic video, shifting the relation to the dead from archival recollection to dialogic simulation. Conceptually, it integrates science, technology, and society studies with phenomenology and 4e cognition to argue that posthumous agents are phenomenologically sufficient to reorganize mourning yet ontologically insufficient as continuants of persons. Empirically, it reads cultural and commercial cases (such as griefbots and animated photo apps) as epistemologies of the technocultural present, demonstrating how engineered responsiveness can both scaffold continuing bonds and entrench dependence, thereby reconfiguring rituals of loss and memory. Normatively, it advances a consent-first, provenance-rich governance program, with mandatory disclosure, machine-readable labeling, and revocability, aligned with frameworks, such as the European Union Artificial Intelligence Act’s transparency duties for synthetic content, and calls for fiduciary stewardship of digital remains. Thus, this study situates these proposals within the emerging digital afterlife industry, noting that social acceptability collapses absent explicit pre-mortem authorization and that professionalization is beginning to reshape industry standards. The result is a political-economic diagnosis: technonecromancy is a world-making apparatus whose risks and benefits can only be adjudicated where ontological critique, clinical harm minimization, and market governance converge","digital afterlife, governance, necrocapitalism, sts studies, technonecromancy. How to Cite da Silva, G. S., & Ulbricht, V. R. (2026). Technonecromancy: Simulacra of Presence and the Politics of Death in the Age of Generative Artificial Intelligence. Trilogía Ciencia Tecnología Sociedad, 18(39), art. e3723. https://doi.org/10.22430/21457778.3723 * This article is an independent study and is not as",marcadores,reflection article,article theoriz technonecromancy novel regime mediation operationaliz spectral presence through generative model voice clon synthetic video shift relation dead archival recollection dialogic simulation conceptually integrat science technology society studi phenomenology 4e cognition argue posthumou agent phenomenologically sufficient reorganize mourn yet ontologically insufficient continuant person empirically read cultural commercial case such griefbot animat photo apps epistemologi technocultural present demonstrat how engineer responsivenes can both scaffold continu bond entrench dependence thereby reconfigur ritual loss memory normatively advanc consent-first provenance-rich governance program mandatory disclosure machine-readable label revocability align framework such european union artificial intelligence act transparency duti synthetic content call fiduciary stewardship digital remain thus study situat these proposal within emerg digital afterlife industry noting social acceptability collaps absent explicit pre-mortem author professional beginn reshape industry standard result political-economic diagnosi technonecromancy world-mak apparatu whose risk benefit can only adjudicat where ontological critique clinical harm minim market governance converge,digital afterlife governance necrocapitalism sts studi technonecromancy how cite da silva ulbricht 2026 technonecromancy simulacra presence politic death age generative artificial intelligence trilogia ciencia tecnologia sociedad 18 39 art e3723 http doi org 10 22430 21457778 3723 article independent study not,reflection article article theoriz technonecromancy novel regime mediation operationaliz spectral presence through generative model voice clon synthetic video shift relation dead archival recollection dialogic simulation conceptually integrat science technology society studi phenomenology 4e cogniti