lgun sector fractur cizalla individual orientad ene-wsw aprovechan fall preexistent reactivacion mineralizacion textur deformacion cuarz q1 q2 q3 q4 muestran cuatro etap mineralizacion mecanism deformacion ductil-fragil ultimo evento deformacion asociado mineralizacion presenta indicador evidenci cinematica dextral estan registrad desplaz diqu band leucocratic neis asi como evidenci deformacion microestructural cizalla simple sigmoid cuarz policristalin rotacion cristal estructur s-c porfiroclast dislocad tipo domino mosaico distribucion tipo cluster polos vetas indica campo esfuerz transtensivo direccion esfuerz principal orientad s1 51deg 271deg s2 22deg 031deg s3 30deg 135deg orientacion campo esfuerz favorece desarrollo zonas dilatacion local controlan migracion precipitacion fluid mineralizant sector sureste distrito minero distrito minero vetas-california event mineralizacion deformacion cuarzo transtension forma citar quiroz-prada suarez-ari osorio-ari pacheco-hernandez forero-ortega 2026 analisis geometrico cinematico dinamico estructur vetiform sector distrito minero vetas-california santander colombia boletin geologia 48,1.0.0,731b7108a5949aaf
2145-8553,"Análisis+geométrico,+cinemático+y+dinámico+de+estructuras+vetiformes+en+el+sector+SE+del+Distrito+Minero+de+Vetas-California,+Santander,+Colombia.pdf","Análisis+geométrico,+cinemático+y+dinámico+de+estructuras+vetiformes+en+el+sector+SE+del+Distrito+Minero+de+Vetas-California,+Santander,+Colombia_0",en,precipitación de fluidos mineralizantes en el sector sureste del distrito minero.,"The Vetas-California Mining District, located in the northeastern portion of the Colombian Andes, is hosted within the igneous-metamorphic basement of the Santander Massif. Mineralization in the district is characterized by epithermal ocurrences distributed along the main La Baja-Angostura (California) and Romeral-Cucutilla (Vetas) fault systems. Described hydrothermal events are categorized into six stages of hydrothermal alteration: the initial three represent early alteration and mineralization (propylitic and phyllic alteration), while the subsequent three are associated with the main phases of mineralization and superimposed alteration within hydrothermal breccias (advanced argillic and silicification). To accurately constrain the geometry, kinematics, and dynamics of the district, this research implemented mapping, petrographic analysis, and macro- and microstructural characterization techniques. This approach allowed for the identification of three mineralized trends oriented NNE-SSW, NE-SW, and ENE-WSW. These trends exhibit both cross-cutting and branching relationships, and in some sectors, individual ENE-WSW oriented fractures leverage the reactivation of pre-existing faults. Textures and deformation of quartz (Q1, Q2, Q3, Q4) reveal four mineralization stages with ductile-brittle deformation mechanisms. The latest deformation event, associated with mineralization, displays indicators of dextral kinematics recorded in dike displacements and leucocratic bands within the gneiss, as well as microstructural evidence of simple shear deformation in polycrystalline quartz sigmoids, crystal rotation, S-C structures, and dislocated porphyroclasts of domino and mosaic types. A cluster-type distribution of vein poles indicates a transtensional stress field with principal stress directions: σ1: 51°/271°; σ2: 22°/031°; σ3: 30°/135°. It is inferred that this paleostress likely generated localized dilation zones, favoring the ascent of mineralizing fluids from the southeastern sector of the Mining District",Vetas-California Mining District; Mineralization events; Quartz deformation; Transtension,marcadores,precipitacion de fluido mineralizant en el sector sureste del distrito minero,vetas-california mining district locat northeastern portion colombian ande host within igneous-metamorphic basement santander massif mineral district characteriz epithermal ocurrenc distribut along main la baja-angostura california romeral-cucutilla veta fault system describ hydrothermal event categoriz into six stag hydrothermal alteration initial three represent early alteration mineral propylitic phyllic alteration while subsequent three associat main phas mineral superimpos alteration within hydrothermal breccia advanc argillic silicification accurately constrain geometry kinematic dynamic district research implement mapp petrographic analysi macro- microstructural character techniqu approach allow identification three mineraliz trend orient nne-ssw ne-sw ene-wsw these trend exhibit both cross-cutt branch relationship some sector individual ene-wsw orient fractur leverage reactivation pre-exist fault textur deformation quartz q1 q2 q3 q4 reveal four mineral stag ductile-brittle deformation mechanism latest deformation event associat mineral display indicator dextral kinematic record dike displacement leucocratic band within gneis well microstructural evidence simple shear deformation polycrystalline quartz sigmoid crystal rotation s-c structur dislocat porphyroclast domino mosaic type cluster-type distribution vein pole indicat transtensional stres field principal stres direction s1 51deg 271deg s2 22deg 031deg s3 30deg 135deg inferr paleostres likely generat localiz dilation zone favor ascent mineraliz fluid southeastern sector mining district,vetas-california mining district mineral event quartz deformation transtension,precipitacion de fluido mineralizant en el sector sureste del distrito minero vetas-california mining district locat northeastern portion colombian ande host within igneous-metamorphic basement santander massif mineral district characteriz epithermal ocurrenc distribut along main la baja-angostura california romeral-cucutilla veta fault system describ hydrothermal event categoriz into six stag hydrothermal alteration initial three represent early alteration mineral propylitic phyllic alteration while subsequent three associat main phas mineral superimpos alteration within hydrothermal breccia advanc argillic silicification accurately constrain geometry kinematic dynamic district research implement mapp petrographic analysi macro- microstructural character techniqu approach allow identification three mineraliz trend orient nne-ssw ne-sw ene-wsw these trend exhibit both cross-cutt branch relationship some sector individual ene-wsw orient fractur leverage reactivation pre-exist fault textur deformation quartz q1 q2 q3 q4 reveal four mineral stag ductile-brittle deformation mechanism latest deformation event associat mineral display indicator dextral kinematic record dike displacement leucocratic band within gneis well microstructural evidence simple shear deformation polycrystalline quartz sigmoid crystal rotation s-c structur dislocat porphyroclast domino mosaic type cluster-type distribution vein pole indicat transtensional stres field principal stres direction s1 51deg 271deg s2 22deg 031deg s3 30deg 135deg inferr paleostres likely generat localiz dilation zone favor ascent mineraliz fluid southeastern sector mining district vetas-california mining district mineral event quartz deformation transtension