2145-9797,99c09a59-eb25-445f-9217-ea8c397d971d.pdf,99c09a59-eb25-445f-9217-ea8c397d971d_0,en,ón responde a la interacción entre vulnerabilidades individuales,"Introduction: Suicide in prison settings constitutes a major public health concern and a challenge for criminal justice systems. This study aimed to analyse the characteristics and factors associated with suicidal behaviour among people deprived of liberty in Colombian national correctional facilities during 2021-2022. Method: A quantitative, cross-sectional census-based design was conducted using 184 official records of completed suicide, suicide attempts and suicidal ideation. Descriptive analyses and chi-square tests were performed to examine associations between suicidal behaviour and so ciodemographic variables, personal history, motivations, prison conditions and contextual factors. Given the census-based descriptive nature of the study and the small number of completed suicides, bivariate associations should be interpreted cautiously and as exploratory. Results: Significant asso ciations were found between suicidal behaviour and variables such as place of occurrence, method used, motivation, personal antecedents, type of offence and participation in redemption activities. Conclusions: Completed suicides were primarily associated with more isolating environments and lethal methods, whereas suicide attempts were linked to psychiatric history and pre-existing clini cal vulnerabilities. Findings suggest that suicidal behaviour in prison emerges from the interaction between individual vulnerabilities and structural conditions of confinement, providing empirical evidence to strengthen suicide prevention and risk-monitoring strategies within the Colombian pen itentiary system","Prison suicide, suicidal behavior, people deprived of liberty, risk factors, correctional mental health, criminal policy © 2026 Fundación Universitaria Konrad Lorenz. This is an open access article under the CC BY-NC-ND license (https:// creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/). El término ‘suicidio’, derivado del latín sui (de sí mismo) y occidere (matar), refiere al acto intencional por el",marcadores,responde la interaccion entre vulnerabilidad individual,introduction suicide prison setting constitut major public health concern challenge criminal justice system study aimed analyse characteristic factor associat suicidal behaviour among people depriv liberty colombian national correctional faciliti during 2021-2022 method quantitative cross-sectional census-bas design conduct using 184 official record complet suicide suicide attempt suicidal ideation descriptive analys chi-square test perform examine associ between suicidal behaviour so ciodemographic variabl personal history motiv prison condition contextual factor given census-bas descriptive nature study small number complet suicid bivariate associ should interpret cautiously exploratory result significant asso ciation found between suicidal behaviour variabl such place occurrence method used motivation personal antecedent type offence participation redemption activiti conclusion complet suicid primarily associat more isolat environment lethal method wherea suicide attempt link psychiatric history pre-exist clini cal vulnerabiliti finding suggest suicidal behaviour prison emerg interaction between individual vulnerabiliti structural condition confinement provid empirical evidence strengthen suicide prevention risk-monitor strategi within colombian pen itentiary system,prison suicide suicidal behavior people depriv liberty risk factor correctional mental health criminal policy 2026 fundacion universitaria konrad lorenz open acces article under cc by-nc-nd license http creativecommon org licens by-nc-nd el termino suicidio derivado del latin sui de si mismo occidere matar refiere al acto intencional por el,responde la interaccion entre vulnerabilidad individual introduction suicide prison setting constitut major public health concern challen