2145-9797,b349b8ab-576a-4944-a7ac-95bbc2355d78.pdf,b349b8ab-576a-4944-a7ac-95bbc2355d78_0,en,* Corresponding author.,"Objective: Mathematics is a fundamental subject in school education; however, it can generate anx iety that negatively impacts attitudes and academic performance. Reports show that achievement levels are low in Peru. The objective of this study was to analyse the psychometric properties of the Abbreviated Mathematical Anxiety Scale in secondary school students in Peru. Method: The sample consisted of 416 Peruvian high school students from 11 to 18 years of age. Along with the AMAS, var ious models were tested using confirmatory factor analysis, and validity based on the relationship with other variables was studied through structural equation modelling. Reliability was estimated using Cronbach’s a and McDonald’s w coefficients. Results: Confirmatory factor analysis demonstrat ed that the two-dimensions related model presented acceptable fit indices. On the other hand, it was demonstrated that the scale presents validity based on the relationship with other variables such as academic self-efficacy, depression, anxiety, and stress. Likewise, it was found that the scale pre sents adequate reliability values in both dimensions: learning anxiety towards mathematics and evaluation anxiety towards mathematics. Conclusion: The results of this study confirm that the Ab breviated Mathematics Anxiety Scale is a useful instrument for measuring mathematics anxiety in high school students in a Peruvian context","Math anxiety, learning anxiety, math, assessment anxiety, high school students © 2026 Fundación Universitaria Konrad Lorenz. This is an open access article under the CC BY-NC-ND license (https:// creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/). Escala Abreviada de Ansiedad Matemática (AMAS): Nuevas evidencias psicométri cas en adolescentes peruanos",marcadores,correspond author,objective mathematic fundamental subject school education however can generate anx 