2145-9797,cb8f6ecb-43f6-4e6f-9233-26dbfc9d9da0.pdf,cb8f6ecb-43f6-4e6f-9233-26dbfc9d9da0_0,en,* Corresponding author.,"Introduction/Objective: Impulsivity in adolescents is associated with risky behaviours, making the UPPS-P Impulsive Behaviour Scale a key tool for its assessment. However, the validity of its brief ver sion in adolescents, particularly in Latin American contexts such as Argentina, has been hardly at all explored. Therefore, this study analysed the psychometric properties of the brief UPPS-P scale in Argentine adolescents. Method: The sample comprised 990 adolescents (60% female, age range 12–18 years, M = 13.89 years, SD = 1.28). The internal structure of the brief UPPS-P was evaluated us ing exploratory, procrustean, and confirmatory factor analyses. Results: Factor analyses revealed inconsistencies in the structure of the short UPPS-P. Both the MORGANA method and the Bayesian Lasso covariance procedure indicated that the presence of item doublets influenced model parsimo ny. Conclusion: The validity of the brief UPPS-P in Argentine adolescents is compromised by residual variance among items. These findings highlight the need to revise the scale to optimise its clinical or educational application in adolescent populations","Impulsivity, UPPS-P scale, factor structure, correlated residuals, exploratory factor analysis © 2026 Fundación Universitaria Konrad Lorenz. This is an open access article under the CC BY-NC-ND license (https:// creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/). Estructura factorial de la versión breve de la Escala de Comportamiento Impulsivo UPPS-P en una muestra argentina de niños y adolescentes Res",marcadores,correspond author,introduction objective impulsivity adolescent associat risky behaviour making upps-p impulsive behaviour scale key tool its assessment however validity its brief ver sion adolescent particularly latin american context such argentina has been hardly all explor therefore study analys psychometric properti brief upps-p scale argentine adolescent method sample compris 990 adolescent 60 female age range 12-18 year 13 89 year sd 28 internal structure brief upps-p evaluat us ing exploratory procrustean confirmatory factor analys result factor analys reveal inconsistenci structure short upps-p both morgana method bayesian lasso covariance procedure indicat presence item doublet influenc model parsimo ny conclusion validity brief upps-p argentine adolescent compromis residual variance among item these finding highlight need revise scale optimise its clinical educational application adolescent popul,impulsivity upps-p scale factor structure correlat residual exploratory factor analysi 2026 fundacion universitaria konrad lorenz open acces article under cc by-nc-nd license http creativecommon org licens by-nc-nd estructura factorial de la version breve de la escala de comportamiento impulsivo upps-p en una muestra argentina de nino adolescent res,correspond author introduction objective impulsivity adolescent associat risky behaviour making upps-p impulsive behaviour scale key tool its assessment however validity its brief ver sion adolescent particularly latin american context such argentina has been hardly all explor therefore study analys psychometric properti brief upps-p scale argentine adolescent method sample compris 990 adolescent 60 female age range 12-18 year 13 89 year sd 28 internal structure brief upps-p evaluat us ing exploratory procrustean confirmatory factor analys result factor analys reveal inconsistenci structure short upps-p both morgana method bayesian lasso covariance procedure indicat presence item doublet influenc model parsimo ny conclusion validity brief upps-p argentine adolescent compromis residual variance among item these finding highlight need revise scale optimise its clinical educational application adolescent popul impulsivity upps-p scale factor structure correlat residual exploratory factor analysi 2026 fundacion universitaria konrad lorenz open