2215-7727,CDR-22-2025+Lote-16732852005.pdf,CDR-22-2025+Lote-16732852005_0,en,atención a las experiencias de los trabajadores mapuches y a la intersección,"This article explores the transformations and continuities of agricultural work in the Araucanía region of Chile, analyzing the perceptions and experiences of agricultural workers. The objective of the paper is to address the different subjectivities surrounding agricultural work in the Araucanía region, highlighting the particular characteristics of the territory studied. Using a qualitative methodology, 27 semi-structured interviews were conducted with workers from various municipalities in the region. Key thematic axes related to the challenges faced by workers in the context of a neoliberal agricultural model oriented to agro-export and dominated by large-scale monoculture and forestry industries are identified. The findings highlight significant issues such as precarious working conditions, chemical exposure, systemic racism and the persistence of patriarchal gender relations in rural labor dynamics. In addition, the research highlights the symbolic and economic undervaluation of agricultural labor, a reflection of broader social inequalities. Particular attention is paid to the experiences of Mapuche workers and the intersection between identity, autonomy and labor in a context of historical and current land dispossession. This article contributes to the understanding of rural labor in Latin America by providing a comprehensive analysis of the multifaceted dimensions of agricultural labor in Araucanía. It calls for the development of public policies that address labor rights, environmental sustainability, and social equity in rural areas, emphasizing the urgent need for structural reforms to ensure the well-being of agricultural workers and the communities they sustain","Agricultural Labor, Agriculture, Sense, Araucanía",marcadores,atencion las experiencia de los trabajador mapuch la interseccion,article explor transform continuiti agricultural work araucania region chile analyz perception experienc agricultural worker objective paper addres different subjectiviti surround agricultural work araucania region highlight particular characteristic territory studi using qualitative methodology 27 semi-structur interview conduct worker variou municipaliti region key thematic axes relat challeng faced worker context neoliberal agricultural model orient agro-export dominat large-scale monoculture forestry industri identifi finding highlight significant issu such precariou work condition chemical exposure systemic racism persistence patriarchal gender relation rural labor dynamic addition research highlight symbolic economic undervaluation agricultural labor reflection broader social inequaliti particular attention paid experienc mapuche worker intersection between identity autonomy labor context historical current land dispossession article contribut understand rural labor latin america provid comprehensive analysi multifacet dimension agricultural labor araucania call development public polici addres labor right environmental sustainability social equity rural area emphasiz urgent need structural reform ensure well-be agricultural worker communiti they sustain,agricultural labor agriculture sense araucania,atencion las experiencia de los trabajador mapuch la interseccion article explor transform continuiti agricultural work araucania region chile analyz perception experienc agricultural worker objective paper addres different subjectiviti surround agricultural work araucania region highlight particular characteristic territory studi using qualitative methodology 27 semi-structur interview conduct worker variou municipaliti region key thematic axes relat challeng faced worker context neoliberal agricultural model orient agro-export dominat large-scale monoculture forestry industri identifi finding highlight significant issu such precariou work condition chemical exposure systemic racism persistence patriarchal gender relation rural labor dynamic addition research highlight symbolic economic undervaluation agricultural labor reflection broader social inequaliti particular attention paid experienc mapuche worker intersection between identity autonomy labor context historical current land dispossession article contribut understand rural labor latin america provid comprehensive analysi multifacet dimension agricultural labor araucania call development public polici addres labor right environmental sustainability social equity rural area emphasiz urgent need structural reform ensure well-be agricultural worker communiti they sustain agricultural labor agriculture sense araucania,1.0.0,3e2e095de0d22dfe
2215-7727,CDR-22-2025+Lote-16732852006.pdf,CDR-22-2025+Lote-16732852006_0,es,Satisfacción laboral y género en los,"A partir de una encuesta estructurada, se analiza la satisfacción laboral con perspectiva de género de propietario/as y gerente/as de los alojamientos turísticos del Parque Natural Sierra de Aracena y Picos de Aroche, así como sus motivos para emprender en este tipo de negocios. Los objetivos están relacionados con determinar el grado de satisfacción laboral de las personas propietarias y las diferencias de género, así como establecer las razones que los llevan a emprender en turismo rural. Los principales hallazgos apuntan a que el tipo de alojamiento rural mayoritario es la vivienda turística, que genera rendimientos de capital inmobiliario. Sin embargo, las mujeres, respecto a los varones, gestionan una mayor proporción de casas rurales y de establecimientos hoteleros. Asimismo, el alojamiento rural no es la principal fuente de ingresos en la mayoría de los casos, por lo que se configura como un complemento a otras fuentes principales de ingresos. En cuanto a su formación, las ª Autor de correspondencia: david.flores@dege.uhu.es Cuadernos de Desarrollo Rural, Colombia, vol. 22, 2025 personas encuestadas, tanto varones como mujeres, poseen un nivel muy alto de cualificación, un alto porcentaje de ellos cuenta con estudios universitarios. Para finalizar, estas personas están altamente satisfechas con la actividad que realizan en relación con el turismo rural, excepto cuando está su familia implicada en la gestión","turismo rural, condiciones de trabajo, mujer, emprendimiento. Job Satisfaction and Gender in Rural Tourist Accommodations in the Sierra de Aracena y Picos de Aroche, Andalusia, Spain",marcadores,satisfaccion laboral genero,partir encuesta estructurada analiza satisfaccion laboral perspectiva genero propietario as gerente as aloj turistic parque natural sierra aracena picos aroche asi como sus motiv emprender este tipo negoci objetiv estan re