elacion turismo rural excepto cuando esta familia implicada gestion turismo rural condicion trabajo mujer emprendimiento job satisfaction and gender in rural tourist accommodations in the sierra aracena picos aroche andalusia spain,1.0.0,43276e00dede0b65
2215-7727,CDR-22-2025+Lote-16732852006.pdf,CDR-22-2025+Lote-16732852006_0,en,"s rurales y de establecimientos hoteleros. Asimismo, el alojamiento rural no es la principal fuente de ingresos en","A structured survey was used to analyze the job satisfaction with a gender perspective of owners and managers of tourist lodgings in the Sierra de Aracena y Picos de Aroche Natural Park, as well as their reasons for starting this type of business. The objectives are related to determine the degree of job satisfaction of the owners and the gender differences, as well as to establish the reasons that lead them to engage in rural tourism. The main findings point to the fact that the main type of rural lodging is tourist housing, which generates returns on real estate capital. However, women, with respect to men, manage a greater proportion of rural houses and hotel establishments. Likewise, rural lodging is not the main source of income in most cases, being configured as a complement to other main sources of income. In terms of training, the people surveyed, both men and women, have a very high level of qualification, with a high percentage having university studies. Finally, these people are highly satisfied with the activity they carry out in relation to rural tourism, except when their family is involved in the management","Rural Tourism, Working Conditions, Women, Entrepreneurship",marcadores,rural de establecimiento hotelero asimismo el alojamiento rural no es la principal fuente de ingreso en,structur survey used analyze job satisfaction gender perspective owner manager tourist lodging sierra de aracena pico de aroche natural park well their reason start type busines objectiv relat determine degree job satisfaction owner gender differenc well establish reason lead them engage rural tourism main finding point fact main type rural lodg tourist hous which generat return real estate capital however women respect men manage greater proportion rural hous hotel establishment likewise rural lodg not main source income most case being configur complement other main sourc income term train people survey both men women have very high level qualification high percentage having university studi finally these people highly satisfi activity they carry out relation rural tourism except when their family involv management,rural tourism work condition women entrepreneurship,rural de establecimiento hotelero asimismo el alojamiento rural no es la principal fuente de ingreso en structur survey used analyze job satisfaction gender perspective owner manager tourist lodging sierra de aracena pico de aroche natural park well their reason start type busines objectiv relat determine degree job satisfaction owner gender differenc well establish reason lead them engage rural tourism main finding point fact main type rural lodg tourist hous which generat return real estate capital however women respect men manage greater proportion rural hous hotel establishment likewise rural lodg not main source income most case being configur complement other main sourc income term train people survey both men women have very high level qualification high percentage having university studi finally these people highly satisfi activity they carry out relation rural tourism except when their family involv management rural tourism work condition women entrepreneurship,1.0.0,4fac14f2ffb8bfcf
2215-7727,Cuadernos6732892001.pdf,Cuadernos6732892001_0,es,De la ciudad al campo: dinámicas,"La migración por amenidades es un fenómeno demográfico contemporáneo que se caracteriza por el desplazamiento voluntario de personas, generalmente de áreas urbanas hacia zonas rurales que ofrecen una alta calidad de vida y atractivos naturales. Este tipo de migración está motivado por la búsqueda de un estilo de vida más tranquilo, un entorno saludable y una conexión estrecha con la naturaleza. Esta investigación analizó las dinámicas socioespaciales de la migración por amenidades en cuatro municipios del Oriente Antioqueño, en Colombia: La Ceja, Concepción, El Carmen de Viboral y Cocorná. Mediante un estudio de caso colectivo cualitativo, se examinaron los perfiles de migrantes, principalmente profesionales de ingresos medios-altos que buscaban tranquilidad y oportunidades de teletrabajo o retiro en zonas rurales. Los resultados revelaron la coexistencia de territorialidades urbanas y rurales, con elecciones espaciales influenciadas por el capital económico de los migrantes. Se identificaron tensiones relacionales, ambientales y espaciales entre migrantes y residentes rurales, afectando las dinámicas territoriales. Se observó una tendencia hacia la urbanización de áreas rurales, con el mercado inmobiliario transformando el espacio rural en un bien de consumo y producción dentro de un marco capitalista. Las conclusiones presentaron nuevas configuraciones socioespaciales, indicando un modelo de expansión urbana hacia el espacio rural","migración por amenidades, oriente antioqueño, ruralidad; urbanización rural, naturaleza. ªAutora de correspondencia. Correo electrónico: katy.millanot@amigo.edu.co Cuadernos de Desarrollo Rural, Colombia, vol. 23, 2026 From City to Countryside: Socio-spatial and Relational Dynamics of Amenity Migration in Eastern Antioquia, Colombia",marcadores,ciudad campo dinamic,migracion amenidad fenomeno demografico contemporaneo caracteriza desplazamiento voluntario person general areas urban hacia zonas rural ofrecen alta calidad vida atractiv natural este tipo migracion esta motivado busqueda estilo vida mas tranquilo entorno saludable conexion estrecha naturaleza esta investigacion analizo dinamic socioespacial migracion amenidad cuatro municipi oriente antioqueno colombia ceja concepcion carmen viboral cocorna mediante estudio caso colectivo cualitativo examinaron perfil migrant principal profesional ingres medios-alt buscaban tranquilidad oportunidad teletrabajo retiro zonas rural resultad revelaron coexistencia territorialidad urban rural eleccion espacial influenciad capital economico migrant identificaron tension relacional ambiental espacial entre migrant resident rural afect dinamic territorial observo tendencia hacia urbanizacion areas rural mercado inmobiliario transform espacio rural bien consumo produccion dentro marco capitalista conclusion presentaron nuev configur socioespacial indic modelo expansion urbana hacia espacio rural,migracion amenidad oriente antioqueno ruralidad urbanizacion rural naturaleza aautora correspondencia correo electronico katy millanot amigo edu co cuadern desarrollo rural colombia vol 23 2026 from city to countryside socio-spatial and relational dynamics of amenity migration in eastern antioquia colombia,ciudad campo dinamic migracion amenidad fenomeno demografico contemporaneo caracteriza desplazamiento voluntario person general areas urban hacia zonas rural ofrecen alta calidad vida atractiv natural este tipo migracion esta motivado busqueda estilo vida mas tranquilo entorno saludable conexion estrecha naturaleza esta investigacion analizo dinamic socioespacial migracion amenidad cuatro municipi oriente antioqueno colombia ceja concepcion carmen viboral cocorna mediante estudio caso colectivo cualitativo examinaron perfil migrant principal profesional ingres medios-alt buscaban tranquilidad oportunidad teletrabajo retiro zonas rural resultad revelaron coexistencia territorialidad urban rural eleccion espacial influenciad capital economico migrant identificaron tension relacional ambiental espacial entre migrant resident rural afect dinamic territorial observo tendencia hacia urbanizacion areas rural mercado inmobiliario transform espacio rural bien consumo produccion dentro marco capitalista conclusion presentaron nuev configur socioespacial indic modelo expansion urbana hacia espacio rural migracion amenidad oriente antioqueno ruralidad urbanizacion rural naturaleza aautora correspondencia correo electronico katy millanot amigo edu co cuadern desarrollo rural colombia vol 23 2026 from city to countryside socio-spatial and relational dynamics of amenity migration in eastern antioquia colombia,1.0.0,e2642542dbff7311
2215-7727,Cuadernos6732892001.pdf,Cuadernos6732892001_0,en,ecciones espaciales influenciadas por el capital económico de,"Amenity migration is a contemporary demographic phenomenon characterized by the voluntary movement of people, generally from urban areas to rural areas that offer a high quality of life and natural attractions. This type of migration is mainly motivated by the search for a quieter lifestyle, a healthier environment, and a closer connection with nature. This research analyzed the socio-spatial dynamics of amenity migration in four municipalities of Eastern Antioquia, Colombia: La Ceja, Concepción, El Carmen de Viboral and Cocorná. Through a qualitative collective case study, the profiles of migrants, mainly upper-middle-income professionals seeking tranquility and opportunities for telecommuting or retirement in rural areas, were examined. The results revealed the coexistence of urban and rural territorialities, with spatial choices influenced by migrants’ economic capital. Relational, environmental and spatial tensions between migrants and rural residents were identified, affecting territorial dynamics. A trend towards urbanization of rural areas was observed, with the real estate market transforming rural space into a commodity for consumption and production within a capitalist framework. The conclusions presented new socio-spatial configurations, indicating a model of urban expansion into rural space","Amenity Migration, Eastern Antioquia, Rurality, Rural urbanization, Nature",marcadores,eccion espacial influenciada por el capital economico de,amenity migration contemporary demographic phenomenon characteriz voluntary movement people generally urban area rural area offer high quality life natural attraction type migration mainly motivat search quieter lifestyle healthier environment closer connection nature research analyz socio-spatial dynamic amenity migration four municipaliti eastern antioquia colombia la ceja concepcion el carmen de viboral cocorna through qualitative collective case study profil migrant mainly upper-middle-income professional seek tranquility opportuniti telecommut retirement rural area examin result reveal coexistence urban rural territorialiti spatial choic influenc migrant economic capital relational environmental spatial tension between migrant rural resident identifi affect territorial dynamic trend toward urban rural area observ real estate market transform rural space into commodity consumption production within capitalist framework conclusion present new socio-spatial configur indicat model urban expansion into rural space,amenity migration eastern antioquia rurality rural urban nature,eccion espacial influenciada por el capital economico de amenity migration contemporary demographic phenomenon characteriz voluntary movement people generally urban area rural area offer high quality life natural attraction type migration mainly motivat search quieter lifestyle healthier environment closer connection nature research analyz socio-spatial dynamic amenity migration four municipaliti eastern antioquia colombia la ceja concepcion el carmen de viboral cocorna through qualitative collective case study profil migrant mainly upper-middle-income professional seek tranquility opportuniti telecommut retirement rural area examin result reveal coexistence urban rural territorialiti spatial choic influenc migrant economic capital relational environmental spatial tension between migrant rural resident identifi affect territorial dynamic trend toward urban rural area observ real estate market transform rural space into commodity consumption production within capitalist framework conclusion present new socio-spatial configur indicat model urban expansion into rural space amenity migration eastern antioquia rurality rural urban nature,1.0.0,a3a5ba86dcfdfd0f
2215-7727,Cuadernos6732892003.pdf,Cuadernos6732892003_0,es,la conformación de redes de,"El Sistema Agroalimentario Global ha provocado la exclusión de actores de pequeña escala que no pueden insertarse en la dinámica que impone la lógica del capital global por ser considerados ineficientes y redundantes, por lo que muchos de los excluidos han generado estrategias para mantenerse y subsistir. El objetivo de este artículo es analizar la conformación de una Red de Colaboración en la región noreste de México, a partir del estudio de las características de los nexos, prácticas y experiencias de producción, comercialización, distribución y consumo de productos alimentarios de pequeña escala para un estudio de caso. Se utilizó la metodología de investigación acción, en el que se estudiaron las características de seis células de producción-consumo ubicadas en la región sureste de Coahuila y en la ciudad de Monterrey, Nuevo León. A partir del análisis teórico de las Redes de Colaboración Solidaria (RCS) y de la evidencia empírica del caso de estudio, se puede señalar que las células productivas y de consumo tienen características estructurales y funcionales que tienden a conformar una verdadera RCS, que contribuye a atender las necesidades de sus integrantes, mejorando su calidad de vida, pero bajo condiciones que superan las relaciones meramente mercantiles y de explotación que se manifiestan en los circuitos de mercado convencionales. Finalmente, se concluye que el caso estudiado no se limita a la generación de ingresos económicos, sino que promueven el intercambio de cultura, saberes, experiencias y amistades, en el que prevalece una ética del cuidado a la salud humana y del ambiente. ªAutor de correspondencia. Correo electrónico: ernesto.navarro@uaaan.edu.mx Cuadernos de Desarrollo Rural, Colombia, vol. 23, 2026","sistema agroalimentario, economía solidaria, circuitos cortos. Towards the Creation of Agri-Food Collaboration Networks in the Northeast Region of Mexico",marcadores,conformacion redes,sistema agroalimentario global ha provocado exclusion actor pequena escala no pueden insertarse dinamica impone logica capital global ser considerad ineficient redundant much excluid han generado estrategi mantenerse subsistir objetivo este articulo analizar conformacion red colaboracion region noreste mexico partir estudio caracteristic nexos practic experienci produccion comercializacion distribucion consumo product alimentari pequena escala estudio caso utilizo metodologia investigacion accion estudiaron caracteristic seis celul produccion-consumo ubicad region sureste coahuila ciudad monterrey nuevo leon partir analisis teorico redes colaboracion solidaria rcs evidencia empirica caso estudio puede senalar celul productiv consumo tienen caracteristic estructural funcional tienden conformar verdadera rcs contribuye atender necesidad sus integrant mejor calidad vida pero bajo condicion superan relacion mera mercantil explotacion manifiestan circuit mercado convencional final concluye caso estudiado no limita generacion ingres economic sino promueven intercambio cultura saber experienci amistad prevalece etica cuidado salud humana ambiente aautor correspondencia correo electronico ernesto navarro uaaan edu mx cuadern desarrollo rural colombia vol 23 2026,sistema agroalimentario economia solidaria circuit cort towards the creation of agri-food collaboration networks in the northeast region of mexico,conformacion redes sistema agroalimentario global ha provocado exclusion actor pequena escala no pueden insertarse dinamica impone logica capital global ser considerad ineficient redundant much excluid han generado estrategi mantenerse subsistir objetivo este articulo analizar conformacion red colaboracion region noreste mexico partir estudio caracteristic nexos practic experienci produccion comercializacion distribucion consumo product alimentari pequena escala estudio caso utilizo metodologia investigacion accion estudiaron caracteristic seis celul produccion-consumo ubicad region sureste coahuila ciudad monterrey nuevo leon partir analisis teorico redes colaboracion solidaria rcs evidencia empirica caso estudio puede senalar celul productiv consumo tienen caracteristic estructural funcional tienden conformar verdadera rcs contribuye atender necesidad sus integrant mejor calidad vida pero bajo condicion superan relacion mera mercantil explotacion manifiestan circuit mercado convencional final concluye caso estudiado no limita generacion ingres economic sino promueven intercambio cultura saber experienci amistad prevalece etica cuidado salud humana ambiente aautor correspondencia correo electronico ernesto navarro uaaan edu mx cuadern desarrollo rural colombia vol 23 2026 sistema agroalimentario economia solidaria circuit cort towards the creation of agri-food collaboration networks in the northeast region of mexico,1.0.0,8eea183eb7a75295
2215-7727,Cuadernos6732892003.pdf,Cuadernos6732892003_0,en,"o tienen características estructurales y funcionales que tienden a conformar una verdadera RCS,","The global agri-food system has led to the exclusion of small-scale actors who are unable to fit into the dynamics imposed by global capital logic, which considers them inefficient and redundant. As a result, many of those excluded have developed strategies to maintain themselves and survive. The objective of this article is to analyze the formation of a collaboration network in northeastern Mexico, based on a case study of the characteristics of the links, practices, and experiences of small-scale food production, marketing, distribution, and consumption. The action research methodology was used to study the characteristics of six production-consumption cells located in the southeastern region of Coahuila and in the city of Monterrey, Nuevo León. Based on the theoretical analysis of Solidarity Collaboration Networks (SCNs) and the empirical evidence from the case study, it can be noted that productive and consumer cells have structural and functional characteristics that tend to form a true SCN, which contributes to meeting the needs of its members, improving their quality of life, but under conditions that go beyond the purely commercial and exploitative relationships found in conventional market circuits. Finally, it is concluded that the case studied is not limited to the generation of economic income, but also promotes the exchange of culture, knowledge, experiences, and friendships, where an ethic of care for human health and the environment prevails","Agri-Food System, Solidarity Economy, Short Supply Chains",marcadores,tienen caracteristica estructural funcional que tienden conformar una verdadera rcs,global agri-food system has led exclusion small-scale actor who unable fit into dynamic impos global capital logic which consider them inefficient redundant result many those exclud have develop strategi m