2215-7727,Cuadernos6732892004.pdf,Cuadernos6732892004_0,en,"cción orgánica, mejores rendimientos, uso de semillas nativas o","The objective of this article is to analyze how public policies implemented by the Mexican government support or hinder the work of Alternative Food Networks (AFNs) and their efforts to build food sovereignty in their territories. To this end, 13 federal programs and two laws in force during the 2018-2024 period were reviewed. These programs and laws consider agroecology, the social solidarity economy, and food sovereignty, among other aspects, in order to determine their accessibility, the challenges they involve, their areas of opportunity, and their current impact on the AFNs. Among the main findings of this review was that the instruments mentioned are insufficient to facilitate the work of the AFNs and generate consolidated and more far-reaching organizational processes. The lack of differentiation in the incentives offered to producers depending on whether or not they adopt more sustainable practices—organic production, better yields, use of native or creole seeds, etc.—and the lack of support for collective organization and management are recurring themes. However, we observed that the AFNs participate in programs that indirectly affect their work. In order to design public policies that strengthen AFNs, it is first necessary to recognize the work carried out by these networks, promote their self-determination, and provide conditions and tools that enable them to resolve the problems they face on their own. The aim is to enable their emergence, growth, and integration, and to ensure that they actively participate in the construction and evolution of public policies themselves","Food Sovereignty, Agroecology, Social And Solidarity Economy, Federal Programs",marcadores,ccion organica mejor rendimiento uso de semilla nativa,objective article analyze how public polici implement mexican government support hinder work alternative food network afns their effort build food sovereignty their territori end 13 federal program two laws force during 2018-2024 period review these program laws consider agroecology social solidarity economy food sovereignty among other aspect order determine their accessibility challeng they involve their area opportunity their current impact afns among main finding review instrument mention insufficient facilitate work afns generate consolidat more far-reach organizational process lack differentiation incentiv offer producer depend whether not they adopt more sustainable practices--organic production better yield use native creole seed etc --and lack support collective organ management recurr them however we observ afns participate program indirectly affect their work order design public polici strengthen afns first necessary recognize work carri out these network promote their self-determination provide condition tool enable them resolve problem they face their own aim enable their emergence growth integration ensure they actively participate construction evolution public polici themselv,food sovereignty agroecology social solidarity economy federal program,ccion organica mejor rendimiento uso de semilla nativa objective article analyze how public polici implement mexican government support hinder work alternative food network afns their effort build food sovereignty their territori end 13 federal program two laws force during 2018-2024 period review these program laws consider agroecology social solidarity economy food sovereignty among other aspect order determine their accessibility challeng they involve their area opportunity their current impact afns among main finding review instrument mention insufficient facilitate work afns generate consolidat more far-reach organizational process lack differentiation incentiv offer producer depend whether not they adopt more sustainable practices--organic production better yield use native creole seed etc --and lack support collectiv