politica sociedad rural mexicana expresa trav practic clientelar refuerzan vincul dependencia entre campesin funcionari public politic public campo neoliberalismo clientelismo politico the procampo model 1994-2024 the impact on rural areas through agricultural polici in mexico,1.0.0,fbeb4dee175fcfbc
2215-7727,Cuadernos6732892005.pdf,Cuadernos6732892005_0,en,adas y las relaciones entre estas;,"PROCAMPO, created in 1994 to mitigate the effects of NAFTA on Mexican peasant economies, was established in Mexico as an emblem of public policy for agricultural development, based on a compensatory scheme that accompanied neoliberal reforms. PROCAMPO was analyzed as an example of trends in agricultural policy, exploring how it reflects the strategies and objectives that have guided Mexican agricultural policy, and how some political narratives are integrated into the country’s institutional structures and bureaucratic processes. Using a historical-institutional analysis of the program’s implementation and transformation over six presidential terms, we examined 1) the program’s structure, based on the network of institutions involved and the relationships between them; 2) its operation, identifying regulatory and financial mechanisms and its scope (beneficiaries and areas covered); and 3) adjustments based on the objectives of each presidential term. The institutional structure was found to mirror the Mexican neoliberal paradox, where the narrative that modernization requires less state participation in productive sectors is reproduced, while the image of the welfare state, deeply rooted in Mexican politics and rural society, persists and is expressed through patronage practices that reinforce ties of dependency between farmers and public officials","Public Policies for Rural Areas, Neoliberalism, Political Patronage",marcadores,adas las relacion entre esta,procampo creat 1994 mitigate effect nafta mexican peasant economi establish mexico emblem public policy agricultural development based compensatory scheme accompani neoliberal reform procampo analyz example trend agricultural policy explor how reflect strategi objectiv have guid mexican agricultural policy how some political narrativ integrat into country institutional structur bureaucratic process using historical-institutional analysi program implementation transformation over six presidential term we examin program structure based network institution involv relationship between them its operation identify regulatory financial mechanism its scope beneficiari area cover adjustment based objectiv each presidential term institutional structure found mirror mexican neoliberal paradox where narrative modern requir less state participation productive sector reproduc while image welfare state deeply root mexican politic rural society persist express through patronage practic reinforce ties dependency between farmer public official,public polici rural area neoliberalism political patronage,adas las relacion entre esta procampo creat 1994 mitigate effect nafta mexican peasant economi establish mexico emblem public policy agricultural development based compensatory scheme accompani neoliberal reform procampo analyz example trend agricultural policy explor how reflect strategi objectiv have guid mexican agricultural policy how some political narrativ integrat into country institutional structur bureaucratic process using historical-institutional analysi program implementation transformation over six presidential term we examin program structure based network institution involv relationship between them its operation identify regulatory financial mechanism its scope beneficiari area cover adjustment based objectiv each presidential term institutional structure found mirror mexican neoliberal paradox where narrative modern requir less state participation productive sector reproduc while image welfare state deeply root mexican politic rural society persist express through patronage practic reinforce ties dependency between farmer public official public polici rural area neoliberalism political patronage,1.0.0,beadf2146651dfc4
2215-7840,document (2).pdf,document (2)_0,es,Percepciones parentales sobre la vacuna contra el,"Introducción: el cáncer de cérvix es el cuarto más frecuente en mujeres a nivel mundial, vinculado al Virus del Papiloma Humano (VPH), cuya prevención se centra en la vacunación. En Colombia, la tasa de vacunación contra el VPH disminuyó tras el incidente de Carmen de Bolívar en 2014, sin haberse recuperado ni conocerse la percepción actual de los padres frente a la vacuna. Objetivo: determinar los factores asociados a la aceptabilidad de la vacuna contra el VPH por parte de padres de niñas menores de trece años, en dos municipios de la Región Caribe, colombiana. Métodos: se realizó un estudio analítico transversal, aplicando un instrumento a padres en San Juan Nepomuceno y San Jacinto, entre noviembre 2022 y diciembre 2023, indagando sus características sociodemográficas y conocimientos sobre el VPH. Resultados: fueron encuestados 238 padres (122 en San Juan y 116 en San Jacinto), de los cuales 87,39 % fueron mujeres. En San Juan, 93,4% pertenecía al estrato socioeconómico 1 frente a 62,07% en San Jacinto. El conocimiento sobre el VPH fue mayor en San Juan (84,4%) comparado con San Jacinto (68,97%). La aceptación de la vacuna alcanzó el 79,5% (73.49% mayores de 30 años) en San Juan, y el 74,14% (84.01% menores de 30 años) en San Jacinto. Conclusión: la desconfianza frente a los efectos adversos constituye la principal barrera para la vacunación en la población estudiada. En San Juan, la aceptación se relaciona con el conocimiento sobre el VPH, mientras en San Jacinto, con factores sociodemográficos. Es crucial implementar estrategias adaptadas a las necesidades de cada comunidad","Vacunación; Virus del Papiloma Humano; Cáncer de cuello uterino; Educación en Salud; Salud Pública; Factores Socioeconómicos; Aceptación de la Atención de Salud. ARTÍCULO ORIGINAL R E V I S T A C I E N C I A S B I O M É D I C A S Para citaciones: Mendoza Carmona, L., Payares Flórez, S., Durán Cordero, V., Marrugo Ortiz, A., Alvis Estrada, L., y Benedetti Padrón, I. (2025). Percepcione",marcadores,percepcion parental sobre vacuna contra,introduccion cancer cervix cuarto mas frecuente mujer nivel mundial vinculado virus papiloma humano vph cuya prevencion centra vacunacion colombia tasa vacunacion contra vph disminuyo tras incidente carmen bolivar 2014 sin haberse recuperado ni conocerse percepcion actual padr frente vacuna objetivo determinar factor asociad aceptabilidad vacuna contra vph parte padr ninas menor trece anos dos municipi region caribe colombiana metod realizo estudio analitico transversal aplic instrumento padr san juan nepomuceno san jacinto entre noviembre 2022 diciembre 2023 indag sus caracteristic sociodemografic conoc sobre vph resultad fueron encuestad 238 padr 122 san juan 116 san jacinto cual 87 39 fueron mujer san juan 93 pertenecia estrato socioeconomico frente 62 07 san jacinto conocimiento sobre vph fue mayor san juan 84 comparado san jacinto 68 97 aceptacion vacuna alcanzo 79 73 49 mayor 30 anos san juan 74 14 84 01 menor 30 anos san jacinto conclusion desconfianza frente efect advers constituye principal barrera vacunacion poblacion estudiada san juan aceptacion relaciona conocimiento sobre vph mientr san jacinto factor sociodemografic crucial implementar estrategi adaptad necesidad cada comunidad,vacunacion virus papiloma humano cancer cuello uterino educacion salud salud publica factor socioeconomic aceptacion atencion salud articulo original citacion mendoza carmona payar florez duran cordero marrugo ortiz alvis estrada benedetti padron 2025 percepcione,percepcion parental sobre vacuna contra introduccion cancer cervix cuarto mas frecuente mujer nivel mundial vinculado virus papiloma humano vph cuya prevencion centra vacunacion colombia tasa vacunacion contra vph disminuyo tras incidente carmen bolivar 2014 sin haberse recuperado ni conocerse percepcion actual padr frente vacuna objetivo determinar factor asociad aceptabilidad vacuna contra vph parte padr ninas menor trece anos dos municipi region caribe colombiana metod realizo estudio analitico transversal aplic instrumento padr san juan nepomuceno san jacinto entre noviembre 2022 diciembre 2023 indag sus caracteristic sociodemografic conoc sobre vph resultad fueron encuestad 238 padr 122 san juan 116 san jacinto cual 87 39 fueron mujer san juan 93 pertenecia estrato socioeconomico frente 62 07 san jacinto conocimiento sobre vph fue mayor san juan 84 comparado san jacinto 68 97 aceptacion vacuna alcanzo 79 73 49 mayor 30 anos san juan 74 14 84 01 menor 30 anos san jacinto conclusion desconfianza frente efect advers constituye principal barrera vacunacion poblacion estudiada san juan aceptacion relaciona conocimiento sobre vph mientr san jacinto factor sociodemografic crucial implementar estrategi adaptad necesidad cada comunidad vacunacion virus papiloma humano cancer cuello uterino educacion salud salud publica factor socioeconomic aceptacion atencion salud articulo original citacion mendoza carmona payar florez duran cordero marrugo ortiz alvis estrada benedetti padron 2025 percepcione,1.0.0,215743c7fab47b0e
2215-7840,document (2).pdf,document (2)_0,en,Aprobado: 7 de julio de 2025,"Introduction: cervical cancer is the fourth most common cancer in women worldwide, linked to the Human Papillomavirus (HPV), and prevention is centered on vaccination. In Colombia, the HPV vaccination rate declined after the Carmen de Bolívar incident in 2014, and it has not recovered, nor is it known how parents currently view the vaccine. Objective: to determine the factors associated with the acceptability of the HPV vaccine among parents of girls under thirteen years of age in two populations of the Caribbean region of Colombia. Methods: a cross-sectional analytical study was conducted by administering an instrument to parents residing in the municipalities of San Juan Nepomuceno and San Jacinto between November 2022 and December 2023, investigating their sociodemographic characteristics and knowledge about HPV. Results: a total of 238 parents were surveyed (122 in San Juan and 116 in San Jacinto), of whom 87.39% were women. In San Juan, 93.4% belonged to socioeconomic stratum 1 compared to 62.07% in San Jacinto. Knowledge about HPV was higher in San Juan (84.4%) compared to San Jacinto (68.97%). Vaccine acceptance reached 79.5% (73.49% over 30 years of age) in San Juan, and 74.14% (84.01% under 30 years of age) in San Jacinto. Conclusions: mistrust of adverse effects is the main barrier to vaccination in the population studied. In San Juan, acceptance is related to knowledge about HPV, while in San Jacinto, it is related to sociodemographic factors. It is crucial to implement strategies tailored to the needs of each community",Vaccination; Human Papillomavirus; Cervical Cancer; Health Education; Public Health; Socioeconomic Factors; Health Care Acceptance,marcadores,aprobado de julio de 2025,introduction cervical cancer fourth most common cancer women worldwide link human papillomaviru hpv prevention center vaccination colombia hpv vaccination rate declin after carmen de bolivar incident