2215-7840,document (3).pdf,document (3)_0,en,Editor: Inés Benedetti. Universidad de,"Introduction: menstruation can cause a variety of physical and emotional symptoms that influence women’s well-being and daily performance. Objective: to identify menstrual symptoms and their association with biopsychosocial alterations in a group of medical students from the University of Cartagena. Methods: a descriptive cross-sectional epidemiological study was conducted among 153 women of reproductive age enrolled in the Medicine program. The MEDI-Q and SSAL questionnaires were applied to assess symptoms, activities, and perceptions during and outside the menstrual period. Results: the mean age of participants was 20.6 years (SD ±2.41); 29.4% were adolescents, 66.6% had normal weight, 35.3% engaged in physical activity, 62.7% had a partner, and 37.7% used contraceptive methods. The most frequent symptoms were breast tenderness or swelling, irritability, and anger. No correlation was found between age or body mass index (BMI) and the quantity or severity of symptoms. Participants aged 20–21 years reported spending more time on affective and academic activities during menstruation. Adolescents reported greater satisfaction and engagement in academic, social, and personal activities outside the menstrual period. Conclusions: the predominant symptoms during menstruation in this population include both physical and psychological manifestations. Overall, students tended to spend less time on and enjoy their activities less during menstruation",Menstruation; Medical students; Biopsychosocial model; Psychological stress; Quality of life; Women’s health,marcadores,editor ines benedetti universidad de,introduction menstruation can cause variety physical emotional symptom influence women well-be daily performance objective identify menstrual symptom their association biopsychosocial alter group medical student university cartagena method descriptive cross-sectional epidemiological study conduct among 153 women reproductive age enroll medicine program medi-q ssal questionnair appli asses symptom activiti perception during outside menstrual period result mean age participant 20 year sd -2 41 29 adolescent 66 had normal weight 35 engag physical activity 62 had partner 37 used contraceptive method most frequent symptom breast tendernes swell irritability anger no correlation found between age body mass index bmi quantity severity symptom participant aged 20-21 year report spend more time affective academic activiti during menstruation adolescent report greater satisfaction engagement academic social personal activiti outside menstrual period conclusion predominant symptom during menstruation population include both physical psychological manifest overall student tend spend less time enjoy their activiti less during menstruation,menstruation medical student biopsychosocial model psychological stres quality life women health,editor ines benedetti universidad de introduction menstruation can cause variety physical emotional symptom influence women well-be daily performance objective identify menstrual symptom their association biopsychosocial alter group medical student university cartagena method descriptive cross-sectional epidemiological study conduct among 153 women reproductive age enroll medicine program medi-q ssal questionnair appli asses symptom activiti perception during outside menstrual period result mean age participant 20 year sd -2 41 29 adolescent 66 had normal weight 35 engag physical activity 62 had partner 37 used contraceptive method most frequent symptom breast tendernes swell irritability anger no correlation found between age body mass index bmi quantity severity symptom participant aged 20-21 year report spend more time affective academic activiti during menstruation adolescent report greater satisfaction engagement academic social personal activiti outside menstrual period conclusion predominant symptom during menstruation population