2215-7840,document (6).pdf,document (6)_0,en,dados Intensivos Pediátricos por el riesgo de complicaciones. El,"Introduction: SARS-CoV-2 infection has a prevalence of 7.6% in the Colombian pediatric population, however, only 0.03% to 0.4% of these patients are admitted to ARTÍCULO DE REVISIÓN R E V I S T A C I E N C I A S B I O M É D I C A S Para citaciones: Montes Fontalvo, L., y Escamilla Arrieta, J. (2025). Factores de riesgo asociados a falla multiorgánica en pacientes pediátricos con diagnóstico de infección por SARS-COV2. Revista Ciencias Biomédicas, 14(2), 84-99. https://doi.org/ Recibido: 26 de noviembre de 2024 Aprobado: 25 de marzo de 2025 Publicado: 15 de abril de 2025 Autor de correspondencia: Laura Montes Fontalvo laura.montes92@hotmail.com Editor: Inés Benedetti. Universidad de Cartagena-Colombia. Copyright: © 2025. Montes Fontalvo, L., y Escamilla Arrieta, J. Este es un artículo de acceso abierto, distribuido bajo los términos de la licencia https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-ncnd/4.0/ la cual permite el uso sin restricciones, distribución y reproducción en cualquier medio, siempre y cuando el original, el autor y la fuente sean acreditados. Factores de riesgo asociados a falla multiorgánica en pacientes pediátricos con diagnóstico de infección por SARS-COV2 the intensive care unit with factors that could contribute to the development of multiple organ failure. Objective: to determine the risk factors associated with the presence of multiple organ failure in pediatric patients diagnosed with SARS-CoV-2 infection. Methods: all children aged 1 month to 18 years hospitalized between March 2020 and January 2022 at the Napoleón Franco Pareja Children's Hospital, Cartagena, Colombia, with a confirmed diagnosis of SARS-COV-2 infection were studied. The association between demographic, biochemical, and imaging variables and outcomes such as acute respiratory distress syndrome, septic shock, multisystem inflammation associated with COVID-19, acute kidney injury, and myocardial damage was investigated. Results: forty-three patients were included, 60.5% of whom were diagnosed with COVID-19-related multisystem inflammatory syndrome, and a high percentage of whom required admission to pediatric intensive care due to the risk of complications. Eleven point six percent of patients had immunosuppression associated with severe (18.6%) and critical (25.6%) disease. A statistically significant association was found between the development of multiple organ failure (14%) and the presence of comorbidities (p=0.00416), disease severity (p=0.0113), and decreased ejection fraction (p=0.0278). Conclusions: pediatric patients with confirmed SARS-CoV-2 infection (COVID-19) rarely present with multiple organ failure. An association was found between the development of multiple organ failure and elevated LDH, myocardial injury established during infection, and the presence of comorbidities, especially those involving primary immunodeficiencies",Covid-19; multiorgan failure; risk factors; outcomes; children,marcadores,dado intensivo pediatrico por el riesgo de complicacion el,introduction sars-cov-2 infection has prevalence colombian pediatric population however only 03 these patient admitt articulo de revision para citacion mont fontalvo escamilla arrieta 2025 factor de riesgo asociado falla multiorganica en pacient pediatrico con diagnostico de infeccion por sars-cov2 revista ciencia biomedica 14 84-99 http doi org recibido 26 de noviembre de 2024 aprobado 25 de marzo de 2025 publicado 15 de abril de 2025 autor de correspondencia laura mont fontalvo laura montes92 hotmail com editor ines benedetti universidad de cartagena-colombia copyright 2025 mont fontalvo escamilla arrieta este es un articulo de acceso abierto distribuido bajo los termino de la licencia http creativecommon org licens by-ncnd la cual permite el uso sin restriccion distribucion reproduccion en cualquier medio siempre cuando el original el autor la fuente sean acredit