2215-8944,(9).+(2025).+RA&D.+Artículo.+Límites+a+la+libertad+de+contratación+en+las+técnicas+de+reproducción+humana+asistida+en+Colombia.pdf,(9).+(2025).+RA&D.+Artículo.+Límites+a+la+libertad+de+contratación+en+las+técnicas+de+reproducción+humana+asistida+en+Colombia_0,en,d ha sido denominada como la escogencia del,"Genetic engineering has been providing medical science with biological technologies that make it possible to improve the physical, functional, and organic conditions of human beings. The use of these technologies is advancing across all fields and, while generating alternatives to overcome human functional and organic deficiencies, it also produces legal and ethical uncertainties. The development of biotechnology, genetic engineering, artificial intelligence, and liberal eugenics, among others, constitutes scientific advances that raise a series of questions and give rise to interdisciplinary debates. Transhumanism has been understood as a scientific movement that seeks the enhancement of humanity and, to this end, makes use of technoscientific advances (Rueda, 2020). In pursuit of this evolutionary aspiration of the human being, transhumanism resorts to reproductive biotechnologies, particularly assisted human reproduction techniques, which allow for the selection of certain genetic characteristics of the conceived subject; that is, access to the possibility of achieving the goal of a desired child, free from the limitations imposed by natural biological processes. This possibility has been referred to as the selection of the best possible child, in accordance with the principle of procreative beneficence (J. Savulescu, 2001). Undoubtedly, transhumanism has become a fertile ground for the emergence of multidisciplinary, ethical, moral, Límites a la libertad de contratación en las técnicas de reproducción humana asistida en Colombia: un enfoque desde el transhumanismo 3 Revista Academia & Derecho, Año 16. No. 31, p.p. 1-19 Julio – Diciembre 2025. E-ISSN: 2539 – 4983 Artículo de Investigación legal, and scientific debates, which is why it is innovative to approach the study of the limits of freedom of contract within the context of assisted human reproduction techniques. The research adopts a qualitative approach, of a legal, dogmatic, and descriptive nature, and has as its central focus an analysis of freedom of contract and its limits, applied to the case of assisted human reproduction techniques, thereby allowing for a perspective informed by transhumanism","assisted human reproduction techniques, freedom of contract, limits, transhumanism",marcadores,ha sido denominada como la escogencia del,genetic engineer has been provid medical science biological technologi make possible improve physical functional organic condition human being use these technologi advanc acros all field while generat alternativ overcome human functional organic deficienci also produc legal ethical uncertainti development biotechnology genetic engineer artificial intelligence liberal eugenic among other constitut scientific advanc raise seri question give rise interdisciplinary debat transhumanism has been understood scientific movement seek enhancement humanity end make use technoscientific advanc rueda 2020 pursuit evolutionary aspiration human being transhumanism resort reproductive biotechnologi particularly assist human reproduction techniqu which allow selection certain genetic characteristic conceiv subject acces possibility achiev goal desir child free limit impos natural biological process possibility has been referr selection best possible child accordance principle procreative beneficence savulescu 2001 undoubt transhumanism has become fertile ground emergence multidisciplinary ethical moral limit la libertad de contratacion en las tecnica de reproduccion humana asistida en colombia un enfoque desde el transhumanismo revista academia derecho ano 16 no 31 1-19 julio diciembre 2025 e-issn 2539 4983 articulo de investigacion legal sc