2215-9959,A3_MAVAE+21-1_vfw2.pdf,A3_MAVAE+21-1_vfw2_0,en,encarnado entre lo íntimo y lo colectivo. La escritura,"] [RESUMO] This article reflects on contemporary Latin American artistic practices that deal with the body as a meeting-ground for memory and resistance. Through an examination of the works of Tatiana Parcero, Carolina Agüero, Malu Valerio and Gabriela Carmona, the text explores how writing (in its various material incarnations) becomes a gesture of symbolic restitution for historical, colonial, and gendered acts of violence that stretch across the region. These products, anchored in contexts of displacement, deprivation and inequality, articulate a poetics of the wound, wherein the body becomes the foundation for both individual and collective memories. The text also addresses the ecological dimension of the Latin American wound, understanding the environmental crisis as an extension of colonial trauma. Through an ecofeminist gaze, writing and art become practices of reconnecting with all beings and all matter on the planet in dialog with the notion of “vibrant matter” originated by Jane Bennett. This perspective widens our concept of “body”, joining the human, the animal and the territorial to create an interspecies connection in which these things coexist in a web of reciprocity. Finally, the text reflects on the voice and on hybrid languages as places of resistance. Recovering our words is a political act that defies colonial hierarchies of speech. To write from Latin America is to write from a wound, as well as from the possibility of a language that comes into being between intimacy and collectivity. Handwriting, and using the body to write, establish themselves as gestures of memory and care on a continent that continues to write itself on its own skin","body; memory; wound; writing; territory Este artigo propõe uma reflexão sobre práticas artísticas contemporâneas latino-americanas que abordam o corpo como território de memória e resistência. A partir de um percurso pelas obras de Tatiana Parcero, Carolina Agüero, Malu Valerio e Gabriela Carmona, explora-se como a escrita (em suas múltiplas materialidades) se torna um gesto de restituição",marcadores,encarnado entre lo intimo lo colectivo la escritura,resumo article reflect contemporary latin american artistic practic deal body meeting-ground memory resistance through examination work tatiana parcero carolina aguero malu valerio gabriela carmona text explor how writ its variou material incarn becom gesture symbolic restitution historical colonial gender acts violence stretch acros region these product anchor context displacement deprivation inequality articulate poetic wound wherein body becom foundation both individual collective memori text also address ecological dimension latin american wound understand environmental crisi extension colonial trauma through ecofeminist gaze writ art become practic reconnect all being all matter planet dialog notion vibrant matter originat jane bennett perspective widen our concept body join human animal territorial create interspeci connection which these thing coexist web reciprocity finally text reflect voice hybrid languag plac resistance recover our word political act defi colonial hierarchi speech write latin america write wound well possibility language come into being between intimacy collectivity handwrit using body write establish themselv gestur memory care continent continu write itself its own skin,body memory wound writ territory este artigo propoe uma reflexao sobre pratica artistica contemporanea latino-americana que abordam corpo como territorio de memoria resistencia partir de um percurso pela obra de tatiana parcero carolina aguero malu valerio gabriela carmona explora-se como escrita em suas multipla materialidad se torna um gesto de restituicao,encarnado entre lo intimo lo colectivo la escritura resumo article reflect contemporary latin american artistic practic deal body meeting-ground memory resistance through examination work tatiana parcero carolina aguero malu valerio gabriela carmona text explor how writ its variou material incarn becom gesture symbolic restitution historical colonial gender acts violence stretch acros region these product anchor context displacement deprivation inequality articulate poetic wound wherein body becom foundation both individual collective memori text also address ecological dimension latin american wound understand environmental crisi extension colonial trauma through ecofeminist gaze writ art become practic reconnect all being all matter planet dialog notion vibrant matter originat jane bennett perspective widen our concept body join human animal territorial create interspeci connection which these thing coexist web reciprocity finally text reflect voice hybrid languag plac resistance recover our word political act defi colonial hierarchi speech write latin america write wound well possibility language come into being between intimacy collectivity handwrit using body write establish themselv gestur memory care continent continu write itself its own skin body memory wound writ territory este artigo propoe uma reflexao sobre pratica artistica contemporanea latino-americana que abordam corpo como territorio de memoria resistencia partir de um percurso pela obra de tatiana parcero carolina aguero malu valerio gabriela carmona explora-se como escrita em suas multipla materialidad se torna um gesto de restituicao,1.0.0,8b69eff46fda41b1
2215-9959,A4_MAVAE+21-2_vfw.pdf,A4_MAVAE+21-2_vfw_0,es,CÓMO CITAR:,"] El arco y la letra: una aproximación sensible y sonora a la obra de Antonio Di Benedetto* Valentina Spina Zapata** Este artículo indaga el problema del sonido, la literatura y la escucha en la obra de Antonio Di Benedetto, a partir del hallazgo de la oralidad materna como matriz de su prosa. Se describe el trayecto en el que una investigación, inicialmente teórica, sobre la novela El silenciero (1964), desborda los límites del texto para entablar un diálogo con otros lenguajes artísticos y con aspectos biográficos de la autora. A través de este recorrido, se reconstruye una historia sensible que recupera la sonoridad del universo de Di Benedetto mediante múltiples dimensiones de la voz: la literaria, la grabada y la del instrumento. Este proceso se materializa en los proyectos Di Benedetto: Derivas sonoras (Valentina Spina Zapata, 2021) y el film Vidas imaginarias (Federico Cardone, 2026)",Antonio Di Benedetto; voz; escucha; cuerpo. Doi 10.11144/javeriana.mavae21-2.also Fecha de recepción: 2 de enero de 2026 Fecha de aceptación: 6 de marzo de 2026 Disponible en línea: 1 de julio de 2026 Artículo de investigación. Doctoranda del programa de Ciencias Sociales de la Facultad de Ciencias Políticas y Sociales (FCPyS) de la Universidad Nacional de Cuyo (UNCuyo). Becaria doctoral de C,marcadores,como citar,arco letra aproximacion sensible sonora obra antonio di benedetto valentina spina zapata este articulo indaga problema sonido literatura escucha obra antonio di benedetto partir hallazgo oralidad materna como matriz prosa describe trayecto investigacion inicial teorica sobre novela silenciero 1964 desborda limit texto entablar dialogo otros lenguaj artistic aspect biografic autora trav este recorrido reconstruye historia sensible recupera sonoridad universo di benedetto mediante multipl dimension voz literaria grabada instrumento este proceso materializa proyect di benedetto deriv sonor valentina spina