2215-9959,A6_MAVAE+21-2_vfw.pdf,A6_MAVAE+21-2_vfw_0,en,veriana.mavae21-2.eamp,"] [RESUMO] This article proposes aguaje — a concept, native to the Colombian Pacific, of the particularity of sound in different areas of land — as a situated epistemology for analyzing ongoing negotiation between tradition and globalization. Through a sound ethnography of music group Cantares del Pacífico, it is shown that aguaje operates as an aesthetic, political, and methodological category. Aesthetically, the concept bases musical creation on the rhythms of water and mangroves. Politically, it functions as a tool for cultural resistance against folklorization, reconfiguring gender roles and reaffirming a bond with the land. Methodologically, it reveals itself as an ethical principle for decolonial research. Our analysis shows that the group’s participation in global circuits does not imply a rejection of their roots, but an active negotiation that creates intergenerational dialog, female agency and embodied memory. Thus, aguaje becomes a keystone for understanding how regional musical genres legitimate themselves, how they circulate and persist in transnational contexts without diluting their communitarian roots","aguaje; situated epistemology; sound ethnography; cultural resistance; Cantares del Pacífico; music industry. Este artigo propõe o aguaje — conceito nativo do Pacífico colombiano que designa a particularidade sonora de cada território — como uma epistemologia situada para analisar as negociações entre tradição e globalização. Por meio de uma etnografia sonora do grupo Cantares del Pacífico, de",marcadores,veriana mavae21-2 eamp,resumo article propos aguaje -- concept native colombian pacific particularity sound different area land -- situat epistemology analyz ongo negotiation between tradition global through sound ethnography music group cantar del pacifico shown aguaje operat aesthetic political methodological category aesthetically concept base musical creation rhythm wa