2215-9959,A7_MAVAE+21-2_vfw.pdf,A7_MAVAE+21-2_vfw_0,en,"estigación social, proponiendo un","] [RESUMO] Between Reality and Fiction, the Academic and the Artistic: The Creative Process of a Documentary Theatre Piece Based on a Sound Ethnography in Istanbul’s Beyoğlu District This article explores the potential of documentary theatre, particularly verbatim theatre, as a methodological and creative tool for disseminating social science research. To this end, it examines the creative process behind the play Beyoğlu: Los sonidos de Estambul (Conchi Mateo Pacheco, 2021), which premiered in Spain in 2021 as the outcome of anthropological fieldwork conducted several years earlier in Istanbul with the support of the Völkerkundemuseum (Zurich) and the Center for Advanced Studies in Music (MIAM, Istanbul). Drawing on the analysis of three documentary theatre productions undertaken as part of a final degree project in Dramatic Arts, the article proposes a set of guidelines for developing dramaturgies that move between reality and fiction, fostering interdisciplinary dialogue and creative practice. This case also provides an opportunity to reflect on key issues in both social research—such as documentary rigour and the role of the anthropologist—and theatrical creation, including distancing in autofiction and character construction. Finally, it proposes sound ethnography and active listening as generative forces for both artistic creation and social research, offering a model through which artistic practice can serve as a bridge for the public dissemination of academic research","sound ethnography; documentary theater; theater anthropology; verbatim. Entre a realidade e a ficção, oacadêmico e o artístico: o processo criativo de uma peça de teatro-documento a partir de uma etnografia sonora no bairro de Beyoğlu, em Istambul Neste artigo, apresento as possibilidades do teatro-documento, especialmente do verbatim, como ferramenta metodológica e criativa para a difusão",marcadores,e