2216-1368,art+corr+3953.pdf,art+corr+3953_0,en,es y una arquitectura de referencia que integra componentes de,"— The adoption of blockchain technologies has fostered the development of decentralized platforms aimed at managing digital assets, smart contracts, Web3 applications, and markets based on nonfungible tokens (NFTs). However, the architectural design of these platforms remains a significant challenge due to the need to balance often conflicting properties such as decentralization, security, scalability, interoperability, and operational cost. Although the scientific literature has extensively addressed specific aspects related to consensus mechanisms, distributed storage, smart contracts, and scalability solutions, a conceptual fragmentation persists, hindering the construction of comprehensive architectural frameworks for the development of decentralized systems. This article presents a structured technical review aimed at synthesizing existing knowledge on blockchain architectures and proposing a multi-layer reference framework for decentralized platforms. The adopted methodology is based on technical review principles and comparative analysis, organizing the literature around five architectural dimensions: data storage, execution infrastructure, security, interoperability, and user experience. As a result, a taxonomy of architectural models, a comparison of relevant blockchain platforms, and a reference architecture integrating presentation, service, persistence, smart contract, and external integration components are developed. Additionally, a set of metrics is proposed to evaluate scalability, decentralization, interoperability, and operational costs, accompanied by a formal cost function applicable to blockchain platforms. Finally, an illustrative case is presented to demonstrate the application of the proposed framework in the conceptual design of a digital asset platform. The results suggest that hybrid architectures currently represent the most suitable approach for balancing technical and operational requirements in general-purpose decentralized applications","— Blockchain Architecture, NFT, Smart Contracts, Decentralized Storage, Scalability, Interoperability, Security. 1",marcadores,es una arquitectura de referencia que integra component de,-- adoption blockchain technologi has foster development decentraliz platform aimed manag digital asset smart contract web3 applic market based nonfungible token nfts however architectural design these platform remain significant challenge due need balance often conflict properti such decentral security scalability interoperability operational cost although scientific literature has extensively address specific aspect relat consensu mechanism distribut storage smart contract scalability solution conceptual fragmentation persist hinder construction comprehensive architectural framework development decentraliz system article present structur technical review aimed synthesiz exist knowledge blockchain architectur propos multi-layer reference framework decentraliz platform adopt methodology based technical review principl comparative analysi organiz literature around five architectural dimension data storage execution infrastructure security interoperability user experience result taxonomy architectural model comparison relevant blockchain platform reference architecture integrat presentation service persistence smart contract external integration component develop additionally set metric propos evaluate scalability decentral interoperability operational cost accompani formal cost function applicable blockchain platform finally illustrative case present demonstrate application propos framework conceptual design digital asset platform result suggest hybrid architectur currently represent most suitable approach balanc technical operational requirement general-purpose decentraliz applic,-- blockchain architecture nft smart contract decentraliz storage scalability interoperability security,es una arquitectura de referencia que integra component de -- adoption blockchain technologi has foster development decentraliz platform aimed manag digital asset smart contract web3 applic market based nonfungible token nfts however architectural design these platform remain significant challenge due need balance often conflict properti such decentral security scalability interoperability operational cost although scientific literature has extensively address specific aspect relat consensu mechanism distribut storage smart contract scalability solution conceptual fragmentation persist hinder construction comprehensive architectural framework development decentraliz system article present structur technical review aimed synthesiz exist knowledge blockchain architectur propos multi-layer reference framework decentraliz platform adopt methodology based technical review principl comparative analysi organiz literature around five architectural dimension data storage execution infrastructure security interoperability user experience result taxonomy architectural model comparison relevant blockchain platform reference architecture integrat presentation service persistence smart contract external integration component develop additionally set metric propos evaluate scalability decentral interoperability operational cost accompani formal cost function applicable blockchain platform finally illustrative case present demonstrate application propos framework conceptual design digital asset platform result suggest hybrid architectur currently represent most suitable approach balanc technical operational requirement general-purpose decentraliz applic -- blockchain architecture nft smart contract decentraliz storage scalability interoperability security,1.0.0,ea45f566cbbd2df1
2216-1368,art+fcorr+3804.pdf,art+fcorr+3804_0,es,ntada y virtual,"La fotogrametría es una técnica utilizada para obtener información métrica y geométrica sobre objetos y entornos a partir de fotografías. Esta investigación tiene como objetivo proponer metodológica e integralmente la digitalización de muestras mediante fotogrametría con algoritmo Structure from Motion (SfM), orientada para su visualización en entornos de realidad aumentada y virtual. Metodológicamente se realizó revisión del estado del arte en las diferentes bases de datos académicas y científicas con el fin de conocer las tendencias referentes a los diferentes métodos integrales para la digitalización y visualización de muestras en entornos de realidad aumentada y virtual; posteriormente, se seleccionaron muestras y se acondicionó el entorno para la captura fotográfica y para el procesamiento fotogramétrico y modelado 3D se utilizó el software Agisoft Metashape Professional. La metodología integral propuesta para la digitalización de muestras geológicas mediante fotogrametría con algoritmo Structure from Motion (SfM) ha demostrado ser una herramienta eficaz y replicable para la generación de modelos tridimensionales de alta calidad. El uso de software especializado como Agisoft Metashape permitió obtener representaciones digitales precisas en términos geométricos y texturales, a partir de imágenes fotográficas capturadas bajo condiciones controladas","Digitalización, fotogrametría, realidad aumentada, realidad virtual, Structure from Motion. PROSPECTIVA VOL. 24 NÚMERO 2",marcadores,ntada virtual,fotogrametria tecnica utilizada obtener informacion metrica geometrica sobre objet entorn partir fotografi esta investigacion tiene como objetivo proponer metodologica integral digitalizacion muestr mediante fotogrametria algoritmo structure from motion sfm orientada visualizacion entorn realidad aumentada virtual metodologica realizo revision estado arte diferent bases datos academic cientific fin conocer t