2248-4078,OJUMa5129.pdf,OJUMa5129_0,en,ipios restaurativos al incorporar elementos como el reconocimiento de,"The objective of this article is to assess whether sanciones propias (own sanctions) —as interpreted by the Special Jurisdiction for Peace (JEP)— fulfill the purpose of positive special prevention (or prevention through integration); that is, whether they resocialize the individual and restore them to society in a constructive manner. To this end, the nature and functions of sanctions within transitional justice are analyzed. Priority is given to identifying the inherent purposes of these measures, considering their impact on truth, reparation, and non-repetition. The methodology comprises a documentary review. As a result, the study evaluates whether the JEP’s own sanctions promote restorative principles by incorporating elements such as the acknowledgment of responsibility, the redress of harm, and social contribution. Finally, challenges related to their implementation and their acceptance by ex-combatants are identified, concluding that their efficacy depends on a differentiated, verifiable, and sustained execution capable of balancing procedural guarantees, appearers’ (comparecientes) commitments, and public trust","transitional justice; special jurisdiction for peace; crime prevention; comprehensive victim reparation; criminal sanction. La dimensión restaurativa de las sanciones propias en la Jurisdicción Especial para la Paz... 3 Opinión Jurídica, 25(53) • enero-junio de 2026 a5129 • pp. 1-23 • ISSN (en línea): 2248-4078 A dimensão restaurativa das sanções próprias na Jurisdição Especial para a Paz: prev",marcadores,ipio restaurativo al incorporar elemento como el reconocimiento de,objective article asses whether sancion propia own sanction --as interpret special jurisdiction peace jep -- fulfill purpose positive special prevention prevention through integration whether they resocialize individual restore them society constructive manner end nature fu