2248-4345,Seec+67+art+5438.pdf,Seec+67+art+5438_0,en,"económica, mercado","This paper aims to analyze the direction and extent to which short-term occupational mobility patterns influence the regulatory and remunerative situation of an urban Argentine workforce in the post-pandemic period. Thus, this analysis examines Argentina's recovery, stagnation, and structural adjustment phases (2021-2024), testing the hypothesis that studied mobility processes and wage changes can be explained by the segmentation of quality employment opportunities due to productive gaps in the employment structure. To this end, interannual panel data from a Permanent Household Survey (EPH-TU) of the National Institute of Statistics and Censuses (INDEC) are used, and linear and logistic regression models with fixed effects are applied. The results show that the productive factors influencing occupational integration have unequal impacts on transitions between formal private sector jobs and informal microenterprises, exposing workers to precarious employment and income loss","Productive segmentation, occupational mobility, precarious employment, labor income. JEL CLASSIFICATION J62, O17 CONTENTS",marcadores,economica mercado,paper aims analyze direction extent which short-term occupational mobility pattern influence regulatory remunerative situation urban argentine workforce post-pandemic period thus analysi examin argentina recovery stagnation structural adjustment phas 2021-2024 test hypothesi studi mobility process wage chang can explain segmentation quality employment opportuniti due productive gaps employment structure end interannual panel data permanent household survey eph-tu national institute statistic census indec used linear logistic regression model fixed effect appli result show productive factor influenc occupational integration have unequal impact transition between formal private sector jobs informal microenterpris expos worker precariou employment income loss,productive segmentation occupational mobility precariou employment labor income jel classification j62 o17 content,economica mercado paper aims analyze direction extent which short-term occupational mobility pattern influence regulatory remunerative situation urban argentine workforce post-pandemic period thus analysi examin argentina recovery stagnation structural adjustment phas 2021-2024 test hypothesi studi mobility process wage chang can explain segmentation quality employment opportuniti due productive gaps employment structure end interannual panel data permanent household survey eph-tu national institute statistic census indec used linear logistic regression model fixed effect appli result show productive factor influenc occupational integration have unequal impact transition between formal private sector jobs informal microenterpris expos worker precariou employment income loss productive segmentation occupational mobility precariou employment labor income jel classification j62 o17 content,1.0.0,51ab4b62f12a33ec
2248-6011,02_(La+calidad+4.0)+Vol+21+Nº41_CLA+conv.pdf,02_(La+calidad+4.0)+Vol+21+Nº41_CLA+conv_0,es,"1. Magíster en Ciencias de la Calidad (Ingeniería y Ciencias Básicas) por la Universidad Autónoma de Tlaxcala, México. Profesor Universidad Politécnica","El objetivo de la presente investigación es realizar un análisis bibliométrico y una revisión sistemática de la literatura sobre el tema de la calidad 4.0, utilizando como evidencia la base de datos Scopus. El análisis bibliométrico identificó el número de publicaciones, autores con más artículos, países con más aportaciones a la calidad 4.0, y la revisión de la literatura determinó las barreras y líneas futuras de investigación a la calidad 4.0. Los resultados muestran que el año 2023 ha sido el de mayor producción científica; la India es el país con más aportaciones y Antony es el investigador más productivo en cuanto a la calidad 4.0. Las limitaciones de esta investigación son el periodo de 2017 a 2025, con la inclusión de solamente artículos en el idioma inglés. Un aporte novedoso es la modelación de la problemática como sistema abierto, empleando el concepto de caja negra y la categorización en personas, procesos y tecnología","calidad 4.0, industria 4.0, análisis bibliométrico y revisión de la literatura",marcadores,magister cienci calidad ingenieria cienci basic universidad autonoma tlaxcala mexico profesor universidad politecnica,objetivo presente investigacion realizar analisis bibliometrico revision sistematica literatura sobre tema calidad utiliz como evidencia base datos scopus analisis bibliometrico identifico numero public autor mas articul pais mas aport calidad revision literatura determino barrer line futur investigacion calidad resultad muestran ano 2023 ha sido mayor produccion cientifica india pais mas aport antony investigador mas productivo cuanto calidad limit esta investigacion son periodo 2017 2025 inclusion sola articul idioma ingl aporte novedoso modelacion problematica como sistema abierto emple concepto caja negra categorizacion person proces tecnologia,calidad industria analisis bibliometrico revision literatura,magister cienci calidad ingenieria cienci basic universidad autonoma tlaxcala mexico profesor universidad politecnica objetivo presente investigacion realizar analisis bibliometrico revision sistematica literatura sobre tema calidad utiliz como evidencia base datos scopus analisis bibliometrico identifico numero public autor mas articul pais mas aport calidad revision literatura determino barrer line futur investigacion calidad resultad muestran ano 2023 ha sido mayor produccion cientifica india pais mas aport antony investigador mas productivo cuanto calidad limit esta investigacion son periodo 2017 2025 inclusion sola articul idioma ingl aporte novedoso modelacion problematica como sistema abierto emple concepto caja negra categorizacion person proces tecnologia calidad industria analisis bibliometrico revision literatura,1.0.0,ffb5c1c9d2fa05e5
2248-6011,02_(La+calidad+4.0)+Vol+21+Nº41_CLA+conv.pdf,02_(La+calidad+4.0)+Vol+21+Nº41_CLA+conv_0,en,", utilizando como evidencia la base de datos Scopus. El análisis bibliométrico","The objective of this research is to conduct a bibliometric analysis and a systematic literature review on the topic of Quality 4.0, using the Scopus database. The bibliometric analysis identified the number of publications by authors with the most articles, and countries with the most contributions to Quality 4.0. The literature review determined the barriers and future lines of research for Quality 4.0. The results show that 2023 was the year with the highest scientific production, India is the country with the most contributions, and Antony is the most productive researcher in terms of Quality 4.0. The limitations of this research are the period from 2017 to 2025, with the inclusion of only articles in English. A novel contribution is the modeling of the problem as an open system, using the black box concept and categorizing it into people, processes, and technology","quality 4.0, industry 4.0, bibliometric analysis, and literature review. 1 Jul - Dic. 2025 | Volumen XXI - Número 41 | Págs.1-18 1 La calidad 4.0: análisis bibliométrico y revisión sistemática de la literatura | Gerardo Hernández Chávez y Yazmin Hernández Chávez, PhD",marcadores,utilizando como evidencia la base de dato scopu el analisi bibliometrico,objective research conduct bibliometric analysi systematic literature review topic quality using scopu database bibliometric analysi identifi number public author most articl countri most contribution quality literature review determin barrier future line research quality result show 2023 year highest scientific production india country most contribution antony most productive researcher term quality limit research period 2017 2025 inclusion only articl english novel contribution model problem open system using black box concept categoriz into people process technology,quality industry bibliometric analysi literature review jul dic 2025 volumen xxi numero 41 pags 1-18 la calidad analisi bibliometrico revision sistematica de la literatura gerardo hernandez chavez yazmin hernandez chavez phd,utilizando como evidencia la base de dato scopu el analisi bibliometrico objective research conduct bibliometric analysi systematic literature review topic quality using scopu database bibliometric analysi identifi number public author most articl countri most contribution quality literature review determin barrier future line research quality result show 2023 year highest scientific production india country most contribution antony most productive researcher term quality limit research period 2017 2025 inclusion only articl english novel contribution model problem open system using black box concept categoriz into people process technology quality industry bibliometric analysi literature review jul dic 2025 volumen xxi numero 41 pags 1-18 la calidad analisi bibliometrico revision sistematica de la literatura gerardo hernandez chavez yazmin hernandez chavez phd,1.0.0,4058e682da8c99cf
2248-6011,03_(Influence+of+Variables)+Vol+21+Nº41_CLA.pdf,03_(Influence+of+Variables)+Vol+21+Nº41_CLA_0,en,"1. PhD., en Administración Estratégica por la Pontificia Universidad Católica del Ecuador, Lima, Perú. Profesor Tecnológico de Monterrey, México.","Although consumers often express willingness to purchase eco-friendly products, a persistent gap remains between their declared intention and actual buying behavior. This study examines the relationship between key variables influencing purchase intention for dairy products with eco-labels, aiming to enhance the probability of environmentally friendly consumption. The research followed a quantitative, non-experimental, correlational approach, employing logistic regression to test predictive relationships. In addition, Pearson’s Chi-Square test was applied to detect associations among variables within each construct, while gamma correlation was calculated to determine the magnitude of these associations. Data collection was conducted through surveys administered to consumers of dairy products in Bogotá, Colombia. Findings indicate that three constructs—awareness, knowledge, and private benefits—are critical factors that producers must strengthen to impact eco-label purchase intention positively. From a managerial perspective, these results provide valuable insights for food sector companies, particularly marketing departments, by clarifying how consumer environmental awareness, environmental knowledge, and private benefits interact as determinants of purchasing behavior. Strengthening these constructs can help close the intention–behavior gap in eco-label adoption",Consumer Behavior; Dairy Food Products; Ecolabel; Ecolabel Purchase Intention; Green Consumerism. 1,marcadores,phd en administracion estrategica por la pontificia universidad catolica del ecuador lima peru profesor tecnologico de monterrey mexico,although consumer often expres willingnes purchase eco-friendly product persistent gap remain between their declar intention actual buying behavior study examin relationship between key variabl influenc purchase intention dairy product eco-label aiming enhance probability environmentally friendly consumption research follow quantitative non-experimental correlational approach employ logistic regression test predictive relationship addition pearson chi-square test appli detect associ among variabl within each construct while gamma correlation calculat determine magnitude these associ data collection conduct through survey administer consumer dairy product bogota colombia finding indicate three constructs--awarenes knowledge private benefits--are critical factor producer must strengthen impact eco-label purchase intention positively managerial perspective these result provide valuable insight food sector compani particularly market department clarify how consumer environmental awarenes environmental knowledge private benefit interact determinant purchas behavior strengthen these construct can help close intention-behavior gap eco-label adoption,consumer behavior dairy food product ecolabel ecolabel purchase intention green consumerism,phd en administracion estrategica por la pontificia universidad catolica del ecuador lima peru profesor tecnologico de monterrey mexico although consumer often expres willingnes purchase eco-friendly product persistent gap remain between their declar intention actual buying behavior study examin relationship between key variabl influenc purchase intention dairy product eco-label aiming enhance probability environmentally friendly consumption research follow quantitative non-experimental correlational approach employ logistic regression test predictive relationship addition pearson chi-square test appli detect associ among variabl within each construct while gamma correlation calculat determine magnitude these associ data collection conduct through survey administer consumer dairy product bogota colombia finding indicate three constructs--awarenes knowledge private benefits--are critical factor producer must strengthen impact eco-label purchase intention positively managerial perspective these result provide valuable insight food sector compani particularly market department clarify how consumer environmental awarenes environmental knowledge private benefit interact determinant purchas behavior strengthen these construct can help close intention-behavior gap eco-label adoption consumer behavior dairy food product ecolabel ecolabel purchase intention green consumerism,1.0.0,f2c076964e4d9ac0
2248-6011,03_(Influence+of+Variables)+Vol+21+Nº41_CLA.pdf,03_(Influence+of+Variables)+Vol+21+Nº41_CLA_0,es,"thin each construct, while gamma correlation was calculated to determine the magnitude of these","Aunque los consumidores suelen expresar disposición a comprar productos ecológicos, persiste una brecha entre la intención declarada y el comportamiento real de compra. Este estudio examina la relación entre variables clave que influyen en la intención de adquirir productos lácteos con ecoetiquetas, con el fin de aumentar la probabilidad de un consumo ambientalmente responsable. La investigación siguió un enfoque cuantitativo, no experimental y correlacional, empleando regresión logística para probar relaciones predictivas. Además, se aplicó la prueba Chi-Cuadrado de Pearson para identificar asociaciones entre variables en cada constructo, mientras que la correlación gamma se utilizó para medir la magnitud de dichas asociaciones. La recolección de datos se realizó mediante encuestas aplicadas a consumidores de productos lácteos en Bogotá, Colombia. Los hallazgos indican que tres constructos —conciencia, conocimiento y beneficios privados— son factores críticos que los productores deben fortalecer para generar un impacto significativo en la intención de compra de productos con ecoetiquetas. Desde una perspectiva gerencial, estos resultados aportan información valiosa al sector alimentario, especialmente a las áreas de mercadotecnia, para comprender cómo dichos constructos influyen en el comportamiento del consumidor y contribuyen a cerrar la brecha intención–acción",Comportamiento del consumidor; Productos lácteos; Ecoetiqueta; Intención de compra con ecoetiqueta; Consumo verde,marcadores,thin each construct while gamma correlation was calculated to determine the magnitude of these,aunque consumidor suelen expresar disposicion comprar product ecologic persiste brecha entre intencion declarada comportamiento real compra este estudio examina relacion entre variabl clave influyen intencion adquirir product lacte ecoetiquet fin aumentar probabilidad consumo ambiental responsable investigacion siguio enfoque cuantitativo no experimental correlacional emple regresion logistica probar relacion predictiv adem aplico prueba chi-cuadrado pearson identificar asoci entre variabl cada constructo mientr correlacion gamma utilizo medir magnitud dich asoci recoleccion datos realizo mediante encuest aplicad consumidor product lacte bogota colombia hallazg indican tres construct --conciencia conocimiento benefici privados-- son factor critic productor deben fortalecer generar impacto significativo intencion compra product ecoetiquet desde perspectiva gerencial estos resultad aportan informacion valiosa sector alimentario especial areas mercadotecnia comprender como dich construct influyen comportamiento consumidor contribuyen cerrar brecha intencion-accion,comportamiento consumidor product lacte ecoetiqueta intencion compra ecoetiqueta consumo verde,thin each construct while gamma correlation was calculated to determine the magnitude of these aunque consumidor suelen expresar disposicion comprar product ecologic persiste brecha entre intencion declarada comportamiento real compra este estudio examina relacion entre variabl clave influyen intencion adquirir product lacte ecoetiquet fin aumentar probabilidad consumo ambiental responsable investigacion siguio enfoque cuantitativo no experimental correlacional emple regresion logistica probar relacion predictiv adem aplico prueba chi-cuadrado pearson identificar asoci entre variabl cada constructo mientr correlacion gamma utilizo medir magnitud dich asoci recoleccion datos realizo mediante encuest aplicad consumidor product lacte bogota colombia hallazg indican tres construct --conciencia conocimiento benefici privados-- son factor critic productor deben fortalecer generar impacto significativo intencion compra product ecoetiquet desde perspectiva gerencial estos resultad aportan informacion valio