2256-201X,CF-24471.pdf,CF-24471_0,en,"Palabras clave: diversidad, facilitación, plántulas, Pteridium, revegetalización.","Species of the genus Pteridium have been classified as invasive due to their influence on vegetation succession; however, their ecological role may vary depending on context. This study evaluated the influence of Pteridium on seedling establishment and growth in an abandoned pasture located in Golconda, Serranía de los Yariguíes National Natural Park, Colombian Andes. Nine 25 m² plots were randomly established with three treatments: no-intervention control (PC), initial cutting (CH-I), and bimonthly cutting (CH-2M) over eight months. Seedling height, cover, diversity, abundance, and survival were recorded. The results indicate that the persistence of the fern favors seedling diversity and growth, whereas periodic cutting (CH-2M) increases seedling abundance but reduces diversity and survival. These findings provide technical criteria for the differentiated management of Pteridium and support its consideration as a potentially facilitative species in ecological restoration processes in Andean ecosystems","Diversity, facilitation, Pteridium, revegetation, seedlings",marcadores,palabra clave diversidad facilitacion plantula pteridium revegetalizacion,speci genu pteridium have been classifi invasive due their influence vegetation succession however their ecological role may vary depend context study evaluat influence pteridium seedl establishment growth abandon pasture locat golconda serrania de los yarigui national natural park colombian ande nine 25 m2 plot randomly establish three treatment no-intervention control pc initial cutt ch-i bimonthly cutt ch-2m over eight month seedl height cover diversity abundance survival record result indicate persistence fern favor seedl diversity growth wherea periodic cutt ch-2m increas seedl abundance but reduc diversity survival these finding provide technical criteria differentiat management pteridium support its consideration potentially facilitative speci ecological restoration process andean ecosystem,diversity facilitation pteridium revegetation seedling,palabra clave diversidad facilitacion plantula pteridium revegetalizacion speci genu pteridium have been classifi invasive due their influence vegetation succession however their ecological role may vary depend context study evaluat influence pteridium seedl establishment growth abandon pasture locat golconda serrania de los yarigui national natural park colombian ande nine 25 m2 plot randomly establish three treatment no-intervention control pc initial cutt ch-i bimonthly cutt ch-2m over eight month seedl height cover diversity abundance survival record result indicate persistence fern favor seedl diversity growth wherea periodic cutt ch-2m increas seedl abundance but reduc diversity survival these finding provide technical criteria differentiat management pteridium support its consideration potentially facilitative speci ecological restoration process andean ecosystem diversity facilitation pteridium revegetation seedling,1.0.0,5d999c3c22157ef5
2256-201X,CF-24605.pdf,CF-24605_0,es,", Colombian Caribbean","Se compara la diversidad de líquenes en tres coberturas vegetales en la cuenca media del río Sinú, Córdoba, las cuales fueron una cobertura ribereña y dos bosques secos fragmentados. En cada sitio se muestrearon 10 forófitos con un cuadrante de 400 cm2 por forófito. Se registraron 17 familias, 35 géneros y 87 especies de líquenes. Las familias Graphidaceae y Arthoniaceae y los talos costrosos fueron dominantes. Se encontró un alto recambio composicional, con una distancia mayor al 80% en cada par de coberturas posibles, se registró un 3% de especies compartidas entre los tres sitios, destacando a la cobertura ribereña por su mayor riqueza y número de especies exclusivas. Este estudio aporta una línea base sobre la diversidad y composición de líquenes en las coberturas vegetales del medio Sinú, con nuevos registros para el Caribe colombiano y Córdoba","bosque seco, estructura, epífitas no vasculares, sotobosque, vegetación de ribera. Diversidad de líquenes en coberturas vegetales en la cuenca media del río Sinú, Caribe colombiano Valencia, J., & Linares-Arias, J.C. Colombia Forestal • ISSN 0120-0739 • e-ISSN 2256-201X • Bogotá-Colombia • Vol. 29 N. 2 • Julio-Diciembre de 2026 [ 2 ]",marcadores,colombian caribbean,compara diversidad liquen tres cobertur vegetal cuenca media rio sinu cordoba cual fueron cobertura riberena dos bosqu secos fragmentad cada sitio muestrearon 10 forofit cuadrante 400 cm2 forofito registraron 17 famili 35 gener 87 especi liquen famili graphidaceae arthoniaceae talos costros fueron dominant encontro alto recambio composicional distancia mayor 80 cada par cobertur posibl registro especi compartid entre tres siti destac cobertura riberena mayor riqueza numero especi exclusiv este estudio aporta linea base sobre diversidad composicion liquen cobertur vegetal medio sinu nuev registr caribe colombiano cordoba,bosque seco estructura epifit no vascular sotobosque vegetacion ribera diversidad liquen cobertur vegetal cuenca media rio sinu caribe colombiano valencia linares-ari colombia forestal issn 0120-0739 e-issn 2256-201x bogota-colombia vol 29 julio-diciembre 2026,colombian caribbean compara diversidad liquen tres cobertur vegetal cuenca media rio sinu cordoba cual fueron cobertura riberena dos bosqu secos fragmentad cada sitio muestrearon 10 forofit cuadrante 400 cm2 forofito registraron 17 famili 35 gener 87 especi liquen famili graphidaceae arthoniaceae talos costros fueron dominant encontro alto recambio composicional distancia mayor 80 cada par cobertur posibl registro especi compartid entre tres siti destac cobertura riberena mayor riqueza numero especi exclusiv este estudio aporta linea base sobre diversidad composicion liquen cobertur vegetal medio sinu nuev registr caribe colombiano cordoba bosque seco estructura epifit no vascular sotobosque vegetacion ribera diversidad liquen cobertur vegetal cuenca media rio sinu caribe colombiano valencia linares-ari colombia forestal issn 0120-0739 e-issn 2256-201x bogota-colombia vol 29 julio-diciembre 2026,1.0.0,924bdb1c418078db
2256-201X,CF-24605.pdf,CF-24605_0,en,e líquenes. Las familias Graphidaceae y Arthoniaceae y los talos costrosos fueron dominantes.,"This study compared lichen diversity across three vegetation covers in the middle Sinú River basin (Córdoba, Colombia): a riparian forest and two tropical dry forest fragments. At each site, 10 phorophytes were sampled using a 400 cm² quadrant per individual. A total of 17 families, 35 genera, and 87 lichen morphospecies were recorded. The families Graphidaceae and Arthoniaceae, along with crustose growth form, were dominant. High compositional turnover was observed, with a dissimilarity distance greater than 80% between each pair of studied localities; only 3% of the species were shared among all three sites. The riparian vegetation stood out due to its higher species richness and number of rare species. This study provides a baseline for lichen diversity and composition in the middle Sinú region, including new records for the Colombian Caribbean and Córdoba","Dry forest, non-vascular epiphytes, riparian vegetation, structure, understory",marcadores,liquen las familia graphidaceae arthoniaceae los talo costroso fueron dominant,study compar lichen diversity acros three vegetation cover middle sinu river basin cordoba colombia riparian forest two tropical dry forest fragment each site 10 phorophyt sampl using 400 cm2 quadrant per individual total 17 famili 35 genera 87 lichen morphospeci record famili graphidaceae arthoniaceae along crustose growth form dominant high compositional turnover observ dissimilarity distance greater than 80 between each pair studi localiti only speci shar among all three site riparian vegetation stood out due its higher speci richnes number rare speci study provid baseline lichen diversity composition middle sinu region includ new record colombian caribbean cordoba,dry forest non-vascular epiphyt riparian vegetation structure understory,liquen las familia graphidaceae arthoniaceae los talo costroso fueron dominant study compar lichen diversity acros three vegetation cover middle sinu river basin cordoba colombia riparian forest two tropical dry forest fragment each site 10 phorophyt sampl using 400 cm2 quadrant per individual total 17 famili 35 genera 87 lichen morphospeci record famili graphidaceae arthoniaceae along crustose growth form dominant high compositional turnover observ dissimilarity distance greater than 80 between each pair studi localiti only speci shar among all three site riparian vegetation stood out due its higher speci richnes number rare speci study provid baseline lichen diversity composition middle sinu region includ new record colombian caribbean cordoba dry forest non-vascular epiphyt riparian vegetation structure understory,1.0.0,ea5567d95fd43248
2256-201X,CF-24629.pdf,CF-24629_0,es,"la, Guerrero, México.","Las sequías prolongadas y las precipitaciones erráticas son cada vez más frecuentes debido al cambio climático, con consecuencias graves para la biodiversidad, comprometiendo la regeneración de especies amenazadas. En un experimento controlado, se evaluó la respuesta de plántulas de Abies hickelii al déficit hídrico, combinando condiciones de riego (con o sin riego) y de luz (sol o sombra). Se observó que el riesgo La disponibilidad hídrica, limita la supervivencia de Abies hickelii Flous & Gaussen ante condiciones de sequía Hernández-Cruz, I., Aquino-Vásquez, C., Alanís-Rodríguez, E., Basave-Villalobos, E., Nolasco-Hipólito, C., & Antúnez, P. Colombia Forestal • ISSN 0120-0739 • e-ISSN 2256-201X • Bogotá-Colombia • Vol. 29 N. 2 • Julio-Diciembre de 2026 [ 2 ] de mortalidad fue cinco veces mayor en ausencia de riego, independientemente de si las plántulas se encontraban bajo sombra o no. Sin riego, las plántulas expuestas al sol toleraron aproximadamente 54 días antes de un colapso total, mientras que las mantenidas bajo sombra toleraron cerca de 62 días. La sombra redujo el índice de marchitez, pero no compensó la falta de agua. Por lo tanto, la disponibilidad de agua se identifica como un factor crítico para la supervivencia temprana de esta especie","cambio climático, escasez de agua, especie endémica, oyamel, plántulas, sequía prolongada",marcadores,guerrero mexico,sequi prolongad precipit erratic son cada vez mas frecuent debido cambio climatico consecuenci grav biodiversidad compromet regeneracion especi amenazad experimento controlado evaluo respuesta plantul abies hickelii deficit hidrico combin condicion riego sin riego luz sol sombra observo riesgo disponibilidad hidrica limita supervivencia abies hickelii flous gaussen ante condicion sequia hernandez-cruz aquino-vasquez alanis-rodriguez basave-villalob nolasco-hipolito antunez colombia forestal issn 0120-0739 e-issn 2256-201x bogota-colombia vol 29 julio-diciembre 2026 mortalidad fue cinco veces mayor ausencia riego independiente si plantul encontraban bajo sombra no sin riego plantul expuest sol toleraron aproximada 54 dias antes colapso total mientr mantenid bajo sombra toleraron cerca 62 dias sombra redujo indice marchitez pero no compenso falta agua tanto disponibilidad agua identifica como factor critico supervivencia temprana esta especie,cambio climatico escasez agua especie endemica oyamel plantul sequia prolongada,guerrero mexico sequi prolongad precipit erratic son cada vez mas frecuent debido cambio climatico consecuenci grav biodiversidad compromet regeneracion especi amenazad experimento controlado evaluo respuesta plantul abies hickelii deficit hidrico combin condicion riego sin riego luz sol sombra observo riesgo disponibilidad hidrica limita supervivencia abies hickelii flous gaussen ante condicion sequia hernandez-cruz aquino-vasquez alanis-rodriguez basave-villalob nolasco-hipolito antunez colombia forestal issn 0120-0739 e-issn 2256-201x bogota-colombia vol 29 julio-diciembre 2026 mortalidad fue cinco veces mayor ausencia riego independiente si plantul encontraban bajo sombra no sin riego plantul expuest sol toleraron aproximada 54 dias antes colapso total mientr mantenid bajo sombra toleraron cerca 62 dias sombra redujo indice marchitez pero no compenso falta agua tanto disponibilidad agua identifica como factor critico supervivencia temprana esta especie cambio climatico escasez agua especie endemica oyamel plantul sequia prolongada,1.0.0,40cef6940d5db612
2256-201X,CF-24629.pdf,CF-24629_0,en,Flous & Gaussen ante condiciones de sequía,"Prolonged droughts and erratic rainfall are becoming increasingly common due to climate change, with serious consequences for biodiversity and jeopardizing the regeneration of threatened species. In a controlled experiment, the response of Abies hickelii seedlings to water stress was evaluated by combining two irrigation conditions (with and without water) and two light conditions (sun and shade). It was observed that the risk of mortality is five times higher in the absence of irrigation, regardless of light exposure. Without irrigation, seedlings exposed to sunlight survived approximately 54 days before total collapse, while those kept in the shade survived about 62 days. Shade reduced the wilting rate but did not compensate for the lack of water. Therefore, water availability is a critical factor for the early survival of this species","Climate change, water scarcity, endemic species, oyamel, seedlings, prolonged drought",marcadores,flou gaussen ante condicion de sequia,prolong drought erratic rainfall becom increas common due climate change seriou consequenc biodiversity jeopardiz regeneration threaten speci controll experiment response abie hickelii seedling water stres evaluat combin two irrigation condition without water two light condition sun shade observ risk mortality five time higher absence irrigation regardles light exposure without irrigation seedling expos sunlight surviv approximately 54 days before total collapse while those kept shade surviv about 62 days shade reduc wilt rate but did not compensate lack water therefore water availability critical factor early survival speci,climate change water scarcity endemic speci oyamel seedling prolong drought,flou gaussen ante condicion de sequia prolong drought erratic rainfall becom increas common due climate change seriou consequenc biodiversity jeopardiz regeneration threaten speci controll experiment response abie hickelii seedling water stres evaluat combin two irrigation condition without water two light condition sun shade observ risk mortality five time higher absence irrigation regardles light exposure without irrigation seedling expos sunlight surviv approximately 54 days before total collapse while those kept shade surviv about 62 days shade reduc wilt rate but did not compensate lack water therefore water availability critical factor early survival speci climate change water scarcity endemic speci oyamel seedling prolong drought,1.0.0,ec15f897d2800e8d
2256-201X,CF-24763.pdf,CF-24763_0,es,Joshua Jiménez-Jiménez,"La ganadería abarca un 33% del territorio y aporta emisiones importantes de gases efecto invernadero. El estudio tuvo como objetivo determinar el efecto de densidad de plantación en un sistema silvopastoril, para producción de madera y captura de carbono. Se evaluó ocho años el desarrollo de clones de teca en seis espaciamientos en franjas de 6 m de ancho, con tres hileras internas plantadas a 1 m; 2 m; 3 m; 4 m; 5 m y 6m. La base de análisis fue la franja de 1000 m lineales por 6 m de ancho. El espaciamiento 3m registró la mayor producción comercial con 110 m3 en 6000 m2 y capturar 105 toneladas de carbono. El mayor valor comercial por árbol se registró con 4 m, entre US$27 y $31. El SSP en franjas optimiza el uso del espacio, aumenta la producción de madera y captura de carbono en 1.2 veces con respecto a la plantación convencional","propiedades de madera, rendimiento, sistemas agroforestales, Tectona grandis, volumen Efecto del espaciamiento en la productividad de teca clonal en sistema silvopastoril en Costa Rica Murillo Gamboa, O., Badilla Valverde, Y., Jiménez-Jiménez, J., & Moya Roque, R. Colombia Forestal • ISSN 0120-0739 • e-ISSN 2256-201X • Bogotá-Colombia • Vol. 29 N. 2 • Julio-Diciembre de 2026 [ 2 ]",marcadores,joshua jimenez-jimenez,ganaderia abarca 33 territorio aporta emision important gases efecto invernadero estudio tuvo como objetivo determinar efecto densidad plantacion sistema silvopastoril produccion madera captura carbono evaluo ocho anos desarrollo clon teca seis espaci franj ancho tres hiler intern plantad 6m base analisis fue franja 1000 lineal ancho espaciamiento 3m registro mayor produccion comercial 110 m3 6000 m2 capturar 105 tonelad carbono mayor valor comercial arbol registro entre us 31 ssp franj optimiza uso espacio aumenta produccion madera captura carbono veces respecto plantacion convencional,propiedad madera rendimiento sistem agroforestal tectona grandis volumen efecto espaciamiento productividad teca clonal sistema silvopastoril costa rica murillo gamboa badilla valverde jimenez-jimenez moya roque colombia forestal issn 0120-0739 e-issn 2256-201x bogota-colombia vol 29 julio-diciembre 2026,joshua jimenez-jimenez ganaderia abarca 33 territorio aporta emision important gases efecto invernadero estudio tuvo como objetivo determinar efecto densidad plantacion sistema silvopastoril produccion madera captura carbono evaluo ocho anos desarrollo clon teca seis espaci franj ancho tres hiler intern plantad 6m base analisis fue franja 1000 lineal ancho espaciamiento 3m registro mayor produccion comercial 110 m3 6000 m2 capturar 105 tonelad carbono mayor valor comercial arbol registro entre us 31 ssp franj optimiza uso espacio aumenta produccion madera captura carbono veces respecto plantacion convencional propiedad madera rendimiento sistem agroforestal tectona grandis volumen efecto espaciamiento productividad teca clonal sistema silvopastoril costa rica murillo gamboa badilla valverde jimenez-jimenez moya roque colombia forestal issn 0120-0739 e-issn 2256-201x bogota-colombia vol 29 julio-diciembre 2026,1.0.0,68cb72b61a086a8f
2256-201X,CF-24763.pdf,CF-24763_0,en,"por árbol se registró con 4 m, entre US$27 y $31. El SSP en franjas optimiza el uso del espacio, aumenta la","Livestock farming in Costa Rica covers 33% of the territory and contributes significantly to greenhouse gas emissions. Timber trees expand environmental services and generate economic impact on livestock farming. The study aimed to determine the effect of planting density in a silvopastoral system for timber production and carbon sequestration. Over 8 years the development of teak clones under six spacings was evaluated, based on three internal tree-rows inside 6m wide strips and the trees planted every 1 m; 2 m; 3 m; 4 m; 5 m and 6 m. The basis for analysis was a strip measuring 1000 linear meters by 6 meters wide. The 3 m spacing recorded the highest production with 110 m3 in the 6000 m2, capturing 105 tons of carbon at 8 years. Highest commercial value per individual tree was recorded under 4 m spacing with US$27 and US$31. SSP optimizes space usage and allows for a 1.2-fold increase in wood production and carbon capture compared to conventional planting","wood properties, yield, agroforestry systems, Tectona grandis, volume",marcadores,por arbol se registro con entre us 31 el ssp en franja optimiza el uso del espacio aumenta la,livestock farm costa rica cover 33 territory contribut significantly greenhouse gas emission timber tree expand environmental servic generate economic impact livestock farm study aimed determine effect plant density silvopastoral system timber production carbon sequestration over year development teak clon under six spacing evaluat based three internal tree-row inside 6m wide strip tree plant every basi analysi strip measur 1000 linear meter meter wide spac record highest production 110 m3 6000 m2 captur 105 tons carbon year highest commercial value per individual tree record under spac us 31 ssp optimiz space usage allow 2-fold increase wood production carbon capture compar conventional plant,wood properti yield agroforestry system tectona grandi volume,por arbol se registro con entre us 31 el ssp en franja optimiza el uso del espacio aumenta la livestock farm costa rica cover 33 territory contribut significantly greenhouse gas emission timber tree expand environmental servic generate economic impact livestock farm study aimed determine effect plant density silvopastoral system timber production carbon sequestration over year development teak clon under six spacing evaluat based three internal tree-row inside 6m wide strip tree plant every basi analysi strip measur 1000 linear meter meter wide spac record highest production 110 m3 6000 m2 captur 105 tons carbon year highest commercial value per individual tree record under spac us 31 ssp optimiz space usage allow 2-fold increase wood production carbon capture compar conventional plant wood properti yield agroforestry system tectona grandi volume,1.0.0,a91d5a441249d5f2
2256-201X,CF-24788.pdf,CF-24788_0,es,"y Técnicas (CONICET), Santiago del Estero, Argentina.","Se evaluó el efecto de la calidad del sitio, micrositios y de tratamientos pregerminativos en la emergencia de plántulas mediante siembra directa, de 4 especies del Chaco semiárido: Aspidosperma quebracho-blanco, Schinopsis lorentzii, Neltuma nigra y Sarcomphalus mistol. Las evaluaciones se realizaron en bosques control y disturbado, y los micrositios incluyeron condiciones con y sin cobertura arbórea. Se realizó la prueba de tetrazolio para evaluar la viabilidad de las semillas. La viabilidad promedio varió entre un 53 % y 63% entre las especies. A. quebracho-blanco mostró mayor germinación en el bosque control, sin efecto significativo del tratamiento pregerminativo ni del micrositio. N. nigra tuvo mayor porcentaje de germinación en bosque disturbado y con semillas tratadas. No se registró germinación en S. lorentzii y S. mistol. Siembra directa para restauración de bosques semiáridos degradados Barraza, C. C., & Bravo, S. J. Colombia Forestal • ISSN 0120-0739 • e-ISSN 2256-201X • Bogotá-Colombia • Vol. 29 N. 2 • Julio-Diciembre de 2026 [ 2 ] Los resultados indican que las especies tienen diferentes requerimientos para la germinación y que el pretratamiento de las semillas podría mejorar el reclutamiento mediante siembra directa","Chaco Semiárido, micrositios, restauración ecológica, tratamientos pregerminativos",marcadores,tecnic conicet santiago estero argentina,evaluo efecto calidad sitio micrositi trat pregerminativ emergencia plantul mediante siembra directa especi chaco semiarido aspidosperma quebracho-blanco schinopsis lorentzii neltuma nigra sarcomphalus mistol evalu realizaron bosqu control disturbado micrositi incluyeron condicion sin cobertura arborea realizo prueba tetrazolio evaluar viabilidad semill viabilidad promedio vario entre 53 63 entre especi quebracho-blanco mostro mayor germinacion bosque control sin efecto significativo tratamiento pregerminativo ni micrositio nigra tuvo mayor porcentaje germinacion bosque disturbado semill tratad no registro germinacion lorentzii mistol siembra directa restauracion bosqu semiarid degradad barraza bravo colombia forestal issn 0120-0739 e-issn 2256-201x bogota-colombia vol 29 julio-diciembre 2026 resultad indican especi tienen diferent requer germinacion pretratamiento semill podria mejorar reclutamiento mediante siembra directa,chaco semiarido micrositi restauracion ecologica trat pregerminativ,tecnic conicet santiago estero argentina evaluo efecto calidad sitio micrositi trat pregerminativ emergencia plantul mediante siembra directa especi chaco semiarido aspidosperma quebracho-blanco schinopsis lorentzii neltuma nigra sarcomphalus mistol evalu realizaron bosqu control disturbado micrositi incluyeron condicion sin cobertura arborea realizo prueba tetrazolio evaluar viabilidad semill viabilidad promedio vario entre 53 63 entre especi quebracho-blanco mostro mayor germinacion bosque control sin efecto significativo tratamiento pregerminativo ni micrositio nigra tuvo mayor porcentaje germinacion bosque disturbado semill tratad no registro germinacion lorentzii mistol siembra directa restauracion bosqu semiarid degradad barraza bravo colombia forestal issn 0120-0739 e-issn 2256-201x bogota-colombia vol 29 julio-diciembre 2026 resultad indican especi tienen diferent requer germinacion pretratamiento semill podria mejorar reclutamiento mediante siembra directa chaco semiarido micrositi restauracion ecologica trat pregerminativ,1.0.0,09ffa2ac92f289fc
2256-201X,CF-24788.pdf,CF-24788_0,en,iabilidad de las semillas. La viabilidad promedio varió entre un 53 % y,"The effects of site quality, microsites, and pre-germination treatments on seedling emergence via direct seeding were evaluated for four species from the semi-arid Chaco: Aspidosperma quebracho-blanco, Schinopsis lorentzii, Neltuma nigra, and Sarcomphalus mistol. The evaluations were conducted in control and disturbed forests, and the microsites included conditions with and without tree cover. The tetrazolium test was performed to assess seed viability. Average viability ranged from 53% to 63% among the species. A. quebracho-blanco showed higher germination in the control forest, with no significant effect of pre-germination treatment or microsite. N. nigra had a higher germination rate in the disturbed forest and with treated seeds. No germination was recorded for S. lorentzii and S. mistol. The results indicate that species have different germination requirements and that seed pretreatment could improve recruitment through direct seeding","Semiarid Chaco, microsites, ecological restoration, pregerminative treatments",marcadores,iabilidad de las semilla la viabilidad promedio vario entre un 53,effect site quality microsit pre-germination treatment seedl emergence via direct seed evaluat four speci semi-arid chaco aspidosperma quebracho-blanco schinopsi lorentzii neltuma nigra sarcomphalu mistol evalu conduct control disturb forest microsit includ condition without tree cover tetrazolium test perform asses seed viability average viability rang 53 63 among speci quebracho-blanco show higher germination control forest no significant effect pre-germination treatment microsite nigra had higher germination rate disturb forest treat seed no germination record lorentzii mistol result indicate speci have different germination requirement seed pretreatment could improve recruitment through direct seed,semiarid chaco microsit ecological restoration pregerminative treatment,iabilidad de las semilla la viabilidad promedio vario entre un 53 effect site quality microsit pre-germination treatment seedl emergence via direct seed evaluat four speci semi-arid chaco aspidosperma quebracho-blanco schinopsi lorentzii neltuma nigra sarcomphalu mistol evalu conduct control disturb forest microsit includ condition without tree cover tetrazolium test perform asses seed viability average viability rang 53 63 among speci quebracho-blanco show higher germination control forest no significant effect pre-germination treatment microsite nigra had higher germination rate disturb forest treat seed no germination record lorentzii mistol result indicate speci have different germination requirement seed pretreatment could improve recruitment through direct seed semiarid chaco microsit ecological restoration pregerminative treatment,1.0.0,4d113155d8e7a16a
2256-201X,CF-24838.pdf,CF-24838_0,es,"d Universidad Técnica de Babahoyo. Extensión Quevedo (UTB). Quevedo, Ecuador.","El estudio analizó la contribución del ingreso forestal a los medios de vida rurales y su relación con la desigualdad en pequeños productores de la Región Amazónica Ecuatoriana (RAE). La investigación se desarrolló en la parroquia Hatun Sumaku, provincia de Napo, mediante encuestas estructuradas aplicadas a 180 hogares rurales, mayoritariamente kichwa. Se estimó la proporción del ingreso forestal sobre el ingreso total del hogar, sus determinantes socioeconómicos y su efecto sobre la distribución del ingreso. Los resultados muestran que los hogares más pobres dependen significativamente del bosque, alcanzando hasta Trayectorias de ingreso y dependencia forestal en pequeños productores de la Amazonía ecuatoriana Torres, B., López-Camacho, R., Torres, A., Vasco, C., García, A., & Reyes, H. Colombia Forestal • ISSN 0120-0739 • e-ISSN 2256-201X • Bogotá-Colombia • Vol. 29 N. 2 • Julio-Diciembre de 2026 [ 2 ] un 68% de su ingreso total, mientras que los quintiles superiores presentan mayor diversificación hacia actividades agrícolas y no agrícolas. La dependencia forestal se relacionó positivamente con la etnicidad kichwa y la disponibilidad de bosque, y negativamente con el acceso a crédito y mayores ingresos. Aunque el ingreso forestal reduce ligeramente la desigualdad, su efecto redistributivo es limitado","Amazonía, dependencia forestal, desigualdad rural, medios de vida, pobreza estructural",marcadores,universidad tecnica babahoyo extension quevedo utb quevedo ecuador,estudio analizo contribucion ingreso forestal medi vida rural relacion desigualdad pequen productor region amazonica ecuatoriana rae investigacion desarrollo parroquia hatun sumaku provincia napo mediante encuest estructurad aplicad 180 hogar rural mayoritaria kichwa estimo proporcion ingreso forestal sobre ingreso total hogar sus determinant socioeconomic efecto sobre distribucion ingreso resultad muestran hogar mas pobr dependen significativa bosque alcanz hasta trayectori ingreso dependencia forestal pequen productor amazonia ecuatoriana torr lopez-camacho torr vasco garcia reyes colombia forestal issn 0120-0739 e-issn 2256-201x bogota-colombia vol 29 julio-diciembre 2026 68 ingreso total mientr quintil superior presentan mayor diversificacion hacia actividad agricol no agricol dependencia forestal relaciono positiva etnicidad kichwa disponibilidad bosque negativa acceso credito mayor ingres aunque ingreso forestal reduce ligera desigualdad efecto redistributivo limitado,amazonia dependencia forestal desigualdad rural medi vida pobreza estructural,universidad tecnica babahoyo extension quevedo utb quevedo ecuador estudio analizo contribucion ingreso forestal medi vida rural relacion desigualdad pequen productor region amazonica ecuatoriana rae investigacion desarrollo parroquia hatun sumaku provincia napo mediante encuest estructurad aplicad 180 hogar rural mayoritaria kichwa estimo proporcion ingreso forestal sobre ingreso total hogar sus determinant socioeconomic efecto sobre distribucion ingreso resultad muestran hogar mas pobr dependen significativa bosque alcanz hasta trayectori ingreso dependencia forestal pequen productor amazonia ecuatoriana torr lopez-camacho torr vasco garcia reyes colombia forestal issn 0120-0739 e-issn 2256-201x bogota-colombia vol 29 julio-diciembre 2026 68 ingreso total mientr quintil superior presentan mayor diversificacion hacia actividad agricol no agricol dependencia forestal relaciono positiva etnicidad kichwa disponibilidad bosque negativa acceso credito mayor ingres aunque ingreso forestal reduce ligera desigualdad efecto redistributivo limitado amazonia dependencia forestal desigualdad rural medi vida pobreza estructural,1.0.0,7bfa807d4bbe3bc3
2256-201X,CF-24838.pdf,CF-24838_0,en,"tran que los hogares más pobres dependen significativamente del bosque, alcanzando hasta","This study analyzed the contribution of forest income to rural livelihoods and its relationship with inequality among smallholders in the Ecuadorian Amazon Region (EAR). The research was conducted in Hatun Sumaku parish, Napo Province, through structured surveys applied to 180 rural households, predominantly in Kichwa. The study estimated the share of forest income in total household income, its socioeconomic determinants, and its effect on income distribution. Results show that the poorest households depend strongly on forest resources, obtaining up to 68% of their total income from forest-related activities, whereas higher-income groups display greater diversification toward agricultural and off-farm activities. Forest dependence was positively associated with Kichwa ethnicity and forest availability and negatively associated with credit access and higher income levels. Although forest income slightly reduced inequality, its redistributive effect remained limited, highlighting persistent structural disparities in rural Amazonian livelihoods","Amazon, forest dependence, rural inequality, livelihoods, structural poverty",marcadores,tran que los hogar mas pobr dependen significativamente del bosque alcanzando hasta,study analyz contribution forest income rural livelihood its relationship inequality among smallholder ecuadorian amazon region ear research conduct hatun sumaku parish napo province through structur survey appli 180 rural household predominantly kichwa study estimat share forest income total household income its socioeconomic determinant its effect income distribution result show poorest household depend strongly forest resourc obtain up 68 their total income forest-relat activiti wherea higher-income group display greater diversification toward agricultural off-farm activiti forest dependence positively associat kichwa ethnicity forest availability negatively associat credit acces higher income level although forest income slightly reduc inequality its redistributive effect remain limit highlight persistent structural dispariti rural amazonian livelihood,amazon forest dependence rural inequality livelihood structural poverty,tran que los hogar mas pobr dependen significativamente del bosque alcanzando hasta study analyz contribution forest income rural livelihood its relationship inequality among smallholder ecuadorian amazon region ear research conduct hatun sumaku parish napo province through structur survey appli 180 rural household predominantly kichwa study estimat share forest income total household income its socioeconomic determinant its effect income distribution result show poorest household depend strongly forest resourc obtain up 68 their total income forest-relat activiti wherea higher-income group display greater diversification toward agricultural off-farm activiti forest dependence positively associat kichwa ethnicity forest availability negatively associat credit acces higher income level although forest income slightly reduc inequality its redistributive effect remain limit highlight persistent structural dispariti rural amazonian livelihood amazon forest dependence rural inequality livelihood structural poverty,1.0.0,e9e9f7218fe09f10
2256-2796,document (2).pdf,document (2)_0,en,sa. Universidad,"This article analyzes how the Colombian Supreme Court of Justice incorporated Inter-American gender perspective standards established by the Inter-American Court of Human Rights (IACtHR) between 2018 and 2025. Employing a mixed methodology—combining reverse chronological review and relevance-based selection—the study systematizes the incorporation of these standards through a matrix that cross-references the Inter-American standard, domestic rule, judicial decision, and degree of incorporation. The findings reveal a progressive convergence around the following axes: contextualization of evidentiary analysis; evidentiary flexibility in cases of gender-based homicide; prohibition of gender stereotypes; due diligence and institutional violence; protection of reproductive rights; and enhanced evidentiary value of the victim’s testimony. The reception of these standards has been predominantly strong, with some instances of partial adoption. This study makes a dual contribution: (i) it offers an explicit systematization of how Inter-American standards have been incorporated into the criminal jurisprudence of the Supreme Court; and (ii) it proposes baseline rules for their effective application, aimed at closing consistency and implementation gaps and ensuring real access to justice for women and individuals with diverse sexual orientations and gender identities",Gender perspective; gender-based violence; structural violence; patriarchal structure; evidence in gender-based violence cases. I,marcadores,sa universidad,article analyz how colombian supreme court justice incorporat inter-american gender perspective standard establish inter-american court human right iacthr between 2018 2025 employ mixed methodology--combin reverse chronological review relevance-bas selection--the study systematiz incorporation these standard through matrix cross-referenc inter-american standard domestic rule judicial decision degree 