2256-2796,document (9).pdf,document (9)_0,en,ge Pallares Bossa. Universidad,"This article explores how leadership influences the fulfillment of corporate social responsibility (CSR) policies in Latin American companies, particularly in the oil sector. The aim is to identify practices and approaches that may contribute to more sustainable production and to actions that respond coherently to the social and environmental demands of the region. To achieve this, more than fifty Scopusindexed articles were reviewed, along with sustainability reports from several oil companies, which made it possible to observe how resources are being managed, what kinds of decisions are made, and how these companies interact with surrounding communities. The findings show that CSR tends to operate under two simultaneous pressures: economic goals and the demands arising from the territory. In that tension, leadership becomes a key factor because it shapes how regulations are interpreted, how risks are addressed, and how environmental and social practices are integrated into organizational processes. The review also showed that when leadership adopts an ethical perspective and engages more openly with stakeholders, CSR actions become more consistent. Overall, the results suggest that leadership, when exercised responsibly, can help balance organizational interests with the needs of communities and the environment",Corporate social responsibility; industry; rights; sustainability. I,marcadores,ge pallar bossa universidad,article explor how leadership influenc fulfillment corporate social responsibility csr polici latin american compani particularly oil sector aim identify practic approach may contribute more sustainable production action respond coherently social environmental demand region achieve more than fifty scopusindex articl review along sustainability report several oil compani which made possible observe how resourc being manag what kind decision made how these compani interact surround communiti finding show csr tend operate under two simultaneou pressur economic goal demand aris territory tension leadership becom key factor because shap how regul interpret how risk address how environmental social practic integrat into organizational process review also show when leadership adopt ethical perspective engag more openly stakeholder csr action become more consistent overall result suggest leadership when exercis responsibly can help balance organizational interest need communiti environment,corporate social responsibility industry right sustainability,ge pallar bossa universidad article explor how leadership influenc fulfillment corporate social responsibility csr polici latin american compani particularly oil sector aim identify practic approach may contribute more sustainable production action respond coherently social environmental demand region achieve more than fifty scopusindex articl review along sustainability report several oil compani which made possible observe how resourc being manag what kind decision made how these compani interact surround communiti finding show csr tend operate under two simultaneou pressur economic goal demand aris territory tension leadership becom key factor because shap how regul interpret how risk address how environmental social practic integrat into organizational process review also show when leadership adopt ethical perspective engag more openly stakeholder csr action become more consistent overall result suggest leadership when exercis responsibly can help balance organizational interest need communiti environment corporate social responsibility industry right sustainability,1.0.0,24328356b2e7e1f4
2256-2958,358631_OK.pdf,358631_OK_0,en,Rev Colomb Cienc Pecu; 39(Jan-Dec):e358631,"Background: Chlamydia abortus is the etiological agent of ovine enzootic abortion (OEA), a worldwide disease that significantly impacts cattle, sheep, and goat production. This bacterium causes abortions during the last third of gestation and is zoonotic. The lack of prior symptoms before an abortive event complicates the clinical diagnosis of OEA and its differentiation from other infections, highlighting the need for an effective diagnostic tool. Some conventional diagnostic methods are accurate but sometimes require expensive equipment and highly trained personnel, limiting their field application. In this context, the loop-mediated isothermal amplification (LAMP) technique emerges as an accessible and efficient alternative, capable of operating at a constant temperature and simplifying result interpretation visually through colorimetry. Objective: To validate a new LAMP assay using colorimetry for the visual detection of Chlamydia abortus in domestic ruminants. Methods: Fifty-six DNA samples collected from ruminants with a history of abortion were used as biological reference controls. LAMP-specific primers were designed for the TARP gene of C. abortus. A colorimetric assay was validated for the LAMP test of C. abortus (crLAMP-Chla). The concordance (K), sensitivity (Se), and specificity (Sp) parameters of crLAMP-Chla were calculated considering real-time PCR as a reference. Results: The crLAMP-Chla detected the pathogen within 15 minutes at 65 °C, even at low DNA concentrations. The K, Se, and Sp values were 1, 100%, and 100% (P = 0.05), respectively. Conclusion: This methodology represents a significant advancement in the control of C. abortus in ruminants, providing an accessible and efficient diagnostic tool to improve public and animal health",Chlamydia abortus; colorimetry; colorimetric detection; enzootic abortion; Loop-mediated isothermal amplification (LAMP); molecular diagnostics; optimization; ruminants; validation; zoonotic. Nueva prueba LAMP colorimétrica permite la detección visual rápida de Chlamydia abortus en rumiantes domésticos Novo teste LAMP colorimétrico permite a detecção visual rápida de Chlamydia abortus em rumin,marcadores,rev colomb cienc pecu 39 jan-dec e358631,background chlamydia abortu etiological agent ovine enzootic abortion oea worldwide disease significantly impact cattle sheep goat production bacterium caus abortion during last third gestation zoonotic lack prior symptom before abortive event complicat clinical diagnosi oea its differentiation other infection highlight need effective diagnostic tool some conventional diagnostic method accurate but sometim require expensive equipment highly train personnel limit their field application context loop-mediat isothermal amplification lamp technique emerg accessible efficient alternative capable operat constant temperature simplify result interpretation visually through colorimetry objective validate new lamp assay using colorimetry visual detection chlamydia abortu domestic ruminant method fifty-six dna sampl collect ruminant history abortion used biological reference control lamp-specific primer design tarp gene abortu colorimetric assay validat lamp test abortu crlamp-chla concordance sensitivity se specificity sp parameter crlamp-chla calculat consider real-time pcr reference result crlamp-chla detect pathogen within 15 minut 65 degc even low dna concentr se sp valu 100 100 05 respectively conclusion methodology represent significant advancement control abortu ruminant provid accessible efficient diagnostic tool improve public animal health,chlamydia abortu colorimetry colorimetric detection enzootic abortion loop-mediat isothermal amplification lamp molecular diagnostic optim ruminant validation zoonotic nueva prueba lamp colorimetrica permite la deteccion visual rapida de chlamydia abortu en rumiant domestico novo teste lamp colorimetrico permite deteccao visual rapida de chlamydia abortu em rumin,rev colomb cienc pecu 39 jan-dec e358631 background chlamydia abortu etiological agent ovine enzootic abortion oea worldwide disease significantly impact cattle sheep goat production bacterium caus abortion during last third gestation zoonotic lack prior symptom before abortive event complicat clinical diagnosi oea its differentiation other infection highlight need effective diagnostic tool some conventional diagnostic method accurate but sometim require expensive equipment highly train personnel limit their field application context loop-mediat isothermal amplification lamp technique emerg accessible efficient alternative capable operat constant temperature simplify result interpretation visually through colorimetry objective validate new lamp assay using colorimetry visual detection chlamydia abortu domestic ruminant method fifty-six dna sampl collect ruminant history abortion used biological reference control lamp-specific primer design tarp gene abortu colorimetric assay validat lamp test abortu crlamp-chla concordance sensitivity se specificity sp parameter crlamp-chla calculat consider real-time pcr reference result crlamp-chla detect pathogen within 15 minut 65 degc even low dna concentr se sp valu 100 100 05 respectively conclusion methodology represent significant advancement control abortu ruminant provid accessible efficient diagnostic tool improve public animal health chlamydia abortu colorimetry colorimetric detection enzootic abortion loop-mediat isothermal amplification lamp molecular diagnostic optim ruminant validation zoonotic nueva prueba lamp colorimetrica permite la deteccion visual rapida de chlamydia abortu en rumiant domestico novo teste lamp colorimetrico permite deteccao visual rapida de chlamydia abortu em rumin,1.0.0,7df003511188ad3d
2256-2958,358631_OK.pdf,358631_OK_0,es,Morales-Pablos MI. A novel colorimetric,"Antecedentes: Chlamydia abortus es el agente etiológico del aborto enzoótico ovino (OEA), una enfermedad mundial que impacta significativamente la producción bovina, ovina y caprina. Esta bacteria provoca abortos durante el último tercio de la gestación y es zoonótica. La falta de síntomas previos antes de un evento abortivo complica el diagnóstico clínico del OEA y su diferenciación de otras infecciones, lo que destaca la necesidad de una herramienta de diagnóstico eficaz. Algunos métodos de diagnóstico convencionales pueden ser precisos, pero en algunos casos requieren equipos costosos y personal altamente capacitado, lo que limita su aplicación en campo. En este contexto, la amplificación isotérmica mediada por bucle (LAMP) surge como una alternativa accesible y eficiente, capaz de operar a temperatura constante y simplificar la interpretación de los resultados visualmente mediante colorimetría. Objetivo: Validar un nuevo ensayo LAMP utilizando colorimetría para la detección visual de Chlamydia abortus en rumiantes domésticos. Métodos: Como referencia en los controles biológicos se utilizaron 56 muestras de ADN colectadas de rumiantes con historial de aborto. Se diseñaron cebadores específicos LAMP para el gen TARP de C. abortus. Se validó un ensayo colorimétrico para la prueba LAMP de C. abortus (crLAMP-Chla). Se calcularon los parámetros de concordancia (K), sensibilidad (Se) y especificidad (Sp) de crLAMP-Chla, tomando como referencia la PCR en tiempo real. Resultados: El crLAMP-Chla detectó el patógeno desde los 15 minutos a 65 °C, incluso a bajas concentraciones de ADN. Los valores de K, Se y Sp fueron de 1, 100% y 100% (P = 0.05), respectivamente. Conclusión: Esta metodología representa un avance significativo para el control de C. abortus en rumiantes, proporcionando una herramienta diagnóstica accesible y eficiente para mejorar la salud pública y animal",aborto enzoótico; amplificación isotérmica mediada por bucles (LAMP); Chlamydia abortus; colorimetría; detección colorimétrica; diagnóstico molecular; isotérmica; optimización; rumiantes; validación; zoonosis,marcadores,morales-pabl mi novel colorimetric,antecedent chlamydia abortus agente etiologico aborto enzootico ovino oea enfermedad mundial impacta significativa produccion bovina ovina caprina esta bacteria provoca abort durante ultimo tercio gestacion zoonotica falta sintom previ antes evento abortivo complica diagnostico clinico oea diferenciacion otras infeccion destaca necesidad herramienta diagnostico eficaz algun metod diagnostico convencional pueden ser precis pero algun casos requieren equip costos personal alta capacitado limita aplicacion campo este contexto amplificacion isotermica mediada bucle lamp surge como alternativa accesible eficiente capaz operar temperatura constante simplificar interpretacion resultad visual mediante colorimetria objetivo validar nuevo ensayo lamp utiliz colorimetria deteccion visual chlamydia abortus rumiant domestic metod como referencia control biologic utilizaron 56 muestr adn colectad rumiant historial aborto disenaron cebador especific lamp gen tarp abortus valido ensayo colorimetrico prueba lamp abortus crlamp-chla calcularon parametr concordancia sensibilidad especificidad sp crlamp-chla tomando como referencia pcr tiempo real resultad crlamp-chla detecto patogeno desde 15 minut 65 degc incluso bajas concentr adn valor sp fueron 100 100 05 respectiva conclusion esta metodologia representa avance significativo control abortus rumiant proporcion herramienta diagnostica accesible eficiente mejorar salud publica animal,aborto enzootico amplificacion isotermica mediada bucl lamp chlamydia abortus colorimetria deteccion colorimetrica diagnostico molecular isotermica optimizacion rumiant validacion zoonosis,morales-pabl mi novel colorimetric antecedent chlamydia abortus agente etiologico aborto enzootico ovino oea enfermedad mundial impacta si