2256-2958,358794.pdf,358794_0,en,Rev Colomb Cienc Pecu; 39(Jan-Dec):e358794,"Background: Bovine trichomoniasis is a sexually transmitted disease caused by Tritrichomonas foetus that significantly impairs the reproductive health of cattle. While bulls are asymptomatic carriers of this protozoan, cows infected with T. foetus exhibit embryonic death, abortions, reproductive tract infections, or infertility. In Mexico, the first report of T. foetus was made more than 60 years ago; however, efforts to control this disease through diagnosis have been limited despite the negative impact on livestock farming. Objective: To confirm the presence of T. foetus in animals from northwest Mexico through molecular detection, sequencing, and phylogenetic analyses. Methods: Forty biological samples (smegma and mucopurulent vaginal secretions) were collected and analyzed by the PCR technique to identify T. foetus using specific primers. To confirm homology and determine genetic relationships, sequencing and phylogenetic analyses were performed using amplicons obtained from T. foetuspositive animals. Results: The PCR technique identified T. foetus in smegma and in clinical cases of metritis. Sequences obtained from PCR products revealed 99.65% similarity and a bootstrap value of 99% with isolates of T. foetus reported in China, Spain, and the USA. Based on the sequencing results, five new Mexican isolates of T. foetus were published in NCBI. Conclusion: This is the first report confirming the presence of T. foetus in Mexico using sequencing and phylogenetic analyses from positive cattle samples. Our research represents the basis for developing alternative and accurate tests to diagnose T. foetus as part of the strategy to epidemiologically control bovine trichomoniasis in the country",abortions; bovine; bulls; cattle; cows; diagnosis; epidemiology; epidemiological surveillance; infertility; molecular detection; phylogeny; phylogenetic analysis; smegma; trichomoniasis; T. foetus. Integración de diagnósticos moleculares para la confirmación de Tritrichomonas foetus en bovinos del noroeste de México Integração de diagnósticos moleculares para a confirmação de Tritrichomonas fo,marcadores,rev colomb cienc pecu 39 jan-dec e358794,background bovine trichomoniasi sexually transmitt disease caus tritrichomona foetu significantly impair reproductive health cattle while bull asymptomatic carrier protozoan cows infect foetu exhibit embryonic death abortion reproductive tract infection infertility mexico first report foetu made more than 60 year ago however effort control disease through diagnosi have been limit despite negative impact livestock farm objective confirm presence foetu animal northwest mexico through molecular detection sequenc phylogenetic analys method forty biological sampl smegma mucopurulent vaginal secretion collect analyz pcr technique identify foetu using specific primer confirm homology determine genetic relationship sequenc phylogenetic analys perform using amplicon obtain foetuspositive animal result pcr technique identifi foetu smegma clinical case metriti sequenc obtain pcr product reveal 99 65 similarity bootstrap value 99 isolat foetu report china spain usa based sequenc result five new mexican isolat foetu publish ncbi conclusion first report confirm presence foetu mexico using sequenc phylogenetic analys positive cattle sampl our research represent basi develop alternative accurate test diagnose foetu part strategy epidemiologically control bovine trichomoniasi country,abortion bovine bull cattle cows diagnosi epidemiology epidemiological surveillance infertility molecular detection phylogeny phylogenetic analysi smegma trichomoniasi foetu integracion de diagnostico molecular para la confirmacion de tritrichomona foetu en bovino del noroeste de mexico integracao de diagnostico molecular para confirmacao de tritrichomona fo,rev colomb cienc pecu 39 jan-dec e358794 background bovine trichomoniasi sexually transmitt disease caus tritrichomona foetu significantly impair reproductive health cattle while bull asymptomatic carrier protozoan cows infect foetu exhibit embryonic death abortion reproductive tract infection infertility mexico first report foetu made more than 60 year ago however effort control disease through diagnosi have been limit despite negative impact livestock farm objective confirm presence foetu animal northwest mexico through molecular detection sequenc phylogenetic analys method forty biological sampl smegma mucopurulent vaginal secretion collect analyz pcr technique identify foetu using specific primer confirm homology determine genetic relationship sequenc phylogenetic analys perform using amplicon obtain foetuspositive animal result pcr technique identifi foetu smegma clinical case metriti sequenc obtain pcr product reveal 99 65 similarity bootstrap value 99 isolat foetu report china spain usa based sequenc result five new mexican isolat foetu publish ncbi conclusion first report confirm presence foetu mexico using sequenc phylogenetic analys positive cattle sampl our research represent basi develop alternative accurate test diagnose foetu part strategy epidemiologically control bovine trichomoniasi country abortion bovine bull cattle cows diagnosi epidemiology epidemiological surveillance infertility molecular detection phylogeny phylogenetic analysi smegma trichomoniasi foetu integracion de diagnostico molecular para la confirmacion de tritrichomona foetu en bovino del noroeste de mexico integracao de diagnostico molecular para confirmacao de tritrichomona fo,1.0.0,60f00e50c6ff4cfe
2256-2958,358794.pdf,358794_0,es,va-Corona JC. Integrating molecular,"Antecedentes: La tricomoniasis bovina es una enfermedad de transmisión sexual causada por Tritrichomonas foetus y tiene un impacto significativo al afectar la salud reproductiva de los hatos bovinos. El toro es el portador asintomático de este protozoario, pero en la vaca T. foetus puede ocasionar muerte embrionaria, aborto, infecciones del aparato reproductivo o infertilidad. En México, el primer reporte de esta enfermedad tiene más de 60 años; sin embargo, los esfuerzos para controlarla a través del diagnóstico han sido escasos, a pesar de su impacto negativo en la ganadería. Objetivo: Confirmar la presencia de T. foetus mediante análisis de secuenciación y filogenia a partir de aislados moleculares obtenidos de animales positivos en el noroeste de México. Métodos: Se colectaron 40 muestras biológicas (esmegma y contenido vaginal purulento) y se analizaron por la técnica de PCR para identificar T. foetus utilizando oligonucleótidos específicos. Para confirmar la homología y determinar las relaciones genéticas, se realizaron secuenciaciones y análisis filogenéticos utilizando amplicones obtenidos de animales positivos a T. foetus. Resultados: La técnica de PCR identificó T. foetus en esmegma y en casos clínicos de metritis. Las secuencias obtenidas de los productos de PCR revelaron una identidad del 99.65% y un valor bootstrap del 99% con aislados reportados de China, España y EE. UU. Con base en los resultados de la secuenciación, cinco nuevos aislados mexicanos de T. foetus se publicaron en NCBI. Conclusión: Este es el primer trabajo que confirma la presencia de T. foetus en México mediante secuenciación y filogenia a partir de casos positivos en bovinos. Este estudio será la base para desarrollar pruebas alternativas y precisas para diagnosticar T. foetus como parte de la estrategia para controlar epidemiológicamente la tricomoniasis bovina en el país",abortos; análisis filogenético; bovinos; 