2256-2958,358801.pdf,358801_0,en,eISSN: 2256-2958,"Background: Pasture structure directly influences the ingestive behavior and feed intake of grazing ruminants, particularly under continuous stocking systems. More heterogeneous swards, with greater variability in plant height, may increase selectivity and alter intake dynamics and feeding efficiency. Objective: To evaluate how different horizontal structures of marandu grass (Urochloa brizantha cv. Marandu) pastures, maintained at an average height of 25 cm, affect feeding behavior and nutrient intake by sheep. Methods: The study was conducted from September 2019 to March 2020, using 16 crossbred sheep (Santa Inês × Dorper) allocated to eight paddocks under two treatments: 1) less heterogeneous pasture (plant height CV <35%) and 2) more heterogeneous pasture (CV >35%). Variables evaluated included nutrient intake, digestibility, feeding behavior (grazing, rumination, idleness, meal time, number and interval between meals, and rumination bouts), as well as forage mass, morphological composition, and chemical composition of the pasture. Data were analyzed by analysis of variance (ANOVA), using the F-test at a 10% significance level (P<0.10). Results: More heterogeneous swards promoted greater dry matter intake by grazing sheep (P<0.10). However, pasture heterogeneity did not significantly affect nutrient digestibility, chemical composition of hand-plucked samples, or behavioral parameters (P>0.10). Conclusion: Under continuous stocking, marandu grass pastures with higher structural heterogeneity (CV between 50.32% and 60.64%) increase dry matter intake in sheep. Although heterogeneity did not influence digestibility or quantitative aspects of behavior, animals showed more frequent grazing during the day and concentrated rumination and idleness at night under the same experimental conditions",available forage; ingestive behavior; nutrient intake; pasture intake; pasture structure; rumination; sheep farming; time spent grazing. Pastizales heterogéneos de pasto Marandu (Urochloa brizantha) bajo pastoreo continuo mejoran el consumo de materia seca en ovejas Pastagens heterogêneas de capim-Marandu (Urochloa brizantha) sob lotação contínua melhoram a ingestão de matéria seca em ovinos J,marcadores,eissn 2256-2958,background pasture structure directly influenc ingestive behavior feed intake graz ruminant particularly under continuou stock system more heterogeneou sward greater variability plant height may increase selectivity alter intake dynamic feed efficiency objective evaluate how different horizontal structur marandu gras urochloa brizantha cv marandu pastur maintain average height 25 cm affect feed behavior nutrient intake sheep method study conduct september 2019 march 2020 using 16 crossbr sheep santa ines dorper allocat eight paddock under two treatment less heterogeneou pasture plant height cv 35 more heterogeneou pasture cv 35 variabl evaluat includ nutrient intake digestibility feed behavior graz rumination idlenes meal time number interval between meal rumination bout well forage mass morphological composition chemical composition pasture data analyz analysi variance anova using f-test 10 significance level 10 result more heterogeneou sward promot greater dry matter intake graz sheep 10 however pasture heterogeneity did not significantly affect nutrient digestibility chemical composition hand-pluck sampl behavioral parameter 10 conclusion under continuou stock marandu gras pastur higher structural heterogeneity cv between 50 32 60 64 increase dry matter intake sheep although heterogeneity did not influence digestibility quantitative aspect behavior animal show more frequent graz during day concentrat rumination idlenes night under same experimental condition,available forage ingestive behavior nutrient intake pasture intake pasture structure rumination sheep farm time spent graz pastizal heterogeneo de pasto marandu urochloa brizantha bajo pastoreo continuo mejoran el consumo de materia seca en oveja pastagen heterogenea de capim-marandu urochloa brizantha sob lotacao continua melhoram ingestao de materia seca em ovino,eissn 2256-2958 background pasture structure directly influenc ingestive behavior feed intake graz ruminant particularly under continuou stock system more heterogeneou sward greater variability plant height may increase selectivity alter intake dynamic feed efficiency objective evaluate how different horizontal structur marandu gras urochloa brizantha cv marandu pastur maintain average height 25 cm affect feed behavior nutrient intake sheep method study conduct september 2019 march 2020 using 16 crossbr sheep santa ines dorper allocat eight paddock under two treatment less heterogeneou pasture plant height cv 35 more heterogeneou pasture cv 35 variabl evaluat includ nutrient intake digestibility feed behavior graz rumination idlenes meal time number interval between meal rumination bout well forage mass morphological composition chemical composition pasture data analyz analysi variance anova using f-test 10 significance level 10 result more heterogeneou sward promot greater dry matter intake graz sheep 10 however pasture heterogeneity did not significantly affect nutrient digestibility chemical composition hand-pluck sampl behavioral parameter 10 conclusion under continuou stock marandu gras pastur higher structural heterogeneity cv between 50 32 60 64 increase dry matter intake sheep although heterogeneity did not influence digestibility quantitative aspect behavior animal show more frequent graz during day concentrat rumination idlenes night under same experimental condition available forage ingestive behavior nutrient intake pasture intake pasture structure rumination sheep farm time spent graz pastizal heterogeneo de pasto marandu urochloa brizantha bajo pastoreo continuo mejoran el consumo de materia seca en oveja pastagen heterogenea de capim-marandu urochloa brizantha sob lotacao continua melhoram ingestao de m