2256-3067,Art.13+Prevalencia+experiencias+traumáticas+infancia.pdf,Art.13+Prevalencia+experiencias+traumáticas+infancia_0,en,relación con las experiencias traumáticas,"Objective: to analyze the prevalence of abuse traumatic experiences and sociopolitical violence in adults between 18 and 60 years old with and without depressive disorders. Method: non-experimental analytical quantitative approach. 106 people participated (53 depressive-disorder cases and 53 controls) matched by age, sex, education, and socioeconomic level; all with the same probability of having been exposed to abuse and sociopolitical violence experiences in childhood. The Traumatic Experiences in Childhood Inventory (ETISRCol) by Posada, Londoño & Gaviria (2019) was applied. Results: in relation to the traumatic experiences associated with sociopolitical violence the significant differences are focused on items related to displacement and extortion as experiences of this factor. In addition, all related items to loss, separation, abandonment, and resignation present high prevalence in the case group. In regards of sexual abuse, the highest prevalence is found in the case group, but the differences are not significant with the control group. Finally, a higher prevalence of emotional abuse was identified in the case group. Conclusions: traumatic events in childhood such as “emotional and physical abuse” have high prevalence in people diagnosed with depressive disorders","child abuse, sociopolitical violence, childhood trauma",marcadores,relacion con las experiencia traumatica,objective analyze prevalence abuse traumatic experienc sociopolitical violence adult between 18 60 year old without depressive disorder method non-experimental analytical quantitative approach 106 people participat 53 depressive-disorder case 53 control match age sex education socioeconomic level all same probability having been expos abuse sociopolitical violence experienc childhood traumatic experienc childhood inventory etisrcol posada londono gaviria 2019 appli result relation traumatic experienc associat sociopolitical violence significant differenc focus item relat displacement extortion experienc factor addition all relat item loss separation abandonment resignation present high prevalence case group regard sexual abuse highest prevalence found case group but differenc not significant control group finally higher prevalence emotional abuse identifi case group conclusion traumatic event childhood such emotional physical abuse have high prevalence people diagnos depressive disorder,child abuse sociopolitical violence childhood trauma,relacion con las experiencia traumatica objective analyze prevalence abuse traumatic experienc sociopolitical violence adult between 18 60 year old without depressive disorder method non-experimental analytical quantitative approach 106 people participat 53 depressive-disorder case 53 control match age sex education socioeconomic level all same probability having been expos abuse sociopolitical violence experienc childhood traumatic experienc childhood inventory etisrcol posada londono gaviria 2019 appli result relation traumatic experienc associat sociopolitical violence significant differenc focus item relat displacement extortion experienc factor addition all relat item loss separation abandonment resignation present high prevalence case group regard sexual abuse highest prevalence found case group but differenc not significant control group finally higher prevalence emotional abuse identifi case group conclusion traumatic event childhood such emotional physical abuse have high prevalence people diagnos depressive disorder child abuse sociopolitical violence childhood trauma,1.0.0,8b66e43cb36fad91
2256-3067,Art.14+Efectos+de+variaciones+autoridad_comportamiento+obediente.pdf,Art.14+Efectos+de+variaciones+autoridad_comportamiento+obediente_0,es,Efectos de variaciones en la señalización de la autoridad,"Se analiza el efecto de variaciones en la señalización de autoridad en el ajuste a normas, en una situación natural simulada. Se trabajó con 24 estudiantes de sexo masculino, con edades entre los 5 y los 8 años, asignados a una de tres condiciones experimentales: intermitencia en la autoridad señalizada (IAS), ambigüedad e intermitencia en la autoridad señalizada (AIAS) y autoridad no señalizada (ANS). El procedimiento consistió en la aplicación de consecuencias positivas o su omisión, según la obediencia o desobediencia a una orden dada por el experimentador. Los resultados indican que a menor posibilidad de discriminar el momento ∗Artículo de investigación. ∗∗Universidad de Chile. Correo: dorian.zutta@ug. uchile.cl. ORCID: 0000-0003-0961-2137. § Universidad de Nariño, Colombia. Correo: lunaedwingerardo@gmail.com. ORCID: 0000- 00026916-8579. en que se entra en contacto funcional con la autoridad, se incrementan las probabilidades de ajuste a la norma a través del tiempo. Por otro lado, se sugiere que la omisión de sanción positiva contingente a la transgresión genera un efecto aversivo equiparable en algunos aspectos al de la sanción negativa, sobre todo cuando el participante transgresor observa a otros recibir la sanción positiva. Finalmente, se identifican comportamientos que pueden ser descritos como elusión en algunos de los participantes","autoridad no señalizada, seguimiento de normas, dimensiones funcionales de la conducta social",marcadores,efect vari senalizacion autoridad,analiza efecto vari senalizacion autoridad ajuste norm situacion natural simulada trabajo 24 estudiant sexo masculino edad entre anos asignad tres condicion experimental intermitencia autoridad senalizada ias ambiguedad intermitencia autoridad senalizada aias autoridad no senalizada ans procedimiento consistio aplicacion consecuenci positiv omision segun obediencia desobediencia orden dada experimentador resultad indican menor posibilidad discriminar momento articulo investigacion universidad chile correo dorian zutta ug uchile cl orcid 0000-0003-0961-2137 SS universidad narino colombia correo lunaedwingerardo gmail com orcid 0000- 00026916-8579 entra contacto funcional autoridad incrementan probabilidad ajuste norma trav tiempo otro lado sugiere omision sancion positiva contingente transgresion genera efecto aversivo equiparable algun aspect sancion negativa sobre todo cuando participante transgresor observa otros recibir sancion positiva final identifican comport pueden ser descrit como elusion algun participant,autoridad no senalizada seguimiento norm dimension funcional conducta social,efect vari senalizacion autoridad analiza efecto vari senalizacion autoridad ajuste norm situacion natural simulada trabajo 24 estudiant sexo masculino edad entre anos asignad tres condicion experimental intermitencia autoridad senalizada ias ambiguedad intermitencia autoridad senalizada aias autoridad no senalizada ans procedimiento consistio aplicacion consecuenci positiv omision segun obediencia desobediencia orden dada experimentador resultad indican menor posibilidad discriminar momento articulo investigacion universidad chile correo dorian zutta ug uchile cl orcid 0000-0003-0961-2137 SS universidad narino colombia correo lunaedwingerardo gmail com orcid 0000- 00026916-8579 entra contacto funcional autoridad incrementan probabilidad ajuste norma trav tiempo otro lado sugiere omision sancion positiva contingente transgresion genera efecto aversivo equiparable algun aspect sancion negativa sobre todo cuando participante transgresor observa otros recibir sancion positiva final identifican comport pueden ser descrit como elusion algun participant autoridad no senalizada seguimiento norm dimension funcional conducta social,1.0.0,1beebc2ceaa1eae3
2256-3067,Art.14+Efectos+de+variaciones+autoridad_comportamiento+obediente.pdf,Art.14+Efectos+de+variaciones+autoridad_comportamiento+obediente_0,en,os indican que a,"The effect of variations in authority signaling on compliance with norms is analyzed in a simulated natural situation. Twentyfour male students, aged between 5 and 8 years, were assigned to one of three experimental conditions: intermittence in signaled authority (IAS), ambiguity and intermittence in signaled authority (AIAS), and non-signaled authority (ANS). The 225 Vol.21 Núm 1 (2025) | enero-junio ISSN:1794-9998 | eISSN:2256-3067 procedure consisted of applying or omitting positive consequences depending on the participant’s obedience or disobedience to an order given by the experimenter. The results indicate that the lower the possibility of discriminating the moment in which functional contact with authority occurs, the greater the likelihood of compliance with the norm over time. Furthermore, it is suggested that the omission of a positive sanction contingent on transgression generates an aversive effect comparable in some respects to that of negative sanction, especially when the transgressing participant observes others receiving the positive sanction. Finally, behaviors that can be described as avoidance were identified in some participants","unmarked authority, monitoring of standards, functional dimensions of social behavior",marcadores,os indican que,effect vari authority signal compliance norm analyz simulat natural situation twentyfour male student aged between year assign one three experimental condition intermittence signal authority ias ambiguity intermittence signal authority aias non-signal authority ans 225 vol 21 num 2025 enero-junio issn 1794-9998 eissn 2256-3067 procedure consist apply omitt positive consequenc depend participant obedience disobedience order given experimenter result indicate lower possibility discriminat moment which functional contact authority occur greater likelihood compliance norm over time furthermore suggest omission positive sanction contingent transgression generat aversive effect comparable some respect negative sanction especially when transgress participant observ other receiv positive sanction finally behavior can describ avoidance identifi some participant,unmark authority monitor standard functional dimension social behavior,os indican que effect vari authority signal compliance norm analyz simulat natural situation twentyfour male student aged between year assign one three experimental condition intermittence signal authority ias ambiguity intermittence signal authority aias non-signal authority ans 225 vol 21 num 2025 enero-junio issn 1794-9998 eissn 2256-3067 procedure consist apply omitt positive consequenc depend participant obedience disobedience order given experimenter result indicate lower possibility discriminat moment which functional contact authority occur greater likelihood compliance norm over time furthermore suggest omission positive sanction contingent transgression generat aversive effect comparable some respect negative sanction especially when transgress participant observ other receiv positive sanction finally behavior can describ avoidance identifi some participant unmark authority monitor standard functional dimension social behavior,1.0.0,b01f3a18845f5ed7
2256-3067,Art.16+Propiedades+psicométricas+grit+académico.pdf,Art.16+Propiedades+psicométricas+grit+académico_0,es,Propiedades psicométricas de la adaptación de la escala,"El grit académico, o tenacidad académica, asociada al establecimiento de metas desafiantes y a la perseverancia ante adversidades es un predictor clave del rendimiento y adaptación escolar. Este estudio tuvo como finalidad adaptar y evaluar las propiedades psicométricas de la ∗Artículo de investigación. ∗∗Universidad Católica de Colombia. Correo de correspondencia: magomez50 @ ucatolica . edu . co. ORCID: 0009-0007-5233-7624. § Universidad de La Sabana, Colombia. Correo: edgar. riveros@unisabana.edu.co. ORCID: 0000-0002-0414674X. ¶ Universidad Católica de Colombia. Correo: blavendano@ucatolica.edu.co. ORCID: 0000- 00028136-5380. ‖ Universidad de Oviedo, España. Correo: fernandezaruben @ uniovi . es. ORCID: 0000 - 0003 - 1867-8074. escala de grit académico como medida de tenacidad académica. Se realizó un diseño instrumental que contó con la participación de 1293 estudiantes, 832 colombianos (64.35%) y 461 mexicanos (35.65%) de 10 a 18 años (M = 12.92; DE = 1.35), 167 del total presentaron alta capacidad. El análisis factorial exploratorio (AFE) y el confirmatorio (AFC), las pruebas de invarianza factorial y los análisis de fiabilidad y validez concurrente con escalas de grit y perfeccionismo confirmaron una estructura unidimensional con los siguientes índices de ajuste (CFI = 0.999; RMSEA = 0.022) e invarianza configuracional, métrica, escalar y estricta entre país, sexo, coeficiente intelectual (CI) y grado académico. La escala mostró consistencia interna (￿= 0.821; ￿ = 0.821) y correlaciones significativas con perseverancia en el esfuerzo (r = 0.374) y esfuerzo perfeccionista (r = 0.346). No se hallaron diferencias significativas en puntajes por país, sexo, CI o grado académico. Los hallazgos respaldan la validez transcultural y utilidad del instrumento para evaluar tenacidad académica en contextos 263 Vol.21 Núm 1 (2025) | enero-junio ISSN:1794-9998 | eISSN:2256-3067 educativos hispanohablantes. La adaptación de esta escala contribuye a la medición de factores no cognitivos en poblaciones no WEIRD (Occidentales, Educados, Industrializados, Ricos y Desarrollados) y facilita la implementación de intervenciones educativas basadas en evidencia, aunque se recomienda ampliar la representatividad muestral en futuros estudios","tenacidad académica, grit, validación, adaptación, propiedades psicométricas, altas capacidades",marcadores,propiedad psicometric adaptacion escala,grit academico tenacidad academica asociada establecimiento metas desafiant perseverancia ante adversidad predictor clave rendimiento adaptacion escolar este estudio tuvo como finalidad adaptar evaluar propiedad psicometric articulo investigacion universidad catolica colombia correo correspondencia magomez50 ucatolica edu co orcid 0009-0007-5233-7624 SS universidad sabana colombia correo edgar river unisabana edu co orcid 0000-0002-0414674x universidad catolica colombia correo blavendano ucatolica edu co orcid 0000- 00028136-5380 universidad oviedo espana correo fernandezaruben uniovi orcid 0000 0003 1867-8074 escala grit academico como medida tenacidad academica realizo diseno instrumental conto participacion 1293 estudiant 832 colombian 64 35 461 mexican 35 65 10 18 anos 12 92 35 167 total presentaron alta capacidad analisis factorial exploratorio afe confirmatorio afc prueb invarianza factorial analisis fiabilidad validez concurrente escal grit perfeccionismo confirmaron estructura unidimensional siguient indic ajuste cfi 999 rmsea 022 invarianza configuracional metrica escalar estricta entre pais sexo coeficiente intelectual ci grado academico escala mostro consistencia interna 821 821 correl significativ perseverancia esfuerzo 374 esfuerzo perfeccionista 346 no hallaron diferenci significativ puntaj pais sexo ci grado academico hallazg respaldan validez transcultural utilidad instrumento evaluar tenacidad academica context 263 vol 21 num 2025 enero-junio issn 1794-9998 eissn 2256-3067 educativ hispanohablant adaptacion esta escala contribuye medicion factor no cognitiv pobl no weird occidental educad industrializad ricos desarrollad facilita implementacion intervencion educativ basad evidencia aunque recomienda ampliar representatividad muestral futur estudi,tenacidad academica grit validacion adaptacion propiedad psicometric altas capacidad,propiedad psicometric adaptacion escala grit academico tenacidad academica asociada establecimiento metas desafiant perseverancia ante adversidad predictor clave rendimiento adaptacion escolar este estudio tuvo como finalidad adaptar evaluar propiedad psicometric articulo investigacion universidad catolica colombia correo correspondencia magomez50 ucatolica edu co orcid 0009-0007-5233-7624 SS universidad sabana colombia correo edgar river unisabana edu co orcid 0000-0002-0414674x universidad catolica colombia correo blavendano ucatolica edu co orcid 0000- 00028136-5380 universidad oviedo espana correo fernandezaruben uniovi orcid 0000 0003 1867-8074 escala grit academico como medida tenacidad academica realizo diseno instrumental conto participacion 1293 estudiant 832 colombian 64 35 461 mexican 35 65 10 18 anos 12 92 35 167 total presentaron alta capacidad analisis factorial exploratorio afe confirmatorio afc prueb invarianza factorial analisis fiabilidad validez concurrente escal grit perfeccionismo confirmaron estructura unidimensional siguient indic ajuste cfi 999 rmsea 022 invarianza configuracional metrica escalar estricta entre pais sexo coeficiente intelectual ci grado academico escala mostro consistencia interna 821 821 correl significativ perseverancia esfuerzo 374 esfuerzo perfeccionista 346 no hallaron diferenci significativ puntaj pais sexo ci grado academico hallazg respaldan validez transcultural utilidad instrumento evaluar tenacidad academica context 263 vol 21 num 2025 enero-junio issn 1794-9998 eissn 2256-3067 educativ hispanohablant adaptacion esta escala contribuye medicion factor no cognitiv pobl no weird occidental educad industrializad ricos desarrollad facilita implementacion intervencion educativ basad evidencia aunque recomienda ampliar representatividad muestral futur estudi tenacidad academica grit validacion adaptacion propiedad psicometric altas capacidad,1.0.0,2a9b9050ee718509
2256-3067,Art.16+Propiedades+psicométricas+grit+académico.pdf,Art.16+Propiedades+psicométricas+grit+académico_0,en,nterna (￿= 0.821;,"Academic grit, encompassing the establishment of challenging goals and sustained perseverance in the face of adversity, emerges as a critical predictor of academic achievement and school adjustment. The purpose of this study was to adapt the Academic Grit Scale and assess its psychometric properties as a measure of academic tenacity. Employing an instrumental design, the research involved 1,293 students, 832 from Colombia (64.35%) and 461 from Mexico (35.65%), aged 10 to 18 years (M = 12.92; SD = 1.35), 167 students of the total sample showed high ability. Exploratory factor analysis (EFA) and confirmatory factor analysis (CFA) were conducted, along with tests of factorial invariance and analyses of reliability and concurrent validity using established grit and perfectionism scales. The results confirmed a unidimensional structure with excellent fit indices (CFI = 0.999; RMSEA = 0.022) and demonstrated configural, metric, scalar, and strict invariance across country, gender, intelligence quotient (IQ) and grade level. The scale exhibited high reliability (￿= 0.821; ￿= 0.821) and significant correlations with perseverance of effort (r = 0.374) and perfectionistic striving (r = 0.346). No significant differences in scores were found based on country, gender, IQ, or grade. The adaptation of this scale contributes to the assessment of non-cognitive factors in nonWEIRD populations (Western, Educated, Industrialized, Rich, and Developed) and facilitates the implementation of evidencebased educational interventions. However, it is recommended to broaden sample representativeness in future studies","tenacity, academic grit, validation, adaptation, psychometric properties, high ability Propiedades psicométricas de la adaptación de la escala de grit académico con población colombiana y mexicana El grit, o tenacidad, ha tomado importancia en la investigación educativa, al constituir un predictor del rendimiento académico y estar estrechamente vinculado con los procesos de adaptación del estudia",marcadores,nterna 821,academic grit encompass establishment challeng goal sustain perseverance face adversity emerg critical predictor academic achievement school adjustment purpose study adapt academic grit scale asses its psychometric properti measure academic tenacity employ instrumental design research involv 293 student 832 colombia 64 35 461 mexico 35 65 aged 10 18 year 12 92 sd 35 167 student total sample show high ability exploratory factor analysi efa confirmatory factor analysi cfa conduct along test factorial invariance analys reliability concurrent validity using establish grit perfectionism scal result confirm unidimensional structure excellent fit indic cfi 999 rmsea 022 demonstrat configural metric scalar strict invariance acros country gender intelligence quotient iq grade level scale exhibit high reliability 821 821 significant correl perseverance effort 374 perfectionistic striv 346 no significant differenc scor found based country gender iq grade adaptation scale contribut assessment non-cognitive factor nonweird popul western educat industrializ rich develop facilitat implementation evidencebas educational intervention however recommend broaden sample representativenes future studi,tenacity academic grit validation adaptation psychometric properti high ability propiedad psicometrica de la adaptacion de la escala de grit academico con poblacion colombiana mexicana el grit tenacidad ha tomado importancia en la investigacion educativa al constituir un predictor del rendimiento academico estar estrechamente vinculado con los proceso de adaptacion del estudia,nterna 821 academic grit encompass establishment challeng goal sustain perseverance face adversity emerg critical predictor academic achievement school adjustment purpose study adapt academic grit scale asses its psychometric properti measure academic tenacity employ instrumental design research involv 293 student 832 colombia 64 35 461 mexico 35 65 aged 10 18 year 12 92 sd 35 167 student total sample show high ability exploratory factor analysi efa confirmatory factor analysi cfa conduct along test factorial invariance analys reliability concurrent validity using establish grit perfectionism scal result confirm unidimensional structure excellent fit indic cfi 999 rmsea 022 demonstrat configural metric scalar strict invariance acros country gender intelligence quotient iq grade level scale exhibit high reliability 821 821 significant correl perseverance effort 374 perfectionistic striv 346 no significant differenc scor found based country gender iq grade adaptation scale contribut assessment non-cognitive factor nonweird popul western educat industrializ rich develop facilitat implementation evidencebas educational intervention however recommend broaden sample representativenes future studi tenacity academic grit validation adaptation psychometric properti high ability propiedad psicometrica de la adaptacion de la escala de grit academico con poblacion colombiana mexicana el grit tenacidad ha tomado importancia en la investigacion educativa al constituir un predictor del rendimiento academico estar estrechamente vinculado con los proceso de adaptacion del estudia,1.0.0,58359c5aef1e1947
2256-3067,Art.1_Participation+productions+Psychology+WoS.pdf,Art.1_Participation+productions+Psychology+WoS_0,en,∗Research article.,"Although developing countries represent a minimal percentage of the world’s scientific production with impact, it is necessary to analyze and study them to appreciate their research policies, publication rates and collaborations. For this study, we have selected all the countries that, according to the Human Development Report 2020, have a research and development expenditure below 0.8, which puts 168 countries in the focus of analysis. Focusing on the articles and review articles that these countries have obtained in the 11 categories that exist in Web of Science (SCI, SSCI and ESCI collections) on psychology, all articles with an impact factor in the years 2017 to 2021 have been selected. In total, 21337 articles were extracted, 62% of which were produced in South America and Asia. The highest number of papers have been published in the categories “Psychology 14 Vol.21 Núm 1 (2025) | enero-junio ISSN:1794-9998 | eISSN:2256-3067 Multidisciplinary” (33.7%) and “Psychology Clinical” (16.0%). Journals indexed in developing countries tend to have a more significant impact within their own continent, and the scientific collaboration networks they maintain are predominantly within the same continent. This leads us to the conclusion that scientific production and dissemination in developing countries are severely constrained, possibly due to social, economic, and political factors",scientific production; scientific collaboration; psychology; developing countries; bibliometrics,marcadores,research article,although develop countri represent minimal percentage world scientific production impact necessary analyze study them appreciate their research polici publication rate collabor study we have select all countri accord human development report 2020 have research development expenditure below which puts 168 countri focu analysi focus articl review articl these countri have obtain 11 categori exist web science sci ssci esci collection psychology all articl impact factor year 2017 2021 have been select total 21337 articl extract 62 which produc south america asia highest number paper have been publish categori psychology 14 vol 21 num 2025 enero-junio issn 1794-9998 eissn 2256-3067 multidisciplinary 33 psychology clinical 16 journal index develop countri tend have more significant impact within their own continent scientific collaboration network they maintain predominantly within same continent lead us conclusion scientific production dissemination develop countri severely constrain possibly due social economic political factor,scientific production scientific collaboration psychology develop countri bibliometric,research article although develop countri represent minimal percentage world scientific production impact necessary analyze study them appreciate their research polici publication rate collabor study we have select all countri accord human development report 2020 have research development expenditure below which puts 168 countri focu analysi focus articl review articl these countri have obtain 11 categori exist web science sci ssci esci collection psychology all articl impact factor year 2017 2021 have been select total 21337 articl extract 62 which produc south america asia highest number paper have been publish categori psychology 14 vol 21 num 2025 enero-junio issn 1794-9998 eissn 2256-3067 multidisciplinary 33 psychology clinical 16 journal index develop countri tend have more significant impact within their own continent scientific collaboration network they maintain predominantly within same continent lead us conclusion scientific production dissemination develop countri severely constrain possibly due social economic political factor scientific production scientific collaboration psychology develop countri bibliometric,1.0.0,1d3bb0a9e3cc3c9f
2256-3067,Art.1_Participation+productions+Psychology+WoS.pdf,Art.1_Participation+productions+Psychology+WoS_0,es,"psychology, all articles with an impact factor","Aunque los países en desarrollo representan un porcentaje mínimo de la producción científica mundial de impacto, es necesario analizarlos y estudiarlos para apreciar sus políticas de investigación, tasas de publicación y colaboraciones. Para este estudio hemos seleccionado todos los países que, según el Informe sobre Desarrollo Humano 2020, no alcanzan el 0,8 % en gasto en investigación y desarrollo, lo que sitúa a 168 países en el foco del análisis. Centrándonos en los artículos y artículos de revisión que estos países han obtenido en las 11 categorías que existen en Web of Science (colecciones SCI, SSCI y ESCI) sobre psicología, se han seleccionado todos los artículos con factor de impacto en los años 2017 a 2021. En total, se extrajeron 21 337 artículos, de los cuales el 62 % se producen en América del Sur y Asia. El mayor número de artículos se ha publicado en las categorías «Psicología multidisciplinar» (33,7 %) y «Psicología clínica» (16,0 %). Las revistas indexadas en países en desarrollo tienden a tener un impacto más significativo dentro de su propio continente, y las redes de colaboración científica que mantienen se encuentran predominantemente dentro del mismo continente. Esto nos lleva a la conclusión de que la producción y la difusión científicas en los países en desarrollo están muy limitadas, posiblemente debido a factores sociales, económicos y políticos",producción científica; colaboración científica; psicología; países en desarrollo; bibliometría. Statements and Declarations Funding: we did not receive any funding for the research presented in this paper. Conflict of interest: the authors declare that they have no conflict of interest,marcadores,psychology all articl with an impact factor,aunque pais desarrollo representan porcentaje minimo produccion cientifica mundial impacto necesario 