2256-3067,Art.2+Supportive+climate+and+dedication.pdf,Art.2+Supportive+climate+and+dedication_0,en,Supportive Climate and Dedication: Analyzing the Role,"Self-efficacy is a personal resource that mediates between antecedent and consequent variables. This study aimed to analyze the influence of a supportive climate on dedication through the mediation of selfefficacy and the moderating role of job ∗Research article. ∗∗Universidad Católica de Pereira, Colombia. Correspondencia. Correo: eliana . quiroz @ ucp . edu . co. ORCID: 0000-0001-9061-8864. § Universidad de Almería, España. Correo: cmsalva@ ual.es. ORCID: 0000-0001-8939-4971. ¶ Universidad de Almería, España. Correo: pfunez@ual. es. ORCID: 0000-0002-3268-1459. ‖ Universidad de Almería, España. Correo: marodrig@ ual.es. ORCID: 0000-0001-9771-0663. tenure among public employees, within the framework of the Job Demands-Resources Theory. The sample consisted of 325 public employees, all belonging to the administrative staff of a Spanish university, who completed a sociodemographic and work-related data sheet, the FOCUS-93 (First Organizational Climate/Culture Unified Search), the PCQ12 (Psychological Capital Questionnaire), and the UWES-9 (Utrecht Work Engagement Scale). Data were analyzed using descriptive statistics, Pearson’s correlation coefficient, and regression analysis with PROCESS. The findings suggest that the influence of a supportive climate on dedication through selfefficacy was positive. Furthermore, higher job tenure moderates the relationship between a supportive climate and self-efficacy. In conclusion, the perception of a supportive climate influences dedication through the mediating of self-efficacy, but this moderates by job tenure. The theoretical and practical implications for public management are discussed. Cultivating resources such as a 41 Vol.21 Núm 1 (2025) | enero-junio ISSN:1794-9998 | eISSN:2256-3067 supportive climate and self-efficacy becomes a healthy organizational practice that improves dedication, especially among employees with longer job tenure",public management; job tenure; self-efficacy; supportive climate; dedication,marcadores,supportive climate dedication analyz role,self-efficacy personal resource mediat between antecedent consequent variabl study aimed analyze influence supportive climate dedication through mediation selfefficacy moderat role job research article universidad catolica de pereira colombia correspondencia correo eliana quiroz ucp edu co orcid 0000-0001-9061-8864 SS universidad de almeria espana correo cmsalva ual es orcid 0000-0001-8939-4971 universidad de almeria espana correo pfunez ual es orcid 0000-0002-3268-1459 universidad de almeria espana correo marodrig ual es orcid 0000-0001-9771-0663 tenure among public employe within framework job demands-resourc theory sample consist 325 public employe all belong administrative staff spanish university who complet sociodemographic work-relat data sheet focus-93 first organizational climate culture unifi search pcq12 psychological capital questionnaire uwes-9 utrecht work engagement scale data analyz using descriptive statistic pearson correlation coefficient regression analysi proces finding suggest influence supportive climate dedication through selfefficacy positive furthermore higher job tenure moderat relationship between supportive climate self-efficacy conclusion perception supportive climate influenc dedication through mediat self-efficacy but moderat job tenure theoretical practical implic public management discuss cultivat resourc such 41 vol 21 num 2025 enero-junio issn 1794-9998 eissn 2256-3067 supportive climate self-efficacy becom healthy organizational practice improv dedication especially among employe longer job tenure,public management job tenure self-efficacy supportive climate dedication,supportive climate dedication analyz role self-efficacy personal resource mediat between antecedent consequent variabl study aimed analyze influence supportive climate 