2256-3067,Art.4+Actitudes+hacia+la+comida+estudiantes+Bucaramanga.pdf,Art.4+Actitudes+hacia+la+comida+estudiantes+Bucaramanga_0,en,analizar las actitudes hacia la comida en,"Attitudes towards food are those beliefs, thoughts, feelings and behaviors in relation to food that lead to different eating disorders and pathologies. Currently, there are studies on eating disorders, but few comprehensively and specifically address the habits, thoughts and attitudes that constitute a serious problem for people’s health. Indeed, the objective of this research is to analyze the attitudes towards food in female university students between the ages of 18 and 25 in the city of Bucaramanga. The study was carried out with a sample of 44 female students from the Universidad Pontificia Bolivariana between the ages of 18 and 25, in which a descriptive analysis was carried out through the EAT-26 scale, which allowed observing the risk or state of the women. with such attitudes. It was found that 56.81% of the respondents are at risk of eating disorders. In the associations that were made, no statistical relevance was found, which means that there is no association between having a risky diet pattern and developing risk of eating disorders, nor with bulimia and oral control","attitudes towards food, eating disorders, risk",marcadores,analizar las actitud hacia la comida en,attitud toward food those belief thought feeling behavior relation food lead different eating disorder pathologi currently there studi eating disorder but few comprehensively specifically addres habit thought attitud constitute seriou problem people health inde objective research analyze attitud toward food female university student between ages 18 25 city bucaramanga study carri out sample 44 female student universidad pontificia bolivariana between ages 18 25 which descriptive analysi carri out through eat-26 scale which allow observ risk state women such attitud found 56 81 respondent risk eating disorder associ made no statistical relevance found which mean there no association between having risky diet pattern develop risk eating disorder nor bulimia oral control,attitud toward food eating disorder risk,analizar las actitud hacia la comida en attitud toward food those belief thought feeling behavior relation food lead different eating disorder pathologi currently there studi eating disorder but few comprehensively specifically addres habit thought attitud constitute seriou problem people health inde objective research analyze attitud toward food female university student between ages 18 25 city bucaramanga study carri out sample 44 female student universidad pontificia bolivariana between ages 18 25 which descriptive analysi carri out through eat-26 scale which allow observ risk state women such attitud found 56 81 respondent risk eating disorder associ made no statistical relevance found which mean there no association between having risky diet pattern develop risk eating disorder nor bulimia oral control attitud toward food eating disorder risk,1.0.0,1ad29ea85dbd7582
2256-3067,Art.5+Adaptation+questionnaire+experiences+video+games.pdf,Art.5+Adaptation+questionnaire+experiences+video+games_0,en,Adaptation of the Questionnaire of Experiences Related,"The objective was to adapt the Questionnaire of Experiences Related to Video Games (CERV) for young people in Oxapampa, 2021. Following an instrumental design, the sample used consisted of 500 young ∗Artículo de investigación. § Universidad Cesar Vallejo, Perú. Correo de correspondencia: detsy . cs . 2 @ gmail . com. ORCID: 0000-0003-1717-7753. ¶ Universidad Cesar Vallejo, Perú. Correo: smraymundoc @ ucvvirtual . edu . pe. ORCID: 0000-0001-6431-3696. ‖ Universidad Cesar Vallejo, Perú. Correo: quispema1194 @ ucvvirtual . edu . pe. ORCID: 0000-0002-1903-2382. ∗∗Universidad Cesar Vallejo, Perú. Correo: dfmt72@ gmail.com. ORCID: 0000-0003-3396-5987. men and women, aged 16 to 18 years, non-probabilistic snowball sampling. The CERV was modified to adapt it to sample sociocultural characteristics. The findings indicated an optimal Aiken’s V index, which implies that the items have an adequate degree of representativeness, clarity and relevance. The two-dimensional structure explained 63% of the variance of scores, dimensions: dependence and avoidance, and negative consequences. These obtained optimal fit indices in the confirmatory factor analysis (CMIN = 1.887; RMSEA = 0.042; IFC = 0.986; TLI = 0.993). Reliability analysis determined that the dimensions had adequate internal consistency (Ω > .80). It is concluded that the modified version of CERV demonstrated optimal validity and reliability, supporting its relevance for measuring video game dependence in this population","videogames; youth; validity, reliability, adaptation 88 Vol.21 Núm 1 (2025) | enero-junio ISSN:1794-9998 | eISSN:2256-3067",marcadores,adaptation questionnaire experienc relat,objective adapt questionnaire experienc relat video game cerv young people oxapampa 2021 follow instrumental design sample used consist 500 young a