2256-3334,361484+final.pdf,361484+final_0,en,"cas de series temporales a fuentes digitales abiertas, reforzando su valor","Objective: The purpose of this study is to evaluate, from a conceptual and procedural perspective, the potential for predicting the time course of the relative search volume (RSV) for the term “COVID” in Google Trends™, in the context of SARS-CoV-2 in Colombia. This will be achieved through the application of time series statistical techniques aimed at analyzing its correlation and predictive capacity in short-term lags with confirmed cases reported by epidemiological surveillance. The study also explores its usefulness as a complement to syndromic surveillance systems for the early detection of epidemiological patterns, with potential applications to other emerging and priority public health events beyond SARS-CoV-2. Methods: A longitudinal ecological study was conducted in Colombia between 2020 and 2022, based on daily aggregated RSV data and confirmed cases reported by the National Institute of Health. The analysis was structured in steps replicable for public health: standardization using Z-scores, seasonal and trend decomposition using STL (Seasonal and Trend decomposition using Loess), cross-correlation analysis, and Granger test, with the purpose of examining patterns, lags, and predictive relationships (temporal precedence). Results: The case series showed fluctuations consistent with the RSV series. A maximum cross-correlation of 0.70 was identified, with a lag of −27 days, indicating that the increase in searches preceded the increase in cases. The Granger test showed significance for lags of 1 to 7 days (F = 189.48; p < 0.0001), confirming the predictive capacity of digital data. Conclusion: Beyond this particular case, these findings illustrate the usefulness of applying time series statistical techniques to open digital sources, reinforcing their value as a complement to traditional epidemiological surveillance systems","time series analysis; information-seeking behavior; COVID-19; infodemiology; public health surveillance. -----------Keywords: time series analysis, information-seeking behavior, COVID-19, infodemiology, public health surveillance. Utilização do Google Trends™ na Vigilância Sindrômica: Um Estudo de Séries Temporais da SARS-CoV-2 na Colômbia",marcadores,cas de seri temporal fuent digital abierta reforzando su valor,objective purpose study evaluate conceptual procedural perspective potential predict time course relative search volume rsv term covid google trend tm context sars-cov-2 colombia will achiev through application time seri statistical techniqu aimed analyz its correlation predictive capacity short-term lags confirm case report epidemiological surveillance study also explor its usefulnes complement syndromic surveillance system early detection epidemiological pattern potential applic other emerg priority public health event beyond sars-cov-2 method longitudinal ecological study conduct colombia between 2020 2022 based daily aggregat rsv data confirm case report national institute health analysi structur step replicable public health standard using z-scor seasonal trend decomposition using stl seasonal trend decomposition using loes cross-correlation analysi granger test purpose examin pattern lags predictive relationship temporal precedence result case seri show fluctu consistent rsv seri maximum cross-correlation 70 identifi lag -27 days indicat increase search preced increase case granger test show significance lags days 189 48 0001 confirm predictive capacity digital data conclusion beyond particular case these finding illustrate usefulnes apply time seri statistical techniqu open digital sourc reinforc their value complement traditional epidemiological surveillance system,time seri analysi information-seek behavior covid-19 infodemiology public health surveillance -keyword time seri analysi information-seek behavior covid-19 infodemiology public health surveillance utilizacao do google trend tm na vigilancia sindromica um estudo de seri temporai da sars-cov-2 na colombia,cas de seri temporal fuent digital abierta reforzando su valor objective purpose study evaluate conceptual procedural perspective potential predict time course relative search volume rsv term covid google trend tm context sars-cov-2 colombia will achiev through application time seri statistical techniqu aimed analyz its correlation predictive capacity short-term lags confirm case report epidemiological surveillance study also explor its usefulnes complement syndromic surveillance system early detection epidemiological pattern potential applic other emerg priority public health event beyond sars-cov-2 method longitudinal ecological study conduct colombia between 2020 2022 based daily aggregat rsv data confirm case report national institute health analysi structur step replicable public health standard using z-scor seasonal trend decomposition using stl seasonal trend decomposition using loes cross-correlation analysi granger test purpose examin pattern lags predictive relationship temporal precedence result case seri show fluctu consistent rsv seri maximum cross-correlation 70 identifi lag -27 days indicat increase search preced increase case granger test show significance lags days 189 48 0001 confirm predictive capacity digital data conclusion beyond particular case these finding illustrate usefulnes apply time seri statistical techniqu open digital sourc reinforc their value complement traditional epidemiological surveillance system time seri analysi information-seek behavior covid-19 infodemiology public health surveillance -keyword time seri analysi information-seek behavior covid-19 infodemiology public health surveillance utilizacao do google trend tm na vigilancia sindromica um estudo de seri temporai da sars-cov-2 na colombia,1.0.0,458e871a629d0ff3
2256-3334,361516+final.pdf,361516+final_0,es,Estrategias sociosanitarias implementadas por las,"Objetivo: Comprender las estrategias sociosanitarias implementadas por la población campesina para afrontar el COVID-19. Métodos: Estudio cualitativo con enfoque etnográfico, realizado entre 2020 y 2023 en ocho regiones rurales del país. Se emplearon entrevistas etnográficas, observación participante, diario de campo y revisión documental. La información se organizó y analizó a partir de categorías preestablecidas. Resultados: Las familias campesinas consideraron inicialmente al COVID-19 como una enfermedad respiratoria leve. Una vez comenzó a morir gente por esta causa, dinamizaron una estrategia sociosanitaria centrada en saberes, para prevenirla y tratarla con los recursos disponibles en cada territorio. Otra estrategia se materializó en el escenario comunitario, en donde el relato oficial sobre esta enfermedad fue objeto de desconfianza. En respuesta a esta crisis, se fortalecieron experiencias organizativas en temas como el control territorial, la restricción de la movilidad, el cuidado colectivo y la soberanía alimentaria. En algunas regiones se incrementó la violencia por parte de grupos armados. Conclusiones: Una estrategia sociosanitaria se dinamizó en las familias, al posicionar sus saberes sobre enfermedades respiratorias para entender, prevenir y atender el COVID-19 con los recursos terapéuticos del entorno. Otra estrategia se impulsó en las comunidades, al promover procesos de control social, el cuidado colectivo, la crítica a la política sanitaria y la exigibilidad del derecho a la salud","COVID-19, población rural, salud rural, servicios de salud rurales. Volumen 44, 2026 DOI: https://doi.org/10.17533/udea.rfnsp. e361516 Recibido: 15/07/2025 Aprobado: 18/03/2026 Publicado: Cita: Ospina-Lozano E, Cruz-Romero S, GutiérrezGarcía K. Estrategias sociosanitarias implementadas por las comunidades campesinas de Colombia frente al COVID-19. Rev. Fac. Nac. Salud Pública. 2026;44:e36115",marcadores,estrategi sociosanitari implementad,objetivo comprender estrategi sociosanitari implementad poblacion campesina afrontar covid-19 metod estudio cualitativo enfoque etnografico realizado entre 2020 2023 ocho region rural pais emplearon entrevist etnografic observacion participante diario campo revision documental informacion organizo analizo partir categori preestablecid resultad famili campesin consideraron inicial covid-19 como enfermedad respiratoria leve vez comenzo morir gente esta causa dinamizaron estrategia sociosanitaria centrada saber prevenirla tratarla recurs disponibl cada territorio otra estrategia materializo escenario comunitario donde relato oficial sobre esta enfermedad fue objeto desconfianza respuesta esta crisis fortalecieron experienci organizativ temas como control territorial restriccion movilidad cuidado colectivo soberania alimentaria algun region incremento violencia parte grup armad conclusion estrategia sociosanitaria dinamizo famili posicionar sus saber sobre enfermedad respiratori entender prevenir atender covid-19 recurs terapeutic entorno otra estrategia impulso comunidad promover proces control social cuidado colectivo critica politica sanitaria exigibilidad derecho salud,covid-19 poblacion rural salud rural servici salud rural volumen 44 2026 doi https doi org 10 17533 udea rfnsp e361516 recibido 15 07 2025 aprobado 18 03 2026 publicado cita ospina-lozano cruz-romero gutierrezgarcia estrategi sociosanitari implementad comunidad campesin colombia frente covid-19 rev fac nac salud publica 2026 44 e36115,estrategi sociosanitari implementad objetivo comprender estrategi sociosanitari implementad poblacion campesina afrontar covid-19 metod estudio cualitativo enfoque etnografico realizado entre 2020 2023 ocho region rural pais emplearon entrevist etnografic observacion participante diario campo revision documental informacion organizo analizo partir categori preestablecid resultad famili campesin consideraron inicial covid-19 como enfermedad respiratoria leve vez comenzo morir gente esta causa dinamizaron estrategia sociosanitaria centrada saber prevenirla tratarla recurs disponibl cada territorio otra estrategia materializo escenario comunitario donde relato oficial sobre esta enfermedad fue objeto desconfianza respuesta esta crisis fortalecieron experienci organizativ temas como control territorial restriccion movilidad cuidado colectivo soberania alimentaria algun region incremento violencia parte grup armad conclusion estrategia sociosanitaria dinamizo famili posicionar sus saber sobre enfermedad respiratori entender prevenir atender covid-19 recurs terapeutic entorno otra estrategia impulso comunidad promover proces control social cuidado colectivo critica politica sanitaria exigibilidad derecho salud covid-19 poblacion rural salud rural servici salud rural volumen 44 2026 doi https doi org 10 17533 udea rfnsp e361516 recibido 15 07 2025 aprobado 18 03 2026 publicado cita ospina-lozano cruz-romero gutierrezgarcia estrategi sociosanitari implementad comunidad campesin colombia frente covid-19 rev fac nac salud publica 2026 44 e36115,1.0.0,0103c6e422026b3f
2256-3334,361516+final.pdf,361516+final_0,en,", Cruz-Romero S, GutiérrezGarcía K. Estrategias sociosanitarias","Objective: To understand the socio-health strategies implemented by the peasant population to cope with COVID-19. Methods: A qualitative study with an ethnographic approach was conducted between 2020 and 2023 in eight rural regions of the country. Ethnographic interviews, participant observation, field diaries, and documentary review were employed. The information was organized and analyzed based on predefined analytical categories. Results: Peasant families initially perceived COVID-19 as a mild respiratory illness. As deaths attributable to the disease began to occur, they activated a socio-health strategy grounded in local knowledge, aimed at prevention and treatment using the resources available in each territory. Another strategy emerged at the community level, where the official narrative regarding the disease was met with distrust. In response to the crisis, organizational experiences were strengthened around issues such as territorial control, mobility restrictions, collective care, and food sovereignty. In some regions, violence perpetrated by armed groups increased. Conclusions: One socio-health strategy was activated within families by positioning their knowledge of respiratory diseases to understand, prevent, and manage COVID-19 using locally available therapeutic resources. Another strategy was promoted at the community level through the encouragement of social control processes, collective care, critical engagement with health policies, and the demand for the right to health","COVID-19, rural population, rural health, rural health services Estratégias sociosanitárias implementadas pelas comunidades rurais da Colômbia diante da COVID-19",marcadores,cruz-romero gutierrezgarcia estrategia sociosanitaria,objective understand socio-health strategi implement peasant population cope covid-19 method qualitative study ethnographic approach conduct bet