2256-3334,362334+final.pdf,362334+final_0,en,Esta obra se distribuye bajo una Licencia Creative,"Objective: To understand how the social support networks of families with children with autism spectrum disorder were configured during the COVID-19 pandemic. Methods: Qualitative research of the multiple case study type. The sample consisted of 42 family members of children with autism spectrum disorder residing in the states of Rio Grande do Sul, Paraná, São Paulo, Ceará, Amapá, and Maranhão. Data collection was carried out between 2020 and 2022 through semi-structured interviews. Deductive-inductive analytical strategies and the analytical technique of ""cross-case synthesis"" were used in the analysis. Results: The following themes emerged: composition of the social support network during COVID-19, the role of the social support network during COVID-19, and pandemic-related aspects of the social support network. The cross-analysis of cases indicates greater family support as a consequence of the increased proximity among family members during the pandemic, as well as less support from health and education services. Family members with a spouse reported a higher level of support. Compared to families in the state of Paraná, those in the state of Ceará presented greater fragility in their support network, which was restricted to the family environment, with a lack of services and the death of network members. Conclusions: The social support networks of families with children with autism spectrum disorder during the COVID-19 pandemic were predominantly comprised of family support, highlighting the fragility of formal support networks. Understanding this configuration can contribute to the development of care strategies and the strengthening of support networks for this population","family support, COVID-19, social support networks, children's health, autism spectrum disorder. Apoio Social para Famílias de Crianças com Transtorno do Espectro Autista Durante a COVID-19",marcadores,esta obra se distribuye bajo una licencia creative,objective understand how social support network famili children autism spectrum disorder configur during covid-19 pandemic method qualitative research multiple case study type sample consist 42 family member children autism spectrum disorder resid stat rio grande do sul parana sao paulo ceara amapa maranhao data collection carri out between 2020 2022 through semi-structur interview deductive-inductive analytical strategi analytical technique cross-case synthesi used analysi result follow them emerg composition social support network during covid-19 role social support network during covid-19 pandemic-relat aspect social support network cross-analysi case indicat greater family support consequence increas proximity among family member during pandemic well less support health education servic family member spouse report higher level support compar famili state parana those state ceara present greater fragility their support network which restrict family environment lack servic death network member conclusion social support network famili children autism spectrum disorder during covid-19 pandemic predominantly compris family support highlight fragility formal support network understand configuration can contribute development care strategi strengthen support network population,family support covid-19 social support network children health autism spectrum disorder apoio social para familia de crianca com transtorno do espectro autista durante covid-19,esta obra se distribuye bajo una licencia creative objective understand how social support network famili children autism spectrum disorder configur during covid-19 pandemic method qualitative research multiple case study type sample consist 42 family member children autism spectrum disorder resid stat rio grande do sul parana sao paulo ceara amapa maranhao data collection carri out between 2020 2022 through semi-structur interview deductive-inductive analytical 