2256-3334,362658+final.pdf,362658+final_0,en,"Valle-Cabrera E, Ome-Osorio I, ChacónMendoza C, Córdoba-Asprilla M. Perfiles en las","Objective: To identify and describe latent profiles of sociodemographic and clinical adversity in children who died from leukemia in Colombia, using latent class analysis. Methods: A retrospective cross-sectional study was conducted using leukemia mortality data from 3,738 children under 14 years of age who died in Colombia (between 2008 and 2023), obtained from the Vital Statistics of the National Administrative Department of Statistics (DANE). Latent class analysis, an unsupervised classification clustering method, was used, incorporating sociodemographic variables, socioeconomic status, and type of leukemia as the underlying cause of death. Model selection was based on the Akaike information criterion, the Bayesian information criterion, log-likelihood, posterior probabilities of latent class membership, and entropy. Sensitivity analysis was performed using k-means clustering in Python. Results: Among the 3,738 children who died from leukemia, the majority were aged 10–14 years (38.5%), lived in urban areas (77.8%), and had only a primary education (34.2%). The four latent profiles model provided the best statistical fit. The four profiles identified were: Class 1, urban female vulnerability profile with lymphatic leukemia (31%); Class 2, intermediate adversity profile with urban myeloid leukemia (37%); Class 3, urban male profile with a higher socioeconomic status with lymphatic leukemia (16%); and Class 4, extreme adversity profile of male with lymphatic leukemia in rural areas (16%). Classes 1, 3, and 4 represent a concentration of acute lymphoblastic leukemia, while Class 2 includes myeloid and mixed leukemias. Class 4 experiences the most adverse circumstances, while Class 3 is the most privileged. Conclusions: The four identified latent class profiles reveal marked heterogeneity in childhood leukemia deaths, reflecting distinct combinations of leukemia type, socioeconomic conditions, territorial context, and gender. The findings demonstrate that even within the same leukemia type, differentiated patterns of social and territorial disadvantage coexist. A predominance of adolescents in urban environments is observed, while acute lymphoblastic leukemia emerges as the leading cause of death in all profiles, regardless of social context. Gender is a determining factor in the distribution of vulnerability. This evidence can inform public health surveillance","latent class analysis, unsupervised machine learning, health inequity, leukemia, mortality. Aprendizado de Máquina não Supervisionado, Análise de Classes Latentes, Leucemia, Desigualdades de Saúde, Mortalidade da Criança",marcadores,valle-cabrera ome-osorio chaconmendoza cordoba-asprilla perfil en las,objective identify describe latent profil sociodemographic clinical adversity children who died leukemia colombia using latent clas analysi method retrospective cross-sectional study conduct using leukemia mortality data 738 children under 14 year age who died colombia between 2008 2023 obtain vital statistic national administrative department statistic dane latent clas analysi unsupervis classification cluster method used incorporat sociodemographic variabl socioeconomic statu type leukemia underly cause death model selection based akaike information criterion bayesian information criterion log-likelihood posterior probabiliti latent clas membership entropy sensitivity analysi perform using k-mean cluster python result among 738 children who died leukemia majority aged 10-14 year 38 lived urban area 77 had only primary education 34 four latent profil model provid best statistical fit four profil identifi clas urban female vulnerability profile lymphatic leukemia 31 clas intermediate adversity profile urban myeloid leukemia 37 clas urban male profile higher socioeconomic statu lymphatic leukemia 16 clas extreme adversity profile male lymphatic leukemia rural area 16 class represent concentration acute lymphoblastic leukemia while clas includ myeloid mixed leukemia clas experienc most adverse circumstanc while clas most privileg conclusion four identifi latent clas profil reveal mark heterogeneity childhood leukemia death reflect distinct combin leukemia type socioeconomic condition territorial context gender finding demonstrate even within same leukemia type differentiat pattern social territorial disadvantage coexist predominance adolescent urban environment observ while acute lymphoblastic leukemia emerg lead cause death all profil regardles social context gender determin factor distribution vulnerability evidence can inform public health surveillance,latent clas analysi unsupervis machine learn health inequity leukemia mortality aprendizado de maquina nao supervisionado analise de class latent leucemia desigualdad de saude mortalidade da crianca,valle-cabrera ome-osorio chaconmendoza cordoba-asprilla perfil en las objective identify describe latent profil sociodemographic clinical adversity children who died leukemia colombia using latent clas analysi method retrospective cross-sectional study conduct using leukemia mortality data 738 children under 14 year age who died colombia between 2008 2023 obtain vital statistic national administrative department statistic dane latent clas analysi unsupervis classification cluster method used incorporat sociodemographic variabl socioeconomic statu type leukemia underly cause death model selection based akaike information criterion bayesian information criterion log-likelihood posterior probabiliti latent clas membership entropy sensitivity analysi perform using k-mean cluster python result among 738 children who died leukemia majority aged 10-14 year 38 lived urban area 77 had only primary education 34 four latent profil model provid best statistical fit four profil identifi clas urban female vulnerability profile lymphatic leukemia 31 clas intermediate adversity profile urban myeloid leukemia 37 clas urban male profile higher socioeconomic statu lymphatic leukemia 16 clas extreme adversity profile male lymphatic leukemia rural area 16 class represent concentration acute lymphoblastic leukemia while clas includ myeloid mixed leukemia clas experienc most adverse circumstanc while clas most privileg conclusion four identifi latent clas profil reveal mark heterogeneity childhood leukemia death reflect distinct combin leukemia type socioeconomic condition territorial context gender finding demonstrate even within same leukemia type differentiat pattern social territorial disadvantage coexist predominance adolescent urban environment observ while acute lymphoblastic leukemia emerg lead cause death all profil regardles social context gender determin factor distribution vulnerability evidence can inform public health surveillance latent clas analysi unsupervis machine learn health inequity leukemia mortality aprendizado de maquina nao supervisionado analise de class latent leucemia desigualdad de saude mortalidade da crianca,1.0.0,069a3085ed04986a
2256-3334,363361_final.pdf,363361_final_0,es,Agroecología: estrategia para la promoción de la,"En Colombia, la agricultura convencional basada en el uso intensivo de agrotóxicos constituye un problema prioritario de salud pública, con impactos desproporcionados en comunidades campesinas e indígenas por exposición ocupacional, doméstica y ambiental. A nivel mundial, se estiman entre 2 y 5 millones de intoxicaciones agudas por plaguicidas al año, y la exposición crónica se asocia con cáncer y alteraciones neurológicas y reproductivas. En 2022, Colombia registró una incidencia de 12,7 casos por cada 100 000 habitantes, con morbilidad rural tres veces mayor que la urbana, además de un peso relevante de intoxicaciones con intencionalidad suicida y mortalidad atribuida a herbicidas altamente peligrosos. La exposición se agrava por prácticas inseguras, almacenamiento intradomiciliario, baja protección personal y por fumigación aérea con glifosato en territorios indígenas, con reportes de afectaciones dermatológicas, respiratorias y reproductivas. Este ensayo plantea que la agroecología, como ciencia, práctica y movimiento social, es una estrategia que permite promover la salud, al fortalecer la soberanía alimentaria y nutricional, la cohesión social y la gobernanza territorial, la resiliencia ecosistémica y la reducción de la exposición a plaguicidas, además de aportar a la prevención de violencias autoinfligidas, al disminuir el acceso a sustancias letales. Se concluye que impulsar transiciones agroecológicas con apoyo institucional y regulación de plaguicidas altamente peligrosos es una estrategia intersectorial pertinente para reducir inequidades y mejorar el bienestar en territorios rurales","agroecología, plaguicidas, promoción de la salud, salud de la población indígena, salud pública. Volumen 44, 2026 DOI: https://doi.org/10.17533/udea.rfnsp. e363361 Recibido: 23/12/2025 Aprobado: 08/05/2026 Publicado: 23/06/2026 Cita: Dussan-Chaux JD. Agroecología: estrategia para la promoción de la salud en comunidades campesinas e indígenas de Colombia. Rev. Fac. Nac. Salud Pública. 2026;44",marcadores,agroecologia estrategia promocion,colombia agricultura convencional basada uso intensivo agrotoxic constituye problema prioritario salud publica impact desproporcionad comunidad campesin indigen exposicion ocupacional domestica ambiental nivel mundial estiman entre millon intoxic agud plaguicid ano exposicion cronica asocia cancer alter neurologic reproductiv 2022 colombia registro incidencia 12 casos cada 100 000 habitant morbilidad rural tres veces mayor urbana adem peso relevante intoxic intencionalidad suicida mortalidad atribuida herbicid alta peligros exposicion agrava practic insegur almacenamiento intradomiciliario baja proteccion personal fumigacion aerea glifosato territori indigen report afect dermatologic respiratori reproductiv este ensayo plantea agroecologia como ciencia practica movimiento social estrategia permite promover salud fortalecer soberania alimentaria nutricional cohesion social gobernanza territorial resiliencia ecosistemica reduccion exposicion plaguicid adem aportar prevencion violenci autoinfligid disminuir acceso sustanci letal concluye impulsar transicion agroecologic apoyo institucional regulacion plaguicid alta peligros estrategia intersectorial pertinente reducir inequidad mejorar bienestar territori rural,agroecologia plaguicid promocion salud salud poblacion indigena salud publica volumen 44 2026 doi https doi org 10 17533 udea rfnsp e363361 recibido 23 12 2025 aprobado 08 05 2026 publicado 23 06 2026 cita dussan-chaux jd agroecologia estrategia promocion salud comunidad campesin indigen colombia rev fac nac salud publica 2026 44,agroecologia estrategia promocion colombia agricultura convencional basada uso intensivo agrotoxic constituye problema prioritario salud publica impact desproporcionad comunidad campesin indigen exposicion ocupacional domestica ambiental nivel mundial estiman entre millon intoxic