legitimacy speak about them study propos comprehensive model capability configuration which agency understood situat capacity train conversion infrastructure epistemic justice principle governance framework make possible identify how train strategy generat process individual collective territorial transformation agency capabiliti collective political capabiliti epistemic justice women entrepreneurship action research colombia,1.0.0,bf73c285251783de
2256-4322,658-245-PB.pdf,658-245-PB_2,en,"Patricio Saavedra Espinosa, Centro de Gestión y Economía Aplicada, Departamento de Ciencias Económicas y Administrativas, Facultad de Ciencias Jurídicas, Económicas y","Financial education is a core component of business school curricula. Despite its importance, persistent instructional barriers limit effective learning, particularly because formal financial models are mathematically intensive and conceptually complex, as well as the limited resources available to business schools in emerging markets. In this context, this article examines how MeanVarLab, an open-source financial software tool, can improve students’ learning experience when working with advanced financial models in undergraduate business programs in emerging markets. Using a mixed-method ex ante and ex post design in a business school in Chile, we assessed a pedagogical intervention involving 11 advanced undergraduate students who interacted directly with the tool. MeanVarLab enables students to engage with complex mathematical models through interactive visualization, facilitating a more intuitive understanding of key financial concepts. Quantitative evidence suggests that nearly all participants would recommend the package to their peers. Qualitative findings indicate that participants perceived the tool’s primary contribution as its ability to streamline and accelerate complex financial analyses. Participants also emphasized that the tool reduces technical barriers, making advanced financial models more accessible to users with limited programming experience. Building on these findings, the article outlines theoretical implications for technology-enhanced finance education and JEL: I23, G11, A22 Recibido: 14/04/2026 Revisado: 10/07/2026 Aceptado: 15/07/2026 51-60 AD-Minister 52 Innovación pedagógica","Active Learning, Data-Driven Learning Environments, Experiential Learning Tools, Financial Education, Business Education",marcadores,patricio saavedra espinosa centro de gestion economia aplicada departamento de ciencia economica administrativa facultad de ciencia juridica economica,financial education core component busines school curricula despite its importance persistent instructional barrier limit effective learn particularly because formal financial model mathematically intensive conceptually complex well limit resourc available busines school emerg market context article examin how meanvarlab open-source financial software tool can improve student learn experience when work advanc financial model undergraduate busines program emerg market using mixed-method ex ante ex post design busines school chile we assess pedagogical intervention involv 11 advanc undergraduate student who interact directly tool meanvarlab enabl student engage complex mathematical model through interactive visual facilitat more intuitive understand key financial concept quantitative evidence suggest nearly all participant would recommend package their peer qualitative finding indicate participant perceiv tool primary contribution its ability streamline accelerate complex financial analys participant also emphasiz tool reduc technical barrier making advanc financial model more accessible user limit programm experience build these finding article outlin theoretical implic technology-enhanc finance education jel i23 g11 a22 recibido 14 04 2026 revisado 10 07 2026 aceptado 15 07 2026 51-60 ad-minister 52 innovacion pedagogica,active learn data-driven learn environment experiential learn tool financial education busines education,patricio saavedra espinosa centro de gestion economia aplicada departamento de ciencia economica administrativa facultad de ciencia juridica economica financial education core component busines school curricula despite its importance persistent instructional barrier limit effective learn particularly because formal financial model mathematically intensive conceptually complex well limit resourc available busines school e