2256-5248,Rhela-28-48-m-115-135.pdf,Rhela-28-48-m-115-135_0,en,"iencias de la Educación,","Objective: This analysis focuses on Mercy Páez Escobar’s pioneering work and advocacy for the recognition and inclusion of people with low vision in Colombia. It highlights her leadership in creating a more accessible, equitable and human rights-based educational and social environment. Originality/Contribution: From a gender perspective, this study highlights the pedagogical and social impact of Mercy, who was the first Colombian woman to be trained in the country as an orientation and mobility instructor for people with sight loss. Method: The study used the biographical method, interviews, documentary review and direct contact to evidence her leadership in inclusive policies and social justice. Key moments in her career, training and contributions were identified. Strategies/Data Collection: Interviews and dialogues provided direct testimonies that demonstrated her influence and leadership in the field of orientation and mobility for blind individuals. This allowed us to understand the dynamics of her work, her pedagogical vision, and her contributions to the development of inclusive policies. Documentary review—archives, publications, reports from organizations on accessibility, and materials created by Mercy—contextualized her work and contributions to inclusive education. Conclusions: Her work, grounded in personal and community development and framed by a human rights approach, fostered the formation of fairer societies that respect diversity. She is also recognized for her contribution to the creation of accessible didactic materials, which has positioned her legacy as key to fostering respect for otherness, participation, and the removal of barriers",learning; blind individuals; low vision; diversity; orientation and mobility instructor; life story; biographical,marcadores,iencia de la educacion,objective analysi focus mercy paez escobar pioneer work advocacy recognition inclusion people low vision colombia highlight her leadership creat more accessible equitable human rights-bas educational social environment originality contribution gender perspective study highlight pedagogical social impact mercy who first colombian woman train country orientation mobility instructor people sight loss method study used biographical method interview documentary review direct contact evidence her leadership inclusive polici social justice key moment her career train contribution identifi strategi data collection interview dialogu provid direct testimoni demonstrat her influence leadership field orientation mobility blind individual allow us understand dynamic her work her pedagogical vision her contribution development inclusive polici documentary review--archiv public report organiz accessibility material creat mercy--contextualiz her work contribution inclusive education conclusion her work ground personal community development fram human right approach foster formation fairer societi respect diversity she also recogniz her contribution creation accessible didactic material which has position her legacy key foster respect othernes participation removal barrier,learn blind individual low vision diversity orientation mobility instructor life story biographical,iencia de la educacion objective analysi focus mercy paez escobar pioneer work advocacy recognition inclusion people low vision colombia highlight her leadership creat more accessible equitable human rights-bas educational social environment originality contribution gender perspective study highlight pedagogical social impact mercy who first colombian woman train country orientation mobility instructor people sight loss method study used biographical method interview documentary review direct contact evidence her leadership inclusive polici social justice key moment her career train contribution identifi strategi data collection interview dialogu provid direct testimoni demonstrat her influence leadership field orientation mobility blind individual allow us understand dynamic her work her pedagogical vision her contribution development inclusive polici documentary review--archiv public report organiz accessibility material creat mercy--contextualiz her work contribution inclusive education conclusion her work ground personal community development fram human right approach foster formation fairer societi respect diversity she also recogniz her contribution creation accessible didactic material which has position her legacy key foster respect othernes participation removal barrier learn blind individual low vision diversity orientation mobility instructor life story biographical,1.0.0,74046226fee420a8
2256-5248,Rhela-28-48-m-115-135.pdf,Rhela-28-48-m-115-135_0,es,s to understand,"Objetivo: analizar la labor de Mercy Páez Escobar como pionera y defensora del reconocimiento y la inclusión de las personas con baja visión en Colombia, y destacar su liderazgo en la creación de un entorno educativo y social más accesible, equitativo y basado en los derechos humanos. 117 Rev. hist.edu.latinoam - Vol. 28 No. 48, enero - junio 2026 - ISSN: 0122-7238 - pp. 115 - 135 Mercy: The Beautiful Eyes of the Soul. A Life Story Originalidad/Contribución: desde una perspectiva de género, este estudio destaca el impacto pedagógico y social de Mercy, la primera mujer colombiana formada en el país como instructora de orientación y movilidad para personas ciegas. Método: se utilizaron el método biográfico, las entrevistas, la revisión documental y el contacto directo, para evidenciar su liderazgo en políticas inclusivas y justicia social. Se rastrearon momentos clave de su carrera, formación y contribuciones. Estrategias/Recolección de datos: las entrevistas y los diálogos proporcionaron testimonios directos que demostraron su influencia y liderazgo en el campo de la orientación y la movilidad para personas ciegas. Esto permitió comprender la dinámica de su trabajo, su visión pedagógica y sus contribuciones al desarrollo de políticas inclusivas. La revisión documental —archivos, publicaciones, informes de organizaciones sobre accesibilidad y materiales creados por Mercy— contextualizó su trabajo y sus contribuciones a la educación inclusiva. Conclusiones: su trabajo, basado en el desarrollo personal y comunitario, y enmarcado en un enfoque de derechos humanos, fomentó la formación de sociedades más justas que respetan la diversidad. También se reconoce su contribución a la creación de materiales didácticos accesibles, lo que posiciona su legado como clave para fomentar el respeto por la alteridad, la participación y la eliminación de barreras",aprendizaje; personas ciegas; baja vision; diversidad; instructora de orientación y movilidad; historia de vida; método biográfico. Mercy: os belos olhos da alma. Uma história de vida,marcadores,to understand,objetivo analizar labor mercy paez escobar como pionera defensora reconocimiento inclusion person baja vision colombia destacar liderazgo creacion entorno educativo social mas accesible equitativo basado derech human 117 rev hist edu latinoam vol 28 no 48 enero junio 2026 issn 0122-7238 pp 115 135 mercy the beautiful eyes of the soul life story originalidad contribucion desde perspectiva genero este estudio destaca impacto pedagogico social mercy primera mujer colombiana formada pais como instructora orientacion movilidad person cieg metodo utilizaron metodo biografico entrevist revision documental contacto directo evidenciar liderazgo politic inclusiv justicia social rastrearon moment clave carrera formacion contribucion estrategi recoleccion datos entrevist dialog proporcionaron testimoni direct demostraron influencia liderazgo campo orientacion movilidad person cieg esto permitio comprender dinamica trabajo vision pedagogica sus contribucion desarrollo politic inclusiv revision documental --archiv public inform organiz sobre accesibilidad material cread mercy-- contextualizo trabajo sus contribucion educacion inclusiva conclusion trabajo basado desarrollo personal comunitario enmarcado enfoque derech human fomento formacion sociedad mas just respetan diversidad tambien reconoce contribucion creacion material didactic accesibl posiciona legado como clave fomentar respeto alteridad participacion eliminacion barrer,aprendizaje person cieg baja vision diversidad instructora orientacion movilidad historia vida metodo biografico mercy os belos olhos da alma uma historia vida,to understand objetivo analizar labor mercy paez escobar como pionera defensora reconocimiento inclusion person baja vision colombia destacar liderazgo creacion entorno educativo social mas accesible equitativo basado derech human 117 re