2256-5248,Rhela-28-48-m-137-164.pdf,Rhela-28-48-m-137-164_0,en,tora del Niño (SPN) y la,"Objective: to historically describe the technical and administrative structure and approach of nanny training in Guatemala during the 20th and 21st centuries, identifying its trajectory, evolution, and current challenges. Originality/Contribution: from an exploratory perspective, the development of this topic has fostered the systematization, description and analysis of historical events related to the training of nannies in Guatemala during the 20th and 21st centuries. Access to information, data and references on events linked to the evolution of nanny schools over different historical periods has become a valuable resource. It provides a description of significant elements and moments in the history of this profession, as well as the background to its current training and the challenges it faces. This information could motivate key stakeholders and decision-makers to improve training processes and pursue competency certification, which would benefit early childhood care. Method: the methods employed — oral history and a descriptive approach — enabled the systematic organization and dissemination of information on the historical development of training for Guatemalan nannies since 1927. This was achieved by basing narratives on the experiences of 20th-century nanny trainees and drawing on the limited historical records held by Guatemalan nanny training schools. Therefore, the study’s scope was exploratory and its design descriptive. Data Collection Strategies: information and data were gathered through focused, semi-structured interviews centered on the study situation. In addition, a document review was conducted; this was limited, but information was obtained through requests to institutions that train nannies in Guatemala. Conclusions: the training of nanny students, as part of its historical trajectory and evolution, has undergone significant changes in terms of the focus and roles assumed by those who graduate from nanny schools. The approach based on an empirical and experiential model that characterized nanny training almost a century ago has evolved into an academic and formal one that no longer envisions the nanny’s role as merely providing assistance, but rather as an educational one, incorporating formative elements related to child development and early childhood education. Furthermore, the Child Protection Society (SPN, by its Spanish acronym) and the Secretariat of Social Welfare of the Presidency of the Republic (SBS by its Spanish acronym)—the only two institutions that train nanny students in Guatemala—could consider monitoring the employment and educational outcomes of their graduates and consider offering, as a complement to the diploma they award, the opportunity to obtain accreditation and certification for early childhood care from the Guatemalan Ministry of Education","nannies; early childhood; nanny schools; training; history of education; early education; evolution. 140 Rev. hist.edu.latinoam - Vol. 28 No. 48, enero - junio 2026 - ISSN: 0122-7238 - pp. 137 - 163 Ana María Hernández Ayala Formação de babás na Guatemala: trajetória histórica, desafios e evolução (séculos XX e XXI)",marcadores,tora del nino spn la,objective historically describe technical administrative structure approach nanny train guatemala during 20th 21st centuri identify its trajectory evolution current challeng originality contribution exploratory perspective development topic has foster systemat description analysi historical event relat train nanni guatemala during 20th 21st centuri acces information data referenc event link evolution nanny school over different historical period has become valuable resource provid description significant element moment history profession well background its current train challeng face information could motivate key stakeholder decision-maker improve train process pursue competency certification which would benefit early childhood care method method employ -- oral history descriptive approach -- enabl systematic organ dissemination information historical development train guatemalan nanni since 1927 achiev basing narrativ experienc 20th-century nanny traine draw limit historical record held guatemalan nanny train school therefore study scope exploratory its design descriptive data collection strategi information data gather through focus semi-structur interview center study situation addition document review conduct limit but information obtain through request institution train nanni guatemala conclusion train nanny student part its historical trajectory evolution has undergone significant chang term focu role assum those who graduate nanny school approach based empirical experiential model characteriz nanny train almost century ago has evolv into academic formal one no longer envision nanny role merely provid assistance but rather educational one incorporat formative element relat child development early childhood education furthermore child protection society spn its spanish acronym secretariat social welfare presidency republic sbs its spanish acronym --the only two institution train nanny student guatemala--could consider monitor employment educational outcom their graduat consider offer complement diploma they award opportunity obtain accreditation certification early childhood care guatemalan ministry education,nanni early childhood nanny school train history education early education evolution 140 rev hist edu latinoam vol 28 no 48 enero junio 2026 issn 0122-7238 pp 137 163 ana maria hernandez ayala formacao de baba na guatemala trajetoria historica desafio evolucao seculo xx xxi,tora del nino spn la objective historically describe technical administrative structure approach nanny train guatemala during 20th 21st centuri identify its trajectory evolution current challeng originality contribution exploratory perspective development topic has foster systemat desc