ual politico metodo retoma historia mentalidad escuela annalista francesa bloch febvre recuperar andami cotidianidad le goff integr analisis critico fuent academic normativ comunitari articula larga duracion historia tiempo presente incorporan categori como ontologia sumapazlogia cartografia social esta ultima como herramienta reconstruir narrativ territorial fortalecer vinculo entre escuela comunidad conservacion estrategi recoleccion informacion estrategia metodologica integra historia educacion saber territorial ancestral analiz practic educativ rural mediante historia dialogica narrativ experienci escolar incluyen ejempl construccion subjetividad maldonado-torr maestr rural sustentad investig regional document archivo sumapaz conclusion defensa paramo exige articular historia mentalidad imaginari educativ enraizad territorio cuidado agua justicia ambiental escuela rural debe trascender line estatal recuperar convivencia ancestral naturaleza sintetizada buen vivir como principio autoaprendizaje esta perspectiva configura modelo educativo transformador sembrar conciencia ecologica tambien sembrar futuro historia escuela rural paramo sumapaz bioaprendizaje historia educacion revista historia educacion latinoamericana history of rural education and the defense of the sumapaz paramo pedagogi for conservation,1.0.0,d9dc631b475e622d
2256-5248,Rhela-28-48-m-185-205.pdf,Rhela-28-48-m-185-205_0,en,n de subjetividades,"Objective: this article analyzes the role of the history of rural education in the Sumapaz páramo as a key factor in defending the territory and the transition toward a biocentric pedagogy. It proposes a comprehensive understanding of the páramo as a subject of rights and as a living classroom for bio-learning, based on the intertwining of community knowledge, eco-social justice, and transformative educational proposals. 187 Rev. hist.edu.latinoam - Vol. 28 No. 48, enero - junio 2026 - ISSN: 0122-7238 - pp. 185 - 205 Historia de la educación rural y defensa del páramo de Sumapaz: pedagogías para la conservación Originality/Contribution: the study articulates historical approaches to education to ground the ontology of SumaPazlogy (Mora), amphibious ontology, and the epistemologies of the South, integrating contributions from authors such as Freire, Escobar, Boff, Gudynas, and Shiva. This perspective reframes the rural school as a space of resistance, historical memory, antifragility, and ecological action, where water becomes a pedagogical, spiritual, and political principle. Method: this approach draws on the history of mentalities from the French Annales School (Bloch and Febvre) to reconstruct the frameworks of everyday life (Le Goff), integrating a critical analysis of academic, normative, and community sources. The long duration is linked with the history of the present, and categories such as SumaPazlogy ontology and social cartography are incorporated. The latter serves as a tool to reconstruct territorial narratives and strengthen the bond between school, community, and conservation. Strategies/Data Collection: the methodological strategy integrates the history of education with ancestral territorial knowledge, analyzing rural educational practices through dialogic history and narratives of school experiences. It includes examples of the construction of subjectivities (Maldonado-Torres) among rural teachers, supported by regional research and archival documents from Sumapaz. Conclusions: defending the páramo requires linking the history of mentalities with educational imaginaries rooted in the territory, water stewardship, and environmental justice. Rural schools must transcend state guidelines to recover ancestral coexistence with nature, synthesized in “good living” as a principle of self-learning. This perspective shapes a transformative educational model in which fostering ecological awareness also fosters the future",history of rural schools; Sumapaz moorlands ; bio-learning; history of education; Journal History of Latin American Education. História da educação rural e defesa do páramo de Sumapaz: Pedagogias para a conservação,marcadores,de subjetividad,objective article analyz role history rural education sumapaz paramo key factor defend territory transition toward biocentric pedagogy propos comprehensive understand paramo subject right living classroom bio-learn based intertwin community knowledge eco-social justice transformative educational proposal 187 rev hist edu latinoam vol 28 no 48 enero junio 2026 issn 0122-7238 pp 185 205 historia de la educacion rural defensa del paramo de sumapaz pedagogia para la conservacion originality contribution study articulat historical approach education ground ontology sumapazlogy mora amphibiou ontology epistemologi south integrat contribution author such freire escobar boff gudyna shiva perspective refram rural school space resistance historical memory antifragility ecological action where water becom pedagogical spiritual political principle method approach draw history mentaliti french annal school bloch febvre reconstruct framework everyday life le goff integrat critical analysi academic normative community sourc long duration link history present categori such sumapazlogy ontology social cartography incorporat latter serv tool reconstruct territorial narrativ strengthen bond between school community conservation strategi data collection methodological strategy integrat history education ancestral territorial knowledge analyz rural educational practic through dialogic history narrativ school experienc includ exampl construction subjectiviti maldonado-torr among rural teacher support regional research archival document sumapaz conclusion defend paramo requir link history mentaliti educational imaginari root territory water stewardship environmental justice rural school must transcend state guidelin recover ancestral coexistence nature synthesiz good living principle self-learn perspective shap transformative educational model which foster ecological awarenes also foster future,history rural school sumapaz moorland bio-learn history education journal history latin american education historia da educacao rural defesa do paramo de sumapaz pedagogia para conservacao,de subjetividad objective article analyz role history rural education sumapaz paramo key factor defend territory transition toward biocentric pedagogy propos comprehensive understand paramo subject right living classroom bio-learn based intertwin community knowledge eco-social justice transformative educational proposal 187 rev hist edu latinoam vol 28 no 48 enero junio 2026 issn 0122-7238 pp 185 205 historia de la educacion rural defensa del paramo de sumapaz pedagogia para la conservacion originality contribution study articulat historical approach education ground ontology sumapazlogy mora amphibiou ontology epistemologi south integrat contribution author such freire escobar boff gudyna shiva perspective refram rural school space resistance historical memory antifragility ecological action where water becom pedagogical spiritual political principle method approach draw history mentaliti french annal school bloch febvre reconstruct framework everyday life le goff integrat critical analysi academic normative community sourc long duration link history present categori such sumapazlogy onto