2256-5248,Rhela-28-48-m-91-113.pdf,Rhela-28-48-m-91-113_0,en,ca y su alcance en las escuelas,"Objective: between 1983-1987, the national government and the provincial authorities in Santa Fe belonged to different political parties, which resulted in tense relations and various disputes. Nevertheless, they proposed common principles for educational policies, namely democratizing the system and promoting equal opportunities. This article analyzes how these principles were addressed by the cabinets that served under President Alfonsín and Governor of Santa Fe, Vernet; how they were articulated in the recommendations of the Federal Council of Culture and Education; what educational policy projects they justified; and what their scope was at the provincial level. 93 Rev. hist.edu.latinoam - Vol. 28 No. 48, enero - junio 2026 - ISSN: 0122-7238 - pp. 91 - 113 Democratización educativa e igualdad de oportunidades: discursos, agendas y políticas educativas (Santa Fe, Argentina, 1983-1987) Originality/Contribution: the analysis focuses on changes designed to encourage greater social participation in the definition of educational policies, to expand access, and to raise the quality of education at the primary and secondary levels. Method: this research draws on theoretical and methodological approaches from the fields of political and regional history. This enables the identification of the various levels of political action and their impact within Santa Fe schools. Strategies/Data Collection: A wide range of written sources, including official and journalistic material, were consulted. Conclusions: the findings suggest that, despite the shared principles that inform educational policies, the provisions aimed at promoting popular education and democratizing the system in Santa Fe schools were fragmented and failed to provide definitive or even partial solutions","Journal History of Latin American Education; recent history of education in Argentina; educational policy; universal education; democratization of education; educational reform; access to education; adult literacy. Democratização educacional e igualdade de oportunidades: discursos e políticas (Santa Fé, Argentina, 1983-1987)",marcadores,ca su alcance en las escuela,objective between 1983-1987 national government provincial authoriti santa fe belong different political parti which result tense relation variou disput nevertheles they propos common principl educational polici namely democratiz system promot equal opportuniti article analyz how these principl address cabinet serv under president alfonsin governor santa fe vernet how they articulat recommend federal council culture education what educational policy project they justifi what their scope provincial level 93 rev hist edu latinoam vol 28 no 48 enero junio 2026 issn 0122-7238 pp 91 113 democratizacion educativa igualdad de oportunidad discurso agenda politica educativa santa fe argentina 1983-1987 originality contribution analysi focus chang design encourage greater social participation definition educational polici expand acces raise quality education primary secondary level method research draw theoretical methodological approach field political regional history enabl identification variou level political action their impact within santa fe school strategi data collection wide range written sourc includ official journalistic material consult conclusion finding suggest despite shar principl inform educational polici provision aimed promot popular education democratiz system santa fe school fragment fail provide definitive even partial solution,journal history latin american education recent history education argentina educational policy universal education democrat education educational reform acces education adult literacy democratizacao educacional igualdade de oportunidad discurso politica santa fe argentina 1983-1987,ca su alcance en las escuela objective between 1983-1987 national government provincial authoriti santa fe belong different political parti which result tense relation variou disput nevertheles they propos common principl educational polici namely democratiz system promot equal opportuniti article analyz how these principl address cabinet serv under president alfonsin governor santa fe vernet how they articulat recommend federal council culture education what educational policy project they justifi what their scope provincial level 93 rev hist edu latinoam vol 28 no 48 enero junio 2026 issn 0122-7238 pp 91 113 democratizacion educativa igualdad de oportunidad discurso agenda politica educativa santa fe argentina 1983-1987 originality contribution analysi focus chang design encourage greater social participation definition educational polici expand acces raise quality education primary secondary level method research draw theoretical methodological approach field political regional history enabl identification variou level political action their impact within santa fe school strategi data collection wide range written sourc includ official journalistic material consult conclusion finding suggest despite shar principl inform educational polici provision aimed promot popular education democratiz system santa fe school fragment fail provide definitive even partial solution journal history latin american education recent history education argentina educational policy universal education democrat education educational reform acces education adult literacy democratizacao educacional igualdade de oportunidad discurso politica santa fe argentina 1983-1987,1.0.0,97296209bfaa3341
2256-5442,TAC_+RCGeo_35-2+_AGO06+V3.pdf,TAC_+RCGeo_35-2+_AGO06+V3_0,es,"Zaragocin, Sofia. 2019. “Feminist Geography in Ecuador”.","Este trabajo desarrolla un marco teórico integrado para el análisis decolonial de conflictos socioterritoriales en América Latina, articulando las propuestas conceptuales de Lorena Cabnal, Silvia Rivera Cusicanqui y Astrid Ulloa en torno a los conceptos de cuerpo-territorio y ontologías relacionales. La investigación responde a la fragmentación conceptual presente en las geografías feministas latinoamericanas y a la necesidad de herramientas analíticas capaces de comprender la complejidad multidimensional de los conflictos asociados al extractivismo. Mediante un análisis textual comparativo y la construcción sistemática de un marco conceptual integrado, el estudio propone una estructura analítica compuesta por tres componentes interrelacionados: la reciprocidad territorial como fundamento ontológico; la tensión ch’ixi como principio de contradicción productiva; y los territorios alternos como horizontes contrahegemónicos. Este enfoque permite comprender cómo los conflictos extractivistas afectan simultáneamente cuerpos y territorios, articulan múltiples temporalidades y generan disputas ontológicas junto con propuestas territoriales alternativas. Su relevancia radica en visibilizar dimensiones frecuentemente ignoradas en las aproximaciones convencionales y en aportar herramientas analíticas para el estudio de las luchas territoriales comunitarias en un contexto regional marcado por la intensificación de políticas neoextractivistas y el avance de posturas antiderechos","cuerpo-territorio, extractivismo, geografías feministas, ontologías relacionales, territorialidad. Ideas destacadas: artículo de investigación que propone un marco teórico decolonial para analizar conflictos socioterritoriales en América Latina. Integra aportes de Cabnal, Rivera Cusicanqui y Ulloa. Plantea tres componentes analíticos: reciprocidad territorial, tensión ch’ixi y territorios alte",marcadores,zaragocin sofia 2019 feminist geography in ecuador,este trabajo desarrolla marco teorico integrado analisis decolonial conflict socioterritorial america latina articul propuest conceptual lorena cabnal silvia rivera cusicanqui astrid ulloa torno concept cuerpo-territorio ontologi relacional investigacion responde fragmentacion conceptual presente geografi feminist latinoamerican necesidad herramient analitic capac comprender complejidad multidimensional conflict asociad extractivismo mediante analisis textual comparativo construccion sistematica marco conceptual integrado estudio propone estructura analitica compuesta tres component interrelacionad reciprocidad territorial como fundamento ontologico tension ch ixi como principio contradiccion productiva territori altern como horizont contrahegemonic este enfoque permite comprender como conflict extractivist afectan simultanea cuerp territori articulan multipl temporalidad generan disput ontologic junto propuest territorial alternativ relevancia radica visibilizar dimension frecuente ignorad aproxim convencional aportar herramient analitic estudio luch territorial comunitari contexto regional marcado intensificacion politic neoextractivist avance postur antiderech,cuerpo-territorio extractivismo geografi feminist ontologi relacional territorialidad ideas destacad articulo investigacion propone marco teorico decolonial analizar conflict socioterritorial america latina integra aport cabnal rivera cusicanqui ulloa plantea tres component analitic reciprocidad territorial tension ch ixi territori alte,zaragocin sofia 2019 feminist geography in ecuador este trabajo desarrolla marco teorico integrado analisis decolonial conflict socioterritorial america latina articul propuest conceptual lorena cabnal silvia rivera cusicanqui astrid ulloa torno concept cuerpo-territorio ontologi relacional investigacion responde fragmentacion conceptual presente geografi feminist latinoamerican necesidad herramient analitic capac comprender complejidad multidimensional conflict asociad extractivismo mediante analisis textual comparativo construccion sistematica marco conceptual integrado estudio propone estructura analitica compuesta tres component interrelacionad reciprocidad territorial como fundamento ontologico tension ch ixi como principio contradiccion productiva territori altern como horizont contrahegemonic este enfoque permite comprender como conflict extractivist afectan simultanea cuerp territori articulan multipl temporalidad generan disput ontologic junto propuest territorial alternativ relevancia radica visibilizar dimension frecuente ignorad aproxim convencional aportar herramient analitic estudio luch territorial comunitari contexto regional marcado intensificacion politic neoextractivist avance postur antiderech cuerpo-territorio extractivismo geografi feminist ontologi relacional territorialidad ideas destacad articulo investigacion propone marco teorico decolonial analizar conflict socioterritorial america latina integra aport cabnal rivera cusicanqui ulloa plantea tres component analitic reciprocidad territorial tension ch ixi territori alte,1.0.0,3de4654fa7d2af0d
2256-5442,TAC_+RCGeo_35-2+_AGO06+V3.pdf,TAC_+RCGeo_35-2+_AGO06+V3_0,en,o integrado para el análisis decolonial de conflictos,"This article develops an integrated theoretical framework for the decolonial analysis of socio-territorial conflicts in Latin America, articulating the contributions of Lorena Cabnal, Silvia Rivera Cusicanqui, and Astrid Ulloa regarding the concepts of body-territory and relational ontologies. The study responds to the conceptual fragmentation present in Latin American feminist geographies and to the need for analytical tools capable of addressing the multidimensional complexity of extractivist-related conflicts. Through comparative textual analysis and the systematic construction of an integrated conceptual framework, the study proposes an analytical structure composed of three interrelated components: territorial reciprocity as an ontological foundation; ch’ixi tension as a principle of productive contradiction; and alternate territories as counter-hegemonic horizons. This framework makes it possible to understand how extractivist conflicts simultaneously affect bodies and territories, articulate multiple temporalities, and generate ontological disputes alongside alternative proposals. Its relevance lies in making visible dimensions often overlooked in conventional approaches and in providing analytical tools for studying community territorial struggles within a regional context marked by the intensification of neo-extractivist policies and the growing influence of anti-rights discourses","body-territory, extractivism, feminist geographies, relational ontologies, territoriality. Highlights: research article. Proposes a decolonial theoretical framework for analyzing socio-territorial conflicts in Latin America. Integrates contributions by Cabnal, Rivera Cusicanqui, and Ulloa. Develops three analytical components: territorial reciprocity, ch’ixi tension, and alternate territories",marcadores,integrado para el analisi decolonial de conflicto,article develop integrat theoretical framework decolonial analysi socio-territorial conflict latin america articulat contribution lorena cabnal silvia rivera cusicanqui astrid ulloa regard concept body-territory relational ontologi study respond conceptual fragmentation present latin american feminist geographi need analytical tool capable address multidimensional complexity extractivist-relat conflict through comparative textual analysi systematic construction integrat conceptual framework study propos analytical structure compos three interrelat component territorial reciprocity ontological foundation ch ixi tension principle productive contradiction alternate territori counter-hegemonic horizon framework make possible understand how extractivist conflict simultaneously affect bodi territori articulate multiple temporaliti generate ontological disput alongside alternative proposal its relevance lies making visible dimension often overlook conventional approach provid analytical tool study community territorial struggl within regional context mark intensification neo-extractivist polici grow influence anti-right discours,body-territory extractivism feminist geographi relational ontologi territoriality highlight research article propos decolonial theoretical framework analyz socio-territorial conflict latin america integrat contribution cabnal rivera cusicanqui ulloa develop three analytical component territorial reciprocity ch ixi tension alternate territori,integrado para el analisi decolonial de conflicto article develop integrat theoretical framework decolonial analysi socio-territorial conflict latin america articulat contribution lorena cabnal silvia rivera cusicanqui astrid ulloa regard concept body-territory relational ontologi study respond conceptual fragmentation present latin american feminist geographi need analytical tool capable address multidimensional complexity extractivist-relat conflict through comparative textual analysi systematic construction integrat conceptual framework study propos analytical structure compos three interrelat component territorial reciprocity ontological foundation ch ixi tension principle productive contradiction alternate territori counter-hegemonic horizon framework make possible understand how extractivist conflict simultaneously affect bodi territori articulate multiple temporaliti generate ontological disput alongside alternative proposal its relevance lies making visible dimension often overlook conventional approach provid analytical tool study community territorial struggl within regional context mark intensification neo-extractivist polici grow influence anti-right discours body-territory extractivism feminist geographi relational ontologi territoriality highlight research article propos decolonial theoretical framework analyz socio-territorial conflict latin america integrat contribution cabnal rivera cusicanqui ulloa develop three analytical component territorial reciprocity ch ixi tension alternate territori,1.0.0,4ef2ce340c0bf8b5
2256-5442,TAC_+RCGeo_35-2+_AGO06+V3.pdf,TAC_+RCGeo_35-2+_AGO06+V3_1,es,Instituto de Estudios Ecologistas del Tercer Mundo.,"En Colombia es muy poco lo que se ha explorado sobre las prácticas corporales y musicales que inciden en la construcción del lugar en las geografías negras. Investigar la geografía desde los cuerpos negros, a través de la danza y el toque del tambor, cuestiona la forma en que se han mapeado los territorios negros y concibe territorialidades otras en el pensamiento geográfico. En este artículo quiero analizar el sonido, toque, fabricación y repique del tambor en las comunidades negras de Nuquí y Jurubirá del departamento del Chocó, como un conocimiento territorial que les fue ombligado: una relación que he llamado cuerpos-tambor, la cual está embebida en las geografías negras agenciadas por el agua, donde convergen cuerpos de agua humanos y no humanos evocados en la sonoridad del tambor. Relato el recorrido de la fabricación del tambor que realicé en Nuquí con maestros y maestras de música tradicional, en el que estuve inmersa, siendo mi cuerpo mestizo con-movido y fluido por cuerpos negros, para mostrar la relación cuerpo-acuatorio en el tambor. Los cuerpostambor encarnan la ontología político-relacional de las comunidades negras de Nuquí y Jurubirá con el espacio acuático; también son cuerpos de agua en los que se manifiesta la relación cuerpo-acuatorio","agua, cuerpos-tambor, espacio acuático, geografías negras, ombligado, tambor. Ideas destacadas: artículo de investigación que analiza como el agua en su movimiento consolida territorialidades negras; sin agua no hay tambor; somos gente de agua; en la tocada del tambor el repique imita el golpe de marea; a todo tambor se le hace un hueco para que salga su sonido, para que sea el cauce de su rep",marcadores,instituto estudi ecologist tercer mundo,colombia muy poco ha explorado sobre practic corporal musical inciden construccion lugar geografi negr investigar geografia desde cuerp negr trav danza toque tambor cuestiona forma han mapeado territori negr concibe territorialidad otras pensamiento geografico este articulo quiero analizar sonido toque fabricacion repique tambor comunidad negr nuqui jurubira departamento choco como conocimiento territorial les fue ombligado relacion he llamado cuerpos-tambor cual esta embebida geografi negr agenciad agua donde convergen cuerp agua human no human evocad sonoridad tambor relato recorrido fabricacion tambor realice nuqui maestr maestr musica tradicional estuve inmersa siendo mi cuerpo mestizo con-movido fluido cuerp negr mostrar relacion cuerpo-acuatorio tambor cuerpostambor encarnan ontologia politico-relacional comunidad negr nuqui jurubira espacio acuatico tambien son cuerp agua manifiesta relacion cuerpo-acuatorio,agua cuerpos-tambor espacio acuatico geografi negr ombligado tambor ideas destacad articulo investigacion analiza como agua movimiento consolida territorialidad negr sin agua no hay tambor somos gente agua tocada tambor repique imita golpe marea todo tambor le hace hueco salga sonido sea cauce rep,instituto estudi ecologist tercer mundo colombia muy poco ha explorado sobre practic corporal musical inciden construccion lugar geografi negr investigar geografia desde cuerp negr trav danza toque tambor cuestiona forma han mapeado territori negr concibe territorialidad otras pensamiento geografico este articulo quiero analizar sonido toque fabricacion repique tambor comunidad negr nuqui jurubira departamento choco como conocimiento territorial les fue ombligado relacion he llamado cuerpos-tambor cual esta embebida geografi negr agenciad agua donde convergen cuerp agua human no human evocad sonoridad tambor relato recorrido fabricacion tambor realice nuqui maestr maestr musica tradicional estuve inmersa siendo mi cuerpo mestizo con-movido fluido cuerp negr mostrar relacion cuerpo-acuatorio tambor cuerpostambor encarnan ontologia politico-relacional comunidad negr nuqui jurubira espacio acuatico tambien son cuerp agua manifiesta relacion cuerpo-acuatorio agua cuerpos-tambor espacio acuatico geografi negr ombligado tambor ideas destacad articulo investigacion analiza como agua movimiento consolida territorialidad negr sin agua no hay tambor somos gente agua tocada tambor repique imita golpe marea todo tambor le hace hueco salga sonido sea cauce rep,1.0.0,6a792c15d3ac9527
2256-5442,TAC_+RCGeo_35-2+_AGO06+V3.pdf,TAC_+RCGeo_35-2+_AGO06+V3_1,en,"Méndez Velásquez, Lixy Daniela. 2026. ““Somos gente de agua”. Cuerpos-tambor una relación ombligada con el acuatorio”. Cuadernos","Very little research has been conducted in Colombia on the bodily and musical practices that shape the construction of place within Black geographies. Examining geography through Black bodies—via dance and drumming—challenges dominant ways in which Black territories have been mapped and opens up alternative territorialities within geographical thought. This article analyzes the sound, touch, crafting, and beating of the drum among Black communities in Nuquí and Jurubirá, in the department of Chocó, as forms of territorial knowledge historically imposed upon them. I conceptualize this relationship as drum-bodies, embedded within Black geographies mediated by water, where human and more-than-human aquatic bodies converge, evoked through the drum’s sonority. I recount my experience of drum-making in Nuquí alongside traditional music practitioners, in which I became immersed as my mestizo body was affected and set in motion by Black bodily practices, in order to illustrate the body-water relationship expressed through the drum. Drum-bodies embody the political-relational ontology through which Black communities in Nuquí and Jurubirá engage with aquatic spaces; they are also water-bodies in which the body-water relationship becomes manifest","water, drum-bodies, aquatic space, black geographies, ombligado, drum. Highlights: a research article that examines how water, through its movement, consolidates Black territorialities, without water there is no drum; we are people of water; in the drum playing, the rhythmic accents imitate the tidal blow, every drum is hollowed out so that its sound can emerge, so that it becomes the channel",marcadores,mendez velasquez lixy daniela 2026 somo gente de agua cuerpos-tambor una relacion ombligada con el acuatorio cuaderno,very little r