2256-5442,TAC_+RCGeo_35-2+_AGO06+V3.pdf,TAC_+RCGeo_35-2+_AGO06+V3_2,en,"egras, escrevivência y el concepto de","The study of masculinities in geography has diversified since the late twentieth century. Despite the advances, it is necessary to address Black masculinities in greater depth, understanding that these identities escape the universality of the categories of “man” and “masculinity”, as they are racialized gender configurations. This article analyzes the representation of the spatial construction of Black male identity in Quibdó, Colombia, during the first half of the twentieth century in Las estrellas son negras by Arnoldo Palacios, based on the methodological horizon of Black geo-graphies and the notion of escrevivência, approaching the novel as a subjective record that emerges both from imagination and lived experience. It is argued that Black male identities in Quibdó during the first half of the twentieth century arose from the socio-racial conditions of the urban space, the roles imposed on Black bodies by coloniality, and the narratives of mestizaje and geographical determinism. These masculinities also emerged from various strategies of resistance exercised by Black men during this period, represented in the novel’s narrative through the control of sex-affective relationships and migration","class, urban space, gender, literature, race. Highlights: research article that analyzes the representation of the spatial construction of Black masculinities in Quibdó during the first half of the twentieth century, based on the novel Las estrellas son negras. To this end, it employs the notions of Black geo-graphies, escrevivência, and the concept of Black masculinities. Da raiva à luz inter",marcadores,egra escrevivencia el concepto de,study masculiniti geography has diversifi since late twentieth century despite advanc necessary addres black masculiniti greater depth understand these identiti escape universality categori man masculinity they racializ gender c