2256-5442,TAC_+RCGeo_35-2+_AGO06+V3.pdf,TAC_+RCGeo_35-2+_AGO06+V3_4,en,omprender mejor este proceso epistemológico.,"Decolonial feminist studies emerged at the beginning of the 21st century, highlighting the importance of gender relations interrelated with issues of patriarchy and colonialism. The aim of this article is to reflect on decolonial feminism in Brazil from the perspective of Maria das Graças Silva Nascimento Silva, a geographer from the northern region of the country. As well as reviewing the literature on the subject, we conducted an interview with the author, whose thoughts helped us to better understand this epistemological process. We conclude that although Brazilian geographers do not define themselves as decolonial feminists, this has been a fruitful debate for the construction of a decolonial feminist geography, which is in the process of becoming","feminist epistemologies, decolonial studies, Brazilian decolonial feminism, feminist geographies, production of geographical knowledge. Highlights: this is an article reflecting on the process of building a Brazilian decolonial feminist geography. It is based on readings and an interview with geographer Maria das Graças Silva Nascimento Silva. The discussion from the perspective of decolonial",marcadores,omprender mejor este proceso epistemologico,decolonial feminist studi emerg beginn 21st century highlight importance gender relation interrelat issu patriarchy colonialism aim article reflect decolonial feminism brazil perspective maria das graca silva nascimento silva geographer northern region country well review literature subject we conduct interview author whose thought help us better understand epistemological proces we conclude although brazilian geographer do not define themselv decolonial feminist has been fruitful debate construction decolonial feminist geography which proces becom,feminist epistemologi decolonial studi brazilian decolonial feminism feminist geographi production geographical 