cion no son neutr sino adquieren significa dos distint segun contexto uso analizar fidelidad como categoria flexible negociada esta investigacion cuestiona idea progreso lineal historia grabacion sonora subraya importancia actor local construccion significad alternativ torno produccion musical estudi social ciencia tecnologia fidelidad grabacion musical hazlo-tu-mismo punk usuari 53 no futuro alta fidelidad practic grabacion punk bogota 1990-2000 re colomb soc vol 48 jul -dic 2025 issn impreso 0120-159x-electronico 2256-5 485 bogota-colombia pp 51-76,1.0.0,729945b2bf7abffa
2256-5485,Sociologia de la musica.pdf,Sociologia de la musica_1,en,ciones y valores de la escena.,"This article examines recording practices in Bogotá’s punk scene between 1990 and 2000 from the perspective of Science and Technology Studies (sts). Through interviews with musicians and producers, as well as analyses of recordings and primary documents, it explores how these actors negotiated the concept of fidelity in a context of transition from analog to digital recording and distribution technologies. The study demonstrates that fidelity is not an absolute technical ideal but rather a situated and socially constructed principle, shaped by both material conditions and the aesthetic and political expectations of users. In this sense, low fidelity was a conscious choice that represented, among other things, resistance against the commercial standards of the music industry. Block recording, the use of home recorders, and the reuse of obso lete technologies were some of the strategies through which musicians redefined sound quality, distancing themselves from the dominant narrative that associates fidelity with technical precision and high-resolution sound. The article also highlights the role of collaborative networks within Bogotá’s punk scene. Musicians, producers, and independent studios established self-managed circuits where sound was defined not only by technical limitations but also by the creativity and experimentation of its actors. These collective dynamics helped shape a distinctive sonic identity, independent from commercial standards, and adapted to the conditions and values of the scene. This work contributes to the debate on the relationship between technology, music, and culture, showing that recording technologies are not neutral but acquire different meanings depending on their context of use. By analyzing fidelity as a flexible and negoti ated category, this research challenges the idea of linear progress in the history of sound recording and underscores the importance of local actors in constructing alternative meanings around music production","diy, fidelity, music recording, punk, sts, users. [54] UNIVERSIDAD NACIONAL DE COLOMBIA Mónica A. Ulloa Ruiz y Javier Guerrero-C",marcadores,cion valor de la escena,article examin record practic bogota punk scene between 1990 2000 perspective science technology studi sts through interview musician producer well analys recording primary document explor how these actor negotiat concept fidelity context transition analog digital record distribution technologi study demonstrat fidelity not absolute technical ideal but rather situat socially construct principle shap both material condition aesthetic political expect user sense low fidelity consciou choice represent among other thing resistance against commercial standard music industry block record use home recorder reuse obso lete technologi some strategi through which musician redefin sound quality distanc themselv dominant narrative associat fidelity technical precision high-resolution sound article also highlight role collaborative network within bogota punk scene musician producer independent studio establish self-manag circuit where sound defin not only technical limit but also creativity experimentation its actor these collective dynamic help shape distinctive sonic identity independent commercial standard adapt condition valu scene work contribut debate relationship between technology music culture show record technologi not neutral but acquire different meaning depend their context use analyz fidelity flexible negoti ated category research challeng idea linear progres history sound record underscor importance local actor construct alternative meaning around music production,diy fidelity music record punk sts user 54 universidad nacional de colombia monica ulloa ruiz javier guerrero-c,cion valor de la escena article examin record practic bogota punk scene between 1990 2000 perspective science technology studi sts t