2256-5485,Sociologia de la musica.pdf,Sociologia de la musica_2,en,"antropológicos guiados por una intención clasificatoria,","This article aims to reflect upon the problem of cultural representation, in a nonexhaustive way, by proposing a classification of the so-called sound studios, meaningful spaces of the audiovisual universe. From the confluence between ethnographic experi ence, literature from different academic fields and other documentary materials, inspired by sound studies, I seek to understand the extent to which these “laboratories” can con tribute to an understanding of varied themes and processes: from rehearsals aimed at live performances, to creative and compositional work, including recording situations and procedures for expanding perception. By suggesting an ordering based on the similarities and differences of specific locations, I establish some definitions, as well as criteria and variables to be considered in identifying the social meanings and the symbolic economy around them. The work is guided by qualitative, empirical and multi-situated research, undertaken at different times, mainly between 2017 and 2018, among the middle classes who frequent seven locations: K9 studios, musician João Werneck’s home studio, Sideral, WeJam, Luminatta, and Space Blues studios, located in Rio de Janeiro and São Paulo cities. The intention is to use this ethnographic material in dialogue with a theoretical framework enriched by anthropological contributions guided by a classificatory inten tion, unfolded in eight analytical axes, proposed to have broad validity in the sense of contributing to a representation of this sui generis universe. As a result, I offer an interpre tation of these environments based on their size, the characteristics of each property, the tangibility of their equipment, their function, the way in which services are contracted, their levels of portability, the worlds of work to which they are linked and its market inser tion, which, I hope, will provide subsidies so that ethnomusicologists, sociomusicolo gists, sound and cultural goods market researchers can reach new understandings about these multifaceted scenarios","audiovisual, phonography, music, sound, sound studies, studios. [81] O que é um estúdio? Notas para uma classificação de ambientes voltados à sonorização∗ RE V. COLOMB. SOC. VOL.48, N.0 2 JUL.-DIC. 2025 ISSN: impreso 0120-159X–electrónico 2256-5 485 BOGOTÁ-COLOMBIA PP. 7 7-1 06 Introdução Neste artigo, busca-se compreender os significados subjacentes a espaços comumente qualificados com",marcadores,antropologico guiado por una intencion clasificatoria,article aims reflect upon problem cultural representation nonexhaustive way propos classification so-call sound studio meaningful spac audiovisual universe confluence between ethnographic experi ence literature different academic field other documentary material inspir sound studi seek understand extent which these laboratori can con tribute understand vari them process rehearsal aimed live performanc creative compositional work includ record situ procedur expand perception suggest order based similariti differenc specific location establish some definition well criteria variabl consider identify social meaning symbolic economy around them work guid qualitative empirical multi-situat research undertaken different time mainly between 2017 2018 among middle class who frequent seven location k9 studio musician joao werneck home studio sideral wejam luminatta space blue studio locat rio de janeiro sao paulo citi intention use ethnographic material dialogue theoretical framework enrich anthropological contribution guid classificatory inten tion unfold eight analytical axes propos have broad validity sense contribut representation sui generi universe result offer interpre tation these environment based their size characteristic each property tangibility their equipment their function way which servic contract their level portability world work which they link its market inser tion which hope will provide subsidi so ethnomusicologist sociomusicolo gist sound cultural good market researcher can reach new understanding about these multifacet scenario,audiovisual phonography music sound sound studi studio 81 que um estudio nota para uma classificacao de ambient voltado sonorizacao re colomb soc vol 48 jul -dic 2025 issn impreso 0120-159x-electronico 2256-5 485 bogota-colombia pp 7-1 06 introducao neste artigo busca-se compreender os significado subjacent espaco comumente qualificado com,antropologico guiado por una intencion clasificatoria article aims reflect upon problem cultural representation nonexhaustive way propos classification so-call sound studio meaningful spac audiovisual universe confluence between ethnographic experi ence literature different academic field other documentary material inspir sound studi seek understand extent which these laboratori can con tribute understand vari them process rehearsal aimed live performanc creative compositional work includ record situ procedur expand perception suggest order based similariti differenc specific location establish some definition well criteria variabl consider identify social meaning symbolic economy around them work guid qualitative empirical multi-situat research undertaken different time mainly between 2017 2018 among middle class who frequent seven location k9 studio musician joao werneck home studio sideral wejam luminatta space blue studio locat rio de janeiro sao paulo citi intention use ethnographic material dialogue theoretical framework enrich anthropological contribution guid classificatory inten tion unfold eight analytical axes propos have broad validity sense contribut representation sui generi universe result offer interpre tation these environment based their size characteristic each property tangibility their equipment their function way which servic contract their level portability world work which they link its market inser tion which hope will provide subsidi so ethnomusicologist sociomusicolo gist sound cultural good market researcher can reach new understanding about these multifacet scenario audiovisual phonography music sound sound studi studio 81 que um estudio nota para uma classificacao de ambient voltado sonorizacao re colomb soc vol 48 jul -dic 2025 issn impreso 0120-159x-electronico 2256-5 485 bogota-colombia pp 7-1 06 introducao neste artigo busca-se compreender os significado subjacent espaco comumente qualificado com,1.0.0,67338e8c9076a9f7
2256-5485,Sociologia de la musica.pdf,Sociologia de la musica_3,es,ro. A criação de,"La música es un mecanismo importante de expresión cultural, que refleja y perpetúa prácticas sociales e ideológicas. En el contexto de la cultura brasileña, esta se caracteriza por prácticas patriarcales, machistas, racistas y misóginas. La música, como práctica cul tural, desempeña un papel clave en el mantenimiento y difusión de estas dinámicas de poder. En esta cultura lo femenino se asocia con la inferioridad, siendo el cuerpo, la ropa, los espacios, las funciones y los comportamientos femeninos subalternizados. La relación con lo femenino está estigmatizada por la percepción de debilidad moral, intelectual, psicológica, sexual y cultural. El estudio propuesto examina las letras de las canciones brasileñas más populares de 2024, desde una perspectiva analítico-comportamental, con el objetivo de identificar y analizar prácticas verbales/reglas misóginas. La investigación se realizó a partir de la selección de las 50 canciones más escuchadas en las principales plataformas, como Spotify, YouTube Music, Deezer y Apple Music. Tras un análisis cua litativo, se seleccionaron 24 canciones por contener elementos misóginos en sus letras, representando un corpus que refleja las dinámicas de género predominantes en la música brasileña. El género más común entre las canciones analizadas fue el funk, seguido por el sertanejo, con algunas fusiones de estilos, como el “funknejo”. Las letras de estas can ciones abordan con frecuencia relaciones sexuales y de interés, asociando el sexo con beneficios materiales o financieros, lo que evidencia la sexualización de las relaciones y la cosificación de las mujeres. La investigación muestra cómo, a través de estas compo siciones, las prácticas culturales misóginas continúan reforzándose y normalizándose, perpetuando la desigualdad de género y la violencia contra las mujeres en la sociedad. La música actúa como un potente vehículo en la reproducción de estereotipos de género. La creación de contranormas —normas que desafían y deconstruyen las reglas culturales opresivas— es esencial para promover el cambio social. Estas contranormas ofrecen una reinterpretación de las emociones, los afectos y la identidad, enfatizando la importancia de una construcción subjetiva que no se somete a las expectativas misóginas. Tales con tranormas resignifican el lugar de la mujer en la sociedad, desafiando prácticas culturales opresivas y contribuyendo a la construcción de un futuro más igualitario","cultura patriarcal, misoginia, música brasileña, normas, cosificación de las mujeres prácticas verbales, violencia de género. [110] UNIVERSIDAD NACIONAL DE COLOMBIA Carla Juliane Martins Rodrigues y Juliana Pato Pereira",marcadores,ro criacao,musica mecanismo importante expresion cultural refleja perpetua practic social ideologic contexto cultura brasilena esta caracteriza practic patriarcal machist racist misogin musica como practica cul tural desempena papel clave mantenimiento difusion estas dinamic poder esta cultura femenino asocia inferioridad siendo cuerpo ropa espaci funcion comport femenin subalternizad relacion femenino esta estigmatizada percepcion debilidad moral intelectual psicologica sexual cultural estudio propuesto examina letr cancion brasilen mas popular 2024 desde perspectiva analitico-comportamental objetivo identificar analizar practic verbal regl misogin investigacion realizo partir seleccion 50 cancion mas escuchad principal plataform como spotify youtube music deezer apple music tras analisis cua litativo seleccionaron 24 cancion contener element misogin sus letr represent corpus refleja dinamic genero predominant musica brasilena genero mas comun entre cancion analizad fue funk seguido sertanejo algun fusion estil como funknejo letr estas can cion abordan frecuencia relacion sexual inter asoci sexo benefici material financier evidencia sexualizacion relacion cosificacion mujer investigacion muestra como trav estas compo sicion practic cultural misogin continuan reforzandose normalizandose perpetu desigualdad genero violencia contra mujer sociedad musica actua como potente vehiculo reproduccion estereotip genero creacion contranorm --norm desafian deconstruyen regl cultural opresivas-- esencial promover cambio social estas contranorm ofrecen reinterpretacion emocion afect identidad enfatiz importancia construccion subjetiva no somete expectativ misogin tales tranorm resignifican lugar mujer sociedad desafi practic cultural opresiv contribuyendo construccion futuro mas igualitario,cultura patriarcal misoginia musica brasilena norm cosificacion mujer practic verbal violencia genero 110 universidad nacional colombia carla juliane martins rodrigu juliana pato pereira,ro criacao musica mecanismo importante expresion cultural refleja perpetua practic social ideologic contexto cultura brasilena esta caracteriza practic patriarcal machist racist misogin musica como practica cul tural desempena papel clave mantenimiento difusion estas dinamic poder esta cultura femenino asocia inferioridad siendo cuerpo ropa espaci funcion comport femenin subalternizad relacion femenino esta estigmatizada percepcion debilidad moral intelectual psicologica sexual cultural estudio propuesto examina letr cancion brasilen mas popular 2024 desde perspectiva analitico-comportamental objetivo identificar analizar practic verbal regl misogin investigacion realizo partir seleccion 50 cancion mas escuchad principal plataform como spotify youtube music deezer apple music tras analisis cua litativo seleccionaron 24 cancion contener element misogin sus letr represent corpus refleja dinamic genero predominant musica brasilena genero mas comun entre cancion analizad fue funk seguido sertanejo algun fusion estil como funknejo letr estas can cion abordan frecuencia relacion sexual inter asoci sexo benefici material financier evidencia sexualizacion relacion cosificacion mujer investigacion muestra como trav estas compo sicion practic cultural misogin continuan reforzandose normalizandose perpetu desigualdad genero violencia contra mujer sociedad musica actua como potente vehiculo reproduccion estereotip genero creacion contranorm --norm desafian deconstruyen regl cultural opresivas-- esencial promover cambio social estas contranorm ofrecen reinterpretacion emocion afect identidad enfatiz importancia construccion subjetiva no somete expectativ misogin tales tranorm resignifican lugar mujer sociedad desafi practic cultural opresiv contribuyendo construccion futuro mas igualitario cultura patriarcal misoginia musica brasilena norm cosificacion mujer practic verbal violencia genero 110 universidad nacional colombia carla juliane martins rodrigu juliana pato pereira,1.0.0,444a02ed1be3e133
2256-5485,Sociologia de la musica.pdf,Sociologia de la musica_3,en,nero y la violencia contra las mujeres en la sociedad.,"Music is an important mechanism of cultural expression, reflecting and perpetuating social and ideological practices. In the context of Brazilian culture, it is widely character ized by patriarchal, sexist, racist, and misogynistic practices. Music, as a cultural practice, plays a fundamental role in maintaining and spreading these power dynamics. In this culture, the feminine is frequently associated with inferiority, with the body, clothing, spaces, functions, and behaviors of women being subordinated. The relationship with the feminine is stigmatized by perceptions of moral, intellectual, psychological, sexual, and cultural weakness. The proposed study examines the lyrics of the most popular Brazilian songs of 2024 from an analytical-behavioral perspective, aiming to identify and analyze misogynistic verbal practices/rules. The research was conducted by selecting the 50 most-played songs on major streaming platforms as Spotify, YouTube Music, Deezer, and Apple Music. After a qualitative analysis, 24 songs were selected for containing mi sogynistic elements in their lyrics, representing a corpus that reflects the dominant gender dynamics in Brazilian music. The most prevalent music genre among the analyzed songs was funk, followed by sertanejo, with some genre fusion, as “funknejo”. The lyrics of these songs often address sexual and transactional relationships, linking sex to material or financial benefits, which highlights the sexualization of relationships and the objecti fication of women. The research reveals how, through these compositions, misogynistic cultural practices continue to be reinforced and normalized, perpetuating gender inequal ity and violence against women in society. Music, therefore, acts as a powerful vehicle in reproducing gender stereotypes. The creation of counter-norms —norms that challenge and deconstruct oppressive cultural rules— is essential to promote social change. These counter-norms offer a reinterpretation of emotions, affections, and identity, emphasizing the importance of a subjective construction that does not submit to misogynistic expecta tions. These counter-norms re-signify the role of women in society, challenging oppres sive cultural practices and contributing to the construction of a more egalitarian future","Brazilian music, gender violence, misogyny, norms, objectification of women, patriarchal culture, verbal practices. [111] Músicas brasileiras e misoginia: uma interpretação analítico-comportamental das produções mais ouvidas em 2024∗ RE V. COLOMB. SOC. VOL.48, N.0 2 JUL.-DIC. 2025 ISSN: impreso 0120-159X–electrónico 2256-5 485 BOGOTÁ-COLOMBIA PP. 1 0 7-134 Introdução No contexto da disc",marcadores,nero la violencia contra las mujer en la sociedad,music important mechanism cultural expression reflect perpetuat social ideological practic context brazilian culture widely character ized patriarchal sexist racist misogynistic practic music cultural practice play fundamental role maintain spread these power dynamic culture feminine frequently associat inferiority body cloth spac function behavior women being subordinat relationship feminine stigmatiz perception moral intellectual psychological sexual cultural weaknes propos study examin lyric most popular brazilian song 2024 analytical-behavioral perspective aiming identify analyze misogynistic verbal practic rule research conduct select 50 most-play song major stream platform spotify youtube music deezer apple music after qualitative analysi 24 song select contain mi sogynistic element their lyric represent corpu reflect dominant gender dynamic brazilian music most prevalent music genre among analyz song funk follow sertanejo some genre fusion funknejo lyric these song often addres sexual transactional relationship link sex material financial benefit which highlight sexual relationship objecti fication women research reveal how through these composition misogynistic cultural practic continue reinforc normaliz perpetuat gender inequal ity violence against women society music therefore acts powerful vehicle reproduc gender stereotyp creation counter-norm --norm challenge deconstruct oppressive cultural rules-- essential promote social change these counter-norm offer reinterpretation emotion affection identity emphasiz importance subjective construction does not submit misogynistic expecta tion these counter-norm re-signify role women society challeng oppr sive cultural practic contribut construction more egalitarian future,brazilian music gender violence misogyny norm objectification women patriarchal culture verbal practic 111 musica brasileira misoginia uma interpretacao analitico-comportamental das produco mais ouvida em 2024 re colomb soc vol 48 jul -dic 2025 issn impreso 0120-159x-electronico 2256-5 485 bogota-colombia pp 7-134 introducao no contexto da disc,nero la violencia contra las mujer en la sociedad music important mechanism cultural expression reflect perpetuat social ideological practic context brazilian culture widely character ized patriarchal sexist racist misogynistic practic music cultural practice play fundamental role maintain spread these power dynamic culture feminine frequently associat inferiority body cloth spac function behavior women being subordinat relationship feminine stigmatiz perception moral intellectual psychological sexual cultural weaknes propos study examin lyric most popular brazilian song 2024 analytical-behavioral perspective aiming identify analyze misogynistic verbal practic rule research conduct select 50 most-play song major stream platform spotify youtube music deezer apple music after qualitative analysi 24 song select contain mi sogynistic element their lyric represent corpu reflect dominant gender dynamic brazilian music most prevalent music genre among analyz song funk follow sertanejo some genre fusion funknejo lyric these song often addres sexual transactional relationship link sex material financial benefit which highlight sexual relationship objecti fication women research reveal how through these composition misogynistic cultural practic continue reinforc normaliz perpetuat gender inequal ity violence against women society music therefore acts powerful vehicle reproduc gender stereotyp creation counter-norm --norm challenge deconstruct oppressive cultural rules-- essential promote social change these counter-norm offer reinterpretation emotion affection identity emphasiz importance subjective construction does not submit misogynistic expecta tion these counter-norm re-signify role women society challeng oppr sive cultural practic contribut construction more egalitarian future brazilian music gender violence misogyny norm objectification women patriarchal culture verbal practic 111 musica brasileira misoginia uma interpretacao analitico-comportamental das produco mais ouvida em 2024 re colomb soc vol 48 jul -dic 2025 issn impreso 0120-159x-electronico 2256-5 485 bogota-colombia pp 7-134 introducao no contexto da disc,1.0.0,1fb076d1f6cd25a1
2256-5485,Sociologia de la musica.pdf,Sociologia de la musica_4,es,"ción de tipologías estilísticas del reggaetón. Fase 1: analítica”, financiado por la Vicerrectoría","En este artículo se analizan las representaciones de género de los 385 videoclips oficiales de las canciones más populares de reggaetón según Billboard Hot Latin Songs entre 2006 y 2023. Se emplea el análisis de contenido mediante una metodología mixta que combina un abordaje numérico de los aspectos analizados con un análisis cualita tivo. Se indagaron aspectos como número de mujeres y hombres que aparecen en los videos, grupos étnicos, complexión física, actitudes que exhiben y roles representados. Los resultados evidencian una narrativa muy definida, con roles de género establecidos y reiterados. Las diferencias entre los videoclips de artistas mujeres y hombres es poca en términos cuantitativos, pero significativa en términos cualitativos","música, reggaetón, representaciones de género, videoclip. [137] Cangris, bichotas y representaciones de género en videoclips de reggaetón: “Videítos, pero con datos”∗ RE V. COLOMB. SOC. VOL.48, N.0 2 JUL.-DIC. 2025 ISSN: impreso 0120-159X–electrónico 2256-5 485 BOGOTÁ-COLOMBIA PP. 135-168",marcadores,cion tipologi estilistic reggaeton fase analitica financiado vicerrectoria,este articulo analizan represent genero 385 videoclips oficial cancion mas popular reggaeton segun billboard hot latin songs entre 2006 2023 emplea analisis contenido mediante metodologia mixta combina abordaje numerico aspect analizad analisis cualita tivo indagaron aspect como numero mujer hombr aparecen vide grup etnic complexion fisica actitud exhiben roles representad resultad evidencian narrativa muy definida roles genero establecid reiterad diferenci entre videoclips artist mujer hombr poca termin cuantitativ pero significativa termin cualitativ,musica reggaeton represent genero videoclip 137 cangris bichot represent genero videoclips reggaeton videit pero datos re colomb soc vol 48 