2256-5485,Sociologia de la musica.pdf,Sociologia de la musica_8,en,percepciones sobre la ruralidad.,"This research article analyzes from feminist sociology and popular feminisms, the perceptions that women in Jebalá, Paniquita, and the municipal capital of Totoró in the department of Cauca, Colombia, have about their identity and rootedness with rurality. Employing a mixed methodology using techniques as documentary review, review of sta tistical techniques of automatic learning, search algorithms, and computational linguistics, to take into consideration that women in this area differ from what is considered by the legal norm on what it is to be a rural woman and aim to apply their own definitions based on their processes of care and support. The approach to agricultural work permeated by an indigenous environmental awareness leads to consider that rural women perceive themselves from an approach different from that referred to in Law 732 of 2002 (Law on rural women in Colombia), allowing to consider their relationship with rurality through care work that gives emotional meaning to their life plans, their family and their commit ment to the territory. Likewise, rural women even belonging to the same municipality have different perspectives, actions, and identities regarding what they consider to be a “rural woman”, due to the specific socioeconomic and cultural dynamics of each rural territory in which they live. This underscores how external factors can influence their emotions and perceptions of what rurality means. Therefore, recognizing and valuing the work of women in rural communities from a holistic perspective can lead to more effective and sustainable solutions. This implies addressing the inequalities and challenges faced by women in rural areas by creating policies that integrate emotional and spiritual aspects, in addition to the physical and economic aspects they face in their daily rural lives. In doing so, rural identities will be strengthened and greater territorial rootedness will be generated","agrochemicals, emotions, feelings, feminisms, perceptions, rural women. Descriptors: feminism, rural women, social policy, sustainable development. [259] Sentimientos y Emociones: Un camino para forjar la percepción rural de las mujeres en Totoró, Cauca, Colombia RE V. COLOMB. SOC. VOL.48, N.0 2 JUL.-DIC. 2025 ISSN: impreso 0120-159X–electrónico 2256-5 485 BOGOTÁ-COLOMBIA PP. 255-282 Res",marcadores,percepcion sobre la ruralidad,research article analyz feminist sociology popular feminism perception women jebala paniquita municipal capital totoro department cauca colombia have about their identity rootednes rurality employ mixed methodology using techniqu documentary review review sta tistical techniqu automatic learn search algorithm computational linguistic take into consideration women area differ what consider legal norm what rural woman aim apply their own definition based their process care support approach agricultural work permeat indigenou environmental awarenes lead consider rural women perceive themselv approach different referr law 732 2002 law rural women colombia allow consider their relationship rurality through care work give emotional mean their life plan their family their commit ment territory likewise rural women even belong same municipality have different perspectiv action identiti regard what they consider rural woman due specific socioeconomic cultural dynamic each rural territory which they live underscor how external factor can influence their emotion perception what rurality mean therefore recogniz valu work women rural communiti holistic perspective can lead more effective sustainable solution impli address inequaliti challeng faced women rural area creat polici integrate emotional spiritual aspect addition physical economic aspect they face their daily rural live doing so rural identiti will strengthen greater territorial rootednes will generat,agrochemical emotion feeling feminism percepti