2256-5485,Sociologia de la musica.pdf,Sociologia de la musica_9,en,intos grados con formas agrarias anteriores.,"This paper examines the social and ecological impacts of a major transformation in Cuyo’s olive sector that began in the late 1990s. Framed within the Third International Food Regime, this transformation involved an exclusionary modernization that reshaped the sector’s social structure. We pursue two main objectives: to describe the spatial and ecological reconfiguration of the agro-industrial olive complex, and to characterize the most relevant agrarian and industrial actors in Mendoza and San Juan. To this end, we ap ply a methodology that triangulates in-depth interviews with quantitative analyses based on census data. Our results show a marked increase in the relative weight of Catamarca and La Rioja, where, due to the absence of a prior olive-growing tradition, a polarized social structure was consolidated. In contrast, San Juan —and especially Mendoza— maintained a more diversified olive production, linked to a preexisting heterogeneous social structure. In these provinces, we identify a diversity of local actors still operating in traditional olive-growing areas, with varying degrees of articulation with earlier agrarian forms. In opposition, large olive enterprises —whether vertically integrated or not— have emerged outside these historical territories, expressing the deeper effects of the structural transformation. The coexistence of both models reveals persistent tensions surrounding agricultural modernization processes in Cuyo","agrarian structure, ecological-territorial reordering, exclusionary mo dernization, Mendoza y San Juan, olive agro-industrial complex, third food regime. Descriptors: Argentina, agricultural economy, food industry, vegetable oil. [286] UNIVERSIDAD NACIONAL DE COLOMBIA Jorge Daniel Ivars",marcadores,into grado con forma agraria anterior,paper examin social ecological impact major transformation cuyo olive sector began la