2256-5493,"Revista Trabajo Social 28(2) - Pervivencias y Transformaciones del Trabajo Social en el Sur Global - Racionalidades, agriet.pdf","Revista Trabajo Social 28(2) - Pervivencias y Transformaciones del Trabajo Social en el Sur Global - Racionalidades, agriet_5",en,lidad social distintiva para fomentar,"This essay aims to characterize the contributions of systematization to the processes of knowledge-building in Chilean Social Work, from the perspective of its distinctive social rationality. A documentary review of specialized thematic publications was conducted, and the main contributions of this systematization and collective reflection, emerging from the experiences of social action over six decades of development, were identified. The results show that systematization has a distinctive social rationality for the development of thoughtful processes grounded in social practices, offering an alternative to the scientific rationality of social research. Its advances challenge the status of social research as a unique form of knowledge, seeking to enable collective knowledge-building by recovering social and professional learning from social programs and projects implemented and legitimized by their own participants",Social Knowledge-Building; Social Research; Scientific Rationality; Social Rationality; Systematization; Chilean Social Work,marcadores,lidad social distintiva para fomentar,essay aims characterize contribution systemat process knowledge-build chilean social work perspective its distinctive social rationality documentary review specializ thematic public conduct main contribution systemat collective reflection emerg experienc social action over six decad development identifi result show systemat has distinctive social rationality development thoughtful process ground social practic offer alternative scientific rationality social research its advanc challenge statu social research unique form knowledge seek enable collective knowledge-build recover so