2256-5493,TAC Rev Tra Social 28_1_V6 (1).pdf,TAC Rev Tra Social 28_1_V6 (1)_5,en,experiencia de las y los estudiantes tutores considerando sus motivaciones de,"In recent years, Chile has made significant progress in reducing gaps in access to higher education, with a highly selective and competitive system that continues to pose challenges to social mobility and exacerbate educational inequality. In this context, peer tutoring programs have emerged to support the permanence of first-year higher education students, facilitated by students from higher academic levels. Based on a qualitative study of peer tutoring programs at a Chilean university, the experiences of students who work as tutors are addressed through in-depth interviews and a thematic categorical analysis regarding their motivations for participation, support strategies, social contributions, and challenges involved in implementing peer tutoring programs. The main results refer to support strategies mobilized by a sense of social justice, tutoring as a space for both social and academic recognition, and horizontality and familiarity as differentiating strategic initiatives in peer tutoring. In conclusion, these experiences contribute to the construction of the university student identity and help foster conditions for educational equity","Educational inequality; Higher Education, Peer Tutoring; Support",marcadores,experiencia de las los estudiant tutor considerando sus motivacion de,recent year chile has made significant progres reduc gaps acces higher education highly selective competitive system continu pose challeng social mobility exacerbate educational inequality context peer tutor program have emerg support permanence first-year higher education student facilitat student higher academic level based qualitative study peer tutor program chilean university experienc student who work tutor address through in-depth interview thematic categorical analysi regard their motiv participation support strategi social contribution challeng involv implement peer tutor program main result refer support strategi mobiliz sense social justice tutor space both social academic recognition horizontality familiarity differentiat strategic initiativ peer tutor conclusion these experienc contribute construction university student identity help foster condition educational equity,educational inequality higher education peer tutor support,experiencia de las los estudiant tutor considerando sus motivacion de recent year chile has made significant progres reduc gaps acces higher education highly selective competitive system continu pose challeng social mobility exacerbate educational inequality context peer tutor program have emerg support permanence first-year higher education student facilitat student higher academic level based qualitative study peer tutor program chilean university experienc student who work tutor address through in-depth interview thematic categorical analysi regard their motiv participation support strategi social contribution challeng involv implement peer tutor program main result refer support strategi mobiliz sense social justice tutor space both social academic recognition horizontality familiarity differentiat strategic initiativ peer tutor conclusion these experienc contribute construction university student identity help foster condition educational equity educational inequality higher education peer tutor support,1.0.0,db989bbe1c8267b6
2256-5493,TAC Rev Tra Social 28_1_V6 (1).pdf,TAC Rev Tra Social 28_1_V6 (1)_6,es,María Antonia Buenaventura Rubio 1*,"Este artículo examina el potencial transformador del Aprendizaje-Servicio (ApS) en el Trabajo Social comunitario. A partir del análisis del proyecto “Els somriures dels casals”, desarrollado entre 2014 y 2019 en el sur de Marruecos, se explora cómo el ApS contribuye a una formación profesional crítica, ética e intercultural, alineada con principios de justicia social y equidad, en un contexto marcado por la crisis de la educación superior pública y los desafíos de la Agenda 2030. La investigación cualitativa y etnográfica, empleó técnicas como grupos de discusión, diarios de campo y reflexiones finales, analizadas mediante el software Atlas.ti. Los resultados muestran un impacto significativo en tres dimensiones del aprendizaje estudiantil: personal, profesional y social. Además, revela efecto positivo en la comunidad amazigh, destacando el fortalecimiento cultural y la participación comunitaria","Aprendizaje-Servicio; Educación Superior Pública; Equidad Cultural; Justicia Social; Trabajo Social Comunitario; Transformación Social. Revista Trabajo Social vol. 28 n.˚ 1, ene-jun 2026, issn (en línea): 2256-5493, Bogotá · 181-199 análisis del aprendizaje-servicio en el trabajo social comunitario como motor de transformación y justicia... [ 183 ]",marcadores,maria antonia buenaventura rubio,este articulo examina potencial transformador aprendizaje-servicio aps trabajo social comunitario partir analisis proyecto els somriur dels casals desarrollado entre 2014 2019 sur marruec explora como aps contribuye formacion profesional critica etica intercultural alineada principi justicia social equidad contexto marcado crisis educacion superior publica desafi agenda 2030 investigacion cualitativa etnografica empleo tecnic como grup discusion diari campo reflexion final analizad mediante software atlas ti resultad muestran impacto significativo tres dimension aprendizaje estudiantil personal profesional social adem revela efecto positivo comunidad amazigh destac fortalecimiento cultural participacion comunitaria,aprendizaje-servicio educacion superior publica equidad cultural justicia social trabajo social comunitario transformacion social revista trabajo social vol 28 ene-jun 2026 issn linea 2256-5493 bogota 181-199 analisis aprendizaje-servicio trabajo social comunitario como motor transformacion justicia 183,maria antonia buenaventura rubio este articulo examina potencial transformador aprendizaje-servicio aps trabajo social comunitario partir analisis proyecto els somriur dels casals desarrollado entre 2014 2019 sur marruec explora como aps contribuye formacion profesional critica etica intercultural alineada principi justicia social equidad contexto marcado crisis educacion superior publica desafi agenda 2030 investigacion cualitativa etnografica empleo tecnic como grup discusion diari campo reflexion final analizad mediante software atlas ti resultad muestran impacto significativo tres dimension aprendizaje estudiantil personal profesional social adem revela efecto positivo comunidad amazigh destac fortalecimiento cultural participacion comunitaria aprendizaje-servicio educacion superior publica equidad cultural justicia social trabajo social comunitario transformacion social revista trabajo social vol 28 ene-jun 2026 issn linea 2256-5493 bogota 181-199 analisis aprendizaje-servicio trabajo social comunitario como motor transformacion justicia 183,1.0.0,df641a2be3be14b6
2256-5493,TAC Rev Tra Social 28_1_V6 (1).pdf,TAC Rev Tra Social 28_1_V6 (1)_6,en,un contexto marcado por la crisis de la educación superior pública y los desafíos de la,"This article examines the transformative potential of Service-Learning (SL) in Community Social Work within a context marked by the crisis in public higher education and the challenges posed by the 2030 Agenda. Based on the analysis of the project “Els somriures dels casals”, carried out between 2014 and 2019 in southern Morocco with interdisciplinary participation from students at the University of Barcelona and local community agents, this study explores how SL contributes to critical, ethical, and intercultural professional training aligned with principles of social justice and equity. The research, which adopted a qualitative and ethnographic approach, used techniques such as discussion groups, field journals, and final reflections, which were analyzed using Atlas. ti software. The results show a significant impact across three dimensions of student learning: personal, professional, and social. Additionally, a positive effect was observed within the Amazigh community, particularly in terms of cultural strengthening and community participation",Service-Learning; Public Higher Education; Community Social Work; Social Justice; Social Transformation; Cultural Equity,marcadores,un contexto marcado por la crisi de la educacion superior publica los desafio de la,article examin transformative potential service-learn sl community social work within context mark crisi public higher education challeng posed 2030 agenda based analysi project els somriur dels casal carri out between 2014 2019 southern morocco interdisciplinary participation student university barcelona local community agent study explor how sl contribut critical ethical intercultural professional train align principl social justice equity research which adopt qualitative ethnographic approach used techniqu such discussion group field journal final reflection which analyz using atla ti software result show significant impact acros three dimension student learn personal professional social additionally positive effect observ within amazigh community particularly term cultural strengthen community participation,service-learn public higher education community social work social justice social transformation cultural equity,un contexto marcado por la crisi de la educacion superior publica los desafio de la article examin transformative potential service-learn sl community social work within context mark crisi public higher education challeng posed 2030 agenda based analysi project els somriur dels casal carri out between 2014 2019 southern morocco interdisciplinary participation student university barcelona local community agent study explor how sl contribut critical ethical intercultural professional train align principl social justice equity research which adopt qualitative ethnographic approach used techniqu such discussion group field journal final reflection which analyz using atla ti software result show significant impact acros three dimension student learn personal professional social additionally positive effect observ within amazigh community particularly term cultural strengthen community participation service-learn public higher education community social work social justice social transformation cultural equity,1.0.0,64a170e719b0a0ec
2256-5493,TAC Rev Tra Social 28_1_V6 (1).pdf,TAC Rev Tra Social 28_1_V6 (1)_7,es,Amarronar la universidad.,"En el artículo se aborda el cruce universidad y Trabajo Social, en Argentina, proponiendo la idea de una universidad sudaka como proyección frente a los desafíos contemporáneos. Para tal fin, se presenta una genealogía que destaca hitos en la historia de la universidad argentina en términos de democratización, se definen las categorías marrón, negro y sudaka como elementos epistémicos que permiten efectuar críticas al carácter blanco-céntrico de la universidad. Asimismo, se registran operaciones del racismo en el ámbito universitario; y se describen aportes del Trabajo Social a las confrontaciones de esas lógicas y prácticas racistas, en pro de la construcción de una Universidad Sudaka y Marrón","Marrón; Negro; Sudaka; Trabajo Social; Universidad; Racismo. Revista Trabajo Social vol. 28 n.˚ 1, ene-jun 2026, issn (en línea): 2256-5493, Bogotá · 199-222 Amarronar la universidad. Apuntes desde Trabajo Social [ 201 ]",marcadores,amarronar universidad,articulo aborda cruce universidad trabajo social argentina propon idea universidad sudaka como proyeccion frente desafi contemporane tal fin presenta genealogia destaca hitos historia universidad argentina termin democratizacion definen categori marron negro sudaka como element epistemic permiten efectuar critic caracter blanco-centrico universidad asimismo registran oper racismo ambito universitario describen aport trabajo social confront esas logic practic racist pro construccion universidad sudaka marron,marron negro sudaka trabajo social universidad racismo revista trabajo social vol 28 ene-jun 2026 issn linea 2256-5493 bogota 199-222 amarronar universidad apunt desde trabajo social 201,amarronar universidad articulo aborda cruce universidad trabajo social argentina propon idea universidad sudaka como proyeccion frente desafi contemporane tal fin presenta genealogia destaca hitos historia universidad argentina termin democratizacion definen categori marron negro sudaka como element epistemic permiten efectuar critic caracter blanco-centrico universidad asimismo registran oper racismo ambito universitario describen aport trabajo social confront esas logic practic racist pro construccion universidad sudaka marron marron negro sudaka trabajo social universidad racismo revista trabajo social vol 28 ene-jun 2026 issn linea 2256-5493 bogota 199-222 amarronar universidad apunt desde trabajo social 201,1.0.0,a541323ead66a773
2256-5493,TAC Rev Tra Social 28_1_V6 (1).pdf,TAC Rev Tra Social 28_1_V6 (1)_7,en,"jo Social, en Argentina,","This article is based on ethnographic research involving Colombian and Spanish Social Work professors, students, and professionals. It was conducted between 2019 and 2024, based on ethnographic work (including interviews and focus groups) that focused on giving prominence to the meanings, points of view, and discourses of social work training among six generations (1950–2000) of participants from Cali, Colombia, and Madrid, Spain. Among the main results is the recognition of the actors who led the processes of university professionalization and institutionalization, with collective action emerging as a central dimension that reshapes the history of the disciplinary field and professional identity. The narratives of the militant experiences of its protagonists during the 1960s, 1970s, and 1980s contribute to the recovery of collective memory, which is to be incorporated into new versions of local disciplinary history, aiming at the recognition of a collective identity linked to political and professional projects that have not necessarily always been conservative",University; Sudaka; Black; Brown; Social Work; Racism,marcadores,jo social en argentina,article based ethnographic research involv colombian spanish social work professor student professional conduct between 2019 2024 based ethnographic work includ interview focu group focus giving prominence meaning point view discours social work train among six gener 1950-2000 participant cali colombia madrid spain among main result recognition actor who led process university professional institutional collective action emerg central dimension reshap history disciplinary field professional identity narrativ militant experienc its protagonist during 1960s 1970s 1980s contribute recovery collective memory which incorporat into new version local disciplinary history aiming recognition collective identity link political professional project have not necessarily alway been conservative,university sudaka black brown social work racism,jo social en argentina article based ethnographic research involv colombian spanish social work professor student professional conduct between 2019 2024 based ethnographic work includ interview focu group focus giving prominence meaning point view discours social work train among six gener 1950-2000 participant cali colombia madrid spain among main result recognition actor who led process university professional institutional collective action emerg central dimension reshap history disciplinary field professional identity narrativ militant experienc its protagonist during 1960s 1970s 1980s contribute recovery collective memory which incorporat into new version local disciplinary history aiming recognition collective identity link political professional project have not necessarily alway been conservative university sudaka black brown social work racism,1.0.0,5f5d7b2e1c409fca
2256-5493,TAC Rev Tra Social 28_1_V6 (1).pdf,TAC Rev Tra Social 28_1_V6 (1)_8,es,"Militancy of Social Work Students,","Este artículo se basa en una investigación etnográfica con docentes, estudiantes y profesionales de Trabajo Social de Colombia y España que se realizó entre 2019 y 2024, otorgando preeminencia a los sentidos, los puntos de vista y los discursos sobre la formación en Trabajo Social con seis generaciones (19502000) de Cali, Colombia, y Madrid, España. Entre los resultados se destacan los reconocimientos a los actores que lideraron los procesos de profesionalización e institucionalización universitaria, emergiendo la acción colectiva como una dimensión central que reconfigura la historia del Trabajo Social. Las narraciones de las experiencias militantes de sus protagonistas durante las décadas de 1960, 1970 y 1980 contribuyen a recuperar las memorias colectivas para ser incorporadas en las historias disciplinares vinculadas a proyectos políticos y profesionales, que no siempre han sido conservadores","Educación Superior; Identidad Cultural; Memoria Colectiva; Movimiento Estudiantil; Movimientos Sociales; Trabajo Social. Revista Trabajo Social vol. 28 n.˚ 1, ene-jun 2026, issn (en línea): 2256-5493, Bogotá · 223-248 Militancia política de estudiantes, docentes y profesionales de Trabajo Social: contribuciones... [ 225 ]",marcadores,militancy of social work students,este articulo basa investigacion etnografica docent estudiant profesional trabajo social colombia espana realizo entre 2019 2024 otorg preeminencia sentid punt vista discurs sobre formacion trabajo social seis gener 19502000 cali colombia madrid espana entre resultad destacan reconoc actor lideraron proces profesionalizacion institucionalizacion universitaria emerg accion colectiva como dimension central reconfigura historia trabajo social narr experienci militant sus protagonist durante decad 1960 1970 1980 contribuyen recuperar memori colectiv ser incorporad histori disciplinar vinculad proyect politic profesional no siempre han sido conservador,educacion superior identidad cultural memoria colectiva movimiento estudiantil movimient social trabajo social revista trabajo social vol 28 ene-jun 2026 issn linea 2256-5493 bogota 223-248 militancia politica estudiant docent profesional trabajo social contribucion 225,militancy of social work students este articulo basa investigacion etnografica docent estudiant profesional trabajo social colombia espana realizo entre 2019 2024 otorg preeminencia sentid punt vista discurs sobre formacion trabajo social seis gener 19502000 cali colombia madrid espana entre resultad destacan reconoc actor lideraron proces profesionalizacion institucionalizacion universitaria emerg accion colectiva como dimension central reconfigura historia trabajo social narr experienci militant sus protagonist durante decad 1960 1970 1980 contribuyen recuperar memori colectiv ser incorporad histori disciplinar vinculad proyect politic profesional no siempre han sido conservador educacion superior identidad cultural memoria colectiva movimiento estudiantil movimient social trabajo social revista trabajo social vol 28 ene-jun 2026 issn linea 2256-5493 bogota 223-248 militancia politica estudiant docent profesional trabajo social contribucion 225,1.0.0,25ca1ed2d60b95b1
2256-5493,TAC Rev Tra Social 28_1_V6 (1).pdf,TAC Rev Tra Social 28_1_V6 (1)_8,en,os resultados se destacan los,"This article is based on ethnographic research involving Colombian and Spanish Social Work professors, students, and professionals. It was conducted between 2019 and 2024, based on ethnographic work (including interviews and focus groups) that focused on giving prominence to the meanings, points of view, and discourses of social work training among six generations (1950–2000) of participants from Cali, Colombia, and Madrid, Spain. Among the main results is the recognition of the actors who led the processes of university professionalization and institutionalization, with collective action emerging as a central dimension that reshapes the history of the disciplinary field and professional identity. The narratives of the militant experiences of its protagonists during the 1960s, 1970s, and 1980s contribute to the recovery of collective memory, which is to be incorporated into new versions of local disciplinary history, aiming at the recognition of a collective identity linked to political and professional projects that have not necessarily always been conservative",Social Work; Cultural Identity; Social Movements; Student Movement; Collective Memory; Higher Education,marcadores,os resultado se destacan los,article based ethnographic research involv colombian spanish social work professor student professional conduct between 2019 2024 based ethnographic work includ interview focu group focus giving prominence meaning point view discours social work train among six gener 1950-2000 participant cali colombia madrid spain among main result recognition actor who led process university professional institutional collective action emerg central dimension reshap history disciplinary field professional identity narrativ militant experienc its protagonist during 1960s 1970s 1980s contribute recovery collective memory which incorporat into new version local disciplinary