2322-9721,"admin,+2+-+14357+-+A+Case.pdf","admin,+2+-+14357+-+A+Case_0",en,ree Finnish pre-service teachers’ emotions and understanding of CLIL during an online practicum. Latin American Journal of Content & Language,"The novel exigencies of the 2020 COVID-19 pandemic caused a shift towards online learning environments and teleconference platforms, which have also affected teaching practicums. The impact of this approach on teacher preparation is yet unknown and may render pre-service teachers (PSTs) more vulnerable to the challenges of early professional learning through practice, especially when implementing a methodology they have been insufficiently introduced to. Following three students of primary teacher education who opted for a practicum in a CLIL class at a Finnish teacher training school, this case study examines how the online practicum affected these PSTs’ emotions and understanding of CLIL. The case study is based on the analytical categories of teacher identity and emotion and draws on essay, diary, and interview data. The thematic analysis of the data suggests that the online practicum met participants’ expectations for building confidence and was perceived as an overall instructive experience, which was improved by the quality of mentorship and peer support they received. However, feelings of frustration or dissatisfaction accompanied moments of conflict with incoming expectations, principally related to using English in CLIL. The analysis further suggests that the online practicum strengthened participants’ earlier conception of CLIL as a language-oriented teaching tool. Regardless of whether online CLIL practicums remain a future option, acquiring disciplinary and language knowledge alike are important aspects in teacher preparation for CLIL, which could be an optional part of teacher education programs for PSTs who are aware of or sensitive to language as a tool for learning",(Source: Unesco Thesaurus): teacher education; Content and Language Integrated Learning; online learning; practicum; student teacher journals,marcadores,ree finnish pre-service teacher emotion understand clil during online practicum latin american journal content language,novel exigenci 2020 covid-19 pandemic caus shift toward online learn environment teleconference platform which have also affect teach practicum impact approach teacher preparation yet unknown may render pre-service teacher psts more vulnerable challeng early professional learn through practice especially when implement methodology they have been insufficiently introduc follow three student primary teacher education who opted practicum clil clas finnish teacher train school case study examin how online practicum affect these psts emotion understand clil case study based analytical categori teacher identity emotion draw essay diary interview data thematic analysi data suggest online practicum met participant expect build confidence perceiv overall instructive experience which improv quality mentorship peer support they receiv however feeling frustration dissatisfaction accompani moment conflict incom expect principally relat using english clil analysi further suggest online practicum strengthen participant earlier conception clil language-orient teach tool regardles whether online clil practicum remain future option acquir disciplinary language knowledge alike important aspect teacher preparation clil which could optional part teacher education program psts who aware sensitive language tool learn,source unesco thesauru teacher education content language integrat learn online learn practicum student teacher journal,ree finnish pre-service teacher emotion understand clil during online practicum latin american journal content language novel exigenci 2020 covid-19 pandemic caus shift toward online learn environment teleconference platform which have also affect teach practicum impact approach teacher preparation yet unknown may render pre-service teacher psts more vulnerable challeng early professional learn through practice especially when implement methodology they have been insufficiently introduc follow three student primary teacher education who opted practicum clil clas finnish teacher train school case study examin how online practicum affect these psts emotion understand clil case study based analytical categori teacher identity emotion draw essay diary interview data thematic analysi data suggest online practicum met participant expect build confidence perceiv overall instructive experience which improv quality mentorship peer support they receiv however feeling frustration dissatisfaction accompani moment conflict incom expect principally relat using english clil analysi further suggest online practicum strengthen participant earlier conception clil language-orient teach tool regardles whether online clil practicum remain future option acquir disciplinary language knowledge alike important aspect teacher preparation clil which could optional part teacher education program psts who aware sensitive language tool learn source unesco thesauru teacher education content language integrat learn online learn practicum student teacher journal,1.0.0,f8cb821fad9bd8a0
2322-9721,"admin,+2+-+14357+-+A+Case.pdf","admin,+2+-+14357+-+A+Case_0",es,"ved as an overall instructive experience, which was improved by the quality of mentorship and peer support they received. However, feelings of frustration or dissatisfaction accompanied","Las nuevas exigencias de la pandemia de la covid-19 de 2020 provocaron un cambio hacia los entornos de aprendizaje en línea y las plataformas de teleconferencia, las cuales también han afectado las prácticas docentes. El impacto de este enfoque en la preparación de los docentes aún se desconoce y puede hacer que los docentes en formación (PST, por sus siglas en inglés) sean más vulnerables a los desafíos del aprendizaje profesional temprano a través de la práctica, especialmente cuando se implementa una metodología con la que no se han familiarizado lo suficiente. En este estudio de caso, se sigue a tres estudiantes de educación primaria que optaron por una práctica en una clase AICLE en una escuela de formación de maestros finlandesa y se examina cómo la práctica en línea afectó las emociones y la comprensión de AICLE de estos PST. El estudio de caso se basa en las categorías analíticas de identidad y emoción del maestro y se basa en datos tomados de una serie de ensayos, diarios y entrevistas. El análisis temático de los datos sugiere que la práctica en línea cumplió con las expectativas de los participantes de generar confianza y se percibió como una experiencia instructiva general, que mejoró gracias a la calidad de la tutoría y el apoyo que recibieron de sus pares. Sin embargo, los sentimientos de frustración o insatisfacción acompañaron los momentos de conflicto con las expectativas entrantes, principalmente relacionados con el uso del inglés en AICLE. El análisis sugiere, además, que la práctica en línea fortaleció la concepción que los participantes tenían anteriormente sobre AICLE como una herramienta de enseñanza orientada al lenguaje. Independientemente de si las prácticas AICLE en línea siguen siendo una opción a futuro, la adquisición de conocimientos tanto disciplinarios como lingüísticos son aspectos importantes en la preparación del profesorado para AICLE, la cual podría ser una parte opcional de los programas de formación do cente para los PST que conocen o son sensibles al lenguaje como herramienta para el aprendizaje",(Fuente: tesauro de la Unesco): formación de docentes; aprendizaje integrado de contenidos y lenguas extranjeras; aprendizaje en línea; prácticum; diarios de estudiantes y profesores,marcadores,ved as an overall instructive experience which was improved by the quality of mentorship and peer support they received however feelings of frustration or dissatisfaction accompanied,nuev exigenci pandemia covid-19 2020 provocaron cambio hacia entorn aprendizaje linea plataform teleconferencia cual tambien han afectado practic docent impacto este enfoque preparacion docent aun desconoce puede hacer docent formacion pst sus sigl ingl sean mas vulnerabl desafi aprendizaje profesional temprano trav practica especial cuando implementa metodologia no han familiarizado suficiente este estudio caso sigue tres estudiant educacion primaria optaron practica clase aicle escuela formacion maestr finlandesa examina como practica linea afecto emocion comprension aicle estos pst estudio caso basa categori analitic identidad emocion maestro basa datos tomad serie ensay diari entrevist analisis tematico datos sugiere practica linea cumplio expectativ participant generar confianza percibio como experiencia instructiva general mejoro graci calidad tutoria apoyo recibieron sus pares sin embargo sent frustracion insatisfaccion acompanaron moment conflicto expectativ entrant principal relacionad uso ingl aicle analisis sugiere adem practica linea fortalecio concepcion participant tenian anterior sobre aicle como herramienta ensenanza orientada lenguaje independiente si practic aicle linea siguen siendo opcion futuro adquisicion conoc tanto disciplinari como linguisti