2322-9721,"admin,+3+-+14815+-+Students’.pdf","admin,+3+-+14815+-+Students’_0",en,Students’ Perceptions on the Use,"The Content and Language Integrated Learning (CLIL) approach has become one of the most frequent teaching options used as a pivotal element of bilingual programs. Over the last two decades, a lot has been written about its characteristics, its potential, and the methodological approaches that should be used to encourage such programs. Since the main objective of CLIL is to improve the use of the foreign language as a vehicle for communication by students when accessing and manipulating content matter, it seems evident that methodological strategies should be promoted to provide the opportunity to maximize the use of the language within the classroom. In this respect, project-based learning (PBL) is depicted, in principle, as an ideal proposal for CLIL, since its implementation will entail an increase in language management. Especially concerning the content, this will result in an improvement in students’ ability to perform more comfortably in school and, presumably, more effectively. Nevertheless, there might not be such a straightforward cause-effect relationship and, therefore, it is necessary to dig deeper into the real impact of using PBL. This study is aimed at analyzing its influence from the students’ point of view, to drill down on their feelings and behavior towards PBL and how they tackle and solve the arising challenges. Results have shown interesting information about their views on the benefits of working by projects but also some concerns regarding the use of this teaching and learning model",(Source: Unesco Thesaurus): project-based learning; content and language integrated learning; learning outcomes; psycho-affective factors; students’ collaboration,marcadores,student perception use,content language integrat learn clil approach has become one most frequent teach option used pivotal element bilingual program over last two decad lot has been written about its characteristic its potential methodological approach should used encourage such program since main objective clil improve use foreign language vehicle communication student when access manipulat content matter seem evident methodological strategi should promot provide opportunity maximize use language within classroom respect project-bas learn pbl depict principle ideal proposal clil since its implementation will entail increase language management especially concern content will result improvement student ability perform more comfortably school presumably more effectively nevertheles there might not such straightforward cause-effect relationship therefore necessary dig deeper into real impact using pbl study aimed analyz its influence student point view drill down their feeling behavior toward pbl how they tackle solve aris challeng result have shown interest information about their view benefit work project but also some concern regard use teach learn model,source unesco thesauru project-bas learn content language integrat learn learn outcom psycho-affective factor student collaboration,student perception use content language integrat learn clil approach has become one most frequent teach option used pivotal element bilingual program over last two decad lot has been written about its characteristic its potential methodological approach should used encourage such program since main objective clil improve use foreign language vehicle communication student when access manipulat content matter seem evident methodological strategi should promot provide opportunity maximize use language within classroom respect project-bas learn pbl depict principle ideal proposal clil since its implementation will entail increase language management especially concern content will result improvement student ability perform more comfortably school presumably more effectively nevertheles there might not such straightforward cause-effect relationship therefore neces