2339-3459,5_124270_Role.pdf,5_124270_Role_0,desconocido,5 124270 Role,"ISSN 1794-6190 e-ISSN 2339-3459 https://doi.org/10.15446/esrj.v30n1.124270 EARTH SCIENCES RESEARCH JOURNAL Earth Sci. Res. J. Vol. 30, No. 1 (March, 2026):53-62 GEOMORPHOLOGY Role of Textural Heterogeneity in Controlling the Geotechnical Properties of the Amb Formation, Upper Indus Basin, Pakistan Subhan Ullah1, Fahad Said1, Muhammad Rizwan2, Muhammad Ibrar1, Abdul Rahim Asif 3,4*, Maaz Ullah1, Umair Mussawar5, Mushtaq Ahmad1, Abbas Khan1, Amjad Ali1 1. Department of Geology, University of Swat, Swat 19120, Pakistan 2. State Key Laboratory of Continental Evolution and Early Life, Department of Geology, Northwest University, Xi’an-710069, China 3. National Centre of Excellence in Geology, University of Peshawar, Peshawar, Pakistan 4. Department of Earth Sciences, FATA University, FR Kohat 26100, Pakistan 5. School of Sciences, University of Wollongong, Wollongong, Australia Corresponding Author: abdulrahimasif@uop.edu.pk ABSTRACT RESUMEN Esta investigación examina las propiedades petrográficas y geotécnicas de la Formación Amb (FA) del Pérmico. El análisis petrográfico revela tres microfacies distintas de caliza: wacke-packstone bioclástico siliciclástico (AL) en la sección inferior, packstone bioclástico siliciclástico (AM) en la sección media y grainstone bioclástico (AU) en la sección superior. La microfacies AL se caracteriza por un empaque deficiente y un alto contenido de matriz, mientras que AM presenta un empaque moderado con menor contenido de matriz y mejor interacci",,respaldo_sin_marcadores,124270 role,issn 1794-6190 e-issn 2339-3459 http doi org 10 15446 esrj v30n1 124270 earth scienc research journal earth sci res vol 30 no march 2026 53-62 geomorphology role textural heterogeneity controll geotechnical properti amb formation upper indu basin pakistan subhan ullah1 fahad said1 muhammad rizwan2 muhammad ibrar1 abdul rahim asif maaz ullah1 umair mussawar5 mushtaq ahmad1 abba khan1 amjad ali1 department geology university swat swat 19120 pakistan state key laboratory continental evolution early life department geology northwest university xi an-710069 china national centre excellence geology university peshawar peshawar pakistan department earth scienc fata university fr kohat 26100 pakistan school scienc university wollongong wollongong australia correspond author abdulrahimasif uop edu pk abstract resumen esta investigacion examina propiedad petrografic geotecnic formacion amb fa permico analisi petrografico revela tres microfaci distint caliza wacke-packstone bioclastico siliciclastico seccion inferior packstone bioclastico siliciclastico am seccion media grainstone bioclastico au seccion superior microfaci caracteriza empaque deficiente alto contenido matriz mientr am presenta empaque moderado menor contenido matriz mejor interacci,,124270 role issn 1794-6190 e-issn 2339-3459 http doi org 10 15446 esrj v30n1 124270 earth scienc research journal earth sci res vol 30 no march 2026 53-62 geomorphology role textural heterogeneity controll geotechnical properti amb formation upper indu basin pakistan subhan ullah1 fahad said1 muhammad rizwan2 muhammad ibrar1 abdul rahim asif maaz ullah1 umair mussawar5 mushtaq ahmad1 abba khan1 amjad ali1 department geology university swat swat 19120 pakistan state key laboratory continental evolution early life department geology northwest university xi an-710069 china national centre excellence geology university peshawar peshawar pakistan department earth scienc fata university fr kohat 26100 pakistan school scienc university wollongong wollongong australia correspond author abdulrahimasif uop edu pk abstract resumen esta investigacion examina propiedad petrografic geotecnic formacion amb fa permico analisi petrografico revela tres microfaci distint caliza wacke-packstone bioclastico siliciclastico seccion inferior packstone bioclastico siliciclastico am seccion media grainstone bioclastico au seccion superior m