colectaron mediante google forms analizaron estadistica descriptiva excel estudio fue clasificado como riesgo minimo segun resolucion 8430 1993 resultad 96 participant afirmo conocer resolucion 3280 2018 pero solo 76 aplica practica observaron debilidad fundacion universitaria area andina pereira risaralda colombia orcid https orcid org 0009-0000-6526-2982 correo sbarbsa estudiat areandina edu co fundacion universitaria area andina pereira risaralda colombia orcid https orcid org 0009-0001-1306-2740 correo kvalderrama estudiat areandina edu co fundacion universitaria area andina pereira risaralda colombia orcid https orcid org 0000-0001-5323-6445 correo crivera16 areandina edu co fundacion universitaria area andina pereira risaralda colombia orcid https orcid org 0000-0002-2677-7171 correo dcarmona areandina edu co archiv medicina barbosa torr valderrama sanchez rivera molano carmona carmona conocimiento medic general sobre ruta cuidado visual infantil segun resolucion 3280 2018 risaralda colombia arch med manizal 2026 26 aspect tecnic como tamizaje visual 44 reflejo rojo 52 solo 48 realiza historia clinica ocular completa conclusion aunque existe alto nivel conocimiento general persisten vaci aplicacion practica recomienda implementar estrategi educativ andragogic como casos clinic infografi mejorar atencion visual infantil prueb vision salud ocular prevencion promocion salud knowledge of general practitioners about the child visual care pathway according to resolution 3280 of 2018 in risaralda colombia,1.0.0,f34476ea65394a04
2339-3874,Investigación-5387.pdf,Investigación-5387_0,en,% realiza historia clínica ocular completa. Conclusión: aunque existe un alto nivel,"Introduction: visual health during the early years of life is essential for a child’s overall development, as it influences learning, socialization, and environmental exploration. In Colombia, Resolution 3280 of 2018 established the Comprehensive Health Care Routes (RIAS), including specific actions for visual care from early childhood, with the goal of ensuring early detection of visual impairments. Objective: to evaluate the level of knowledge and practice of general practitioners regarding the visual care pathway for early childhood, according to Resolution 3280 of 2018, in a State Social Enterprise (ESE) in Risaralda during the first semester of 2025. Materials and methods: a cross-sectional descriptive study was conducted in a Risaralda ESE with 25 general practitioners. A KAP-type questionnaire, validated by experts, was used and applied by health audit students. Data was collected through Google Forms and analyzed using descriptive statistics in Excel. The study was classified as minimal risk according to Resolution 8430 of 1993. Results: 96 % of participants reported being familiar with Resolution 3280 of 2018, but only 76 % apply it in their clinical practice. Technical weaknesses were observed in areas such as visual screening (44 %) and the red reflex test (52 %). Only 48 % reported performing a complete ocular history. Conclusion: although there is a high level of general knowledge, gaps remain in practical application. It is recommended to implement andragogical educational strategies, such as clinical case studies and infographics, to improve pediatric visual care",vision tests; eye health; prevention; and health promotion,marcadores,realiza historia clinica ocular completa conclusion aunque existe un alto nivel,introduction visual health during early year life essential child overall development influenc learn social environmental exploration colombia resolution 3280 2018 establish comprehensive health care rout rias includ specific action visual care early childhood goal ensur early detection visual impairment objective evaluate level knowledge practice general practitioner regard visual care pathway early childhood accord resolution 3280 2018 state social enterprise ese risaralda during first semester 2025 material method cross-sectional descriptive study conduct risaralda ese 25 general practitioner kap-type questionnaire validat expert used appli health audit student data collect through google form analyz using descriptive statistic excel study classifi minimal risk accord resolution 8430 1993 result 96 participant report being familiar resolution 3280 2018 but only 76 apply their clinical practice technical weakness observ area such visual screen 44 red reflex test 52 only 48 report perform complete ocular history conclusion although there high level general knowledge gaps remain practical application recommend implement andragogical educational strategi such clinical case studi infographic improve pediatric visual care,vision test eye health prevention health promotion,realiza historia clinica ocular completa conclusion aunque existe un alto nivel introduction visual health during early year life essential child overall development influenc learn social environmental exploration colombia resolution 3280 2018 establish comprehensive health care rout rias includ specific action visual care early childhood goal ensur early detection visual impairment objective evaluate level knowledge practice general practitioner regard visual care pathway early childhood accord resolution 3280 2018 state social enterprise ese risaralda during first semester 2025 material method cross-sectional descriptive study conduct risaralda ese 25 general practitioner kap-type questionnaire validat expert used appli health audit student data collect through google form analyz using descriptive statistic excel study classifi minimal risk accord resolution 8430 1993 result 96 participant report being familiar resolution 3280 2018 but only 76 apply their clinical practice technical weakness observ area such visual screen 44 red reflex test 52 only 48 report perform complete ocular history conclusion although there high level general knowledge gaps remain practical application recommend implement andragogical educational strategi such clinical case studi infographic improve pediatric visual care vision test eye health prevention health promotion,1.0.0,0b533c38617f1b92
2344-7214,1316-110-PB.pdf,1316-110-PB_0,en,PhD. Jimmy Alexander Cortes Osorio,"— Applying the methodology NTP-ISO 9612-2010 which establishes standardized procedures to evaluate exposure to noise at work, on the other hand the WHO recommends maintaining noise around 65 dB in a work environment, the research is based on the evaluation of noise levels generated by various equipment used in the area of maestranza in a metalworking company, for the measurement stage noise measurements were made for 3 days in five areas of maestranza with 30 results which at 1 point the measurement showed that on average there was 0. For the control stage, a test of averages was performed using the values used with personal protective equipment and thus decreasing the noise level, which showed that the decrease in the point was significant, however the lack of proper management of these noise levels could lead to occupational diseases, whose long-term effects could cause an irreversible impact on the health of workers. Numerous authors have used normative calculations to gather data on occupational noise in different work areas",maximum permissible limits; metalworking; occupational healt; occupational noise,marcadores,phd jimmy alexander cort osorio,-- apply methodology ntp-iso 9612-2010 which establish standardiz procedur evaluate exposure noise work other hand who recommend maintain noise around 65 db work environment research based evaluation noise level generat variou equipment used area maestranza metalwork company measurement stage noise measurement made days five area maestranza 30 result which point measurement show average there control stage test averag perform using valu used personal protective equipment thus decreas noise level which show decrease point significant however lack proper management these noise level could lead occupational diseas whose long-term effect could cause irreversible impact health worker numerou author have used normative calcul gather data occupational noise different work area,maximum permissible limit metalwork occupational healt occupational noise,phd jimmy alexander cort osorio -- apply methodology ntp-iso 9612-2010 which establish standardiz procedur evaluate exposure noise work other hand who recommend maintain noise around 65 db work environment research based evaluation noise level generat variou equipment used area maestranza metalwork company measurement stage noise measurement made days five area maestranza 30 result which point measurement show average there control stage test averag perform using valu used personal protective equipment thus decreas noise level which show decrease point significant however lack proper management these noise level could lead occupational diseas whose long-term effect could cause irreversible impact health worker numerou author have used normative calcul gather data occupational noise different work area maximum permissible limit metalwork occupational healt occupational noise,1.0.0,4d76d5d1fb0127c3
2344-7214,1316-110-PB.pdf,1316-110-PB_0,es,noise levels generated by,"— Aplicando la metodología NTP-ISO 9612-2010 el cual establece procedimientos estandarizados para evaluar la exposición al ruido en el trabajo , por otro lado la OMS recomienda mantener ruido alrededor de 65 dB en un ambiente laboral, la investigación fundamenta en la evaluación de los niveles de ruido generados por diversos equipos utilizados en el área de maestranza en una empresa metalmecánica , para la etapa de medición se realizaron las mediciones de ruido durante 3 días en cinco áreas de maestranza con 30 resultados los cuales en 1 punto la medición arrojo que en promedio hubo 0.5 puntos con nivel de ruido superior a lo permitido por la norma , para la etapa de control se realizó una prueba de medias utilizando los valores usados con equipos de protección personal así disminuyendo el nivel de ruido , la cual mostró que la disminución en el punto fue significativa, no obstante la falta de manejo adecuado de estos niveles de ruido podría dar lugar a enfermedades ocupacionales, cuyos efectos a largo plazo podrían causar un impacto irreversible en la salud de los trabajadores. Este manuscrito fue recibido el 06 de Agosto, 2025. Fue aceptado el 06 de Marzo de, 2025 y publicado el 19 de Diciembre de 2025. Fabrizio M. Márquez es un estudiante de la carrera profesional de Ingeniería de Seguridad Industrial y Minera de la Universidad Tecnológica del Perú, Arequipa, Perú (email: fjcmanrique@gmail.com) Tania C. Apaza es un estudiante de la carrera profesional de Ingeniería de Seguridad Industrial y Minera de la Universidad Tecnológica del Perú, Arequipa, Perú (e-mail: melcua.mt@gmail.com) Numerosos autores han utilizado cálculos normativos para reunir datos sobre el ruido ocupacional en diferentes áreas laborales",Límites máximos permisibles; metalmecánica; ruido ocupacional; salud laboral. I,marcadores,noise levels generated by,-- aplic metodologia ntp-iso 9612-2010 cual establece proced estandarizad 