2344-8350,RC52-3-23436.pdf,RC52-3-23436_0,es,Prototipo de bicicleta estática generadora de electricidad para centros,"Esta investigación propone una alternativa educativa orientada a promover el uso de energías renovables no convencionales y buenas prácticas de consumo eléctrico. Para ello, se diseñó y fabricó un prototipo de bicicleta estática generadora de electricidad para su implementación en centros deportivos. El dispositivo genera un nivel de tensión máximo de 12 V, lo cual permite alimentar cargas de baja potencia, tales como cargadores de dispositivos móviles e iluminación LED. Con el fin de medir el impacto del prototipo, se aplicaron encuestas para identificar el interés de los usuarios en la eficiencia energética. Como resultado principal, se destaca que la totalidad de los participantes manifestó interés en métodos de autogeneración tras el uso del prototipo; asimismo, la vinculación del esfuerzo físico con la producción eléctrica fomentó la concienciación sobre el uso responsable de la energía. El prototipo destaca por su bajo costo, facilidad de operación y contribución al bienestar ambiental y social, lo que lo posiciona como una alternativa viable y ecológica en entornos recreativos. Finalmente, se subraya la relevancia de estas iniciativas para fomentar la sostenibilidad entre los usuarios","bicicleta estática, educación, energías renovables, generación eléctrica, prototipo. Artículo de revisión Prototipo de bicicleta estática generadora de electricidad para centros deportivos: promoción de energías renovables y eficiencia energética Ponce-León, A. A. Revista Científica • ISSN 0124-2253 • e-ISSN 2344-8350 • septiembre-diciembre 2025 • Bogotá-Colombia • N. 52(3) • pp. -78 [ 63 ] Abstr",marcadores,prototipo bicicleta estatica generadora electricidad centr,esta investigacion propone alternativa educativa orientada promover uso energi renovabl no convencional buen practic consumo electrico ello diseno fabrico prototipo bicicleta estatica generadora electricidad implementacion centr deportiv dispositivo genera nivel tension maximo 12 cual permite alimentar carg baja potencia tales como cargador dispositiv movil iluminacion led fin medir impacto prototipo aplicaron encuest identificar inter usuari eficiencia energetica como resultado principal destaca totalidad participant manifesto inter metod autogeneracion tras uso prototipo asimismo vinculacion esfuerzo fisico produccion electrica fomento concienciacion sobre uso responsable energia prototipo destaca bajo costo facilidad operacion contribucion bienestar ambiental social posiciona como alternativa viable ecologica entorn recreativ final subraya relevancia estas iniciativ fomentar sostenibilidad entre usuari,bicicleta estatica educacion energi renovabl generacion electrica prototipo articulo revision prototipo bicicleta estatica generadora electricidad centr deportiv promocion energi renovabl eficiencia energetica ponce-leon revista cientifica issn 0124-2253 e-issn 2344-8350 septiembre-diciembre 2025 bogota-colombia 52 pp -78 63 abstr,prototipo bicicleta estatica generadora electricidad centr esta investigacion propone alternativa educativa orientada promover uso energi renovabl no convencional buen practic consumo electrico ello diseno fabrico prototipo bicicleta estatica generadora electricidad implementacion centr deportiv dispositivo genera nivel tension maximo 12 cual permite alimentar carg baja potencia tales como cargador dispositiv movil iluminacion led fin medir impacto prototipo aplicaron encuest identificar inter usuari eficiencia energetica como resultado principal destaca totalidad participant manifesto inter metod autogeneracion tras uso prototipo asimismo vinculacion esfuerzo fisico produccion electrica fomento concienciacion sobre uso responsable energia prototipo destaca bajo costo facilidad operacion contribucion bienestar ambiental social posiciona como alternativa viable ecologica entorn recreativ final subraya relevancia estas iniciativ fomentar sostenibilidad entre usuari bicicleta estatica educacion energi renovabl generacion electrica prototipo articulo revision prototipo bicicleta estatica generadora electricidad centr deportiv promocion energi renovabl eficiencia energetica ponce-leon revista cientifica issn 0124-2253 e-issn 2344-8350 septiembre-diciembre 2025 bogota-colombia 52 pp -78 63 abstr,1.0.0,d54e1a2dc8521557
2344-8350,RC52-3-23436.pdf,RC52-3-23436_0,en,"utogeneración tras el uso del prototipo; asimismo,","This research seeks an education alternative focused on promoting the use of renewable and non-conventional energy sources and good electricity consumption practices. To this end, a prototype of a stationary bicycle that generates electricity was designed and manufactured for use in sports centers. The prototype generates a maximum voltage of 12 volts. This voltage level allows for the power supply of small loads such as cell phone chargers and LED lighting. Surveys were used to measure the impact of this prototype, seeking to demonstrate users' interest in renewable energy and energy efficiency. The main result is that all users, after using this prototype, became interested in selfgeneration methods and in linking their physical effort with electricity production, which helped raise awareness about responsible energy use. The prototype stands out for its low cost, ease of use, and its ability to contribute to environmental and social well-being, making it a viable and environmentally friendly alternative for sports and recreational spaces. It also highlights the importance of this type of initiative in promoting sustainable practices and ecological awareness among users","Stationary Bike, Education, Renewable Energy, Electricity Generation, Prototype",marcadores,utogeneracion tras el uso del prototipo asimismo,research seek education alternative focus promot use renewable non-conventional energy sourc good electricity consumption practic end prototype stationary bicycle generat electricity design manufactur use sport center prototype generat maximum voltage 12 volt voltage level allow power supply small load such cell phone charger led light survey used measure impact prototype seek demonstrate user interest renewable energy energy efficiency main result all user after using prototype became interest selfgeneration method link their physical effort electricity production which help raise awarenes about responsible energy use prototype stand out its low cost ease use its ability contribute environmental social well-be making viable environmentally friendly alternative sport recreational spac also highlight importance type initiative promot sustainable practic ecological awarenes among user,stationary bike education renewable energy electricity generation prototype,utogeneracion tras el uso del prototipo asimismo research seek education alternative focus promot use renewable non-conventional energy sourc good electricity consumption practic end prototype stationary bicycle generat electricity design manufactur use sport center prototype generat maximum voltage 12 volt voltage level allow power supply small load such cell phone charger led light survey used measure impact prototype seek demonstrate user interest renewable energy energy efficiency main result all user after using prototype became interest selfgeneration method link their physical effort electricity production which help raise awarenes about responsible energy use prototype stand out its low cost ease use its ability contribute environmental social well-be making viable environmentally friendly alternative sport recreational spac also highlight importance type initiative promot sustainable practic ecological awarenes among user stationary bike education renewable energy electricity generation prototype,1.0.0,b43efcf52755dbe6
2344-8350,RC52-3-23926.pdf,RC52-3-23926_0,en,hanesulfonyl)imide Electrolytes Based on,"In this work, biopolymer electrolyte membranes based on rice starch and CF3SO2NLiSO2CF3 (LiTFSI) were prepared via the solution casting method and characterized by impedance spectroscopy (IS), differential scanning calorimetry (DSC), and cyclic voltammetry (CV). The graphs of the ionic conductivity logarithm as a function of the inverse of the temperature exhibit an Arrhenius behavior, which indicates a thermally activated conduction process, while the DSC results reveal a step-shaped anomaly associated with the glass transition temperature (Tg) of a new polymer complex. The cyclic voltammetry analysis suggests a qualitative electrochemical stability range between -2.5 and +2.5 V. At room temperature, the highest ionic conductivity obtained was higher than 9 × 10⁻³ S·cm⁻¹ for the membrane containing 50 wt.% LiTFSI. Despite the notable enhancement in ionic conductivity, membranes with higher salt content exhibit reduced mechanical robustness and may be affected by residual moisture. These findings highlight the potential of rice starch-LiTFSI systems as promising candidates for future electrochemical devices, although further optimizations are required, such as mechanical reinforcement and more detailed stability assessments for practical implementation","polymer electrolytes, ionic conductivity, biopolymers, starch, impedance spectroscopy Artículo de investigación científica New Lithium Bis(trifluoromethanesulfonyl)imide Electrolytes Based on Rice Starch Delgado, M. I., Jurado, N. M., y Uribe, R. Revista Científica • ISSN 0124-2253 • e-ISSN 2344-8350 • septiembre-diciembre 2025 • Bogotá-Colombia • N. 52(3) • pp. 25-39 [ 26 ]",marcadores,hanesulfonyl imide electrolyt based,work biopolymer electrolyte membran based rice starch cf3so2nliso2cf3 litfsi prepar via solution cast method characteriz impedance spectroscopy differential scann calorimetry dsc cyclic voltammetry cv graph ionic conductivity logarithm function inverse temperature exhibit arrheniu behavior which indicat thermally activat conduction proces while dsc result reveal step-shap anomaly associat glas transition temperature tg new polymer complex cyclic voltammetry analysi suggest qualitative electrochemical stability range between -2 room temperature highest ionic conductivity obtain higher than 10-3 cm-1 membrane contain 50 wt litfsi despite notable enhancement ionic conductivity membran higher salt content exhibit reduc mechanical robustnes may affect residual moisture these finding highlight potential rice starch-litfsi system promis candidat future electrochemical devic although further optimiz requir such mechanical reinforcement more detail stability assessment practical implementation,polymer electrolyt ionic conductivity biopolymer starch impedance spectroscopy articulo de investigacion cientifica new lithium bis trifluoromethanesulfonyl imide electrolyt based rice starch delgado jurado uribe revista cientifica issn 0124-2253 e-issn 2344-8350 septiembre-diciembre 2025 bogota-colombia 52 pp 25-39 26,hanesulfonyl imide electrolyt based work biopolymer electrolyte membran based rice starch cf3so2nliso2cf3 litfsi prepar via solution cast method characteriz impedance spectroscopy differential scann calorimetry dsc cyclic voltammetry cv graph ionic conductivity logarithm function inverse temperature exhibit arrheniu behavior which indicat thermally activat conduction proces while dsc result reveal step-shap anomaly associat glas transition temperature tg new polymer complex cyclic voltammetry analysi suggest qualitative electrochemical stability range between -2 room temperature highest ionic conductivity obtain higher than 10-3 cm-1 membrane contain 50 wt litfsi despite notable enhancement ionic conductivity membran higher salt content exhibit reduc mechanical robustnes may affect residual moisture these finding highlight potential rice starch-litfsi system promis candidat future electrochemical devic although further optimiz requir such mechanical reinforcement more detail stability assessment practical implementation polymer electrolyt ionic conductivity biopolymer starch impedance spectroscopy articulo de investigacion cientifica new lithium bis trifluoromethanesulfonyl imide electrolyt based rice starch delgado jurado uribe revista cientifica issn 0124-2253 e-issn 2344-8350 septiembre-diciembre 2025 bogota-colombia 52 pp 25-39 26,1.0.0,81ff6c94e63302b2
2344-8350,RC52-3-23926.pdf,RC52-3-23926_0,es,"S·cm⁻¹ for the membrane containing 50 wt.% LiTFSI. Despite the notable enhancement in ionic conductivity,","En este trabajo se prepararon membranas de electrolito biopolimérico a base de almidón de arroz y CF3SO2NLiSO2CF3 (LiTFSI) mediante el método de solución y se caracterizaron mediante espectroscopía de impedancia (IS), calorimetría diferencial de barrido (DSC) y voltametría cíclica (CV). Las gráficas del logaritmo de la conductividad iónica en función del inverso de la temperatura se ajustan a un modelo de tipo Arrhenius, lo que indica un proceso de conducción térmicamente activado, mientras los resultados de DSC revelaron una anomalía en forma de escalón asociada a la temperatura de transición vítrea (Tg) de un nuevo complejo polimérico. El análisis de voltametría cíclica sugiere un rango cualitativo de estabilidad electroquímica entre -2.5 V y +2.5 V. A temperatura ambiente, la mayor conductividad iónica obtenida fue superior a 9 × 10⁻³ S·cm⁻¹ para la membrana con 50 wt.% LiTFSI. A pesar del notable incremento en la conductividad iónica, las membranas con mayor contenido de sal presentan una menor robustez mecánica y pueden verse afectadas por la humedad residual. Estos resultados destacan el potencial de los sistemas almidón de arroz-LiTFSI como candidatos prometedores para futuros dispositivos electroquímicos, si bien se requieren optimizaciones adicionales, como el refuerzo mecánico y evaluaciones más detalladas de estabilidad para su implementación práctica","electrolitos poliméricos, conductividad iónica, biopolímeros, almidón, impedancia, espectroscopía",marcadores,cm-1 for the membrane containing 50 wt litfsi despite the notable enhancement in ionic conductivity,este trabajo prepararon membran electrolito biopolimerico base almidon arroz cf3so2nliso2cf3 litfsi mediante metodo solucion caracterizaron mediante espectroscopia impedancia is calorimetria diferencial barrido dsc voltametria ciclica cv grafic logaritmo conductividad ionica funcion inverso temperatura ajustan modelo tipo arrhenius indica proceso conduccion termica activado mientr resultad dsc revelaron anomalia forma escalon asociada temperatura transicion vitrea tg nuevo complejo polimerico analisis voltametria ciclica sugiere rango cualitativo estabilidad electroquimica entre -2 temperatura ambiente mayor conductividad ionica obtenida fue superior 10-3 cm-1 membrana 50 wt litfsi pesar notable incremento conductividad ionica membran mayor contenido sal presentan menor robustez mecanica pueden verse afectad humedad residual estos resultad destacan potencial sistem almidon arroz-litfsi como candidat prometedor futur dispositiv electroquimic si bien requieren optimiz adicional como refuerzo mecanico evalu mas detallad estabilidad implementacion practica,electrolit polimeric conductividad ionica biopolimer almidon impedancia espectroscopia,cm-1 for the membrane containing 50 wt litfsi despite the notable enhancement in ionic conductivity este trabajo prepararon membran electrolito biopolimerico base almidon arroz cf3so2nliso2cf3 litfsi mediante metodo solucion caracterizaron mediante espectroscopia impedancia is calorimetria diferencial barrido dsc voltametria ciclica cv grafic logaritmo conductividad ionica funcion inverso temperatura ajustan modelo tipo arrhenius indica proceso conduccion termica activado mientr resultad dsc revelaron anomalia forma escalon asociada temperatura transicion vitrea tg nuevo complejo polimerico analisis voltametria ciclica sugiere rango cualitativo estabilidad electroquimica entre -2 temperatura ambiente mayor conductividad ionica obtenida fue superior 10-3 cm-1 membrana 50 wt litfsi pesar notable incremento conductividad ionica membran mayor contenido sal presentan menor robustez mecanica pueden verse afectad humedad residual estos resultad destacan potencial sistem almidon arroz-litfsi como candidat prometedor futur dispositiv electroquimic si bien requieren optimiz adicional como refuerzo mecanico evalu mas detallad estabilidad implementacion practica electrolit polimeric conductividad ionica biopolimer almidon impedancia espectroscopia,1.0.0,8a68e9c69d1af41e
2344-8350,RC52-3-ed.pdf,RC52-3-ed_0,desconocido,RC52-3-ed,"http://revistas.udistrital.edu.co/ojs/index.php/revcie/index Revista Científica • ISSN 0124-2253 • e-ISSN 2344-8350 • septiembre-diciembre 2025 • Bogotá-Colombia • N. 52(3) Editorial AI in Healthcare: Augmenting Care, Preserving Humanity Kiran Puttegowda 1 Hector Florez 2 Medicine is based on human expertise, experiential learning, and ethical judgment. Howe ver, in recent years, it has been supported by algorithms capable of analyzing large amounts of data with high speed and precision. While these technologies offer efficiency, accuracy, and accessibility, they also raise questions about trust, equity, and the role of healthcare professionals. Artificial intelligence (AI) systems—specifically systems that operate on machine and deep learning platforms—are good at recognizing patterns in large datasets, but they do not pos sess inherent and actionable knowledge. This contrast brings a root cause of tension into the limelight: the need to incorporate algorithmic intelligence into the sphere, where human ju dgment cannot and will never be dispensed with. The new achievements of medical AI have been impressive. Deep networks are currently competitive or even superior to human profes sionals in applications like tumor detection in radiological images, the detection of diabetic retinopathy in retina scans, and the detection of cardiac abnormalities in electrocardiograms. Large language models (LLMs) can be helpful to clinicians by summarizing patient records, writing discharge no",,respaldo_sin_marcadores,rc52-3-ed,http revist udistrital edu co ojs index php revcie index revista cientifica issn 0124-2253 e-issn 2344-8350 septiembre-diciembre 2025 bogota-colombia 52 editorial ai healthcare augment care preserv humanity kiran puttegowda hector florez medicine based human expertise experiential learn ethical judgment howe ver recent year has been support algorithm capable analyz large amount data high speed precision while these technologi offer efficiency accuracy accessibility they also raise question about trust equity role healthcare professional artificial intelligence ai systems--specifically system operate machine deep learn platforms--are good recogniz pattern large dataset but they do not pos sess inherent actionable knowledge contrast bring root cause tension into limelight need incorporate algorithmic intelligence into sphere where human ju dgment cannot will never dispens new achievement medical ai have been impressive deep network currently competitive even superior human prof sional applic like tumor detection radiological imag detection diabetic retinopathy retina scan detection cardiac abnormaliti electrocardiogram large language model llms can helpful clinician summariz patient record writ discharge no,,rc52-3-ed http revist udistrital edu co ojs index php revcie index revista cientifica issn 0124-2253 e-issn 2344-8350 septiembre-diciembre 2025 bogota-colombia 52 editorial ai healthcare augment care preserv humanity kiran puttegowda hector florez medicine based human expertise experiential learn ethical judgment howe ver recent year has been support algorithm capable analyz large amount data high speed precision while these technologi offer efficiency accuracy accessibility they also raise question about trust equity role healthcare professional artificial intelligence ai systems--specifically system operate machine deep learn platforms--are good recogniz pattern large dataset but they do not pos sess inherent actionable knowledge contrast bring root cause tension into limelight need incorporate algorithmic intelligence into sphere where human ju dgment cannot will never dispens new achievement medical ai have been impressive deep network currently competitive even superior human prof sional applic like tumor detection radiological imag detection diabetic retinopathy retina scan detection cardiac abnormaliti electrocardiogram large language model llms can helpful clinician summariz patient record writ discharge no,1.0.0,f1242df7dc8aec69
2344-8350,RC53-1-24600.pdf,RC53-1-24600_0,en,"Para citar este artículo: Valdés-Souto, F., Richard-Ramírez, D., Domínguez-Valenzuela, E., Rodríguez-Flores,","Recent advances in language models and retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) systems have highlighted the importance of optimizing parameters such as chunk size and overlap when vectorizing unstructured data for efficient information retrieval. This study explores the impact of varying chunking configurations on the performance of a RAG system designed to answer queries regarding the Regulations of the Social Service of the Faculty of Science at UNAM. Using N8N as the integration platform and OpenAI’s gpt-4o-mini as the LLM tool, different chunking strategies were evaluated based on four key metrics: correctness, semantic similarity, context relevance, and answer relevance. The results suggest that, while the overall performance differences between chunking strategies were not statistically significant, variations in chunk size and overlap can influence the consistency and quality of responses, particularly regarding answer relevance. These findings offer practical guidelines for optimizing chunking parameters in a RAG system for retrieving information from regulations documents, in order to enhance retrieval accuracy and response reliability","artificial intelligence, retrieval-augmented generation, large language models, information retrieval, document vectorization, AI agent automation Artículo de revisión Analysis of Chunk Size and Overlap in Optimizing Vector Databases for AI Agent Automation Valdés-Souto, F., Richard-Ramírez, D., Domínguez-Valenzuela, E., Rodríguez-Flores, M. y Mejía-Bautista, N. E. Revista Científica • ISSN 0124",marcadores,para citar este articulo valdes-souto richard-ramirez dominguez-valenzuela rodriguez-flor,recent advanc language model retrieval-augment generation rag system have highlight importance optimiz parameter such chunk size overlap when vectoriz unstructur data efficient information retrieval study explor impact vary chunk configur performance rag system design answer queri regard regul social service faculty science unam using n8n integration platform openai gpt-4o-mini llm tool different chunk strategi evaluat based four key metric correctnes semantic similarity context relevance answer relevance result suggest while overall performance differenc between chunk strategi not statistically significant vari chunk size overlap can influence consistency quality respons particularly regard answer relevance these finding offer practical guidelin optimiz chunk parameter rag system retriev information regul document order enhance retrieval accuracy response reliability,artificial intelligence retrieval-augment generation large language model information retrieval document vector ai agent automation articulo de revision analysi chunk size overlap optimiz vector databas ai agent automation valdes-souto richard-ramirez dominguez-valenzuela rodriguez-flor mejia-bautista revista cientifica issn 0124,para citar este articulo valdes-souto richard-ramirez dominguez-valenzuela rodriguez-flor recent advanc language model retrieval-augment generation rag system have highlight importance optimiz parameter such chunk size overlap when vectoriz unstructur data efficient information retrieval study explor impact vary chunk configur performance rag system design answer queri regard regul social service faculty science unam using n8n integration platform openai gpt-4o-mini llm tool different chunk strategi evaluat based four key metric correctnes semantic similarity context relevance answer relevance result suggest while overall performance differenc between chunk strategi not statistically significant vari chunk size overlap can influence consistency quality respons particularly regard answer relevance these finding offer practical guidelin optimiz chunk parameter rag system retriev information regul document order enhance retrieval accuracy response reliability artificial intelligence retrieval-augment generation large language model information retrieval document vector ai agent automation articulo de revision analysi chunk size overlap optimiz vector databas ai agent automation valdes-souto richard-ramirez dominguez-valenzuela rodriguez-flor mejia-bautista revista cientifica issn 0124,1.0.0,77f4d65a67dfe366
2344-8350,RC53-1-24600.pdf,RC53-1-24600_0,es,"were not statistically significant, variations in chunk size and overlap can influence the consistency and quality","Los avances recientes en modelos de lenguaje y sistemas de generación aumentada por recuperación (RAG) han destacado la importancia de optimizar parámetros como el tamaño de los fragmentos y su solapamiento al vectorizar datos no estructurados para una recuperación de información eficiente. Este estudio explora el impacto de diferentes configuraciones de fragmentación en el rendimiento de un sistema RAG diseñado para responder consultas sobre el Reglamento del Servicio Social de la Facultad de Ciencias de la UNAM. Utilizando N8N como plataforma de integración y OPENAI gpt-4o-mini como herramienta de LLM, se evaluaron diferentes estrategias de fragmentación con base en cuatro métricas clave: corrección, similitud semántica, relevancia del contexto y relevancia de la respuesta. Los resultados sugieren que, si bien las diferencias generales de rendimiento entre las estrategias de fragmentación no fueron estadísticamente significativas, las variaciones en el tamaño de los fragmentos y su solapamiento pueden influir en la consistencia y calidad de las respuestas, particularmente en lo que respecta a la relevancia de la respuesta. Estos hallazgos ofrecen lineamientos prácticos para optimizar los parámetros de fragmentación en un sistema RAG destinado a recuperar información de documentos reglamentarios, con el fin de mejorar la precisión de la recuperación y la confiabilidad de las respuestas","inteligencia artificial, generación aumentada por recuperación, modelos de lenguaje a gran escala, recuperación de información, vectorización de documentos, automatización de agentes de IA",marcadores,were not statistically significant variations in chunk size and overlap can influence the consistency and quality,avanc recient model lenguaje sistem generacion aumentada recuperacion rag han destacado importancia optimizar 