2346-0806,sph03-e1513+(3).pdf,sph03-e1513+(3)_0,en,Introducción: el rendimiento académico en áreas críticas como las matemáticas es el foco de este artículo.,"Introduction: Academic performance in critical areas such as mathematics is the focus of this article. Objective: To identify the sociodemographic and institutional factors that influence the performance of engineering students in the subject of Differential Calculus. Materials and methods: A quantitative, descriptive, and correlational study was conducted, analyzing students' prior academic data and living conditions. Results: A strong correlation was revealed between the type of school attended, results on Sophia Recibido: 01/02/2025-Aceptado: 30/01/2026-Publicado: 25/03/2026 DOI: https://doi.org/10.18634/sophiaj.22v.1i.1513 Volumen 22, número 1, 2026, p: e1513 ISSN 2346-0806 e1513 national tests, and success in the subject. Conclusions: The study concludes that it is necessary to implement targeted leveling and pedagogical support programs to reduce failure rates in these fundamental subjects","academic performance, differential calculus, linear regression, factors",marcadores,introduccion el rendimiento academico en area critica como las matematica es el foco de este articulo,introduction academic performance critical area such mathematic focu article objective identify sociodemographic institutional factor influence performance engineer student subject differential calculu material method quantitative descriptive correlational study conduct analyz student prior academic data living condition result strong correlation reveal between type school attend result sophia recibido 01 02 2025-aceptado 30 01 2026-publicado 25 03 2026 doi http doi org 10 18634 sophiaj 22v 1i 1513 volumen 22 numero 2026 e1513 issn 2346-0806 e1513 national test succes subject conclusion study conclud necessary implement target level pedagogical support program reduce failure rate these fundamental subject,academic performance differen