2346-0806,sph07-e1568+(3).pdf,sph07-e1568+(3)_0,en,Research article,"Introduction: This study highlights the importance of English as a foreign language in enriching the learning experience of engineering students. Objective: To evaluate the impact of a digital intervention on their linguistic development. Materials and methods: A pedagogical digital intervention methodology was used, designed to integrate technical content with language learning. Results: The results showed that the use of technological tools facilitated the understanding of concepts and increased students' interest in mastering a second language. Conclusions: The integration of specialized digital resources is key to enhancing the linguistic and professional development of future civil engineers","reading plan; English for Specific Purposes (ESP); digital magazines; virtual learning environments. Sophia Received: 31/12/2025-Accepted: 20/01/2026-Published: 22/03/2026. DOI: https://doi.org/10.18634/sophiaj.22v.1i.1568 Volume 22, issue 1, 2026, p: e1568 ISSN 2346-0806 e1568",marcadores,research article,introduction study highlight importance english foreign language enrich learn experience engineer student objective evaluate impact digital intervention their linguistic development material method pedagogical digital intervention methodology used design integrate technical content language learn result result show use technological tool facilitat understand concept increas student interest master second language conclusion integration specializ digital resourc key enhanc linguistic professional development future civil engineer,read plan english specific purpos esp digital magazin virtual learn environment sophia receiv 31 12 2025-accepted 20 01 2026-published 22 03 2026 doi http doi org 10 18634 sophiaj 22v 1i 1568 volume 22 issue 2026 e1568 issn 2346-0806 e1568,research article introduction study highlight importance english foreign language enrich learn experience engineer student objective evaluat