2346-206X,document (13).pdf,document (13)_0,en,PRODUCCIÓN CIENTÍFICA,"Nature tourism has been established as a strategy for conservation and local development. Its growth prompted the development of methodologies and studies aimed at identifying trends, theoretical models, and gaps in the scientific literature. However, the fragmentation of knowledge and the absence of rigorous techniques hindered its development. Given this situation, the research problem was defined as follows: Does scientific production to date contribute to the development of new trends related to nature tourism? To answer this question, the following objectives were established: to determine the impact of nature tourism and scientific research and to analyze indicators of scientific production in nature tourism from 2014 to 2024. Additionally, a new line of specialized research was proposed. The documentary methodology was applied using the following software: EndNote 8, BibExcel, PAJEK, VOSviewer, SPSS 24, and Tableau. This software allowed us to analyze productivity indicators,",", collaborations, and the timeliness of references. A literature review was conducted using databases such as Scopus, Web of Science, and SciELO. The study revealed an increase in scientific production highlighting themes such as ecotourism, tourism safety, conservation, sustainability, innovation, impact assessment, and community participation. The geographical concentrations were most signific",marcadores,produccion cientifica,nature tourism has been establish strategy conservation local development its growth prompt development methodologi studi aimed identify trend theoretical model gaps scientific literature however fragmentation knowledge absence rigorou techniqu hinder its development given situation research problem defin follow does scientific production date contribute development new trend relat nature tourism answer question follow objectiv establish determine impact nature tourism scientific research ana