2346-206X,document (14).pdf,document (14)_0,en,Doctor en Turismo por la Universidad Necmettin Erbakan,"Thanks to technology and the pandemic, wine experiences have evolved. Now, tasters can participate in digital wine tastings from the comfort of their own homes. This study compares physical and digital wine tasting experiences (DWEs) using qualitative methods. Semi-structured interviews were conducted with participants who had experienced both types of tastings. A cyclic and interpretive qualitative data analysis approach was employed. The findings show that both formats offer socialization opportunities, though DWEs enable social interaction from home. The sensory dimensions were similar, while the cognitive and emotional aspects differed. As DWEs grow in popularity, they are emerging as valid tourism products. Understanding behavioral tendencies across both modalities can help the wine industry adapt and improve experience design","wine, wine taster, wine experience, physical wine experience, digital wine experience, Turkish wine",marcadores,doctor en turismo por la universidad necmettin erbakan,thank technology pandemic wine experienc have evolv now taster can participate digital wine tasting comfort their own home study compar physical digital wine tast experienc dwes using qualitative method semi-structur interview conduct participant who had experienc both type tasting cyclic interpretive qualitative data analysi approach employ finding show both format offer social opportuniti though dwes enable social interaction home sensory dimension similar while cognitive emotional aspect differ dwes grow popularity they emerg valid tourism product understand behavioral tendenci acros both modaliti can help wine industry adapt improve experience design,wine wine taster wine experience physical wine experience digital wine experience turkish wine,doctor en turismo por la universidad necmettin erbakan thank technology pandemic wine experienc have evolv now taster can part