2346-206X,document (6).pdf,document (6)_0,en,"cero, identificar estrategias de gestión","This study aims to propose a tourism corridor strategy to promote sustainable C a r l o s W . H e r n á n d e z M o n t e n e g r o e t a l . 96 Rev. Turismo y Sociedad, vol. XXXIX, julio-diciembre 2026, pp. 95-123 local development in the districts of Lagunas, Zaña, Cayaltí, Nueva Arica, and Oyotún. The study focuses on the Zaña River Valley in the Chiclayo province of the Lambayeque department in Peru. Due to the specifics of this study, a qualitative research approach was used for a year, employing the Participatory Action Research (PAR) method. The various stakeholders actively and responsibly participated in each phase of community development. The following were achieved as a result of this participatory and collaborative work: first, the potential tourism resources of each district were recognized; second, the stakeholders involved in tourism development were mapped; third, tourism management strategies were identified; fourth, mechanisms were implemented to receive input and feedback from stakeholders; and fifth, a proposal for an integrative tourism corridor was made for the districts. The results are clear: the districts have potential resources but also have gaps and problems that need to be resolved. Therefore, we highlight the importance of tourism in promoting development and the responsibility of stakeholders in implementing the project. We encourage the creation of the «Tourism Association of the Zaña River Valley» to generate synergies between the different stakeholders in the valley","sustainable local development, tourism corridor, tourism resources, tourism strategy, tourism association 1",marcadores,cero identificar estrategia de gestion,study aims propose tourism corridor strategy promote sustainable 96 rev turismo sociedad vol xxxix julio-diciembre 2026 pp 95-123 local development district laguna zana cayalti nueva arica oyotun study focus zana river valle