2346-206X,document (9).pdf,document (9)_0,en,"Finalmente, se proponen","Population aging poses challenges to the labor market, especially with regard to the inclusion of older adults. Although life expectancy has increased, this group still faces barriers, such as stereotypes and prejudices, that limit their job opportunities. Professionalization and training are key tools for overcoming these obstacles, especially in growing, adaptable sectors like tourism that can accommodate diverse labor profiles. This article examines how professionalization can facilitate the inclusion of older adults in the tourism labor market. Through a review of literature and previous studies, the article highlights the benefits of professional training in improving job prospects and quality of life. Despite structural and cultural barriers, the findings suggest that adequate training can significantly enhance older adults’ employability and strengthen the tourism sector. Finally, the article proposes recommendations for designing inclusive public policies and effective programs to promote their labor integration","older adult, tourism, employment inclusion, professionalization 1",marcadores,finalmente se proponen,population aging pose challeng labor market especially regard inclusion older adult although life expectancy has increas group still face barrier such stereotyp prejudic limit their job opportuniti professional train key tool overcom these obstacl especially grow adaptable sector like tourism can accommodate diverse labor profil article examin how professional can facilitate inclusion older adult tourism labor market through review literature previou studi article highlight benefit professional train improv job prospect quality life despite structural cultural barrier finding suggest adequate train can significantly enhance older adult employability strengthen tourism sector finally article propos recommend design inclusive public polici effective program promote their labor integration,older adult tourism employment inclusion professional,finalmente se proponen population aging pose challeng labor market especially regard inclusion older adult although life expectancy has increas group still face barrier such stereotyp prejudic limit their job opportuniti professional train key tool overcom these obstacl especially grow adaptable sector like tourism can accommodate diverse labor profil article examin how professional can facilitate inclusion older adult tourism labor market through review literature previou studi article highlight benefit professional train improv job prospect quality life despite structural cultural barrier finding suggest adequate train can significantly enhance older adult employability strengthen tourism sector finally article propos recommend design inclusive public polici effective program promote their labor integration older adult tourism employment inclusion professional,1.0.0,0d225e75b5ed4ca2
2346-2183,01_121522.FINAL.pdf,01_121522.FINAL_0,en,Universidad Nacional de Colombia.,"Mobile banking has emerged as a key tool for financial inclusion, particularly in rural areas where geographical and infrastructural barriers hinder access to traditional banking services. This study analyzes the determinants of mobile banking acceptance among cattle farmers in western Antioquia, Colombia, using the unified theory of acceptance and use of technology (UTAUT) model. A quantitative methodology was applied through structured surveys conducted with 132 rural producers to evaluate variables such as performance expectancy, effort expectancy, social influence, risk, and trust. The results indicate that performance expectancy and effort expectancy are the main factors influencing mobile banking adoption, while trust, risk, and social influence do not show significant impacts. These findings highlight the need to develop strategies that promote access to user-friendly digital platforms and training focused on the effective use of these tools",mobile banking; financial inclusion; technology adoption; UTAUT; rural areas. Determinantes de la aceptación del uso de la banca móvil por parte de ganaderos,marcadores,universidad nacional de colombia,mobile bank has emerg key tool financial inclusion particularly rural area where geographical infrastructural barrier hinder acces traditional bank servic study analyz determinant mobile bank acceptance among cattle farmer western antioquia colombia using unifi theory acceptance use technology utaut model quantitative methodology appli through structur survey conduct 132 rural producer evaluate variabl such performance expectancy effort expectancy social influence risk trust result indicate performance expectancy effort expectancy main factor influenc mobile bank adoption while trust risk social influence do not show significant impact these finding highlight need develop strategi promote acces user-friendly digital platform train focus effective use these tool,mobile bank financial inclusion technology adoption utaut rural area determinant de la aceptacion del uso de la banca movil por parte de ganadero,universidad nacional de colombia mobile bank has emerg key tool financial inclusion particularly rural area where geographical infrastructural barrier hinder acces traditional bank servic study analyz determinant mobile bank acceptance among cattle farmer western antioquia colombia using unifi theory acceptance use technology utaut model quantitative methodology appli through structur survey conduct 132 rural producer evaluate variabl such performance expectancy effort expectancy social influence risk trust result indicate performance expectancy effort expectancy main factor influenc mobile bank adoption while trust risk social influence do not show significant impact these finding highlight need develop strategi promote acces user-friendly digital platform train focus effective use these tool mobile bank financial inclusion technology adoption utaut rural area determinant de la aceptacion del uso de la banca movil por parte de ganadero,1.0.0,62543ecbb8c1280d
2346-2183,01_121522.FINAL.pdf,01_121522.FINAL_0,es,tance among cattle farmers in,"La banca móvil se ha consolidado como una herramienta clave para la inclusión financiera, particularmente en zonas rurales donde las barreras geográficas y de infraestructura limitan el acceso a servicios bancarios tradicionales. Este estudio analiza los determinantes de la aceptación de la banca móvil en ganaderos del occidente de Antioquia, Colombia, utilizando el modelo UTAUT. Se aplicó una metodología cuantitativa basada en encuestas estructuradas a 132 productores rurales, evaluando variables como la expectativa de rendimiento, la expectativa de esfuerzo, la influencia social, el riesgo y la confianza. Los resultados revelan que la expectativa de rendimiento y la facilidad de uso son los principales factores que influyen en la adopción de la banca móvil, mientras que la confianza, el riesgo y la influencia social no mostraron un impacto significativo. Estos hallazgos destacan la necesidad de desarrollar estrategias que promuevan el acceso a plataformas digitales intuitivas y capacitaciones enfocadas en el uso de estas herramientas",banca móvil; inclusión financiera; adopción tecnológica; UTAUT; áreas rurales. 1,marcadores,tance among cattle farmers in,banca movil ha consolidado como herramienta clave inclusion financiera particular zonas rural donde barrer geografic infraestructura limitan acceso servici bancari tradicional este estudio analiza determinant aceptacion banca movil ganader occidente antioquia colombia utiliz modelo utaut aplico metodologia cuantitativa basada encuest estructurad 132 productor rural evalu variabl como expectativa rendimiento expectativa esfuerzo influencia social riesgo confianza resultad revelan expectativa rendimiento facilidad uso son principal factor influyen adopcion banca movil mientr confianza riesgo influencia social no mostraron impacto significativo estos hallazg destacan necesidad desarrollar estrategi promuevan acceso plataform digital int