2346-3775,49-12-PB.pdf,49-12-PB_1,en,Protected urea as a nitrogen source for Mulato II grass: impacts on,"The growing demand for high-yielding forage cultivars with drought tolerance, broad environmental adaptation and sustained feed quality has stimulated the development of new Urochloa (syn. Brachiaria) genotypes, such as Mulato II. Efficient nitrogen (N) fertilization strategies are essential to optimize their productivity and nutritional value. This study aimed to evaluate the effects of N fertilization, using conventional and protected urea at 0, 50, 100 and 150 kg N/ha on green mass production (GMP), dry matter production (DMP), leaf:stem ratio (LSR), nutritional value, apparent nitrogen recovery (ANR), apparent nitrogen conversion efficiency (ANCE), and crude protein yield per hectare (CP/ha) of Mulato II. The experiment followed a completely randomized 4 × 2 factorial design. The results showed that the N source significantly affected GMP, DMP, neutral detergent fiber (NDF) during the second growth period, and ANCE. Increasing N rates led to higher GMP, DMP and CP concentration, while decreasing ANCE. Fertilization with protected urea improved ANCE and reduced NDF concentration, indicating greater efficiency in nitrogen utilization. These findings support the strategic use of protected urea at moderate N rates to enhance forage productivity and nitrogen use efficiency in Mulato II","biomass production, fiber concentration, nitrogen conversion, nitrogen fertilization, nitrogen recovery",marcadores,protect urea nitrogen source mulato ii gras impact,grow demand high-yield forage cultivar drought tolerance broad environmental adaptation sustain feed quality has stimulat development new urochloa syn brachiaria genotyp such mulato ii efficient nitrogen fertil strategi essential optimize their productivity nutritional value study aimed evaluate effect fertil using conventional protect urea 50 100 150 kg ha green mass production gmp dry matter production dmp leaf stem ratio lsr nutritional value apparent nitrogen recovery anr apparent nitrogen conversion efficiency ance crude protein yield per hectare cp ha mulato ii experiment follow completely randomiz factorial design result show source significantly affect gmp dmp neutral detergent fiber ndf during second growth period ance increas rate led higher gmp dmp cp concentration while decreas ance fertil protect urea improv ance reduc ndf concentration indicat greater efficiency nitrogen util these finding support strategic use protect urea moderate rate enhance forage productivity nitrogen use efficiency mulato ii,biomas production fiber concentration nitrogen conversion nitrogen fertil nitrogen recovery,protect urea nitrogen source mulato ii gras impact grow demand high-yield forage cultivar drought tolerance broad environmental adaptation sustain feed quality has stimulat development new urochloa syn brachiaria genotyp such mulato ii efficient nitrogen fertil strategi essential optimize their productivity nutritional value study aimed evaluate effect fertil using conventional protect urea 50 100 150 kg ha green mass production gmp dry matter production dmp leaf stem ratio lsr nutritional value apparent nitrogen recovery anr apparent nitrogen conversion efficiency ance crude protein yield per hectare cp ha mulato ii experiment follow completely randomiz factorial design result show source significantly affect gmp dmp neutral detergent fiber ndf during second growth period ance increas rate led higher gmp dmp cp concentration while decreas ance fertil protect urea improv ance reduc ndf concentration indicat greater efficiency nitrogen util these finding support strategic use protect urea moderate rate enhance forage productivity nitrogen use efficiency mulato ii biomas production fiber concentration nitrogen conversion nitrogen fertil nitrogen recovery,1.0.0,090a5610378d17f5
2346-3775,49-12-PB.pdf,49-12-PB_1,es,"(DMP), leaf:stem ratio (LSR), nutritional value,","La creciente demanda de cultivares de forraje de alto rendimiento con tolerancia a la sequía, amplia adaptación ambiental y calidad sostenida del valor nutritivo ha estimulado el desarrollo de nuevos genotipos de Urochloa (sin. Brachiaria), como Mulato II. Las estrategias eficientes de fertilización nitrogenada (N) son esenciales para optimizar su productividad y valor nutricional. Este estudio tuvo como objetivo evaluar los efectos de la fertilización con N, utilizando urea convencional y protegida a 0, 50, 100 y 150 kg N/ha en la producción de de biomasa fresca (GMP), de materia seca (DMP), relación hoja:tallo (LSR), valor nutricional, recuperación aparente de nitrógeno (ANR), eficiencia aparente de conversión de nitrógeno (ANCE) y rendimiento de proteína cruda por hectárea (PC/ha) del pasto Mulato II. El experimento siguió un diseño factorial 4 × 2 completamente aleatorizado. Los resultados mostraron que la fuente Correspondence: Ludmilla Costa Brunes, Animal Performance Center, Embrapa Cerrados, Santo Antonio de Goiás, GO, C.P. 75.375.000, Brazil. Email: ludmillabrunes@hotmail.com Tropical Grasslands-Forrajes Tropicales (ISSN: 2346-3775) 83 Impacts of protected urea on forage productivity and composition of Mulato II grass de N afectó significativamente GMP, DMP, fibra detergente neutro (FDN) durante el segundo período de crecimiento y ANCE. El aumento de las dosis de N resultó en una mayor GMP, DMP y contenido de PC, a la vez que disminuyó la ANCE. La fertilización con urea protegida mejoró la ANCE y redujo la concentración de FDN, lo que indica una mayor eficiencia en la utilización del nitrógeno. Estos hallazgos respaldan el uso estratégico de urea protegida con dosis moderadas de N para mejorar la productividad del forraje y la eficiencia en el uso del nitrógeno en Mulato II","Concentración de fibra, eficiencia de conversión de nitrógeno, fertilización nitrogenada, producción de biomasa, recuperación de nitrógeno. crucial for promoting pasture recovery, enhancing forage productivity, and supporting sustainable animal production. N plays a key role in plant metabolism and directly influences tillering, leaf expansion and protein synthesis. However, due to its mobil",marcadores,dmp leaf stem ratio lsr nutritional value,creciente demanda cultivar forraje alto rendimiento tolerancia sequia amplia adaptacion ambiental calidad sostenida valor nutritivo ha estimulado desarrollo nuev genotip urochloa sin brachiaria como mulato ii estrategi eficient fertilizacion nitrogenada son esencial optimizar productividad valor nutricional este estudio tuvo como objetivo evaluar efect fertilizacion utiliz urea convencional protegida 50 100 150 kg ha produccion biomasa fresca gmp materia seca dmp relacion hoja tallo lsr valor nutricional recuperacion aparente nitrogeno anr eficiencia aparente conversion nitrogeno ance rendimiento proteina cruda hectarea pc ha pasto mulato ii experimento siguio diseno factorial completa aleatorizado resultad mostraron fuente correspondence ludmilla costa brun animal performance center embrapa cerrad santo antonio goias go 75 375 000 brazil email ludmillabrun hotmail com tropical grasslands-forraj tropical issn 2346-3775 83 impacts of protected urea on forage productivity and composition of mulato ii grass afecto significativa gmp dmp fibra detergente neutro fdn durante segundo periodo crecimiento ance aumento dosis resulto mayor gmp dmp contenido pc vez disminuyo ance fertilizacion urea protegida mejoro ance redujo concentracion fdn indica mayor eficiencia utilizacion nitrogeno estos hallazg respaldan uso estrategico urea protegida dosis moderad mejorar productividad forraje eficiencia uso nitrogeno mulato ii,concentracion fibra eficiencia conversion nitrogeno fertilizacion nitrogenada produccion biomasa recuperacion nitrogeno crucial for promoting pasture recovery enhancing forage productivity and supporting sustainabl