2346-3775,49-12-PB.pdf,49-12-PB_3,en,CC BY 4.0) license.,"Use of ethephon on buds from different positions on the culm of BRS Capiaçú elephant grass was evaluated to improve development of shoots during planting. The experiment compared buds originating from the apex and base of the BRS Capiaçú culm without ethephon application, cut culms with buds immersed for 1 min in ethephon solution (0.650 L ethephon/ha) and application of 150 L ethephon/ha directly on the bud on the standing culm. The position of the bud in the culm and the application of ethephon positively influenced the development and gaseous exchange of BRS Capiaçú. Buds immersed for 1 min in ephethon showed better development, CO2 assimilation rate (A), transpiration (E) and stomatal conductance. Plants growing from buds from the base of the culm produced more leaves, with higher biomass and higher transpiration, It is recommended to use buds from the base of the BRS Capiaçú culm for propagation when using ethephon","Cenchrus purpureus (Schumach.) Morrone, forage, phytohormone, stomatal conductance, transpiration",marcadores,cc license,use ethephon buds different position culm brs capiacu elephant gras evaluat improve development shoot during plant experiment compar buds originat apex base brs capiacu culm without ethephon application cut culm buds immers min ethephon solution 650 ethephon ha application 150 ethephon ha directly bud stand culm position bud culm application ethephon positively influenc development gaseou exchange brs capiacu buds immers min ephethon show better development co2 assimilation rate transpiration stomatal conductance plant grow buds base culm produc more leav higher biomas higher transpiration recommend use buds base brs capiacu culm propagation when using ethephon,cenchru purpureu schumach morrone forage phytohormone stomatal conductance transpiration,cc license use ethephon buds different position culm brs capiacu elephant gras evaluat improve development shoot during plant 