ad resolucion problem colaboracion asimismo identificaron desafi relacionad formacion docente 50 falta infraestructura tecnologica 44 resistencia institucional 29 conjunto resultad revelan interdisciplinariedad convierte matematica lenguaje integrador capaz doctora cienci matematic estancia posdoctoral facultad cienci fisico matematic benemerita universidad autonoma puebla mexico frandmr gmail com orcid https orcid org 0009-0003-7774-549x maestra educacion matematica universidad autonoma guerrero mexico stefanynavanl gmail com orcid https orcid org 0000-00026105-1587 doctora cienci estancia posdoctoral facultad cienci fisico matematic benemerita universidad autonoma puebla mexico cprosasc2012ny gmail com doctor cienci segundo nivel fisica matematic benemerita universidad autonoma puebla buap mexico fraguela fcfm buap mx orcid https orcid org 0000-0001-5273-8777 recibido noviembre 2025 aceptado julio 10 2026 matlalcuatzi nava rosas fraguela 2026 gondola ensenanza aprendizaje cienci e-issn 2346-4712 vol 21 no mayo agosto 2026 pp e-24329 articular saber divers fomentar investigacion apoyar adquisicion aprendizaje final proponen reflexion orientad fortalecer formacion docente reduccion brech tecnologic consolidacion instrument no solo valoren aprendizaje conceptual sino tambien impacto pensamiento critico creatividad colaboracion interdisciplinariedad ensenanza matematic resolucion problem pensamiento critico formacion docente,1.0.0,9b64d78a989cb754
2346-4712,09+V21N2+24329.pdf,09+V21N2+24329_0,en,"articular saberes diversos, fomentar la investigación y apoyar la adquisición del","This paper presents a document-based reflection based on a critical review of the literature on mathematics education through interdisciplinary approaches. The problem addressed is the persistent fragmentation between mathematics and other disciplines, which limits the development of comprehensive competencies and the transfer of knowledge to real-world contexts. The aim of this study was to identify the theoretical foundations and educational experiences that support interdisciplinary mathematics education, compare the effectiveness of strategies such as Problem-Based Learning (PBL) and Project-Based Learning (PjBL), and analyze the main challenges associated with their implementation. The methodology consisted of a systematic documentary analysis of articles published in indexed journals, reports from the Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development (OECD), and policy documents related to the New Mexican School. The findings reveal a high level of effectiveness (76%) of interdisciplinary approaches, particularly in fostering creativity, problem-solving, and collaboration. Likewise, challenges were identified regarding teacher education (50%), inadequate technological infrastructure (44%), and institutional resistance (29%). Overall, the results show that interdisciplinarity transforms mathematics into an integrative language capable of connecting diverse fields of knowledge, promoting inquiry, and fostering meaningful learning. Finally, the study offers reflections aimed at strengthening teacher education, reducing technological gaps, and consolidating assessment instruments that evaluate not only conceptual learning but also the development of critical thinking, creativity, and collaboration",Interdisciplinary Learning; Mathematics Instruction; Problem Solving; Critical Thinking; Teacher Training,marcadores,articular sabe