2346-4712,11+V21N2+23900.pdf,11+V21N2+23900_0,en,"es elementos: consciência de classe, temática e domínio do","This study is characterized as an Investigation-Training-Action in Science (IFAEC) project, employing a qualitative approach and a document analysis methodology to examine the self-reflective practices of Biological Sciences pre-service teachers during their Supervised Curricular Internship in middle school science education. To this end, the pre-service teachers' reflective narratives regarding their classes and conclusions were analyzed to identify the developmental processes fostered by reflecting on one's own practice. The results were organized through thematic content analysis into three categories: constitutive elements of science teacher training emerging from the reflective writings; constitutive elements of the ""recipe"" for a good teacher; and an understanding of the developmental potential of InvestigationTraining-Action in science education. Regarding the constitutive elements of training, the following stood out: the students' reality; inquiry-based methodologies; the value placed on visual methodologies; the experience and role of the co-educator; teaching challenges; the first class/start of the career; commitment and affectivity; teaching theories and practices; school placement via institutional programs; and a focus on fostering autonomy and inquiry-based, critical processes with students. Regarding what constitutes a good teacher, the following elements emerged: class consciousness; thematic knowledge and content mastery; the students' reality; experimental and practical activities; training needs; innovations and reflections; scientific background; and the identity of the teacher-researcher who is continuously developing. Finally, regarding the understanding of the inquiry-based developmental potential present in the narratives, the results confirm the value of IFAEC in science education for the professional development of pre-service science teachers and its impact on inquiry-based science teaching; by grasping the developmental role of IFAEC processes, the science teacher evolves into a researcher of their own pedagogical practice","initial training; narratives; action research; investigative teaching; pedagogical practice. Marin J, da Costa R. (2026). Investigar é preciso: processos formativos que permeiam a prática autorreflexiva da investigaçãoformação-ação em ciências para licenciandos de ciências biológicas [ 3 ] Góndola, Enseñanza y Aprendizaje de las Ciencias e-ISSN: 2346-4712 Vol. 21, No. 2 (mayo – agosto, 2026),",marcadores,es elemento consciencia de classe tematica dominio do,study characteriz investigation-training-action science ifaec project employ qualitative approach document analysi methodology examine self-reflective practic biological scienc pre-service teacher during their supervis curricular internship middle school science education end pre-service teacher reflective narrativ regard their class conclusion analyz identify developmental process foster reflect one own practice result organiz through thematic content analysi into three categori constitutive element science teacher train emerg reflective writing constitutive element recipe good teacher understand developmental potential investigationtraining-action science education regard constitutive element train follow stood out student reality inquiry-bas methodologi value plac visual methodologi experience role co-educator teach challeng first clas start career commitment affectivity teach theori practic school placement via institutional program focu foster autonomy inquiry-bas critical process student regard what constitut good teacher follow element emerg clas consciousnes thematic knowledge content mastery student reality experimental practical activiti train need innov reflection scientific background identity teacher-researcher who continuously develop finally regard understand inquiry-bas developmental potential pre