2357-4100,Achak.pdf,Achak_0,en,Uncertainty principles for generalized,"In this paper, we investigate uncertainty principles and stable signal reconstruction in the framework of the generalized Dunkl transform. Extending classical results of Donoho and Stark, we establish quantitative lower bounds linking the concentration of a function and its generalized Dunkl transform on measurable sets. We introduce the concept of strongly annihilating pairs adapted to this transform and prove stability results for the reconstruction of bandlimited functions from incomplete and noisy data. Furthermore, we develop Tikhonov regularization methods and iterative algorithms to address ill-posed recovery problems, providing explicit error bounds and convergence analysis. Our work broadens the scope of harmonic analysis uncertainty principles to singular differential-difference operators and contributes novel tools for signal processing applications within this setting","and phrases. generalized Dunkl transform; Benedicks’ theorem; Donoho-Stark uncertainty principle. 2020 Mathematics Subject Classification. 42A38, 44A35, 34B30",marcadores,uncertainty principl generaliz,paper we investigate uncertainty principl stable signal reconstruction framework generaliz dunkl transform extend classical result donoho stark we establish quantitative lower bound link concentration function its generaliz dunkl transform measurable sets we introduce concept strongly annihilat pair adapt transform prove stability result reconstruction bandlimit function incomplete noisy data furthermore we develop tikhonov regular method iterative algorithm addres ill-pos recovery problem provid explicit error bound convergence analysi our work broaden scope harmonic analysi uncertainty principl singular differential-difference operator contribut novel tool signal process applic within sett,phras generaliz dunkl transform benedick theorem donoho-stark uncertainty principle 2020 mathematic subject classification 42a38 44a35 34b30,uncertainty principl generaliz paper we investigate uncertainty principl stable signal reconstruction framework generaliz dunkl transform extend classical result donoho stark we establish quantitative lower bound link concentration function its generaliz dunkl transform measurable sets we introduce concept strongly annihilat pair adapt transform prove stability result reconstruction bandlimit function incomplete noisy data furthermore we develop tikhonov regular method iterative algorithm addres ill-pos recovery problem provid explicit error bound convergence analysi our work broaden scope harmonic analysi uncertainty principl singular differential-difference operator contribut novel tool signal process applic within sett phras generaliz dunkl transform benedick theorem donoho-stark uncertainty principle 2020 mathematic subject classification 42a38 44a35 34b30,1.0.0,cfbca484c3204aad
2357-4100,abdaqui.pdf,abdaqui_0,en,A Refined Block Arnoldi Method for,"Krylov methods have been successfully used to solve large matrix equations with sparse coefficients. In this paper, we are interested on solving the low-rank Lyapunov equation whether in the continuous or discrete case. We propose to modify the block Arnoldi process so that the projection Krylov subspace contains some additional blocks that involves the inverse of the square coefficient of this equation. Our goal with this approach is to reduce the number of iterations and convergence time required by the classical block Arnoldi method. To show the effectiveness of the proposed method, some numerical experiments are carried out","and phrases. Krylov subspaces, Block Arnoldi process, Lyapunov equation. 2020 Mathematics Subject Classification. 34D08, 37L30",marcadores,refin block arnoldi method,krylov method have been successfully used solve large matrix equation sparse coefficient paper we interest solv low-rank lyapunov equation whether continuou discrete case we propose modify block arnoldi proces so projection krylov subspace contain some additional block involv inverse square coefficient equation our goal approach reduce number iter convergence time requir classical block arnoldi method show effectivenes propos method some numerical experiment carri out,phras krylov subspac block arnoldi proces lyapunov equation 2020 mathematic subject classification 34d08 37l30,refin block arnoldi method krylov method have been successfully used solve large matrix equation sparse coefficient paper we interest solv low-rank lyapunov equation whether continuou discrete case we propose modify block arnoldi proces so projection krylov subspace contain some additional block involv inverse square coefficient equation our goal approach reduce number iter convergence time requir classical block arnoldi method show effectivenes propos method some numerical experiment carri out phras krylov subspac block arnoldi proces lyapunov equation 2020 mathematic subject classification 34d08 37l30,1.0.0,f500cc0fded5473c
2357-4100,azraib.pdf,azraib_0,en,On strongly Elliptic problem with weak,"In this study, we prove the existence of solutions to the nonlinear elliptic boundary value problem described by the equation −div a(x, u, ∇u) + Ψ(x, u) = f where f, Ψ(x, u) are elements of L1(Ω), and where no monotonicity condition will be supposed on the function a(x, s, ξ)","and phrases. Weighted Sobolev, elliptic problem, Truncation, L1data, weak monotonicity. 2020 Mathematics Subject Classification. 35J62, 46E35",marcadores,strongly elliptic problem weak,study we prove existence solution nonlinear elliptic boundary value problem describ equation -div ps where ps element l1 where no monotonicity condition will suppos function,phras weight sobolev elliptic problem truncation l1data weak monotonicity 2020 mathematic subject classification 35j62 46e35,strongly elliptic problem weak study we prove existence solution nonlinear elliptic boundary value problem describ equation -div ps where ps element l1 where no monotonicity condition will suppos function phras weight sobolev elliptic problem truncation l1data weak monotonicity 2020 mathematic subject classification 35j62 46e35,1.0.0,54384cf07ce36289
2357-4100,cezaro.pdf,cezaro_0,en,On a multi-fractional virotherapy model,"In this paper, we enhance the oncolytic virotherapy model examined by [23] by incorporating multi-fractional derivatives of the Caputo type, assigning distinct derivative orders to each model variable. We establish the Hadamard well-posedness of the new model and confirm that the solutions remain within the positive half-plane, aligning with the criteria of the modeled problem. Furthermore, we conduct a stability analysis for the equilibrium solutions of these multi-fractional dynamics, demonstrating their dependence on the derivative orders specified in the dynamics. The theoretical insights are supported by numerical simulations","and phrases. Oncolytic virotherapy, Modeling, Fractional derivatives. 2020 Mathematics Subject Classification. 92B05, 37N25, 34D20",marcadores,multi-fractional virotherapy model,paper we enhance oncolytic virotherapy model examin 23 incorporat multi-fractional derivativ caputo type assign distinct derivative order each model variable we establish hadamard well-posednes new model confirm solution remain within positive half-plane align criteria model problem furthermore we conduct stability analysi equilibrium solution these multi-fractional dynamic demonstrat their dependence derivative order specifi dynamic theoretical insight support numerical simul,phras oncolytic virotherapy model fractional derivativ 2020 mathematic subject classification 92b05 37n25 34d20,multi-fractional virotherapy model paper we enhance oncolytic virotherapy model examin 23 incorporat multi-fractional derivativ caputo type assign distinct derivative order each model variable we establish hadamard well-posednes new model confirm solution remain within positive half-plane align criteria model problem furthermore we conduct stability analysi equilibrium solution these multi-fractional dynamic demonstrat their dependence derivative order specifi dynamic theoretical insight support numerical simul phras oncolytic virotherapy model fractional derivativ 2020 mathematic subject classification 92b05 37n25 34d20,1.0.0,985739821faaecb7
2357-4100,fer-hji-zer.pdf,fer-hji-zer_0,en,Renormalized Solutions for Nonlinear,"This work is centered around the study of the following noncoercive elliptic problem : ( Au + g(x, u, ∇u) = f(x) + |u|p0−2u |x|p0 in Ω, u = 0 on ∂Ω, In the anisotropic Sobolev space, where Ωis a bounded open subset of RN (N ≥2) that includes the origin, with g(x, s, ξ) subject to certain growth conditions and f ∈L1(Ω). We prove the existence of renormalized solutions for the strongly nonlinear and non-coercive elliptic Dirichlet problem. Furthermore, we establish several regularity results","and phrases. Anisotropic Sobolev spaces, strongly nonlinear elliptic equation, non-coercive problems, renormalized solutions. 2020 Mathematics Subject Classification. Primary 35J15; Secondary 35J25",marcadores,renormaliz solution nonlinear,work center around study follow noncoercive elliptic problem au p0-2u p0 anisotropic sobolev space where ois bound open subset rn includ origin subject certain growth condition l1 we prove existence renormaliz solution strongly nonlinear non-coercive elliptic dirichlet problem furthermore we establish several regularity result,phras anisotropic sobolev spac strongly nonlinear elliptic equation non-coercive problem renormaliz solution 2020 mathematic subject classification primary 35j15 secondary 35j25,renormaliz solution nonlinear work center around study follow noncoercive elliptic problem au p0-2u p0 anisotropic sobolev space where ois bound open subset rn includ origin subject certain growth condition l1 we prove existence renormaliz solution strongly nonlinear non-coercive elliptic dirichlet problem furthermore we establish several regularity result phras anisotropic sobolev spac strongly nonlinear elliptic equation non-coercive problem renormaliz solution 2020 mathematic subject classification primary 35j15 secondary 35j25,1.0.0,1cfb949ebd158943
2357-4100,lalili.pdf,lalili_0,en,Solving Strongly Sublinear,"We study the existence of weak solutions to the nonlinear elliptic problem −∆p(x)u = λ|u|s(x)−2u + f(x, u, ∇u) in a bounded domain Ω⊂RN with smooth boundary ∂Ω, under homogeneous Dirichlet conditions. The equation features a variable exponent p(x) in the p(x)-Laplacian operator, an eigenvalue term λ|u|s(x)−2u, and a Carath´eodory perturbation f with sublinear growth, depending on both u and ∇u. Using a topological approach based on fixed-point theorems, we establish the existence of weak solutions to the problem","and phrases. Strongly nonlinear elliptic problem, p(x)-Laplacian, generalized Lebesgue-Sobolev spaces, fixed point. 2020 Mathematics Subject Classification. 35J60, 46E35, 47H05, 47H11",marcadores,solv strongly sublinear,we study existence weak solution nonlinear elliptic problem -p -2u bound domain orn smooth boundary under homogeneou dirichlet condition equation featur variable exponent -laplacian operator eigenvalue term -2u carath eodory perturbation sublinear growth depend both using topological approach based fixed-point theorem we establish existence weak solution problem,phras strongly nonlinear elliptic problem -laplacian generaliz lebesgue-sobolev spac fixed point 2020 mathematic subject classification 35j60 46e35 47h05 47h11,solv strongly sublinear we study existence weak solution nonlinear elliptic problem -p -2u bound domain orn smooth boundary under homogeneou dirichlet condition equation featur variable exponent -laplacian operator eigenvalue term -2u carath eodory perturbation sublinear growth depend both using topological approach based fixed-point theorem we establish existence weak solution problem phras strongly nonlinear elliptic problem -laplacian generaliz lebesgue-sobolev spac fixed point 2020 mathematic subject classification 35j60 46e35 47h05 47h11,1.0.0,067d9bdc6d4b3a75
2357-4100,lopez.pdf,lopez_0,en,Relationship between Uniqueness Sets,We obtain new results on the relationship between uniqueness sets and stable sampling sets in function quasinormed spaces. The concept of perturbation of a uniformly discrete set plays an essential role. We also state and prove a result on stability for sampling sets and interpolation sets in a wide class of function quasinormed spaces,"and phrases. Quasinormed spaces, Banach spaces, p-stable sampling set, p-stable interpolation set, Hurwitz convergence, uniqueness set. 2020 Mathematics Subject Classification. 32A10, 32A20, 46B25, 46E99, 46B20",marcadores,relationship between uniquenes sets,we obtain new result relationship between uniquenes sets stable sampl sets function quasinorm spac concept perturbation uniformly discrete set play essential role we also state prove result stability sampl sets interpolation sets wide clas function quasinorm spac,phras quasinorm spac banach spac p-stable sampl set p-stable interpolation set hurwitz convergence uniquenes set 2020 mathematic subject classification 32a10 32a20 46b25 46e99 46b20,relationship between uniquenes sets we obtain new result relationship between uniquenes sets stable sampl sets function quasinorm spac concept perturbation uniformly discrete set play essential role we also state prove result stability sampl sets interpolation sets wide clas function quasinorm spac phras quasinorm spac banach spac p-stable sampl set p-stable interpolation set hurwitz convergence uniquenes set 2020 mathematic subject classification 32a10 32a20 46b25 46e99 46b20,1.0.0,11563e0de11608b1
2357-4100,mec-abd-dec.pdf,mec-abd-dec_0,en,Existence results for some anisotropic,"In this study, we establish the existence and regularity of weak solutions for the anisotropic degenerate parabolic equation, namely. ∂tu − N X i=1 (Di(ai(t, x, u)|Diu|pi−2Diu) + |u|τpi−2u|Diu|pi) = |u|r−2u, if 1 ≤r < τp−+ 1 and τ ≥ 1 p−with p−= min1≤i≤N pi, then there exists a non-negative weak solution for every positive initial data in L1","and phrases. L∞estimates, nonlinear anisotropic parabolic equations, degenerate coercivity. 2020 Mathematics Subject Classification. 35K10, 35K20, 35K55, 35K65",marcadores,existence result some anisotropic,study we establish existence regularity weak solution anisotropic degenerate parabolic equation namely tu di ai diu pi-2diu tpi-2u diu pi r-2u if tp- p-with p- min1 pi then there exist non-negative weak solution every positive initial data l1,phras lestimat nonlinear anisotropic parabolic equation degenerate coercivity 2020 mathematic subject classification 35k10 35k20 35k55 35k65,existence result some anisotropic study we establish existence regularity weak solution anisotropic degenerate parabolic equation namely tu di ai diu pi-2diu tpi-2u diu pi r-2u if tp- p-with p- min1 pi then there exist non-negative weak solution every positive initial data l1 phras lestimat nonlinear anisotropic parabolic equation degenerate coercivity 2020 mathematic subject classification 35k10 35k20 35k55 35k65,1.0.0,7ea502cdac1154b0
2357-4100,rothman.pdf,rothman_0,en,A Decomposition Theorem with an,"We prove a decomposition theorem for a linear transformation using only linear algebra techniques. This result leads to a completely different proof of a well-known decomposition theorem from representation theory, a result that is known to have an application to the Dirac spinor representation","and phrases. complex conjugate vector space, complexification, realification, Dirac equation. 2020 Mathematics Subject Classification. 20C35,15A04",marcadores,decomposition theorem,we prove decomposition theorem linear transformation using only linear algebra techniqu result lead completely different proof well-known decomposition theorem representation theory result known have application dirac spinor representation,phras complex conjugate vector space complexification realification dirac equation 2020 mathematic subject classification 20c35 15a04,decomposition theorem we prove decomposition theorem linear transformation using only linear algebra techniqu result lead completely different proof well-known decomposition theorem representation theory result known have application dirac spinor representation phras complex conjugate vector space complexification realification dirac equation 2020 mathematic subject classification 20c35 15a04,1.0.0,3918eb726b1f8364
2357-4100,talha.pdf,talha_0,en,Existence results of renormalized,"In this paper, we prove the existence of renormalized solutions for a nonlinear parabolic problem of the type ∂u ∂t −div ␀a(x, t, u, ∇u) + Φ(u)  + g(u)φ(x, |∇u|) = f in Q (a bounded subset of RN), in the setting of MusielakOrlicz, where −div(a(x, t, u, ∇u)) is a Leray-Lions operator, Φ ∈C0 ␀R, RN . The term g(u)φ(x, |∇u|) represents a nonlinear lower-order term with natural growth with respect to |∇u| and satisfies a sign condition. Note that the ∆2condition is not assumed on the Musielak function and the source term f belongs to L1(Q)","and phrases. Inhomogeneous Musielak-Orlicz-Sobolev spaces, Parabolic problems, Musielak-Orlicz function, Renormalized solutions. 2020 Mathematics Subject Classification. 46E35, 35K15, 35K20, 35K60",marcadores,existence result renormaliz,paper we prove existence renormaliz solution nonlinear parabolic problem type -div ph ph bound subset rn sett musielakorlicz where -div leray-lion operator ph c0 rn term ph represent nonlinear lower-order term natural growth respect satisfi sign condition note 2condition not assum musielak function source term belong l1,phras inhomogeneou musielak-orlicz-sobolev spac parabolic problem musielak-orlicz function renormaliz solution 2020 mathematic subject classification 46e35 35k15 35k20 35k60,existence result renormaliz paper we prove existence renormaliz solution nonlinear parabolic problem type -div ph ph bound subset rn sett musielakorlicz where -div leray-lion operator ph c0 rn term ph represent nonlinear lower-order term natural growth respect satisfi sign condition note 2condition not assum musielak function source term belong l1 phras inhomogeneou musielak-orlicz-sobolev spac parabolic problem musielak-orlicz function renormaliz solution 2020 mathematic subject classification 46e35 35k15 35k20 35k60,1.0.0,ddc36106f9d80531
2357-4720,HyS51.pdf,HyS51_0,en,rafia como metodologia de análise.,"| This article sought to demonstrate the interdependent relationship between the Hermeneutics method, Cultural History, and praxeological theory— the technical options for approaching sources— (bibliographic, documentary, and field research, Oral History) —, and the methodology of prosopography for trajectory analysis. To this end, it aimed to outline some assumptions of Hermeneutics, Cultural History, and praxeological theory; to explain the possible relationship between these theoretical constructs; and to discuss feasible technical options for source collection and the fruitful use of prosopography as an analytical methodology. This is bibliographic research that relied on the theoretical framework of Ricœur’s Hermeneutics, Chartier and Burke’s Cultural History and representations; and the assumptions of praxeological theory— habitus, capital and field— of Bourdieu, of the methodology of Oral History of Amado and Ferreira; and of the prosopography of Stone. The results demonstrate that, in trajectory studies, the articulation between Hermeneutics, Cultural History, and Praxeological Theory constitutes a possible path to historically understand ways of acting and thinking, relating representations and practices to the contexts of interdependence that shape social spaces",| history; Historical,marcadores,rafia como metodologia de analise,article sought demonstrate interdependent relationship between hermeneutic method cultural history praxeological theory-- technical option approach sources-- bibliographic documentary field research oral history -- methodology prosopography trajectory analysi end aimed outline some assumption hermeneutic cultural history praxeological theory explain possible relationship between these theoretical construct discus feasible technical option source collection fruitful use prosopography analytical methodology bibliographic research reli theoretical framework ricoeur hermeneutic chartier burke cultural history represent assumption praxeological theory-- habitu capital field-- bourdieu methodology oral history amado ferreira prosopography stone result demonstrate trajectory studi articulation between hermeneutic cultural history praxeological theory constitut possible path historically understand ways acting think relat represent practic context interdependence shape social spac,history historical,rafia como metodologia de analise article sought demonstrate interdependent relationship between hermeneutic method cultural history praxeological theory-- technical option approach sources-- bibliographic documentary field research oral history -- methodology prosopography trajectory analysi end aimed outline some assumption hermeneutic cultural history praxeological theory explain possible relationship between these theoretical construct discus feasible technical option source collection fruitful use prosopography analytical methodology bibliographic research reli theoretical framework ricoeur hermeneutic chartier burke cultural history represent assumption praxeological theory-- habitu capital field-- bourdieu methodology oral history amado ferreira prosopography stone result demonstrate trajectory studi articulation between hermeneutic cultural history praxeological theory constitut possible path historically understand ways acting think relat represent practic context interdependence shape social spac history historical,1.0.0,d60911bacdbc40c7
2357-4720,HyS51.pdf,HyS51_0,es,tical methodology. This is,"| Este artículo buscó demostrar la interdependencia entre la hermenéutica, la historia cultural y la teoría praxeológica, las opciones técnicas para el abordaje de fuentes Hist.Soc. 51 (julio-diciembre de 2026) / pp. 11-37 ISSN-L 0121-8417 / E-ISSN: 2357-4720 / DOI: https://doi.org/10.15446/hys.n51.122135 [13] Alexandra Ferreira Martins-Ribeiro / Alboni Marisa Dudeque Pianovski-Vieira / Maria Cecilia Barreto Amorim-Pilla (bibliográficas, documentales y de campo - historia oral) y la metodología de la prosopografía para el análisis de trayectorias. Para ello, se propuso esbozar algunos postulados de la hermenéutica, la historia cultural y la teoría praxeológica; explicar la posible relación entre estos constructos teóricos; y analizar opciones técnicas viables para la recolección de fuentes y el uso fructífero de la prosopografía como metodología analítica. Se trata de una investigación bibliográfica sustentada en el marco teórico de la hermenéutica de Ricœur, la historia cultural y el concepto de representaciones desarrollado por Chartier y Burke, así como en los presupuestos de la teoría praxeológica de Bourdieu —habitus, capital y campo—, la metodología de la Historia Oral propuesta por Amado y Ferreira, y la prosopografía de Stone. Los resultados muestran que, en los estudios de trayectoria, la articulación entre la hermenéutica, la historia cultural y la teoría praxeológica constituye una vía fecunda para comprender históricamente las formas de pensar y actuar, al vincular las representaciones y las prácticas con los contextos de interdependencia que configuran los espacios sociales","| historia; Método histórico; biografías; historia oral; prosopografía; historia social. Introdução Nesse artigo, consideraram-se os pressupostos, acerca de trajetória, que compreendem a vida entrelaçada ao contexto histórico, político, social, cultural e as múltiplas relações em que essa se estabelece. Nessa perspectiva, a trajetória de uma pessoa é complexa e multifacetada, como enfatiza Bour",marcadores,tical methodology this is,este articulo busco demostrar interdependencia entre hermeneutica historia cultural teoria praxeologica opcion tecnic abordaje fuent hist soc 51 julio-diciembre 2026 pp 11-37 issn-l 0121-8417 e-issn 2357-4720 doi https doi org 10 15446 hys n51 122135 13 alexandra ferreira martins-ribeiro alboni marisa dudeque pianovski-vieira maria cecilia barreto amorim-pilla bibliografic documental campo historia oral metodologia prosopografia analisis trayectori ello propuso esbozar algun postulad hermeneutica historia cultural teoria praxeologica explicar posible relacion entre estos construct teoric analizar opcion tecnic viabl recoleccion fuent uso fructifero prosopografia como metodologia analitica trata investigacion bibliografica sustentada marco teorico hermeneutica ricoeur historia cultural concepto represent desarrollado chartier burke asi como presupuest teoria praxeologica bourdieu --habitus capital campo-- metodologia historia oral propuesta amado ferreira prosopografia stone resultad muestran estudi trayectoria articulacion entre hermeneutica historia cultural teoria praxeologica constituye via fecunda comprender historica form pensar actuar vincular represent practic context interdependencia configuran espaci social,historia metodo historico biografi historia oral prosopografia historia social introducao nesse artigo consideraram-se os pressupost acerca trajetoria compreendem vida entrelacada ao contexto historico politico social cultural as multipl relaco em essa estabelece nessa perspectiva trajetoria uma pessoa complexa multifacetada como enfatiza bour,tical methodology this is este articulo busco demostrar interdependencia entre hermeneutica historia cultural teoria praxeologica opcion tecnic abordaje fuent hist soc 51 julio-diciembre 2026 pp 11-37 issn-l 0121-8417 e-issn 2357-4720 doi https doi org 10 15446 hys n51 122135 13 alexandra ferreira martins-ribeiro alboni marisa dudeque pianovski-vieira maria cecilia barreto amorim-pilla bibliografic documental campo historia oral metodologia prosopografia analisis trayectori ello propuso esbozar algun postulad hermeneutica historia cultural teoria praxeologica explicar posible relacion entre estos construct teoric analizar opcion tecnic viabl recoleccion fuent uso fructifero prosopografia como metodologia analitica trata investigacion bibliografica sustentada marco teorico hermeneutica ricoeur historia cultural concepto represent desarrollado chartier burke asi como presupuest teoria praxeologica bourdieu --habitus capital campo-- metodologia historia oral propuesta amado ferreira prosopografia stone resultad muestran estudi trayectoria articulacion entre hermeneutica historia cultural teoria praxeologica constituye via fecunda comprender historica form pensar actuar vincular represent practic context interdependencia configuran espaci social historia metodo historico biografi historia oral prosopografia historia social introducao nesse artigo consideraram-se os pressupost acerca trajetoria compreendem vida entrelacada ao contexto historico politico social cultural as multipl relaco em essa estabelece nessa perspectiva trajetoria uma pessoa complexa multifacetada como enfatiza bour,1.0.0,42f1b140814fe645
2357-4720,HyS51.pdf,HyS51_1,es,"de Colombia, editado por Álvaro Tirado, 9-61. Bogotá: Planeta.","| A mediados de un siglo XVIII, caracterizado por constantes cambios ideológicos y la llegada de la Ilustración al territorio de la Nueva España, María Ignacia de Azlor y Echeverz decidió fundar el colegio y convento de Nuestra Señora del Pilar mejor conocido como “La Enseñanza”, esto con la firme intención de instruir a todas las mujeres —sin distinción de clases o castas—, para que pudieran integrarse a los requerimientos que los nuevos tiempos exigían. Dentro de la educación que pretendía proporcionar, un aspecto de suma importancia fue el conjunto religioso y colegial que desde su portada presentaba un discurso claro y bien definido a partir del uso de un léxico barroco, pero ¿cuál era el mensaje? Bajo la hipótesis que en dicha portada se plasmó un razonamiento que posicionaba a la mujer como parte integral y trascendente de la educación masculina, el presente artículo tiene como objetivo proporcionar un primer acercamiento a la lectura que subyace en ella, esto a partir de su análisis iconográfico e iconológico con la intención de comprender la manera en que podía ser leído, a la par de intentar conocer el mensaje que su fundadora buscó aportar a la sociedad de su época",| educación; mujeres; Nueva España; simbolismo; colegios; siglo XVIII. A fragment of history: the façade of the Church of Our Lady of Pilar “La Enseñanza” in Mexico City and its symbolic implication for the New Spanish society in the 18th century,marcadores,colombia editado alvaro tirado 9-61 bogota planeta,mediad siglo xviii caracterizado constant cambi ideologic llegada ilustracion territorio nueva espana maria ignacia azlor echeverz decidio fundar colegio convento nuestra senora pilar mejor conocido como ensenanza esto firme intencion instruir todas mujer --sin distincion clas castas-- pudieran integrarse requer nuev tiemp exigian dentro educacion pretendia proporcionar aspecto suma importancia fue conjunto religioso colegial desde portada presentaba discurso claro bien definido partir uso lexico barroco pero cual era mensaje bajo hipotesis dicha portada plasmo razonamiento posicionaba mujer como parte integral trascendente educacion masculina presente articulo tiene como objetivo proporcionar primer acercamiento lectura subyace ella esto partir analisis iconografico iconologico intencion comprender manera podia ser leido par intentar conocer mensaje fundadora busco aportar sociedad epoca,educacion mujer nueva espana simbolismo colegi siglo xviii fragment of history the facade of the church of our lady of pilar ensenanza in mexico city and its symbolic implication for the new spanish society in the 18th century,colombia editado alvaro tirado 9-61 bogota planeta mediad siglo xviii caracterizado constant cambi ideologic llegada ilustracion territorio nueva espana maria ignacia azlor echeverz decidio fundar colegio convento nuestra senora pilar mejor conocido como ensenanza esto firme intencion instruir todas mujer --sin distincion clas castas-- pudieran integrarse requer nuev tiemp exigian dentro educacion pretendia proporcionar aspecto suma importancia fue conjunto religioso colegial desde portada presentaba discurso claro bien definido partir uso lexico barroco pero cual era mensaje bajo hipotesis dicha portada plasmo razonamiento posicionaba mujer como parte integral trascendente educacion masculina presente articulo tiene como objetivo proporcionar primer acercamiento lectura subyace ella esto partir analisis iconografico iconologico intencion comprender manera podia ser leido par intentar conocer mensaje fundadora busco aportar sociedad epoca educacion mujer nueva espana simbolismo colegi siglo xviii fragment of history the facade of the church of our lady of pilar ensenanza in mexico city and its symbolic implication for the new spanish society in the 18th century,1.0.0,a8b5d3f2a5f85032
2357-4720,HyS51.pdf,HyS51_1,en,oso y colegial que desde su portada presentaba un discurso claro y bien,"| In the mid-18th century—a period marked by ideological transformations and the diffusion of Enlightenment thought into New Spain—María Ignacia de Azlor y Echeverz established the Colegio and Convent of Our Lady of Pilar, popularly known as La Enseñanza. 38-64 Un fragmento de historia Cómo citar / How to Cite Item: Pascacio-Guillén, Bertha. 2026. “Un fragmento de historia: la portada de la iglesia de Nuestra Señora del Pilar “La Enseñanza” en la Ciudad de México y su implicación simbólica para la sociedad novohispana del siglo XVIII”. Historia y Sociedad (51): 38-64. https://doi.org/10.15446/hys.n51.123993 ? *Recibido: 19 de noviembre de 2025/ Aprobado: 27 de abril de 2026/ Modificado: 20 de mayo de 2026. El artículo no contó con ningún apoyo ni financiación institucional. **Doctora en Historia del Arte por la Universidad Nacional Autónoma de México. Áreas de especialización: Historia del arte, patrimonio mueble e inmueble, patrimonio histórico, historia cultural, etnohistoria del área maya. https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2153-623X sakilja@gmail.com Hist.Soc. 51 (julio-diciembre de 2026) / pp. 38-64 ISSN-L 0121-8417 / E-ISSN: 2357-4720 / DOI: https://doi.org/10.15446/hys.n51.123993 [39] Un fragmento de historia Conceived as an inclusive project, it sought to provide education for women of all social classes and castes, thereby enabling their participation in the intellectual and civic demands of the new era. Within this initiative, the architectural and religious ensemble itself played a decisive role: its façade articulated a deliberate visual discourse through the deployment of Baroque vocabulary. The central question, however, concerns the nature of this message. Proceeding from the hypothesis that the façade inscribed a reasoning which positioned women as integral and transcendent within the framework of male education, this article advances a preliminary interpretive approach. Through iconographic and iconological analysis, it aims to reconstruct the modes of reception available to contemporaries and to elucidate the symbolic program that its founder sought to embed in the social fabric of her time",| education; women; New Spain; symbolism; colegios; 18th century Um fragmento da história: a fachada da Igreja de Nossa Senhora do Pilar “La Enseñanza” na Cidade do México e suas implicações simbólicas para a sociedade neoespanhola do século XVIII,marcadores,oso colegial que desde su portada presentaba un discurso claro bien,mid-18th century--a period mark ideological transform diffusion enlightenment thought into new spain--maria ignacia de azlor echeverz establish colegio convent our lady pilar popularly known la ensenanza 38-64 un fragmento de historia como citar how cite item pascacio-guillen bertha 2026 un fragmento de historia la portada de la iglesia de nuestra senora del pilar la ensenanza en la ciudad de mexico su implicacion simbolica para la sociedad novohispana del siglo xviii historia sociedad 51 38-64 http doi org 10 15446 hys n51 123993 recibido 19 de noviembre de 2025 aprobado 27 de abril de 2026 modificado 20 de mayo de 2026 el articulo no conto con ningun apoyo ni financiacion institucional doctora en historia del arte por la universidad nacional autonoma de mexico area de especializacion historia del arte patrimonio mueble inmueble patrimonio historico historia cultural etnohistoria del area maya http orcid org 0000-0002-2153-623x sakilja gmail com hist soc 51 julio-diciembre de 2026 pp 38-64 issn-l 0121-8417 e-issn 2357-4720 doi http doi org 10 15446 hys n51 123993 39 un fragmento de historia conceiv inclusive project sought provide education women all social class cast thereby enabl their participation intellectual civic demand new era within initiative architectural religiou ensemble itself play decisive role its facade articulat deliberate visual discourse through deployment baroque vocabulary central question however concern nature message proceed hypothesi facade inscrib reason which position women integral transcendent within framework male education article advanc preliminary interpretive approach through iconographic iconological analysi aims reconstruct mode reception available contemporari elucidate symbolic program its founder sought embed social fabric her time,education women new spain symbolism colegio 18th century um fragmento da historia fachada da igreja de nossa senhora do pilar la ensenanza na cidade do mexico suas implicaco simbolica para sociedade neoespanhola do seculo xviii,oso colegial que desde su portada presentaba un discurso claro bien mid-18th century--a period mark ideological transform diffusion enlightenment thought into new spain--maria ignacia de azlor echeverz establish colegio convent our lady pilar popularly known la ensenanza 38-64 un fragmento de historia como citar how cite item pascacio-guillen bertha 2026 un fragmento de historia la portada de la iglesia de nuestra senora del pilar la ensenanza en la ciudad de mexico su implicacion simbolica para la sociedad novohispana del siglo xviii historia sociedad 51 38-64 http doi org 10 15446 hys n51 123993 recibido 19 de noviembre de 2025 aprobado 27 de abril de 2026 modificado 20 de mayo de 2026 el articulo no conto con ningun apoyo ni financiacion institucional doctora en historia del arte por la universidad nacional autonoma de mexico area de especializacion historia del arte patrimonio mueble inmueble patrimonio historico historia cultural etnohistoria del area maya http orcid org 0000-0002-2153-623x sakilja gmail com hist soc 51 julio-diciembre de 2026 pp 38-64 issn-l 0121-8417 e-issn 2357-4720 doi http doi org 10 15446 hys n51 123993 39 un fragmento de historia conceiv inclusive project sought provide education women all social class cast thereby enabl their participation intellectual civic demand new era within initiative architectural religiou ensemble itself play decisive rol