2357-626X,2-6187-Biomimetic+Kinetic_2026.pdf,2-6187-Biomimetic+Kinetic_2026_0,es,"ovement mechanism of Spanish moss, and the geometric form","* ** *** Master’s Student in Architectural Design, Gazi University, Ankara (Türkiye) Gazi University, Graduate School of Natural and Applied Sciences, Department of Architecture, Architectural Design Program, Ankara (Türkiye) https://orcid.org/0009-0003-8399-007X oznur.kar7@gmail.com / 23831101010@gazi.edu.tr Integrated PhD in Architectural Design, METU, Ankara (Türkiye) University of Bath, Department of Architecture & Civil Engineering, Bath (England) Postdoctoral Texas A&M University, Department of Architecture, Texas (USA) Gazi University,Graduate School of Natural and Applied Sciences, Department of Architecture, Architectural Design Program, Ankara (Türkiye) https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2128-2858 https://scholar.google.com/citations?hl=tr&user=A2ZSb2YAAAAJ semraarslanselcuk@gmail.com / semraselcuk@gazi.edu.tr Master’s in Architectural Design, Karadeniz Technical University, Trabzon (Türkiye) PhD in Architectural Design, Gazi University, Ankara (Türkiye) Faculty of Architecture, Karadeniz Technical University, Trabzon (Türkiye) https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1049-2689 https://scholar.google.com/citations?hl=tr&user=P0X6KQUAAAAJ gunesavinc@gmail.com /gunesavinc@gazi.edu.tr En tiempos recientes, debido al cambio climático, al aumento de la conciencia ambiental y al avance tecnológico, las “estructuras ecológicas” han cobrado gran importancia. La tecnología facilita la comprensión y la aplicación de los principios de la naturaleza en el diseño mediante la promoción de estrategias sostenibles. En climas cálidos, la termorregulación es vital: el aumento de la temperatura afecta la eficiencia energética y el confort, lo que impulsa soluciones como las fachadas cinéticas. Estos sistemas, inspirados en la naturaleza, responden a factores externos, como la luz solar y la temperatura, y mejoran la armonía entre lo construido y el medio natural. Este estudio propone un modelo de fachada cinética para el equilibrio térmico y la optimización de la luz natural. Inspirado en la base de datos de AskNature, imita los micropelos de la hormiga plateada del Sahara para reflejar el calor, el mecanismo de movimiento del musgo español y la geometría del panal. Así, ofrece una solución sostenible de termorregulación para envolventes arquitectónicas modernas",biomimética; diseño inspirado en la naturaleza; fachada cinética; fachada receptiva; termorregulación · Öznur KARAKUŞ · Semra ARSLAN-SELÇUK · Güneş MUTLU-AVİNÇ (Bogotá) VOL 28 · Nº 2 · JULIO-DICIEMBRE 2026 · ISSN: 1657-0308 · E-ISSN: 2357-626X | 37,marcadores,ovement mechanism of spanish moss and the geometric form,master student in architectural design gazi university ankara turkiye gazi university graduate school of natural and applied scienc department of architecture architectural design program ankara turkiye https orcid org 0009-0003-8399-007x oznur kar7 gmail com 23831101010 gazi edu tr integrated phd in architectural design metu ankara turkiye university of bath department of architecture civil engineering bath england postdoctoral texas university department of architecture texas usa gazi university graduate school of natural and applied scienc department of architecture architectural design program ankara turkiye https orcid org 0000-0002-2128-2858 https scholar google com citations hl tr user a2zsb2yaaaaj semraarslanselcuk gmail com semraselcuk gazi edu tr master in architectural design karadeniz technical university trabzon turkiye phd in architectural design gazi university ankara turkiye faculty of architecture karadeniz technical university trabzon turkiye https orcid org 0000-0003-1049-2689 https scholar google com citations hl tr user p0x6kquaaaaj gunesavinc gmail com gunesavinc gazi edu tr tiemp recient debido cambio climatico aumento conciencia ambiental avance tecnologico estructur ecologic han cobrado gran importancia tecnologia facilit