2357-626X,5-5878-Semiotica+interpretativa_2026.pdf,5-5878-Semiotica+interpretativa_2026_0,es,"ignificados, prácticas y configuraciones simbólicas","Cómo citar | 95 REVISTA DE (BOGOTÁ) 96 | Abstract * ** *** Licenciada en Arquitectura, Universidad del Valle de México. Tuxtla Gutiérrez (México). Doctora en Arquitectura, Universidad de Guanajuato. Guanajuato (México). Filiación institucional: Secretaría de Ciencia, Humanidades, Tecnología e Innovación, comisionada en la Facultad de Humanidades de la Universidad de Ciencias y Artes de Chiapas. Centro Mexicano de Investigación, Diseño, Cultura y Ciencias Aplicadas, CIDICA. https://scholar.google.com/citations?hl=es&user=B8zH110AAAAJ https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4933-5154 talia.figueroa@cidica.mx; talia.figueroa@gmail.com Licenciada en Arquitectura, Universidad Autónoma del Estado de México. Toluca (México). Doctora en Diseño, Universidad Autónoma del Estado de México. Toluca (México). Filiación institucional: Universidad Autónoma del Estado de México, Facultad de Arquitectura y Diseño, Centro de Investigación en Arquitectura y Diseño, Cuerpo académico Diseño, Territorio e Inclusión. https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=ZkYHakUAAAAJ&hl=es https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5974-1511 eesolanome@uaemex.mx; eskasolano@gmail.com Ingeniera Civil, Universidad del Valle de México. Tuxtla Gutiérrez (México). Doctora en Arquitectura, Diseño y Urbanismo, Universidad Autónoma del Estado de Morelos (México). Filiación institucional: Universidad Nacional Autónoma de México, Facultad de Ingeniería. https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=LXVh5YQAAAAJ&hl=es https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1156-5958 angelafigueroa@comunidad.unam.mx; figueroaesquinca@gmail.com This article proposes and applies a qualitative method grounded in interpretive semiotics to identify variables or analytical categories in urban phenomena, specifically ethnic residential segregation, and to contrast them with variables employed in previous quantitative studies. The research is based on the epistemological assumption that a semiotic-hermeneutic approach makes it possible to identify sociocultural dimensions that have not been sufficiently addressed by the quantitative tradition dominant in this field. Drawing on a review of the quantitative origins of residential segregation studies and the application of the interpretive approach to urban text, context, and interpretation, a procedure is developed for analyzing meanings, practices, and symbolic configurations present in urban space. This process made it possible to construct analytical categories comparable to variables previously established in the specialized literature. The results highlight the relevance of historical conflicts, religion, and forms of self-government linked to crime as explanatory dimensions of ethnic residential segregation. These categories broaden the prevailing socioeconomic emphasis by incorporating sociocultural dimensions that add complexity to the understanding of the phenomenon. Overall, the article contributes a replicable methodological model that expands the analytical framework of residential segregation and provides conceptual tools for the study of urban phenomena in Mexico and Latin America",city; ethnic; hermeneutics; indigenous; methodology; segregation; sign; symbolic Talía Esther Figueroa-Esquinca · Eska Elena Solano-Meneses · Carla Ángela Figueroa-Esquinca (Bogotá) VOL 28 · Nº 2 · JULIO-DICIEMBRE 2026 · ISSN: 1657-0308 · E-ISSN: 2357-626X | 97,marcadores,ignificad practic configur simbolic,como citar 95 revista bogota 96 abstract licenciada arquitectura universidad valle mexico tuxtla gutierrez mexico doctora arquitectura universidad guanajuato guanajuato mexico filiacion institucional secretaria ciencia humanidad tecnologia innovacion comisionada facultad humanidad universidad cienci artes chiap centro mexicano investigacion diseno cultura cienci aplicad cidica https scholar google com citations hl user b8zh110aaaaj https orcid org 0000-