2357-6308,3-embarazo-adolescente-v44-n2.pdf,3-embarazo-adolescente-v44-n2_0,en,", informes y documentos en las bases","Objective: Teenage pregnancy is defined as gestation in women between 15 and 19 years of age. This article aims to analyze the behavior of adolescent pregnancy based on public policies and sexual and reproductive health strategies in Medellín, Antioquia and Colombia between 2012 to 2022. Methods: Research was carried out through reviews and documentary analysis of sexual and reproductive health policies and strategies, and the compilation of secondary information sources obtained from DANE based on epidemiological estimators such as 13-26 ARTÍCULO ORIGINAL - ORIGINAL ARTICLE - ARTIGO ORIGINAL | Análisis de la tendencia del embarazo adolescente, políticas públicas y estrategias de salud sexual y reproductiva en Medellín, Antioquia y Colombia entre 2012 y 2022 14 | julio-diciembre 2025 | MEDICINA U.P.B. 44(2) : the percentage of teenage pregnancies, percentage of live births to mothers aged 15 to 19, and the total number of cases of teenage pregnancy at the municipal, departmental, and national levels. Results: A total of 106 813 articles, reports, and documents were obtained from the databases. For the writing of the documentary analysis, 30 were finally selected. 14 corresponded to articles on strategies to impact teenage pregnancy, three were government technical documents, seven were public policies, and six were other related norms. All of these demonstrate the impact of policies and strategies on sexual and reproductive health in the social, family, and community environment. Conclusion: The set of public policies and strategies implemented in the city of Medellín positively impact indicators related to teenage pregnancy; however, there is a need to continue improving and emphasize citizen participation and education in sexual and reproductive health",Teenage Pregnancy; Public Policies; Sexual and Reproductive Health; Contraception,marcadores,inform documento en las base,objective teenage pregnancy defin gestation women between 15 19 year age article aims analyze behavior adolescent pregnancy based public polici sexual reproductive health strategi medellin antioquia colombia between 2012 2022 method research carri out through review documentary analysi sexual reproductive health polici strategi compilation secondary information sourc obtain dane based epidemiological estimator such 13-26 articulo original original article artigo original analisi de la tendencia del embarazo adolescente politica publica estrategia de salud sexual reproductiva en medellin antioquia colombia entre 2012 2022 14 julio-diciembre 2025 medicina 44 percentage teenage pregnanci percentage live birth mother aged 15 19 total number case teenage pregnancy municipal departmental national level result total 106 813 articl report document obtain databas writ documentary analysi 30 finally select 14 correspond articl strategi impact teenage pregnancy three government technical document seven public polici six other relat norm all these demonstrate impact polici strategi sexual reproductive health social family community environment conclusion set public polici strategi implement city medellin positively impact indicator relat teenage pregnancy however there need continue improv emphasize citizen participation education sexual reproductive health,teenage pregnancy public polici sexual reproductive health contraception,inform documento en las base objective teenage pregnancy defin gestation women between 15 19 year age article aims analyze behavior adolescent pregnancy based public polici sexual reproductive health strategi medellin antioquia colombia between 2012 2022 method research carri out through review documentary analysi sexual reproductive health polici strategi compilation secondary information sourc obtain dane based epidemiological estimator such 13-26 articulo original original article artigo original analisi de la tendencia del embarazo adolescente politica publica estrategia de salud sexual reproductiva en medellin antioquia colombia entre 2012 2022 14 julio-diciembre 2025 medicina 44 percentage teenage pregnanci percentage live birth mother aged 15 19 total number case teenage pregnancy municipal departmental national level result total 106 813 articl report document obtain databas writ documentary analysi 30 finally select 14 correspond articl strategi impact teenage pregnancy three government technical document seven public polici six other relat norm all these demonstrate impact polici strategi sexual reproductive health social family community environment conclusion set public polici strategi implement city medellin positively impact indicator relat teenage pregnancy however there need continue improv emphasize citizen participation education sexual reproductive health teenage pregnancy public polici sexual reproductive health contraception,1.0.0,6eea164d63ab4b73
2357-6308,4-artritis-psoriásica-v44-n2.pdf,4-artritis-psoriásica-v44-n2_0,es,"inosa Bohorquez I,","Objetivo: la artritis psoriásica, como manifestación de la enfermedad psoriásica, es una condición crónica e inflamatoria con manifestaciones articulares, dactilitis, entesitis y cambios en la piel y uñas. A pesar de las diversas recomendaciones de tratamiento, los factores que determinan la respuesta estos, en la población latinoamericana, no han sido esclarecidos. El objetivo de este estudio es describir las características de los pacientes con artritis psoriásica e identificar las diferencias en la respuesta al tratamiento y su impacto en la calidad de vida en un centro médico de Medellín. Métodos: se analizaron registros médicos de 114 pacientes con enfermedad psoriásica y artritis, para evaluar variables sociodemográficas, clínicas, de tratamiento y clinimétricas. Se realizó un análisis univariado para variables cuantitativas y cualitativas, y un análisis bivariado para evaluar las diferencias entre las variables, comparándolas mediante la prueba de Chi². Resultados: se observó una diferencia significativa entre la afiliación al régimen contributivo de EPS (p 0,041) y el tratamiento inicial con biológicos (p 0,044). Existe una asociación negativa entre la psoriasis vulgar y la artritis axial (OR 0,11; IC 95 % 0,0269–0,476; p < 0,001) y entre psoriasis ungular y artritis axial (OR 0,20; IC 95 % 0,0567–0,767; p=0,011). Niveles elevados de colesterol total y LDL se relacionaron con menor probabilidad de mejora del 90 % según la evaluación de la severidad y área de la psoriasis, PASI 90 (p < 0,05). La hemoglobina más baja se relaciona con peor respuesta terapéutica (p<0,05). Conclusión: los hombres fueron los más afectados por la enfermedad psoriásica, las comorbilidades y el riesgo cardiovascular. El metotrexato es el medicamento más utilizado asociado con una mejora en la calidad de vida. Los medicamentos biológicos se asociaron positivamente con el logro de un PASI 90",Psoriasis; Artritis psoriásica; Tratamiento,marcadores,inosa bohorquez,objetivo artritis psoriasica como manifestacion enfermedad psoriasica condicion cronica inflamatoria manifest articular dactilitis entesitis cambi piel unas pesar divers recomend tratamiento factor determinan respuesta estos poblacion latinoamericana no han sido esclarecid objetivo este estudio describir caracteristic pacient artritis psoriasica identificar diferenci respuesta tratamiento impacto calidad vida centro medico medellin metod analizaron registr medic 114 pacient enfermedad psoriasica artritis evaluar variabl sociodemografic clinic tratamiento clinimetric realizo analisis univariado variabl cuantitativ cualitativ analisis bivariado evaluar diferenci entre variabl comparandol mediante prueba chi2 resultad observo diferencia significativa entre afiliacion regimen contributivo eps 041 tratamiento inicial biologic 044 existe asociacion negativa entre psoriasis vulgar artritis axial or 11 ic 95 0269-0 476 001 entre psoriasis ungular artritis axial or 20 ic 95 0567-0 767 011 nivel elevad colesterol total ldl relacionaron menor probabilidad mejora 90 segun evaluacion severidad area psoriasis pasi 90 05 hemoglobina mas baja relaciona peor respuesta terapeutica 05 conclusion hombr fueron mas afectad enfermedad psoriasica comorbilidad riesgo cardiovascular metotrexato medicamento mas utilizado asociado mejora calidad vida medicament biologic asociaron positiva logro pasi 90,psoriasis artritis psoriasica tratamiento,inosa bohorquez objetivo artritis psoriasica como manifestacion enfermedad psoriasica condicion cronica inflamatoria manifest articular dactilitis entesitis cambi piel unas pesar divers recomend tratamiento factor determinan respuesta estos poblacion latinoamericana no han sido esclarecid objetivo este estudio describir caracteristic pacient artritis psoriasica identificar diferenci respuesta tratamiento impacto calidad vida centro medico medellin metod analizaron registr medic 114 pacient enfermedad psoriasica artritis evaluar variabl sociodemografic clinic tratamiento clinimetric realizo analisis univariado variabl cuantitativ cualitativ analisis bivariado evaluar diferenci entre variabl comparandol mediante prueba chi2 resultad observo diferencia significativa entre afiliacion regimen contributivo eps 041 tratamiento inicial biologic 044 existe asociacion negativa entre psoriasis vulgar artritis axial or 11 ic 95 0269-0 476 001 entre psoriasis ungular artritis axial or 20 ic 95 0567-0 767 011 nivel elevad colesterol total ldl relacionaron menor probabilidad mejora 90 segun evaluacion severidad area psoriasis pasi 90 05 hemoglobina mas baja relaciona peor respuesta terapeutica 05 conclusion hombr fueron mas afectad enfermedad psoriasica comorbilidad riesgo cardiovascular metotrexato medicamento mas utilizado asociado mejora calidad vida medicament biologic asociaron positiva logro pasi 90 psoriasis artritis psoriasica tratamiento,1.0.0,81e3495fcad44b0f
2357-6308,4-artritis-psoriásica-v44-n2.pdf,4-artritis-psoriásica-v44-n2_0,en,Niveles elevados de colesterol total y LDL se relacionaron con menor probabilidad de,"Objective: psoriatic arthritis, as a manifestation of psoriatic disease, is a chronic and inflammatory condition, with articular symptoms, dactylitis, enthesitis and changes in the skin and nails. Despite the existence of various treatment recommendations, the factors determining the treatment response in the Latin American population have not been clarified. The aim of this study was to describe the characteristics of patients with psoriatic arthritis and identify the differences in the response to treatment and its impact on quality of life in a medical center in Medellín. 27-36 ARTÍCULO ORIGINAL - ORIGINAL ARTICLE - ARTIGO ORIGINAL | Artritis psoriásica, respuesta al tratamiento y cambio en la calidad de vida en población atendida en un centro de referencia en Medellín 28 | julio-diciembre 2025 | MEDICINA U.P.B. 44(2) : Methods: medical records of 114 patients with psoriatic disease and arthritis were analyzed to evaluate sociodemographic, clinical, treatment, and clinimetric variables. A univariate analysis was carried out for quantitative and qualitative variables and a bivariate analysis was carried out to evaluate differences between variables, comparing them using the Chi-squared test. Results: a significant difference was observed between affiliation to the EPS contributory regime (p 0.041) and initial treatment with biologicals (p 0.044). There is a negative association between psoriasis vulgaris and axial arthritis (OR 0.11; 95 % CI 0.0269–0.476; p< 0.001) and between nail psoriasis and axial arthritis (OR 0.20; 95 % CI 0.0567–0.767; p=0.011). High levels of total and LDL cholesterol were related to a lower probability of achieving a 90 % of improvement according to the scale PASI 90 (p<0.05). Lower hemoglobin is related to worse therapeutic response (p<0.05). Conclusion: men were the most affected with a higher association with comorbidities and cardiovascular risk. Methotrexate is the most used medication associated with an improvement in quality of life. Biological medications were positively associated with achieving a PASI 90 goal",Psoriasis; Psoriatic arthritis; Treatment,marcadores,nivel elevado de colesterol total ldl se relacionaron con menor probabilidad de,objective psoriatic arthriti manifestation psoriatic disease chronic inflammatory condition articular symptom dactyliti enthesiti chang skin nail despite existence variou treatment recommend factor determin treatment response latin american population have not been clarifi aim study describe characteristic patient psoriatic arthriti identify differenc response treatment its impact quality life medical center medellin 27-36 articulo original original article artigo original artriti psoriasica respuesta al tratamiento cambio en la calidad de vida en poblacion atendida en un centro de referencia en medellin 28 julio-diciembre 2025 medicina 44 method medical record 114 patient psoriatic disease arthriti analyz evaluate sociodemographic clinical treatment clinimetric variabl univariate analysi carri out quantitative qualitative variabl bivariate analysi carri out evaluate differenc between variabl compar them using chi-squar test result significant difference observ between affiliation eps contributory regime 041 initial treatment biological 044 there negative association between psoriasi vulgari axial arthriti 11 95 ci 0269-0 476 001 between nail psoriasi axial arthriti 20 95 ci 0567-0 767 011 high level total ldl cholesterol relat lower probability achiev 90 improvement accord scale pasi 90 05 lower hemoglobin relat worse therapeutic response 05 conclusion men most affect higher association comorbiditi cardiovascular risk methotrexate most used medication associat improvement quality life biological medic positively associat achiev pasi 90 goal,psoriasi psoriatic arthriti treatment,nivel elevado 