2357-6308,5-servicios-farmacéuticos-v44-n2.pdf,5-servicios-farmacéuticos-v44-n2_0,en,definieron adecuadamente la educación para,"Objective: To identify patients’ knowledge and needs regarding pharmaceutical care services in drugstores, pharmacies-drugstores, and outpatient pharmaceutical services in Antioquia, Colombia. Methods: A descriptive cross-sectional study was conducted with users of pharmaceutical establishments and outpatient pharmaceutical services. A semi-structured interview was designed, divided into three parts: sociodemographic characteristics, knowledge and perceived needs, and use of Information and Communication Technologies. 37-51 ARTÍCULO ORIGINAL - ORIGINAL ARTICLE - ARTIGO ORIGINAL | Acceso a servicios profesionales farmacéuticos: motivaciones, preferencias, barreras, conocimientos y uso de las TIC en pacientes de Antioquia 38 | julio-diciembre 2025 | MEDICINA U.P.B. 44(2) : Results: Of the 30 people interviewed, 53.3 % were users of Pharmaceutical Establishments (Drugstores, Pharmacies-Drugstores) and 46.7 % were users of Pharmaceutical Services. 100 % of the users of Pharmaceutical Establishments visited to acquire medications and other products, while 100 % of the users of Pharmaceutical Services visited solely to collect medications. Regarding knowledge about pharmaceutical care services, 10 % of the respondents correctly defined dispensing, while 6.7 % adequately defined health education. In contrast, 26.7 % agreed with the definition of pharmacovigilance. Additionally, regarding access to dispensing and health education services, respondents reported accessing these services at rates of 30 % and 10 %, respectively. Meanwhile, 96.7 % of the respondents stated they did not access pharmacovigilance services. Conclusions: Obstacles were identified in the provision of information and care, such as the willingness and knowledge of staff, their lack of time, and a focus on sales. These findings highlight the need to improve staff training and patient care",Community Pharmacy Services; Patient Participation; Information Technology; Medicine-Dispensing Establishments; Health Education,marcadores,definieron adecuadamente la educacion para,objective identify patient knowledge need regard pharmaceutical care servic drugstor pharmacies-drugstor outpatient pharmaceutical servic antioquia colombia method descriptive cross-sectional study conduct user pharmaceutical establishment outpatient pharmaceutical servic semi-structur interview design divid into three part sociodemographic characteristic knowledge perceiv need use information communication technologi 37-51 articulo original original article artigo original acceso servicio profesional farmaceutico motivacion preferencia barrera conocimiento uso de las tic en pacient de antioquia 38 julio-diciembre 2025 medicina 44 result 30 people interview 53 user pharmaceutical establishment drugstor pharmacies-drugstor 46 user pharmaceutical servic 100 user pharmaceutical establishment visit acquire medic other product while 100 user pharmaceutical servic visit solely collect medic regard knowledge about pharmaceutical care servic 10 respondent correctly defin dispens while adequately defin health education contrast 26 agre definition pharmacovigilance additionally regard acces dispens health education servic respondent report access these servic rate 30 10 respectively meanwhile 96 respondent stat they did not acces pharmacovigilance servic conclusion obstacl identifi provision information care such willingnes knowledge staff their lack time focu sale these finding highlight need improve staff train patient care,community pharmacy servic patient participation information technology medicine-dispens establishment health education,definieron adecuadamente la educacion para objective identify patient knowledge need regard pharmaceutical care servic drugstor pharmacies-drugstor outpatient pharmaceutical servic antioquia colombia method descriptive cross-sectional study conduct user pharmaceutical establishment outpatient pharmaceutical servic semi-structur interview design divid into three part sociodemographic characteristic knowledge perceiv need use information communication technologi 37-51 articulo original original article artigo original acceso servicio profesional farmaceutico motivacion preferencia barrera conocimiento uso de las tic en pacient de antioquia 38 julio-diciembre 2025 medicina 44 result 30 people interview 53 user pharmaceutical establishment drugstor pharmacies-drugstor 46 user pharmaceutical servic 100 user pharmaceutical establishment visit acquire medic other product while 100 user pharmaceutical servic visit solely collect medic regard knowledge about pharmaceutical care servic 10 respondent correctly defin dispens while adequately defin health education contrast 26 agre definition pharmacovigilance additionally regard acces dispens health education servic respondent report access these servic rate 30 10 respectively meanwhile 96 respondent stat they did not acces pharmacovigilance servic conclusion obstacl identifi provision information care such willingnes knowledge staff their lack time focu sale these finding highlight need improve staff train patient care community pharmacy servic patient participation information technology medicine-dispens establishment health education,1.0.0,cd5dcd83ef1557a6
2357-6308,Revista+45(1)+art+1+chequeo+1.pdf,Revista+45(1)+art+1+chequeo+1_0,es,Universidad de Antioquía.,"Objetivo: describir los factores relacionados con la mortalidad en población pediátrica menor de 5 años, debida a infección respiratoria aguda (IRA), en Antioquia durante el año 2022. Métodos: estudio cuantitativo, transversal y descriptivo que incluyó el universo de Fichas de Notificación número 591 de menores de 5 años fallecidos por IRA confirmada y su respectiva unidad de análisis, recolección de información posterior a la aprobación del Comité de Ética de la Institución Educativa y de la Secretaría Seccional de Salud de Antioquia. Análisis de información en el programa estadístico Jamovi 2.3. Resultados: el 53,5 % de los menores fallecidos eran niños, la tercera parte residía en centro poblado o área rural. El 60,6 % pertenecía a los estratos socioeconómicos 1 y 2 y al régimen subsidiado en salud, mientras que otros no contaban con afiliación al sistema de salud. El 10,7 % pertenecían a comunidades indígenas. Un 39,3 % de las madres no tenía ningún grado de escolaridad y el 75 % de las muertes sucedieron en el hospital. Como factores relacionados se identificó la ignorancia sobre los síntomas y signos de alerta por parte de la persona encargada del cuidado, incumplimiento de acciones de demanda inducida por el personal de salud, debilidad en la calidad de la atención recibida y demora de los cuidadores para buscar atención oportuna. Conclusiones: determinantes sociales de la salud, por ejemplo, la baja escolaridad materna o la pobreza, aumentan el riesgo de muerte en por infección respiratoria aguda en Antioquía, en la población estudiada",Mortalidad infantil; Menores; Determinantes sociales de la salud; Educación para la salud; Signos y síntomas,marcadores,universidad antioquia,objetivo describir factor relacionad mortalidad poblacion pediatrica menor anos debida infeccion respiratoria aguda ira antioquia durante ano 2022 metod estudio cuantitativo transversal descriptivo incluyo universo fich notificacion numero 591 menor anos fallecid ira confirmada respectiva unidad analisis recoleccion informacion posterior aprobacion comite etica institucion educativa secretaria seccional salud antioquia analisis informacion programa estadistico jamovi resultad 53 menor fallecid eran ninos tercera parte residia centro poblado area rural 60 pertenecia estrat socioeconomic regimen subsidiado salud mientr otros no contaban afiliacion sistema salud 10 pertenecian comunidad indigen 39 madr no tenia ningun grado escolaridad 75 muert sucedieron hospital como factor relacionad identifico ignorancia sobre sintom sign alerta parte persona encargada cuidado incumplimiento accion demanda inducida personal salud debilidad calidad atencion recibida demora cuidador buscar atencion oportuna conclusion determinant social salud ejemplo baja escolaridad materna pobreza aumentan riesgo muerte infeccion respiratoria aguda antioquia poblacion estudiada,mortalidad infantil menor determinant social salud educacion salud sign sintom,universidad antioquia objetivo describir factor relacionad mortalidad poblacion pediatrica menor anos debida infeccion respiratoria aguda ira antioquia durante ano 2022 metod estudio cuantitativo transversal descriptivo incluyo universo fich notificacion numero 591 menor anos fallecid ira confirmada respectiva unidad analisis recoleccion informacion posterior aprobacion comite etica institucion educativa secretaria seccional salud antioquia analisis informacion programa estadistico jamovi resultad 53 menor fallecid eran ninos tercera parte residia centro poblado area rural 60 pertenecia estrat socioeconomic regimen subsidiado salud mientr otros no contaban afiliacion sistema salud 10 pertenecian comunidad indigen 39 madr no tenia ningun grado escolaridad 75 muert sucedieron hospital como factor relacionad identifico ignorancia sobre sintom sign alerta parte persona encargada cuidado incumplimiento accion demanda inducida personal salud debilidad calidad atencion recibida demora cuidador buscar atencion oportuna conclusion determinant social salud ejemplo baja escolaridad materna pobreza aumentan riesgo muerte infeccion respiratoria aguda antioquia poblacion estudiada mortalidad infantil menor determinant social salud educacion salud sign sintom,1.0.0,88be8f8879788880
2357-6308,Revista+45(1)+art+1+chequeo+1.pdf,Revista+45(1)+art+1+chequeo+1_0,en,"alud, mientras que otros no contaban con afiliación al sistema","Objective: To describe the factors related to the mortality of minors under five years due to Acute Respiratory Infection in Antioquia during 2022. Methods: Cross-sectional descriptive study. It includes the universe of Notification Cards number 591 of children under five years who died of verified ARI and their respective Analysis Unit. Information collection after approval by the Ethics Committee of the Educational Institution and the Sectional Health Secretariat of Antioquia. The information was analyzed in the statistical software Jamovi 2.3. Results: 53.5% of the deceased children were boys, a third of whom lived in populated centers or rural areas. 60.6% belonged to socioeconomic strata 1 and 2 and were enrolled in subsidized health care, while the rest were not affiliated with the health system. 10.7% were from indigenous communities. 39.3% of the mothers had no schooling, and 75% of the deaths occurred in hospitals. Related factors were identified: caregiver ignorance of 2-11 López Herrera FE, et al. : MEDICINA U.P.B. 45(1) | enero-junio 2026 | 3 warning signs and symptoms, failure to comply with actions induced by demand by health personnel, poor quality of care received, and caregivers’ delay in seeking timely care. Conclusions: Social determinants of health such as poverty and low maternal schooling increase the risk of death due to Acute Respiratory Infection in children under five years in Antioquia",Infant Mortality; Minors; Determinants of Social Health; Health Education; Signs and Symptoms,marcadores,alud mientra que otro no contaban con afiliacion al sistema,objective describe factor relat mortality minor under five year due acute respiratory infection antioquia during 2022 method cross-sectional descriptive study includ universe notification card number 591 children under five year who died verifi ari thei