2382-3860,e6783.pdf,e6783_0,en,predice significativamente en la satisfacción laboral a través del,"Driven by technological advances and organizational changes following the pandemic, teleworking has transformed traditional work dynamics and gained greater relevance in the business environment. The objective of this research is to analyze its impact on job satisfaction among workers in the service sector in Metropolitan Lima. The study adopts a quantitative approach, with an applied and causal scope. Structured surveys using a Likert scale were administered to a sample of 207 workers through the QuestionPro platform. The data were processed using reliability tests, normality tests, and inferential analysis. The results show that teleworking significantly influences job satisfaction through work-life balance, stress reduction, and job autonomy, with work-life balance being the most influential dimension. In contrast, flexibility and schedule control did not show a significant relationship. It is concluded that teleworking represents a relevant modality for strengthening job satisfaction in the service sector, especially when it promotes autonomy, emotional well-being, and work-life balance. Furthermore, these findings contribute to understanding how specific dimensions of teleworking are associated with job satisfaction in the service sector, providing relevant empirical evidence in the context of Lima Metropolitana","Work autonomy, remote work, labor flexibility, service sector, work well-being. Jauregui Arroyo, R. R., Barrantes Limahuaya, T. L., Rojas Pomallanqui, F. N., Ccanto Canales, J. S., Carpio Meneses, M. E. & Aramayo Martínez, M. P. A / Económicas CUC, vol.47 no.1, pp.e6783, Enero – Junio, 2026 TELETRABAJO Y SATISFACCIÓN LABORAL: EVIDENCIA EN TRABAJADORES DEL SECTOR SERVICIOS DE LIMA METROPOLITANA",marcadores,predice significativamente en la satisfaccion laboral trav del,driven technological advanc organizational chang follow pandemic telework has transform 