2382-3860,e6932.pdf,e6932_0,en,instrumento validado y confiable que aporta al mejoramiento,"Today, people have become the central axis of organizational development, creating the need to identify tools that improve relationship processes between individuals and companies. For this purpose, a model for measuring human management practices is presented, along with the construction of a validated and reliable instrument that contributes to the improvement of Human Management. This instrument was later applied to MSMEs in Villavicencio, Colombia. The results showed differential elements between the practices carried out by organizations and the theoretical foundations. Based on this, a six-dimensional model is proposed, structured as follows: Organizational Aspects, Suitable People, Helping People Grow, Work Quality, Healthy Environment, and Human Management Practices. Different associations were found, showing the relevance of having a well-developed organizational process within the institution in order to strengthen the other dimensions. The association between dimensions allows the presentation of a tool that promotes the improvement of Human Management in organizations","Human resources management, micro, small and medium-sized enterprises, performance management, human capital. Torres-Flórezz, D., & Gallardo, N. / Económicas CUC, vol.47 no.1, pp..e236932, Enero – Junio, 2026 MODELO PARA MEDIR LA GESTIÓN HUMANA POR DIMENSIONES EN MIPYMES DE VILLAVICENCIO, COLOMBIA 2",marcadores,instrumento validado confiable que aporta al mejoramiento,today people have become central axis organizational development creat need identify tool improve relationship process between individual compani purpose model measur human management practic present along construction validat reliable instrument contribut improvement human management instrument later appli msme villavicencio colombia result show differential element between practic carri out organiz theoretical found based six-dimens