acteria total coli recuento microbiologico qp,reuse potential efficient sustainable technologi disinfection domestic wastewater critical safeguard public health environment pathogen contaminant threaten human well-be ecological balance application uv radiation consider environmentally sound alternative does not alter physicochemical characteristic treat effluent nor produce hazardou by-product nevertheles concern persist about durability uv lamp under adverse condition susceptibility system mechanical failure reduc efficiency deriv suspend solid induce clogg foul attenuation uv radiation study assess impact suspend solid compar unfilter wastewater ufww filter wastewater fww under low 471 mws cm2 medium 941 mw cm2 high 3722 mw cm2 uv dose 254 nm disinfection efficienci nearly 99 acros all treatment indicat solid concentration 50mg does not significantly impair uv performance coli inactivation measur most probable number mpn achiev efficienci 99 all case logarithmic inactivation valu rang tabc mpn qpcr confirm higher uv dose enhance microbial inactivation study also evaluat effectivenes microbiological total aerobic bacteria count tabc molecular quantitative real-time polymerase chain reaction qpcr result show qpcr target rpob gene detect higher microbial recovery log compar tabc highlight its superior sensitivity study underscor advantag uv disinfection includ its efficiency compact design cost-effectivenes compar chemical method palabra clave affiliation evaluacion de un sistema uv para la desinfeccion de agua residual domestica con potencial de reuso uv disinfection inactivation logarithm efficiency wastewater total bacteria coli microbiological count qpcr desinfeccion uv logaritmo de inactivacion eficiencia agua residual bacteria total coli recuento microbiologico qp,1.0.0,8be2481fc1a471ed
2382-4581,articulo+4+ID_2108_version_publicada.pdf,articulo+4+ID_2108_version_publicada_0,en,DESIGN AND EXECUTION,"The Dina Cretaceous field, operated by Ecopetrol S.A., is situated in the basin of Colombia's Upper Magdalena Valley. Peripheral water injection started in 1985, reaching a peak oil production rate of about 10,000 BOPD in 1988. Subsequently, water production increased, leading to a decline in oil output, primarily due to reservoir heterogeneity and an unfavorable mobility ratio. Between 2011 and 2015, Colombia undertook its first pilot initiative using Colloidal Dispersion Gels (CDG) for in‑depth profile modification. This effort later evolved into a full‑field application between 2019 and 2022, translating into substantial advancement in implementing chemical conformance technologies. During the new waterflooding phase, water channeling in some injection patterns highlighted the need to address thief zones. To avoid this, a novel rigid gel (BG) formulation was proposed, which uses a higher polymer concentration than CDG and replaces aluminum citrate with chromium acetate, thereby ensuring more effective conformance control under reservoir conditions. The BG injection was successfully executed through the existing CDG facilities. Over eight days of injection and a four‑day shut‑in, the treatment improved vertical sweep efficiency, blocked water channeling, and increased contact with unswept zones. Results showed enhanced oil production, reduced water cuts, and changes in injectivity, which confirmed the effectiveness of alternating bulk gel injections for reservoir conformance control",/ PALABRAS CLAVE AFFILIATION DISEÑO Y EJECUCIÓN DE UN TRATAMIENTO NOVEDOSO DE CONFORMANCE QUÍMICO USANDO GELES POLIMÉRICOS PARA MEJORAR LA EFICIENCIA VOLUMÉTRICA DE UN CAMPO DEL VALLE SUPERIOR DEL MAGDALENA. Waterflooding | Chemical conformance | Bulk gels | Colloidal Dispersion Gels . Inyección de agua | conformance químico | geles obturantes | geles de dispersión coloidal. A R T I C L E,marcadores,design execution,dina cretaceou field operat ecopetrol situat basin colombia upper magdalena valley peripheral water injection start 1985 reach peak oil production rate about 10 000 bopd 1988 subsequently water production increas lead decline oil output primarily due reservoir heterogeneity unfavorable mobility ratio between 2011 2015 colombia undertook its first pilot initiative using colloidal dispersion gels cdg in-depth profile modification effort later evolv into full-field application between 2019 2022 translat into substantial advancement implement chemical conformance technologi during new waterflood phase water channel some injection pattern highlight need addres thief zone avoid novel rigid gel bg formulation propos which uses higher polymer concentration than cdg replac aluminum citrate chromium acetate thereby ensur more effective conformance control under reservoir condition bg injection successfully execut through exist cdg faciliti over eight days injection four-day shut-in treatment improv vertical sweep efficiency block water channel increas contact unswept zone result show enhanc oil production reduc water cuts chang injectivity which confirm effectivenes alternat bulk gel injection reservoir conformance control,palabra clave affiliation diseno ejecucion de un tratamiento novedoso de conformance quimico usando gele polimerico para mejorar la eficiencia volumetrica de un campo del valle superior del magdalena waterflood chemical conformance bulk gels colloidal dispersion gels inyeccion de agua conformance quimico gele obturant gele de dispersion coloidal,design execution dina cretaceou field operat ecopetrol situat basin colombia upper magdalena valley peripheral water injection start 1985 reach peak oil production rate about 10 000 bopd 1988 subsequently water production increas lead decline oil output primarily due reservoir heterogeneity unfavorable mobility ratio between 2011 2015 colombia undertook its first pilot i