2382-4581,articulo+5+ID+2498_publicado.pdf,articulo+5+ID+2498_publicado_0,en,COMBINED EFFECT OF,"Vehicle emissions have significantly contributed to environmental degradation, ultimately leading to climate change. Extensive research is being conducted to identify alternative fuels with the potential to improve efficiency and decrease emissions. The objective of this study is to conduct experimental investigations on the engine efficiency and emission characteristics of a variable compression ratio engine fuelled with a blend of two biodiesels, ethanol, and Al2O3 nanoparticles. Biodiesels and ethanol were blended at 10% and 20% on a volume/volume basis, respectively, while 100 ppm of Al2O3 nanoparticles were incorporated into blends as additives. Experimental tests were conducted at a constant compression ratio of 18:1, while adjusting the loads to different levels. The percentage improvements in mechanical efficiency, brake thermal efficiency, and volumetric efficiency varied within specific ranges: 1.6–4.8%, 1.3–4.1%, and 1.0–2.4%, respectively. Diverse reductions in the emission percentages of HC, CO, CO2, smoke, and NO were observed. Specifically, reductions ranged from 1.7% to 13.7% for HC, 1.8% to 8.9% for CO, 2.7% to 13.8% for CO2, 1.2% to 8.9% for smoke, and 1.8% to 6.5% for NO. Importantly, the proposed fuel formulation can be implemented in existing compression ignition engines without hardware modification, offering a practical strategy for near-term decarbonisation of the diesel sector","/ PALABRAS CLAVE AFFILIATION EFECTO COMBINADO DE NANOPARTÍCULAS DE AL2O3 Y MEZCLAS CUATERNARIAS DE BIODIÉSEL EN EL RENDIMIENTO, LA COMBUSTIÓN Y LAS CARACTERÍSTICAS DE EMISIÓN DE UN MOTOR DE ENCENDIDO POR COMPRESIÓN Tamarind | Jatropha | Ethanol | Alumina | quaternary blend | nanoadditives Tamarindo | Jatropha | Etanol | Almina | mezcla cuaternaria | nanoaditivos A R T I C L E I N F O R",marcadores,combin effect,vehicle emission have significantly contribut environmental d