2389-7848,PLANTILLA_10_7368__JRR.pdf,PLANTILLA_10_7368__JRR_0,en,"al explícita. Para analizar y contratar el, modelo, se aplicaron regresiones","The purpose of this research is to analyze the relationship between Gross Domestic Product (GDP), Research and This study presents a job search model designed to improve the effectiveness of outplacement or assisted relocation programs. The model brings together antecedent variables --such as self-efficacy, self-regulation traits, job search skills, and social support-- with behavioral variables including search intensity, search strategies, and information channels. Unlike previous approaches, our proposal explicitly incorporates job search strategies as a behavioral variable to be tested. To examine and validate the model, we conducted hierarchical regression analyses using a sample of 106 unemployed individuals in Spain. The findings show that, among the antecedent variables, only self-efficacy has a direct, positive, and statistically significant effect on receiving job offers. The results also suggest that exploratory search strategies and search intensity may act as mediating factors, contributing to an increase in the number of offers obtained. Overall, the study highlights 1 PhD. Universidad de Vigo. España. Email: pedropablo.rey@uvigo.gal ORCID: https://orcid.org/0009-0009-6667-2495 2 PhD. Universidad de Vigo. España. Email: hugo.perez.moure@uvigo.gal ORCID: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2233-0057 3 PhD. Universidad de Vigo. España. Email: velando@uvigo.gal ORCID: https://orcid.org/0009-0009-2584-9442 4 PhD. Universidad de Vigo. España. Email: miguelangel.crespo@uvigo.gal ORCID: https://orcid.org/0009-0004-4011-9580 Factores de la búsqueda de empleo y su incidencia en el diseño de los programas de recolocación asistidas 16 Clío América / ISSN Impreso: 1909-941X / ISSN Web: 2389-7848 / Vol. 20 No. 39 enero – junio de 2026 https://doi.org/10.21676/23897848.7368 the need for outplacement programs to move beyond a traditional focus on technical assistance and adopt an approach centered on behavioral and motivational change","outplacement; job search; job search intensity; self-efficacy; exploratory strategy.. JEL: J64, M51, M53",marcadores,al explicita para analizar contratar el modelo se aplicaron regresion,purpose research analyze relationship between gros domestic product gdp research study present job search model design improve effectivenes outplacement assist relocation program model bring together antecedent variabl such self-efficacy self-regulation trait job search skill social support behavioral variabl includ search intensity search strategi information channel unlike previou approach our proposal explicitly incorporat job search strategi behavioral variable test examine validate model we conduct hierarchical regression analys using sample 106 unemploy individual spain finding show among antecedent variabl only self-efficacy has direct positive statistically significant effect receiv job offer result also suggest exploratory search strategi search intensity may act mediat factor contribut increase number offer obtain overall study highlight phd universidad de vigo espana email pedropablo rey uvigo gal orcid http orcid org 0009-0009-6667-2495 phd universidad de vigo espana email hugo perez moure uvigo gal orcid http orcid org 0000-0002-2233-0057 phd universidad de vigo espana email velando uvigo gal orcid http orcid org 0009-0009-2584-9442 phd universidad de vigo espana email miguelangel crespo uvigo gal orcid http orcid org 0009-0004-4011-9580 factor de la busqueda de empleo su incidencia en el diseno de los programa de recolocacion asistida 16 clio america issn impreso 1909-941x issn web 2389-7848 vol 20 no 39 enero junio de 2026 http doi org 10 21676 23897848 7368 need outplacement program move beyond traditional focu technical assistance adopt approach center behavioral motivational change,outplacement job search job search intensity self-efficacy exploratory strategy