xtual como expositivo argumentativo favorecen desarrollo habilidad inferencial critic advierte adem transicion enfoqu tradicional hacia practic centrad comprension produccion textual estrategi didactic escritura lectura escuela primaria educacion basica,1.0.0,564f78185e85049b
2389-7856,6_6762+Art_Estrategias+didácticas+lectura_109-128.pdf,6_6762+Art_Estrategias+didácticas+lectura_109-128_0,en,"on una baja presencia de textos científicos. Asimismo, se identificaron diversas","Although reading and writing are essential processes for academic development, their results in assessments are not always satisfactory. The purpose of this study was to identify the most used text types in primary education and to characterize the teaching strategies that accompany them. To this end, the PRISMA methodology was used, and a systematic review of articles published between 2020 and 2024 was carried out in specialized databases such as ERIC, Scopus, Redalyc, and SciELO. The results show a predominance of narrative texts in the classroom, in contrast to a low presence of scientific texts. Likewise, various teaching strategies were identified, among which those that stimulate creativity, the use of rubrics, planning through teaching sequences, the use of digital resources, and cooperative activities stand out. To a lesser extent, the implementation of strategies aimed at interdisciplinary learning was observed. The conclusions indicate that, although narrative texts continue to be the most used, other types of texts, such as expository and argumentative texts, are also incorporated, which favors the development of inferential and critical skills. There is also a transition from traditional approaches to practices focused on meaningful textual comprehension and production","didactic strategies; writing; reading; primary school; basic education. 1. Universidad Antonio Nariño, Bogotá, Colombia. susaboca@gmail.com. ORCID: https://orcid.org/0009-0003-2690-9060 2. Universidad Antonio Nariño, Bogotá, Colombia. marisbuitrago@uan.edu.co. ORCID: https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8254-4025 Tipo de artículo: Revisión Recibido: 07 de agosto de 2025 Aceptado: 30 de nov",marcadores,una baja presencia de texto cientifico asimismo se identificaron diversa,although read writ esse