2389-7864,Begambre-Pacheco++et+al.+Intropica.pdf,Begambre-Pacheco++et+al.+Intropica_0,en,*Autor de correspondencia:,"The ascidian Phallusia nigra has a wide distribution in the Caribbean; however, there are currently no published records of this species in the Colombian Caribbean. This study quantified the presence and density of P. nigra in an international marina located in Puerto Velero, in the central Colombian Caribbean, characterized by the presence of various artificial substrates, as well as adjacent areas with natural substrates. The region is strongly influenced by high sediment loads associated with discharges from the Magdalena River, resulting in pronounced physicochemical variability. A total area of 79 m² was examined, encompassing concrete slabs and metal pilings. Sampling carried out between July and September 2024 revealed a high abundance of P. nigra , with a total of 1032 individuals recorded associated with artificial substrates. Of these, 62.8 % were found in the shaded areas of the structures studied. The predominance of P. nigra in shaded areas over well-lit sides suggests that light availability, substrate type, and possible disturbances from marina operations play an important role in its spatial distribution. The species exhibited an average density of 17.3 ± 8.6 individuals/m² across the substrates. Additionally, based on field observations, the species was recorded on natural substrates in nearby locations such as Caño Dulce and Puerto Caimán. These results demonstrate the species’ ability to colonize both artificial and natural environments under conditions of elevated turbidity and pronounced salinity variability. These findings constitute a key baseline for monitoring the species and its ecological role in coastal ecosystems of the Colombian Caribbean","solitary tunicate; black ink tunicate; marina; biofouling, artificial and natural substrates",marcadores,autor de correspondencia,ascidian phallusia nigra has wide distribution caribbean however there currently no publish record speci colombian caribbean study quantifi presence density nigra international marina locat puerto velero central colombian caribbean characteriz presence variou artificial substrat well adjacent area natural substrat region strongly influenc high sediment load associat discharg magdalena river result pronounc physicochemical variability total area 79 m2 examin encompass concrete slab metal piling sampl carri out between july september 2024 reveal high abundance nigra total 1032 individual record associat artificial substrat these 62 found shad area structur studi predominance nigra shad area over well-lit side suggest light availability substrate type possible disturbanc marina oper play important role its spatial distribution speci exhibit average density 17 individual m2 acros substrat additionally based field observ speci record natural substrat nearby location such cano dulce puerto caiman these result demonstrate speci ability colonize both artificial natural environment under condition elevat turbidity pronounc salinity variability these finding constitute key baseline monitor speci its ecological role coastal ecosystem colombian caribbean,solitary tunicate black ink tunicate marina biofoul artificial natural substrat,autor de correspondencia ascidian phallusia nigra has wide distribution caribbean however there currently no publish record speci colombian caribbean study quantifi presence density nigra international marina locat puerto velero central colombian caribbean characteriz presence variou artificial substrat well adjacent area natural substrat region strongly influenc high sediment load associat discharg magdalena river result pronounc physicochemical variability total area 79 m2 examin encompass concrete slab metal piling sampl carri out between july september 2024 reveal high abundance nigra total 1032 individual record associat artificial substrat these 62 found shad area structur studi predominance nigra shad area over well-lit side suggest light availability substrate type possible disturbanc marina oper play important role its spatial distribution speci exhibit average density 17 individual m2 acros substrat additionally based field observ speci record natural substrat nearby location such cano dulce puerto caiman these result demonstrate speci ability colonize both artificial natural environment under condition elevat turbidity pronounc salinity variability these finding constitute key baseline monitor speci its ecological role coastal ecosystem colombian caribbean solitary tunicate black ink tunicate marina biofoul artificial natural substrat,1.0.0,aa7a8a3999002be2
2389-7864,Begambre-Pacheco++et+al.+Intropica.pdf,Begambre-Pacheco++et+al.+Intropica_0,es,"ed areas over well-lit sides suggests that light availability, substrate type, and possible","La ascidia Phallusia nigra presenta una amplia distribución en el Caribe, sin embargo, actualmente, no existen registros publicados de esta especie en el Caribe colombiano. Este estudio cuantificó la presencia y densidad de P. nigra en una marina internacional ubicada en Puerto Velero, en el Caribe central colombiano, caracterizada por la presencia de diversos sustratos artificiales, así como áreas adyacentes con sustratos naturales. La región está fuertemente influenciada por altas cargas de sedimentos asociadas a las descargas del río Magdalena, lo que genera una marcada variabilidad fisicoquímica. En total se examinó un área de 79 m2 comprendiendo losas de concreto y pilotes metálicos. Los muestreos realizados entre julio y septiembre de 2024 evidenciaron una alta abundancia de P. nigra , con un total de 1032 individuos registrados asociados a sustratos artificiales. De estos, el 62,8 % se encontraron en las áreas sombreadas de las estructuras estudiadas. El predominio de P. nigra en superficies sombreadas sobre superficies iluminadas sugiere que la disponibilidad de luz, el tipo de sustrato y posibles perturbaciones derivadas de las operaciones de la marina desempeñan un papel importante en su distribución espacial. La especie presentó una densidad promedio entre los sustratos igual a de 17,3 ± 8,6 individuos/m². Adicionalmente, con base en observaciones de campo, la especie fue registrada en sustratos naturales en localidades cercanas como Caño Dulce y Puerto Caimán. Los resultados evidencian la capacidad de la especie para colonizar tanto ambientes artificiales como naturales bajo condiciones de alta turbidez y variabilidad en la salinidad. Estos resultados constituyen una línea base clave para el seguimiento de la especie y su papel ecológico en ecosistemas costeros del Caribe colombiano","tunicado solitario; ascidia negra; marina; fauna incrustante, sustratos artificiales y naturales Karen Begambre-Pacheco* , Adriana Gracia C. , Alex Paternina-Ramos y Kelly Pacheco-Medina Programa de Biología, Facultad de Ciencias Básicas, Universidad del Atlántico, Puerto Colombia, Atlántico, Colombia INTROPICA Phallusia nigra in the Department of Atlántico Enero - junio de 2026",marcadores,ed areas over well-lit sides suggests that light availability substrate type and possible,ascidia phallusia nigra presenta amplia distribucion caribe sin embargo actual no existen registr publicad esta especie caribe colombiano este estudio cuantifico presencia densidad nigra marina internacional ubicada puerto velero caribe central colombiano caracterizada presencia divers sustrat artificial asi como areas adyacent sustrat natural region esta fuerte influenciada altas carg sediment asociad descarg rio magdalena genera marcada variabilidad fisicoquimica total examino area 79 m2 comprend losas concreto pilot metalic muestre realizad entre julio septiembre 2024 evidenciaron alta abundancia nigra total 1032 individu registrad asociad sustrat artificial estos 62 encontraron areas sombread estructur estudiad predominio nigra superfici sombread sobre superfici iluminad sugiere disponibilidad luz tipo sustrato posibl perturb derivad oper marina desempenan papel importante distribucion espacial especie presento densidad promedio entre sustrat igual 17 individu m2 adicional base observ campo especie fue registrada sustrat natural localidad cercan como cano dulce puerto caiman resultad evidencian capacidad especie colonizar tanto ambient artificial como natural bajo condicion alta turbidez variabilidad salinidad estos resultad constituyen linea base clave seguimiento especie papel ecologico ecosistem coster caribe colombiano,tunicado solitario ascidia negra marina fauna incrustante sustrat artificial natural karen begambre-pacheco adriana gracia alex paternina-ram kelly pacheco