2389-7864,"Gamboa+et+al.,.....Intropica.pdf","Gamboa+et+al.,.....Intropica_0",en,Editor en jefe: Juan Carlos Narvaéz Barandica,"Andean rivers are characterized by high environmental heterogeneity, where physicochemical conditions strongly influence aquatic communities. To better understand these dynamics, we analyzed the spatio-temporal variation of macroinvertebrate assemblages in two reaches of La Sicha stream (Moniquirá, Boyacá) from November 2023 to May 2024. Bimonthly sampling was conducted using a Surber net (0.09 m²), and water parameters were measured both in the field and in the laboratory. A total of 1.064 individuals belonging to nine orders and 15 families were collected, with Diptera (49 %) and Ephemeroptera (42.5 %) being the most abundant orders; the family Baetidae dominated during most sampling periods. Diversity indices ranged from 0.96 to 1.65 (Shannon) and from 1.11 to 2.23 (Margalef), reflecting variation in community heterogeneity among sampling months. Temperature varied significantly among months (F = 10.051; p = 0.025), whereas pH differed significantly between reaches (t = -4.594; p = 0.007). Functional Feeding Groups were dominated by collectors and shredders; however, no significant differences were found between reaches (t = - 0.39; p = 0.71), and no clear seasonal patterns in their composition were detected. Principal Component Analysis explained 85.27 % of the total variation, revealing associations between Smicridea sp. and pH, Petrophila sp. and Heterelmis sp. with dissolved oxygen, and Andesiops sp. with conductivity and total dissolved solids. In contrast, Gigantodax sp., Simulium sp., Baetodes sp., and Hydroptila sp. showed no clear correlation with the evaluated variables. These results highlight the sensitivity of macroinvertebrate assemblages to physicochemical gradients and demonstrate their relevance for understanding ecological processes in Andean streams, while providing baseline information for the development of environmental monitoring programs and conservation strategies in the region",altitude; Andean Mountain streams; water quality; lotic ecosystems; functional feeding groups; seasonality,marcadores,editor en jefe juan carlo narvaez barandica,andean river characteriz high environmental heterogeneity where physicochemical condition strongly influence aquatic communiti better understand these dynamic we analyz spatio-temporal variation macroinvertebrate assemblag two reach la sicha stream moniquira boyaca november 2023 may 2024 bimonthly sampl conduct using surber net 09 m2 water parameter measur both field laboratory total 064 individual belong nine order 15 famili collect diptera 49 ephemeroptera 42 being most abundant order family baetidae dominat during most sampl period diversity indic rang 96 65 shannon 11 23 margalef reflect variation community heterogeneity among sampl month temperature vari significantly among month 10 051 025 wherea ph differ significantly between reach -4 594 007 functional feed group dominat collector shredder however no significant differenc found between reach 39 71 no clear seasonal pattern their composition detect principal component analysi explain 85 27 total variation reveal associ between smicridea sp ph petrophila sp heterelmi sp dissolv oxygen andesiop sp conductivity total dissolv solid contrast gigantodax sp simulium sp baetod sp hydroptila sp show no clear correlation evaluat variabl these result highlight sensitivity macroinvertebrate assemblag physicochemical gradient demonstrate their relevance understand ecological process andean stream while provid baseline information development environmental monitor program conservation strategi region,altitude andean mountain stream water quality lotic ecosystem functional feed group seasonality,editor en jefe juan carlo narvaez barandica andean river characteriz high environmental heterogeneity where physicochemical condition strongly influence aquatic communiti better understand these dynamic we