2389-8194,672-Texto del artículo-1215-4-10-20260901.pdf,672-Texto del artículo-1215-4-10-20260901_0,en,"3 PhD en Gestión Universidad EAN. Profesora de la Universidad Surcolombiana de Pitalito, Huila. E-mail:","This paper reanalyzes the empirical database of a doctoral study involving 900 11th-grade students, evenly distributed across Bogotá, Medellín, Cali, Neiva, Pitalito, and Timaná, to identify where variation in financial education is actually concentrated. The instrument includes 25 items organized into five dimensions: perceived basic financial knowledge, budgeting and planning, saving and foresight, consumption and decision-making, and financial attitude and self-control. Scores were recalculated from item-level responses, the negatively worded item was reversecoded, and internal consistency, territorial differences, institutional clustering, and differentiated family socioeconomic conditions were examined. The global scale showed high reliability (α = .937). The overall financial education index was favorable (M = 3.532; SD = 0.482), but financial attitude and self-control had the lowest mean (M = 3.400; SD = 0.506). The gap between this dimension and the average of the other four dimensions was 0.165 points and was statistically robust (t = 11.09; p < .001; d_z = .37). In contrast, overall differences across territories were not statistically detectable (F = 1.83; p = .104; η² = .010; Kruskal-Wallis p = .239), and the variance attributable to the 30 schools was negligible (ICC ≈ .0015). Household stratum, SISBEN classification, technological access, caregiver education, and main household income source likewise did not robustly differentiate the global index when analyzed as separate categorical conditions. The findings suggest that, in this sample, the main empirical signal is not an aggregate territorial gap but an internal self-regulation gap that remains relatively stable across contexts. This shifts the discussion away from monolithic socioeconomic explanations and toward mechanisms closer to financial behavior, socialization, autonomy, and habit formation",financial education; adolescents; self-regulation; financial literacy; territory; socioeconomic conditions,marcadores,phd en gestion universidad ean profesora de la universidad surcolombiana de pitalito huila e-mail,paper reanalyz empirical database doctoral study involv 900 11th-grade student evenly distribut acros bogota medellin cali neiva pitalito timana identify where variation financial education actually concentrat instrument includ 25 item organiz into five dimension perceiv basic financial knowledge budget plann saving foresight consumption decision-mak financial attitude self-control scor recalculat item-level respons negatively word item reversecod internal consistency territorial differenc institutional cluster differentiat family socioeconomic condition examin global scale show high reliability 937 overall financial education index favorable 532 sd 482 but financial attitude self-control had lowest mean 400 sd 506 gap between dimension average other four dimension 165 point statistically robust 11 09 001 d_z 37 contrast overall differenc acros territori not statistically detectable 83 104 e2 010 kruskal-walli 239 variance attributable 30 school negligible icc 0015 household stratum sisben classification technological acces caregiver education main household income source likewise did not robustly differentiate global index when analyz separate categorical condition finding suggest sample main empirical signal not aggregate territorial gap but internal self-regulation gap remain relatively stable acros context shift discussion away monolithic socioeconomic explan toward mechanism closer financial behavior social autonomy habit formation,financial education adolescent self-regulation financial literacy territory socioeconomic condition,phd en gestion universidad ean profesora de la universidad surcolombiana de pitalito huila e-mail paper reanalyz empirical database doctoral study involv 900 11th-grade student evenly distribut acros bogota medellin cali neiva pitalito timana identify where variation financial education actually concentrat instrument includ 25 item organiz into five dimension perceiv basic financial knowledge budget plann saving foresight consumption decision-mak financial attitude self-control scor recalculat item-level respons negatively word item reversecod internal consistency territorial differenc institutional cluster differentiat family socioeconomic condition examin global scale show high reliability 937 overall financial education index favorable 532 sd 482 but financial attitude self-control had lowest mean 400 sd 506 gap between dimension average other four dimension 165 point statistically robust 11 09 001 d_z 37 contrast overall differenc acros territori not statistically detectable 83 104 e2 010 kruskal-walli 239 variance attributable 30 school negligible icc 0015 household stratum sisben classification technological acces caregiver education main household income source likewise did not robustly differentiate global index when analyz separate categorical condition finding suggest sample main empirical signal not aggregate territorial gap but internal self-regulation gap remain relatively stable acros context shift discussion away monolithic socioeconomic explan toward mechanism closer financial behavior social autonomy habit formation financial education adolescent self-regulation financial literacy territory socioeconomic condition,1.0.0,d2c78ae9e7c2ebeb
2389-8194,673-Texto del artículo-1216-5-10-20260907.pdf,673-Texto del artículo-1216-5-10-20260907_0,es,PRÁCTICAS DE TRANSFORMACIÓN DE CONFLICTOS Y CONSTRUCCIÓN,"El estudio tuvo como objetivo analizar las prácticas de transformación de conflictos y construcción de paz presentes entre estudiantes universitarios, mediante un proceso de investigación-acción orientado al fortalecimiento del diálogo, la convivencia y la gestión constructiva de las diferencias. Se desarrolló un estudio cualitativo, exploratorio e inductivo, con orientación participativa y reflexiva. Participaron siete líderes estudiantiles de los programas de Derecho e Ingeniería Agroecológica de la Universidad de la Amazonia. La información se obtuvo mediante entrevistas semiestructuradas, un grupo focal, cuatro talleres participativos y un encuentro final de retroalimentación. El corpus fue examinado mediante análisis temático inductivo y triangulación entre fuentes y momentos del proceso. Los resultados mostraron que el conflicto es reconocido como una experiencia cotidiana y potencialmente formativa, aunque su gestión está condicionada por emociones, confianza, relaciones de poder y condiciones institucionales. Los estudiantes empleaban repertorios diversos, entre ellos diálogo, evitación, confrontación y mediación informal, caracterizados por su carácter espontáneo y desigual. Los talleres favorecieron la reflexión sobre estas prácticas, la experimentación con escucha activa, comunicación no violenta y mediación, y la construcción de propuestas dirigidas a estudiantes, docentes e institución. Se concluye que la construcción de paz universitaria requiere articular capacidades personales, prácticas relacionales y condiciones institucionales que favorezcan el reconocimiento, la participación y la transformación constructiva de los conflictos","transformación de conflictos; construcción de paz; educación para la paz; estudiantes universitarios; investigación-acción; mediación; convivencia universitaria. 1 Magíster en Ciencias de la Educación. Docente e Investigador del programa de Maestría en Transformación de Conflictos y Construcción de Paz de la Universidad INCCA de Colombia. Bogotá, Colombia. Email: carlosalberto.gomez@uninc",marcadores,practic transformacion conflict construccion,estudio tuvo como objetivo analizar practic transformacion conflict construccion paz present entre estudiant universitari mediante proceso investigacion-accion orientado fortalecimiento dialogo convivencia gestion constructiva diferenci desarrollo estudio cualitativo exploratorio inductivo orientacion participativa reflexiva participaron siete lider estudiantil program derecho ingenieria agroecologica universidad amazonia informacion obtuvo mediante entrevist semiestructurad grupo focal cuatro taller participativ encuentro final retroalimentacion corpus fue examinado mediante analisis tematico inductivo triangulacion entre fuent moment proceso resultad mostraron conflicto reconocido como experiencia cotidiana potencial formativa aunque gestion esta condicionada emocion confianza relacion poder condicion institucional estudiant empleaban repertori divers entre ellos dialogo evitacion confrontacion mediacion informal caracterizad caracter espontaneo desigual taller favorecieron reflexion sobre estas practic experimentacion escucha activa comunicacion no violenta mediacion construccion propuest dirigid estudiant docent institucion concluye construccion paz universitaria requiere articular capacidad personal practic relacional condicion institucional favorezcan reconocimiento participacion transformacion constructiva conflict,transformacion conflict construccion paz educacion paz estudiant universitari investigacion-accion mediacion convivencia universitaria magister cienci educacion docente investigador programa maestria transformacion conflict construccion paz universidad incca colombia bogota colombia email carlosalberto gomez uninc,practic transformacion conflict construccion estudio tuvo como objetivo analizar practic transformacion conflict construccion paz present entre estudiant universitari mediante proceso investigacion-accion orientado fortalecimiento dialogo convivencia gestion constructiva diferenci desarrollo estudio cualitativo exploratorio inductivo orientacion participativa reflexiva participaron siete lider estudiantil program derecho ingenieria agroecologica universidad amazonia informacion obtuvo mediante entrevist semiestructurad grupo focal cuatro taller participativ encuentro final retroalimentacion corpus fue examinado mediante analisis tematico inductivo triangulacion entre fuent moment proceso resultad mostraron conflicto reconocido como experiencia cotidiana potencial formativa aunque gestion esta condicionada emocion confianza relacion poder condicion institucional estudiant empleaban repertori divers entre ellos dialogo evitacion confrontacion mediacion informal caracterizad caracter espontaneo desigual taller favorecieron reflexion sobre estas practic experimentacion escucha activa comunicacion no violenta mediacion construccion propuest dirigid estudiant docent institucion concluye construccion paz universitaria requiere articular capacidad personal practic relacional condicion institucional favorezcan reconocimiento participacion transformacion constructiva conflict transformacion conflict construccion paz educacion paz estudiant universitari investigacion-accion mediacion convivencia universitaria magister cienci educacion docente investigador programa maestria transformacion conflict construccion paz universidad incca colombia bogota colombia email carlosalberto gomez uninc,1.0.0,da7c30e0783f2349
2389-8194,673-Texto del artículo-1216-5-10-20260907.pdf,673-Texto del artículo-1216-5-10-20260907_0,en,"2 Magíster en Derecho. Docente e Investigador del programa de Derecho de la Universidad de la Amazonia, Florencia,","The study aimed to analyze conflict transformation and peacebuilding practices among university students through an action research process focused on strengthening dialogue, coexistence, and constructive management of differences. A qualitative, exploratory, and inductive study with a participatory and reflective orientation was conducted. Seven student leaders from the Law and Agroecological Engineering programs at Universidad de la Amazonia participated. Data were collected through semi-structured interviews, one focus group, four participatory workshops, and a final feedback meeting. The corpus was examined through inductive thematic analysis and triangulation across sources and stages of the research process. The findings showed that conflict was understood as an everyday and potentially formative experience, although its management was conditioned by emotions, trust, power relations, and institutional conditions. Students relied on diverse repertoires, including dialogue, avoidance, confrontation, and informal mediation, which were largely spontaneous and unevenly developed. The workshops encouraged reflection on these practices, experimentation with active listening, nonviolent communication, and mediation, and the collaborative construction of proposals addressed to students, faculty members, and the institution. The study concludes that peacebuilding in universities requires the articulation of personal capacities, relational practices, and institutional conditions that promote recognition, participation, and the constructive transformation of conflicts",conflict transformation; peacebuilding; peace education; university students; action research; mediation; university coexistence,marcadores,magister en derecho docente investigador del programa de derecho de la universidad de la amazonia florencia,study aimed analyze conflict transformation peacebuild practic among university student through action research proces focus strengthen dialogue coexistence constructive management differenc qualitative exploratory inductive study participatory reflective orientation conduct seven student leader law agroecological engineer program universidad de la amazonia participat data collect through semi-structur interview one focu group four participatory workshop final feedback meet corpu examin through inductive thematic analysi triangulation acros sourc stag research proces finding show conflict understood everyday potentially formative experience although its management condition emotion trust power relation institutional condition student reli diverse repertoir includ dialogue avoidance confrontation informal mediation which largely spontaneou unevenly develop workshop encourag reflection these practic experimentation active listen nonviolent communication mediation collaborative construction proposal address student faculty member institution study conclud peacebuild universiti requir articulation personal capaciti relational practic institutional condition promote recognition participation constructive transformation conflict,conflict transformation peacebuild peace education university student action research mediation university coexistence,magister en derecho docente investigador del programa de derecho de la universidad de la amazonia florencia study aimed analyze conflict transformation peacebuild practic among university student through action research proces focus strengthen dialogue coexistence constructive management differenc qualitative exploratory inductive study participatory reflective orientation conduct seven student leader law agroecological engineer program universidad de la amazonia participat data collect through semi-structur interview one focu group four participatory workshop final feedback meet corpu examin through inductive thematic analysi triangulation acros sourc stag research proces finding show conflict understood everyday potentially formative experience although its management condition emotion trust power relation institutional condition student reli diverse repertoir includ dialogue avoidance confrontation informal mediation which largely spontaneou unevenly develop workshop encourag reflection these practic experimentation active listen nonviolent communication mediation collaborative construction proposal address student faculty member institution study conclud peacebuild universiti requir articulation personal capaciti relational practic institutional condition promote recognition participation constructive transformation conflict conflict transformation peacebuild peace education university student action research mediation university coexistence,1.0.0,588465c4d63fb670
2389-8194,674-Texto del artículo-1218-2-10-20260901.pdf,674-Texto del artículo-1218-2-10-20260901_0,es,DE LA DOCENCIA TRADICIONAL A LA COLABORACIÓN HUMANO–IA:,"La inteligencia artificial generativa está transformando la educación superior y exige que el profesorado desarrolle capacidades que trasciendan el manejo instrumental de herramientas. Este estudio tuvo como propósito comprender las experiencias e interpretaciones de profesores universitarios especialistas en tecnología educativa e inteligencia artificial que capacitan a otros docentes, respecto de las necesidades de alfabetización en IA que emergen durante su integración en la enseñanza y el aprendizaje. Se adoptó un enfoque cualitativo, de alcance exploratorio y orientación fenomenológica hermenéutica. Participaron diez profesores universitarios seleccionados mediante muestreo intencional por criterios y acceso por bola de nieve. La información se obtuvo mediante entrevistas semiestructuradas realizadas por WhatsApp y Zoom, grabadas con consentimiento informado, transcritas manualmente y analizadas con apoyo de ATLAS.ti. Los hallazgos muestran que la alfabetización docente en IA requiere comprensión conceptual, juicio crítico, capacidad de verificación, rediseño pedagógico, criterios éticos y conocimiento de los usos estudiantiles. Asimismo, la colaboración humano–IA fue interpretada como una relación asimétrica en la que la tecnología amplía capacidades, mientras el docente conserva la intencionalidad, la contextualización y la responsabilidad educativa. Se concluye que la formación debe ser situada, continua y vinculada con problemas disciplinares auténticos y apoyada institucionalmente para favorecer experimentación, acompañamiento y reflexión profesional","Inteligencia artificial; Enseñanza superior; Personal académico docente; Formación de docentes en activo; Tecnología educacional. 1Docente-Investigadora de la Universidad Industrial de Santander. Bucaramanga, Colombia. Email: mltorres@uis.edu.co ORCID: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4388-5991 2 Docente-Investigador de la Universidad del Tolima. Ibagué, Colombia. Email: dvalenciao@ut.edu.co ORC",marcadores,docencia tradicional colaboracion humano-ia,inteligencia artificial generativa esta transform educacion superior exige profesorado desarrolle capacidad trasciendan manejo instrumental herramient este estudio tuvo como proposito comprender experienci interpret profesor universitari especialist tecnologia educativa inteligencia artificial capacitan otros docent respecto necesidad alfabetizacion ia emergen durante integracion ensenanza aprendizaje adopto enfoque cualitativo alcance exploratorio orientacion fenomenologica hermeneutica participaron diez profesor universitari seleccionad mediante muestreo intencional criteri acceso bola nieve informacion obtuvo mediante entrevist semiestructurad realizad whatsapp zoom grabad consentimiento informado transcrit manual analizad apoyo atlas ti hallazg muestran alfabetizacion docente ia requiere comprension conceptual juicio critico capacidad verificacion rediseno pedagogico criteri etic conocimiento usos estudiantil asimismo colaboracion humano-ia fue interpretada como relacion asimetrica tecnologia amplia capacidad mientr docente conserva intencionalidad contextualizacion responsabilidad educativa concluye formacion debe ser situada continua vinculada problem disciplinar autentic apoyada institucional favorecer experimentacion acompanamiento reflexion profesional,inteligencia artificial ensenanza superior personal academico docente formacion docent activo tecnologia educacional 1docente-investigadora universidad industrial santander bucaramanga colombia email mltorr uis edu co orcid https orcid org 0000-0002-4388-5991 docente-investigador universidad tolima ibague colombia email dvalenciao ut edu co orc,docencia tradicional colaboracion humano-ia inteligencia artificial generativa esta transform educacion superior exige profesorado desarrolle capacidad trasciendan manejo instrumental herramient este estudio tuvo como proposito comprender experienci interpret profesor universitari especialist tecnologia educativa inteligencia artificial capacitan otros docent respecto necesidad alfabetizacion ia emergen durante integracion ensenanza aprendizaje adopto enfoque cualitativo alcance exploratorio orientacion fenomenologica hermeneutica participaron diez profesor universitari seleccionad mediante muestreo intencional criteri acceso bola nieve informacion obtuvo mediante entrevist semiestructurad realizad whatsapp zoom grabad consentimiento informado transcrit manual analizad apoyo atlas ti hallazg muestran alfabetizacion docente ia requiere comprension conceptual juicio critico capacidad verificacion rediseno pedagogico criteri etic conocimiento usos estudiantil asimismo colaboracion humano-ia fue interpretada como relacion asimetrica tecnologia amplia capacidad mientr docente conserva intencionalidad contextualizacion responsabilidad educativa concluye formacion debe ser situada continua vinculada problem disciplinar autentic apoyada institucional favorecer experimentacion acompanamiento reflexion profesional inteligencia artificial ensenanza superior personal academico docente formacion docent activo tecnologia educacional 1docente-investigadora universidad industrial santander bucaramanga colombia email mltorr uis edu co orcid https orcid org 0000-0002-4388-5991 docente-investigador universidad tolima ibague colombia email dvalenciao ut edu co orc,1.0.0,4098456d09d3a2bc
2389-8194,674-Texto del artículo-1218-2-10-20260901.pdf,674-Texto del artículo-1218-2-10-20260901_0,en,encia artificial; Enseñanza superior; Personal académico docente;,"Generative artificial intelligence is transforming higher education and requires university faculty to develop capabilities that go beyond the instrumental use of tools. This study aimed to understand the experiences and interpretations of university professors specializing in educational technology and artificial intelligence who train other faculty members, regarding the AI literacy needs that emerge during its integration into teaching and learning. A qualitative, exploratory study with a hermeneutic phenomenological orientation was conducted. Ten university professors were selected through criterion-based purposive sampling and snowball recruitment. Data were collected through semi-structured interviews conducted via WhatsApp and Zoom, recorded with informed consent, manually transcribed, and analyzed with the support of ATLAS.ti. Findings indicate that faculty AI literacy requires conceptual understanding, critical judgment, verification skills, pedagogical redesign, ethical criteria, and knowledge of students’ AI uses. Human–AI collaboration was also interpreted as an asymmetrical relationship in which technology expands capabilities while faculty retain educational intentionality, contextualization, and responsibility. The study concludes that professional development should be situated, continuous, linked to authentic disciplinary problems, and institutionally supported to promote experimentation, ongoing guidance, and professional reflection. These findings frame AI literacy as a professional and pedagogical capacity rather than as mere operational proficiency with rapidly changing digital applications",Artificial intelligence; Higher education; Academic teaching personnel; Inservice teacher education; Educational technology,marcadores,encia artificial ensenanza superior personal academico docente,generative artificial intelligence transform higher education requir university faculty develop capabiliti go beyond instrumental use tool study aimed understand experienc interpret university professor specializ educational technology artificial intelligence who train other faculty member regard ai literacy need emerge during its integration into teach learn qualitative exploratory study hermeneutic phenomenological orientation conduct ten university professor select through criterion-bas purposive sampl snowball recruitment data collect through semi-structur interview conduct via whatsapp zoom record inform consent manually transcrib analyz support atla ti finding indicate faculty ai literacy requir conceptual understand critical judgment verification skill pedagogical redesign ethical criteria knowledge student ai uses human-ai collaboration also interpret asymmetrical relationship which technology expand capabiliti while faculty retain educational intentionality contextual responsibility study conclud professional development should situat continuou link authentic disciplinary problem institutionally support promote experimentation ongo guidance professional reflection these finding frame ai literacy professional pedagogical capacity rather than mere operational proficiency rapidly chang digital applic,artificial intelligence higher education academic teach personnel inservice teacher education educational technology,encia artificial ensenanza superior personal academico docente generative artificial intelligence transform higher education requir university faculty develop capabiliti go beyond instrumental use tool study aimed understand experienc interpret university professor specializ educational technology artificial intelligence who train other faculty member regard ai literacy need emerge during its integration into teach learn qualitative exploratory study hermeneutic phenomenological orientation conduct ten university professor select through criterion-bas purposive sampl snowball recruitment data collect through semi-structur interview conduct via whatsapp zoom record inform consent manually transcrib analyz support atla ti finding indicate faculty ai literacy requir conceptual understand critical judgment verification skill pedagogical redesign ethical criteria knowledge student ai uses human-ai collaboration also interpret asymmetrical relationship which technology expand capabiliti while faculty retain educational intentionality contextual responsibility study conclud professional development should situat continuou link authentic disciplinary problem institutionally support promote experimentation ongo guidance professional reflection these finding frame ai literacy professional pedagogical capacity rather than mere operational proficiency rapidly chang digital applic artificial intelligence higher education academic teach personnel inservice teacher education educational technology,1.0.0,222b34c63f0bf129
2389-8194,675-Texto del artículo-1220-2-10-20260901.pdf,675-Texto del artículo-1220-2-10-20260901_0,en,ENTREPRENEURIAL INTENTION AMONG STUDENTS OF PUBLIC ACCOUNTING,"Entrepreneurship constitutes a relevant alternative for economic and social development in regional contexts where formal employment opportunities are limited. In this context, the present research aimed to analyze the level of entrepreneurial intention among students of the Business Administration and Public Accounting programs at the Universidad Francisco de Paula Santander, Cúcuta, with the purpose of identifying the perceptions, attitudes, and factors associated with interest in creating business initiatives. The study was developed under a quantitative approach, with a descriptive cross-sectional design. The sample consisted of 227 students enrolled in the aforementioned programs. For data collection, the Entrepreneurial Intention Questionnaire (EIQ) was applied, an instrument that measures variables related to attitude toward entrepreneurship, perception of social support, and entrepreneurial self-efficacy. The results showed that a significant proportion of students present favorable levels of entrepreneurial intention, expressing willingness to develop business projects in the future. Likewise, it was identified that factors such as confidence in one's own abilities, perception of opportunities in the environment, and support from the academic context positively influence the intention to undertake entrepreneurial activities. In conclusion, the findings show that the university environment constitutes a favorable setting for the strengthening of entrepreneurial competencies, which highlights the importance of promoting institutional strategies aimed at fostering innovation, company creation, and entrepreneurial education among students","Entrepreneurship, public policy, entrepreneurship trends, economic growth and formalization of employment. 1 Administrador Financiero UDES, Especialista en Emprendimiento de la UFPS, Maestrante de la Universidad de Pamplona. – Colombia. Email: luisrojascucuta@gmail.com ORCID: https://orcid.org/0009-0002-0532-9481 2 Administradora de Empresas de la Universidad de Pamplona, Magister en Admi",marcadores,entrepreneurial intention among student public account,entrepreneurship constitut relevant alternative economic social development regional context where formal employment opportuniti limit context present research aimed analyze level entrepreneurial intention among student busines administration public account program universidad francisco de paula santander cucuta purpose identify perception attitud factor associat interest creat busines initiativ study develop under quantitative approach descriptive cross-sectional design sample consist 227 student enroll aforemention program data collection entrepreneurial intention questionnaire eiq appli instrument measur variabl relat attitude toward entrepreneurship perception social support entrepreneurial self-efficacy result show significant proportion student present favorable level entrepreneurial intention express willingnes develop busines project future likewise identifi factor such confidence one own abiliti perception opportuniti environment support academic context positively influence intention undertake entrepreneurial activiti conclusion finding show university environment constitut favorable sett strengthen entrepreneurial competenci which highlight importance promot institutional strategi aimed foster innovation company creation entrepreneurial education among student,entrepreneurship public policy entrepreneurship trend economic growth formal employment administrador financiero udes especialista en emprendimiento de la ufps maestrante de la universidad de pamplona colombia email luisrojascucuta gmail com orcid http orcid org 0009-0002-0532-9481 administradora de empresa de la universidad de pamplona magister en admi,entrepreneurial intention among student public account entrepreneurship constitut relevant alternative economic social development regional context where formal employment opportuniti limit context present research aimed analyze level entrepreneurial intention among student busines administration public account program universidad francisco de paula santander cucuta purpose identify perception attitud factor associat interest creat busines initiativ study develop under quantitative approach descriptive cross-sectional design sample consist 227 student enroll aforemention program data collection entrepreneurial intention questionnaire eiq appli instrument measur variabl relat attitude toward entrepreneurship perception social support entrepreneurial self-efficacy result show significant proportion student present favorable level entrepreneurial intention express willingnes develop busines project future likewise identifi factor such confidence one own abiliti perception opportuniti environment support academic context positively influence intention undertake entrepreneurial activiti conclusion finding show university environment constitut favorable sett strengthen entrepreneurial competenci which highlight importance promot institutional strategi aimed foster innovation company creation entrepreneurial education among student entrepreneurship public policy entrepreneurship trend economic growth formal employment administrador financiero udes especialista en emprendimiento de la ufps maestrante de la universidad de pamplona colombia email luisrojascucuta gmail com orcid http orcid org 0009-0002-0532-9481 administradora de empresa de la universidad de pamplona magister en admi,1.0.0,b96151be7bf0c6e2
2389-8194,675-Texto del artículo-1220-2-10-20260901.pdf,675-Texto del artículo-1220-2-10-20260901_0,es,"S, Especialista en Emprendimiento de la UFPS, Maestrante de la Universidad de","El emprendimiento constituye una alternativa relevante para el desarrollo económico y social en contextos regionales donde las oportunidades de empleo formal son limitadas. En este contexto, la presente investigación tuvo como objetivo analizar el nivel de intención emprendedora de los estudiantes de los programas de Administración de Empresas y Contaduría Pública de la Universidad Francisco de Paula Santander, Cúcuta, con el propósito de identificar las percepciones, actitudes y factores asociados con el interés por crear iniciativas empresariales. El estudio se desarrolló bajo un enfoque cuantitativo, con un diseño descriptivo de corte transversal. La muestra estuvo conformada por 227 estudiantes matriculados en los programas mencionados. Para la recolección de la información se aplicó el Cuestionario de Intención Emprendedora (EIQ), instrumento que mide variables relacionadas con la actitud hacia el emprendimiento, la percepción de apoyo social y la autoeficacia emprendedora. Los resultados evidenciaron que una proporción significativa de los estudiantes presenta niveles favorables de intención emprendedora, manifestando disposición para desarrollar proyectos empresariales en el futuro. Asimismo, se identificó que factores como la confianza en las propias capacidades, la percepción de oportunidades en el entorno y el apoyo proveniente del contexto académico influyen positivamente en la intención de emprender. En conclusión, los hallazgos muestran que el entorno universitario constituye un escenario favorable para el fortalecimiento de las competencias emprendedoras, lo que resalta la importancia de promover estrategias institucionales orientadas al fomento de la innovación, la creación de empresas y la educación emprendedora entre los estudiantes","Emprendimiento, política pública, tendencias del emprendimiento, crecimiento económico y formalización del empleo",marcadores,especialista emprendimiento ufps maestrante universidad,emprendimiento constituye alternativa relevante desarrollo economico social context regional donde oportunidad empleo formal son limitad este contexto presente investigacion tuvo como objetivo analizar nivel intencion emprendedora estudiant program administracion empres contaduria publica universidad francisco paula santander cucuta proposito identificar percepcion actitud factor asociad inter crear iniciativ empresarial estudio desarrollo bajo enfoque cuantitativo diseno descriptivo corte transversal muestra estuvo conformada 227 estudiant matriculad program mencionad recoleccion informacion aplico cuestionario intencion emprendedora eiq instrumento mide variabl relacionad actitud hacia emprendimiento percepcion apoyo social autoeficacia emprendedora resultad evidenciaron proporcion significativa estudiant presenta nivel favorabl intencion emprendedora manifest disposicion desarrollar proyect empresarial futuro asimismo identifico factor como confianza propi capacidad percepcion oportunidad entorno apoyo proveniente contexto academico influyen positiva intencion emprender conclusion hallazg muestran entorno universitario constituye escenario favorable fortalecimiento competenci emprendedor resalta importancia promover estrategi institucional orientad fomento innovacion creacion empres educacion emprendedora entre estudiant,emprendimiento politica publica tendenci emprendimiento crecimiento economico formalizacion empleo,especialista emprendimiento ufps maestrante universidad emprendimiento constituye alternativa relevante desarrollo economico social context regional donde oportunidad empleo formal son limitad este contexto presente investigacion tuvo como objetivo analizar nivel intencion emprendedora estudiant program administracion empres contaduria publica universidad francisco paula santander cucuta proposito identi