2389-8526,5443_final.pdf,5443_final_0,en,ficaron debilidades en,"This study evaluates municipal animal welfare strategies implemented in Montería, Córdoba, between 2020 and 2023, within the framework of “One Health” and “One Welfare” principles. The research arises from the need to analyze the real impact of public policies aimed at protecting and caring for companion animals. A qualitativedescriptive approach was used, including a documentary review of regulations, action plans, and official reports, as well as semi-structured interviews with key actors from the public sector and civil organizations. The results show progress in regulatory structu ring, awareness campaigns, and the creation of free veterinary care programs. However, 2 Gabriel Andrés Díaz Pacheco • Juan Carlos Carrascal Velásquez Rev. Med. Vet. issn 0122-9354. issne 2389-8526: Bogotá (Colombia) n.° 52: e5443 • enero-junio, 2026 weaknesses were identified in budget allocation, institutional coordination, and monitoring mechanisms. The discussion highlights the importance of consoli dating sustainable, integrated, and contextualized policies aligned with the “One Health” approach, which promotes the connection between human, animal, and environmental well-being. It is concluded that although Montería has made pro gress in policy formulation, structural and operational challenges persist that limit their effectiveness. The study proposes an evidence-based roadmap to strengthen institutional management of animal welfare, with the potential to be replicated in other intermediate cities in Latin America",animal welfare; public policy; veterinary public health; one health; animal protection; Colombia,marcadores,ficaron debilidad en,study evaluat municipal animal welfare strategi implement monteria cordoba between 2020 2023 within framework one health one welfare principl research aris need analyze real impact public polici aimed protect caring companion animal qualitativedescriptive approach used includ documentary review regul action plan official report well semi-structur interview key actor public sector civil organiz result show progres regulatory structu ring awarenes campaign creation free veterinary care program however gabriel andr diaz pacheco juan carlo carrascal velasquez rev med vet issn 0122-9354 issne 2389-8526 bogota colombia deg 52 e5443 enero-junio 2026 weakness identifi budget allocation institutional coordination monitor mechanism discussion highlight importance consoli dating sustainable integrat contextualiz polici align one health approach which promot connection between human animal environmental well-be conclud although monteria has made pro gres policy formulation structural operational challeng persist limit their effectivenes study propos evidence-bas roadmap strengthen institutional management animal welfare potential replicat other intermediate citi latin america,animal welfare public policy veterinary public health one health animal protection colombia,ficaron debilidad en study evaluat municipal animal welfare strategi implement monteria cordoba between 2020 2023 within framework one health one welfare principl research aris need analyze real impact public polici aimed protect caring companion animal qualitativedescriptive approach used includ documentary review regul action plan official report well semi-structur interview key actor public sector civil organiz result show progres regulatory structu ring awarenes campaign creation free veterinary care program however gabriel andr diaz pacheco juan carlo carrascal velasquez rev med vet issn 0122-9354 issne 2389-8526 bogota colombia deg 52 e5443 enero-junio 2026 weakness identifi budget allocation institutional coordination monitor mechanism discussion highlight importance consoli dating sustainable integrat contextualiz polici align one health approach which promot connection between human animal environmental well-be conclud although monteria has made pro gres policy formulation structural operational challeng persist limit their effectivenes study propos evidence-bas roadmap strengthen institutional management animal welfare potential replicat other intermediate citi latin america animal welfare public policy veterinary public health one health animal protection colombia,1.0.0,83824440da3d7d9b
2389-8526,5481_VF.pdf,5481_VF_0,es,"4 Médico veterinario, zootecnista,","Ante las limitaciones de la caracterización morfológica en especímenes incompletos, producto del tráfico ilegal de fauna silvestre, el análisis molecular surge como una he rramienta de identificación indispensable. Este estudio evaluó la eficiencia de extrac ción del adn en 50 muestras de sangre y 44 de heces de aves silvestres, pertenecientes al Parque de la Conservación de Medellín. La pureza y la concentración del material genético se determinaron por espectrofotometría y agarosa, además, su funcionalidad se confirmó mediante la amplificación del marcador citocromo c oxidasa I (coxi), por reacción en cadena de la polimerasa (pcr). Las diferencias métricas entre ambas ma trices biológicas se analizaron estadísticamente en el software R (v. 4.2.2; p < 0,05). En términos cuantitativos, las muestras de sangre presentaron un rendimiento significa tivamente mayor (mediana de 34,5 ng/μL) frente a las heces (mediana de 6,05 ng/μL; p = 0,0013). Asimismo, se observaron diferencias estadísticamente significativas en la pureza del adn (χ² = 42,162; p < 0,001), cuando el 42,9 % de las muestras de sangre alcanzaron una relación 260/280 óptima (1,8-2), en comparación con el 12,5 % de las heces (p = 0,0068). A pesar de que la sangre evidenció parámetros de concentración y calidad superiores, ambas muestras permitieron la correcta amplificación del fragmento coxi mediante pcr. Esto confirma que, si bien la sangre es una matriz más eficiente, las muestras de heces son adecuadas y funcionales para desarrollar estudios genéticos en aves. En particular, el uso de heces representa una alternativa valiosa en trabajos de cam po, al obtener material genético sin necesidad de recurrir a la captura y manipulación directa de los individuos","biodiversidad, coxi, código de barras, fauna silvestre. Efficiency of dna extraction from blood and fecal samples of wild birds",marcadores,medico veterinario zootecnista,ante limit caracterizacion morfologica especimen incomplet producto trafico ilegal fauna silvestre analisis molecular surge como he rramienta identificacion indispensable este estudio evaluo eficiencia extrac cion adn 50 muestr sangre 44 heces aves silvestr pertenecient parque conservacion medellin pureza concentracion material genetico determinaron espectrofotometria agarosa adem funcionalidad confirmo mediante amplificacion marcador citocromo oxidasa coxi reaccion cadena polimerasa pcr diferenci metric entre ambas ma tric biologic analizaron estadistica software 05 termin cuantitativ muestr sangre presentaron rendimiento significa tiva mayor mediana 34 ng ml frente heces mediana 05 ng ml 0013 asimismo observaron diferenci estadistica significativ pureza adn kh2 42 162 001 cuando 42 muestr sangre alcanzaron relacion 260 280 optima 8-2 comparacion 12 heces 0068 pesar sangre evidencio parametr concentracion calidad superior ambas muestr permitieron correcta amplificacion fragmento coxi mediante pcr esto confirma si bien sangre matriz mas eficiente muestr heces son adecuad funcional desarrollar estudi genetic aves particular uso heces representa alternativa valiosa trabaj cam po obtener material genetico sin necesidad recurrir captura manipulacion directa individu,biodiversidad coxi codigo barr fauna silvestre efficiency of dna extraction from blood and fecal sampl of wild birds,medico veterinario zootecnista ante limit caracterizacion morfologica especimen incomplet producto trafico ilegal fauna silvestre analisis molecular surge como he rramienta identificacion indispensable este estudio evaluo eficiencia extrac cion adn 50 muestr sangre 44 heces aves silvestr pertenecient parque conservacion medellin pureza concentracion material genetico determinaron espectrofotometria agarosa adem funcionalidad confirmo mediante amplificacion marcador citocromo oxidasa coxi reaccion cadena polimerasa pcr diferenci metric entre ambas ma tric biologic analizaron estadistica software 05 termin cuantitativ muestr sangre presentaron rendimiento significa tiva mayor mediana 34 ng ml frente heces mediana 05 ng ml 0013 asimismo observaron diferenci estadistica significativ pureza adn kh2 42 162 001 cuando 42 muestr sangre alcanzaron relacion 260 280 optima 8-2 comparacion 12 heces 0068 pesar sangre evidencio parametr concentracion calidad superior ambas muestr permitieron correcta amplificacion fragmento coxi mediante pcr esto confirma si bien sangre matriz mas eficiente muestr heces son adecuad funcional desarrollar estudi genetic aves particular uso heces representa alternativa valiosa trabaj cam po obtener material genetico sin necesidad recurrir captura manipulacion directa individu biodiversidad coxi codigo barr fauna silvestre efficiency of dna extraction from blood and fecal sampl of wild birds,1.0.0,9f8184beeb1e5fbb
2389-8526,5481_VF.pdf,5481_VF_0,en,amente significativas en la,"Given the limitations of morphological characterization in incomplete specimens re sulting from the illegal wildlife trade, molecular analysis emerges as an indispensa ble identification tool. This study evaluated the efficiency of dna extraction from 50 blood and 44 fecal samples from wild birds housed at the Parque de la Conservación in Medellín. The purity and concentration of the extracted genetic material were de termined via spectrophotometry and agarose gel electrophoresis, and its functionali ty was confirmed through pcr amplification of the coxi marker. Metric differences 2 Tatiana Jiménez-Herrera • Daisy Gómez-Ruiz • Ingrid Muñoz-Marín • Albeiro López-Herrera • Cristina Úsuga-Monroy Rev. Med. Vet. issn 0122-9354. issne 2389-8526: Bogotá (Colombia) n.° 52: e5481 • enero-junio, 2026 between both biological matrices were statistically analyzed using R software (v. 4.2.2; p < 0,05). Quantitatively, blood samples exhibited a significantly higher dna yield (median of 34,5 ng/μL) compared to fecal samples (median of 6,05 ng/ μL; p = 0,0013). Furthermore, statistically significant differences were observed in dna purity (χ² = 42,162; p < 0,001), with 42,9 % of blood samples achieving an optimal 260/280 ratio (1,8-2), compared to only 12,5 % of fecal samples (p = 0,0068). Despite blood demonstrating superior concentration and quality para meters, both sample types allowed for the successful pcr amplification of the coxi fragment. This confirms that, although blood is a more efficient biological matrix, fecal samples are fully adequate and viable for conducting avian genetic studies. In particular, the use of feces represents a highly valuable non-invasive alternative for fieldwork, as it allows for the collection of genetic material without the need for animal capture and direct handling","biodiversity, coxi, barcode, wildlife",marcadores,amente significativa en la,given limit morphological character incomplete specimen re sult illegal wildlife trade molecular analysi emerg indispensa ble identification tool study evaluat efficiency dna extraction 50 blood 44 fecal sampl wild bird hous parque de la conservacion medellin purity concentration extract genetic material de termin via spectrophotometry agarose gel electrophoresi its functionali ty confirm through pcr amplification coxi marker metric differenc tatiana jimenez-herrera daisy gomez-ruiz ingrid munoz-marin albeiro lopez-herrera cristina usuga-monroy rev med vet issn 0122-9354 issne 2389-8526 bogota colombia deg 52 e5481 enero-junio 2026 between both biological matric statistically analyz using software 05 quantitatively blood sampl exhibit significantly higher dna yield median 34 ng ml compar fecal sampl median 05 ng ml 0013 furthermore statistically significant differenc observ dna purity kh2 42 162 001 42 blood sampl achiev optimal 260 280 ratio 8-2 compar only 12 fecal sampl 0068 despite blood demonstrat superior concentration quality para meter both sample type allow successful pcr amplification coxi fragment confirm although blood more efficient biological matrix fecal sampl fully adequate viable conduct avian genetic studi particular use fece represent highly valuable non-invasive alternative fieldwork allow collection genetic material without need animal capture direct handl,biodiversity coxi barcode wildlife,amente significativa en la given limit morphological character incomplete specimen re sult illegal wildlife trade molecular analysi emerg indispensa ble identification tool study evaluat efficiency dna extraction 50 blood 44 fecal sampl wild bird hous parque de la conservacion medellin purity concentration extract genetic material de termin via spectrophotometry agarose gel electrophoresi its functionali ty confirm through pcr amplification coxi marker metric differenc tatiana jimenez-herrera daisy gomez-ruiz ingrid munoz-marin albeiro lopez-herrera cristina usuga-monroy rev med vet issn 0122-9354 issne 2389-8526 bogota colombia deg 52 e5481 enero-junio 2026 between both biological matric statistically analyz using software 05 quantitatively blood sampl exhibit significantly higher dna yield median 34 ng ml compar fecal sampl median 05 ng ml 0013 furthermore statistically significant differenc observ dna purity kh2 42 162 001 42 blood sampl achiev optimal 260 280 ratio 8-2 compar only 12 fecal sampl 0068 despite blood demonstrat superior concentration quality para meter both sample type allow successful pcr amplification coxi fragment confirm although blood more efficient biological matrix fecal sampl fully adequate viable conduct avian genetic studi particular use fece represent highly valuable non-invasive alternative fieldwork allow collection genetic material without need animal capture direct handl biodiversity coxi barcode wildlife,1.0.0,88aa79898e640154
2389-8526,5579_VF.pdf,5579_VF_0,en,"Agropecuarios, Universidad","Background: This work aimed to identify gastrointestinal parasites in birds from the Moroleón Zoo collection, Gua najuato, Mexico. Methods: The birds studied were inhabitants of the “Ru minant” section without restriction. However, during the autumn season, birds cohabited in the “Safari” (antelope, deer, and ostrich) and “Cameroon goat” sections. The bird collection consisted of 62 specimens, which are medically reviewed on a permanent basis as part of a routine veteri nary care program; thus, a total of 33 fecal samples, grouped into the orders Galliformes (n = 18), Anseriformes (n = 13), and Struthioniformes (n = 2), were non-probabilistically ob tained. Fecal samples were collected directly from the cloaca and preserved in 70 % alcohol. The samples were analyzed using two fecal parasitoscopic techniques: (1) direct micros copy and (2) zinc sulfate concentration (Faust). Addition ally, all samples were subjected to Kinyoun staining. Results: Overall, parasites were identified in 84.8 % of samples, with most containing 2 or more parasite types. The most frequent genera were Blastocystis (66.7 %) and Crypto sporidium (27.3 %), the former associated with Numina me leagridis (Galliformes; p = 0.01668) and the latter associated with Anseriformes (p = 0.03854). Conclusion: Knowledge of parasitic biodiversity in birds is crucial to understanding their transmission potential. Therefore, new studies must be conducted to determine the genotypes of the parasites transmitted between birds and other hosts. 2 Rev. Med. Vet. issn 0122-9354. issn-e 2389-8526: Bogotá (Colombia) n.° 52: e5579 • enero-junio, 2026 Karla de-la-Cruz • Marie Bartilotti • Jorge de-la-Rosa • Anelly Juárez • Andrez Ruiz • Axel Santiago Geiner Álvarez • Ernesto Cárdenas • Hugo Molina • Amador Martínez • Jesús Ponce","Blastocystis; Cryptosporidium; birds; zoo; parasite. Identificación de parásitos gastrointestinales en aves de la colección del Zoológico Moroleón, Guanajuato, México",marcadores,agropecuario universidad,background work aimed identify gastrointestinal parasit bird moroleon zoo collection gua najuato mexico method bird studi inhabitant ru minant section without restriction however during autumn season bird cohabit safari antelope deer ostrich cameroon goat section bird collection consist 62 specimen which medically review permanent basi part routine veteri nary care program thus total 33 fecal sampl group into order galliform 18 anseriform 13 struthioniform non-probabilistically ob tain fecal sampl collect directly cloaca preserv 70 alcohol sampl analyz using two fecal parasitoscopic techniqu direct micro copy zinc sulfate concentration faust addition ally all sampl subject kinyoun stain result overall parasit identifi 84 sampl most contain more parasite type most frequent genera blastocysti 66 crypto sporidium 27 former associat numina me leagridi galliform 01668 latter associat anseriform 03854 conclusion knowledge parasitic biodiversity bird crucial understand their transmission potential therefore new studi must conduct determine genotyp parasit transmitt between bird other host rev med vet issn 0122-9354 issn-e 2389-8526 bogota colombia deg 52 e5579 enero-junio 2026 karla de-la-cruz marie bartilotti jorge de-la-rosa anelly juarez andrez ruiz axel santiago geiner alvarez ernesto cardena hugo molina amador martinez jesu ponce,blastocysti cryptosporidium bird zoo parasite identificacion de parasito gastrointestinal en aves de la coleccion del zoologico moroleon guanajuato mexico,agropecuario universidad background work aimed identify gastrointestinal parasit bird moroleon zoo collection gua najuato mexico method bird studi inhabitant ru minant section without restriction however during autumn season bird cohabit safari antelope deer ostrich cameroon goat section bird collection consist 62 specimen which medically review permanent basi part routine veteri nary care program thus total 33 fecal sampl group into order galliform 18 anseriform 13 struthioniform non-probabilistically ob tain fecal sampl collect directly cloaca preserv 70 alcohol sampl analyz using two fecal parasitoscopic techniqu direct micro copy zinc sulfate concentration faust addition ally all sampl subject kinyoun stain result overall parasit identifi 84 sampl most contain more parasite type most frequent genera blastocysti 66 crypto sporidium 27 former associat numina me leagridi galliform 01668 latter associat anseriform 03854 conclusion knowledge parasitic biodiversity bird crucial understand their transmission potential therefore new studi must conduct determine genotyp parasit transmitt between bird other host rev med vet issn 0122-9354 issn-e 2389-8526 bogota colombia deg 52 e5579 enero-junio 2026 karla de-la-cruz marie bartilotti jorge de-la-rosa anelly juarez andrez ruiz axel santiago geiner alvarez ernesto cardena hugo molina amador martinez jesu ponce blastocysti cryptosporidium bird zoo parasite identificacion de parasito gastrointestinal en aves de la coleccion del zoologico moroleon guanajuato mexico,1.0.0,bfcae9c661c0a5aa
2389-8526,5579_VF.pdf,5579_VF_0,es,e Blastocystis (66.7 %) and Crypto,"Antecedentes: este trabajo tuvo como objetivo identificar pará sitos gastrointestinales en aves de la colección del Zoológico de Moroleón, Guanajuato, México. Métodos: las aves estudiadas pertenecían a la sección de rumiantes sin restricciones. Sin embar go, durante el otoño, cohabitaban en las secciones de safari (antí lope, venado y avestruz) y en la de cabra de Camerún. La colección constaba de 62 especímenes, que recibían atención veterinaria permanente como parte de un programa de cuidados rutinarios. Se obtuvieron 33 muestras fecales, agrupadas en los órdenes Ga lliformes (n = 18), Anseriformes (n = 13) y Struthioniformes (n = 2), de manera no probabilística. Las muestras fecales se recolecta ron directamente de la cloaca y se conservaron en alcohol al 70 %. Se analizaron mediante dos técnicas parasitoscópicas fecales: (1) microscopía directa y (2) concentración con sulfato de zinc (Faust). Además, todas las muestras se sometieron a la tinción de Kinyoun. Resultados: en general, se identificaron parásitos en el 84,8 % de las muestras, la mayoría de ellas con dos o más tipos de parásitos. Los géneros más frecuentes fueron Blastocystis (66,7 %) y Cryptosporidium (27,3 %); el primero, asociado a Numina melea gridis (Galliformes; p = 0,01668), y el segundo, a Anseriformes (p = 0,03854). Conclusión: el conocimiento de la biodiversidad parasitaria en las aves es crucial para comprender su potencial de transmisión. Por lo tanto, se deben realizar nuevos estudios para determinar los genotipos de los parásitos transmitidos entre aves y otros huéspedes","Blastocystis; Cryptosporidium; aves; zoológico; parásito. 3 Identification of gastrointestinal parasites in birds from the Moroleón Zoo collection, Guanajuato, Mexico Rev. Med. Vet. issn 0122-9354. issn-e 2389-8526: Bogotá (Colombia) n.° 52: e5579 • enero-junio, 2026",marcadores,blastocystis 66 and crypto,antecedent este trabajo tuvo como objetivo id