2389-993X,N42e20915563-PDF.pdf,N42e20915563-PDF_0,en,os de género. El estudio visibiliza la necesidad de diseñar estrategias de intervención,"Rural educational establishments are central scenarios in the configuration of the social representations that guide gender relations and forms of youth coexistence. There, the life experiences built in the interaction between family, school, and community reproduce traditional gender roles that have an impact on inequality, exclusion, and various expressions of symbolic violence. From this perspective, the rural context is assumed as a category whose cultural and relational dynamics influence gender construction. This article presents the results of a qualitative research project developed from a critical-social approach with collaborative ethnography design. Data collection was carried out through body mapping, semi-structured interviews, and participatory photography, instruments that allowed exploring the experiences, meanings, and practices associated with gender roles in rural young people from a rural area of the municipality of Neiva (Huila). The analysis was carried out through grounded theory, using coding and categorization processes. The results show that social representations about gender and gender roles are mainly configured in the family sphere, reinforced in school and rural community spaces, affecting individual and social relationships, naturalizing hierarchies and gender mandates. The study makes visible the need to design contextualized intervention strategies that recognize the, particularities of rurality, strengthen work with families, and promote inclusive educational practices oriented towards gender equality and violence prevention",Social representation; Gender; Gender roles; Rural sociology; Rural youth; Social change. Sumario: 1,marcadores,os de genero el estudio visibiliza la necesidad de disenar estrategia de intervencion,rural educational establishment central scenario configuration social represent guide gender relation form youth coexistence there life experienc built interaction between family school community reproduce traditional gender role have impact inequality exclusion variou expression symbolic violence perspective rural context assum category whose cultural relational dynamic influence gender construction article present result qualitative research project develop critical-social approach collaborative ethnography design data collection carri out through body mapp semi-structur interview participatory photography instrument allow explor experienc meaning practic associat gender role rural young people rural area municipality neiva huila analysi carri out through ground theory using coding categor process result show social represent about gender gender role mainly configur family sphere reinforc school rural community spac affect individual social relationship naturaliz hierarchi gender mandat study make visible need design contextualiz intervention strategi recognize particulariti rurality strengthen work famili promote inclusive educational practic orient toward gender equality violence prevention,social representation gender gender role rural sociology rural youth social change sumario,os de genero el estudio visibiliza la necesidad de disenar estrategia de intervencion rural educational establishment central scenario configuration social represent guide gender relation form youth coexistence there life experienc built interaction between family school community reproduce traditional gender role have impact inequality exclusion variou expression symbolic violence perspective rural context assum category whose cultural relational dynamic influence gender construction article present result qualitative research project develop critical-social approach collaborative ethnography design data collection carri out through body mapp semi-structur interview participatory photography instrument allow explor experienc meaning practic associat gender 