2422-3182,3674_v12n29_PDF.pdf,3674_v12n29_PDF_0,en,"cipal, aportando","Objective: To explore the relationship between nostalgia marketing and kidults’ purchase intention, considering the associations among the constructs that comprise the proposed model. Design/Methodology: This study adopted an exploratory, descriptive, correlational, and cross - sectional design with a quantitative approach. A structured questionnaire was administered to a sample of 302 kidults over the age of 30, selected through non -probabilistic convenien ce sampling. The data were analyzed using descriptive statistics, reliability and validity tests, normality tests, and Spearman’s rho correlations to examine the relationships between the dimensions of nostalgia marketing and purchase intention. Findings: The results indicate that kidults represent a segment highly receptive to nostalgia marketing, showing a strong emotional connection to products that evoke memories of their childhood or adolescence. Moreover, a significant positive correlation was found between exposure to nostalgia marketing strategies and purchase intention (r = 0.681, p < 0.01). Notably, 60.20% of respondents reported having purchased at least one product motivated by a recent nostalgic experience. Conclusions: A positive and statistically significant relationship was identified between nostalgia marketing and kidults’ purchase intention ( ρ = 0.681; p < 0.01; N = 302). These findings suggest that as stimuli associated with nostalgia marketing increase, purchase intention tends to increase as well. Given the correlational nature of the study, the results reveal an association between the vari ables analyzed, without implying a direct causal relationship. Originality: This paper provides a novel perspective for understanding kidult consumer behavior by considering nostalgia marketing as the central variable. Furthermore, it offers quantitative evidence and new insights that may contribute to the development of more eff ective and emotionally relevant advertising strategies","kidult consumer, emotions in consumption, purchase intention, nostalgia marketing, emotional advertising. Highlights ▪ Nostalgia influences purchasing behavior because it strengthens emotional bonds. ▪ Nostalgic advertising increases purchase intention through the evocation of memories. ▪ This study explains how nostalgic emotions drive consumption. ▪ The proposed model helps to u",marcadores,cipal aportando,objective explore relationship between nostalgia market kidult purchase intention consider associ among construct comprise propos model design methodology study adopt exploratory descriptive correlational cros sectional design quantitative approach structur questionnaire administer sample 302 kidult over age 30 select through non -probabilistic convenien ce sampl data analyz using descriptive statistic reliability validity test normality test spearman rho correl examine relationship between dimension nostalgia market purchase intention finding result indicate kidult represent segment highly receptive nostalgia market show strong emotional connection product evoke memori their childhood adolescence moreover significant positive correlation found between exposure nostalgia market strategi purchase intention 681 01 notably 60 20 respondent report having purchas least one product motivat recent nostalgic experience conclusion positive statistically significant relationship identifi between nostalgia market kidult purchase intention 681 01 302 these finding suggest stimuli associat nostalgia market increase purchase intention tend increase well given correlational nature study result reveal association between vari able analyz without imply direct causal relationship originality paper provid novel perspective understand kidult consumer behavior consider nostalgia market central variable furthermore offer quantitative evidence new insight may contribute development more eff ective emotionally relevant advertis str