2422-3719,19(3)_19666+Detection+and+molecular+RCCH19(3).pdf,19(3)_19666+Detection+and+molecular+RCCH19(3)_0,en,Detection and molecular characterization of potato yellow vein,"The potato yellow vein virus (PYVV) is a Crinivirus transmitted by the whitefly Trialeurodes vaporariorum and is associated with significant economic losses in potato (Solanum spp.) cultivation in the Andean region. Until now, the presence of PYVV had not been reported in the department of Norte de Santander, Colombia. In this study, we report for the first time the detection of PYVV in Solanum phureja plants exhibiting typical vein yellowing symptoms in the locality of Chitaga. Leaf samples were collected and subjected to molecular analysis by RT-PCR, confirming the presence of the virus. The obtained amplicon was sequenced and deposited in GenBank under accession number PV593540. Phylogenetic analysis revealed that the sequence shares 98.8% nucleotide identity with other Colombian isolates of PYVV and clusters closely with sequences from the department of Nariño. This finding suggests a possible introduction of the virus into Norte de Santander through infected seed tubers. These results underscore the importance of implementing robust epidemiological surveillance systems and promoting the use of virus-free certified seed to prevent the dissemination of PYVV and other pathogens across potato-growing regions. Additional","Crinivirus; geographic spread; phylogenetic analysis; vegetative propagation; whitefly transmission. Doi: https://doi.org/10.19053/uptc.24223719.19666 REVISTA COLOMBIANA DE CIENCIAS HORTÍCOLAS - Vol. 19 - No. 3, 1-9, September-December, 2025 e-ISSN: 2422-3719 · ISSN-L: 2011-2173 1 Universidad Francisco de Paula Santander– , Facultad de Ciencias Básicas, Grupo de investigación Fitobiomol, San",marcadores,detection molecular character potato yellow vein,potato yellow vein viru pyvv criniviru transmitt whitefly trialeurod vaporariorum associat significant economic loss potato so