2422-3719,2_Heavy+metals+on+strawberry.pdf,2_Heavy+metals+on+strawberry_0,en,Effect of heavy metals on strawberry,"Despite their high nutritional properties, strawberries are classified as the most contaminated fruits. Their contaminants include heavy metals (HM) such as cadmium (Cd), lead (Pb), mercury (Hg), chromium (Cr) and the metalloid arsenic (As). The sources of these contaminants are water, air and soils of geogenic and anthropogenic origin, the last of which is the biggest contributor. This situation poses a health risk to humans. Between 3 and 16% of agricultural soils are affected by excessive levels of HM, especially those near industrial and mining areas, as well as those with high concentrations of pesticides and fertilizers. There is a strong correlation between the HM content in the soil and the HM content in the strawberry plants, with the greatest accumulation of HM in the root system. HM are absorbed by the roots but also aerially by the leaves, and they are also retained in the cuticle wax of the fruits. Excess HMs, especially Cd, in strawberry plants manifest themselves in a decrease in biomass, chlorophyll, stomatal conductance, growth hormones, and leaf area, as well as in oxidative damage, lower photosynthetic efficiency, and changes in the accumulation and redistribution of mineral elements. Strategies for reducing contamination in strawberry plants include the application of silicon, humic acid, melatonin, abscisic acid, or Bacillus spp., as well as the use of nanoparticles (e.g. SiNPs), inoculation with arbuscular mycorrhizal fungi, biochar amendments, and planting HM hyperaccumulators, among others. Additional","contamination; cadmium; oxidative damage; biomass; sewage sludge; remediation. 1 Universidad Nacional de Colombia , Facultad de Ciencias Agrarias, Departamento de Agronomía, Bogota (Colombia) 2 Universidad de Almería , Departamento de Biología y Geología, Almeria (Spain) 3 Author for correspondence. gfischer@unal.edu.co REVISTA COLOMBIANA DE CIENCIAS HORTÍCOLAS - Vol. 19 - No. 3, 1-16, Septemb",marcadores,effect heavy metal strawberry,despite their high nutritional properti strawberri classifi most contaminat fruit their contaminant include heavy metal hm such cadmium cd lead pb mercury hg chromium cr metalloid arsenic sourc these contaminant water air soil geogenic anthropogenic origin last which biggest contributor situation pose health risk human between 16 agricultural soil affect excessive level hm especially those near industrial mining area well those high concentr pesticid fertilizer there strong correlation between hm content soil hm content strawberry plant greatest accumulation hm root system hm absorb root but also aerially leav they also retain cuticle wax fruit exces hms especially cd strawberry plant manifest themselv decrease biomas chlorophyll stomatal conductance growth hormon leaf area well oxidative damage lower photosynthetic efficiency chang accumulation redistribution mineral element strategi reduc contamination strawberry plant include application silicon humic acid melatonin abscisic acid bacillu spp well use nanoparticl sinp inoculation arbuscular mycorrhizal fungi biochar amendment plant hm hyperaccumulator among other additional,contamination cadmium oxidative damage biomas sewage sludge remediation universidad nacional de colombia facultad de ciencia agraria departamento de agronomia bogota colombia universidad de almeria departamento de biologia geologia almeria spain author correspondence gfischer unal edu co revista colombiana de ciencia horticola vol 19 no 1-16 septemb,effect heavy metal strawberry despite their high nutritional properti strawberri classifi most contaminat fruit their contaminant include heavy metal hm such cadmium cd lead pb mercury hg chromium cr metalloid arsenic sourc these contaminant water air soil geogenic anthropogenic origin last which biggest contributor situation pose health risk human between 16 agricultural soil affect excessive 