2422-3719,3_Proteomic+insights+into+water+stress+in+potato.pdf,3_Proteomic+insights+into+water+stress+in+potato_0,en,Proteomics reveals an association between water stress,"Water stress is among the most critical factors limiting plant performance. Proteomics serves as a powerful tool for assessing changes in protein expression and identifying mechanisms underlying drought stress tolerance in plants. This study aims to identify proteins associated with water stress severity in potato (Solanum tuberosum L.) and to characterize their differential expression as potential defense mechanisms against stress. Potato plants at the tuber differentiation stage were subjected to mild, moderate, and severe water stress by withholding irrigation. Gas exchange measurements and proteomic analyses were conducted at each stress level. For protein extraction and proteome profiling using two-dimensional polyacrylamide gel electrophoresis (2D-PAGE), leaf samples were collected from plants under different stress conditions and from well-watered controls. A total of 74 protein spots were detected, and proteins associated with water stress were selected based on correlation analysis between their relative abundance and leaf water potential. Seven proteins were identified via mass spectrometry. Increasing water stress severity was associated with a decline in gas exchange and an increase in water use efficiency. Notably, an increase in the relative abundance of Rubisco activase, Photosystem I subunit IV B reaction center, and the manganese-stabilizing protein of Photosystem II under water stress suggests a potential protective strategy for maintaining photosynthetic function. Conversely, three isoforms of cytochrome oxidase (COX) subunit I exhibited decreased expression, which may be linked to a heat dissipation mechanism aimed at mitigating reactive oxygen species (ROS) formation during water stress. The identification of these proteins provides a baseline to further understand water stress in potatoes. Additional","abiotic stress; plant proteins; chloroplasts; enzyme activity; water use efficiency; Solanum tuberosum L.; two-dimensional electrophoresis; metabolic pathways. Doi: https://doi.org/10.19053/uptc.24223719.19193 REVISTA COLOMBIANA DE CIENCIAS HORTÍCOLAS - Vol. 19 - No. 3, 1-12, September-December, 2025 e-ISSN: 2422-3719 · ISSN-L: 2011-2173 1 Universidad Nacional de Colombia – , Facultad de Cienc",marcadores,proteomic reveal association between water stres,water stres among most critical factor limit plant performance proteomic serv powerful tool assess chang protein expression identify mechanism underly drought stres tolerance plant study aims identify protein associat water stres severity potato solanum tuberosum characterize their differential expression potential defense mechanism against stres potato plant tuber differentiation stage subject mild moderate severe water stres withhold irrigation gas exchange measurement proteomic analys conduct each stres level protein extraction proteome profil using two-dimensional polyacrylamide gel electrophoresi 2d-page leaf sampl collect plant under different stres condition well-water control total 74 protein spot detect protein associat water stres select based correlation analysi between their relative abundance leaf water potential seven protein identifi via mass spectrometry increas water stres severity associat decline gas exchange increase water use efficiency notably increase relative abundance rubisco activase photosystem subunit iv reaction center manganese-stabiliz protein photosystem ii under water stres suggest potential protective strategy maintain photosynthetic function conversely three isoform cytochrome oxidase cox subunit exhibit decreas expression which may link heat dissipation mechanism aimed mitigat reactive oxygen speci ros formation during water stres identification these protein provid baseline further understand water stres potato additional,abiotic stres plant protein chloroplast enzyme activity water use efficiency solanum tuberosum two-dimensional electrophoresi metabolic pathway doi http doi org 10 19053 uptc 24223719 19193 revista colombiana de ciencia horticola vol 19 no 1-12 september-december 2025 e-issn 2422-3719 issn-l 2011-2173 universidad nacional de colombia facultad de cienc,proteomic reveal association between water stres water stres among most critical factor limit plant performance proteomic serv powerful tool assess chang protein expression identify mechanism underly drought stres tolerance plant study aims identify protein associat water stres severity potato solanum tuberosum characterize their differential expression potential defense mechanism against stres potato plant tuber differentiation stage subject mild moderate severe water stres withhold irrigation gas exchange measurement proteomic analys conduct each stres level protein extraction proteome profil using two-dimensional polyacrylamide gel electrophoresi 2d-page leaf sampl collect plant under different stres condition well-water control total 74 protein spot detect protein associat water stres select based correlation analysi between their relative abundance leaf water potential seven protein identifi via mass spectrometry increas water stres severity associat decline gas exchange increase water use efficiency notably increase relative abundance rubisco activase photosystem subunit iv reaction center manganese-stabiliz protein photosystem ii under water stres suggest potential protective strategy maintain photosynthetic function conversely three isoform cytochrome oxidase cox subunit exhibit decreas expression which may link heat dissipation mechanism aimed mitigat reactive oxygen speci ros formation during water stres identification these protein provid baseline further understand water stres potato additional abiotic stres plant protein chloroplast enzyme activity water use efficiency solanum tuberosum two-dimensional electrophoresi metabolic pathway 