2462-8190,BCCM+29(2)_2.pdf,BCCM+29(2)_2_0,en,4 Magister en Ciencias Ambientales. Universidad Surcolombiana. Grupo de Investigación y Pedagogía en,"The edge effect on the distribution and interactions of animal and plant species has been extensively studied across different regions. However, there are no references to arbuscular mycorrhizal fungi (AMF) in tropical areas. This study aimed to evaluate the edge effect on root colonisation by AMF in the relict tropical dry forest of La Tribuna in southern Colombia. The homogeneity of colonisation values was also evaluated in relation to the selection of sampling sites. Five sampling sites, known as 'wells' due to their proximity to oil extraction wells, were selected, and forest edge zones were determined at these sites and labelled 'interior', 'transition' and 'exterior'. A predominant tree or shrub species was selected in each zone, and three individuals of this species were selected. Root samples were taken from each individual to quantify AMF colonization, and rhizosphere samples were collected for physicochemical analysis during the dry and rainy seasons. The results indicated significant variability in soil parameters, with no evidence of an edge effect on colonization. However, significant differences in root colonisation levels were observed between the wells. It was concluded that root colonisation by AMF responded more to local soil factors within each edge zone than to the edge effect itself","tropical dry forest, edge effect, plant species, mycorrhizae",marcadores,magister en ciencia ambiental universidad surcolombiana grupo de investigacion pedagogia en,edge effect distribution interaction animal plant speci has been extensively studi acros different region however there no referenc arbuscular mycorrhizal fungi amf tropical area study aimed evaluate edge effect root colonisation amf relict tropical dry forest la tribuna southern colombia homogeneity colonisation valu also evaluat relation selection sampl site five sampl site known well due their proximity oil extraction well select forest edge zone determin these site labell interior transition exterior predominant tree shrub speci select each zone three individual speci select root sampl taken each individual quantify amf colon rhizosphere sampl collect physicochemical analysi during dry rainy season result indicat significant variability soil parameter no evidence edge effect colon however significant differenc root colonisation level observ between well conclud root colonisation amf respond more local soil factor within each edge zone than edge effect itself,tropical dry forest edge effect plant speci mycorrhizae,magister en ciencia ambiental universidad surcolombiana grupo de investigacion pedagogia en edge effect distribution interaction animal plant speci has been extensively studi acros different region however there no referenc arbuscular mycorrhizal fungi amf tropical area study aimed evaluate edge effect root colonisation amf relict tropical dry forest la tribuna southern colombia homogeneity colonisation valu also evaluat relation selection sampl site five sampl site known well due their proximity oil extraction well select forest edge zone determin these site labell interior transition exterior predominant tree shrub speci select each zone three individual speci select root sampl taken each individual quantify amf colon rhizosphere sampl collect physicochemical analysi during dry rainy season result indicat significant variability soil parameter no evidence edge effect colon however significant differenc root colonisation level observ between well conclud root colonisation amf respond more local soil factor within each edge zone than edge effect itself tropical dry forest edge effect plant speci mycorrhizae,1.0.0,fa903ddfe06d9d64
2462-8190,BCCM+29(2)_4.pdf,BCCM+29(2)_4_0,es,Patrones de diversidad y estructura de bosques amazónicos colombianos,"El estudio de la vegetación en gradientes ecológicos es útil como indicador de su función ecosistémica y para orientar acciones de manejo. Esta investigación analizó los patrones de riqueza, diversidad y estructura de bosques húmedos de la Amazonía colombiana. Se realizaron 18 parcelas de 0,1 ha en la vegetación arbórea, recolectando la información de individuos con DAP ≥ 10 cm, en 5 localidades de 3 departamentos de Colombia, y abarcando las zonas de vida bh-T, bmh-PM y bmh-MB (69-2225 msnm). Se encontró que la riqueza (α < 0.01), la diversidad (α < 0,05) y el área basal -AB- (α < 0,05) decrece a medida que aumenta el gradiente altitudinal. El AB se asoció a individuos de categorías diamétricas entre 30-40 cm y > 40 cm, y de altura total de 20-30 m y > 30 m. Se encontraron diferencias significativas solo a nivel de diversidad y riqueza (α < 0,1) entre las dos localidades con más baja y más alta elevación altitudinal. La diversidad beta presentó una disimilitud muy alta (> 85 %) y no se encontraron superposiciones en las elipses del diagrama de ordenación (α < 0,05). Lo anterior, está relacionado con un conjunto de especies característico de cada localidad, las cuales no se distribuyen de manera uniforme a lo largo del gradiente","bosques amazónicos, diversidad forestal, ecología de comunidades arbóreas, gradientes ecológicos. 1 Magister en Manejo, Uso y Conservación del Bosque, e Ingeniero Forestal de la Universidad Distrital Francisco José de Caldas. Department of Marine, Earth, and Atmospheric Sciences, North Carolina State University, Raleigh, Estados Unidos; Grupo de Investigación en Uso y Conservación de la Divers",marcadores,patron diversidad estructura bosqu amazonic colombian,estudio vegetacion gradient ecologic util como indicador funcion ecosistemica orientar accion manejo esta investigacion analizo patron riqueza diversidad estructura bosqu humed amazonia colombiana realizaron 18 parcel ha vegetacion arborea recolect informacion individu dap 10 cm localidad departament colombia abarc zonas vida bh-t bmh-pm bmh-mb 69-2225 msnm encontro riqueza 01 diversidad 05 area basal -ab- 05 decrece medida aumenta gradiente altitudinal ab asocio individu categori diametric entre 30-40 cm 40 cm altura total 20-30 30 encontraron diferenci significativ solo nivel diversidad riqueza entre dos localidad mas baja mas alta elevacion altitudinal diversidad beta presento disimilitud muy alta 85 no encontraron superposicion elips diagrama ordenacion 05 anterior esta relacionado conjunto especi caracteristico cada localidad cual no distribuyen manera uniforme largo gradiente,bosqu amazonic diversidad forestal ecologia comunidad arbore gradient ecologic magister manejo uso conservacion bosque ingeniero forestal universidad distrital francisco jose cald department of marine earth and atmospheric scienc north carolina state university raleigh estad unid grupo investigacion uso conservacion divers,patron diversidad estructura bosqu amazonic colombian estudio vegetacion gradient ecologic util como indicador funcion ecosistemica orientar accion manejo esta investigacion analizo patron riqueza diversidad estructura bosqu humed amazonia colombiana realizaron 18 parcel ha vegetacion arborea recolect informacion individu dap 10 cm localidad departament colombia abarc zonas vida bh-t bmh-pm bmh-mb 69-2225 msnm encontro riqueza 01 diversidad 05 area basal -ab- 05 decrece medida aumenta gradiente altitudinal ab asocio individu categori diametric entre 30-40 cm 40 cm altura total 20-30 30 encontraron diferenci significativ solo nivel diversidad riqueza entre dos localidad mas baja mas alta elevacion altitudinal diversidad beta presento disimilitud muy alta 85 no encontraron superposicion elips diagrama ordenacion 05 anterior esta relacionado conjunto especi caracteristico cada localidad cual no distribuyen manera uniforme largo gradiente bosqu amazonic diversidad forestal ecologia comunidad arbore gradient ecologic magister manejo uso conservacion bosque ingeniero forestal universidad distrital francisco jose cald department of marine earth and atmospheric scienc north carolina state university raleigh estad unid grupo investigacion uso conservacion divers,1.0.0,b6c2130b829d74a0
2462-8190,BCCM+29(2)_4.pdf,BCCM+29(2)_4_0,en,"Distrital Francisco José de Caldas. Proyecto Curricular de Ingeniería Forestal, Universidad Distrital Francisco José de","Researching vegetation along ecological gradients is useful as an indicator of its ecosystem function and for forest management. In this study, we analyzed patterns of richness, diversity and structure in Colombian Amazon forests. We sampled 18 0.1-hectare plots, focusing on tree vegetation and collecting data on individuals with a diameter at breast height (DBH) of at least 10 cm across five localities in three departments of Colombia. The life zones included tropical moist forest, as well as premontane and lower montane wet forests (69–2,225 m a.s.l.). We found that richness, diversity and basal area decreased with altitude (α < 0.01, α < 0.05 and α < 0.05, respectively). BA is associated with individuals in the diameter categories 30–40 cm and >40 cm, as well as total heights of 20–30 m and >30 m . Beta diversity exhibited very high dissimilarity (>85%), with no overlap of ellipses on the ordination diagram (p < 0.05). This is related to a specific set of characteristic species in each locality that are not uniformly distributed along the gradient","Amazon rainforests, ecological gradients, forest diversity, tree community ecology",marcadores,distrital francisco jose de calda proyecto curricular de ingenieria forestal universidad distrital francisco jose de,research vegetation along ecological gradient useful indicator its ecosystem function forest management study we analyz pattern richnes diversity structure colombian amazon forest we sampl 18 1-hectare plot focus tree vegetation collect data individual diameter breast height dbh least 10 cm acros five localiti three department colombia life zone includ tropical moist forest well premontane lower montane wet forest 69-2 225 we found richnes diversity basal area decreas altitude 01 05 05 respectively ba associat individual diameter categori 30-40 cm 40 cm well total height 20-30 30 beta diversity exhibit very high dissimilarity 85 no overlap ellips ordination diagram 05 relat specific set characteristic speci each locality not uniformly distribut along gradient,amazon rainforest ecological gradient forest diversity tree community ecology,distrital francisco jose de calda proyecto curricular de ingenieria forestal universidad distrital francisco jose de research vegetation along ecological gradient useful indicator its ecosystem function forest management study we analyz pattern richnes diversity structure colombian amazon forest we sampl 18 1-hectare plot focus tree vegetation collect data individual diameter breast height dbh least 10 cm acros five localiti three department colombia life zone includ tropical moist forest well premontane lower montane wet forest 69-2 225 we found richnes diversity basal area decreas altitude 01 05 05 respectively ba associat individual diameter categori 30-40 cm 40 cm well total height 20-30 30 beta diversity exhibit very high dissimilarity 85 no overlap ellips ordination diagram 05 relat specific set characteristic speci each locality not uniformly distribut along gradient amazon rainforest ecological gradient forest diversity tree community ecology,1.0.0,3dde7b5013632f6d
2462-8190,BCCM+29(2)_6.pdf,BCCM+29(2)_6_0,es,"Nuevas subespecies de Panyapedaliodes phila (Hewitson, 1862) y","Se describe una nueva subespecie de Panyapedaliodes phila que habita en la Cordillera Occidental de Colombia y dos nuevas subespecies de Pedaliodes praxithea, una de ellas habita en el Macizo de Santander, parte norte de la Cordillera Oriental y la otra subespecie se localiza en las cordilleras Central y Occidental, pertenecientes a la subtribu Pronophilina (Lepidoptera: Nymphalidae: Satyrinae) de mariposas de medio ambientes montanos de la región Neotropical","Colombia, Cordillera Central, Cordillera Occidental Especialista en Proyectos Mineros, Servicio Geológico Colombiano, Medellín, Antioquia, gabrieldimera@gmail.com orcid.org/0000-0003-1422-3523 Google Scholar CÓMO CITAR: Rodríguez, G. (2025). Nuevas subespecies de Panyapedaliodes phila (Hewitson, 1862) y Pedaliodes praxithea (Hewitson, 1870) de Colombia (Lepidoptera, Nymphalidae, Satirinae). Bo",marcadores,nuev subespeci panyapedaliod phila hewitson 1862,describe nueva subespecie panyapedaliod phila habita cordillera occidental colombia dos nuev subespeci pedaliod praxithea ellas habita macizo santander parte norte cordillera oriental otra subespecie localiza cordiller central occidental pertenecient subtribu pronophilina lepidoptera nymphalidae satyrinae maripos medio ambient montan region neotropical,colombia cordillera central cordillera occidental especialista proyect miner servicio geologico colombiano medellin antioquia gabrieldimera gmail com orcid org 0000-0003-1422-3523 google scholar como citar rodriguez 2025 nuev subespeci panyapedaliod phila hewitson 1862 pedaliod praxithea hewitson 1870 colombia lepidoptera nymphalidae satirinae bo,nuev subespeci panyapedaliod phila hewitson 1862 describe nueva subespecie panyapedaliod phila habita cordillera occidental colombia dos nuev subespeci pedaliod praxithea ellas habita macizo santander parte norte cordillera oriental otra subespecie localiza cordiller central occidental pertenecient subtribu pronophilina lepidoptera nymphalidae satyrinae maripos medio ambient montan region neotropical colombia cordillera central cordillera occidental especialista proyect miner servicio geologico colombiano medellin antioquia gabrieldimera gmail com orcid org 0000-0003-1422-3523 google scholar como citar rodriguez 2025 nuev subespeci panyapedaliod phila hewitson 1862 pedaliod praxithea hewitson 1870 colombia lepidoptera nymphalidae satirinae bo,1.0.0,a738d9aed970f729
2462-8190,BCCM+29(2)_6.pdf,BCCM+29(2)_6_0,en,rdillera Occidental,"This paper describes a new subspecies of Panyapedaliodes phila from the western Andes of Colombia, as well as two new subspecies of Pedaliodes praxithea. One inhabits the Santander Massif in the northern part of the Eastern Andes and the other is found in the Central and Western Andes. All three subspecies belong to the subtribe Pronophilina (Lepidoptera: Nymphalidae: Satyrinae) of butterflies inhabiting montane environments in the Neotropical region","Central Andes, Colombia, Western Andes, Panyapedaliodes phila frontina",marcadores,rdillera occidental,paper describ new subspeci panyapedaliod phila western ande colombia well two new subspeci pedaliod praxithea one inhabit santander massif northern part eastern ande other found central western ande all three subspeci belong subtribe pronophilina lepidoptera nymphalidae satyrinae butterfli inhabit montane environment neotropical region,central ande colombia western ande panyapedaliod phila frontina,rdillera occidental paper describ new subspeci panyapedaliod phila western ande colombia well two new subspeci pedaliod praxithea one inhabit santander massif northern part eastern ande other found central western ande all three subspeci belong subtribe pronophilina lepidoptera nymphalidae satyrinae butterfli inhabit montane environment neotropical region central ande colombia western ande panyapedaliod phila frontina,1.0.0,3649a2e1f5f50aa5
2462-8190,BCCM+29(2)_7.pdf,BCCM+29(2)_7_0,en,Coastal Amphipods of Bahía Málaga and Bahía Buenaventura in the,"Objectives: Characterize the amphipods collected at six coastal sites in the central Colombian Pacific. Scope: Increase biodiversity knowledge of a poorly studied group in the Colombian Pacific, but of great importance in benthic ecosystems. Methodology: Amphipod biodiversity was characterized in Bahía Málaga (intertidal and subtidal rocky shores, and sandy beaches) and Bahía Buenaventura (intertidal rocky shores, mangrove roots, and sandy beaches), two important estuaries in the central Pacific coast of Colombia. Results: Sixteen species in eleven families were found; Hourstonius baciroa, Leptocheirus rhizophorae, Leucothoe alata, Elasmopus ocoroni, Melita bousfieldi, and Neomegamphopus heardi represent new records for Colombia. Conclusions: This study significantly increases knowledge of amphipod biodiversity in coastal ecosystems of the Eastern Tropical Pacific, and highlights that systematic studies should be carried out to better understand the ecological function of this group in the Colombian Pacific","Crustacea, Peracarida, biodiversity, rocky shores, mangroves, sand beaches. 1 PhD Oceanografía Biológica. Universidad del Valle, Facultad de Ciencias Naturales y Exactas, Departamento de Biología, Grupo de Investigación en Ecología Animal. Cali, Colombia. Correo electrónico: bellineth.valencia@ correounivalle.edu.co orcid.org/0000-0002-1471-8270 Google Scholar 2 PhD Oceanografía. Universidad d",marcadores,coastal amphipod bahia malaga bahia buenaventura,objectiv characterize amphipod collect six coastal site central colombian pacific scope increase biodiversity knowledge poorly studi group colombian pacific but great importance benthic ecosystem methodology amphipod biodiversity characteriz bahia malaga intertidal subtidal rocky shor sandy beach bahia buenaventura intertidal rocky shor mangrove root sandy beach two important estuari central pacific coast colombia result sixteen speci eleven famili found hourstoniu baciroa leptocheiru rhizophorae leucothoe alata elasmopu ocoroni melita bousfieldi neomegamphopu heardi represent new record colombia conclusion study significantly increas knowledge amphipod biodiversity coastal ecosystem eastern tropical pacific highlight systematic studi should carri out better understand ecological function group colombian pacific,crustacea peracarida biodiversity rocky shor mangrov sand beach phd oceanografia biologica universidad del valle facultad de ciencia natural exacta departamento de biologia grupo de investigacion en ecologia animal cali colombia correo electronico bellineth valencia correounivalle edu co orcid org 0000-0002-1471-8270 google scholar phd oceanografia universidad,coastal amphipod bahia malaga bahia buenaventura objectiv characterize amphipod collect six coastal site central colombian pacific scope increase biodiversity knowledge poorly studi group colombian pacific but great importance benthic ecosystem methodology amphipod biodiversity characteriz bahia malaga intertidal subtidal rocky shor sandy beach bahia buenaventura intertidal rocky shor mangrove root sandy beach two important estuari central pacific coast colombia result sixteen speci eleven famili found hourstoniu baciroa leptocheiru rhizophorae leucothoe alata elasmopu ocoroni melita bousfieldi neomegamphopu heardi represent new record colombia conclusion study significantly increas knowledge amphipod biodiversity coastal ecosystem eastern tropical pacific highlight systematic studi should carri out better understand ecological function group colombian pacific crustacea peracarida biodiversity rocky shor mangrov sand beach phd oceanografia biologica universidad del valle facultad de ciencia natural exacta departamento de biologia grupo de investigacion en ecologia animal cali colombia correo electronico bellineth valencia correounivalle edu co orcid org 0000-0002-1471-8270 google scholar phd oceanogra