2462-859X,05_7994_RLB+26(1)+(2).pdf,05_7994_RLB+26(1)+(2)_0,en,do la autonomía futura y redistribuyendo la agencia moral hacia actores actuales sin,"Germline genetic editing has radically expanded human capacities to intervene in the biological constitution of future individuals, raising unprecedented ethical challenges concerning identity, autonomy, and justice. This article examines the normative implications of such interventions through an interdisciplinary theoretical-normative approach, arguing that heritable modifications affect not only the biological and psychological dimensions of personal identity but also shape narrative and relational possibilities of the self, thereby compromising future autonomy and reallocating moral agency to present actors lacking direct legitimacy. Structural risks of inequality, stigmatization, and biotechnological exclusion are also identified. In response, the article proposes a transgenerational bioethical framework grounded in human dignity, protection of the open future, and inclusive justice, operationalized through multilevel governance structures and pluralistic public deliberation. This framework helps guide ethical decision-making in a global technoscientific context, fostering intergenerational responsibility and biopolitical equity",Germline genetic editing; personal identity; future autonomy; moral agency; intergenerational justice; normative bioethics. Identidade e agência moral: implicações normativas da edição genética germinal em contextos transgeracionais,marcadores,do la autonomia futura redistribuyendo la agencia moral hacia actor actual sin,germline genetic edit has radically expand human capaciti intervene biological constitution future individual rais unprecedent ethical challeng concern identity autonomy justice article examin normative implic such intervention through interdisciplinary theoretical-normative approach argu heritable modific affect not only biological psychological dimension personal identity but also shape narrative relational possibiliti self thereby compromis future autonomy reallocat moral agency present actor lack direct legitimacy structural risk inequality stigmat biotechnological exclusion also identifi response article propos transgenerational bioethical framework ground human dignity protection open future inclusive justice operationaliz through multilevel governance structur pluralistic public deliberation framework help guide ethical decision-mak global technoscientific context foster intergenerational responsibility biopolitical equity,germline genetic edit personal identity future autonomy moral agency intergenerational justice normative bioethic identidade agencia moral implicaco normativa da edicao genetica germinal em contexto transgeracionai,do la autonomia futura redistribuyendo la agencia moral hacia actor actual sin germline genetic edit has radically expand human capaciti intervene biological constitution future individual rais unprecedent ethical challeng concern identity autonomy justice article examin normative implic such intervention through interdisciplinary theoretical-normative approach argu heritable modific affect not only biological psychological dimension personal identity but also shape narrative relational possibiliti self thereby compromis future autonomy reallocat moral agency present actor lack direct legitimacy structural risk inequality stigmat biotechnological exclusion also identifi response article propos transgenerational bioethical framework ground human dignity protection open future inclusive justice operationaliz through multilevel governance structur pluralistic public deliberation framework help guide ethical decision-mak global technoscientific context foster intergenerational responsibility biopolitical equity germline genetic edit personal identity future autonomy moral agency intergenerational justice normative bioethic identidade agencia moral implicaco normativa da edicao genetica germinal em con