2462-859X,06_7631_RLB+25(2).pdf,06_7631_RLB+25(2)_0,en,"ilibre los derechos individuales con las demandas colectivas, promoviendo","During the COVID-19 pandemic, the global debate surrounding mandatory vaccination intensified. This study aims to explore the philosophical arguments underpinning this discussion through a qualitative review of the specialized literature. Documentary research was conducted in March 2022 through bibliographic searches in the Scopus and Web of Science databases, using combinations of terms related to vaccination and ethics to identify relevant studies. Thirty articles were selected for in-depth analysis using the constant comparative method. Arguments in favor of mandatory vaccination focus on the primacy of the common good, moral responsibility, the need for restrictions in the face of social risks, and public utility. Oppositions against it, however, highlight the lack of information transparency, threats to individual freedom, the possibility of discrimination and undue influence, as well as criticism of the idea that vaccination constitutes, in and of itself, a public good. From an ethics of responsibility perspective, the need to impose it is also questioned. The study concludes that the discussion on mandatory vaccination must be approached from a perspective that balances individual rights with collective needs, promoting an ethical dialogue that considers both public health and trust in institutions. This reflection is essential to understanding the complexity of health decisions in the context of a global crisis","bioethics, coronavirus, immunization, pandemic, qualitative review. Argumentos filosóficos para a defesa ou rejeição da vacinação obrigatória contra a COVID-19",marcadores,ilibre los derecho individual con las demanda colectiva promoviendo,during covid-19 pandemic global debate surround mandatory vaccination intensifi study aims explore philosophical argument underpinn discussion through qualitative review specializ literature documentary research conduct march 2022 through bibliographic search scopu web science databas using combin term relat vaccination ethic identify relevant studi thirty articl select in-depth analysi using constant comparative method argument favor mandatory vaccination focu primacy common good moral responsibility need restriction face social risk public utility opposition against however highlight lack information transparency threat individual freedom possibility discrimination undue influence well criticism idea vaccination constitut itself public good ethic responsibility perspective need impose also question study conclud discussion mandatory vaccination must approach perspective balanc individual right collective need promot ethical dialogue consider both public health trust institution reflection essential understand complexity health decision context global crisi,bioethic coronaviru immun pandemic qualitative review argumento filosofico para defesa ou rejeicao da vacinacao obrigatoria contra covid-19,ilibre los derecho individual con las demanda colectiva promoviendo during covid-19 pandemic global debate surround mandatory vaccination intensifi study aims explore philosophical argument underpinn discussion through qualitative review specializ literature documentary research conduct march 2022 through bibliographic search scopu web science databas using combin term relat vaccination ethic identify relevant studi thirty articl select in-depth analysi using constant comparative method argument favor mandatory vaccination focu primacy common good moral responsibility need restriction face social risk public utility opposition against however highlight lack information transparency threat individual freedom possibility discrimination undue influence well criticism idea vaccination constitut itself public good ethic responsibility perspective need impose also question study conclud discussion mandatory vaccination must approach perspective balanc individu