2462-9448,06+emergency+triage.pdf,06+emergency+triage_0,en,.google.com/citations?user=rr9A1ygAAAAJ&hl=es,"Introduction. This study presents innovative research on classifying emergency depart ment patients using advanced machine-learning techniques. Objective. Provide a deci sion-support tool for identifying patients who require urgent intervention promptly. Me thod. A balanced Random Forest model was developed, which showed promising triage results. The approach created triage subcategories and assigned different priorities based on critical status. Results. The results were encouraging, with an accuracy of 80.14% for high-priority patients, 79.45% for referred patients, and 81.29% for patients who ul timately died. Conclusion. The findings support the model’s effectiveness in improving decision-making in emergency departments. The research aims to enhance patient classifi cation efficiency, optimize resource allocation, and ensure timely care. It provides new in sights and can benefit healthcare professionals by improving the quality of emergency care","Machine Learning, Classification Algorithms, Data Analysis, Operations Research, Emergencies, Triage Received: 18/07/2025 Accepted: 18/09/2025 NOVA. 2025; 24 (46) 118",marcadores,google com citation user rr9a1ygaaaaj hl es,introduction study present innovative research classify emergency depart ment patient using advanc machine-learn techniqu objective provide deci sion-support tool identify patient who require urgent intervention promptly me thod balanc random forest model develop which show promis triage result approach creat triage subcategori assign different prioriti based critical statu result result encourag accuracy 80 14 high-priority patient 79 45 referr patient 81 29 patient who ul timately died conclusion finding support model effectivenes improv decision-mak emergency department research aims enhance patient classifi cation efficiency optimize resource allocation ensure timely care provid new sight can benefit healthcare professional improv quality emergency care,machine learn classification algorithm data analysi oper research emergenci triage receiv 18 07 2025 accept 18 09 2025 nova 2025 24 46 118,google com citation user rr9a1ygaaaaj hl es introduction study present innovative research classify emergency depart ment patient using advanc machine-learn techniqu objective provide deci sion-support tool identify patient who require urgent intervention promptly me thod balanc random forest model develop which show promis triage result approach creat triage subcategori assign different prioriti based critical statu result result encourag accuracy 80 14 high-priority patient 79 45 referr patient 81 29 patient who ul timately died conclusion finding support model effectivenes improv decision-mak emergency department research aims enhance patient classifi cation efficiency optimize resource allocation ensure timely care provid new sight can benefit healthcare professional improv quality emergency care machine learn classification algorithm data analysi oper research emergenci triage receiv 18 07 2025 accept 18 09 2025 nova 2025 24 46 118,1.0.0,336b40b11bcfed86
2462-9448,06+emergency+triage.pdf,06+emergency+triage_0,es,"thod. A balanced Random Forest model was developed, which showed promising triage","Introducción. Este estudio presenta una investigación innovadora sobre la clasificación de pacientes en servicios de urgencias mediante técnicas avanzadas de aprendizaje auto mático. Objetivo. Proporcionar una herramienta de apoyo a la toma de decisiones para identificar rápidamente a los pacientes que requieren una intervención urgente. Método. Se desarrolló un modelo equilibrado de Random Forest, que mostró resultados promete dores en la clasificación. El enfoque creó subcategorías de clasificación y asignó diferentes prioridades en función del estado crítico. Resultados. Los resultados fueron alentadores, con una precisión del 80,14 % para los pacientes de alta prioridad, del 79,45 % para los pacientes derivados y del 81,29 % para los pacientes que finalmente fallecieron. Los resul tados respaldan la eficacia del modelo para mejorar la toma de decisiones en los servicios de urgencias. Conclusiones. La investigación tiene como objetivo mejorar la eficiencia de la clasificación de pacientes, optimizar la asignación de recursos y garantizar una atención oportuna. Aporta nuevos conocimientos y puede beneficiar a los profesionales sanitarios al mejorar la calidad de la atención de urgencias","Aprendizaje automático, Algoritmos de clasificación, Análisis de datos, Investigación operativa, Emergencias, Triaje",marcadores,thod balanced random forest model was developed which showed promising triage,introduccion este estudio presenta investigacion innovadora sobre clasificacion pacient servici urgenci mediante tecnic avanzad aprendizaje auto matico objetivo proporcionar herramienta apoyo toma decision identificar rapida pacient requieren intervencion urgente metodo desarrollo modelo equilibrado random forest mostro resultad promete dores clasificacion enfoque creo subcategori clasificacion asigno diferent prioridad funcion estado 