02 previou protocol 10 645 new protocol obtain 66 68 ssi rate respectively 461 discussion organ space ssis 56 76 most common type ssis most them occurr general surgery service 58 78 when compar prior protocol new protocol prior protocol show greater adherence antibiotic prophylaxi administration 89 vs 88 881 within adequate time prior incision 16 vs 05 rapid surgical procedure initiation stand out 50 among caus non-adherence conclusion finding highlight importance ensur monitor adherence antibiotic prophylaxi surgical unit while strengthen healthcare personnel knowledge feedback antibiotic prophylaxi surgical site infection therapeutic adherence compliance antibiotic surgical wound treatment protocol surgery 2026 universidad fucs open acces article under cc by-nc-nd license http creativecommon org licens by-nc-nd,1.0.0,444dde19648d5727
2462-991X,2.+Art.+Influencia+del+nivel+educativo+materno+en+los+resultados+perinatales+del+embarazo+adolescente+una+revisión+sistemática.pdf,2.+Art.+Influencia+del+nivel+educativo+materno+en+los+resultados+perinatales+del+embarazo+adolescente+una+revisión+sistemática_0,en,s perinatales del,"Introduction: to synthesize scientific evidence on the association between maternal education level and perinatal results (prematurity, low birth weight and mortality) in teenagers, by analyzing biological, nutritional and social mediating mechanisms. Methodology: a systematic review of 122 studies (2010-2025) identified in PubMed, Scopus, Web of Science, ScienceDirect and Google Scholar. Studies on adolescent mothers (aged 10-17 years) with data stratified by educational level (low vs. high), were included. The Newcastle-Ottawa Scale was used to assess methodological quality. Results: lower maternal education in teenage girls is strongly associated with preterm births, low birth weight, and perinatal mortality rates comparable to those of high-risk pregnancies. This vulnerability operates through multiple mediators: delayed first prenatal check-up (at more than 12 weeks), limited health literacy, higher anemia prevalence and increased exposure to intimate partner violence and psychosocial stress. Education is a protective factor enhancing psychological resilience and agency capacity to navigate healthcare systems. Conclusions: educational level is a central and modifiable determinant of perinatal disparities. Findings suggest the need to move beyond the biomedical model toward intersectoral strategies prioritizing educational continuity and adapting clinical care to low health literacy levels to improve mother-child outcomes","maternal education, teenage pregnancy, perinatal results, prenatal care, social determinants. © 2026 Universidad FUCS. This is an open access article under the CC BY-NC-ND license (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/)",marcadores,perinatal del,introduction synthesize scientific evidence association between maternal education level perinatal result prematurity low birth weight mortality teenager analyz biological nutritional social mediat mechanism methodology systematic review 122 studi 2010-2025 identifi pubm scopu web science sciencedirect google scholar studi adolescent mother aged 10-17 year data stratifi educational level low vs high includ newcastle-ottawa scale used asses methodological quality result lower maternal education teenage girl strongly associat preterm birth low birth weight perinatal mortality rate comparable those high-risk pregnanci vulnerability operat through multiple mediator delay first prenatal check-up more than 12 week limit health literacy higher anemia prevalence increas exposure intimate partner violence psychosocial stres education protective factor enhanc psychological resilience agency capacity navigate healthcare system conclusion educational level central modifiable determinant perinatal dispariti finding suggest need move beyond biomedical model toward intersectoral strategi prioritiz educational continuity adapt clinical care low health literacy level improve mother-child outcom,maternal education teenage pregnancy perinatal result prenatal care social determinant 2026 universidad fucs open acces article under cc by-nc-nd license http creativecommon org licens by-nc-nd,perinatal del introduction synthesize scientific evidence association between maternal education level perinatal result prematurity low birth weight mortality teenager analyz biological nutritional social mediat mechanism methodology systematic review 122 studi 2010-2025 identifi pubm scopu web science sciencedirect google scholar studi adolescent mother aged 10-17 year data stratifi educational level low vs high includ newcastle-ottawa scale used asses methodological quality result lower maternal education teenage girl strongly associat preterm birth low birth weight perinatal mortality rate comparable those high-risk pregnanci vulnerability operat through multiple mediator delay first prenatal check-up more than 12 week limit health literacy higher anemia prevalence increas exposure intimate partner violence psychosocial stres education protective factor enhanc psychological resilience agency capacity navigate healthcare system conclusion educational level central modifiable determinant perinatal dispariti finding suggest need move beyond biomedical model toward intersectoral strategi prioritiz educational continuity adapt clinical care low health literacy level improve mother-child outcom maternal education teenage pregnancy perinatal result prenatal care social determinant 2026 universidad fucs open acces article under cc by-nc-nd license http creativecommon org licens by-nc-nd,1.0.0,9f005d93a9c70a82
2462-991X,3.+Art.+Impacto+de+la+monitoría+intracerebral+por+espectrofotometría+en+pacientes+sometidos+a+cirugía+cardíaca.pdf,3.+Art.+Impacto+de+la+monitoría+intracerebral+por+espectrofotometría+en+pacientes+sometidos+a+cirugía+cardíaca_0,en,dos a cirugía cardíaca y,"Introduction: Cardiac surgery has required intraoperative hemodynamic monitoring with emphasis on cerebral perfusion due to the risk of complications, with ischemic cerebrovascular events being the most prevalent. NIRS (Near-Infrared Spectroscopy) has been proposed for non-invasive monitoring of cerebral oxygenation and as an early marker of hypoxia to reduce adverse events in the postoperative period of cardiac surgery. Objective: to conduct a non-systematic review of available information on the usefulness of NIRS during cardiac surgery. Materials and methods: a review of publications between January 2011 and February 2024 including literature and systematic reviews, meta-analyses and clinical trials in patients over 18 years of age undergoing cardiac surgery monitored with NIRS. Results: currently, there is no standard for monitoring cardiac surgery patients, however NIRS can detect cerebral oxygen supply and demand factors, reducing intra and postoperative complications. Conclusion: the use of NIRS for cerebral monitoring during cardiac surgery is suggested as a quantitative measure of perfusion, cerebral saturation and diagnosing reversible alterations such as hypovolemia, anemia and hypotension, to manage them during surgery","intracerebral monitoring, spectrophotometry, cerebral oxygenation, cardiovascular surgery, extracorporeal circulation, NIRS. © 2026 Universidad FUCS. This is an open access article under the CC BY-NC-ND license (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/)",marcadores,dos cirugia cardiaca,introduction cardiac surgery has requir intraoperative hemodynamic monitor emphasi cerebral perfusion due risk complic ischemic cerebrovascular event being most prevalent nirs near-infrar spectroscopy has been propos non-invasive monitor cerebral oxygenation early marker hypoxia reduce adverse event postoperative period cardiac surgery objective conduct non-systematic review available information usefulnes nirs during cardiac surgery material method review public between january 2011 february 2024 includ literature systematic review meta-analys clinical trial patient over 18 year age undergo cardiac surgery monitor nirs result currently there no standard monitor cardiac surgery patient however nirs can detect cerebral oxygen supply demand factor reduc intra postoperative complic conclusion use nirs cerebral monitor during cardiac surgery suggest quantitative measure perfusion cerebral saturation diagnos reversible alter such hypovolemia anemia hypotension manage them during surgery,intracerebral monitor spectrophotometry cerebral oxygenation cardiovascular surgery extracorporeal circulation nirs 2026 universidad fucs open acces article under cc by-nc-nd license http creativecommon org licens by-nc-nd,dos cirugia cardiaca introduction cardiac surgery has requir intraoperative hemodynamic monitor emphasi cerebral perfusion due risk complic ischemic cerebrovascular event being most prevalent nirs near-infrar spectroscopy has been propos non-invasive monitor cerebral oxygenation early marker hypoxia reduce adverse event postoperative period cardiac surgery objective conduct non-systematic review available information usefulnes nirs during cardiac surgery material method review public between january 2011 february 2024 includ literature systematic review meta-analys clinical trial patient over 18 year age undergo cardiac surgery monitor nirs result currently there no standard monitor cardiac surgery patient however nirs can detect cerebral oxygen supply demand factor reduc intra postoperative complic conclusion use nirs cerebral monitor during cardiac surgery suggest quantitative measure perfusion cerebral saturation diagnos reversible alter such hypovolemia anemia hypotension manage them during surgery intracerebral monitor spectrophotometry cerebral oxygenation cardiovascular surgery extracorporeal circulation nirs 2026 universidad fucs open acces article under cc by-nc-nd license http creativecommon org licens by-nc-nd,1.0.0,d64889d094dffe6e
2462-991X,4.+Art.+Incidencia+de+un+primer+infarto+de+miocardio+o+accidente+cerebrovascular+en+pacientes+de+un+programa+de+control+del+riesgo.pdf,4.+Art.+Incidencia+de+un+primer+infarto+de+miocardio+o+accidente+cerebrovascular+en+pacientes+de+un+programa+de+control+del+riesgo_0,en,primer infarto de,"MÉTODOS Introduction: cardiovascular risk (CVR) prevention programs seek reducing morbidity and mortality associated with cardiovascular events (CVEs) in at-risk populations. The chronic disease comprehensive care and management plan (PAICEC) in public hospitals in Boyacá, Colombia, allowed comparing the incidence of first-time cardiovascular events (CVEs), including non-fatal acute myocardial infarction (AMI), cerebrovascular accident (CVA), or cardiovascular death, in adherent and non-adherent patients. Methodology: a historical cohort study conducted between January 2015 and June 2022, including patients older than 18 years with high or very high CVR (hypertension, type 2 diabetes mellitus or dyslipidemia) who had been followed for at least 2 years. Those with previous CV disease or illnesses not associated with CVR were excluded. The cohort was considered adherent if patients had attended at least 80% of the program´s visits. Primary outcome: first time AMI, CVA or cardiovascular death. Fisher exact test and x2 test, were used for comparing qualitative variables, and the Mann-Whitney and Wilcoxon tests for comparing quantitative variables. CV event-free-survival was estimated by the Kaplan-Meier method. Results: of the 2.833 clinical records reviewed, 832 corresponded to patients with high and very high CVR, 46 corresponded to adherent patients and 187 to non-adherent patients, who served as the control group. Adherence was found to have a protective trend, RR 0.58 (95%:CI 0.073 - 4.6), and a higher proportion of improved CVR factors control. Conclusions: adherence to the PAICEC program may reduce CVEs incidence and improve CV risk factors control. Although no statistically significant associations were found, the results are clinically relevant and potentially applicable","cardiovascular risk factors, primary prevention, myocardial infarction, cerebrovascular accident. © 2026 Universidad FUCS. This is an open access article under the CC BY-NC-ND license (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/)",marcadores,primer infarto de,metodo introduction cardiovascular risk cvr prevention program seek reduc morbidity mortality associat cardiovascular event cves at-risk popul chronic disease comprehensive care management plan paicec public hospital boyaca colombia allow compar incidence first-time cardiovascular event cves includ non-fatal acute myocardial infarction ami cerebrovascular accident cva cardiovascular death adherent non-adherent patient methodology historical cohort study conduct between january 2015 june 2022 includ patient older than 18 year high very high cvr hypertension type diabet mellitu dyslipidemia who had been follow least year those previou cv disease illness not associat cvr exclud cohort consider adherent if patient had attend least 80 program visit primary outcome first time ami cva cardiovascular death fisher exact test x2 test used compar qualitative variabl mann-whitney wilcoxon test compar quantitative variabl cv event-free-survival estimat kaplan-meier method result 833 clinical record review 832 correspond patient high very high cvr 46 correspond adherent patient 187 non-adherent patient who serv control group adherence found have protective trend rr 58 95 ci 073 higher proportion improv cvr factor control conclusion adherence paicec program may reduce cves incidence improve cv risk factor control although no statistically significant associ found result clinically relevant potentially applicable,cardiovascular risk factor primary prevention myocardial infarction cerebrovascular accident 2026 universidad fucs open acces article under cc by-nc-nd license http creativecommon org licens by-nc-nd,primer infarto de metodo introduction cardiovascular risk cvr prevention program seek reduc morbidity mortality associat cardiovascular event cves at-risk popul chronic disease comprehensive care management plan paicec public hospital boyaca colombia allow compar incidence first-time cardiovascular event cves includ non-fatal acute myocardial infarction ami cerebrovascular accident cva cardiovascular death adherent non-adherent patient methodology historical cohort study conduct between january 2015 june 2022 includ patient older than 18 year high very high cvr hypertension type diabet mellitu dyslipidemia who had been follow least year those previou cv disease illness not associat cvr exclud cohort consider adherent if patient had attend least 80 program visit primary outcome first time ami cva cardiovascular death fisher exact test x2 test used compar qualitative variabl mann-whitney wilcoxon test compar quantitative variabl cv event-free-survival estimat kaplan-meier method result 833 clinical record review 832 correspond patient high very high cvr 46 correspond adherent patient 187 non-adherent patient who serv control group adherence found have protective trend rr 58 95 ci 073 higher proportion improv cvr factor control conclusion adherence paicec program may reduce cves incidence improve cv risk factor control although no statistically significant associ found result clinically relevant potentially applicable cardiovascular risk factor primary prevention myocardial infarction cerebrovascular accident 2026 universidad fucs open acces article under cc by-nc-nd license http creativecommon org licens by-nc-nd,1.0.0,ceb618ca4b7b0a2c
2462-991X,5.+Art.+Percepción+de+los+métodos+de+estudio+en+el+aprendizaje+de+farmacología+en+estudiantes+de+enfermería.pdf,5.+Art.+Percepción+de+los+métodos+de+estudio+en+el+aprendizaje+de+farmacología+en+estudiantes+de+enfermería_0,en,s debilidades fueron la comprensión profunda y la seguridad,"Introduction: a solid foundation in basic sciences is essential for nursing students to effectively understand pharmacology, impacting safe patient care. Medication errors are common in Colombia, underscoring the need to analyze nursing students learning strategies. Objective: to describe nursing students´ perceptions of their pharmacology learning methods and strategies, at a university in Bogotá in 2023. Methodology: a purposive sampling qualitative study with a descriptive phenomenological approach exploring learning methods perceptions among nursing students in advanced semesters who have already taken the course. Data analysis was conducted through triangulation of student and teacher observations and syllabus content, and Atlas ti was used for coding and categorization. Results: student perceptions analysis revealed strengths such as autonomy and the use of technology; weaknesses were a lack of in-depth understanding and practical confidence. A main theme supported by two categories: 21 subcategoríes and 67 codes, was identified. Simulation-based clinical practice, audiovisual aids and interactive strategies were rated as effective methods. Discussion: active learning strategies and practical experience are fundamental in pharmacology. Combining clinical case-studies, simulation-based practice, and game-based learning enhances understanding and skill development. Active information seeking and critical reading act as complementary learning strategies. Conclusions: this research describes students´ perceptions of pharmacology learning strategies, highlighting the effectiveness of interactive teaching methods and the importance of clinical experience. Insufficient class time was identified as a limitation. Findings indicate that adjusting curricula and pedagogy approaches are critical for optimizing pharmacology learning and preparing future nursing professionals","perception, pharmacology, study",marcadores,debilidad fueron la comprension profunda la seguridad,introduction solid foundation basic scienc essential nurs student effectively understand pharmacology impact safe patient care medication error common colombia underscor need analyze nurs student learn strategi objective describe nurs student perception their pharmacology learn method strategi university bogota 2023 methodology purposive sampl qualitative study descriptive phenomenological approach explor learn method perception among nurs student advanc semester who have already taken course data analysi conduct through triangulation student teacher observ syllabu content atla ti used coding categor result student perception analysi reveal strength such autonomy use technology weakness lack in-depth understand practical confidence main theme support two categori 21 subcategori 67 code identifi simulation-bas clinical practice audiovisual aids interactive strategi rated effective method discussion active learn strategi practical experience fundamental pharmacology combin clinical case-studi simulation-bas practice game-bas learn enhanc understand skill development active information seek critical read act complementary learn strategi conclusion research describ student perception pharmacology learn strategi highlight effectivenes interactive teach method importance clinical experience insufficient clas time identifi limitation finding indicate adjust curricula pedagogy approach critical optimiz pharmacology learn prepar future nurs professional,perception pharmacology study,debilidad fueron la comprension profunda la seguridad introduction solid foundation basic scienc essential nurs student effectively understand pharmacology impact safe patient care medication error common colombia underscor need analyze nurs student learn strategi objective describe nurs student perception their pharmacology learn method strategi university bogota 2023 methodology purposive sampl qualitative study descriptive phenomenological approach explor learn method perception among nurs student advanc semester who have already taken course data analysi conduct through triangulation student teacher observ syllabu content atla ti used coding categor result student perception analysi reveal strength such autonomy use technology weakness lack in-depth understand practical confidence main theme support two categori 21 subcategori 67 code identifi simulation-bas clinical practice audiovisual aids interactive strategi rated effective method discussion active learn strategi practical experience fundamental pharmacology combin clinical case-studi simulation-bas practice game-bas learn enhanc understand skill development active information seek critical read act complementary learn strategi conclusion research describ student perception pharmacology learn strategi highlight effectivenes interactive teach method importance clinical experience insufficient clas time identifi limitation finding indicate adjust curricula pedagogy approach critical optimiz pharmacology learn prepar future nurs professional perception pharmacology study,1.0.0,dca2231a166c892f
2462-991X,6.+Art.+Diagnostic+accuracy+of+E-FAST+ultrasound+performed+by+general+surgery+residents.pdf,6.+Art.+Diagnostic+accuracy+of+E-FAST+ultrasound+performed+by+general+surgery+residents_0,en,determine the diagnostic accuracy of E-FAST,"Diagnostic accuracy of E-FAST Diagnostic accuracy of E-FAST ultrasound performed by general ultrasound performed by general surgery residents surgery residents Precisión del ultrasonido E-FAST realizado Precisión del ultrasonido E-FAST realizado por residentes de cirugía general por residentes de cirugía general Artículo de investigación INFORMACIÓN DEL ARTÍCULO Historia del artículo: Date received: August 4, 2025 Date accepted: February 18, 2026 Autor para correspondencia. Dra. Angela María Merchán G. angelamerchan@unicauca.edu.co DOI 10.31260/RepertMedCir.01217372.1718 de Medicina y Cirugía Vol. 35 N°3 . 2026 de Medicina y Cirugía REPERT MED CIR. 2026;35(3):263-268 264 ABSTRACT Introducción: el politraumatismo severo es un problema de salud pública y una causa frecuente de atención urgente. En Colombia, el homicidio y los accidentes automovilísticos son las principales causas. El estudio FAST/E-FAST optimiza la atención identificando lesiones potencialmente mortales. Objetivo: determinar la precisión del E-FAST realizado por residentes de cirugía general para identificar lesiones en pacientes con traumatismo toracoabdominal. Métodos: estudio tipo prueba diagnóstica en un hospital de tercer nivel de Colombia durante los años 2021 y 2022 en pacientes con traumatismo toracoabdominal. El FAST/E-FAST fue realizado por residentes de cirugía general de segundo a cuarto año. Los hallazgos se compararon con ecografías o tomografías computarizadas realizadas y leídas por radiólogos, o con hallazgos intraoperatorios (toracotomía y laparotomía) para calcular la precisión de la prueba. Resultados: se incluyeron 123 pacientes, 91,1% varones con una mediana de edad de 31 años. Los residentes de segundo año realizaron 55,9% de los estudios FAST. La tomografía fue la prueba más solicitada (77,9%); la sensibilidad de la prueba FAST/E-FAST respecto a la tomografía fue de 48% (IC 95%: 30,0-66,5) y la especificidad fue de 94,2% (IC 95%: 86,0-97,7). Al comparar la ecografía FAST con la cirugía, la sensibilidad fue de 70,8% (IC 95%: 50,8-85,1) y la especificidad fue de 100% (IC 95%: 56,6-100), el valor predictivo positivo fue de 100% (IC 95%: 81,6-100). Conclusión: la prueba FAST/E-FAST realizada por residentes mostró mejor especificidad que sensibilidad en el diagnóstico de alteraciones de la cavidad torácica y abdominal de pacientes politraumatizados, con valores similares a los descritos en la literatura","educación, E-FAST, FAST, formación quirúrgica, residente de cirugía, trauma. © 2026 Universidad FUCS. This is an open access article under the CC BY-NC-ND license (http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/)",marcadores,determine diagnostic accuracy e-fast,diagnostic accuracy e-fast diagnostic accuracy e-fast ultrasound perform general ultrasound perform general surgery resident surgery resident precision del ultrasonido e-fast realizado precision del ultrasonido e-fast realizado por resident de cirugia general por resident de cirugia general articulo de investigacion informacion del articulo historia del articulo date receiv august 2025 date accept february 18 2026 autor para correspondencia dra angela maria merchan angelamerchan unicauca edu co doi 10 31260 repertmedcir 01217372 1718 de medicina cirugia vol 35 ndeg3 2026 de medicina cirugia repert med cir 2026 35 263-268 264 abstract introduccion el politraumatismo severo es un problema de salud publica una causa frecuente de atencion urgente en colombia el homicidio los accident automovilistico son las principal causa el estudio fast e-fast optimiza la atencion identificando lesion potencialmente mortal objetivo determinar la precision del e-fast realizado por resident de cirugia general para identificar lesion en pacient con traumatismo toracoabdominal metodo estudio tipo prueba diagnostica en un hospital de tercer nivel de colombia durante los anos 2021 2022 en pacient con traumatismo toracoabdominal el fast e-fast fue realizado por resident de cirugia general de segundo cuarto ano los hallazgo se compararon con ecografia tomografia computarizada realizada leida por radiologo con hallazgo intraoperatorio toracotomia laparotomia para calcular la precision de la prueba resultado se incluyeron 123 pacient 91 varon con una mediana de edad de 31 anos los resident de segundo ano realizaron 55 de los estudio fast la tomografia fue la prueba mas solicitada 77 la sensibilidad de la prueba fast e-fast respecto la tomografia fue de 48 ic 95 30 0-66 la especificidad fue de 94 ic 95 86 0-97 al comparar la ecografia fast con la cirugia la sensibilidad fue de 70 ic 95 50 8-85 la especificidad fue de 100 ic 95 56 6-100 el valor predictivo positivo fue de 100 ic 95 81 6-100 conclusion la prueba fast e-fast realizada por resident mostro mejor especificidad que sensibilidad en el diagnostico de alteracion de la cavidad toracica abdominal de pacient politraumatizado con valor similar los descrito en la literatura,educacion e-fast fast formacion quirurgica residente de cirugia trauma 2026 universidad fucs open acces article under cc by-nc-nd license http creativecommon org licens by-nc-nd,determine diagnostic accuracy e-fast diagnostic accuracy e-fast diagnostic accuracy e-fast ultrasound perform general ultrasound perform general surgery resident surgery resident precision del ultrasonido e-fast realizado precision del ultrasonido e-fast realizado por resident de cirugia general por resident de cirugia general articulo de investigacion informacion del articulo historia del articulo date receiv august 2025 date accept february 18 2026 autor para correspondencia dra angela maria merchan angelamerchan unicauca edu co doi 10 31260 repertmedcir 01217372 1718 de medicina cirugia vol 35 ndeg3 2026 de medicina cirugia repert med cir 2026 35 263-268 264 abstract introduccion el politraumatismo severo es un problema de salud publica una causa frecuente de atencion urgente en colombia el homicidio los accident automovilistico son las principal causa el estudio fast e-fast optimiza la atencion identificando lesion potencialmente mortal objetivo determinar la precision del e-fast realizado por resident de cirugia general para identificar lesion en pacient con traumatismo toracoabdominal metodo estudio tipo prueba diagnostica en un hospital de tercer nivel de colombia durante los anos 2021 2022 en pacient con traumatismo toracoabdominal el fast e-fast fue realizado por resident de cirugia general de segundo cuarto ano los hallazgo se compararon con ecografia tomografia computarizada realizada leida por radiologo con hallazgo intraoperatorio toracotomia laparotomia para calcular la precision de la prueba resultado se incluyeron 123 pacient 91 varon con una mediana de edad de 31 anos los resident de segundo ano realizaron 55 de los estudio fast la tomografia fue la prueba mas solicitada 77 la sensibilidad de la prueba fast e-fast respecto la tomografia fue de 48 ic 95 30 0-66 la especificidad fue de 94 ic 95 86 0-97 al comparar la ecografia fast con la cirugia la sensibilidad fue de 70 ic 95 50 8-85 la especificidad fue de 100 ic 95 56 6-100 el valor predictivo positivo fue de 100 ic 95 81 6-100 conclusion la prueba fast e-fast realizada por resident mostro mejor especificidad que sensibilidad en el diagnostico de alteracion de la cavidad toracica abdominal de pacient politraumatizado con valor similar los descrito en la literatura educacion e-fast fast formacion quirurgica residente de cirugia trauma 2026 universidad fucs open acces article under cc by-nc-nd license http creativecommon org licens by-nc-nd,1.0.0,b4f7f721c0b18a1d
2462-991X,7.+Art.+Desenlaces+clínicos+en+pacientes+hemofílicos+operados+en+un+centro+de+referencia.pdf,7.+Art.+Desenlaces+clínicos+en+pacientes+hemofílicos+operados+en+un+centro+de+referencia_0,en,"los menores de 3,5 días. La mediana de dosis de factores en procedimientos","Introduction: Hemophilia A and B are rare disorders characterized by factor VIII (A) or factor IX (B) deficiencies. Patients with hemophilia often require surgical interventions. An understanding of surgical procedures outcomes is essential to provide proper management. Objective: describing demographic and clinical characteristics and outcomes in hemophilia patients undergoing surgeries between 2021 and 2022 at Hospital de San José in Bogotá, Colombia. Materials and methods: a descriptive retrospective cohort study in patients over 18 years old with hemophilia A and B, undergoing surgeries. Stata 17® software was used for descriptive analyses. Results: 28 procedures were performed on 21 male patients, median age 41.5 years. 60.7% of procedures were performed on hemophilia A patients, and an equal proportion were orthopedic interventions. Median hospital stay in major surgeries was 11 days and 3.5 days in minor interventions. The median factor replacement dose for major surgeries was 424 UI/k and 149 UI/k for minor procedures. Hemostatic response in major interventions was rated as excellent or good in 92.8% of cases. A 14% rate of surgical site infection leading to rehospitalization was reported. Distal deep vein thrombosis incidence was 3.5%, with 0% mortality. Conclusion: this study reports achieving favorable surgical outcomes with low complication rate and no mortality. To address surgical patient-specific needs is critical for mitigating risks and complications","hemophilia A, hemophilia B, surgical procedures, postoperative complications. © 2026 Universidad - FUCS. This is an open access article under the CC BY-NC-ND license (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/)",marcadores,