dur perform hemophilia patient equal proportion orthopedic intervention median hospital stay major surgeri 11 days days minor intervention median factor replacement dose major surgeri 424 ui 149 ui minor procedur hemostatic response major intervention rated excellent good 92 case 14 rate surgical site infection lead rehospital report distal deep vein thrombosi incidence mortality conclusion study report achiev favorable surgical outcom low complication rate no mortality addres surgical patient-specific need critical mitigat risk complic hemophilia hemophilia surgical procedur postoperative complic 2026 universidad fucs open acces article under cc by-nc-nd license http creativecommon org licens by-nc-nd,1.0.0,ceb342c758f80b2a
2462-991X,"8.+Art.+Conocimientos,+actitudes+y+experiencias+de+estudiantes,+padres+y+docentes+sobre+métodos+anticonceptivos+y+educación.pdf","8.+Art.+Conocimientos,+actitudes+y+experiencias+de+estudiantes,+padres+y+docentes+sobre+métodos+anticonceptivos+y+educación_0",es,"d de Enfermería, Universidad FUCS, Bogotá DC, Colombia.","Conocimientos, actitudes y experiencias Conocimientos, actitudes y experiencias de estudiantes, padres y docentes sobre de estudiantes, padres y docentes sobre métodos anticonceptivos y educación métodos anticonceptivos y educación sexual en un colegio femenino sexual en un colegio femenino Students, parents and teachers´ knowledge, Students, parents and teachers´ knowledge, attitudes and experiences regarding contraceptive attitudes and experiences regarding contraceptive methods and sex education in an all-girls school methods and sex education in an all-girls school Artículo de investigación INFORMACIÓN DEL ARTÍCULO Historia del artículo: Fecha recibido: abril 7 de 2026 Fecha aceptado: junio 2 de 2026 Autor para correspondencia. Dr. Carlos Alberto Castro cacastro@fucsalud.edu.co DOI 10.31260/RepertMedCir.01217372.1709 de Medicina y Cirugía Vol. 35 N°3 . 2026 de Medicina y Cirugía 277 REPERT MED CIR. 2026;35(3):276-283 ABSTRACT Introduction: sex education poses a challenge to parents, teachers and adolescents, who need a comprehensive development of sexuality to empower them to realize their health and well-being. However, barriers to access health services and lack of knowledge about contraception persist in Colombia. Objective: to determine adequate contraception knowledge, and understand students, parents and teachers´ sex education experiences at a public girl´s school in Bogotá, Colombia, in 2020 and 2021. Material and Methods: a mixed-methods study combining descriptive cross-sectional and phenomenological and hermeneutic approaches. The study included ninth, tenth and eleventh grade students from a public school in Bogotá who completed a questionnaire on knowledge and attitudes toward contraception. Focus groups were used in the qualitative study to evaluate students, parents and teachers´ sex education experiences. Results: out of 127 students, 70% had adequate knowledge about contraceptive methods, 92.9% showed attitudes of acceptance and 70% of students talked with their parents about sex education. Focus groups included 15 students, 7 parents and 15 teachers, where: 1) perception of sexuality as a dimension of the human being; 2) perception of sex education; 3) role of the stakeholders; 4) contraceptive methods, and 5) sexual and reproductive rights, were the emerging five categories. Conclusions: as sex education is limited by multiple barriers, the need for engaging parents, school and students is emphasized to enhance family communication which strengthens the educational process. Key words: sex education, contraception, knowledge, attitude, sexual health, reproductive health. © 2026 Universidad FUCS. This is an open access article under the CC BY-NC-ND license (http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/). INTRODUCCIÓN oficial de Bogotá que diligenciaron un cuestionario sobre conocimientos y actitudes sobre anticoncepción. En el aspecto cualitativo, mediante grupos focales se indagaron las experiencias sobre educación sexual de estudiantes, padres y profesores. Resultados: de 127 estudiantes 70% tenían conocimientos adecuados sobre métodos anticonceptivos, 92,9% actitudes de aceptación y 70% comunicación con sus padres sobre educación sexual. En los grupos focales participaron 15 estudiantes, 7 padres y 15 docentes, y emergieron 5 categorías finales: 1) percepción sobre la sexualidad como una dimensión del ser humano; 2) percepción de la educación sexual; 3) rol de los actores involucrados; 4) métodos anticonceptivos; y 5) identificación de los derechos sexuales y reproductivos. Conclusiones: la educación sexual recibida está limitada por múltiples barreras, se enfatiza en la necesidad de la participación de padres, colegios y estudiantes, con el fin de mejorar la comunicación con las familias lo cual fortalece el proceso educativo","educación sexual, anticoncepción, conocimiento, actitud, salud sexual, salud reproductiva. © 2026 Universidad FUCS. Este es un artículo Open Access bajo la licencia CC BY-NC-ND (http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/). La adolescencia es una etapa del ciclo vital de transición entre la niñez y adultez que se caracteriza por ser un periodo de transformación que involucra cambios físi",marcadores,enfermeria universidad fucs bogota dc colombia,conoc actitud experienci conoc actitud experienci estudiant padr docent sobre estudiant padr docent sobre metod anticonceptiv educacion metod anticonceptiv educacion sexual colegio femenino sexual colegio femenino students parents and teachers knowledge students parents and teachers knowledge attitud and experienc regarding contraceptive attitud and experienc regarding contraceptive methods and sex education in an all-girls school methods and sex education in an all-girls school articulo investigacion informacion articulo historia articulo fecha recibido abril 2026 fecha aceptado junio 2026 autor correspondencia dr carl alberto castro cacastro fucsalud edu co doi 10 31260 repertmedcir 01217372 1709 medicina cirugia vol 35 ndeg3 2026 medicina cirugia 277 repert med cir 2026 35 276-283 abstract introduction sex education poses challenge to parents teachers and adolescents who need comprehensive development of sexuality to empower them to realize their health and well-being however barriers to access health servic and lack of knowledge about contraception persist in colombia objective to determine adequate contraception knowledge and understand students parents and teachers sex education experienc at public girl school in bogota colombia in 2020 and 2021 material and methods mixed-methods study combining descriptive cross-sectional and phenomenological and hermeneutic