2462-991X,9.+Art+Prevalencia+de+trastornos+músculo+esqueléticos+en+docentes+de+secundaria.pdf,9.+Art+Prevalencia+de+trastornos+músculo+esqueléticos+en+docentes+de+secundaria_0,en,realizó mediante el uso de la plataforma Ergoyes y el programa estadístico SPSSV25. Resultados: se,"Introduction: musculoskeletal disorders (MSDs) are conditions affecting the locomotor system caused by ordinary or work-related activities. For teachers, this constitutes a common health problem associated with exposure to ergonomic risk factors, such as posture, repetitive motions and load handling. Objective: to determine the prevalence of musculoskeletal disorders associated with educational practice among secondary school teachers at an institution in Barranquilla, Colombia. Methodology: a descriptive cross-sectional study in a population of teachers and staff in a secondary school applying body mapping and ERIN assessment tools. The Ergoyes Platform and SPSSV25 statistical software were used for data analysis. Results: upper back pain was identified as the most significant work-related disorder (0.95), representing a moderate risk factor (21.0) Conclusion: it is important to note that a moderate risk factor indicates that while tasks are not extremely harmful in the short-term, they require attention and corrective measures to prevent long-term health issues","prevalence, risks, musculoskeletal disorders, educational practice, teacher. © 2026 Universidad FUCS. This is an open access article under the CC BY-NC-ND license (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/)",marcadores,realizo mediante el uso de la plataforma ergoy el programa estadistico spssv25 resultado se,introduction musculoskeletal disorder msds condition affect locomotor system caus ordinary work-relat activiti teacher constitut common health problem associat exposure ergonomic risk factor such posture repetitive motion load handl objective determine prevalence musculoskeletal disorder associat educational practice 