2463-0225,4349_stamped.pdf,4349_stamped_0,en,Original research,"Objective: To describe the incidence, clinical characteristics, and complications of obstetric hysterectomy in a tertiary hospital in Chile from 2021 to 2023. Methods: Retrospective descriptive cohort study including all women with a gestational age ≥20 weeks or up to six weeks postpartum who underwent obstetric hysterectomy at Santiago Oriente Dr. Luis Tisné Brousse Hospital. Clinical and surgical data were collected from institutional records. Descriptive statistics were performed. Results: Twenty-five obstetric hysterectomies were performed during the study period. Incidence per 1,000 live births decreased from 3.22 in 2021 to 1.81 in 2023. Postpartum hemorrhage was the main indication (52%), followed by placenta accreta spectrum (32%), infection (12%), and uterine rupture (4%). Supracervical hysterectomy was performed in 52% of cases, and total hysterectomy Safety and clinical outcomes of obstetric hysterectomies in patients treated at a tertiary hospital in Chile Seguridad y desenlaces clínicos de las histerectomías obstétricas en pacientes atendidas en un hospital de atención terciaria en Chile Sebastián Lavanderos1,2 , Benjamín Moraga-Arias1 , Fernanda Muñoz-Baeza1 , Sebastián Cifuentes-Espinoza1 , Víctor Córdova-Padilla2 in 48%; 68% were emergencies. One intraoperative complication (bladder injury) was reported. Postoperative complications occurred in 84% of cases, the most frequent being anemia (84%) and hemorrhagic shock (36%). No significant associations were found between baseline characteristics and complications. Conclusion: Although its incidence is declining, obstetric hysterectomy remains associated with high morbidity. Strengthening prevention, early detection, and timely multidisciplinary care is essential. Further prospective, multicenter studies are needed to inform strategies to improve maternal outcomes",Hysterectomy; postpartum hemorrhage; cesarean section; placenta accreta; postoperative complications,marcadores,original research,objective describe incidence clinical characteristic complic obstetric hysterectomy tertiary hospital chile 2021 2023 method retrospective descriptive cohort study includ all women gestational age 20 week up six week postpartum who underwent obstetric hysterectomy santiago oriente dr luis tisne brousse hospital clinical surgical data collect institutional record descriptive statistic perform result twenty-five obstetric hysterectomi perform during study period incidence per 000 live birth decreas 22 2021 81 2023 postpartum hemorrhage main indication 52 follow placenta accreta spectrum 32 infection 12 uterine rupture supracervical hysterectomy perform 52 case total hysterectomy safety clinical outcom obstetric hysterectomi patient treat tertiary hospital chile seguridad desenlac clinico de las histerectomia obstetrica en pacient atendida en un hospital de atencion terciaria en chile sebastian lavanderos1 benjamin moraga-arias1 fernanda munoz-baeza1 sebastian cifuentes-espinoza1 victor cordova-padilla2 48 68 emergenci one intraoperative complication bladder injury report postoperative complic occurr 84 case most frequent being anemia 84 hemorrhagic shock 36 no significant associ found between baseline characteristic complic conclusion although its incidence declin obstetric hysterectomy remain associat high morbidity strengthen prevention early detection timely multidisciplinary care essential further prospective multicenter studi need inform strategi improve maternal outcom,hysterectomy postpartum hemorrhage cesarean section placenta accreta postoperative complic,original research objective describe incidence clinical characteristic complic obstetric hysterectomy tertiary hospital chile 2021 2023 method retrospective descriptive cohort study includ all women gestational age 20 week up six week postpartum who underwent obstetric hysterectomy santiago oriente dr luis tisne brousse hospital clinical surgical data collect institutional record descriptive statistic perform result twenty-five obstetric hysterectomi perform during study period incidence per 000 live birth decreas 22 2021 81 2023 postpartum hemorrhage main indication 52 follow placenta accreta spectrum 32 infection 12 uterine rupture supracervical hysterectomy perform 52 case total hysterectomy safety clinical outcom obstetric hysterectomi patient treat tertiary hospital chile seguridad desenlac clinico de las histerectomia obstetrica en pacient atendida en un hospital de atencion terciaria en chile sebastian lavanderos1 benjamin moraga-arias1 fernanda munoz-baeza1 sebastian cifuentes-espinoza1 victor cordova-padilla2 48 68 emergenci one intraoperative complication bladder injury report postoperative complic occurr 84 case most frequent being anemia 84 hemorrhagic shock 36 no significant associ found between baseline characteristic complic conclusion although its incidence declin obstetric hysterectomy remain associat high morbidity strengthen prevention early detection timely multidisciplinary care essential further prospective multicenter studi need inform strategi improve maternal outcom hysterectomy postpartum hemorrhage cesarean section placenta accreta postoperative complic,1.0.0,f9f975b0ba19bd21
2463-0225,4349_stamped.pdf,4349_stamped_0,es,atención terciaria en Chile,"Objetivos: describir la incidencia, características clínicas y complicaciones de la histerectomía obstétrica (HO) en un hospital terciario en Chile entre 2021 y 2023. Métodos: estudio descriptivo de cohorte retrospectivo que incluyó a todas las mujeres con una edad gestacional ≥20 semanas o hasta seis semanas posparto que se sometieron a HO en el Hospital Santiago Oriente, Dr. Luis Tisné Brousse. Se recolectaron datos clínicos y Received: 17 November 2024 Accepted: 18 June, 2025 * Correspondence: Ejército 141. Santiago, Chile. sebastian.lavanderos@mail. udp.cl 1. School of Medicine, Faculty of Medicine. Universidad Diego Portales, Ejército 141. Santiago (Chile). 2. OBGYN Department, Hospital Santiago Oriente, Dr. Luis Tisné Brousse. Santiago (Chile). https://doi.org/10.18597/rcog.4349 Revista Colombiana de Obstetricia y Ginecología Vol. 76 No.2 • April-June 2025 • 4349 How to cite this article: Lavanderos S, Moraga-Arias B, Muñoz-Baeza F, Cifuentes-Espinoza S, Córdova-Padilla V. Safety and clinical outcomes of obstetric hysterectomies in patients treated at a tertiary hospital in Chile. Rev Colomb Obstet Ginecol. 2025;76:4349. https://doi.org/10.18597/rcog.4349 Lea la versión en español de este artículo en https://revista.fecolsog.org Copyright © 2025 Federación Colombiana de Obstetricia y Ginecología (FECOLSOG). This is an open access article under the CC BY-NC-ND licen (http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/) Revista Colombiana de Obstetricia y Ginecología Vol. 76 No.2 • 2025 quirúrgicos a partir los registros institucionales. Se realizó un análisis estadístico descriptivo. Resultados: se realizaron 25 HO durante el período de estudio. La incidencia disminuyó de 3,22 en 2021 a 1,81 en 2023 por cada 1.000 nacidos vivos. La indicación principal fue hemorragia posparto (52%), seguida de espectro de acretismo placentario (32%), infección (12%) y ruptura uterina (4%). Se realizó histerectomía supracervical en el 52% y total en el 48%; el 68% fueron de urgencia. Se registró una complicación intraoperatoria (lesión vesical). Las complicaciones posoperatorias ocurrieron en el 84% de los casos, siendo las más frecuentes la anemia (84%) y el shock hipovolémico (36%). No se encontraron asociaciones significativas entre las características basales y las complicaciones. Conclusión: aunque su incidencia ha disminuido, la HO sigue asociada a una alta morbilidad. Es fundamental fortalecer la prevención, detección precoz y atención multidisciplinaria oportuna. Se requieren estudios prospectivos y multicéntricos para mejorar los resultados maternos",histerectomía; hemorragia posparto; cesárea; placenta accreta; complicaciones posoperatorias,marcadores,atencion terciaria chile,objetiv describir incidencia caracteristic clinic complic histerectomia obstetrica ho hospital terciario chile entre 2021 2023 metod estudio descriptivo cohorte retrospectivo incluyo todas mujer edad gestacional 20 seman hasta seis seman posparto sometieron ho hospital santiago oriente dr luis tisne brousse recolectaron datos clinic received 17 november 2024 accepted 18 june 2025 correspondence ejercito 141 santiago chile sebastian lavander mail udp cl school of medicine faculty of medicine universidad diego portal ejercito 141 santiago chile obgyn department hospital santiago oriente dr luis tisne brousse santiago chile https doi org 10 18597 rcog 4349 revista colombiana obstetricia ginecologia vol 76 no april-june 2025 4349 how to cite this article lavander moraga-ari munoz-baeza cifuentes-espinoza cordova-padilla safety and clinical outcom of obstetric hysterectomi in patients treated at tertiary hospital in chile rev colomb obstet ginecol 2025 76 4349 https doi org 10 18597 rcog 4349 lea version espanol este articulo https revista fecolsog org copyright 2025 federacion colombiana obstetricia ginecologia fecolsog this is an open access article under the cc by-nc-nd licen http creative