2463-0225,4510_stamped.pdf,4510_stamped_0,en,ctividad de la inclusión de la doble tinción p16/,"Objectives: To assess the cost-effectiveness of incorporating p16/Ki-67 dual-stain cytology into cervical cancer screening protocols compared to the standard diagnostic pathway in Colombia. Material and methods: A decision-tree model was developed from the healthcare provider perspective, using real-world data and scientific evidence. The primary outcome was the number of invasive procedures avoided. Deterministic and probabilistic sensitivity analyses were performed to address uncertainty. Results: Incorporating p16/Ki-67 dual-stain cytology proved to be a dominant strategy, significantly reducing unnecessary colposcopies and biopsies and Recibido: 7 julio 2025 Aceptado: 27 marzo 2026 * Correspondencia: Invalue Health Solutions S.A.S., Calle 23 # 68-50, 8-604. Bogotá, Colombia. yudely.medina@invaluehs.com 1. Viva 1A. Medellín, Colombia. 2. Invalue Health Solutions S.A.S. Bogotá, Colombia. Revista Colombiana de Obstetricia y Ginecología Vol. 77 No.1 • Enero - Marzo 2026 • 4510 Cómo citar este artículo: Álvarez A, Díaz S, Niño RA, Medina YA, Chacón A, Franco A. Costo-efectividad de la inclusión de la doble tinción p16/Ki-67 en detección de lesiones cervicales en Colombia, 2024. Rev Colomb Obstet Ginecol. 2026;77:4510. https://doi.org/10.18597/rcog.4510 Rev Colomb Obstet Ginecol ISSN 2463-0225 (On line) 2026;77:4510 Read the English version of this article at https://revista.fecolsog.org Copyright © 2026 Federación Colombiana de Obstetricia y Ginecología (FECOLSOG). Este es un artículo de acceso abierto bajo la licencia CC BY-NC-ND (http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/) https://doi.org/10.18597/rcog.4510 Revista Colombiana de Obstetricia y Ginecología Vol. 77 No.1 • 2026 generating cost savings (–COP $80 million for women aged 25 to 29 and –COP $54 million for women aged 30 to 65). Sensitivity analyses confirmed model robustness. Conclusions: The cost-effectiveness analysis suggests the advisability of incorporating the p16/Ki-67 dualstaining test into cervical cancer screening protocols, as it reduces unnecessary examinations and improves resource allocation. Studies are needed that evaluate the performance of screening tests in the local context and that incorporate morbidity and mortality outcomes to assess hard outcomes over a longer time horizon",Uterine cervical neoplasms; Cost-benefit analysis; Cytology; Biomarkers; Papillomavirus infections,marcadores,ctividad de la inclusion de la doble tincion p16,objectiv asses cost-effectivenes incorporat p16 ki-67 dual-stain cytology into cervical cancer screen protocol compar standard diagnostic pathway colombia material method decision-tree model develop healthcare provider perspective using real-world data scientific evidence primary outcome number invasive procedur avoid deterministic probabilistic sensitivity analys perform addres uncertainty result incorporat p16 ki-67 dual-stain cytology prov dominant strategy significantly reduc unnecessary colposcopi biopsi recibido julio 2025 aceptado 27 marzo 2026 correspondencia invalue health solution calle 23 68-50 8-604 bogota colombia yudely medina invalueh com viva 1a medellin colombia invalue health solution bogota colombia revista colombiana de obstetricia ginecologia vol 77 no enero marzo 2026 4510 como citar este articulo alvarez diaz nino ra medina ya chacon franco costo-efectividad de la inclusion de la doble tincion p16 ki-67 en deteccion de lesion cervical en colombia 2024 rev colomb obstet ginecol 2026 77 4510 http doi org 10 18597 rcog 4510 rev colomb obstet ginecol issn 2463-0225 line 2026 77 4510 read english version article http revista fecolsog org copyright 2026 federacion colombiana de obstetricia ginecologia fecolsog este es un articulo de acceso abierto bajo la licencia cc by-nc-nd http creativecommon org licens by-nc-nd http doi org 10 18597 rcog 4510 revista colombiana de obstetricia ginecologia vol 77 no 