2463-0470,document (5).pdf,document (5)_0,en,Pedagogical practices and contextual approach: Why,"Background and objectives: This article examines technocratic accounting education and specifically challenges the orthodox, business-oriented teaching practices commonly used in the instruction of cost accounting. Given that this type of knowledge is rooted in a practitioner’s epistemology through which processes of valuation, control, and efficiency analysis, it was necessary to employ a pedagogical practice that, based on the epistemology of liberation, would challenge the dominant view of the business world and establish a link between the topics covered in the course and debates on democracy and the struggles for environmental and social justice. Methods: To carry this out, dialogue was considered the central pedagogical axis, which allowed for addressing content that involved, in addition to traditional cost manuals, other types of experiences that brought the educational actors closer to their broader social, economic, cultural, environmental, and political context. The description of this pedagogical practice follows the narrative documentation methodology to show how the course was planned, what occurred during the classes, and what the students’ reactions and feedback were. Findings: The activities carried out have enabled an understanding of the orthodox concepts and procedures of cost accounting and, at the same time, have given rise to reflections that have encouraged a critical view of the environment, society, and accounting. Conclusion: The contextual approach has enabled the design of a cost accounting course from the perspective of the geopolitics of knowledge, helping students recognize for what and for whom what they have learned is relevant","Contextual approach; Cost accounting; Pedagogical practice; Popular education; Vocational training, JEL: A22; B50; D24; I24; M40 NUMBER OF REFERENCES 26 NUMBER OF FIGURES 0 NUMBER OF TABLES 0 ORIGINAL RESEARCH PAPER ARTICLE INFO Article History: Received: 13/06/2025 Accepted: 30/08/2025 Published: 15/10/2025",marcadores,pedagogical practic contextual approach why,background objectiv article examin technocratic account education specifically challeng orthodox business-orient teach practic commonly used instruction cost account given type knowledge root practitioner epistemology through which process valuation control efficiency analysi necessary employ pedagogical practice based epistemology liberation would challenge dominant view busines world establish link between topic cover course debat democracy struggl environmental social justice method carry out dialogue consider central pedagogical axis which allow address content involv addition traditional cost manual other type experienc brought educational actor closer their broader social economic cultural environmental political context description pedagogical practice follow narrative documentation methodology show how course plann what occurr during class what student reaction feedback finding activiti carri out have enabl understand orthodox concept procedur cost account same time have given rise reflection have encourag critical view environment society account conclusion contextual approach has enabl design cost account course perspective geopolitic knowledge help student recognize what whom what they have learn relevant,contextual approach cost account pedagogical practice popular education vocational train jel a22 b50 d24 i24 m40 number referenc 26 number figur number tabl original research paper article info article history receiv 13 06 2025 accept 30 08 2025 publish 15 10 2025,pedagogical practic contextual approach why background objectiv article examin technocratic account education specifically challeng orthodox business-orient teach practic commonly used instruction cost account given type knowledge root practitioner epistemology through which process valuation control efficiency analysi necessary employ pedago