2463-0470,document (6).pdf,document (6)_0,en,Compliance audit and ESG practices as a contribution,"Background and objectives: Compliance auditing has gained increasing relevance within the framework of corporate sustainability, particularly in highly regulated sectors such as energy. However, its articulation with Environmental, Social and Governance (ESG) frameworks remains uneven and reveals significant conceptual and methodological gaps. Accordingly, the objective of this article is to systematically analyze the existing scientific literature on compliance auditing as an instrument for corporate sustainability in the energy sector, identifying emerging trends, analytical categories, and research gaps. Methods: A systematic literature review was conducted following the PRISMA guidelines, based on indexed academic databases and specialized sources. This process resulted in the identification of 20 studies that constituted the main analytical corpus, complemented by additional contextual and normative literature. Findings: The comparative analysis revealed four emerging categories: (i) compliance auditing as a strategic governance function; (ii) its role in ESG risk mitigation; (iii) the use of technological tools and information systems as enablers of control; and (iv) the evolution toward results-oriented and performance-based auditing approaches. The findings indicate that, despite growing consensus regarding the potential of compliance auditing to strengthen corporate sustainability, its implementation remains characterized by methodological fragmentation and limited standardization of auditable ESG metrics, particularly in emerging economies where empirical evidence remains scarce. The study also highlights the prospective role of compliance auditing as a mechanism for risk anticipation and strategic decision-making in energy transition processes. Conclusion: It concludes that compliance auditing can consolidate itself as an articulating axis between governance and sustainable corporate performance in the energy sector, provided that integrated and contextually adapted models are developed. Finally, the article proposes a future research agenda focused on hybrid audit models and the empirical validation of ESG methodologies, especially in Latin American contexts",Compliance auditing; Corporate sustainability; Energy sector; ESG; Governance. JEL: M40; M41; M42 NUMBER OF REFERENCES 30 NUMBER OF FIGURES 1 NUMBER OF TABLES 3 ORIGINAL RESEARCH PAPER ARTICLE INFO Article History: Received: 03/04/2025 Accepted: 16/06/2025 Published: 15/07/2025 *Corresponding author: Email: fqui,marcadores,compliance audit esg practic contribution,background objectiv compliance audit has gain increas relevance within framework corporate sustainability particularly highly regulat sector such energy however its articulation environmental social governance esg framework remain uneven reveal significant conceptual methodological gaps accord objective article systematically analyze exist scientific literature compliance audit instrument corporate sustainability energy sector identify emerg trend analytical categori research gaps method systematic literature review conduct follow prisma guidelin based index academic databas specializ sourc proces result identification 20 studi constitut main analytical corpu complement additional contextual normative literature finding comparative analysi reveal four emerg categori compliance audit strategic governance function ii its role esg risk mitigation iii use technological tool information system enabler control iv evolution toward results-orient performance-bas audit approach finding indicate despite grow consensu regard potential compliance audit strengthen corporate sustainability its implementation remain characteriz methodological fragmentation limit standard auditable esg metric particularly emerg economi where empirical evidence remain scarce study also highlight prospective role compliance audit mechanism risk anticipation strategic decision-mak energy transition process conclusion conclud compliance audit can consolidate itself articulat axis between governance sustainable corporate performance energy sector provid integrat contextually adapt model develop finally article propos future research agenda focus hybrid audit model empirical validation esg methodologi especially latin american context,compliance audit corporate sustainability energy sector esg governance jel m40 m41 m42 number referenc 30 number figur number tabl original research paper article info article history receiv 03 04 2025 accept 16 06 2025 publish 15 07 2025 correspond author email fqui,compliance audit esg practic contribution background objectiv compliance audit has gain increas relevance within framework corporate sustainability particularly highly regulat sector such energy however its articulation environmental social governance esg framework remain uneven reveal significant conceptual methodological gaps accord objective article systematically analyze exist scientific literature compliance audit instrument corporate sustainability energy sector identify emerg trend analytical categori research gaps method systematic literature review conduct follow prisma guidelin based index academic databas specializ sourc proces result identification 20 studi constitut main analytical corpu complement additional contextual normative literature finding comparative analysi reveal four emerg categori compliance audit strategic governance function ii its role esg risk mitigation iii use technological tool information system enabler control iv evolution toward results-orient performance-bas audit approach finding indicate despite grow consensu regard potential compliance audit strengthen corporate sustainability its implementation remain characteriz methodological fragmentation limit standard auditable esg metric particularly emerg economi where empirical evidence remain scarce study also highlight prosp