2463-0470,document (7).pdf,document (7)_0,en,Generative artificial intelligence (GenAI) tools: a new,"Background and objectives: This article analyzes generative artificial intelligence tools in higher education for public accounting, with the aim of guiding teachers and students in their effective pedagogical integration. Methods: A literature review was conducted based on 47 academic documents from databases such as Scopus, Web of Science, and Google Scholar (2013-2025), supplemented with 12 non-academic sources, following the bibliographic synthesis methodology of Zupic and Cater (2015). Findings: The main findings categorize these tools into four functional groups: curriculum design, classroom activities, assessment, and research, which optimize educational processes by freeing up time for activities of high cognitive value. Conclusion: It is concluded that their critical, ethical, and contextualized adoption is essential to closing digital divides in emerging contexts, requiring continuous teacher training and responsible institutional frameworks",AI tools; Educational tools; Generative Artificial Intelligence; Learning tools; Higher education. JEL: M40; M41; M49 NUMBER OF REFERENCES 60 NUMBER OF FIGURES 4 NUMBER OF TABLES 4 ORIGINAL RESEARCH PAPER ARTICLE INFO Article History: Received: 03/04/2025 Accepted: 17/06/2025 Published: 15/07/2025,marcadores,generative artificial intelligence genai tool new,background objectiv article analyz generative artificial intelligence tool higher education public account aim guid teacher student their effective pedagogical integration method literature review conduct based 47 academic document databas such scopu web science google scholar 2013-2025 supplement 12 non-academic sourc follow bibliographic synthesi methodology zupic cater 2015 finding main finding categorize these tool into four functional group curriculum design classroom activiti assessment research which optimize educational process free up time activiti high cognitive value conclusion conclud their critical ethical contextualiz adoption essential clos digital divid emerg context requir continuou teacher train responsible institutional framework,ai tool educational tool generative artificial intelligence learn tool higher education jel m40 m41 m49 number referenc 60 number figur number tabl original research paper article info article history receiv 03 04 2025 accept 17 06 2025 publish 15 07 2025,generative artificial intelligence genai tool new background objectiv article analyz generative artificial intelligence tool higher education public account aim guid teacher student their effective pedagogical integration method literature review conduct based 47 academic document databas such scopu web science google scholar 2013-2025 supplement 12 non-academic sourc follow bibliographic synthesi methodology zupic cater 2015 finding main finding categorize these tool into four functional group curriculum design classroom activiti assessment research which optimize educational process free up time activiti high cognitive value conclusion conclud their critical ethical contextualiz adoption essential clos digital divid emerg context requir continuou teacher train responsible institutional framework ai tool educational tool generative artificial intelligence learn tool higher education jel m40 m41 m49 number referenc 60 number figur number tabl original research paper article info article history receiv 03 04 2025 accept 17 06 2025 publish 15 07 2025,1.0.0,ad8196e60b25ad51
2463-0470,document (7).pdf,document (7)_0,es,Andrés Escobar E. Universidad de CartagenaColombia.,"Objetivos: El presente artículo analiza las herramientas de Inteligencia Artificial generativa en la educación superior de contaduría pública, con el objetivo de orientar a docentes y estudiantes en su integración pedagógica efectiva. Métodos: Se realizó una revisión de la literatura basada en 47 documentos académicos de como Scopus, WoS, Google Scholar (2013-2025), complementado con 12 fuentes no académicas siguiendo la metodología de síntesis bibliográfica de Zupic y Cater (2015). Resultados: Los hallazgos principales categorizas estas herramientas en cuatro grupos funcionales diseño curricular, actividades áulicas, evaluación e investigación, que optimizan los procesos educativos al liberar tiempo para actividades de alto valor cognitivo. Conclusión: Se concluye que su adopción critica, ética y contextualizada es esencial para cerrar brechas digitales en contextos emergentes, requiriendo formación docente continua y marcos institucionales responsables","Educación superior; Inteligencia Artificial generativa, Herramientas de IA, Herramientas educativas. Clasificación JEL: M40; M41; M49 ARTICULO ORIGINAL 203 Herramientas de inteligencia artificial generativa (IAG): un nuevo horizonte para la educación superior en Contaduría Pública Panorama Económico, Vol. 33 No. 3",marcadores,andr escobar universidad cartagenacolombia,objetiv presente articulo analiza herramient inteligencia artificial generativa educacion superior contaduria publica objetivo orientar docent estudiant integracion pedagogica efectiva metod realizo revision literatura basada 47 document academic como scopus wos google scholar 2013-2025 complementado 12 fuent no academic sigu metodologia sintesis bibliografica zupic cater 2015 resultad hallazg principal categoriz estas herramient cuatro grup funcional diseno curricular actividad aulic evaluacion investigacion optimizan proces educativ liberar tiempo acti