2463-0470,document (8).pdf,document (8)_0,en,Humanistic teaching-based competency model,"Background and objectives: The evaluation of a competency-based graduate profile constitutes an essential component in ensuring comprehensive higher education, as it enables the systematic measurement of both specific and transversal competencies throughout the entire academic trajectory of university students. For this reason, the objective of this article is to analyze the evaluation of the graduate profile under a humanistic competency-based educational model, considering its epistemological foundations and applicability to Accounting students. Methods: The study was conducted using a quantitative approach, with a nonexperimental, field-based, and descriptive-analytical design. It began with a literature review supporting the epistemological foundations of the humanistic competency-based educational model, followed by the application of assessment instruments in four courses corresponding to different stages of the Accounting program at a university located in Guayaquil, Ecuador. Findings: The main findings reveal a progressive advancement from “in progress” to “acceptable achievement” and “outstanding achievement,” with greater consolidation observed in the final stages of training; however, challenges were identified in competencies requiring higher cognitive complexity, particularly financial analysis and accounting systems management. Conclusion: The evaluation system of the graduate profile under a humanistic competency-based approach is both relevant and functional, as it not only measures technical and disciplinary mastery within the specific field of knowledge, but also, in coherence with the socio-critical epistemological stance, assesses—through a transversal perspective—the development of critical consciousness oriented toward the responsible transformation of social reality","Humanistic educational model, Socio-critical approach; Specific competencies; Transversal competencies; Undegraduate profile assessment. JEL: M49; I20; I21 NUMBER OF REFERENCES 22 NUMBER OF FIGURES 8 NUMBER OF TABLES 0 ORIGINAL RESEARCH PAPER ARTICLE INFO Article History: Received: 15/02/2025 Accepted: 30/05/2025 Pu",marcadores,humanistic teaching-bas competency model,background objectiv evaluation competency-bas graduate profile constitut essential component ensur comprehensive higher education enabl systematic measurement both specific transversal competenci throughout entire academic trajectory university student reason objective article analyze evaluation graduate profile under humanistic competency-bas educational model consider its epistemological found applicability account student method study conduct using quantitative approach nonexperimental field-bas descriptive-analytical design began literature review support epistemological found humanistic competency-bas educational model follow application assessment instrument four cours correspond different stag account program university locat guayaquil ecuador finding main finding reveal progressive advancement progres acceptable achievement outstand achievement greater consolidation observ final stag train however challeng identifi competenci requir higher cognitive complexity particularly financial analysi account system management conclusion evaluation system graduate profile under humanistic competency-bas approach both relevant functional not only measur technical disciplinary mastery within specific field knowledge but also coherence socio-critical epistemological stance assesses--through transversal perspective--the development critical consciousnes orient toward responsible transformation social reality,humanistic educational model socio-critical approach specific competenci transversal competenci undegraduate profile assessment jel m49 i20 i21 number referenc 22 number figur number tabl original research paper article info article history receiv 15 02 2025 accept 30 05 2025 pu,humanistic te