2463-0470,document (9).pdf,document (9)_0,en,"Accounting, ethics and sustainability: a critical reflection from","Background and objectives: Sustainable development has gained increasing importance due to the evident social and environmental damage caused by business economic activities. Accounting has begun to address these issues, as it is not isolated from these new realities. In this sense, the central objective is to reflect on the social responsibilities that companies and public accountants have acquired in their professional roles in pursuit of the public interest. Methods: Through a literature review of the disciplinary categories of accounting and ethics in this field, as well as sustainability, key opinions from scholars in this area are considered to reflect on the nature of accounting professional training, which is focused on responding to the needs for maximizing financial resources while neglecting social and environmental needs. The central idea and its main argument are presented descriptively. Results: The training of public accountants has focused on responding to the needs of individuals centered on maximizing financial resources, without real emphasis on social and environmental aspects. Therefore, it is necessary to rethink accounting education processes in universities to consider social and changing aspects, since public accountants have an ethical responsibility to these latter, who are beginning to demand non-financial information from companies to ensure collective well-being. Conclusion: It is necessary to reflect on whether the accounting professional is meant to respond to the needs of the public sector, or whether they are also meant to serve the public interest, considering these new contexts","Accounting Education; Environmental Accounting; Professional Ethics; Social Accounting, Sustainability. JEL: M41 NUMBER OF REFERENCES 30 NUMBER OF FIGURES 1 NUMBER OF TABLES 0 ORIGINAL RESEARCH PAPER ARTICLE INFO Article History: Received: 02/02/2025 Accepted: 24/05/2025 Published: 15/07/2025 *Corresp",marcadores,account ethic sustainability critical reflection,background objectiv sustainable development has gain increas importance due evident social environmental damage caus busines economic activiti account has begun addres these issu not isolat these new realiti sense central objective reflect social responsibiliti compani public accountant have acquir their professional role pursuit public interest method through literature review disciplinary categori account ethic field well sustainability key opinion scholar area consider reflect nature account professional train which focus respond need maximiz financial resourc while neglect social environmental need central idea its main argument present descriptively result train public accountant has focus respond need individual center maximiz financial resourc without real emphasi social environmental aspect therefore necessary rethink account education process universiti consider social chang aspect since public accountant have ethical responsibility these latter who beginn demand non-financial information compani ensure collective well-be conclusion necessary reflect whether account professional meant respond need public sector whether they also meant serve public interest consider these new context,account education environmental account professional ethic social account sustainability jel m41 number referenc 30 number figur number tabl original research paper article info article history receiv 02 02 2025 accept 24 05 2025 publish 15 07 2025 corresp,account ethic sustainability critical reflection background objectiv sustainable development has gain increas importance due evident social environmental damage caus busines economic activiti account has begun addres these issu not isolat these new realiti sense central objective reflect social responsibiliti compani public accountant have acquir their professional role pursuit public interest method through literature review disciplinary categori account ethic field well sustainability key opinion scholar area consider reflect nature account professional train which focus respond need maximiz financial resourc while neglect social environmental need central idea its main argument present descriptively result train public accountant has focus respond need individual center maximiz financial resourc without real emphasi social environmental aspect therefore necessary rethink account education process universiti consider social chang aspect since public accountant have ethical responsibility these latter who beginn demand non-financial information compani ensure collective well-be conclusion necessary reflect whether account professional meant respond need public sector whether they also meant serve public interest consider these new context account education environmental account professional ethic social account sustainability jel m41 number referenc 30 number figur number tabl original research paper article info article history receiv 02 02 2025 accept 24 05 2025 publish 15 07 2025 corresp,1.0.0,c4a8ad5c4f8685ec
2463-0470,document (9).pdf,document (9)_0,es,Article History:,"Introducción y objetivos: Actualmente el desarrollo sostenible ha tomado mayor importancia por los evidentes deterioros sociales y ambientales por el desarrollo de las actividades económicas de las empresas. Desde la contabilidad estos asuntos se han comenzado a abordar, pues la contabilidad no está aislada de estas nuevas realidades, en este sentido, el objetivo central es reflexionar sobre las responsabilidades sociales que han adquirido las empresas y el contador público desde su rol profesional en procura del interés público. Métodos: Mediante una revisión literaria de las categorías disciplinares de lo contable y la ética en este accionar, así como la sostenibilidad, se toman opiniones centrales de estudiosos en esta materia para reflexionar sobre la naturaleza en la formación de los profesionales de la contaduría centrada en responder a las necesidades para la maximización de los recursos financieros dejando de lado las necesidades sociales y ambientales. En este sentido, de manera descriptiva se presenta la idea a reflexionar y el argumento principal sobre ella. Resultados: La formación de los contadores públicos se ha centrado en responder a las necesidades de particulares centradas en la maximización de los recursos financieros, sin énfasis real en aspectos sociales y ambientales. De manera que es necesario repensar los procesos de educación contable de las universidades para considerar los aspectos sociales y cambiantes, pues el contador público éticamente tiene una responsabilidad con estos últimos, los cuales empiezan a demandar información no financiera de las empresas para procurar por el bienestar colectivo. Conclusión: Es necesario reflexionar si el profesional de la contaduría está para responder a las necesidades del sector público, o está también para los intereses públicos, teniendo en cuenta los nuevos contextos","Contabilidad Social, Contabilidad Ambiental, Ética profesional, Educación Contable, Sostenibilidad. Clasificación JEL: M41 ARTICULO ORIGINAL 252 Contabilidad, ética y sostenibilidad: una reflexión crítica desde la educación contable Panorama Económico, Vol. 33 No. 3",marcadores,article history,introduccion objetiv actual desarrollo sostenible ha tomado mayor importancia evident deterior social ambiental desarrollo actividad economic empres desde contabilidad estos asunt han comenzado abordar pues contabilidad no esta aislada estas nuev realidad este sentido objetivo central reflexionar sobre responsabilidad social han adquirido empres contador publico desde rol profesional procura inter publico metod mediante revision literaria categori disciplinar contable etica este accionar asi como sostenibilidad toman opinion central estudios esta materia reflexionar sobre naturaleza formacion profesional contaduria centrada responder necesidad maximizacion recurs financier dejando lado necesidad social ambiental este sentido manera descriptiva presenta idea reflexionar argumento principal sobre ella resultad formacion contador public ha centrado responder necesidad particular centrad maximizacion recurs financier sin enfasis real aspect social ambiental manera necesario repensar proces educacion contable universidad considerar aspect social cambiant pues contador publico etica tiene responsabilidad estos ultim cual empiezan demandar informacion no financiera empres procurar bienestar colectivo conclusion necesario reflexionar si profesional contaduria esta responder necesidad sector publico esta tambien interes public teniendo cuenta nuev context,contabilidad social contabilidad ambiental etica profesional educacion contable sostenibilidad clasificacion jel m41 articulo original 252 contabilidad etica sostenibilidad reflexion critica desde educacion contable panorama economico vol 33 no,article history introduccion objetiv actual desarrollo sostenible ha tomado mayor importancia evident deterior social ambiental desarrollo actividad economic emp