2500-5316,pr3+rFCB+20(1)_8160+Barrios&Morales_3.pdf,pr3+rFCB+20(1)_8160+Barrios&Morales_3_0,en,ión con otras ciudades importantes del,"Air pollution poses a significant risk to people’s respiratory health and, in addition to its health consequences, has negative environmental and economic effects. This study worked with PM2.5 concentration data, a pollutant formed by particles suspended in the air with an aerodynamic diameter less than or equal to 2.5 micrometers (µm). For the analysis, historical air quality data from monitoring stations located in Bogotá, Medellín, and Cali during 2023 were used, analyzed through functional data analysis techniques such as one-way functional analysis of variance (F-ANOVA), mul tiple comparisons for outlier curve detection, and heat maps to visualize the spatial distribution of concentrations. The F-ANOVA results showed evidence of significant differences between the aver age PM2.5 concentrations of the three selected cities (p < 0.001). Medellín presented the highest concentration levels, with values between 20.65 and 77.08 µg/m³, exceeding the intermediate an nual targets recommended by the World Health Organization. Additionally, the city showed greater spatial and temporal variability in the recorded concentrations, while Bogotá and Cali, with average concentrations of 15.20 µg/m³ and 13.13 µg/m³, respectively, did not show significant differences be tween each other. It is concluded that Medellín presents a concerning situation in terms of air quality compared to other major cities in the country, as well as the usefulness of functional data analysis in this context","air quality; PM2.5; functional analysis of variance; functional data analysis. Caracterização das variações espaçotemporais do material particulado PM2,5 em três cidades da Colômbia por meio de técnicas de análise de dados funcionáis",marcadores,ion con otra ciudad important del,air pollution pose significant risk people respiratory health addition its health con