2500-5421,v2_01+procrastinacion+RIIEP19_vol1.pdf,v2_01+procrastinacion+RIIEP19_vol1_0,en,culpa. Conclusión. La procrastinación entre profesores universitarios,Objective. To analyze the procrastination behavior of university faculty and its causes. Method. A qualitative descriptive phenomenological study was conducted with 114 public university professors. Results. Professors delay tasks mainly due to problems with organization and time management. They indicate that workload overload and distractions contribute to procrastination in their work. This behavior sometimes affects teaching quality and leads to increased stress and feelings of guilt. Conclusion. Procrastination among university professors is linked to organizational and contextual factors that negatively impact their performance and emotional well-being,"causal analysis, quality of education, teacher behavior, time management, teaching staff, procrastination. Procrastinação: uma forma contemporânea de comportamento docente",marcadores,culpa conclusion la procrastinacion entre profesor universitario,objective analyze procrastination behavior university faculty its caus method qualitative descriptive phenomenological study conduct 114 public university professor result professor delay task mainly due problem organ time management they indicate workload overload distraction contribute procrastination their work behavior sometim affect teach quality lead increas stres feeling guilt conclusion procrastination among university professor link organizational contextual factor negatively impact their performance emotional well-be,causal analysi quality education teacher behavior time management teach staff procrastination procrastinacao uma forma contemporanea de comportamento docente,culpa conclusion la procrastinacion entre profesor universitario objective analyze procrastination behavior university faculty its caus method qualitative descriptive phenomenological study conduct 114 public university professor result professor delay task mainly due problem organ time management they indicate workload overload distraction contribute procrastination their work behavior sometim affect teach quality lead increas stres feeling guilt conclusion procrastination among university professor link organizational contextual factor negatively impact their performance emotional well-be causal analysi quality education teacher behavior time management teach staff procrastination procrastinacao uma forma contemporanea de comportamento docente,1.0.0,facb39abde033e03
