 (OIC) en la Dirección de Investigación y Prospectiva (DIP) del Instituto Geográfico Agustín (IGAC). Investigadora del Grupo (AMECI). Correo electrónico: anamariamontes@usantotomas.edu.co ORCID: https://orcid.org/0009-0005-7260-991X María Cristina Gamboa Mora, Vicky Ahumada, Anamaría Montes Gamboa Estimation of university students’ autonomy, its relationship with academic performance, and the validity of the measurement instrument. Research article 44 Volumen 19. número 1. enero - junio 2026 and Outfit), and Confirmatory Factor Analysis to determine each item’s contribution. Individual autonomy scores were assigned using the Rasch model. Academic performance was measured via average final grades. Results. The Spearman correlation showed that 16 scale items had a positive correlation between autonomy perception and academic grades. The instrument showed overall reliability, although some items required adjustment to better assess average and extreme values. Additionally, 44.88% of students were classified as autonomous. Conclusion. The Autonomy Level Scale is a reliable tool for measuring autonomy in university students in virtual education, with some recommendations for item modification to improve accuracy","Autonomy, reliability, distance education, measurement instrument, academic performance. Estimación de la autonomía de estudiantes universitarios, su relación con el rendimiento académico y la validez del instrumento de medición",marcadores,research article,objective estimate level autonomy among university student virtual distance learn environment method descriptive analytical correlational educational research conduct using sample 430 student autonomy level scale consist 67 likert-type item acros dimension validat calculat cronbach alpha rasch model analysi infit doctora en innovacion investigacion en didactica docente asociado de la escuela ciencia de la educacion lider del grupo de investigacion interinstitucional ameci avalado por la universidad nacional 