2500-5421,v2_06+percepciones+limita+RIIEP19_vol1.pdf,v2_06+percepciones+limita+RIIEP19_vol1_0,en,files docentes diferenciados:,"Objective. To analyze the perceptions, knowledge, and obstacles faced by teachers at a rural school in Palestina (Huila, Colombia) regarding the curricular integration of educational ecotourism as a pedagogical strategy that promotes environmental sustainability and territorial belonging. Method. A quantitative, cross-sectional, and correlational study conducted with 50 teachers. A structured REVISTA INTERAMERICANA DE INVESTIGACIÓN, EDUCACIÓN Y PEDAGOGÍA DOI: https://doi.org/10.15332/8kkgr784 179 ISSN: 1657-107X e-ISSN: 2500-5421 questionnaire was applied, and data were processed using chi-square tests, hierarchical cluster analysis, and principal component analysis. Results. The level of knowledge about educational ecotourism was found to be significantly associated with teachers› prior training, perception of environmental benefits, and existing institutional barriers. Three differentiated teacher profiles were identified: those who actively apply educational ecotourism strategies, those who show interest but face implementation limitations, and those with low familiarity with the concept. Conclusion. It is necessary to strengthen differentiated teacher training according to the identified profiles, increase institutional support, and promote contextualized curricular integration of educational ecotourism. These findings provide fundamental inputs for designing educational policies and pedagogical practices with a territorial approach in rural contexts",Educational ecotourism; Environmental education; Rural teachers; Educational sustainability; Curriculum integration; Institutional barriers. Percepções e limitações na implementação do ecoturismo educativo em escolas rurais: evidências do sul da Colômbia,marcadores,file docent diferenciado,objective analyze perception knowledge obstacl faced teacher rural school palestina huila colombia regard curricular integration educational ecotourism pedagogical strategy promot environmental sustainability territorial belong method quantitative cross-sectional correlational study conduct 50 teacher structur revista interamericana de investigacion educacion pedagogia doi http doi org 10 15332 8kkgr784 179 issn 1657-107x e-issn 2500-5421 questionnaire appli data process using chi-square test hierarchical cluster analysi principal component analysi result level knowledge about educational ecotourism found significantly associat teacher prior train perception environmental benefit exist institutional barrier three differentiat teacher profil identifi those who actively apply educational ecotourism strategi those who show interest but face implementation limit those low familiarity concept conclusion necessary strengthen differentiat teacher train accord identifi profil increase institutional support promote contextualiz curricular integration educational ecotourism these finding provide fundamental input design educational polici pedagogical practic territorial approach rural context,educational ecotourism environmental education rural teacher educational sustainability curriculum integration institutional barrier percepco limitaco na implementacao do ecoturismo educativo em escola rurai evidencia do sul da colombia,file docent diferenciado objective analyze perception knowledge obstacl faced teacher rural school palestina huila colombia regard curricular integration educational ecotourism pedagogical strategy promot environmental sustainability territorial belong method quantitative cross-sectional correlational study conduct 50 teacher structur revista interamericana de investigacion educacion pedagogia doi http doi org 10 15332 8kkgr784 179 issn 1657-107x e-issn 2500-5421 questionnaire appli data process using chi-square test hierarchical cluster analysi principal component analysi result level knowledge about educational ecotourism found significantly associat teacher prior train perception environmental benefit exist institutional barrier three differentiat teacher profil identifi those who actively apply educational ecotourism strategi those who show interest but face implementation limit those low familiarity concept conclusion necessary strengthen differentiat teacher train accord identifi profil increase institutional support promote contextualiz curricular integration educational ecotourism these finding provide fundamental input design educational polici pedagogical practic territorial approach rural context educational ecotourism environmental education rural teacher educational sustainability curriculum integration institutional barrier percepco limitaco na implementacao do ecoturismo educativo em escola rurai evidencia do sul da colombia,1.0.0,16d4d2c85f0024d7
2500-5421,v2_07+estado+arte+IA+RIIEP19_vol1.pdf,v2_07+estado+arte+IA+RIIEP19_vol1_0,es,ARTÍCULO DE REVISIÓN,"Objetivo. Examinar la influencia de la inteligencia artificial (IA) en el desarrollo del pensamiento matemático en contextos educativos. Método. Revisión sistemática de la literatura publicada entre 2019 y 2024, mediante búsqueda en bases de datos académicas. Se identificaron 138 artículos y se seleccionaron 45 que cumplieron los criterios de inclusión. Resultados. Se identificaron tres tendencias clave: (1) uso de sistemas tutores inteligentes para personalizar el aprendizaje, (2) aplicación de analíticas de aprendizaje basadas en IA para evaluar el pensamiento matemático, y (3) creación de entornos adaptativos que promueven el razonamiento matemático. Conclusión. Las tecnologías de IA están transformando la enseñanza * Universidad del Atlántico. ORCID: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7421-1754 Correo electrónico: carmonarjconde@mail.uniatlantico.edu.co ** Universidad del Atlántico. ORCID: https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3667-1087 Correo electrónico: soniabalbuena@mail.uniatlantico.edu.co; *** Universidad del Atlántico. ORCID: https://orcid.org/0009-0008-2110-5078 Correo electrónico: Lsofiacastillo@mail.uniatlantico.edu.co Robinson Junior Conde-Carmona, Sonia Valbuena Duarte, Laura Sofía Castillo Ochoa Estado del Arte sobre Inteligencia Artificial y Pensamiento Matemático: Una Revisión Sistemática. Artículo de revisión 206 Volumen 19. número 1. enero - junio 2026 de las matemáticas, ofreciendo oportunidades para la personalización y evaluación más precisas, y abriendo líneas de investigación pedagógica futuras","inteligencia artificial, educación matemática, pensamiento matemático, sistemas tutores inteligentes, aprendizaje adaptativo. State of the Art on Artificial Intelligence and Mathematical Thinking: A Systematic Review",marcadores,articulo revision,objetivo examinar influencia inteligencia artificial ia desarrollo pensamiento matematico context educativ metodo