2500-5421,v2_11+validacion+escala+RIIEP19_vol1+(1).pdf,v2_11+validacion+escala+RIIEP19_vol1+(1)_0,en,dades competitivas en educación superior. Artículo producto de la investigación,"Objective. To validate an instrument for measuring competitive priorities in Higher Education Institutions from the perspective of their stakeholders. Method. The Competitive Priorities Scale in Higher Education was applied to 855 individuals from the Eje Cafetero region. Content validity was assessed through expert judgment, and a confirmatory factor analysis was conducted to estimate construct validity. Internal consistency was evaluated using the omega coefficient. Results. The average content validity index of the items was 0.78 for the total scale. Confirmatory factor analysis indicated a unifactorial structure with good fit across different indices. The scale demonstrated high internal consistency (0.81). Conclusion. For the stakeholders REVISTA INTERAMERICANA DE INVESTIGACIÓN, EDUCACIÓN Y PEDAGOGÍA DOI: https://doi.org/10.15332/0cghpq79 343 ISSN: 1657-107X e-ISSN: 2500-5421 analyzed, the most relevant competitive priorities are quality, flexibility, innovation, and sustainability","Competitive Priorities, Higher Education, Instrument, Measurement Scale. Validação de uma escala para medir prioridades competitivas no ensino superior",marcadores,dade competitiva en educacion superior articulo producto de la investigacion,objective validate instrument measur competitive prioriti higher education institution perspective their stakeholder method competitive prioriti scale higher education appli 855 individual eje cafetero region content validity assess through expert judgment confirmatory factor analysi conduct estimate construct validity internal consistency evaluat using omega coefficient result average content validity index item 78 total scale confirmatory factor analysi indicat unifactorial structure good fit acros different indic scale demonstrat high internal consistency 81 concl