2500-5421,v2_13+lectura+critica+RIIEP19_vol1.pdf,v2_13+lectura+critica+RIIEP19_vol1_0,en,sivos de complejidad. La encuesta de percepción,"Objective: To describe the conceptualization, design, and initial assessment of Virtual Learning Objects constructed to strengthen critical reading and quantitative reasoning competencies in higher education students, acknowledging their positive link to learning and academic trajectory. Method. The design of Virtual Learning Objects was grounded in the TPACK model (Technological Pedagogical REVISTA INTERAMERICANA DE INVESTIGACIÓN, EDUCACIÓN Y PEDAGOGÍA DOI: https://doi.org/10.15332/kwy5t156 415 ISSN: 1657-107X e-ISSN: 2500-5421 Content Knowledge) and incorporated Problem-Based Learning methodology. Forty-eight objects were constructed—24 for each competency—differentiated according to three levels of cognitive development: basic, intermediate, and advanced. Initial assessment was conducted through a survey administered to 108 students. Results. Forty-eight Virtual Learning Objects were developed (24 for critical reading and 24 for quantitative reasoning), structured according to three progressive levels of complexity. The usability and utility perception survey demonstrated favorable student evaluation of these resources, providing positive indication of their pedagogical acceptability. Conclusion. The Virtual Learning Objects designed demonstrate viability as tools for strengthening critical reading and quantitative reasoning competencies. Future research is required to establish the direct relationship between the use of these objects and effective competency development, beyond perception and usability measurements","Learning Objects (LO), critical reading, quantitative reasoning, usability, problem-based learning. Leitura Crítica e Raciocínio Quantitativo no Ensino Superior: Desenho Pedagógico e Percepção dos Alunos sobre Objetos Virtuais de Aprendizagem",marcadores,sivo de complejidad la encuesta de percepcion,objective describe conceptual design initial assessment virtual learn object construct strengthen critical read quantitative reason competenci higher education student acknowledg their positive link learn academic trajectory method design virtual learn object ground tpack model technological pedagogical revista interamericana de investigacion educacion pedagogia doi http doi org 10 15332 kwy5t156 415 issn 1657-107x e-issn 2500-5421 content knowledge incorporat problem-bas learn methodology forty-eight object constructed--24 each competency--differentiat accord three level cognitive development basic intermediate advanc initial assessment conduct through survey administer 108 student result forty-eight virtual learn object develop 24 critical read 24 quantitative reason structur accord three progressive level complexity usability utility perception survey demonstrat favorable student evaluation these resourc provid positive indication their pedagogical acceptability conclusion virtual learn object design demonstrate viability tool strengthen critical read quantitative reason competenci future research requir establish direct relationship between use these object effective competency development beyond perception usability measurement,learn object lo critical read quantitative reason usability problem-bas learn leitura critica raciocinio quantitativo no ensino superior desenho pedagogico percepcao dos aluno sobre objeto virtuai de aprendizagem,sivo de complejidad la encuesta de percepcion objective describe conceptual design initial assessment virtual learn object construct strengthen critical read quantitative reason competenci higher education student acknowledg their positive link learn academic trajectory method design virtual learn object ground tpack model technological pedagogical revista interamericana de investigacion educacion pedagogia doi http doi org 10 15332 kwy5t156 415 issn 1657-107x e-issn 2500-5421 content knowledge incorporat problem-bas learn methodology forty-eight object constructed--24 each competency--differentiat accord three level cognitive development basic intermediate advanc initial assessment conduct through survey administer 108 student result forty-eight virtual learn object develop 24 critical read 24 quantitative reason structur accord three progressive level complexity usability utility perception survey demonstrat favorable student evaluation these resourc provid positive indication their pedagogical acceptability conclusion virtual learn object design demonstrate viability tool strengthen critical read quantitative reason competenci future research requir establish direct relationship between use these object effective competency development beyond perception usability measurement learn object lo critical read quantitative reason usability problem-bas learn leitura critica raciocinio quantitativo no ensino superior desenho pedagogico percepcao dos aluno sobre objeto virtuai de aprendizagem,1.0.0,5a0cd487841137b7
2500-5421,v2_14+instructor+assessment+RIIEP19_vol1.pdf,v2_14+instructor+assessment+RIIEP19_vol1_0,en,RESEARCH ARTICLE,"Objective. To examine the relationship between instructors› assessment literacy (IAL) and the reported implementation of formative and alternative assessment methodology (FAAM) adopted at a Colombian university during the COVID-19 pandemic, analyzing how assessment strategies and institutional factors influence both constructs. Method. A survey was administered to 159 instructors addressing topics including benefits and challenges experienced with FAAM implementation, assessment strategies employed, perspectives on student assessment, and background experiences with assessment. Multiple regression analyses were conducted to identify predictors of IAL and FAAM implementation. Results. Assessment strategy use *Universidad Surcolombiana, Neiva, Colombia. Email: leonardo.herrera@usco.edu.co ORCID: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4054-7209 **The University of North Carolina at Charlotte, USA. Email: rglamber@charlotte.edu ORCID: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5791-962X ***The University of North Carolina at Charlotte, USA. Email: JaeHoon.Lim@charlotte.edu ORCID: https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8167-1866 Leonardo Herrera-Mosquera, Richard George Lambert, Jae Hoon Lim Instructor Assessment Literacy and the Implementation of a Student Assessment Methodology in Higher Education. Research article 444 Volumen 19. número 1. enero - junio 2026 during FAAM implementation emerged as a significant predictor of IAL. IAL was significantly associated with FAAM component implementation. The colleges of Law and Education functioned as significant positive predictors of FAAM implementation. The School of Education demonstrated the strongest institutional influence, serving as a significant predictor of all outcome variables. IAL emerged as both the most influential explanatory variable and the outcome variable with the highest number of significant predictors. Conclusion. Instructors› assessment literacy represents a critical mediating factor in the successful implementation of formative and alternative assessment methodologies during institutional transformations. Disciplinary context, particularly within education and law faculties, significantly influences both assessment literacy development and FAAM adoption, suggesting that assessment reform requires disciplinary-sensitive approaches and comprehensive professional development in assessment practices","Assessment literacy, formative and alternative assessment, student assessment, assessment strategies, multiple regression. La Competencia de los Docentes en Evaluación y la Implementación de una",marcadores,research article,objective examine relationship between instructor assessment literacy ial report implementation formative alternative assessment methodology faam adopt colombian university during covid-19 pandemic analyz how assessment strategi institutional factor influence both construct method survey administer 159 instructor address topic includ benefit challeng experienc faam implementation assessment strategi employ perspectiv student assessment background experienc assessment multiple regression analys conduct identify predictor ial faam implementation result assessment strategy use universidad surcolombiana neiva colombia email leonardo herrera usco edu co orcid http orcid org 0000-0002-4054-7209 university north carolina charlotte usa email rglamber charlotte edu orcid http orcid org 0000-0002-5791-962x university north carolina charlotte usa email jaehoon lim charlotte edu orcid http orcid org 0000-0001-8167-1866 leonardo herrera-mosquera richard george lambert jae hoon lim instructor assessment literacy implementation student assessment methodology higher education research article 444 volumen 19 numero enero junio 2026 during faam implementation emerg significant predictor ial ial significantly associat faam component implementation colleg law education function significant