2500-6177,10a+(1)(1).pdf,10a+(1)(1)_0,en,lizada mediante revisión narrativa. Se identificó una,"This paper presents the results of a participatory assessment of barriers and facilitators to accessing early detection services for breast cancer in Soledad, Atlántico (Colombia). The assessment involved representatives of all stakeholders responsible for organizing and delivering these services, including patient representatives. It was conducted within the implementation of the “Pilot Program to strengthen early diagnosis and populationbased organized screening in two intermediate Colombian cities, 2023-2028,” led by the National Cancer Institute (Colombia). Using a qualitative approach, data were collected and analyzed through thematic analysis, and findings were organized and presented using Tanahashi’s framework. Key results were discussed in light of national and international scientific evidence, reviewed narratively. We found substantial consistency with results from other lowerand middle-income country contexts. Major availability barriers included the limited number of mammography units and a shortage of trained personnel. Accessibility barriers included low ability to pay and the health insurance scheme. Acceptability barriers included fear of pain and of a possible diagnosis, as well as reluctance to shoulder the burden of administrative paperwork. The main contact barrier was weak proactive outreach, whereas the greatest obstacle to effective access was the lack of coordination among responsible actors in managing service delivery networks","Barriers to Accessing Health Services, Breast Cancer, Early Detection of Cancer, Mammography, Colombia",marcadores,lizada mediante revision narrativa se identifico una,paper present result participatory assessment barrier facilitator access early detection servic breast cancer soledad atlantico colombia assessment involv representativ all stakeholder responsible organiz deliver these servic includ patient representativ conduct within implementation pilot program strengthen early diagnosi populationbas organiz screen two intermediate colombian citi 2023-2028 led national cancer institute colombia using qualitative approach data collect analyz through thematic analysi finding organiz present using tanahashi framework key result discuss light national international scientific evidence review narratively we found substantial consistency result other lowerand middle-income country context major availability barrier includ limit number mammography unit shortage train personnel accessibility barrier includ low ability pay health insurance scheme acceptability barrier includ fear pain possible diagnosi well reluctance shoulder burden administrative paperwork main contact barrier weak proactive outreach wherea greatest obstacle effective acces lack coordination among responsible actor manag service delivery network,barrier access health servic breast cancer early detection cancer mammography colombia,lizada mediante revision narrativa se identifico una paper present result participatory assessment barrier facilitator access early detection servic breast cancer soledad atlantico colombia assessment involv representativ all stakeholder responsible organiz deliver these servic includ patient representativ conduct within implementation pilot program strengthen early diagnosi populationbas organiz screen two intermediate colombian citi 2023-2028 led national cancer institute colombia using qualitative approach data collect analyz through thematic analysi finding organiz present using tanahashi framework key result discuss light national international scientific evidence review narratively we found substantial consistency result other lowerand middle-income country context major availability barrier includ limit number mammography unit shortage train personnel accessibility barrier includ low ability pay health insurance scheme acceptability barrier includ fear pain possible diagnosi well relucta