2500-6177,4a.pdf,4a_0,en,"ó durante un año e incluyó entrevistas grupales, diarios reflexivos y textos de escritura colectiva.","Introduction: The COVID-19 pandemic exacerbated pre-existing social, economic, and health crises, requiring negotiation and decision-making agreements among actors and institutions within health systems. These agreements were often mediated by syncretic processes in community settings, particularly in areas affected by armed conflict. Objective: To understand governance experiences during the COVID-19 pandemic in rural and ethnically diverse communities in two municipalities in Colombia. Methods: A qualitative study was conducted using a collaborative autoethnographic approach. Primary data were collected based on the authors’ own experiences to build an interpretive analysis. Data collection took place over one year and included group interviews, reflective journals, and collectively written texts. Results: A key dimension emerged related to the dynamics and lived experiences that shaped decisionmaking processes within and for the communities. These were interpreted through two main axes: the tensions between government-imposed pandemic control measures and the sociocultural and territorial context; and the organizational forms of regulation and governance led by communities and other actors with territorial control. Conclusions: Syncretic forms of governance may contribute to the development of adaptive governmental responses in contexts of crisis and socio-economic and health emergencies","Coronavirus Infections, Armed Conflicts, Health Systems, Governance, Leadership and Governance Capacity (Source: Health Sciences Descriptors - DeCS)",marcadores,durante un ano incluyo entrevista grupal diario reflexivo texto de escritura colectiva,introduction covid-19 pandemic exacerbat pre-exist social economic health cris requir negotiation decision-mak agreement among actor institution within health system these agreement often mediat syncretic process community setting particularly area affect armed conflict objective understand governance experienc during covid-19 pandemic rural ethnically diverse communiti two municipaliti colombia method qualitative study conduct using collaborative autoethnographic approach primary data collect based author own experienc build interpretive analysi data collection took place over one year includ group interview reflective journal collectively written text result key dimension emerg relat dynamic lived experienc shap decisionmak process within communiti these interpret through two main axes tension between government-impos pandemic control measur sociocultural territorial context organizational form regulation governance led communiti other actor territorial control conclusion syncretic form governance may contribute development adaptive governmental respons context crisi socio-economic health emergenci,coronaviru infection armed conflict health system governance leadership governance capacity source health scienc descriptor decs,durante un ano incluyo entrevista grupal diario reflexivo texto de escritura colectiva introduction covid-19 pandemic exacerbat pre-exist social economic health cris requir negotiation decision-mak agreement among actor institution within health system these agreement often mediat syncretic process community setting particularly area affect armed conflict objective understand governance experienc during covid-19 pandemic rural ethnically diverse communiti two municipaliti colombia method qualitative study conduct using collaborative autoethnographic approach primary data collect based author own experienc build interpretive analysi data collection took place over one year includ group interview reflective journal collectively written text result key dimension emerg relat dynamic lived experienc shap decisionmak process within communiti these interpret through two main axes tension between government-impos pandemic control measur sociocultural territorial context organizational form regulation governance led communiti other actor territorial control conclusion syncretic form governance may contribute development adaptive governmental respons context crisi socio-economic health emergenci coronaviru infection armed conflict health system governance leadership governance capacity source health scienc descriptor decs,1.0.0,a3d5a1eb97494b22
2500-6177,5a.pdf,5a_0,es,Patricia Eugenia Molano Builes,"La educación en el campo de la salud pública, biomédica y tradicional limita el carácter libertario y autonómico de una formación crítico-dialógica. Objetivo: comprender las prácticas pedagógicas y la construcción de sujetos críticos en los escenarios formativos de la Mesa por la Salud y la Seguridad Social de Antioquia (Medellín, Colombia) entre los años 2011 y 2018. Metodología: etnografía crítica. Resultados: el hacer común, a través del proceder dialógico como método relacional, dio forma a una praxis pedagógica prefigurativa, una praxis de sí y una praxis social. El hacer de lo diferente un lugar común se configuró como vector agonístico del movimiento popular por la salud. En el ámbito de lo pedagógico-crítico se configuraron subjetividades críticas con dimensiones pedagógicas, éticas, políticas y espirituales. La praxis, como condición de formabilidad, dio lugar a un concepto propio de formación. Conclusiones: la formación crítica, entendida como una forma particular de prefiguración, concreta la dialéctica formación-transformación (praxis de sí - praxis social) en una praxis pedagógica prefigurativa que anticipa en el presente educativo el futuro deseado. La educación en el campo de la salud pública requiere procesos de formación crítica que potencien praxis pedagógicas prefigurativas, capaces de subvertir la relación pedagógica dominante e instituir relaciones dialógicas que, desde la agonía de lo diferente, propicien escenarios pedagógicos críticos orientados a la construcción de una vida saludable (armónica, autónoma y digna) y de mayores niveles de justicia sociosanitaria","pedagogía, formación profesional, salud, organización social, educación",marcadores,patricia eugenia molano buil,educacion campo salud publica biomedica tradicional limita caracter libertario autonomico formacion critico-dialogica objetivo comprender practic pedagogic construccion sujet critic escenari formativ mesa salud seguridad social antioquia medellin colombia entre anos 2011 2018 metodologia etnografia critica resultad hacer comun trav proceder dialogico como metodo relacional dio forma praxis pedagogica prefigurativa praxis si praxis social hacer diferente lugar comun configuro como vector agonistico movimiento popular salud ambito pedagogico-critico configuraron subjetividad critic dimension pedagogic etic politic espiritual praxis como condicion formabilidad dio lugar concepto propio formacion conclusion formacion critica entendida como forma particular prefiguracion concreta dialectica formacion-transformacion praxis si praxis social praxis pedagogica prefigurativa anticipa presente educativo futuro deseado educacion campo salud publica requiere proces formacion critica potencien praxis pedagogic prefigurativ capac subvertir relacion pedagogica dominante instituir relacion dialogic desde agonia diferente propicien escenari pedagogic critic orientad construccion vida saludable armonica autonoma digna mayor nivel justicia sociosanitaria,pedagogia formacion profesional salud organizacion social educacion,patricia eugenia molano buil educacion campo salud publica biomedica tradicional limita caracter libertario autonomico formacion critico-dialogica objetivo comprender practic pedagogic construccion sujet critic escenari formativ mesa salud seguridad social antioquia medellin colombia entre anos 2011 2018 metodologia etnografia critica resultad hacer comun trav proceder dialogico como metodo relacional dio forma praxis pedagogica prefigurativa praxis si praxis social hacer diferente lugar comun configuro como vector agonistico movimiento popular salud ambito pedagogico-critico configuraron subjetividad critic dimension pedagogic etic politic espiritual praxis como condicion formabilidad dio lugar concepto propio formacion conclusion formacion critica entendida como forma particular prefiguracion concreta dialectica formacion-transformacion praxis si praxis social praxis pedagogica prefigurativa anticipa presente educativo futuro deseado educacion campo salud publica requiere proces formacion critica potencien praxis pedagogic prefigurativ capac subvertir relacion pedagogica dominante instituir relacion dialogic desde agonia diferente propicien escenari pedagogic critic orientad construccion vida saludable armonica autonoma digna mayor nivel justicia sociosanitaria pedagogia formacion profesional salud organizacion social educacion,1.0.0,b184118fd1b0e0d9
2500-6177,5a.pdf,5a_0,en,"políticas y espirituales. La praxis, como condición de formabilidad, dio lugar a un concepto propio de formación.","Education in the fields of public, biomedical, and traditional health often constrains the libertarian and autonomous potential of a critical-dialogical training approach. Objective: To understand pedagogical practices and the construction of critical subjectivities within the educational processes of the “Mesa por la Salud y la Seguridad Social de Antioquia” (Medellín, Colombia) between 2011 and 2018. Methods: Critical ethnography. Results: Collective action, grounded in dialogical interaction as a relational method, shaped a prefigurative pedagogical praxis—simultaneously a praxis of the self and a social praxis. The act of making difference a shared space emerged as an agonistic vector of the popular health movement. Within the realm of critical pedagogy, critical subjectivities were shaped, encompassing pedagogical, ethical, political, and spiritual dimensions. Praxis, as a condition for formative potential, gave rise to a distinct concept of education and training. Conclusions: Critical training, understood as a specific form of prefiguration, materializes the dialectic of formation-transformation (praxis of the self - social praxis) in a prefigurative pedagogical praxis that anticipates a desired future within present educational settings. Public health education demands critical training processes that foster prefigurative pedagogical practices capable of subverting dominant pedagogical relationships and establishing dialogical interactions that, through the tension of difference, cultivate critical pedagogical spaces oriented toward the construction of a healthy (harmonious, autonomous, and dignified) life and greater socio-health justice","Pedagogy, Professional training, Health, Social organization, Education",marcadores,politica espiritual la praxi como condicion de formabilidad dio lugar un concepto propio de formacion,education field public biomedical traditional health often constrain libertarian autonomou potential critical-dialogical train approach objective understand pedagogical practic construction critical subjectiviti within educational process mesa por la salud la seguridad social de antioquia medellin colombia between 2011 2018 method critical ethnography result collective action ground dialogical interaction relational method shap prefigurative pedagogical praxis--simultaneously praxi self social praxi act making difference shar space emerg agonistic vector popular health movement within realm critical pedagogy critical subjectiviti shap encompass pedagogical ethical political spiritual dimension praxi condition formative potential gave rise distinct concept education train conclusion critical train understood specific form prefiguration materializ dialectic formation-transformation praxi self social praxi prefigurative pedagogical praxi anticipat desir future within present educational setting public health education demand critical train process foster prefigurative pedagogical practic capable subvert dominant pedagogical relationship establish dialogical interaction through tension difference cultivate critical pedagogical spac orient toward construction healthy harmoniou autonomou dignifi life greater socio-health justice,pedagogy professional train health social organ education,politica espiritual la praxi como condicion de formabilidad dio lugar un concepto propio de formacion education field public biomedical traditional health often constrain libertarian autonomou potential critical-dialogical train approach objective understand pedagogical practic construction critical subjectiviti within educational process mesa por la salud la seguridad social de antioquia medellin colombia between 2011 2018 method critical ethnography result collective action ground dialogical interaction relational method shap prefigurative pedagogical praxis--simultaneously praxi self social praxi act making difference shar space emerg agonistic vector popular health movement within realm critical pedagogy critical subjectiviti shap encompass pedagogical ethical political spiritual dimension praxi condition formative potential gave rise distinct concept education train conclusion critical train understood specific form prefiguration materializ dialectic formation-transformation praxi self social praxi prefigurative pedagogical praxi anticipat desir future within present educational setting public health education demand critical train process foster prefigurative pedagogical practic capable subvert dominant pedagogical relationship establish dialogical interaction through tension difference cultivate critical pedagogical spac orient toward construction healthy harmoniou autonomou dignifi life greater socio-health justice pedagogy professional train health social organ education,1.0.0,ed4b011db3489997
2500-6177,6872842011.pdf,6872842011_0,es,"ta Rica, Costa Rica","Introducción. La pandemia de COVID-19 expuso fragilidades y desigualdades en los sistemas de salud de Iberoamérica, impulsando la necesidad de establecer prioridades de investigación que fortalezcan la resiliencia, la innovación y la equidad en el periodo posterior a la sindemia. Objetivos. Identificar, mediante consenso de expertos, las prioridades de investigación en sistemas y servicios de salud en Iberoamérica tras la sindemia de COVID-19. Metodología. Se realizó un eDelphi modificado entre septiembre de 2022 y marzo de 2023. Se enviaron 228 invitaciones, de las cuales 167 personas aceptaron participar (73,2 %). En la primera ronda, 99 expertos (43,7 %) generaron 164 propuestas, que se agruparon en seis dimensiones. En la segunda ronda, 66 panelistas (39,5 %) evaluaron la importancia de los temas mediante escala Likert (1-5). Finalmente, en la tercera ronda, 66 especialistas (39,5 %) completaron la valoración final. Se consideraron prioritarios los temas puntuados con 4 o 5 por al menos el 70% de los panelistas, se utilizó el rango intercuartílico para medir el nivel de consenso. Resultados. Se identificaron 59 temas prioritarios organizados en seis dimensiones temáticas: (1) modelos organizativos y planificación en crisis sanitarias; (2) respuesta ante amenazas ambientales con enfoque One Health; (3) equidad y ética en asignación de recursos; (4) vigilancia, prevención y control de enfermedades transmisibles y zoonosis; (5) participación ciudadana y pacientes, e (6) innovación y tecnologías en crisis de salud pública. El rango intercuartílico indicó alto consenso sobre la mayoría de los temas. Conclusiones. Este consenso iberoamericano aporta un marco estratégico para orientar la agenda de investigación en sistemas y servicios de salud posteriores a la sindemia. Contribuye a guiar políticas, financiamiento y cooperación internacional, fortaleciendo la resiliencia de los sistemas y promoviendo la equidad regional","COVID-19, investigación en servicios de salud, investigación en sistemas de salud pública, políticas de investigación en salud",marcadores,ta rica costa rica,introduccion pandemia covid-19 expuso fragilidad desigualdad sistem salud iberoamerica impuls necesidad establecer prioridad investigacion fortalezcan resiliencia innovacion equidad periodo posterior sindemia objetiv identificar mediante consenso expert prioridad investigacion sistem servici salud iberoamerica tras sindemia covid-19 metodologia realizo edelphi modificado entre septiembre 2022 marzo 2023 enviaron 228 invit cual 167 person aceptaron participar 73 primera ronda 99 expert 43 generaron 164 propuest agruparon seis dimension segunda ronda 66 panelist 39 evaluaron importancia temas mediante escala likert 1-5 final tercera ronda 66 especialist 39 completaron valoracion final consideraron prioritari temas puntuad menos 70 panelist utilizo rango intercuartilico medir nivel consenso resultad identificaron 59 temas prioritari organizad seis dimension tematic model organizativ planificacion crisis sanitari respuesta ante amenaz ambiental enfoque one health equidad etica asignacion recurs vigilancia prevencion control enfermedad transmisibl zoonosis participacion ciudadana pacient innovacion tecnologi crisis salud publica rango intercuartilico indico alto consenso sobre mayoria temas conclusion este consenso iberoamericano aporta marco estrategico orientar agenda investigacion sistem servici salud posterior sindemia contribuye guiar politic financiamiento cooperacion internacional fortalec resiliencia sistem promov equidad regional,covid-19 investigacion servici salud investigacion sistem salud publica politic investigacion salud,ta rica costa rica introduccion pandemia covid-19 expuso fragilidad desigualdad sistem salud iberoamerica impuls necesidad establecer prioridad investigacion fortalezcan resiliencia innovacion equidad periodo posterior sindemia objetiv identificar mediante consenso expert prioridad investigacion sistem servici salud iberoamerica tras sindemia covid-19 metodologia realizo edelphi modificado entre septiembre 2022 marzo 2023 enviaron 228 invit cual 167 person aceptaron participar 73 primera ronda 99 expert 43 generaron 164 propuest agruparon seis dimension segunda ronda 66 panelist 39 evaluaron importancia temas mediante escala likert 1-5 final tercera ronda 66 especialist 39 completaron valoracion final consideraron prioritari temas puntuad menos 70 panelist utilizo rango intercuartilico medir nivel consenso resultad identificaron 59 temas prioritari organizad seis dimension tematic model organizativ planificacion crisis sanitari respuesta ante amenaz ambiental enfoque one health equidad etica asignacion recurs vigilancia prevencion control enfermedad transmisibl zoonosis participacion ciudadana pacient innovacion tecnologi crisis salud publica rango intercuartilico indico alto consenso sobre mayoria temas conclusion este consenso iberoamericano aporta marco estrategico orientar agenda investigacion sistem servici salud posterior sindemia contribuye guiar politic financiamiento cooperacion internacional fortalec resiliencia sistem promov equidad regional covid-19 investigacion servici salud investigacion sistem salud publica politic investigacion salud,1.0.0,eacb5e490ea5cbf7
2500-6177,6872842011.pdf,6872842011_0,en,1) modelos organizativos y planificación en crisis sanitarias;,"Introduction. The COVID-19 pandemic exposed fragilities and inequities in Ibero-American health systems, underscoring the need to set research priorities that strengthen resilience, innovation, and equity in the post-syndemic period. Objectives. To identify, through expert consensus, research priorities in health systems and services in IberoAmerica after the COVID-19 syndemic. Methods. A modified eDelphi (electronic Delphi) was conducted from September 2022 to March 2023. A total of 228 invitations were issued; 167 individuals agreed to participate (73,2 %). In Round 1, 99 experts (43,7 %) generated 164 proposals, which were grouped into six domains. In Round 2, 66 panelists (39,5 %) rated the importance of topics using a 1-5 Likert scale. In Round 3, 66 specialists (39,5 %) completed the final assessment. Topics were deemed priorities if scored 4 or 5 by at least 70% of panelists; the interquartile range (IQR) was used to quantify consensus. Results. Fifty-nine priority topics were identified and organized into six thematic domains: (1) organizational models and planning for health crises; (2) responses to environmental threats using a One Health approach; (3) equity and ethics in resource allocation; (4) surveillance, prevention, and control of communicable diseases and zoonoses; (5) citizen and patient participation; and (6) innovation and technologies in public health emergencies. The IQR indicated high consensus for most topics. Conclusions. This Ibero-American consensus provides a strategic framework to guide the post-syndemic research agenda in health systems and services. It informs policy, funding, and international cooperation, strengthening systems’ resilience and promoting regional equity","COVID-19, Health Services Research, Public Health Systems Research, Health Research Policy",marcadores,modelo organizativo planificacion en crisi sanitaria,introduction covid-19 pandemic expos fragiliti inequiti ibero-american health system underscor need set research prioriti strengthen resilience innovation equity post-syndemic period objectiv identify through expert consensu research prioriti health system servic iberoamerica after covid-19 syndemic method modifi edelphi electronic delphi conduct september 2022 march 2023 total 228 invit issu 167 individual agre participate 73 round 99 expert 43 generat 164 proposal which group into six domain round 66 panelist 39 rated importance topic using 1-5 likert scale round 66 specialist 39 complet final assessment topic deem prioriti if scor least 70 panelist interquartile range iqr used quantify consensu result fifty-nine priority topic identifi organiz into six thematic domain organizational model plann health cris respons environmental threat using one health approach equity ethic resource allocation surveillance prevention control communicable diseas zoonos citizen patient participation innovation technologi public health emergenci iqr indicat high consensu most topic conclusion ibero-american consensu provid strategic framework guide post-syndemic research agenda health system servic inform policy fund international cooperation strengthen system resilience promot regional equity,covid-19 health servic research public health system research health research policy,modelo organizativo planificacion en crisi sanitaria introduction covid-19 pandemic expos fragiliti inequiti ibero-american health system underscor need set research prioriti strengthen resilience innovation equity post-syndemic period objectiv identify through expert consensu research prioriti health system servic iberoamerica after covid-19 syndemic method modifi edelphi electronic delphi conduct september 2022 march 2023 total 228 invit issu 167 individual agre participate 73 round 99 expert 43 generat 164 proposal which group into six domain round 66 panelist 39 rated importance topic using 1-5 likert scale round