2500-6177,9a1.pdf,9a1_0,en,e diferentes sentidos y acentos en las investigaciones sobre sistemas de,"Objective: To analyze the meanings and emphases of the category of hegemony in the literature on health systems, published in English and Spanish, between 2000 and 2022. Methods: We conducted a narrative review of the literature, in English and Spanish, in PubMed and Scopus, as well as the Google Scholar search engine, which indexes gray literature, for the years 2000-2022. We included studies that explicitly referenced the category hegemony in analyses of health systems, and through analysis of definitions and canonical authors we developed an overall understanding of how the category is construed in the academic literature. We also noted that the category of hegemony arose in the social and political sciences in the early twentieth century, with much of its development linked to Antonio Gramsci. Results: The category of hegemony assumes different meanings and emphases in research on health systems. However, explicit references to definitions or to canonical authors are often lacking. One usage invokes a general notion that multiple hegemonies coexist and intersect; another centers on sociopolitical and historical processes of contestation within health systems over political, intellectual, and moral leadership. Conclusions: The analytical power of the category of hegemony for health systems analysis lies in its focus— beyond legal milestones—on the ethical-political level and on the cultural operation of building persuasion, consensus, or domination. Most studies that employ the category, however, tend to curtail its analytical and explanatory power","Hegemony, Health Systems, Health Policy, Global Health. La categoría hegemonía en la investigación sobre sistemas de salud: una revisión narrativa de literatura entre los años 2000 y 2022*",marcadores,diferent sentido acento en las investigacion sobre sistema de,objective analyze meaning emphas category hegemony literature health system publish english spanish between 2000 2022 method we conduct narrative review literature english spanish pubm scopu well google scholar search engine which index gray literature year 2000-2022 we includ studi explicitly referenc category hegemony analys health system through analysi definition canonical author we develop overall understand how category constru academic literature we also noted category hegemony arose social political scienc early twentieth century much its development link antonio gramsci result category hegemony assum different meaning emphas research health system however explicit referenc definition canonical author often lack one usage invok general notion multiple hegemoni coexist intersect another center sociopolitical historical process contestation within health system over political intellectual moral leadership conclusion analytical power category hegemony health system analysi lies its focus-- beyond legal milestones--on ethical-political level cultural operation build persuasion consensu domination most studi employ category however tend curtail its analytical explanatory power,hegemony health system health policy global health la categoria hegemonia en la investigacion sobre sistema de salud una revision narrativa de literatura entre los anos 2000 2022,diferent sentido acento en las investigacion sobre sistema de objective analyze meaning emphas category hegemony literature health system publish english spanish between 2000 2022 method we conduct narrative review literature english spanish pubm scopu well google scholar search engine which index gray literature year 2000-2022 we includ studi explicitly referenc category hegemony analys health system through analysi definition canonical author we develop overall understand how category constru academic literature we also noted category hegemony arose social political scienc early twentieth century much its development link antonio gramsci result category hegemony assum different meaning emphas research health system however explicit referenc definition canonical author often lack one usage invok general notion multiple hegemoni coexist intersect another center sociopolitical historical process contestation within health system over political intellectual moral leadership conclusion analytical power category hegemony health system analysi lies its focus-- beyond legal milestones--on ethical-political level cultural operation build persuasion consensu domination most studi employ category however tend curtail its analytical explanatory power hegemony health system health policy global health la categoria hegemonia en la investigacion sobre sistema de salud una revision narrativa de literatura entre los anos 2000 2022,1.0.0,458b917cc6358ebd
2500-6517,rip-18300.pdf,rip-18300_0,desconocido,rip-18300,"Psicología Revista Iberoamericana de ISSN-l: 2027-1786 | e-ISSN: 2500-6517 Publicación Cuatrimestral Desigualdad, Violencia de Género y Psicología El presente número especial de la Revista Iberoamericana de Psicología, denominado Desigualdad, Violencia de Género y Psicología, reúne un conjunto de trabajos de investigación que comparten una preocupación común: el abordaje de la desigualdad de género y sus manifestaciones en los distintos ámbitos de la vida, desde una perspectiva psicológica. Esta preocupación no solo pone de relieve un problema social y de salud pública, sino un desafío para la sociedad en su conjunto y, especialmente, para la psicología como ciencia y profesión. En este sentido, la lectura de las investigaciones aquí recogidas invita a reflexionar sobre la necesidad de seguir profundizando en el estudio de esta realidad, muchas veces invisibilizada, a través de distintos enfoques teóricos y metodológicos basados en la evidencia científica. El número especial se alinea con los desafíos globales para el desarrollo sostenible recogidos en la Agenda 2030 (Organización de las Naciones Unidas, 2015), en particular con los Objetivos de Desarrollo Sostenible (ODS) vinculados con la igualdad de género (ODS 5), la salud y el bienestar (ODS 3), la reducción de las desigualdades (ODS 10) y la promoción de sociedades pacíficas, justas e inclusivas (ODS 16). La psicología desempeña un papel esencial en la comprensión de los procesos que perpetúan las desigualdades, en la a",,respaldo_sin_marcadores,rip-18300,psicologia revista iberoamericana issn-l 2027-1786 e-issn 2500-6517 publicacion cuatrimestral desigualdad violencia genero psicologia presente numero especial revista iberoamericana psicologia denominado desigualdad violencia genero psicologia reune conjunto trabaj investigacion comparten preocupacion comun abordaje desigualdad genero sus manifest distint ambit vida desde perspectiva psicologica esta 