2500-6517,rip-18310.pdf,rip-18310_0,en,"levó en 2023, y usó",Purpose: The indicators of domestic violence are higher in people with mental disorders and could further increase the barriers to access to health. The aim of this study was to identify these barriers in people with mental disorders who experience domestic violence. Design/methodology/approach: The search was conducted in 2023 and used the following,"as codes ((Mental Disorders OR Persons with Mental Disabilities) AND (Sex Offenses OR GenderBased Violence OR Domestic Violence)) AND (Barriers to Access to Health Services). Findings: Of the 71 articles included from databases and three from gray literature, 43 referenced barriers to Access to Health Services in people with mental disorders. These barriers are diverse and are influenced by indi",marcadores,levo en 2023 uso,purpose indicator domestic violence higher people mental disorder could further increase barrier acces health aim study identify these barrier people mental disorder who experience domestic violence design methodology approach search conduct 2023 used follow,code mental disorder person mental disabiliti sex offens genderbas violence domestic violence barrier acces health servic finding 71 articl includ databas three gray literature 43 referenc barrier acces health servic people mental disorder these barrier diverse influenc indi,levo en 2023 uso purpose indicator domestic violence higher people mental disorder could further increase barrier acces health aim study identify these barrier people mental disorder who experience domestic violence design methodology approach search conduct 2023 used follow code mental disorder person mental disabiliti sex offens genderbas violence domestic violence barrier acces health servic finding 71 articl includ databas three gray literature 43 referenc barrier acces health servic people mental disorder these barrier diverse influenc indi,1.0.0,d97020d6ba6143ca
2500-7645,1527_stamped.pdf,1527_stamped_0,es,abierto bajo una licencia Creative,"Los conflictos contemporáneos se caracterizan por la expansión del poder y el control territorial mediante complejas redes de intereses políticos, económicos y sociales vinculadas con los mercados transnacionales y las dinámicas de la globalización. Desde una perspectiva cualitati va e interpretativa, sustentada en los estudios críticos de seguridad y el constructivismo, se analizan los conflictos de la Franja de Gaza, la guerra de Rusia en Ucrania, Burkina Faso, Somalia y Sudán. Los resultados muestran que los actores estatales y no estatales recurren a discursos sobre iden tidad, tradición y pertenencia para legitimar la violencia, mientras articulan alianzas e intereses económicos transnacionales. Estas dinámicas afectan gravemente a las poblaciones y debilitan la capacidad institucional de protección. En este contexto, la seguridad se redefine como una cons trucción social que integra dimensiones globales, humanas y ambientales",constructivismo; estudios críticos; globalización; guerra; seguridad,marcadores,abierto bajo licencia creative,conflict contemporane caracterizan expansion poder control territorial mediante complej redes interes politic economic social vinculad mercad transnacional dinamic globalizacion desde perspectiva cualitati va interpretativa sustentada estudi critic seguridad constructivismo analizan conflict franja gaza guerra rusia ucrania burkina faso somalia sudan resultad muestran actor estatal no estatal recurren discurs sobre iden tidad tradicion pertenencia legitimar violencia mientr articulan alianz interes economic transnacional estas dinamic afectan grave pobl debilitan capacidad institucional proteccion este contexto seguridad redefine como cons truccion social integra dimension global human ambiental,constructivismo estudi critic globalizacion guerra seguridad,abierto bajo licencia creative conflict contemporane caracterizan expansion poder control territorial mediante complej redes interes politic economic social vinculad mercad transnacional dinamic globalizacion desde perspectiva cualitati va interpretativa sustentada estudi critic seguridad constructivismo analizan conflict franja gaza guerra rusia ucrania burkina faso somalia sudan resultad muestran actor estatal no estatal recurren discurs sobre iden tidad tradicion pertenencia legitimar violencia mientr articulan alianz interes economic transnacional estas dinamic afectan grave pobl debilitan capacidad institucional proteccion este contexto seguridad redefine como cons truccion social integra dimension global human ambiental constructivismo estudi critic globalizacion guerra seguridad,1.0.0,ab55671a5e725ccf
2500-7645,1527_stamped.pdf,1527_stamped_0,en,"olíticos, económicos y sociales vinculadas con","Contemporary conflicts are characterized by the expansion of power and territorial con trol through complex networks of political, economic, and social interests linked to transnational markets and the dynamics of globalization. From a qualitative and interpretive perspective, grounded in critical security studies and constructivism, this study analyzes the conflicts in the Gaza Strip, Russia’s war in Ukraine, Burkina Faso, Somalia, and Sudan. The results show that state and non-state actors resort to discourses on identity, tradition, and belonging to legitimize violence, while simulta neously forging transnational alliances and economic interests. These dynamics severely affect pop ulations and weaken institutional capacity for protection. In this context, security is redefined as a social construct that integrates global, human, and environmental dimensions","constructivism; critical studies; globalization; security; war Sentidos y valores para una redefinición de la seguridad global: estudio crítico sobre las guerras contemporáneas Meanings and Values for a Redefinition of Global Security: A Critical Study of Contemporary Wars Luz Alejandra Cerón Rincón Universidad de la Salle, Bogotá D.C., Colombia Autor de correspondencia: Luz Alejandra Cerón",marcadores,olitico economico social vinculada con,contemporary conflict characteriz expansion power territorial con trol through complex network political economic social interest link transnational market dynamic global qualitative interpretive perspective ground critical security studi constructivism study analyz conflict gaza strip russia war ukraine burkina faso somalia sudan result show state non-state actor resort discours identity tradition belong legitimize violence while simulta neously forg transnational allianc economic interest these dynamic severely affect pop ulation weaken institutional capacity protection context security redefin social construct integrat global human environmental dimension,constructivism critical studi global security war sentido valor para una redefinicion de la seguridad global estudio critico sobre las guerra contemporanea meaning valu redefinition global security critical study contemporary wars luz alejandra ceron rincon universidad de la salle bogota colombia autor de correspondencia luz alejandra ceron,olitico economico social vinculada con contemporary conflict characteriz expansion power territorial con trol through complex network political economic social interest link transnational market dynamic global qualitative interpretive perspective ground critical security studi constructivism study analyz conflict gaza strip russia war ukraine burkina faso somalia sudan result show state non-state actor resort discours identity tradition belong legitimize violence while simulta neously forg transnational allianc economic interest these dynamic severely affect pop ulation weaken institutional capacity protection context security redefin social construct integrat global human environmental dimension constructivism critical studi global security war sentido valor para una redefinicion de la seguridad global estudio critico sobre las guerra contemporanea meaning valu redefinition global security critical study contemporary wars luz alejandra ceron rincon universidad de la salle bogota colombia autor de correspondencia luz alejandra ceron,1.0.0,0dbef118636aa282
2500-7645,1577_stamped.pdf,1577_stamped_0,es,ción - No Comercial - Sin Derivados.,"Este artículo examina el deterioro de la seguridad en Malí desde 2012 y sus efectos so bre el Sahel, en un contexto marcado por la crisis del enfoque occidental y la creciente presencia de Rusia y China. Su objetivo es analizar cómo la respuesta inicial de Francia, la ONU y la Unión Europea, aunque produjo resultados en el corto plazo, no tuvo los efectos esperados en los años posteriores y fue aprovechada por las juntas militares, respaldadas por Rusia, para responsabilizar a Occidente del avance yihadista. Desde una metodología cualitativa, se revisan fuentes primarias, documentos estratégicos y literatura especializada, y se realizaron entrevistas semiestructuradas. Los resultados muestran que Rusia capitalizó el rechazo a Occidente mediante propaganda y cooperación militar, mientras China priorizó intereses comerciales y extractivos. Se concluye que el binomio seguridad-desarrollo defendido por la Unión Europea sigue siendo pertinente, aunque hoy ocupa un lugar secundario",cooperación internacional; desarrollo económico y social; Sahel; seguridad inter nacional; terrorismo; Unión Europea,marcadores,cion no comercial sin derivad,este articulo examina deterioro seguridad mali desde 2012 sus efect so bre sahel contexto marcado crisis enfoque occidental creciente presencia rusia china objetivo analizar como respuesta inicial francia onu union europea aunque produjo resultad corto plazo no tuvo efect esperad anos posterior fue aprovechada junt militar respaldad rusia responsabilizar occidente avance yihadista desde metodologia cualitativa revisan fuent primari document estrategic literatura especializada realizaron entrevist semiestructurad resultad muestran rusia capitalizo rechazo occidente mediante propaganda cooperacion militar mientr china priorizo interes comercial extractiv concluye binomio seguridad-desarrollo defendido union europea sigue siendo pertinente aunque hoy ocupa lugar secundario,cooperacion internacional desarrollo economico social sahel seguridad inter nacional terrorismo union europea,cion no comercial sin derivad este articulo examina deterioro seguridad mali desde 2012 sus efect so bre sahel contexto marcado crisis enfoque occidental creciente presencia rusia china objetivo analizar como respuesta inicial francia onu union europea aunque produjo resultad corto plazo no tuvo efect esperad anos posterior fue aprovechada junt militar respaldad rusia responsabilizar occidente avance yihadista desde metodologia cualitativa revisan fuent primari document estrategic literatura especializada realizaron entrevist semiestructurad resultad muestran rusia capitalizo rechazo occidente mediante propaganda cooperacion militar mientr china priorizo interes comercial extractiv concluye binomio seguridad-desarrollo defendido union europea sigue siendo pertinente aunque hoy ocupa lugar secundario cooperacion internacional desarrollo economico social sahel seguridad inter nacional terrorismo union europea,1.0.0,d955eb3c7fe98c33
2500-7645,1577_stamped.pdf,1577_stamped_0,en,"la respuesta inicial de Francia, la ONU y la Unión","This article examines the deterioration of security in Mali since 2012 and its effects on the Sahel, within a context marked by the crisis of the Western approach and the growing presence of Russia and China. Its aim is to analyze how the initial response from France, the UN, and the European Union, while producing short-term results, failed to have the expected impact in subsequent years and was exploited by Russian-backed military juntas to blame the West for the jihadist advance. Using a qualitative methodology, primary sources, strategic documents, and specialized literature are re viewed, and semi-structured interviews are conducted. The results show that Russia capitalized on the rejection of the West through propaganda and military cooperation, while China prioritized commer cial and extractive interests. The article concludes that the security-development nexus championed by the European Union remains relevant, although it now occupies a secondary position",economic and social development; European Union; international cooperation; interna tional security; Sahel; terrorism Orden multipolar y seguridad en el Sahel: Malí como epicentro de la crisis del paradigma occidental frente a Rusia y China Multipolar Order and Security in the Sahel: Mali as the Epicenter of the Crisis of the Western Paradigm in the Face of Russia and China Alfredo Crespo Alcáz,marcadores,la respuesta inicial de francia la onu la union,article examin deterioration security mali since 2012 its effect sahel within context mark crisi western approach grow presence russia china its aim analyze how initial response france un european union while produc short-term result fail have expect impact subsequent year exploit russian-back military junta blame west jihadist advance using qualitative methodology primary sourc strategic document specializ literature re view semi-structur interview conduct result show russia capitaliz rejection west through propaganda military cooperation while china prioritiz commer cial extractive interest article conclud security-development nexu champion european union remain relevant although now occupi secondary position,economic social development european union international cooperation interna tional security sahel terrorism orden multipolar seguridad en el sahel mali como epicentro de la crisi del paradigma occidental frente rusia china multipolar order security sahel mali epicenter crisi western paradigm face russia china alfredo crespo alcaz,la respuesta inicial de francia la onu la union article examin deterioration security mali since 2012 its effect sahel within context mark crisi western approach grow presence russia china its aim analyze how initial response france un european union while produc short-term result fail have expect impact subsequent year exploit russian-back military junta blame west jihadist advance using qualitative methodology primary sourc strategic document specializ literature re view semi-structur interview conduct result show russia capitaliz rejection west through propaganda military cooperation while china prioritiz commer cial extractive interest article conclud security-development nexu champion european union remain relevant although now occupi secondary position economic social development european union international cooperation interna tional security sahel terrorism orden multipolar seguridad en el sahel mali como epicentro de la crisi del paradigma occidental frente rusia china multipolar order security sahel mali epicenter crisi western paradigm face russia china alfredo crespo alcaz,1.0.0,fe926982683e31c7
2500-7645,1610_stamped.pdf,1610_stamped_0,en,-Mexico Security Relationship,"This article identifies the factors that have facilitated security cooperation between the United States and Mexico in the past and analyses the factors that have complicated cooperation in recent years. Its purpose is to find possible courses of action to reestablish a functioning bilateral col laboration that contributes to safer societies in both the United States and Mexico. It argues that to find common ground and restore efficient bilateral security collaboration, it is important to institutionalize cooperation mechanisms further and, in the case of Mexico, to address ingrained official corruption; and, in the case of the United States, to address the demand for drugs more decisively",asymmetric interdependence; counternarcotics cooperation; Mérida Initiative; security community; U.S.-Mexico relations,marcadores,-mexico security relationship,article identifi factor have facilitat security cooperation between unit stat mexico past analys factor have complicat cooperation recent year its purpose find possible cours action reestablish function bilateral col laboration contribut safer societi both unit stat mexico argu find common ground restore efficient bilateral security collaboration important institutionalize cooperation mechanism further case mexico addres ingrain official corruption case unit stat addres demand drug more decisively,asymmetric interdependence counternarcotic cooperation merida initiative security community -mexico relation,-mexico security relationship article identifi factor have facilitat security cooperation between unit stat mexico past analys factor have complicat cooperation recent year its purpose find possible cours action reestablish function bilateral col laboration contribut safer societi both unit stat mexico argu find common ground restore efficient bilateral security collaboration important institutionalize cooperation mechanism further case mexico addres ingrain official corruption case unit stat addres demand drug more decisively asymmetric interdependence counternarcotic cooperation merida initiative security community -mexico relation,1.0.0,379e5a9c0fdec525
2500-7645,1610_stamped.pdf,1610_stamped_0,es,ABSTRACT. This article identifies the factors that have facilitated security cooperation between the,"Este articulo identifica los factores que han facilitado la cooperación en materia de seguridad entre Estados Unidos y México en el pasado y analiza los factores que la han complicado en los últimos años. Su propósito es encontrar posibles líneas de acción para restablecer una colaboración bilateral eficaz que contribuya a sociedades más seguras tanto en Estados Unidos como en México. Sostiene que, para encontrar puntos en común y restaurar una colaboración bilateral en materia de seguridad eficiente, es importante institucionalizar aún más los mecanismos de cooperación y, en el caso de México, abordar la corrupción oficial arraigada; y, en el caso de Estados Unidos, abordar la demanda de drogas con mayor determinación","comunidad de seguridad; cooperación en la lucha contra el narcotráfico; Iniciativa Mérida; interdependencia asimétrica; relaciones entre Estados Unidos y México. Corresponding author: Agustín Maciel-Padilla apadilla@ra.ac.ae Received: May 8, 2026 • Accepted: August 8, 2026 RESEARCH ARTICLE Agustin Maciel-Padilla & John Harrison 690 Volume 24 y Issue 55 y pp. 689-714 y July-September 2026 y Bo",marcadores,abstract this article identifi the factors that have facilitated security cooperation between the,este articulo identifica factor han facilitado cooperacion materia seguridad entre estad unid mexico pasado analiza factor han complicado ultim anos proposito encontrar posibl line accion restablecer colaboracion bilateral eficaz contribuya sociedad mas segur tanto estad unid como mexico sostiene encontrar punt comun restaurar colaboracion bilateral materia seguridad eficiente importante institucionalizar aun mas mecanism cooperacion caso mexico abordar corrupcion oficial arraigada caso estad unid abordar demanda drog mayor determinacion,comunidad seguridad cooperacion lucha contra narcotrafico iniciativa mer