2500-8684,19691_16_04_2026_V.30-N.2.pdf,19691_16_04_2026_V.30-N.2_0,en,y analítico mediante una recopilación,"This article examines the regulatory provisions that have shaped land occupation and land-use patterns in the neighbourhood of Villas de Granada (upz 73), located in the Engativá district of Bogotá D. C., and analyses the role of citizen and community participation in decisionmaking processes. Particular attention is given to the formulation of the District’s Territorial Planning Plans (Planes de Ordenamiento Territorial), as well as to the specific planning measures adopted by the Engativá Local Mayor’s Office concerning the upz and the neighbourhood. Adopting a critical human geography perspective grounded in the social construction of space, the study addresses the complex dynamics arising from the interaction of diverse and not always convergent actors, including environmental authorities, public institutions, private sector stakeholders, and community organisations. The research explores how these actors have influenced the configuration of urban regulations and spatial planning in this peripheral urban expansion area. A qualitative methodological approach was employed to investigate the urban issues affecting Villas de Granada. The research adopted a descriptive and analytical framework, based on a comprehensive review of regulatory instruments and planning guidelines impacting the neighbourhood, in order to assess the scope and limitations of citizen participation in territorial planning processes. As a principal finding, the study identifies the underlying causes of dissatisfaction and conflict among community members. Additionally, it analyses a corpus of complaints and formal claims submitted to district authorities between 2016 and 2022","Socio-spatial conflict, spatial justice, urban regulations, planning, Citizen participation, land use, Villas de Granada. Normativas Urbanas e Alcances da Participação Comunitária na Urbanização Villas de Granada, Localidade de Engativá, Bogotá D. C",marcadores,analitico mediante una recopilacion,article examin regulatory provision have shap land occupation land-use pattern neighbourhood villa de granada upz 73 locat engativa district bogota analys role citizen community participation decisionmak process particular attention given formulation district territorial plann plan plan de ordenamiento territorial well specific plann measur adopt engativa local mayor office concern upz neighbourhood adopt critical human geography perspective ground social construction space study address complex dynamic aris interaction diverse not alway convergent actor includ environmental authoriti public institution private sector stakeholder community organis research explor how these actor have influenc configuration urban regul spatial plann peripheral urban expansion area qualitative methodological approach employ investigate urban issu affect villa de granada research adopt descriptive analytical framework based comprehensive review regulatory instrument plann guidelin impact neighbourhood order asses scope limit citizen participation territorial plann process principal find study identifi underly caus dissatisfaction conflict among community member additionally analys corpu complaint formal claim submitt district authoriti between 2016 2022,socio-spatial conflict spatial justice urban regul plann citizen participation land use villa de granada normativa urbana alcanc da participacao comunitaria na urbanizacao villa de granada localidade de engativa bogota,analitico mediante una recopilacion article examin regulatory provision have shap land occupation land-use pattern neighbourhood villa de granada upz 73 locat engativa district bogota analys role citizen community participation decisionmak process particular attention given formulation district territorial plann plan plan de ordenamiento territorial well specific plann measur adopt engativa local mayor office concern upz neighbourhood ad