2500-8684,20594_01_09_2026_V2_DIAG.pdf,20594_01_09_2026_V2_DIAG_0,en,"ón no responde únicamente a decisiones individuales, sino a políticas urbanas que favorecen la concentración socioespacial.","This article analyses residential segregation in Girardot, Colombia, an intermediate city whose urban dynamics reflect processes commonly observed across many Latin American cities. Drawing on a methodological approach that combines statistical and spatial techniques, the study examines a database of 666 georeferenced urban planning licences granted between 2012 and 2022. The use of these data makes it possible to move beyond exclusive reliance on census information and demonstrates how formal urbanisation processes reproduce patterns of socioeconomic differentiation. The findings reveal a marked concentration of housing by socioeconomic stratum, limited interaction among social groups, and the consolidation of clearly defined socioeconomic clusters. Although no direct causal relationship is established between the spatial location of urban planning licences and residential segregation, the study interprets this configuration as an expression of institutional and market dynamics that constrain equitable access to urban land and reproduce social exclusion. The research contributes to debates on urban inequality in intermediate cities by demonstrating that segregation does not arise solely from individual decisions, but is also shaped by urban policies that favour sociospatial concentration. The evidence indicates a trend towards the consolidation of homogeneous residential enclaves and a limited number of spaces characterised by genuine social mixing, thereby reinforcing existing social inequalities. In this regard, the study concludes that segregation in intermediate cities should not be understood as a localised phenomenon, but rather as an expression of structural dynamics of inequality that require public policies oriented towards spatial justice and social inclusion","residential segregation, socioeconomic strata, urban planning licences, statistical analysis. Segregação Residencial a Partir de Licenças Urbanísticas: Análise em uma Cidade Intermediária Colombiana",marcadores,no responde unicamente decision individual sino politica urbana que favorecen la concentracion socioespacial,article analys residential segregation girardot colombia intermediate city whose urban dynamic reflect process commonly observ acros many latin american citi draw methodological approach combin statistical spatial techniqu study examin database 666 georeferenc urban plann licenc grant between 2012 2022 use these data make possible move beyond exclusive reliance censu information demonstrat how formal urbanisation process reproduce pattern socioeconomic differentiation finding reveal mark concentration hous socioeconomic stratum limit interaction among social group consolidation clearly defin socioeconomic cluster although no direct causal relationship establish between spatial location urban plann licenc residential segregation study interpret configuration expression institutional market dynamic constrain equitable acces urban land reproduce social exclusion research contribut debat urban inequality intermediate citi demonstrat segregation does not arise solely individual decision but also shap urban polici favour sociospatial concentration evidence indicat trend toward consolidation homogeneou residential enclav limit number spac characteris genuine social mixing thereby reinforc exist social inequaliti regard study conclud segregation intermediate citi should not understood localis phenomenon but rather expression structural dynamic inequality require public polici orient toward spatial justice social inclusion,residential segregation socioeconomic strata urban plann licenc statistical analysi segregacao residencial partir de licenca urbanistica analise em uma cidade intermediaria colombiana,no responde unicamente decision individual sino politica urbana que favorecen la concentracion socioespacial article analys residential segregation girardot colombia intermediate city whose urban dynamic reflect process commonly observ acros many latin american citi draw methodological approach combin statistical spatial techniqu study examin database 666 georeferenc urban plann licenc grant between 2012 2022 use these data make possible move beyond exclusive reliance censu information demonstrat how formal urbanisation process reproduce pattern socioeconomic differentiation finding reveal mark concentration hous socioeconomic stratum limit interaction among social group consolidation clearly defin socioeconomic cluster although no direct causal relationship establish between spatial location urban plann licenc residential segregation study interpret configuration expression institutional market dynamic constrain equitable acces urban land reproduce social exclusion research contribut debat urban inequality intermediate citi demonstrat segregation does not arise solely individual decision but also shap urban polici favour sociospatial concentration evidence indicat trend toward consolidation homogeneou residential enclav limit number spac characteris genuine social mixing thereby reinforc exist social inequaliti regard study conclud segregation intermediate citi should not understood localis phenomenon but rather expression structural dynamic inequality require public polici orient toward spatial justice social inclusion residential segregation socioeconomic strata urban plann licenc statistical analysi segregacao residencial partir de licenca urbanistica analise em uma cidade intermediaria colombiana,1.0.0,9c3536f18343d389
2500-8684,20967_02_07_2026_V2_DIAG.pdf,20967_02_07_2026_V2_DIAG_0,en,Manek Kolhatkar ,"This paper argues that neither heritage-making nor place-making are adequate for envisioning the political future of La Martre, a little-known but key 10,000-year-old archaeological site located in Gespe’gewa’gi, one of the seven districts of Mi’gma’gi, the Mi’gmaw Ancestral land, and a Quebecois village of about 200 residents. I analyse the archaeological management of the place by considering La Martre as the framework with which to extend our knowledge beyond that permitted by both makings. It appears that despite their recent theoretical developments, heritage- and place-making remain tied to: (i) a colonial and extractive heritage regime structured by Quebec’s heritage law; (ii) a privatized cultural resource management (CRM) archaeology; and (iii) ongoing dispossession that keeps Indigenous communities away from the land base that their cultural systems need. Both makings also conceal other frameworks, such as the Mi’gmaq legal traditions that have been in place in Mi’gma’gi for thousands of years and that emphasize harmony, sharing, deliberation, and treaty renewal, while also being able to produce new normative structures from different world orders (Mi’gmaq and non-Mi’gmaq). I suggest that archaeological residencies could function as an apparatus through which Mi’gmaw law becomes more visible and archaeological practice begins to support a more durable and plural framework for governing the place",archaeological residencies; cultural resource management (CRM) archaeology; heritage-making; place-making; Mi’gmaq legal traditions; grounded normativity; positive criticism; epistemic frictions.  ISSN 0123-3769 eISSN 2500-8684  VOL. 31 [N.º 2]  julio - diciembre de 2026  PP. 1-21 2 Ni patrimonialización ni construcción de lugar: cultivar un lugar mi’gmaq en La Martre,marcadores,manek kolhatkar,paper argu neither heritage-mak nor place-mak adequate envision political future la martre little-known but key 10 000-year-old archaeological site locat gespe gewa gi one seven district mi gma gi mi gmaw ancestral land quebecoi village about 200 resident analyse archaeological management place consider la martre framework which extend our knowledge beyond permitt both making appear despite their recent theoretical development heritage- place-mak remain tied colonial extractive heritage regime structur quebec heritage law ii privatiz cultural resource management crm archaeology iii ongo dispossession keep indigenou communiti away land base their cultural system need both making also conceal other framework such mi gmaq legal tradition have been place mi gma gi thousand year emphasize harmony shar deliberation treaty renewal while also being able produce new normative structur different world order mi gmaq non-mi gmaq suggest archaeological residenci could function apparatu through which mi gmaw law becom more visible archaeological practice begin support more durable plural framework govern place,archaeological residenci cultural resource management crm archaeology heritage-mak place-mak mi gmaq legal tradition ground normativity positive criticism epistemic friction issn 0123-3769 eissn 2500-8684 vol 31 julio diciembre de 2026 pp 1-21 ni patrimonializacion ni construccion de lugar cultivar un lugar mi gmaq en la martre,manek kolhatkar paper argu neither heritage-mak nor place-mak adequate envision political future la martre little-known but key 10 000-year-old archaeological site locat gespe gewa gi one seven district mi gma gi mi gmaw ancestral land quebecoi village about 200 resident analyse archaeological management place consider la martre framework which extend our knowledge beyond permitt both making appear despite their recent theoretical development heritage- place-mak remain tied colonial extractive heritage regime structur quebec heritage law ii privatiz cultural resource management crm archaeology iii ongo dispossession keep indigenou communiti away land base their cultural system need both making also conceal other framework such mi gmaq legal tradition have been place mi gma gi thousand year emphasize harmony shar deliberation treaty renewal while also being able produce new normative structur different world order mi gmaq non-mi gmaq suggest archaeological residenci could function apparatu through which mi gmaw law becom more visible archaeological practice begin support more durable plural framework govern place archaeological residenci cultural resource management crm archaeology heritage-mak place-mak mi gmaq legal tradition ground normativity positive criticism epistemic friction issn 0123-3769 eissn 2500-8684 vol 31 julio diciembre de 2026 pp 1-21 ni patrimonializacion ni construccion de lugar cultivar un lugar mi gmaq en la martre,1.0.0,c3a57fba00bf90f3
2500-8684,20967_02_07_2026_V2_DIAG.pdf,20967_02_07_2026_V2_DIAG_0,es,legal traditions that have been in place in Mi’gma’gi for thousands of years and that emphasize,"Este artículo sostiene que ni la patrimonialización ni la construcción de lugar constituyen marcos adecuados para imaginar el futuro político de La Martre, un sitio arqueológico de aproximadamente 10.000 años de antigüedad, poco conocido pero fundamental, ubicado en Gespe’gewa’gi, uno de los siete distritos de Mi’gma’gi, territorio ancestral mi’gmaq, y en una localidad quebequense de cerca de 200 habitantes. Analizo la gestión arqueológica del sitio considerando a La Martre como un marco conceptual que permite ampliar el conocimiento más allá de los límites impuestos por ambos enfoques. Los resultados muestran que, pese a sus recientes desarrollos teóricos, la patrimonialización y la construcción de lugar continúan: (i) vinculadas a un régimen patrimonial colonial y extractivista estructurado por la legislación patrimonial de Quebec; (ii) subordinadas a una arqueología de gestión de recursos culturales (CRM) privatizada; y (iii) asociadas a procesos continuos de desposesión que mantienen a las comunidades indígenas alejadas de la base territorial requerida para la reproducción de sus sistemas culturales. Asimismo, ambos enfoques invisibilizan otros marcos normativos, como las tradiciones jurídicas mi’gmaq, vigentes en Mi’gma’gi desde hace milenios, que enfatizan la armonía, el compartir, la deliberación y la renovación de tratados, además de generar nuevas estructuras normativas a partir de distintos órdenes de mundo. Se propone que las residencias arqueológicas funcionen como un dispositivo mediante el cual el derecho mi’gmaq adquiera mayor visibilidad y la práctica arqueológica contribuya a un marco más duradero y plural para la gobernanza del lugar",residencias arqueológicas; arqueología de gestión de recursos culturales (CRM); patrimonialización; construcción de lugar; tradiciones jurídicas mi’gmaq; normatividad situada; crítica positiva; fricciones epistémicas. Nem patrimonialização nem construção de lugar: cultivando um lugar mi’gmaq em La Martre,marcadores,legal traditions that have been in place in mi gma gi for thousands of years and that emphasize,este articulo sostiene ni patrimonializacion ni construccion lugar constituyen marc adecuad imaginar futuro politico martre sitio arqueologico aproximada 10 000 anos antiguedad poco conocido pero fundamental ubicado gespe gewa gi uno siete distrit mi gma gi territorio ancestral mi gmaq localidad quebequense cerca 200 habitant analizo gestion arqueologica sitio consider martre como marco conceptual permite ampliar conocimiento mas alla limit impuest ambos enfoqu resultad muestran pese sus recient desarroll teoric patrimonializacion construccion lugar continuan vinculad regimen patrimonial colonial extractivista estructurado legislacion patrimonial quebec ii subordinad arqueologia gestion recurs cultural crm privatizada iii asociad proces continu desposesion mantienen comunidad indigen alejad base territorial requerida reproduccion sus sistem cultural asimismo ambos enfoqu invisibilizan otros marc normativ como tradicion juridic mi gmaq vigent mi gma gi desde hace mileni enfatizan armonia compartir deliberacion renovacion tratad adem generar nuev estructur normativ partir distint orden mundo propone residenci arqueologic funcionen como dispositivo mediante cual derecho mi gmaq adquiera mayor visibilidad practica arqueologica contribuya marco mas duradero plural gobernanza lugar,residenci arqueologic arqueologia gestion recurs cultural crm patrimonializacion construccion lugar tradicion juridic mi gmaq normatividad situada critica positiva friccion epistemic nem patrimonializacao nem construcao lugar cultiv um lugar mi gmaq em martre,legal traditions that have been in place in mi gma gi for thousands of years and that emphasize este articulo sostiene ni patrimonializacion ni construccion lugar constituyen marc adecuad imaginar futuro politico martre sitio arqueologico aproximada 10 000 anos antiguedad poco conocido pero fundamental ubicado gespe gewa gi uno siete distrit mi gma gi territorio ancestral mi gmaq localidad quebequense cerca 200 habitant analizo gestion arqueologica sitio consider martre como marco conceptual permite ampliar conocimiento mas alla limit impuest ambos enfoqu resultad muestran pese sus recient desarroll teoric patrimonializacion construccion lugar continuan vinculad regimen patrimonial colonial extractivista estructurado legislacion patrimonial quebec ii subordinad arqueologia gestion recurs cultural crm privatizada iii asociad proces continu desposesion mantienen comunidad indigen alejad base territorial requerida reproduccion sus sistem cultural asimismo ambos enfoqu invisibilizan otros marc normativ como tradicion juridic mi gmaq vigent mi gma gi desde hace mileni enfatizan armonia compartir deliberacion renovacion tratad adem generar nuev estructur normativ partir distint orden mundo propone residenci arqueologic funcionen como dispositivo mediante cual derecho mi gmaq adquiera mayor visibilidad practica arqueologica contribuya marco mas duradero plural gobernanza lugar residenci arqueologic arqueologia gestion recurs cultural crm patrimonializacion construccion lugar tradicion juridic mi gmaq normatividad situada critica positiva friccion epistemic nem patrimonializacao nem construcao lugar cultiv um lugar mi gmaq em martre,1.0.0,931bcf6cc0dcb59f
2500-8692,NOVUM+JUS+20-2+art+1+DERECHO+INTERNACIONAL.pdf,NOVUM+JUS+20-2+art+1+DERECHO+INTERNACIONAL_0,es,El derecho internacional humanitario,"La creciente urbanización de los conflictos armados ha generado la necesidad de revaluación de las herramientas de protección de las víctimas civiles, entre las que destaca el principio de proporcionalidad. Ello se debe a que la utilización del entorno urbano como espacio de batalla genera obstáculos en la aplicabilidad del principio de distinción, lo que aumenta la importancia del principio de proporcionalidad como segundo escalón en la determinación del cumplimiento de la normativa humanitaria y como herramienta para reducir los daños colaterales civiles derivados de un determinado ataque. El presente artículo pretende, a través de una metodología cualitativa, conceptualizar el principio de proporcionalidad y evaluar su eficacia en contextos de conflictos armados desarrollados en áreas densamente pobladas. Posteriormente, a través de la triangulación de datos, se identifican los elementos fundamentales presentes en el examen de proporcionalidad, con la finalidad de poder identificar los problemas a los que se enfrenta este principio en la práctica actual. Este análisis constata la necesidad de adaptar y articular un marco protector adecuado frente a los desafíos de los conflictos armados actuales","Principio de proporcionalidad; urbanización; Derecho Internacional Humanitario; necesidad militar; humanidad; daño colateral. https://doi.org/10.14718/NovumJus.2026.20.2.1. * Graduada en Derecho por la Universidad de Salamanca. Magíster en Estudios de la Unión Europea en la misma institución, con el reconocimiento del Premio Extraordinario de promoción. Actualmente, personal docente e investi",marcadores,derecho internacional humanitario,creciente urbanizacion conflict armad ha generado necesidad revaluacion herramient proteccion victim civil entre destaca principio proporcionalidad ello debe utilizacion entorno urbano como espacio batalla genera obstacul aplicabilidad principio distincion aumenta importancia principio proporcionalidad como segundo escalon determinacion cumplimiento normativa humanitaria como herramienta reducir danos colateral civil derivad determinado ataque presente articulo pretende trav metodologia cualitativa conceptualizar principio proporcionalidad evaluar eficacia context conflict armad desarrollad areas densa poblad posterior trav triangulacion datos identifican element fundamental present examen proporcionalidad finalidad poder identificar problem enfrenta este principio practica actual este analisis constata necesidad adaptar articular marco protector adecuado frente desafi conflict armad actual,principio proporcionalidad urbanizacion derecho internacional humanitario necesidad militar humanidad dano colateral https doi org 10 14718 novumjus 2026 20 graduada derecho universidad salamanca magister estudi union europea misma institucion reconocimiento premio extraordinario promocion actual personal docente investi,derecho internacional humanitario creciente urbanizacion conflict armad ha generado necesidad revaluacion herramient proteccion victim civil entre destaca principio proporcionalidad ello debe utilizacion entorno urbano como espacio batalla genera obstacul aplicabilidad principio distincion aumenta importancia principio proporcionalidad como segundo escalon determinacion cumplimiento normativa humanitaria como herramienta reducir danos colateral civil derivad determinado ataque presente articulo pretende trav metodologia cualitativa conceptualizar principio proporcionalidad evaluar eficacia context conflict armad desarrollad areas densa poblad posterior trav triangulacion datos identifican element fundamental present examen proporcionalidad finalidad poder identificar problem enfrenta este principio practica actual este analisis constata necesidad adaptar articular marco protector adecuado frente desafi conflict armad actual principio proporcionalidad urbanizacion derecho internacional humanitario necesidad militar humanidad dano colateral https doi org 10 14718 novumjus 2026 20 graduada derecho universidad salamanca magister estudi union europea misma institucion reconocimiento premio extraordinario promocion actual personal docente investi,1.0.0,bb2c833e16337ebe
2500-8692,NOVUM+JUS+20-2+art+1+DERECHO+INTERNACIONAL.pdf,NOVUM+JUS+20-2+art+1+DERECHO+INTERNACIONAL_0,en,alabras clave: Principio de proporcionalidad; urbanización; Derecho Internacional Humanitario; necesidad,"The increasing urbanization of armed conflicts has created the need to reassess the tools available for the protection of civilian victims, among which the principle of proportionality is particularly significant. This is because the use of urban environments as battlefields creates obstacles to the application of the principle of distinction, thereby increasing the importance of the principle of proportionality as a second level of assessment in determining compliance with international humanitarian law and as a means of reducing civilian collateral damage resulting from a given attack. Using a qualitative methodology, this article seeks to conceptualize the principle of proportionality and assess its effectiveness in the context of armed conflicts conducted in densely populated areas. Subsequently, through data triangulation, it identifies the fundamental elements involved in the proportionality assessment in order to identify the challenges that this principle faces in current practice. This analysis confirms the need to adapt and articulate an appropriate protective framework to address the challenges posed by contemporary armed conflicts",principle of proportionality; urbanization; international humanitarian law; military necessity; humanity; collateral damage https://doi.org/10.14718/NovumJus.2026.20.2.1. El derecho internacional humanitario al filo del equilibrio: el principio de proporcionalidad 25 NOVUM JUS • ISSN: 1692-6013 • E-ISSN: 2500-8692 • Volumen 20 No. 2 • mayo-agosto 2026 • Págs. 23-49 Antecedentes históricos del pr,marcadores,alabra clave principio de proporcionalidad urbanizacion derecho internacional humanitario necesidad,increas urban armed conflict has creat need reasses tool available protection civilian victim among which principle proportionality particularly significant because use urban environment battlefield creat obstacl application principle distinction thereby increas importance principle proportionality second level assessment determin compliance international humanitarian law mean reduc civilian collateral damage result given attack using qualitative methodology article seek conceptualize principle proportionality asses its effectivenes context armed conflict conduct densely populat area subsequently through data triangulation identifi fundamental element involv proportionality assessment order identify challeng principle face current practice analysi confirm need adapt articulate appropriate protective framework addres challeng posed contemporary armed conflict,principle proportionality urban international humanitarian law military necessity humanity collateral damage http doi org 10 14718 novumju 2026 20 el derecho internacional humanitario al filo del equilibrio el principio de proporcionalidad 25 novum jus issn 1692-6013 e-issn 2500-8692 volumen 20 no mayo-agosto 2026 pags 23-49 antecedent historico del pr,alabra clave principio de proporcionalidad urbanizacion derecho internacional humanitario necesidad increas urban armed conflict has creat need reasses tool available protection civilian victim among which principle proportionality particularly significant because use urban environment battlefield creat obstacl application principle distinction thereby increas importance principle proportionality second level assessment determin compliance international humanitarian law mean reduc civilian collateral damage result given attack using qualitative methodology article seek conceptualize principle proportionality asses its effectivenes context armed conflict conduct densely populat area subsequently through data triangulation identifi fundamental element involv proportionality assessment order identify challeng principle face current practice analysi confirm need adapt articulate appropriate protective framework addres challeng posed contemporary armed conflict principle proportionality urban international humanitarian law military necessity humanity collateral damage http doi org 10 14718 novumju 2026 20 el derecho internacional humanitario al filo del equilibrio el principio de proporcionalidad 25 novum jus issn 1692-6013 e-issn 2500-8692 volumen 20 no mayo-agosto 2026 pags 23-49 antecedent historico del pr,1.0.0,dbf6b24c904cfb90
2500-8692,NOVUM+JUS+20-2+art+10+CURRENT.pdf,NOVUM+JUS+20-2+art+10+CURRENT_0,en,he Territory of Ukraine,"Throughout the 20th century, international humanitarian law (IHL) underwent significant evolution in combating crimes against peace (aggression), crimes against humanity, war crimes, and genocide. The armed aggression of the Russian Federation against Ukraine has led to the temporary occupation of about 20% of the internationally recognized territory of Ukraine (as of 2025), which is accompanied by large-scale violations of human rights and the commission of war crimes. In the context of active hostilities, the absence of legal jurisdiction and the inability of the law enforcement system to function in the occupied territories have created a legal vacuum that complicates the effective investigation of crimes. This poses serious challenges in bringing war criminals to justice, taking into account the norms of IHL, inter-state cooperation, and the use of modern digital forensic technologies. Methodologically, the study employs an interdisciplinary approach that combines content analysis, historical and legal methods, case studies, and legal modeling. Materials and judicial practice of international tribunals, including the ICC, are studied. In this case, particular attention should be paid to the use of artificial intelligence, satellite analytics, 3D modeling, OSINT, and remote collection of digital evidence. Based on international experience and lessons learned from other armed conflicts, the article offers practical recommendations aimed at improving investigation methods and mechanisms for bringing to justice those guilty of committing war crimes. Practical examples of integrating such tools into the investigation process are also considered, in particular, the use of virtual modeling by the Bavarian police. The evolution of IHL in the context of state responsibility, as well as the legal assessment of crimes committed in occupied territories, is also analyzed",war crimes; armed conflict; combatant; genocide; ecocide; occupied territories; digital evidence; artificial intelligence. https://doi.org/10.14718/NovumJus.2026.20.2.10 * Doctor of Law. Candidate of Philosophy. Professor. Government Commissioner for Gender Policy. Email: levchenkokateryna@yahoo.com. ORCID: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8334-7362 ** Doctor of Law. Associate Professor. First Vic,marcadores,he territory ukraine,throughout 20th century international humanitarian law ihl underwent significant evolution combat crim against peace aggression crim against humanity war crim genocide armed aggression russian federation against ukraine has led temporary occupation about 20 internationally recogniz territory ukraine 2025 which accompani large-scale viol human right commission war crim context active hostiliti absence legal jurisdiction inability law enforcement system function occupi territori have creat legal vacuum complicat effective investigation crim pose seriou challeng bring war criminal justice taking into account norm ihl inter-state cooperation use modern digital forensic technologi methodologically study employ interdisciplinary approach combin content analysi historical legal method case studi legal model material judicial practice international tribunal includ icc studi case particular attention should paid use artificial intelligence satellite analytic 3d model osint remote collection digital evidence based international experience lesson learn other armed conflict article offer practical recommend aimed improv investigation method mechanism bring justice those guilty committ war crim practical exampl integrat such tool into investigation proces also consider particular use virtual model bavarian police evolution ihl context state responsibility well legal assessment crim committ occupi territori also analyz,war crim armed conflict combatant genocide ecocide occupi territori digital evidence artificial intelligence http doi org 10 14718 novumju 2026 20 10 doctor law candidate philosophy professor government commissioner gender policy email levchenkokateryna yahoo com orcid http orcid org 0000-0002-8334-7362 doctor law associate professor first vic,he territory ukraine throughout 20th century international humanitarian law ihl underwent significant evolution combat crim against peace aggression crim against humanity war crim genocide armed aggression russian federation against ukraine has led temporary occupation about 20 internationally recogniz territory ukraine 2025 which accompani large-scale viol human right commission war crim context active hostiliti absence legal jurisdiction inability law enforcement system function occupi territori have creat legal vacuum complicat effective investigation crim pose seriou challeng bring war criminal justice taking into account norm ihl inter-state cooperation use modern digital forensic technologi methodologically study employ interdisciplinary approach combin content analysi historical legal method case studi legal model material judicial practice international tribunal includ icc studi case particular attention should paid use artificial intelligence satellite analytic 3d model osint remote collection digital evidence based international experience lesson learn other armed conflict article offer practical recommend aimed improv investigation method mechanism bring justice those guilty committ war crim practical exampl integrat such tool into investigation proces also consider particular use virtual model bavarian police evolution ihl context state responsibility well legal assessment crim committ occupi territori also analyz war crim armed conflict combatant genocide ecocide occupi territori digital evidence artificial intelligence http doi org 10 14718 novumju 2026 20 10 doctor law candidate philosophy professor government commissioner gender policy email levchenkokateryna yahoo com orcid http orcid org 0000-0002-8334-7362 doctor law associate professor first vic,1.0.0,5a0320caa010cec0
2500-8692,NOVUM+JUS+20-2+art+10+CURRENT.pdf,NOVUM+JUS+20-2+art+10+CURRENT_0,es,"PhD in Law, Associate Professor of the Department of Law Enforcement and Anti-Corruption Activities, Interregional","A lo largo del siglo XX, el derecho internacional humanitario (DIH) experimentó una evolución importante en la lucha contra los crímenes contra la paz (agresión), los crímenes contra la humanidad, los crímenes de guerra y el genocidio. La agresión armada de la Federación de Rusia contra Ucrania ha dado lugar a la ocupación temporal de aproximadamente el 20 % del territorio internacionalmente reconocido de Ucrania (al año 2025), lo que ha estado acompañado de violaciones a gran escala de los derechos humanos y de la comisión de crímenes de guerra. En el contexto de las hostilidades activas, la ausencia de jurisdicción legal y la incapacidad del sistema de aplicación de la ley para operar en los territorios ocupados han generado un vacío legal que dificulta la investigación eficaz de los delitos cometidos. Esto plantea serios retos para llevar ante la justicia a los criminales de guerra, teniendo en cuenta las normas del DIH, la cooperación interestatal y el uso de tecnologías forenses digitales avanzadas. Desde el punto de vista metodológico, el estudio se basa en un enfoque interdisciplinario que combina el análisis de contenidos, métodos históricos y jurídicos, estudios de casos y modelos jurídicos. Se estudian los materiales y la práctica judicial de los tribunales internacionales y de la CPI. En este caso, se debe prestar especial atención al uso de la inteligencia artificial, al análisis satelital, al modelado 3D, a la OSINT y a la recopilación remota de pruebas digitales. Con base en la experiencia internacional y en las lecciones aprendidas de otros conflictos armados, el artículo ofrece recomendaciones prácticas para mejorar los métodos y mecanismos de investigación destinados a llevar ante la justicia a los responsables de crímenes de guerra. También se examinan ejemplos prácticos de integración de estas herramientas en el proceso de investigación, en particular, el uso de modelos virtuales por parte de la policía bávara. También se analiza la evolución del DIH en el contexto de la responsabilidad del Estado y de la evaluación jurídica de los crímenes cometidos en territorios ocupados",crímenes de guerra; conflicto armado; combatiente; genocidio; ecocidio; territorios ocupados; pruebas digitales; inteligencia artificial. https://doi.org/10.14718/NovumJus.2026.20.2.10 293 Current Realities of Investigation and the Possibility of Bringing to Justice Those Guilty of Committing War Crimes... NOVUM JUS • ISSN: 1692-6013 • E-ISSN: 2500-8692 • Volumen 20 No. 2 • mayo-agosto 2026 • Pá,marcadores,phd in law associate professor of the department of law enforcement and anti-corruption activiti interregional,largo siglo xx derecho internacional humanitario dih experimento evolucion importante lucha contra crimen contra paz agresion crimen contra humanidad crimen guerra genocidio agresion armada federacion rusia contra ucrania ha dado lugar ocupacion temporal aproximada 20 territorio internacional reconocido ucrania ano 2025 ha estado acompanado viol gran escala derech human comision crimen guerra contexto hostilidad activ ausencia jurisdiccion legal incapacidad sistema aplicacion ley operar territori ocupad han generado vacio legal dificulta investigacion eficaz delit cometid esto plantea seri retos llevar ante justicia criminal guerra teniendo cuenta norm dih cooperacion interestatal uso tecnologi forens digital avanzad desde punto vista metodologico estudio basa enfoque interdisciplinario combina analisis contenid metod historic juridic estudi casos model juridic estudian material practica judicial tribunal internacional cpi este caso debe prestar especial atencion uso inteligencia artificial analisis satelital modelado 3d osint recopilacion remota prueb digital base experiencia internacional leccion aprendid otros conflict armad articulo ofrece recomend practic mejorar metod mecanism investigacion destinad llevar ante justicia responsabl crimen guerra tambien examinan ejempl practic integracion estas herramient proceso investigacion particular uso model virtual parte policia bavara tambien analiza evolucion dih contexto responsabilidad estado evaluacion juridica crimen cometid territori ocupad,crimen guerra conflicto armado combatiente genocidio ecocidio territori ocupad prueb digital inteligencia artificial https doi org 10 14718 novumjus 2026 20 10 293 current realiti of investigation and the possibility of bringing to justice those guilty of committing war crim novum jus issn 1692-6013 e-issn 2500-8692 volumen 20 no mayo-agosto 2026 pa,phd in law associate professor of the department of law enforcement and anti-corruption activiti interregional largo siglo xx derecho internacional humanitario dih experimento evolucion importante lucha contra crimen contra paz agresion crimen contra humanidad crimen guerra genocidio agresion armada federacion rusia contra ucrania ha dado lugar ocupacion temporal aproximada 20 territorio internacional reconocido ucrania ano 2025 ha estado acompanado viol gran escala derech human comision crimen guerra contexto hostilidad activ ausencia jurisdiccion legal incapacidad sistema aplicacion ley operar territori ocupad han generado vacio legal dificulta investigacion eficaz delit cometid esto plantea seri retos llevar ante justicia criminal guerra teniendo cuenta norm dih cooperacion interestatal uso tecnologi forens digital avanzad desde punto vista metodologico estudio basa enfoque interdisciplinario combina analisis contenid metod historic juridic estudi casos model juridic estudian material practica judicial tribunal internacional cpi este caso debe prestar especial atencion uso inteligencia artificial analisis satelital modelado 3d osint recopilacion remota prueb digital base experiencia internacional leccion aprendid otros conflict armad articulo ofrece recomend