ps orcid org 0000-0001-6562-1930 scopus id 57223086456 dra maria lorena rossel castagneto facultad derecho universid,1.0.0,86eaa2219f4bc7aa
2500-8692,NOVUM+JUS+20-2+art+11+DEMOCRACIA.pdf,NOVUM+JUS+20-2+art+11+DEMOCRACIA_0,en,Palabras clave: democracia; desinformación; inteligencia artificial; polarización; regulación; discursos de odio.,"This study examines the complex relationship between artificial intelligence, disinformation, and hate speech, all of which have become crucial factors in recent electoral campaigns across Latin America. Indeed, in political processes such as those in Brazil, Colombia, Ecuador, and Chile, the dissemination of fake news and aggressive narratives has become a common political tool. Moreover, several of these cases have involved highly specific techniques, including the use of bots, astroturfing, and deepfakes, all of which distort public debate and undermine fairness in electoral competition. The research combines documentary review and a comparative analysis of national experiences to assess how digital manipulation intensifies polarization and erodes public trust in institutions. Based on these findings, it proposes measures to guide regulation and education, with the aim of enabling States to address the challenges of the digital age without compromising fundamental rights or the protection of democracy","democracy; disinformation; artificial intelligence; polarization; regulation; hate speech. https://doi.org/10.14718/NovumJus.2026.20.2.11 317 Democracia en riesgo: IA, desinformación y discursos de odio en los procesos políticos latinoamericanos NOVUM JUS • ISSN: 1692-6013 • E-ISSN: 2500-8692 • Volumen 20 No. 2 • mayo-agosto 2026 • Págs. 315-340",marcadores,palabra clave democracia desinformacion inteligencia artificial polarizacion regulacion discurso de odio,study examin complex relationship between artificial intelligence disinformation hate speech all which have become crucial factor recent electoral campaign acros latin america inde political process such those brazil colombia ecuador chile dissemination fake news aggressive narrativ has become common political tool moreover several these case have involv highly specific techniqu includ use bots astroturf deepfak all which distort public debate undermine fairnes electoral competition research combin documentary review comparative analysi national experienc asses how digital manipulation intensifi polar erod public trust institution based these finding propos measur guide regulation education aim enabl stat addres challeng digital age without compromis fundamental right protection democracy,democracy disinformation artificial intelligence polar regulation hate speech http doi org 10 14718 novumju 2026 20 11 317 democracia en riesgo ia desinformacion discurso de odio en los proceso politico latinoamericano novum jus issn 1692-6013 e-issn 2500-8692 volumen 20 no mayo-agosto 2026 pags 315-340,palabra clave democracia desinformacion inteligencia artificial polarizacion regulacion discurso de odio study examin complex relationship between artificial intelligence disinformation hate speech all which have become crucial factor recent electoral campaign acros latin america inde political process such those brazil colombia ecuador chile dissemination fake news aggressive narrativ has become common political tool moreover several these case have involv highly specific techniqu includ use bots astroturf deepfak all which distort public debate undermine fairnes electoral competition research combin documentary review comparative analysi national experienc asses how digital manipulation intensifi polar erod public trust institution based these finding propos measur guide regulation education aim enabl stat addres challeng digital age without compromis fundamental right protection democracy democracy disinformation artificial intelligence polar regulation hate speech http doi org 10 14718 novumju 2026 20 11 317 democracia en riesgo ia desinformacion discurso de odio en los proceso politico latinoamericano novum jus issn 1692-6013 e-issn 2500-8692 volumen 20 no mayo-agosto 2026 pags 315-34