andscape geopolitical military allianc dominate world order shift focu present study methodologically article develop qualitative case study based documentary interpretative review specializ academic doctrinal institutional journalistic sourc analysi guid analogical hermeneutic which enabl interpretation historical geopolitical strategic evolution russo-ukrainian relation well transformation so-call special military operation into hybrid war central thesi center gravity war no longer locat exclusively within ukrainian theater oper but has shift toward west due six factor study conclud shift increas complexity conflict prolong its global effect redefin strategic condition its conclusion center gravity hybrid warfare west special military operation new world order http doi org 10 14718 novumju 2026 20 141 el desplazamiento del centro de gravedad de la guerra ruso-ucraniana de cara al futuro novum jus issn 1692-6013 e-issn 2500-8692 volumen 20 no mayo-agosto 2026 pags 139-168,1.0.0,7445c3699a80b621
2500-8692,NOVUM+JUS+20-2+art+6+THE+ENVIRONMENTAL.pdf,NOVUM+JUS+20-2+art+6+THE+ENVIRONMENTAL_0,en,Luciana Lara de Carvalho /,"This article examines the process of regulatory consolidation to protect the Cerrado in Brazil, linking the scientific development of the biome concept to the formation of the legal-environmental framework. The qualitative, exploratory research is based on a bibliographic and documentary analysis of the works of authors in ecology and environmental law. It begins by noting that although Brazil has comprehensive environmental legislation, the effectiveness of regulations governing the Cerrado is limited by institutional, economic, and epistemological factors. The article highlights a lack of understanding among legal professionals of the scientific and ecological foundations that define the biome. This conceptual gap hampers the proper application of environmental regulations and undermines ecological protection. The article emphasizes the need for greater integration between science and legal practice, so that ecological knowledge informs legal interpretation and environmental governance. It concludes that the adequate protection of the Cerrado requires an interdisciplinary approach and legally grounded environmental education to transform the regulatory framework into an accurate tool for conservation and sustainability","Cerrado, Brazilian biomes, environmental law, political ecology, regulatory effectiveness. https://doi.org/10.14718/NovumJus.2026.20.2.6 * MSc in Environmental Sciences (Evangelical University of Goiás), environmental lawyer at the law firm Luciana Carvalho Advocacia Ambiental, Goiânia, Brazil. Email: lucianalcarvalhoadv@gmail.com ORCID: https://orcid. org/0009-0005-3136-9999. ** PhD in Relig",marcadores,luciana lara de carvalho,article examin proces regulatory consolidation protect cerrado brazil link scientific development biome concept formation legal-environmental framework qualitative exploratory research based bibliographic documentary analysi work author ecology environmental law begin noting although brazil has comprehensive environmental legislation effectivenes regul govern cerrado limit institutional economic epistemological factor article highlight lack understand among legal professional scientific ecological found define biome conceptual gap hamper proper application environmental regul undermin ecological protection article emphasiz need greater integration between science legal practice so ecological knowledge inform legal interpretation environmental governance conclud adequate protection cerrado requir interdisciplinary approach legally ground environmental education transform regulatory framework into accurate tool conservation sustainability,cerrado brazilian biom environmental law political ecology regulatory effectivenes http doi org 10 14718 novumju 2026 20 msc environmental scienc evangelical university goia environmental lawyer law firm luciana carvalho advocacia ambiental goiania brazil email lucianalcarvalhoadv gmail com orcid http orcid org 0009-0005-3136-9999 phd relig,luciana lara de carvalho article examin proces regulatory consolidation protect cerrado brazil link scientific development biome concept formation legal-environmental framework qualitative exploratory research based bibliographic documentary analysi work author ecology environmental law begin noting although brazil has comprehensive environmental legislation effectivenes regul govern cerrado limit institutional economic epistemological factor article highlight lack understand among legal professional scientific ecological found define biome conceptual gap hamper proper application environmental regul undermin ecological protection article emphasiz need greater integration between science legal practice so ecological knowledge inform legal interpretation environmental governance conclud adequate protection cerrado requir interdisciplinary approach legally ground environmental education transform regulatory framework into accurate tool conservation sustainability cerrado brazilian biom environmental law political ecology regulatory effectivenes http doi org 10 14718 novumju 2026 20 msc environmental scienc evangelical university goia environmental lawyer law firm luciana carvalho advocacia ambiental goiania brazil email lucianalcarvalhoadv gmail com orcid http orcid org 0009-0005-3136-9999 phd relig,1.0.0,de8102c98c8610c5
2500-8692,NOVUM+JUS+20-2+art+6+THE+ENVIRONMENTAL.pdf,NOVUM+JUS+20-2+art+6+THE+ENVIRONMENTAL_0,es,"idade de São Paulo), professor and researcher at the Universidade Evangélica de Goiás,","Este artículo examina el proceso de consolidación normativa para la protección del Cerrado en Brasil, vinculando el desarrollo científico del concepto de bioma con la formación del marco jurídico-ambiental. La investigación cualitativa y exploratoria se basa en un análisis bibliográfico y documental de autores de las áreas de la ecología y del derecho ambiental. Se parte de la observación de que, si bien Brasil cuenta con una legislación ambiental integral, la eficacia de las normas dirigidas al Cerrado se ve limitada por factores institucionales, económicos y epistemológicos. El artículo destaca la insuficiente comprensión por parte de los profesionales del derecho de los fundamentos científicos y ecológicos que definen el bioma, ya que dicha brecha conceptual dificulta la aplicación adecuada de las normas ambientales y perjudica la protección del medio ambiente. El artículo enfatiza la necesidad de una mayor integración entre la ciencia y la práctica jurídica para que el conocimiento ecológico influya en la interpretación jurídica y en la gobernanza ambiental. Se concluye que la adecuada protección del Cerrado requiere un enfoque interdisciplinario y una educación ambiental con fundamento jurídico, a fin de transformar el marco regulatorio en un instrumento eficaz para la conservación y la sostenibilidad","Cerrado, biomas brasileños, derecho ambiental, ecología política, efectividad normativa. https://doi.org/10.14718/NovumJus.2026.20.2.6 The Environmental Crossroads: Ecological Concepts, Regulations, and the Challenges of Protecting the Brazilian Cerrado 171 NOVUM JUS • ISSN: 1692-6013 • E-ISSN: 2500-8692 • Volumen 20 No. 2 • mayo-agosto 2026 • Págs. 169-200",marcadores,idade sao paulo professor and researcher at the universidade evangelica goias,este articulo examina proceso con