2538-9866,v49n2e359625Final.pdf,v49n2e359625Final_0,en,ção da desinformação nas eleições brasileiras,"This study analyzes the similarities between disinformation produced in the 2022 elections and on the eve of the 2026 elections. The objective is to understand how narratives are structured to manipulate events related to electoral processes in both periods. To achieve this, a Descending Hierarchical Classification (DHC) was performed using the Iramuteq software. The analyzed sample encompasses disinformation verified by Lupa Agency and consists of cross-referencing textual data from October 1 to December 31, 2022, and March 20, 2025, and 2026. The results indicate that disinformation has a chain production system based on historical events involving coups d'état, fostering doubts about the legitimacy of the electoral process, rumors of voter fraud, and narratives of military intervention. They also point out that the criteria for voter preference are based on an ideological war that threatens the democratic rule of law and the critical participation of citizens in electoral processes","disinformation; 2022 elections; 2026 elections; coup d'état. Iramuteq. 1. Introdução Os processos eleitorais brasileiros possuem históricos marcados pela manipulação da informação, acentuada na medida em que as Tecnologias de Informação e Comunicação (TICs) foram/são aprimoradas. Nesse quesito, a produção de desinformação não se limita à propagação de inverdades pontuais, mas opera como um",marcadores,cao da desinformacao nas eleico brasileira,study analyz similariti between disinformation produc 2022 election eve 2026 election objective understand how narrativ structur manipulate event relat electoral process both period achieve descend hierarchical classification dhc perform using iramuteq software analyz sample encompass disinformation verifi lupa agency consist cross-referenc textual data october december 31 2022 march 20 2025 2026 result indicate disinformation has chain production system based historical event involv coup etat foster doubt about legitimacy electoral proces rumor voter fraud narrativ military intervention they also point out criteria voter preference based ideological war threaten democratic rule law critical participation citizen electoral process,disinformation 2022 election 2026 election coup etat iramuteq introducao os processo eleitorai brasileiro possuem historico marcado pela manipulacao da informacao acentuada na medida em que tecnologia de informacao comunicacao tics foram sao aprimorada nesse quesito producao de desinformacao nao se limita propagacao de inverdad pontuai mas opera como um,cao da desinformacao nas eleico brasileira study analyz similariti between disinformation produc 2022 election eve 2026 election objective understand how narrativ structur manipulate event relat electoral process both period achieve descend hierarchical classification dhc perform using iramuteq software analyz sample encompass disinformation verifi lupa agency consist cross-referenc textual data october december 31 2022 march 20 2025 2026 result indicate disinformation has chain production system based historical event involv coup etat foster doubt about legitimacy electoral proces rumor voter fraud narrativ military intervention they also point out criteria voter preference based ideological war threaten democratic rule law critical participation citizen electoral process disinformation 2022 election 2026 election coup etat iramuteq introducao os processo eleitorai brasileiro possuem historico marcado pela manipulacao da informacao acentuada na medida em que tecnologia de informacao comunicacao tics foram sao aprimorada nesse quesito producao de desinformacao nao se limita propagacao de inverdad pontuai mas opera como um,1.0.0,718c7d8c86ec02a9
2538-9866,v49n2e360860FINAL.pdf,v49n2e360860FINAL_0,es,Doctoranda en Educación por la,"El artículo presenta un análisis del posicionamiento, entre 2015 y 2024, de las investigaciones publicadas por Honduras en Scopus la cual es una base de datos bibliográfica de resúmenes y citas de literatura científica revisada por pares, parte de la Editorial Elsevier. La exploración usó un paradigma cuantitativo y la técnica de análisis documental. El análisis presenta tipos de publicación por año, áreas temáticas que abordaron las investigaciones, idiomas de publicación, filiaciones institucionales y países con mayor recurrencia de publicación. Como conclusión se observa que en la última década la producción científica en Honduras ha tenido un incremento de 389% correspondiente a un total de 3,089 documentos publicados, evidenciando un mayor aumento entre 2019 y 2020 cuando pasó de 240 a 424 documentos, representado en 77% de aumento para ese año. El mayor énfasis de las publicaciones está en los artículos de investigación, la medicina y el inglés","Honduras; investigaciones; Scopus; bibliometría; medicina. Análisis de la producción científica de Honduras en Scopus (2015-2024)* © 2026 Universidad de Antioquia. Publicado por Universidad de Antioquia, Colombia. * Este trabajo deriva de la tesis doctoral titulada Análisis bibliometrico e institucional de la Universidad Nacional Autónoma de Honduras (UNAH): aportes para el diseño de un modelo",marcadores,doctoranda educacion,articulo presenta analisis posicionamiento entre 2015 2024 investig publicad hondur scopus cual base datos bibliografica resumen citas literatura cientifica revisada pares parte editorial elsevier exploracion uso paradigma cuantitativo tecnica analisis documental analisis presenta tipos publicacion ano areas tematic abordaron investig idiom publicacion fili institucional pais mayor recurrencia publicacion como conclusion observa ultima decada produccion cientifica hondur ha tenido incremento 389 correspondiente total 089 document publicad evidenci mayor aumento entre 2019 2020 cuando paso 240 424 document representado 77 aumento ese ano mayor enfasis public esta articul investigacion medicina ingl,hondur investig scopus bibliometria medicina analisis produccion cientifica hondur scopus 2015-2024 2026 universidad antioquia publicado universidad antioquia colombia este trabajo deriva tesis doctoral titulada analisis bibliometrico institucional universidad nacional autonoma hondur unah aport diseno modelo,doctoranda educacion articulo presenta analisis posicionamiento entre 2015 2024 investig publicad hondur scopus cual base datos bibliografica resumen citas literatura cientifica revisada pares parte editorial elsevier exploracion uso paradigma cuantitativo tecnica analisis documental analisis presenta tipos publicacion ano areas tematic abordaron investig idiom publicacion fili institucional pais mayor recurrencia publicacion como conclusion observa ultima decada produccion cientifica hondur ha tenido incremento 389 correspondiente total 089 document publicad evidenci mayor aumento entre 2019 2020 cuando paso 240 424 document representado 77 aumento ese ano mayor enfasis public esta articul investigacion medicina ingl hondur investig scopus bibliometria medicina analisis produccion cientifica hondur scopus 2015-2024 2026 universidad antioquia publicado universidad antioquia colombia este trabajo deriva tesis doctoral titulada analisis bibliometrico institucional universidad nacional autonoma hondur unah aport diseno modelo,1.0.0,384bfe22e1edbb58
2538-9866,v49n2e360860FINAL.pdf,v49n2e360860FINAL_0,en,as publicaciones está en los,"This article presents an analysis of the ranking, between 2015 and 2024, of research published in Honduras in Scopus, a bibliographic database of abstracts and citations of peerreviewed scientific literature, part of Elsevier Publishing. The analysis presents publication types by year, thematic areas addressed by the research, languages of publication, institutional affiliations, and countries with the highest frequency of publications. A quantitative approach and document analysis technique were used for the exploration. The main conclusion is that in the last decade, scientific production in Honduras has increased by 389%, corresponding to a total of 3,089 published documents. The most significant increase occurred between 2019 and 2020, when the number of documents rose from 240 to 424, representing a 77% increase for that year. The publications are primarily focused on research articles, medicine, and English",Honduras; research; Scopus: bibliometrics; medicine. 1,marcadores,publicacion esta en los,article present analysi rank between 2015 2024 research publish hondura scopu bibliographic database abstract citation peerreview scientific literature part elsevier publish analysi present publication type year thematic area address research languag publication institutional affili countri highest frequency public quantitative approach document analysi technique used exploration main conclusion last decade scientific production hondura has increas 389 correspond total 089 publish document most significant increase occurr between 2019 2020 when number document rose 240 424 represent 77 increase year public primarily focus research articl medicine english,hondura research scopu bibliometric medicine,publicacion esta en los article present analysi rank between 2015 2024 research publish hondura scopu bibliographic database abstract citation peerreview scientific literature part elsevier publish analysi present publication type year thematic area address research languag publication institutional affili countri highest frequency public quantitative approach document analysi technique used exploration main conclusion last decade scientific production hondura has increas 389 correspond total 089 publish document most significant increase occurr between 2019 2020 when number document rose 240 424 represent 77 increase year public primarily focus research articl medicine english hondura research scopu bibliometric medicine,1.0.0,3fb49e19098e4cf4
2539-200X,BC-1243.pdf,BC-1243_0,en,Type specimens in the Herbarium of the,"This article presents the catalogue of type specimens held at the Herbarium of the Faculty of Forest Sciences at the National Agrarian University La Molina (MOLF). It provides detailed information on type status, currently accepted names, and conservation status for 84 vascular plant taxa. The MOLF Herbarium houses 38 holotypes, 100 isotypes, one lectotype, and one isolectotype, associated with collections made between 1963 and 2022. The majority of taxa documented belong to the families Orchidaceae, Melastomataceae, and Fabaceae","botanical collections, plant taxonomy, Neotropical flora, vascular plant diversity. Palacios et al. Type specimens in the Herbarium of Forestry Sciences of the National Agrarian University La Molina BIOTA COLOMBIANA 26 - 2025 | 2",marcadores,type specimen herbarium,article present catalogue type specimen held herbarium faculty forest scienc national agrarian university la molina molf provid detail information type statu currently accept name conservation statu 84 vascular plant taxa molf herbarium hous 38 holotyp 100 isotyp one lectotype one isolectotype associat collection made between 1963 2022 majority taxa document belong famili orchidaceae melastomataceae fabaceae,botanical collection plant taxonomy neotropical flora vascular plant diversity palacio et al type specimen herbarium forestry scienc national agrarian university la molina biota colombiana 26 2025,type specimen herbarium article present catalogue type specimen held herbarium faculty forest scienc national agrarian university la molina molf provid detail information type statu currently accept name conservation statu 84 vascular plant taxa molf herbarium hous 38 holotyp 100 isotyp one lectotype one isolectotype associat collection made between 1963 2022 majority taxa document belong famili orchidaceae melastomataceae fabaceae botanical collection plant taxonomy neotropical flora vascular plant diversi