2539-200X,BC-1266.pdf,BC-1266_0,en,____________________________,"This study documents the first inventory of Auchenorrhyncha hemipterans in the La Tribuna Ecological Reserve (Neiva, Huila), which preserves a remnant of tropical dry forest. A total of 211 membracids from 17 genera and 5 aetalionids of Aetalion reticulatum were collected using Malaise traps, sweeping, and direct observation in three zones with different vegetation cover. Twelve membracid genera and one aetalionid genus are reported for the first time in Huila. Species richness was highest in the forest zone and during the rainy seasons. These findings highlight the value of tropical dry forest for hemipteran diversity and support its continued monitoring and conservation","insects, ecological indicators, monitoring, entomology, Hemiptera. _____________________________________________________________________________________________",marcadores,____________________________,study document first inventory auchenorrhyncha hemipteran la tribuna ecological reserve neiva huila which preserv remnant tropical dry forest total 211 membracid 17 genera aetalionid aetalion reticulatum collect using malaise trap sweep direct observation three zone different vegetation cover twelve membracid genera one aetalionid genu report first time huila speci richnes highest forest zone during rainy season these finding highlight value tropical dry forest hemipteran diversity support its continu monitor conservation,insect ecological indicator monitor entomology hemiptera _____________________________________________________________________________________________,____________________________ study document first inventory auchenorrhyncha hemipteran la tribuna ecological reserve neiva huila which preserv remnant tropical dry forest total 211 membracid 17 genera aetalionid aetalion reticulatum collect using malaise trap sweep direct observation three zone different vegetation cover twelve membracid genera one aetalionid genu report first time huila speci richnes highest forest zone during rainy season these finding highlight value tropical dry forest hemipteran diversity support its continu monitor conservation insect ecological indicator monitor entomology hemiptera _____________________________________________________________________________________________,1.0.0,b90ad774738e05b9
2539-200X,BC-1282.pdf,BC-1282_0,es,Caracterización anatómica de tres especies,"Este artículo caracteriza la anatomía de la madera de Cassipourea guianensis, Qualea lineata y Goupia glabra, especies de árboles del Chocó biogeográfico, y la compara la de individuos que crecen en bosques menos lluviosos del Neotrópico. Los resultados indican que las tres especies difieren en densidad, diámetro y longitud de los elementos de vaso. Todas presentan vasos que van de solitarios a múltiples, lo que sugiere estrategias contrastantes de adquisición y uso del agua. Este estudio busca fortalecer el conocimiento sobre las especies arbóreas tropicales, con miras a su gestión sostenible y a futuras investigaciones","ecología funcional, estrategias hídricas, anatomía comparada, morfología xilemática, biodiversidad tropical. Londoño, Franco, Trujillo, Serna & Giraldo Caracterización anatómica de tres especies arbóreas del Chocó BIOTA COLOMBIANA 26 - 2025 | 2",marcadores,caracterizacion anatomica tres especi,este articulo caracteriza anatomia madera cassipourea guianensis qualea lineata goupia glabra especi arbol choco biogeografico compara individu crecen bosqu menos lluvios neotropico resultad indican tres especi difieren densidad diametro longitud element vaso todas presentan vasos van solitari multipl sugiere estrategi contrastant adquisicion uso agua este estudio busca fortalecer conocimiento sobre especi arbore tropical miras gestion sostenible futur investig,ecologia funcional estrategi hidric anatomia comparada morfologia xilematica biodiversidad tropical londono franco trujillo serna giraldo caracterizacion anatomica tres especi arbore choco biota colombiana 26 2025,caracterizacion anatomica tres especi este articulo caracteriza anatomia madera cassipourea guianensis qualea lineata goupia glabra especi arbol choco biogeografico compara individu crecen bosqu menos lluvios neotropico resultad indican tres especi difieren densidad diametro longitud element vaso todas presentan vasos van solitari multipl sugiere estrategi contrastant adquisicion uso agua este estudio busca fortalecer conocimiento sobre especi arbore tropical miras gestion sostenible futur investig ecologia funcional estrategi hidric anatomia comparada morfologia xilematica biodiversidad tropical londono franco trujillo serna giraldo caracterizacion anatomica tres especi arbore choco biota colombiana 26 2025,1.0.0,17b5c2bbbee41b45
2539-200X,BC-1282.pdf,BC-1282_0,en,"tículo caracteriza la anatomía de la madera de Cassipourea guianensis, Qualea lineata y Goupia glabra,","This study characterizes the wood anatomy of Cassipourea guianensis, Qualea lineata, and Goupia glabra, tree species from the Chocó biogeographic region, and compares it with that of individuals growing in less rainy Neotropical forests. The results indicate that the three species differ in density, diameter, and length of vessel elements. All exhibit vessels ranging from solitary to multiple, suggesting contrasting strategies for water acquisition and use. This study aims to strengthen knowledge of tropical tree species to support their sustainable management and future research","functional ecology, water-use strategies, comparative anatomy, xylem morphology, tropical biodiversity. _____________________________________________________________________________________________",marcadores,ticulo caracteriza la anatomia de la madera de cassipourea guianensi qualea lineata goupia glabra,study characteriz wood anatomy cassipourea guianensi qualea lineata goupia glabra tree speci choco biogeographic region compar individual grow less rainy neotropical forest result indicate three speci differ density diameter length vessel element all exhibit vessel rang solitary multiple suggest contrast strategi water acquisition use study aims strengthen knowledge tropical tree speci support their sustainable management future research,functional ecology water-use strategi comparative anatomy xylem morphology tropical biodiversity _____________________________________________________________________________________________,ticulo caracteriza la anatomia de la madera de cassipourea guianensi qualea lineata goupia glabra study characteriz wood anatomy cassipourea guianensi qualea lineata goupia glabra tree speci choco biogeographic region compar individual grow less rainy neotropical forest result indicate three speci differ density diameter length vessel element all exhibit vessel rang solitary multiple suggest contrast strategi water acquisition use study aims strengthen knowledge tropical tree speci support their sustainable management future research functional ecology water-use strategi comparative anatomy xylem morphology tropical biodiversity _____________________________________________________________________________________________,1.0.0,e1b7a52ab0e40969
2539-200X,BC-1302.pdf,BC-1302_0,es,Diversidad taxonómica y funcional de,"Este artículo evalúa la composición, diversidad taxonómica y diversidad funcional de comunidades de macroinvertebrados acuáticos en cuerpos de agua de la Ecoreserva La Tribuna, un remanente de bosque seco tropical impactado por la expansión de la frontera agropecuaria y la contaminación por hidrocarburos. En sistemas lóticos, se identificaron relaciones entre el caudal y el oxígeno disuelto con parámetros de diversidad y diversidad funcional. En sistemas lénticos, la eutrofización elevada generó hipoxia y acidificación, favoreciendo especies tolerantes y reduciendo la diversidad y los parámetros funcionales. Los resultados evidencian que los cambios en la estructura y diversidad funcional de las comunidades de macroinvertebrados son indicadores sensibles del gradiente de perturbación en sistemas hídricos del bosque seco tropical","bioindicadores, rasgos funcionales, integridad ecológica, gradiente ambiental, códigos de barras ADN. Cuéllar-Cardozo Diversidad taxonómica y funcional de comunidades de macroinvertebrados BIOTA COLOMBIANA 26 - 2025 | 2",marcadores,diversidad taxonomica funcional,este articulo evalua composicion diversidad taxonomica diversidad funcional comunidad macroinvertebrad acuatic cuerp agua ecoreserva tribuna remanente bosque seco tropical impactado expansion frontera agropecuaria contaminacion hidrocarbur sistem lotic identificaron relacion entre caudal oxigeno disuelto parametr diversidad diversidad funcional sistem lentic eutrofizacion elevada genero hipoxia acidificacion favorec especi tolerant reduc diversidad parametr funcional resultad evidencian cambi estructura diversidad funcional comunidad macroinvertebrad son indicador sensibl gradiente perturbacion sistem hidric bosque seco tropical,bioindicador rasg funcional integridad ecologica gradiente ambiental codig barr adn cuellar-cardozo diversidad taxonomica funcional comunidad macroinvertebrad biota colombiana 26 2025,diversidad taxonomica funcional este articulo evalua composicion diversidad taxonomica diversidad funcional comunidad macroinvertebrad acuatic cuerp agua ecoreserva tribuna remanente bosque seco tropical impactado expansion frontera agropecuaria contaminacion hidrocarbur sistem lotic identificaron relacion entre caudal oxigeno disuelto parametr diversidad diversidad funcional sistem lentic eutrofizacion elevada genero hipoxia acidificacion favorec especi tolerant reduc diversidad parametr funcional resultad evidencian cambi estructura diversidad funcional comunidad macroinvertebrad son indicador sensibl gradiente perturbacion sistem hidric bosque seco tropical bioindicador rasg funcional integridad ecologica gradiente ambiental codig barr adn cuellar-cardozo diversidad taxonomica funcional comunidad macroinvertebrad biota colombiana 26 2025,1.0.0,ba09e861f63ffe11
2539-200X,BC-1302.pdf,BC-1302_0,en,tropical impactado por la expansión de la frontera agropecuaria y la contaminación por hidrocarburos. En sistemas,"This article assesses the composition, taxonomic diversity, and functional diversity of aquatic macroinvertebrate communities in water bodies of the Ecoreserva La Tribuna, a remnant of tropical dry forest affected by agricultural frontier expansion and hydrocarbon pollution. In lotic systems, relationships were identified between flow rate and dissolved oxygen with diversity and functional parameters. In lentic systems, high eutrophication led to hypoxia and acidification, favoring tolerant species and reducing diversity and functional metrics. The results demonstrate that changes in the structure and functionality of macroinvertebrate communities are sensitive indicators of disturbance gradients in aquatic systems of the tropical dry forest","bioindicators, functional traits, ecological integrity, environmental gradient, DNA barcoding. _____________________________________________________________________________________________",marcadores,tropical impactado por la expansion de la frontera agropecuaria la contaminacion por hidrocarburo en sistema,article assess composition taxonomic diversity functional diversity aquatic macroinvertebrate communiti water bodi ecoreserva la tribuna remnant tropical dry forest affect agricultural frontier expansion hydrocarbon pollution lotic system relationship identifi between flow rate dissolv oxygen diversity functional parameter lentic system high eutrophication led hypoxia acidification favor tolerant speci reduc diversity functional metric result demonstrate chang structure functionality macroinvertebrate communiti sensitive indicator disturbance gradient aquatic system tropical dry forest,bioindicator functional trait ecological integrity environmental gradient dna barcod _____________________________________________________________________________________________,tropical impactado por la expansion de la frontera agropecuaria la contaminacion por hidrocarburo en sistema article assess composition taxonomic diversity functional diversity aquatic macroinvertebrate communiti water bodi ecoreserva la tribuna remnant tropical dry forest affect agricultural frontier expansion hydrocarbon pollution lotic system relationship identifi between flow rate dissolv oxygen diversity functional parameter lentic system high eutrophication led hypoxia acidification favor tolerant speci reduc diversity functional metric result demonstrate chang structure functionality macroinvertebrate communiti sensitive indicator disturbance gradient aquatic system tropical dry forest bioindicator functional trait ecological integrity environmental gradient dna barcod _____________________________________________________________________________________________,1.0.0,08b6e31ed8b53b13
2539-3804,Online+Language+Learning+in+Colombian+Graduate+Education_+Students’+Perceptions+from+a+Survey+Study.pdf,Online+Language+Learning+in+Colombian+Graduate+Education_+Students’+Perceptions+from+a+Survey+Study_0,en,Online Language Learning in,"This survey-based study investigated graduate students’ perceptions of online skillsbased English for Academic Purposes (EAP) courses. A survey gathered data from 181 participants. Descriptive and inferential statistics, as well as content analysis, were used to analyze the data. Findings revealed a favorable perception of the online learning modality, tutors’ teaching practices, and assessment processes, with students valuing flexibility, accessibility, and structured course design. In contrast, students’ perceptions of language learning were lower, indicating a need for more interactive and relevant materials. While students reported gains in autonomy development, challenges such as lack of motivation and limited tutor guidance were also observed. The study suggests integrating discipline-specific authentic tasks, enhancing tutor training, and balancing synchronous and asynchronous interactions to improve online EAP learning",Online language learning; graduate education; student perceptions; survey study; EAP,marcadores,online language learn,survey-bas study investigat graduate student perception online skillsbas english academic purpos eap cours survey gather data 181 participant descriptive inferential statistic well content analysi used analyze data finding reveal favorable perception online learn modality tutor teach practic assessment process student valu flexibility accessibility structur course design contrast student perception language learn lower indicat need more interactive relevant material while student report gain autonomy development challeng such lack motivation limit tutor guidance also observ study suggest integrat discipline-specific authentic task enhanc tutor train balanc synchronou asynchronou inte