2590-8669,349-106-PB.pdf,349-106-PB_0,en,"de la perspectiva del institucionalismo histórico, para","The article examines the evolution of Colombian intelligence from the perspective of historical institutionalism, in order to explain how the armed conflict shaped its configuration and transformation. It argues that this trajectory cannot be understood solely as continuity or as a scattered succession of reforms, but rather as the result of two main critical junctures: the one that emerged in the early years of the National Front and the one opened by the peace negotiations between the Colombian state and the FARC-EP. Between these two moments, the text analyses different forms of gradual institutional change and highlights the importance of institutional weakness and informal institutions in understanding the historical trajectories of the intelligence community in Colombia","institutionalization, organizational change, Colombia, State security, political institutions. 1",marcadores,de la perspectiva del institucionalismo historico para,article examin evolution colombian intelligence perspective historical institutionalism order explain how armed conflict shap its configuration transformation argu trajectory cannot understood solely continuity scatter succession reform but rather result two main critical junctur one emerg early year national front one open peace negoti between colombian state farc-ep between these two moment text analys different form gradual institutional change highlight importance institutional weaknes informal institution understand historical trajectori intelligence community colombia,institutional organizational change colombia state security political institution,de la perspectiva del institucionalismo historico para article examin evolution colombian intelligence perspective historical institutionalism order explain how armed conflict shap its configuration transformation argu trajectory cannot understood solely continuity scatter succession reform but rather result two main critical junctur one emerg early year national front one open peace negoti between colombian state farc-ep between these two moment text analys different form gradual institutional change highlight importance institutional weaknes informal institution understand historical trajectori intelligence community colombia institutional organizational change colombia state security political institution,1.0.0,a178e1d5c68fc2d2
2590-8669,349-106-PB.pdf,349-106-PB_1,es,", JCS, and NSC. Stanford University Press.","Este artículo analiza el alcance y los límites del cambio en la política de erradicación de cultivos de uso ilícito en Colombia a partir del Programa Nacional Integral de Sustitución (PNIS) a diez años de la firma del “Acuerdo final para la terminación del conflicto y la construcción de una paz estable y duradera” (2016). Para ello, se adopta un enfoque cualitativo histórico-analítico sustentado en el marco de las coaliciones promotoras (advocacy coalition framework [ACF]) y el análisis documental de fuentes oficiales e informes de seguimiento. Los resultados evidencian que el PNIS representó un cambio institucional relevante en las creencias secundarias del subsistema, sin lograr alterar el núcleo de la política prohibicionista ni la estructura material de poder. En consecuencia, se concluye que el cambio fue parcial y de estabilidad limitada, condicionado por la brecha entre diseño e implementación territorial, y las presiones externas de la cooperación con Estados Unidos","política sobre drogas, desarrollo rural, acuerdo de paz, elaboración de políticas, Colombia",marcadores,jcs and nsc stanford university press,este articulo analiza alcance limit cambio politica erradicacion cultiv uso ilicito colombia partir programa nacional integral sustitucion pnis diez anos firma acuerdo final terminacion conflicto construccion paz estable duradera 2016 ello adopta enfoque cualitativo historico-analitico sustentado marco coalicion promotor advocacy coalition framework acf analisis documental fuent oficial inform seguimiento resultad evidencian pnis represento cambio institucional relevante creenci secundari subsistema sin lograr alterar nucleo politica prohibicionista ni estructura material poder consecuencia concluye cambio fue parcial estabilidad limitada condicionado brecha entre diseno implementacion territorial presion extern cooperacion estad unid,politica sobre drog desarrollo rural acuerdo paz elaboracion politic colombia,jcs and nsc stanford university press este articulo analiza alcance limit cambio politica erradicacion cultiv uso ilicito colombia partir programa nacional integral sustitucion pnis diez anos firma acuerdo final terminacion conflicto construccion paz estable duradera 2016 ello adopta enfoque cualitativo historico-analitico sustentado marco coalicion promotor advocacy coalition framework acf analisis documental fuent oficial inform seguimiento resultad evidencian pnis represento cambio institucional relevante creenci secundari subsistema sin lograr alterar nucleo politica prohibicionista ni estructura material poder consecuencia concluye cambio fue parcial estabilidad limitada condicionado brecha entre diseno implementacion territorial presion extern cooperacion estad unid politica sobre drog desarrollo rural acuerdo paz elaboracion politic colombia,1.0.0,b5ab4e8256c46d57
2590-8669,349-106-PB.pdf,349-106-PB_1,en,a firma del “Acuerdo final para,"This article analyzes the scope and limits of change in the illicit crop eradication policy in Colombia through the National Comprehensive Illicit Crop Substitution Program (PNIS), ten years after the signing of the Final Agreement between the Colombian State and the FARC-EP (2016-2026). To this end, a qualitative historical-analytical approach grounded in the Advocacy Coalition Framework (ACF) and documentary analysis of official sources and monitoring reports. The findings show that the PNIS represented a significant institutional change in the secondary beliefs of the policy subsystem, without managing to alter the prohibitionist policy core or the material structure of power. Leading to the conclusion that this change was partial and of limited stability, conditioned by the gap between design and territorial implementation and the external pressures derived from cooperation with the United States","drug policy, rural development, peace agreement, policy making, Colombia. Paola Andrea Trujillo Colmenares Universidad Complutense de Madrid, Madrid, España paoltruj@ucm.es 23 1",marcadores,firma del acuerdo final para,article analyz scope limit change illicit crop eradication policy colombia through national comprehensive illicit crop substitution program pnis ten year after sign final agreement between colombian state farc-ep 2016-2026 end qualitative historical-analytical approach ground advocacy coalition framework acf documentary analysi official sourc monitor report finding show pnis represent significant institutional change secondary belief policy subsystem without manag alter prohibitionist policy core material structure power lead conclusion change partial limit stability condition gap between design territorial implementation external pressur deriv cooperation unit stat,drug policy rural development peace agreement policy making colombia paola andrea trujillo colmenar universidad complutense de madrid madrid espana paoltruj ucm es 23,firma del acuerdo final para article analyz scope limit change illicit crop eradication policy colombia through national comprehensive illicit crop substitution program pnis ten year after sign final agreement between colombian state farc-ep 2016-2026 end qualitative historical-analytical approach ground advocacy coalition framework acf documentary analysi official sourc monitor report finding show pnis represent significant institutional change secondary belief policy subsystem without manag alter prohibitionist policy core material structure power lead conclusion change partial limit stability condition gap between design territorial implementation external pressur deriv cooperation unit stat drug policy rural development peace agreement policy making colombia paola andrea trujillo colmenar universidad complutense de madrid madrid espana paoltruj ucm es 23,1.0.0,fb3fc0d7167e2668
2590-8669,349-106-PB.pdf,349-106-PB_2,es,"epartment of State, Bureau for International Narcotics and Law Enforcement Affairs. (2025). International","Este artículo analiza la conceptualización, desarrollo y evolución de la justicia restaurativa dentro del marco de implementación del Acuerdo de Paz en Colombia, así como su papel como paradigma orientador del Sistema Integral de Verdad, Justicia, Reparación y No repetición (SIVJRNR), con especial atención a la Jurisdicción Especial para la Paz (JEP). Asimismo, examina los principales retos y limitaciones a los que se enfrenta este modelo a la hora de reparar a las víctimas del conflicto armado, identificando sus limitaciones estructurales, institucionales y contextuales, extrayendo lecciones relevantes para su avance y consolidación futura",Acuerdo de Paz; Jurisdicción Especial para la Paz (JEP); Justicia restaurativa; Justicia Transicional; Reparación,marcadores,epartment of state bureau for international narcotics and law enforcement affairs 2025 international,este articulo analiza conceptualizacion desarrollo evolucion justicia restaurativa dentro marco implementacion acuerdo paz colombia asi como papel como paradigma orientador sistema integral verdad justicia reparacion no repeticion sivjrnr especial atencion jurisdiccion especial paz jep asimismo examina principal retos limit enfrenta este modelo hora reparar victim conflicto armado identific sus limit estructural institucional contextual extrayendo leccion relevant avance consolidacion futura,acuerdo paz jurisdiccion especial paz jep justicia restaurativa justicia transicional reparacion,epartment of state bureau for international narcotics and law enforcement affairs 2025 international este articulo analiza conceptualizacion desarrollo evolucion justicia restaurativa dentro marco implementacion acuerdo paz colombia asi como papel como paradigma orientador sistema integral verdad justicia reparacion no repeticion sivjrnr especial atencion jurisdiccion especial paz jep asimismo examina principal retos limit enfrenta este modelo hora reparar victim conflicto armado identific sus limit estructural institucional contextual extrayendo leccion relevant avance consolidacion futura acuerdo paz jurisdiccion especial paz jep justicia restaurativa justicia transicional reparacion,1.0.0,0a75ea5d286653f2
2590-8669,349-106-PB.pdf,349-106-PB_2,en,"Este artículo analiza la conceptualización, desarrollo y evolución de la justicia restaurativa dentro del marco de","This article analyzes the conceptualization, development, and evolution of restorative justice within the framework of the implementation of the Peace Agreement in Colombia, as well as its role as a guiding paradigm of the Comprehensive System of Truth, Justice, Reparation, and Non-Repetition (SIVJRNR), with particular attention to its judicial component, the Special Jurisdiction for Peace (JEP). It also examines the main challenges and limitations this model faces in repairing victims of the armed conflict, identifying its structural, institutional, and contextual constraints, and drawing relevant lessons for its future advancement and consolidation",Peace Agreement; Special Jurisdiction for Peace; Reparation; Restorative justice; Transitional justice. 1,marcadores,este articulo analiza la conceptualizacion desarrollo evolucion de la justicia restaurativa dentro del marco de,article analyz conceptual development evolution restorative justice within framework implementation peace agreement colombia well its role guid paradigm comprehensive system truth justice reparation non-repetition sivjrnr particular attention its judicial component special jurisdiction peace jep also examin main challeng limit model face repair victim armed conflict identify its structural institutional contextual constraint draw relevant lesson its future advancement consolidation,peace agreement special jurisdiction peace reparation restorative justice transitional justice,este articulo analiza la conceptualizacion desarrollo evolucion de la justicia restaurativa dentro del marco de article analyz conceptual development evolution restorative justice within framework implementation peace agreement colombia well its role guid paradigm comprehensive system truth justice reparation non-repetition sivjrnr particular attention its judicial co