2619-2551,Análisis+Bovinométrico_Met.pdf,Análisis+Bovinométrico_Met_0,es,"Cómo citar: Amaya, A.; Parra-Cortés, R.I.; Chay-Canul, A.J. 2026. Ecuación bovinométrica para la estimación del peso vivo en hembras","La estimación precisa del peso vivo (PV) es esencial para decisiones zootécnicas y transacciones comerciales justas; sin embargo, en sistemas de pequeña y mediana escala, el pesaje con báscula se suele ver limitado por costos e infraestructura, lo que favorece el uso de métodos indirectos, como cintas comerciales bovinométricas basadas en el perímetro torácico (PT), cuya validez puede variar según la raza y el biotipo. Este estudio ajustó una ecuación bovinométrica para hembras de ganado criollo Blanco Orejinegro (BON) de Colombia, con el fin de estimar el PV a partir del PT. Se analizaron datos de 59 hembras con medidas morfométricas y dos registros de PV, uno con cinta comercial bovinométrica y otro con báscula. Se estimaron correlaciones de Pearson y se cuantificó el acuerdo mediante sesgo, el error absoluto medio, la raíz del error cuadrático medio y el error porcentual absoluto medio, además de explorar el sesgo proporcional a través de regresión. La relación PT– PV se modeló con una función de potencia en escala logarítmica. El PT mostró las asociaciones más altas con el PV y la cinta métrica comercial presentó evidencia de sobreestimación creciente en animales más grandes. La ecuación local basada en báscula mejoró la precisión, lo que respalda el uso de calibraciones específicas para hembras BON en condiciones de campo",Alometría; Biotipo; Bovidae; Ganado criollo colombiano; Morfometría,marcadores,como citar amaya parra-cort chay-canul 2026 ecuacion bovinometrica estimacion peso vivo hembr,estimacion precisa peso vivo pv esencial decision zootecnic transaccion comercial just sin embargo sistem pequena mediana escala pesaje bascula suele ver limitado cost infraestructura favorece uso metod indirect como cint comercial bovinometric basad perimetro toracico pt cuya validez puede variar segun raza biotipo este estudio ajusto ecuacion bovinometrica hembr ganado criollo blanco orejinegro bon colombia fin estimar pv partir pt analizaron datos 59 hembr medid morfometric dos registr pv uno cinta comercial bovinometrica otro bascula estimaron correl pearson cuantifico acuerdo mediante sesgo error absoluto medio raiz error cuadratico medio error porcentual absoluto medio adem explorar sesgo proporcional trav regresion relacion pt- pv modelo funcion potencia escala logaritmica pt mostro asoci mas altas pv cinta metrica comercial presento evidencia sobreestimacion creciente animal mas grand ecuacion local basada bascula mejoro precision respalda uso calibr especific hembr bon condicion campo,alometria biotipo bovidae ganado criollo colombiano morfometria,como citar amaya parra-cort chay-canul 2026 ecuacion bovinometrica estimacion peso vivo hembr estimacion precisa peso vivo pv esencial decision zootecnic transaccion comercial just sin embargo sistem pequena mediana escala pesaje bascula suele ver limitado cost infraestructura favorece uso metod indirect como cint comercial bovinometric basad perimetro toracico pt cuya validez puede variar segun raza biotipo este estudio ajusto ecuacion bovinometrica hembr ganado criollo blanco orejinegro bon colombia fin estimar pv partir pt analizaron datos 59 hembr medid morfometric dos registr pv uno cinta comercial bovinometrica otro bascula estimaron correl pearson cuantifico acuerdo mediante sesgo error absoluto medio raiz error cuadratico medio error porcentual absoluto medio adem explorar sesgo proporcional trav regresion relacion pt- pv modelo funcion potencia escala logaritmica pt mostro asoci mas altas pv cinta metrica comercial presento evidencia sobreestimacion creciente animal mas grand ecuacion local basada bascula mejoro precision respalda uso calibr especific hembr bon condicion campo alometria biotipo bovidae ganado criollo colombiano morfometria,1.0.0,269b0ab8a70f6123
2619-2551,Análisis+Bovinométrico_Met.pdf,Análisis+Bovinométrico_Met_0,en,n de estimar el PV a partir del PT.,"Precise estimation of live weight (LW) is essential for zootechnical decision-making and fair commercial transactions. However, in small and medium scale production systems, scale weighing is often limited by cost and infrastructure constraints, favoring the use of indirect methods such as commercial bovinometric tapes based on heart girth (HG), whose validity may vary according to breed and biotype. This study fitted a bovinometric equation for females of the Colombian Creole Blanco Orejinegro (BON) cattle breed to estimate LW based on HG. Data from 59 females with morphometric measurements and two LW records were analyzed: commercial bovinometric tape and scale weight. Pearson correlations were estimated, and agreement was quantified using bias, mean absolute error, root mean squared error, and mean absolute percentage error; proportional bias was also explored through regression. The HG–LW relationship was modeled using a power function on a logarithmic scale. HG showed the strongest associations with LW, and the commercial measuring tape showed evidence of increasing overestimation in larger animals. The scalebased equation improved accuracy, supporting the use of specific calibrations for BON females under field conditions","Allometry; Biotype; Bovidae; Colombian Creole cattle; Morphometry. 2 Amaya, A.; Parra-Cortés, R.I.; Chay-Canul, A.J.: bovinometría en ganado blanco orejinegro",marcadores,de estimar el pv partir del pt,precise estimation live weight lw essential zootechnical decision-mak fair commercial transaction however small medium scale production system scale weigh often limit cost infrastructure constraint favor use indirect method such commercial bovinometric tape based heart girth hg whose validity may vary accord breed biotype study fitt bovinometric equation femal colombian creole blanco orejinegro bon cattle breed estimate lw based hg data 59 femal morphometric measurement two lw record analyz commercial bovinometric tape scale weight pearson correl estimat agreement quantifi using bias mean absolute error root mean squar error mean absolute percentage error proportional bias also explor through regression hg-lw relationship model using power function logarithmic scale hg show strongest associ lw commercial measur tape show evidence increas overestimation larger animal scalebas equation improv accuracy support use specific calibr bon femal under field condition,allometry biotype bovidae colombian creole cattle morphometry amaya parra-cort chay-canul bovinometria en ganado blanco orejinegro,de estimar el pv partir del pt precise estimation live weight lw essential zootechnical decision-mak fair commercial transaction however small medium scale production system scale weigh often limit cost infrastructure constraint favor use indirect method such commercial bovinometric tape based heart girth hg whose validity may vary accord breed biotype study fitt bovinometric equation femal colombian creole blanco orejinegro bon cattle breed estimate lw based hg data 59 femal morphometric measurement two lw record analyz commercial bovinometric tape scale weight pearson correl estimat agreement quantifi using bias mean absolute error root mean squar error mean absolute percentage error proportional bias also explor through regression hg-lw relationship model using power function logarithmic scale hg show strongest associ lw commercial measur tape show evidence increas overestimation larger animal scalebas equation improv accuracy support use specific calibr bon femal under field condition allometry biotype bovidae colombian creole cattle morphometry amaya parra-cort chay-canul bovinometria en ganado blanco orejinegro,1.0.0,15c5a4c5c82dc53f
2619-2551,Bacteriocinas_Met.pdf,Bacteriocinas_Met_0,es,"Cómo citar: Lopez-Pazos, S.A.; Estupiñán-Torres, S.M.; Landinez-Velandia, S.M. 2026. Prospección de bacteriocinas de Bacillus subtilis y","La creciente resistencia bacteriana representa un problema de salud global que demanda el desarrollo de nuevos agentes antimicrobianos. Las bacteriocinas han demostrado un gran potencial para el control de patógenos, y Bacillus subtilis y Pseudomonas extremaustralis podrían ser fuentes viables de estos compuestos. Este estudio tuvo como objetivo determinar la presencia de bacteriocinas de B. subtilis ATCC 6633 y P. extremaustralis CMPUJU 515 para su caracterización in silico y evaluación antimicrobiana en patógenos humanos. Se realizó un análisis in silico para identificar y caracterizar secuencias de bacteriocinas. Se realizaron pruebas de inhibición bacteriana e identificación de bandas proteicas asociadas, mediante PCR y SDS-PAGE. Se identificaron 21 secuencias de bacteriocinas en B. subtilis ATCC 6633 y tres en P. extremaustralis CMPUJU 515. Las características bioquímicas in silico revelaron diferencias en punto isoeléctrico, estabilidad y peso molecular. En las pruebas experimentales se confirmó la presencia de proteínas de bajo peso molecular, aunque B. subtilis ATCC 6633 y P. extremaustralis CMPUJU 515 presentan varios tipos de bacteriocinas en los genomas examinados in silico. Se identificaron molecularmente tres bacteriocinas de B. subtilis ATCC 6633, pero no se encontró actividad antimicrobiana con extractos que contienen bacteriocinas",Antibiograma; Bacillus subtilis ATCC 6633; Péptido antimicrobiano; PCR y clonación; Pseudomonas extremaustralis CMPUJU 515,marcadores,como citar lopez-paz estupinan-torr landinez-velandia 2026 prospeccion bacteriocin bacillus subtilis,creciente resistencia bacteriana representa problema salud global demanda desarrollo nuev agent antimicrobian bacteriocin han demostrado gran potencial control patogen bacillus subtilis pseudomon extremaustralis podrian ser fuent viabl estos compuest este estudio tuvo como objetivo determinar presencia bacteriocin subtilis atcc 6633 extremaustralis cmpuju 515 caracterizacion in silico evaluacion antimicrobiana patogen human realizo analisis in silico identificar caracterizar secuenci bacteriocin realizaron prueb inhibicion bacteriana identificacion band proteic asociad mediante pcr sds-page identificaron 21 secuenci bacteriocin subtilis atcc 6633 tres extremaustralis cmpuju 515 caracteristic bioquimic in silico revelaron diferenci punto isoelectrico estabilidad peso molecular prueb experimental confirmo presencia protein bajo peso molecular aunque subtilis atcc 6633 extremaustralis cmpuju 515 presentan vari tipos bacteriocin genom examinad in silico identificaron molecular tres bacteriocin subtilis atcc 6633 pero no encontro actividad antimicrobiana extract contienen bacteriocin,antibiograma bacillus subtilis atcc 6633 peptido antimicrobiano pcr clonacion pseudomon extremaustralis cmpuju 515,como citar lopez-paz estupinan-torr landinez-velandia 2026 prospeccion bacteriocin bacillus subtilis creciente resistencia bacteriana representa problema salud global demanda desarrollo nuev agent antimicrobian bacteriocin han demostrado gran potencial control patogen bacillus subtilis pseudomon extremaustralis podrian ser fuent viabl estos compuest este estudio tuvo como objetivo determinar presencia bacteriocin subtilis atcc 6633 extremaustralis cmpuju 515 caracterizacion in silico evaluacion antimicrobiana patogen human realizo analisis in silico identificar caracterizar secuenci bacteriocin realizaron prueb inhibicion bacteriana identificacion band proteic asociad mediante pcr sds-page identificaron 21 secuenci bacteriocin subtilis atcc 6633 tres extremaustralis cmpuju 515 caracteristic bioquimic in silico revelaron diferenci punto isoelectrico estabilidad peso molecular prueb experimental confirmo presencia protein bajo peso molecular aunque subtilis atcc 6633 extremaustralis cmpuju 515 presentan vari tipos bacteriocin genom examinad in silico identificaron molecular tres bacteriocin subtilis atcc 6633 pero no encontro actividad antimicrobiana extract contienen bacteriocin antibiograma bacillus subtilis atcc 6633 peptido antimicrobiano pcr clonacion pseudomon extremaustralis cmpuju 515,1.0.0,4158683a9dde7e85
2619-2551,Bacteriocinas_Met.pdf,Bacteriocinas_Met_0,en,Se realizaron pruebas de inhibición,"Increasing bacterial resistance represents a global health problem that demands the development of new antimicrobial agents. Bacteriocins have proved their potential in pathogen control, Bacillus subtilis and Pseudomonas extremaustralis could be viable sources of these compounds. The aim was to determine presence of bacteriocins from B. subtilis ATCC 6633 and P. extremaustralis CMPUJU 515, in silico characterization, and evaluation on human pathogens. An in silico analysis was performed to identify bacteriocin sequences, followed by its physicochemical evaluation. Bacterial inhibition tests and identification of bands associated with bacteriocins with PCR and SDS-PAGE were carried out. 21 bacteriocin sequences were identified in B. subtilis ATCC 6633 and three in P. extremaustralis CMPUJU 515. The in silico biochemical characteristics revealed differences in isoelectric point, stability and molecular weight. Experimental tests confirmed the presence of low molecular weight proteins, although there was no evidence of growth inhibition of the pathogens evaluated. B. subtilis ATCC 6633 and P. extremaustralis CMPUJU 515 exhibit biocontrol potential because of presence of various bacteriocins in their genomes, as determined by in silico analysis. Three bacteriocins were experimentally identified in B. subtilis ATCC 6633, but no antimicrobial activity was observed against the study pathogens using bacteriocin-containing extracts. Further research is needed to improve bacteriocin synthesis, or to develop recombinant production","Antibiogram; Antimicrobial peptide; Bacillus subtilis ATCC 6633; PCR and cloning; Pseudomonas extremaustralis CMPUJU 515. 2 Lopez-Pazos, S.A.; Estupiñán-Torres, S.M.; Landinez-Velandia, S.M.: Bacteriocinas en Bacillus y Pseudomonas",marcadores,se realizaron prueba de inhibicion,increas bacterial resistance represent global health problem demand development new antimicrobial agent bacteriocin have prov their potential pathogen control bacillu subtili pseudomona extremaustrali could viable sourc these compound aim determine presence bacteriocin subtili atcc 6633 extremaustrali cmpuju 515 silico character evaluation human pathogen silico analysi perform identify bacteriocin sequenc follow its physicochemical evaluation bacterial inhibition test identification band associat bacteriocin pcr sds-page carri out 21 bacteriocin sequenc identifi subtili atcc 6633 three extremaustrali cmpuju 515 silico biochemical characteristic reveal differenc isoelectric point stability molecular weight experimental test confirm presence low molecular weight protein although there no evidence growth inhibition pathogen evaluat subtili atcc 6633 extremaustrali cmpuju 515 exhibit biocontrol potential because presence variou bacteriocin their genom determin silico analysi three bacteriocin experimentally identifi subtili atcc 6633 but no antimicrobial activity observ against study pathogen using bacteriocin-contain extract further research need improve bacteriocin synthesi develop recombinant production,antibiogram antimicrobial peptide bacillu subtili atcc 6633 pcr clon pseudomona extremaustrali cmpuju 515 lopez-pazo estupinan-torr landinez-velandia bacteriocina en bacillu pseudomona,se realizaron prueba de inhibicion increas bacterial resistance represent global health problem demand development new antimicrobial agent bacteriocin have prov their potential pathogen control bacillu subtili pseudomona extremaustrali could viable sourc these compound aim determine presence bacteriocin subtili atcc 6633 extremaustrali cmpuju 515 silico character evaluation human pathogen silico analysi perform identify bacteriocin sequenc follow its physicochemical evaluation bacterial inhibition test identification band associat bacteriocin pcr sds-page carri out 21 bacteriocin sequenc identifi subtili atcc 6633 three extremaustrali cmpuju 515 silico biochemical characteristic reveal differenc isoelectric point stability molecular weight experimental test confirm presence low molecular weight protein although there no evidence growth inhibition pathogen evaluat subtili atcc 6633 extremaustrali cmpuju 515 exhibit biocontrol potential because presence variou bacteriocin their genom determin silico analysi three bacteriocin experimentally identifi subtili atcc 6633 but no antimicrobial activity observ against study pathogen using bacteriocin-contain extract further research need improve bacteriocin synthesi develop recombinant production antibiogram antimicrobial peptide bacillu subtili atcc 6633 pcr clon pseudomona extremaustrali cmpuju 515 lopez-pazo estupinan-torr landinez-velandia bacteriocina en bacillu pseudomona,1.0.0,df95ac13110b08bf
2619-2551,Biominería+en+Colombia_met.pdf,Biominería+en+Colombia_met_0,en,"Agrícolas, Pecuarias y del Medio Ambiente (ECAPMA). Bogotá,","Biooxidation and bioleaching are biotechnological processes used as part of biomining, which use acidophilic bacteria to extract metals from low-grade sulfide ores, mining waste, and electronic waste. The use of these technologies represents cleaner and more environmentally friendly alternatives compared to conventional pyrometallurgical extraction methods, as they generate fewer greenhouse gases without evidence of increased operational costs for businesses. Despite substantial research on this topic and the successful industrial implementation of acidophilic bacteria in mineral processing plants worldwide, development in Colombia are still limited, with efforts largely confined to laboratory-scale studies. Notwithstanding the evident lag in the development of biomining processes, microorganism-based technologies for the treatment of minerals and electronic waste represent a promising alternative for maintaining an economically important sector in Colombia while minimizing negative environmental impacts on communities, and with a view to contributing to climate change mitigation, promoting a circular economy, and supporting responsible waste management. The objective of this study was to compile and critically analyze current information on the various technologies associated with biomining. We summarized the biological principles underlying these processes and examined their physicochemical and operational foundations. Finally, we assess the potential for research and technological development in biomining as a viable alternative for adoption within the Colombian mining industry",Acidophilic bacteria; Biomining; Electronic waste; Greenhouse gases; Minerals,marcadores,agricola pecuaria del medio ambiente ecapma bogota,biooxidation bioleach biotechnological process used part biomin which use acidophilic bacteria extract metal low-grade sulfide ores mining waste electronic waste use these technologi represent cleaner more environmentally friendly alternativ compar conventional pyrometallurgical extraction method they generate fewer greenhouse gase without evidence increas operational cost business despite substantial research topic successful industrial implementation acidophilic bacteria mineral process plant worldwide development colombia still limit effort largely confin laboratory-scale studi notwithstand evident lag development biomin process microorganism-bas technologi treatment mineral electronic waste represent promis alternative maintain economically important sector colombia while minimiz negative environmental impact communiti view contribut climate change mitigation promot circular economy support responsible waste management objective study compile critically analyze current information variou technologi associat biomin we summariz biological principl underly these process examin their physicochemical operational found finally we asses potential research technological development biomin viable alternative adoption within colombian mining industry,acidophilic bacteria biomin electronic waste greenhouse gase mineral,agricola pecuaria del medio ambiente ecapma bogota biooxidation bioleach biotechnological process used part biomin which use acidophilic bacteria extract metal low-grade sulfide ores mining waste electronic waste use these technologi represent cleaner more environmentally friendly alternativ compar conventional pyrometallurgical extraction method they generate fewer greenhouse gase without evidence increas operational cost business despite substantial research topic successful industrial implementation acidophilic bacteria mineral process plant worldwide development colombia still limit effort largely confin laboratory-scale studi notwithstand evident lag development biomin process microorganism-bas technologi treatment mineral electronic waste represent promis alternati