2619-2551,Vertebrados+silvestres_Met.pdf,Vertebrados+silvestres_Met_0,en,e sumaron datos,"Wildlife roadkill represents a growing global problem for biodiversity and road safety, with limited monitoring and limited implementation of mitigation measures. This study corresponds to the second systematic survey conducted in Cundinamarca, completed along the Patios–La Calera and La Calera–Sopó sections of the Corredor Perimetral Oriental de Bogotá (POB). A total of 51 roadkill events were recorded, yielding higher rates compared to those reported for other roads, such as the Bogotá–Girardot corridor, the Bogotá–Puerto Salgar corridor, and the Bogotá– Chiquinquirá corridor. Additional data provided by the Agencia Nacional de Infraestructura (ANI) were incorporated, resulting in a total of 70 records. The most affected species were Didelphis pernigra, Turdus fuscater, and Atractus crassicaudatus, likely due to their synanthropic behavior. Events were concentrated at three critical hotspots, with the most relevant located adjacent to the San Rafael reservoir. Logistic regressions and generalized non-linear models showed that higher speed limits significantly increase the probability of wildlife collisions. Likewise, distance to water bodies, vegetation patches, and urbanized areas influenced the probability of roadkill occurrence among the evaluated taxa with varying intensity","Ecological connectivity; Green infrastructure; Habitat fragmentation; Road ecology; Road environmental management. 2 Duarte-Velandia, A.M.; Pérez-Torres, J.; Jaramillo-Fayad, J.C.: riesgo vial para fauna",marcadores,sumaron dato,wildlife roadkill represent grow global problem biodiversity road safety limit monitor limit implementation mitigation measur study correspond second systematic survey conduct cundinamarca complet along patios-la calera la calera-sopo section corredor perimetral oriental de bogota pob total 51 roadkill event record yield higher rate compar those report other road such bogota-girardot corridor bogota-puerto salgar corridor bogota- chiquinquira corridor additional data provid agencia nacional de infraestructura ani incorporat result total 70 record most affect speci didelphi pernigra turdu fuscater atractu crassicaudatu likely due their synanthropic behavior event concentrat three critical hotspot most relevant locat adjacent san rafael reservoir logistic regression generaliz non-linear model show higher speed limit significantly increase probability wildlife collision likewise distance water bodi vegetation patch urbaniz area influenc probability roadkill occurrence among evaluat taxa vary intensity,ecological connectivity green infrastructure habitat fragmentation road ecology road environmental management duarte-velandia perez-torr jaramillo-fayad riesgo vial para fauna,sumaron dato wildlife roadkill represent grow global problem biodiversity road safety limit monitor limit implementation mitigation measur study correspond second systematic survey conduct cundinamarca complet along patios-la calera la calera-sopo section corredor perimetral oriental de bogota pob total 51 roadkill event record yield higher rate compar those report other road such bogota-girardot corridor bogota-puerto salgar corridor bogota- chiquinquira corridor additional data provid agencia nacional de infraestructura ani incorporat result total 70 record most affect speci didelphi pernigra turdu fuscater atractu crassicaudatu likely due their synanthropic behavior event concentrat three critical hotspot most relevant locat adjacent san rafael reservoir logistic regression generaliz non-linear model show higher speed limit significantly increase probability wildlife collision likewise distance water bodi vegetation patch urbaniz area influenc probability roadkill occurrence among evaluat taxa vary intensity ecological connectivity green infrastructure habitat fragmentation road ecology road environmental management duarte-velandia perez-torr jaramillo-fayad riesgo v