2619-2551,propiedades+fisioquímicas_Met.pdf,propiedades+fisioquímicas_Met_0,en,"de almidón, pH cercano a la neutralidad, menor temperatura de","Green plantain starch is a promising raw material for the agroindustrial valorization of tropical crops due to its functional properties and potential applications in food systems and biodegradable materials. This study determined the physicochemical and functional properties of starch extracted from three plantain varieties grown in Caldas, Colombia: Hartón (Musa paradisiaca), Dominico-Hartón (Musa AAB Simmonds), and Dominico (Musa paradisiaca var. sapientum). Starch was extracted through washing, blending, sedimentation, decantation, drying, and milling. Moisture, pH, color, starch content, gelatinization temperature, water absorption index, solubility, swelling power, clarity, and resistant starch content were evaluated. The experiment followed a completely randomized design, and data was analyzed by ANOVA. The Dominico variety showed the best overall performance, with the highest extraction yield, near-neutral pH, lower gelatinization temperature, higher water absorption index, greater swelling power, better paste clarity, and higher resistant starch content. These results demonstrate significant variability among varieties and identify Dominico starch as a promising source for the development of formulated foods, products with modulated digestibility, extruded systems, and starch-based biodegradable packaging, with technological, industrial, and nutritional potential, especially in functional formulations, low-digestibility matrices, value-added ingredients, and sustainable developments oriented toward agrofood innovation","Agro-industrial valorization; Biodegradable packaging; Functional differentiation; Resistant starch; Technological utilization. 2 Ormaza-Zapata, A.M.; Mejia-Gutierrez, L.F.; Caicedo-Eraso, J.C.: variabilidad del almidón de plátano",marcadores,de almidon ph cercano la neutralidad menor temperatura de,