2619-4066,187-98-PB.pdf,187-98-PB_11,en,"aptable, para enfrentar los fenómenos emergentes","This paper analyzes the historical development of Western constitutionalism, from its Greek and Roman origins to its modern consolidation, identifying its foundations, evolution, and the contemporary challenges it faces in the current global context. A qualitative and socio-critical approach is employed, based on a thematic review of academic, historical, and legal sources. It integrates normative, theoretical, and comparative analysis to examine the trajectory of cons- 347 ¦ Revista Ratio Juris Vol. 20 N.º 41 • UNAULA ¦ ISSN 1794-663 · ISSNe: 2619-4066 ¦ doi: 10.24142/raju Neoliberalismo, democracia iliberal y batalla cultural: entre neofascismos emergentes y nuevas derechas neoliberal-conservadoras. Una revisión temática titutionalism and its adaptation to current complexities. The central question concerning justice and political organization is addressed. To develop this, a brief history of constitutionalism is presented, followed by a description of the concept of Western constitutionalism, and finally an analysis of the challenges and difficulties the model presents, reflecting on the need to rethink constitutionalism from a complex, interdisciplinary, and adaptable perspective to address emerging phenomena of the 21st century. Constitutionalism is understood as a paradigm to limit power and guarantee rights, with historical milestones such as the Magna Carta, liberal revolutions, and modern constitutions. Currently, it faces challenges such as the erosion of state sovereignty by global powers (corporations, technologies), normative rigidity, and a crisis of representativeness. A reconceptualization of constitutionalism and neoconstitutionalism from the sciences of complexity is proposed, integrating interdisciplinarity, adaptability, and new tools to respond to dynamic and multicausal realities","constitutionalism, neoconstitutionalism, paradigm, complexity, fundamental rights, globalization, crisis of legitimacy",marcadores,aptable para enfrentar los fenomeno emergent,paper analyz historical development western constitutionalism its greek roman origin its modern consolidation identify its found evolution contemporary challeng face current global context qualitative socio-critical approach employ based thematic review academic historical legal sourc integrat normative theoretical comparative analysi examine trajectory cons- 347 revista ratio juri vol 20 41 unaula issn 1794-663 issne 2619-4066 doi 10 24142 raju neoliberalismo democracia iliberal batalla cultural entre neofascismo emergent nueva derecha neoliberal-conservadora una revision tematica titutionalism its adaptation current complexiti central question concern justice political organ address develop brief history constitutionalism present follow description concept western constitutionalism finally analysi challeng difficulti model present reflect need rethink constitutionalism complex interdisciplinary adaptable perspective addres emerg phenomena 21st century constitutionalism understood paradigm limit power guarantee right historical mileston such magna carta liberal revolution modern constitution currently face challeng such erosion state sovereignty global power corpor technologi normative rigidity crisi representativenes reconceptual constitutionalism neoconstitutionalism scienc complexity propos integrat interdisciplinarity adaptability new tool respond dynamic multicausal realiti,constitutionalism neoconstitutionalism paradigm complexity fundamental right global crisi legitimacy,aptable para enfrentar los fenomeno emergent paper analyz historical development western constitutionalism its greek roman origin its modern consolidation identify its found evolution contemporary challeng face current global context qualitative socio-critical approach employ based thematic review academic historical legal sourc integrat normative theoretical comparative analysi examine trajectory cons- 347 revista ratio juri vol 20 41 unaula issn 1794-663 issne 2619-4066 doi 10 24142 raju neoliberalismo democracia iliberal batalla cultural entre neofascismo emergent nueva derecha neoliberal-conservadora una revision tematica titutionalism its adaptation current complexiti central question concern justice political organ address develop brief history constitutionalism present follow description concept western constitutionalism finally analysi challeng difficulti model present reflect need rethink constitutionalism complex interdisciplinary adaptable perspective addres emerg phenomena 21st century constitutionalism understood paradigm limit power guarantee right historical mileston such magna carta liberal revolution modern constitution currently face challeng such erosion state sovereignty global power corpor technologi normative rigidity crisi representativenes reconceptual constitutionalism neoconstitutionalism scienc complexity propos integrat interdisciplinarity adaptability new tool respond dynamic multicausal realiti constitutionalism neoconstitutionalism paradigm complexity fundamental right global crisi legitimacy,1.0.0,0c3ffee8e36d909d
2619-4066,187-98-PB.pdf,187-98-PB_12,es,"(UNAULA), 20(41). Recuperado a partir de https://publicaciones.unaula.edu.co/","La educación para la paz y la convivencia intercultural es un eje central de las discusiones contemporáneas de las ciencias sociales, en la dimensión crítica de nuestra América. En esta ponencia se reflexiona sobre el papel de la universidad mexicana como actor social frente a las violencias estructurales y simbólicas que atraviesan a los sectores históricamente excluidos. En ese sentido, se examina la universidad no solo como espacio de formación profesional, sino como territorio de disputa epistémica, política y ética, donde emergen iniciativas orientadas hacia la construcción de una paz integral e intercultural crítica. Desde la perspectiva de la interculturalidad crítica, se argumenta que la educación superior debe involucrarse activamente en la superación de las desigualdades socioeconómicas, culturales y políticas que persisten en el país, generando espacios de diálogo, deliberación y acción colectiva entre las comunidades y las instituciones públicas y privadas. Este artículo sostiene que la paz no puede pensarse sin justicia social ni sin el reconocimiento de las diferencias, por lo que resulta urgente la construcción de programas educativos interinstitucionales que promuevan la convivencia pacífica, la equidad y el respeto mutuo dentro y fuera de las universidades mexicanas","educación para la paz, universidad mexicana, interculturalidad crítica, convivencia, justicia social",marcadores,unaula 20 41 recuperado partir https public unaula edu co,educacion paz convivencia intercultural eje central discusion contemporane cienci social dimension critica nuestra america esta ponencia reflexiona sobre papel universidad mexicana como actor social frente violenci estructural simbolic atraviesan sector historica excluid ese sentido examina universidad no solo como espacio formacion profesional sino como territorio disputa epistemica politica etica 