2619-4066,187-98-PB.pdf,187-98-PB_12,en,e emergen iniciativas,"Education for peace and intercultural coexistence is a central topic in current debates within the social sciences and humanities in Latin America. This presentation reflects on the role of Mexican universities as social actors in the face of structural and symbolic violence affecting historically marginalized sectors. The university is examined not merely as a space for professional training, but as a site of epistemic, political, and ethical struggle where initiatives aimed at constructing integral and critical intercultural peace are emerging. From a critical interculturality perspective, the argument is made that higher education institutions must actively engage in addressing the 381 ¦ Revista Ratio Juris Vol. 20 N.º 41 • UNAULA ¦ ISSN 1794-663 · ISSNe: 2619-4066 ¦ doi: 10.24142/raju La educación y la formación universitaria para la paz: aprendizajes en convivencia pacífica e intercultural en México social, economic, and political inequalities that persist in the country. This involves creating spaces for dialogue, deliberation, and collective action among communities, and between public and private institutions. The article, contends that peace cannot be conceived without social justice or the recognition of difference, making it urgent to develop inter-institutional educational programs that promote peaceful coexistence, equity, and mutual respect within and beyond Mexican universities","peace education, Mexican university, critical interculturality, coexistence, social justice",marcadores,emergen iniciativa,education peace intercultural coexistence central topic current debat within social scienc humaniti latin america presentation reflect role mexican universiti social actor face structural symbolic violence affect historically marginaliz sector university examin not merely space professional train but site epistemic political ethical struggle where initiativ aimed construct integral critical in