2745-1402,2026-2+ART-4.pdf,2026-2+ART-4_0,en,tal de alcance descriptivo; cuya información se obtuvo mediante,"Introduction: Gender-based domestic violence continues to be a recurring and persistent social and legal problem in Peru, despite the existence of public policies and mechanisms aimed at preventing it. Objective: To determine whether domestic violence against women is a recurring problem in Peruvian society in 2024, in order to obtain better and more up-to-date information on gender-based domestic violence, as well as to contribute to the analysis of this identified problem. Methodology: This study was conducted using a basic quantitative approach with a non-experimental, descriptive design. Data were collected through a structured questionnaire administered to a sample of 20 Peruvian women and supplemented by a review of the literature and official statistics on domestic violence in Peru. Results: The findings from the surveys indicate and reaffirm that gender-based violence within the family unit is a very common problem in our current society and has been so for a long time. It manifests in physical, emotional, psychological, verbal, sexual, or economic forms, with physical violence being the most prevalent. Conclusions: Although there are government efforts to curb or reduce this type of violence, the statistics do not indicate a successful outcome",Status of women; Family environment; Domestic violence; Gender-based violence. 1 Los términos clave han sido recuperados a partir del Tesauro https://vocabularies.unesco.org/browser/thesaurus/es/. Domestic Violence from a Gender Perspective in Peru During 2024: A Recurring Problem Violência Intrafamiliar na Perspectiva de Gênero no Peru em 2024: Um Problema Recorrente ARTÍCULO DE REVISIÓN DO,marcadores,tal de alcance descriptivo cuya informacion se obtuvo mediante,introduction gender-bas domestic violence continu recurr persistent social legal problem peru despite existence public polici mechanism aimed preve