2745-1402,2026-2+ART-6+(1).pdf,2026-2+ART-6+(1)_0,es,ARTÍCULO DE REFLEXIÓN,"Introducción: En el marco de la neuropsicología y la psicología de las organizaciones, surge el interés por estudiar la toma de decisiones en el liderazgo, proceso que depende, entre otros factores de dominios cerebrales específicos relacionados con las funciones ejecutivas, como se ha abordado en estudios sobre liderazgo y neurociencias. Objetivo: Analizar la existencia de asociaciones entre las variables estudiadas: estilos de liderazgo y la toma de decisiones en el sector salud. Metodología: Estudio cuantitativo, con diseño no experimental de corte transversal y alcance asociativo. Los participantes, 50 líderes que desempeñan su actividad laboral en el sector salud. Los instrumentos utilizados fueron el cuestionario de liderazgo (MLQ-6S, adaptado, 2017), el Iowa Gambling Task y un cuestionario sociodemográfico. Resultados: Las asociaciones observadas fueron de magnitud pequeña, con coeficientes comprendidos entre r = -0,265 y r = 0,101. Los factores de Bayes y los intervalos de credibilidad del 95% respaldaron la ausencia de asociaciones entre los estilos de liderazgo y el desempeño en la toma de decisiones. Conclusiones: Estos hallazgos contradicen las hipótesis teóricas (H1, H2 y H3); esto sugiere que determinados estilos, aunque tradicionalmente valorados, no tienen relación con la eficiencia en la toma de decisiones en ciertos contextos organizacionales",Funciones ejecutivas; Liderazgo; Toma de decisiones; Servicios de salud,marcadores,articulo reflexion,introduccion marco neuropsicologia psicologia organiz surge inter estudiar toma decision liderazgo proceso depende entre otros factor domini cerebral especific relacionad funcion ejecutiv como ha abordado estudi sobre liderazgo neurocienci objetivo analizar existencia asoci entre variabl estudiad estil liderazgo toma decision sector salud metodologia estudio cuantitativo diseno no experimental corte transversal alcance asociativo participant 50 lider desempenan actividad laboral sector salud instrument utilizad fueron cuestionario liderazgo mlq-6s adaptado 2017 iowa gambling task cuestionario sociodemografico resultad asoci observad fueron magnitud pequena coeficient comprendid entre -0 265 101 factor bayes interval credibilidad 95 respaldaron ausencia asoci entre estil liderazgo desempeno toma decision conclusion estos hallazg contradicen hipotesis teoric h1 h2 h3 esto sugiere determinad estil aunque tradicional valorad no tienen relacion eficiencia toma decision ciert context organizacional,funcion ejecutiv liderazgo toma decision servici salud,articulo reflexion introduccion marco neuropsicologia psicologia organiz surge inter estudiar toma decision liderazgo proceso depende entre otros factor domini cerebral especific relacionad funcion ejecutiv como ha abordado estudi sobre liderazgo neurocienci objetivo analizar existencia asoci entre variabl estudiad estil liderazgo toma decision sector salud metodologia estudio cuantitativo diseno no experimental corte transversal alcance asociativo participant 50 lider desempenan actividad laboral sector salud instrument utilizad fueron cuestionario liderazgo mlq-6s adaptado 2017 iowa gambling task cuestionario sociodemografico resultad asoci observad fueron magnitud pequena coeficient comprendid entre -0 265 101 factor bayes interval credibilidad 95 respaldaron ausencia asoci entre estil liderazgo desempeno toma decision conclusion estos hallazg contradicen hipotesis teoric h1 h2 h3 esto sugiere determinad estil aunque tradicional valorad no tienen relacion eficiencia toma decision ciert context organizacional funcion ejecutiv liderazgo toma decision servici salud,1.0.0,68286fa56daea069
2745-1402,2026-2+ART-6+(1).pdf,2026-2+ART-6+(1)_0,en,"asociativo. Los participantes, 50","Introduction: Within the fields of neuropsychology and organizational psychology, there is growing interest in studying decision-making in leadership—a process that depends, among other factors, on specific brain regions related to executive functions, as has been addressed in studies on leadership and neuroscience. Objective: To analyze the existence of associations between the variables studied: leadership styles and decision-making in the healthcare sector. Methodology: A quantitative study with a non-experimental, cross-sectional design and an associative scope. The participants consisted of 50 leaders working in the healthcare sector. The instruments used were the leadership questionnaire (MLQ-6S, adapted, 2017), the Iowa Gambling Task, and a sociodemographic questionnaire. Results: The observed associations were small in magnitude, with coefficients ranging from r = -0.265 to r = 0.101. Bayes’ factors and 95% credibility intervals supported the absence of associations between leadership styles and decision-making performance. Conclusions: These findings contradict the theoretical hypotheses (H1, H2, and H3); this suggests that certain leadership styles, although traditionally valued, are not related to decision-making efficiency in certain organizational contexts",Executive functions; Leadership; Decision-making; Health services. Leadership styles and decision-making in the healthcare sector from a neuropsychological perspective Estilos de liderança e tomada de decisões no setor da saúde sob a perspetiva da neuropsicologia ARTICULO DE INVESTIGACIÓN DOI: https://doi.org/10.21803/penamer.19.40.1049 2 Estilos de liderazgo y toma de decisiones en el sector sal,marcadores,asociativo los participant 50,introduction within field neuropsychology organizational psychology there grow interest study decision-mak leadership--a proces depend among other factor specific brain region relat executive function has been address studi leadership neuroscience objective analyze existence associ between variabl studi leadership styl decision-mak healthcare sector methodology quantitative study non-experimental cross-sectional design associative scope participant consist 50 leader work healthcare sector instrument used leadership questionnaire mlq-6s adapt 2017 iowa gambl task sociodemographic questionnaire result observ associ small magnitude coefficient rang -0 265 101 baye factor 95 credibility interval support absence associ between leadership styl decision-mak performance conclusion these finding contradict theoretical hypothes h1 h2 h3 suggest certain leadership styl although traditionally valu not relat decision-mak efficiency certain organizational context,executive function leadership decision-mak health servic leadership styl decision-mak healthcare sector neuropsychological perspective estilo de lideranca tomada de deciso no setor da saude sob perspetiva da neuropsicologia articulo de investigacion doi http doi org 10 21803 penamer 19 40 1049 estilo de liderazgo toma de decision en el sector sal,asociativo los participant 50 introduction within field neuropsychology organizational psychology there grow interest study decision-mak leadership--a proces depend among other factor specific brain region relat executive function has been address studi leadership neuroscience objective analyze existence associ between variabl studi leadership styl decision-mak healthcare sector methodology quantitative study non-experimental cross-sectional design associative scope participant consist 50 leader work healthcare sector instrument used leadership questionnaire mlq-6s adapt 2017 iowa gambl task sociodemographic questionnaire result observ associ small magnitude coefficient rang -0 265 101 baye factor 95 credibility interval support absence associ between leadership styl decision-mak performance conclusion these finding contradict theoretical hypothes h1 h2 h3 suggest certain leadership styl although traditionally valu not relat decision-mak efficiency certain organizational context executive function leadership decision-mak health servic leadership styl decision-mak healthcare sector neuropsychological perspective estilo de lideranca tomada de deciso no setor da saude sob perspetiva da neuropsicologia articulo de investigacion doi http doi org 10 21803 penamer 19 40 1049 estilo de liderazgo toma de decision en el sector sal,1.0.0,a780302e34b495eb
2745-1402,2026-2+ART-7+(2).pdf,2026-2+ART-7+(2)_0,en,ARTÍCULO DE REFLEXIÓN,"Introduction: Research training in teacher education requires the articulation of methodological knowledge, inquiry experiences, and opportunities for participation throughout university education. Objective: To analyze the development of research skills among fifth-year teacher education students at the Adventist University of Chile, considering their self-reported levels and training experiences. Methodology: A mixed-methods approach with a convergent parallel design was used. Twenty-seven students completed a validated research skills scale, and eight participated in a focus group. Quantitative data were analyzed using descriptive statistics and qualitative data through narrative analysis; both components were integrated through methodological triangulation. Results: Medium research skill levels predominated (63%), followed by high (33.3%) and low levels (3.7%). The main strengths were concentrated in the communication and cooperative domains, whereas the greatest difficulties were observed in the exploratory and analytical and interpretive domains. Participants described research training as late, predominantly theoretical, and weakly connected to practice. Conclusions: The findings reveal discontinuities in research training and support curricular review aimed at greater continuity, stronger theory–practice articulation, and active student participation, while restricting these conclusions to the institutional context studied",Higher education; Initial teacher education; Preservice teachers; Research skills; Research training,marcadores,articulo de reflexion,introduction research train teacher education requir articulation methodological knowledge inquiry experienc opportuniti participation throughout university education objective analyze development research skill among fifth-year teacher education student adventist university chile consider their self-report level train experienc methodology mixed-method approach convergent parallel design used twenty-seven student complet validat research skill scale eight participat focu group quantitative data analyz using descriptive statistic qualitative data through narrative analysi both component integrat through methodological triangulation result medium research skill level predominat 63 follow high 33 low level main strength concentrat communication cooperative domain wherea greatest difficulti observ exploratory analytical interpretive domain participant describ research train late predominantly theoretical weakly connect practice conclusion finding reveal discontinuiti research train support curricular review aimed greater continuity stronger theory-practice articulation active student participation while restrict these conclusion institutional context studi,higher education initial teacher education preservice teacher research skill research train,articulo de reflexion introduction research train teacher education requir articulation methodological knowledge inquiry experienc opportuniti participation throughout university education objective analyze development research skill among fifth-year teacher education student adventist university chile consider their self-report level train experienc methodology mixed-method approach convergent parallel design used twenty-seven student complet validat research skill scale eight participat focu group quantitative data analyz using descriptive statistic qualitative data through narrative analysi both component integrat through methodological triangulation result medium research skill level predominat 63 follow high 33 low level main strength concentrat communication cooperative domain wherea greatest difficulti observ exploratory analytical interpretive domain participant describ research train late predominantly theoretical weakly connect practice conclusion finding reveal discontinuiti research train support curricular review aimed greater continuity stronger theory-practice articulation active student participation while restrict these conclusion institutional context studi higher education initial teacher education preservice teacher research skill research train,1.0.0,434013055b7e64b7
2745-1402,2026-2+ART-7+(2).pdf,2026-2+ART-7+(2)_0,es,through narrative analysis; both components were integrated through methodological,"Introducción: La formación investigativa en pedagogía requiere articular conocimientos metodológicos, experiencias de indagación y oportunidades de participación durante la trayectoria universitaria. Objetivo: Analizar el desarrollo de las habilidades investigativas en estudiantes de quinto año de pedagogía de la Universidad Adventista de Chile, considerando sus niveles autorreportados y experiencias de formación. Metodología: Se empleó un enfoque mixto con diseño paralelo convergente. Participaron 27 estudiantes en la aplicación de una escala validada de habilidades investigativas y ocho en un grupo focal. Los datos cuantitativos se analizaron mediante estadística descriptiva y los cualitativos mediante análisis narrativo; ambos componentes se integraron mediante triangulación metodológica. Resultados: Predominó el nivel medio de habilidades investigativas (63%), seguido del nivel alto (33,3%) y bajo (3,7%). Las principales fortalezas se concentraron en los dominios comunicativos y cooperativo, mientras que las mayores dificultades se observaron en los dominios exploratorio y analítico e interpretativo. Los relatos describieron una formación investigativa tardía, predominantemente teórica y poco articulada con la práctica. Conclusiones: Los hallazgos evidencian discontinuidades en la formación investigativa y orientan la revisión curricular hacia una mayor continuidad, articulación teoría-práctica y participación estudiantil activa, circunscribiendo estas conclusiones al contexto institucional estudiado",Educación superior; Formación inicial del profesorado; Futuros docentes; Habilidades de investigación; Capacitación en investigación. Habilidades investigativas en estudiantes de pedagogía de la Universidad Adventista de Chile Habilidades de pesquisa em estudantes de pedagogia da Universidade Adventista do Chile RESEARCH ARTICLE D